window.AKK_ZOMBIE_CAT_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_ZOMBIE_CAT_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":1,"title":"Chapter 1","paragraphs":["An ordinary weekend.","An ordinary little apartment.","Jiang Cheng was curled up in a beanbag chair by the floor-to-ceiling window, dozing off like she usually did. Sunlight streamed through the window, dust particles floating lazily, just like every other summer afternoon.","But this afternoon took a sudden turn. Jiang Cheng snapped open her eyes in the middle of her nap—a strange current seemed to surge through her body, leaving her numb and weak, her fingertips twitching.","It felt like a switch had been flipped in her brain, and information that had been locked away for who knows how long came flooding in like a dam breaking.","Jiang Cheng’s pupils contracted. She remembered everything!","So she wasn’t from this world after all. She was a transmigrator.","When the electric sensation faded, Jiang Cheng rolled onto the floor, drenched in cold sweat, gasping for air.","She closed her eyes to calm herself, sorting through and absorbing the flood of information.","She still had all the memories of growing up as “Jiang Cheng”—childhood, adolescence, college, her parents’ deaths, graduation, dealing with relatives, selling the house, moving to this city alone to settle down. Yet now, she knew with absolute clarity that she was a transmigrator, from a different world.","But who she was before the transmigration, what kind of world she came from, and when she had crossed over—all of that was a blank, completely blank.","Jiang Cheng rubbed her face, sat up, and stretched her hands in front of her, examining them. She checked her body—nothing seemed particularly different. She had full control over it.","But being told now that this body might not even belong to her? That was hard to accept.","In her memories, up until this awakening, “Jiang Cheng” had lived a complete, ordinary life as a regular person.","She glanced around her apartment—though it was just a small studio, the floor-to-ceiling window was bright, and the decor was cozy.","The layout felt like a hotel: the bathroom was right next to the entrance, and the rest was an open space. Near the window was the sofa, TV wall, dining table, and a sideboard. Further in was the bed, with a wardrobe at the foot of it, and a desk that doubled as a vanity, holding cosmetics and a laptop.","There was no balcony, just an oddly shaped floor-to-ceiling window with a bit of extra space where she kept the beanbag chair, perfect for soaking up the sun.","The inheritance from her parents had bought this apartment with some leftover change. Her salary wasn’t huge, but it was enough to live on and maintain a fairly comfortable life in this city.","It was ordinary, uneventful—nothing to complain about, really. Maybe it was because she was sitting in the sunlight pouring through the window, which made it easy to feel lazy and content.","This sudden awakening as a transmigrator seemed utterly meaningless to her life.","Just... let it be.","She turned her gaze to see someone walking a pet downstairs. Jiang Cheng picked up her phone and checked the time.","Living alone without much financial pressure, she had bought the latest phone model this year. It was a slim clamshell phone, nine buttons with a comfortable feel, equipped with a color screen and even a built-in camera for taking photos.","This phone, the newest model of the year, was arguably the most advanced personal device in this world right now. The joy and novelty she felt when she first got it were still vivid in her memory. That was just a few months ago.","But now, holding this latest phone in her hand, Jiang Cheng somehow felt none of her old fondness for it. Instead, there was a faint... disappointment?","Deep down, it felt like this device hadn’t quite met her expectations, that it wasn’t worthy of her liking.","Why had she liked it so much before?","Because before, she hadn’t awakened.","Jiang Cheng realized that even though she still hadn’t unlocked the memories of her life before transmigrating, her true self was already influencing the consciousness and perceptions of the identity called “Jiang Cheng.”","The phone showed it was almost three in the afternoon.","At this time on a weekend, she was supposed to...","“Meow~”","A cat’s meow echoed from downstairs.","Jiang Cheng leaned out to look—two cats were already staring up at her window from below.","“Coming! Coming!” Jiang Cheng hurried to her feet.","The youth apartment complex, with its small unit sizes, attracted investors who rented them out. Tenants came and went, and some irresponsible ones would abandon their pets when leaving, so the neighborhood had quite a few stray cats.","Weekend afternoons were her designated time to feed them.","Jiang Cheng quickly gathered cat food and bowls, grabbed her bag, and headed downstairs.","When she appeared, four or five stray cats she usually saw had already gathered downstairs.","As she approached, two friendly cats came over to rub against her leg, while the others backed away cautiously, finding cover to watch her warily. It was easy to tell which ones were recently abandoned and which had been stray long enough to be hurt by humans.","Jiang Cheng crouched down to pet the heads of the two affectionate cats, then walked through the courtyard garden to her usual spot. She took out two bowls, filling one with cat food and the other with bottled water.","Compared to food, it was harder for cats to find clean water outside.","Her chosen spot was on one side of a path in the garden, opposite a bench meant for residents. After setting up, Jiang Cheng moved to the other side of the path and sat on the bench, keeping a safe distance. That way, the more wary cats would come over to eat.","Ideally, the best approach would be to take the stray cats home and adopt them.","But Jiang Cheng had lost her parents before she even graduated. After that, she had to handle their funeral, graduate, find a job, sell the house, buy an apartment, move, and adjust to the workplace—all on her own. Facing both entering society and living alone, she wasn’t sure yet if she could take on the responsibility of a pet.","Having experienced the loss of a loved one made her unusually cautious about matters of life, death, and parting. She feared she might also give up and abandon a pet, so she had held back until now.","But at this moment, sitting on the bench and watching the cats across the path—some eating cheerfully, others cautiously—eating cat food and drinking clean water, the world felt completely different yet utterly unchanged. Even if she had remembered she was a transmigrator, so what? Monday would still come, with work to do, a salary to earn, and the same routine of eating, drinking, and sleeping.","Thinking like this, Jiang Cheng felt at peace.","Transmigrator or not, it didn’t make a difference.","Jiang Cheng brushed back the hair from her forehead. Turning her gaze, she noticed that at the other end of the bench, a black cat had appeared out of nowhere.","Completely black, no stray hairs, shiny like obsidian.","The black cat sat quietly on the bench, staring at the cats across the path just like Jiang Cheng. From this angle, its profile looked as soft as a baby’s.","It carried a hint of loneliness.","When you spend a lot of time around animals, you tend to develop a habit of talking to them. Especially for someone living alone.","“New here?” Jiang Cheng asked.","The few cats grabbing at the cat food weren’t all familiar to her, but she had definitely never seen this black cat before.","The black cat ignored her.","“Kitty~kitty~” Jiang Cheng reached out a tentative hand. “Here, kitty~”","Just as her hand was about to touch it, the black cat tilted its head and dodged her reach.","She was like a little person. You could tell she had a temper, not the kind of cat that liked to cling and cuddle.","Jiang Cheng had been scratched several times before she finally learned how to keep the right distance from the cat. When the little black cat didn’t want to be touched, she withdrew her hand. “Go eat some cat food, or else the others will finish it all,” she said.","The little black cat ignored her, just silently watching the crowd of cats scrambling for food.","Even though cats could be very quiet, Jiang Cheng couldn’t shake the feeling that this one’s stillness was a bit off. Maybe it was because black cats always gave off a mysterious vibe?","Usually, white cats might get bullied by a group, but that didn’t mean other cats were immune.","Jiang Cheng couldn’t help glancing at the cats across the alley, then turned back and asked softly, “...Are they freezing you out?”","This time, the black cat actually turned its head to look at her.","Did animals have expressions in their eyes, too? Yes, they did. Especially cats and dogs.","The black cat glanced at her and then turned its head away. But that look didn’t strike Jiang Cheng as a pitiful little victim—it was more like a gangster cat.","Cold and indifferent.","The black cat lifted a paw and began to lick it.","Jiang Cheng reached out her hand toward the black cat again, this time moving slowly, stopping at a spot still a short distance from its head.","She had touched the cat food earlier, so her fingertips carried the scent. There was no way a kitty could resist that.","Sure enough, even the aloof little black cat twitched its nose and turned its head. It seemed reluctant, but in the end, instinct won out as it leaned in to sniff Jiang Cheng’s fingers, then licked its lips.","Jiang Cheng chuckled. When the little black cat finished sniffing, she raised her hand to stroke its fluffy little head.","The black cat flinched slightly, but since it had already sniffed her fingers, it wasn’t as resistant as before. Jiang Cheng gently rubbed the top of the black cat’s head.","Even a thug cat couldn’t fight its instincts. Liking head rubs and chin scratches was just a born-in urge for kittens.","After a few strokes, the little black cat seemed to relax.","“Go on, eat quickly,” Jiang Cheng urged, “otherwise the others will eat it all.”","As if it understood, the black cat actually glanced toward the other cats. Its gaze rested on the stray cats fighting over the food, watching intently.","“Go ahead,” Jiang Cheng said, giving it a gentle push.","But the black cat suddenly hissed at her!","Jiang Cheng jumped back, startled, and quickly withdrew her hands.","The black cat turned its head and licked the spot where she had pushed it.","Jiang Cheng sensed something was wrong. She tried to look more closely, but the cat’s head blocked her view. When she raised her hand, she saw red on her knuckles from where she had pushed the black cat—it had a wound.","“You’re hurt?” Jiang Cheng hesitated for a moment, then stood up. “Wait for me here, little one. Stay right here.”","She ran back upstairs.","She had read some knowledge about raising cats on a pet forum and knew that some medicines could be used for both humans and cats.","Jiang Cheng grabbed the medicine from upstairs and hurried back down, afraid the little black cat might leave. Luckily, it was still on the bench.","“This might sting a little,” Jiang Cheng tried to comfort the cat. “Don’t be scared, little one.”","But what good could human words do for a cat? Jiang Cheng aimed at the wound and pressed the nozzle. The medicine sprayed onto the wound with a puff, stinging sharply.","The black cat let out a piercing cry and leaped off the bench like lightning, diving into the bushes.","Jiang Cheng crouched down to look, but its dark fur blended in completely.","“Ah,” she sighed, a little worried. She had only sprayed once, and though it seemed to have hit the wound, she wasn’t sure if the amount was enough.","The stray cats finished eating and left one by one.","Jiang Cheng went over to clean up. There was still some cat food and water left in the bowls. She picked them up and glanced back at the bench.","She moved both bowls over to the bench and crouched down, calling, “Kitty, kitty—”","But the little black cat didn’t come out.","Still, Jiang Cheng decided to leave the food and water there in case the antisocial cat got hungry. She would come back to collect them tomorrow.","“Kitty, kitty—” she called into the bushes. “There’s food here. Eat if you’re hungry.”","After she left, the sun slowly sank. The sky was awash with twilight, and the trees stretched their long shadows until the sky went completely dark.","The streetlights came on right on time, and tiny bugs fluttered around the bulbs.","Suddenly, the bushes rustled faintly. A cat black as the night crept out. It had been hiding in the bushes all along, using its dark coat as camouflage, warily watching Jiang Cheng.","But after that sharp sting, the wound clearly felt much better.","The little black cat vaguely understood something.","Its stomach was growling. It looked at the two bowls Jiang Cheng had left behind, padded over, and ate everything cleanly.","Then it sniffed the empty bowls. The girl’s scent lingered on them.","The black cat memorized that scent."]},{"number":2,"title":"Chapter 2","paragraphs":["Even though she had awakened to the realization that she was a time traveler, it didn't really change anything about her life.","When Monday came around, she still had to go to work as usual. Mondays were always the most hectic day of the week, sometimes even requiring overtime.","After Jiang Cheng finished her overtime and returned to her residential complex, the sky had already grown dim.","The lights in the community garden weren't as bright as the streetlights outside, nor were they as densely placed. They were sparse, and the winding pathways created a quiet, secluded atmosphere.","Property management was getting more and more negligent. One of the lamp posts had even been broken for days without the bulb being replaced.","Jiang Cheng had to go to the garden to collect the two stainless steel bowls she had left for the black kitten the day before. Seeing that the path ahead was pitch black because of the broken light, she thought to herself that she would definitely file a complaint with the property management later and urge them to fix the lamp quickly. Suddenly, she noticed a figure standing in the darkness.","It was too dark. She could only see clearly when she got closer.","This was a gated residential community with condo-style apartment buildings; incidents like robberies were unlikely. Jiang Cheng didn't pay much attention and continued walking, intending to pass by the person.","It was only when she got much closer that she saw the person's hands were positioned in a strange way around their waist.","By the time Jiang Cheng realized something was wrong, it was already too late. The person had been holding onto the waistband of their pants, and the moment Jiang Cheng looked at them, they gave a creepy grin, yanked their pants down, and exposed themselves.","An exhibitionist.","A total pervert!","Jiang Cheng stepped forward, swung her shoulder bag in a half-circle, and lashed out!","The bag smacked the sicko's right cheek!","The pervert yelped in pain, stumbled, tripped over his own half-pulled-down pants, and fell out of the pathway onto the grass.","Jiang Cheng's parents had died in an accident before she even graduated from college. Her relatives had been greedy for her inheritance, so she had sold the house in her hometown and moved far away to the big city. Since then, she had always lived alone.","When you only have yourself, even if you're frail and slender, you have to stand your ground and protect yourself.","Jiang Cheng always carried a small, light dumbbell in her bag. It wasn't heavy, but in a situation like this, it could turn a girl's bag into a flail, letting her surprise an attacker with a sudden blow.","Perverts usually targeted young girls, and most young girls who encountered such a shock would panic and run away screaming. Someone like Jiang Cheng, who would silently attack without a word, was rare.","The pervert knew he had picked on the wrong person this time. He rolled on the ground, hastily pulled up his pants, and tried to run.","Jiang Cheng wouldn't let him get away. Shouting \"Stop!\", she tried to grab his arm and collar. The pervert twisted around and shoved her hard. He was strong, and Jiang Cheng was knocked to the ground.","The pervert took the chance and bolted!","But from the bushes, a black shadow suddenly shot out!","It tore across the pervert's face, appearing like lightning and then vanishing into the night in an instant. It happened so fast that Jiang Cheng, just getting up from the ground, only saw a blur.","Jiang Cheng couldn't even be sure if she had seen anything.","But the pervert's screams as he clutched his face proved that something had indeed happened.","The pervert stumbled forward, clutching his face. The black shadow darted through the darkness again to attack his face. This time, its claws slashed his arm, which was still covering his face. The pervert shrieked and thrashed his now bloody arm to drive the shadow away.","The black shadow nimbly turned in midair and landed steadily, right in a patch of light.","Jet black all over, with piercing green eyes and long, powerful legs.","A black cat.","Was it the same one from yesterday? It seemed so.","The black cat was attacking the pervert so ferociously that Jiang Cheng didn't dare approach immediately.","When she first started interacting with stray cats, she had been scratched several times. Later, an older woman she fed cats with advised her not to forget that cats, no matter how cute, were still animals. All animals have wild instincts.","As feline creatures, cats were at the upper size limit of animals that could be kept as pets. Among animals of similar size, cats were near the top in fighting prowess.","\"Shit! Shit!\" The pervert finally saw that his attacker was just a cat. He flew into a rage and looked around the ground and the grass, clearly searching for something to use as a weapon.","The black cat hissed at the man.","Hissing was a cat's declaration of war.","But instead of attacking again, it looked at Jiang Cheng.","There was no hostility in the glance the black cat gave her right after hissing.","It was like a tiny, faint electric current passing through her heart. It didn't hurt, it wasn't even a shock. It was more like someone gently poked you with a finger.","Like a reminder.","Jiang Cheng felt as if she had been snapped out of a daze. She yelled at the top of her lungs, \"Stop him, a pervert! Stop him!\"","It was dinnertime, but that didn't mean the community garden was deserted.","The pervert forgot about taking revenge on the cat. He scrambled on all fours to get up and flee. But Jiang Cheng wouldn't let him. Still shouting \"Someone help! Stop that pervert!\", she kicked him in the back, sending him tumbling to the ground, and then lunged onto him to pin him down.","The pervert wasn't prepared for her. She twisted one of his arms behind his back, pressed a knee into his lower back, and used her body weight to hold him against the ground.","\"What's going on?\" Some neighbors who were residents of the complex came running over. \"What happened?\"","He was strong, and Jiang Cheng was struggling to hold him. She explained quickly, \"He pulled down his pants and was exposing himself! Help me out! Hurry, he's—\"","The pervert tried to twist free and run again. But he hadn't even fastened his pants properly. The struggle caused them to slip down, revealing half his bare backside. He wasn't wearing underwear. It confirmed what the young woman had said.","Some of the male neighbors stepped in to help pin him down. \"Stay still!\"","\"Thank you, thank you!\" Jiang Cheng panted as she stood up. She picked her bag off the ground and pulled out her phone. \"I'll call the police now.\"","With the phone to her ear, waiting for the call to connect, she scanned her surroundings.","The black cat was gone.","It was the real hero of the day.","Police from the local precinct arrived quickly.","This area comprised several large housing developments and was quite densely populated. The commercial streets were busy enough, and the area even had its own police booth for faster response times.","The situation was simple. Jiang Cheng explained the entire story to the officer in three minutes.","The officer ordered the pervert to pull up his pants, handcuffed him, and put him in the patrol car. As the person who reported the incident and the victim, Jiang Cheng got into the car and went to the local police station with them.","Once at the station, she gave a brief written account, signed her name, and was told she could leave.","By then, it was completely dark. Strangely, there were even more people in the community garden than before. Many neighbors had finished their dinner and were out for a walk.","Jiang Cheng went back to the bench hopefully. To her delight, the black cat was right there, sitting on the bench. It was looking at the pathway under the streetlamp, like a contemplative person.","\"Mimi,\" Jiang Cheng said, her eyes curving into a smile, slowing her steps as she approached.","She had come back just to see if she could find this black cat. If it hadn't been for him today, that pervert would have used the chance to escape after shoving her. That stretch of road was pitch black; she hadn't gotten a good look at his face at all. If he had gotten away, it would have been impossible to catch him.","Today, she really had this little black cat to thank.","The black cat glanced at her. It showed no strange reaction to her approach; its demeanor was perfectly calm.","Relieved, Jiang Cheng sat down on the bench too.","\"Thank you so much for today,\" she said. \"Thanks to you, we caught that creep.\"","But the little black cat simply stood there, calmly gazing at the corridor bathed in the warm orange light and the greenery.","Well, of course—how could a little animal truly understand human speech? The way the black cat had looked at her amidst the chaos earlier had seemed so uncannily intelligent that she'd gotten the impression it might understand her.","But in reality, it didn't.","In the garden, under the night sky, on the bench along the lamp-lit path, there was only one person and one cat.","\"Anyway, you're the real hero,\" Jiang Cheng said.","She tentatively reached out her hand. Maybe because she had petted it the day before, or perhaps thanks to the bond formed during their shared battle earlier today, the little black cat didn't flinch and let her stroke its head.","It even enjoyed it so much that it couldn't help lifting its chin. Jiang Cheng readily scratched under its jaw. She was gradually getting better at interacting with cats.","After the petting session, Jiang Cheng pulled a cat treat stick from her bag and wagged it. \"This is my thank-you gift.\"","The black cat stared at the treat stick.","Jiang Cheng tore it open, and an enticing aroma wafted through the air.","Perhaps lured by the scent of food, or maybe feeling it had earned a reward for its merits, the black cat moved—for the first time, approaching Jiang Cheng on its own and began munching noisily from her hand.","As she finished feeding it the treat stick, Jiang Cheng noticed several feline shadows darting across the path and vanishing into the bushes in the distance.","She couldn't help asking, \"Why are you always alone? Do you not get along with the other Mimis?\"","The black cat seemed disinclined to hear this. It turned away to lick its paw and clean its face.","Its black silhouette, outlined by the lamplight, looked a little lonely.","Just like Jiang Cheng.","Jiang Cheng was lonely too.","In truth, she had never established a real life for herself in this city. Work was merely a means of survival; colleagues were just people she had to cooperate with on the job. Her current state could barely be called living.","After all, a big city meant being alone. All her social interactions stayed on the surface because her roots weren't here.","When both parents were gone, a person didn't even know where their roots were anymore.","Suddenly, Jiang Cheng froze.","Were these feelings and memories truly Jiang Cheng's, or 'Jiang Cheng's'?","She couldn't tell.","Her gaze drifted back to the black cat.","She had never been able to make up her mind about getting a companion animal, but at that moment, looking at the black cat's lonely silhouette, a longing suddenly arose.","\"How about,\" she said, \"you come home with me?\"","The black cat, absorbed in its meticulous washing, paused and turned to look at her.","How strange—did it understand human language or not? Sometimes it seemed oblivious, and other times eerily perceptive.","Jiang Cheng stared at the black cat, anticipation flooding her heart.","The black cat held her gaze for a moment, then leaped silently to the ground and vanished into the bushes.","Ah, so it didn't want to?","I'd take care of you."]},{"number":3,"title":"Chapter 3","paragraphs":["Jiang Cheng brought home the two bowls left from yesterday, changed clothes, and opened her laptop to log into the community’s homeowners’ forum.","Although broadband had already become widespread in big cities, many middle-aged people mostly only read the news or played casual games on portal sites; they weren’t very skilled at using interactive platforms like forums.","Only in communities with a high number of young people did the owners’ forums get lively. In the youth apartment complex’s forum, several hot posts were already discussing the indecent exposure incident that had been dealt with today.","People had also replied.","One girl said: [I’ve run into that too! It scared me to death. I just ran away]","Several other girls had similar experiences. When young women saw a man’s private parts, most felt both disgusted and terrified, and their first instinct was to turn and run.","Jiang Cheng clicked on the reply box and typed: [Don’t be afraid. People who do bad things may seem tough, but they’re actually full of guilt. Especially creeps like this—if they had any real guts, they’d rob a bank. The fact that they only dare to harass girls in secluded spots shows they’re cowards. Even if you’re not brave enough to fight back, just shouting loudly to attract nearby people can work. That’ll teach them not to dare do it again.]","Without parents, even if you turn and run, there’s no home to go back to, and no one will protect you. Soon, you realize you have to rely on yourself.","Although it had only been two years since “Jiang Cheng” left school, she was already completely different from when her parents were still alive.","Someone else asked: [How did that guy get into the complex? Could he be living here?]","Jiang Cheng took a sip of cola and typed: [Building 4, surname Chen.]","That was all she knew. Earlier, she had overheard a bit, and later the two suspects were interrogated separately.","After replying, she went to wash up. When she came back and opened the forum again, the neighbors had left a string of questions: [Is that the creep from today?]","[Really?]","[How do you know?]","[I’ll check out Building 4 later to see if it’s true. I helped hold that guy down today—I remember his face.]","Jiang Cheng didn’t bother with that thread anymore. There would always be nosy neighbors willing to investigate.","She closed that post and clicked on the pet forum, happily browsing people’s experiences and fun stories about raising pets.","Some things don’t occur to you until you start thinking about them, but once you do, you can’t let them go.","Jiang Cheng, who had been hesitant about whether to get a cat, couldn’t stop herself once the idea took hold. She wanted to adopt one.","And not just any cat—only the little black cat that had bravely faced that pervert alongside her.","Just like her, all alone.","Just like her, fearless of bad people.","They were too similar. She felt that together, they could make a good life.","Jiang Cheng scrolled through many posts and wrote down everything needed for raising a cat.","The next day, Tuesday, was less busy than Monday; she at least got off work on time. On her way home, Jiang Cheng stopped by the Duomart supermarket near her place and bought cat beds, cat litter, a litter box, and everything else she needed. She didn’t need to buy cat food—there was still some at home for feeding stray cats.","Everything was ready, just waiting for the little black cat to move in.","But things didn’t go as planned. Over the next few evenings, Jiang Cheng couldn’t find the little black cat in the complex. Had it stopped hanging around here?","Jiang Cheng was disappointed.","Other cats came over to rub against her, but there’s a fate between people and cats. Jiang Cheng only wanted to take that little black cat home.","Luckily, on Friday evening, Jiang Cheng spotted the little black cat she’d been thinking about as she walked through the garden after work.","The pitch-black kitten was sitting on the same bench as before, quietly licking its paw.","Jiang Cheng wasn’t entirely sure at first—since black cats have no distinctive markings to go by—so she tested the waters with a tentative, “Here, kitty kitty?”","The black cat paused mid-lick and turned its head to look at her.","Its eyes gleamed an emerald green, like a pair of precious jewels.","It was definitely the cat she’d been thinking about. It had been a few days, and it seemed to have grown a little.","“Here, kitty?” Jiang Cheng approached slowly, controlling her pace.","The black cat stared at her without fear, showing no signs of defensiveness or wariness. Jiang Cheng was sure now—this was the same cat.","Her spirits lifted, and she walked over to the bench, reaching out to pet it.","But as she moved, she noticed that the evening sunlight reflected off several spots on the black cat’s fur in an unusual way.","Jiang Cheng squinted. Sure enough, it was blood.","That was the bad thing about black cats—too dark to see any bleeding. If it was a white cat, you’d notice right away.","“Are you hurt?” Jiang Cheng realized. So that’s why she hadn’t seen it for a few days—it must have gotten into a fight somewhere and only now came back injured.","The little black cat ignored her and kept licking its wounds.","Jiang Cheng crouched in front of the bench to get a closer look. At first glance, the kitten was completely black, but a closer look showed the wounds were still bleeding. Much worse than last time.","Jiang Cheng had medicine at home, but this time she saw a chance to lure the cat in for good. “You’re hurt, huh? Why don’t you come home with me? I’ve got medicine there. How about it? Be good~”","As she coaxed it with her voice, Jiang Cheng tentatively reached her hand out to the little black cat. To her delight, the kitten seemed familiar with her now, not flinching or resisting, but staying docile and calm.","Jiang Cheng successfully scooped the black cat up into her arms.","“Our little kitty’s so smart,” she praised aloud, all the while hurrying toward her building in big strides, afraid the kitten might change its mind and bolt.","Luckily, the black cat stayed obedient the whole way, not struggling at all. At the entrance to her building, it even lifted its head for a look, as if memorizing the address.","Jiang Cheng triumphantly lured the black cat into her home.","Once inside, she kicked the door shut and set the kitten down on the floor. In that moment, she felt a joy like she’d just pulled off something huge—","She had a cat now!","A cat! Hers!","No more being alone from now on!","“Stay right there, don’t move. Wait for me a second.”","Jiang Cheng dropped her bag, quickly washed her hands, and opened her first-aid kit to find medicine that was safe for cats. She placed the black cat on her desk, cranked the desk lamp up to full brightness, and carefully searched for its wounds.","Now she could see clearly enough—it was pretty bad. There were several wounds.","“What have you been up to?” Jiang Cheng asked as she carefully applied the medicine. “Were you fighting over territory? Or...”","Out of curiosity, she lifted the black cat’s tail for a quick peek.","A pair of jet-black testicles, completely adorable.","“A boy, huh? Did you get into a fight over a girl cat?”","The black cat had been patiently holding out its front paws, letting her tend to it, but it was caught off guard by Jiang Cheng’s sudden move—an invasion of feline privacy! It nearly bristled with indignation.","The black cat let out a sharp “Mew~” and yanked its tail back, flicking it forcefully as if in protest.","“Oh, my, my,” Jiang Cheng laughed. “What a shy little kitten!”","Normally, she didn’t add so many cutesy words like “oh” or “my,” but for some reason, the moment she talked to the cat, they came flooding out, and her voice turned all cooey.","But it lifted her spirits all the same.","Jiang Cheng carefully applied medicine to the black cat’s wounds. She had prepared many things for adopting the kitten, and now she put a collar on it, held it steady, and dabbed on the ointment. Though the cat let out a few protests, it no longer tried to run away.","“All done.” Jiang Cheng unclasped the collar from the little black cat. “No more wounds, right? I’ve treated everything.”","The black cat lowered its head to examine the injuries on its body, feeling the medicine’s healing effects soothing its flesh.","After Jiang Cheng put the first-aid kit back and settled at her desk, the black cat voluntarily rubbed its head against her.","Was this... acknowledging her as its owner?","“Then I’ll give you a name first.” Jiang Cheng grew excited. “You’re not a stray anymore. You need a name of your own.”","“How about... Coal Ball?”","“Charcoal?”","“You don’t like either?” Seeing the little black cat’s indifferent reaction, Jiang Cheng racked her brains. “In ancient times, cats were called ‘li nu’—how about... Mo Li?”","Before the black cat could respond, Jiang Cheng had already fallen in love with the name herself. “Mo Li, that’s it! This one sounds nice!”","“From now on, you’re my cat, understand, Mo Li?”","“Remember, your name is Mo Li.”","“Our Mo Li is such a handsome little guy.”","Mo Li’s green eyes stared at her, and he let out a soft meow, as if accepting the name.","Cats were such quiet animals—completely unlike the neighbor’s dog next door, which barked every time someone passed by the door.","Jiang Cheng fetched the cat bed and litter box she had bought earlier. She opened the bag of cat litter, poured it into the box, filled the food bowl with kibble, and added fresh water to the water bowl.","She turned around, gently picked up Mo Li, and showed him around his new home. “This is your bed, this is your bathroom, and these are your food and water bowls.”","Jiang Cheng set Mo Li down. He took a few steps, lapped up some water, went over to inspect the bed, and then walked to the litter box and sniffed it.","Jiang Cheng’s heart filled with anticipation.","When raising a pet, the biggest worry was always potty training—especially for a first-timer. The posts on pet forums all said kittens instinctively knew how to use the litter box, so there was no need to worry.","But how could a new cat owner not worry?","Mo Li sniffed the litter. The scent was too strong—too stimulating for a cat. He turned his head to look at Jiang Cheng.","Jiang Cheng: “...?”","Naturally, Jiang Cheng had no idea what a cat was trying to say. She stared at Mo Li for a moment, then he turned back, crawled into his bed, buried his face, and curled up.","Jiang Cheng felt both joy and worry.","She was happy that Mo Li had accepted his new home, but she was anxious that he wouldn’t use the litter box and might pee or poop all over the place.","Jiang Cheng rubbed the kitten’s fluffy head, pointed at the litter box, and warned him, “Remember, poop and pee go in the box.”","Mo Li buried his face even deeper.","Carrying the happy feeling of “I have a cat now,” Jiang Cheng drifted peacefully to sleep.","Though it was just a small, furry kitten, her apartment suddenly felt full and warm.","In her sleep, she seemed to hear the sound of a window opening. Jiang Cheng turned over groggily and continued sleeping.","Jiang Cheng had expected to wake up on Saturday morning happily playing with her cat. Instead, all that greeted her was an empty apartment and a half-open window screen.","The cat bed was vacant, with only a few stray hairs scattered inside.","The litter box showed no sign of use at all.","But the food bowl was empty, and the water bowl had been drunk from significantly.","An indescribable disappointment settled in Jiang Cheng’s heart.","Had he left just like that? Without any hesitation?","Her apartment was small, but it was more than enough for the two of them to live happily together.","Wasn’t having a home a good thing?","Or was he really just born to love freedom?","The joy of \"having a cat\" lasted only one night before it faded away.","Jiang Cheng sighed. Oh well, maybe the timing just wasn’t right.","It was another perfectly ordinary weekend, just like the one before.","Last weekend, Jiang Cheng had realized she was a time traveler.","She thought it was a rare coincidence. Her attitude toward this world was to take things as they came—she just wanted to live peacefully and quietly.","But it seemed the world didn’t feel the same way.","That afternoon, as usual, Jiang Cheng went to the garden to bring food and water to the cats. She even looked around carefully and called out a few times, \"Mo Li.\" But she didn’t see the little black cat again.","Feeling disappointed, Jiang Cheng noticed her head was strangely dizzy and heavy.","People in the garden were pointing at the sky.","The usually bright blue sky had taken on an eerie purple hue.","Someone said, \"That looks scary. Is there going to be a thunderstorm?\"","But the air wasn’t humid. The sky just wasn’t as bright, as if dusk had arrived early.","Jiang Cheng glanced at the somewhat ominous sky and felt her head grow worse.","She put away the cat bowls and went back upstairs. She thought she might have caught a chill from the air conditioning and took a packet of cold medicine.","But the dizziness and headache didn’t ease.","The strange purple light in the sky wouldn’t fade; it just shifted over time from a bright violet to a dull, murky gray-purple.","By evening, the outdoor temperature was much cooler than during the day. Quite a few people were in the courtyard—some enjoying the cool air, others jogging.","Someone had just returned to the neighborhood after a day out. Someone else had just showered, dressed, and styled their hair, ready to head to a bar for the night.","The next-door complex was filled with standard apartment units, mostly families. Even more people were hanging out in their courtyard that evening.","On a summer night, no one went to bed too early, especially on the weekend. Some kids were still awake, playing in the yard.","There were also moms, dads, grandparents, nannies, and babysitters pushing strollers or holding babies.","The small shops around the youth apartments were mostly closed—either with steel shutters pulled down or U-shaped locks hanging on their glass doors.","The BuDuoDuo supermarket, less than a kilometer from the neighborhood, had finished its business for the day. Customers had left, and employees locked up and clocked out.","The road was still fairly busy, with cars driving by constantly. On weekend nights, traffic even jammed near the commercial entertainment areas.","The clock on the wall ticked away second by second: click, click, click—","Jiang Cheng felt no relief from her cold. Her dizziness was getting worse. She thought she had a fever, so she dug out a thermometer and measured her temperature. It was 39 degrees Celsius—she definitely had a fever.","She took some cold medicine and fever reducers. When she stood up again, her vision blurred, and she could barely keep her balance. Luckily, her room was small. She stumbled a few steps to her bed, collapsed onto it, and lost consciousness...","Jiang Cheng thought she was just sick. She didn’t know that at that moment, the neighborhood was terrifyingly silent.","Because her neighbors were the same. Even though they hadn’t felt strange all afternoon like she had, at the same moment Jiang Cheng fell into bed and passed out—whether at home, outdoors, in restaurants, on the road, walking, or driving—everyone suddenly felt dizzy and feverish, and lost consciousness at the same time.","The entire city was like this.","Those who were at home collapsed onto the floor or the sofa. Those who had gone to bed early fell into a feverish unconsciousness in their sleep.","In the bar, lights flashed and music roared. Yet the people on the dance floor seemed unable to keep moving; one by one, they grabbed the railings and shuffled back to their seats. Before they could even sit down, they collapsed onto the floor, their faces pressed against the soles of other people's shoes.","On the streets and roads, people were also fainting. A taxi driver sat motionless by the curb, his eyes closed as if asleep.","Again and again, drivers on the road sensed something wrong in time to pull over, but they lost consciousness before they could call for an ambulance.","Even so, car crashes were inevitable everywhere. Cars burst into flames, drivers and passengers dying in their sleep.","No one called the police.","The purple glow in the night sky finally faded. The moon shone down on the world, and time seemed to stand still.","Every person across the globe had fallen unconscious, burning with high fever.","Some died directly in the throes of that fever.","Others woke up.","Next door to Jiang Cheng’s home, a dog sensed something amiss and barked anxiously.","Its owner, lying on the floor, had been twitching on all fours. Then suddenly, he lifted his head.","No whites in his eyes—his entire eyes were pitch black. His lips peeled back, and drool dripped down.","The human’s aura had changed. To the dog, which relied on its sense of smell, it was as if its owner had suddenly become a stranger.","Or a strange creature.","The dog backed away cautiously, baring its teeth and growling low.","Mo Li hadn’t actually gone far. He had eaten his fill, relieved himself in the soil outside, and was hiding in a tree in the garden, sleeping.","The world was eerily quiet, just right for sleeping.","Until the dog’s screams tore through the air.","Mo Li’s emerald eyes snapped open."]},{"number":4,"title":"Chapter 4","paragraphs":["It was the scream that woke Jiang Cheng.","The frame-structured building carried sound easily, and Jiang Cheng lived right next door, so she heard it most clearly.","She snapped her eyes open, gasping sharply. Her heart ached for several seconds before she finally regained clarity, slowly pushing herself upright.","What was going on next door? Why was the dog barking like that?","She had taken her medicine and slept—how long had it been?","Jiang Cheng sat on the edge of the bed, catching her breath, while the dog’s barking next door grew eerie.","After a minute or two, she felt her strength return. But the barking next door faded, then stopped entirely.","An unsettling silence fell over the entire complex.","Even more chilling than before.","Jiang Cheng stood up, her legs still a little weak. After a few steps, she felt better.","First, she went to turn on the light.","Turning on the light was meant to chase away fear, but somehow, the harsh, pale glow illuminating her empty apartment gave her an unnatural feeling.","The dog next door had gone completely silent. The way it had barked earlier was definitely wrong. Either something had happened to the dog, or something had happened to the person.","Jiang Cheng picked up her phone and dialed the police. But the emergency number, which should have connected immediately, rang several times without an answer.","She hung up and tried twice more—same result.","She called the property management. No one answered there either.","Jiang Cheng hung up again and glanced toward the floor-to-ceiling window.","At that moment, she suddenly realized why her own familiar home felt so strange now—it was too quiet. Where were the cars on the nearby road? She couldn’t hear a single sound.","Silence so deep it was terrifying.","Jiang Cheng felt that the whole world was off, even vaguely sensed that something was wrong with herself. But she didn’t have time to investigate what was happening to the world. She had to first see what was happening around her—what had happened next door.","Why had the dog’s sound vanished completely?","Jiang Cheng picked up the baseball bat she kept at home for self-defense and opened her door.","It was a small-unit youth apartment building, twenty-four apartments per floor. The hallway was long, more like a corridor in an office building. Looking down it, all she could see were doors.","At this moment, not a single person was in sight.","Even though the dog’s barking had been so agonizing just moments ago, no one had opened their door to check.","Jiang Cheng went to knock on the neighbor’s door. “Hello?”","“I’m from 0306 next door.”","“Is something wrong? Do you need help?”","Actually, the dog next door was quite cute—the only problem was that it barked whenever anyone passed by. But the neighbor was a reasonable person; whenever someone complained, he would apologize, making it hard for the others to stay upset with him.","But now, as Jiang Cheng knocked, the dog that usually started barking at the sound of footsteps was completely silent. Yet faint noises came from inside, clearly indicating someone was home.","She knocked again. “Hello? Do you need help?”","“Are you there?” Jiang Cheng decided to bluff, “I’ve called the property management. They’ll be here soon.”","She suspected there might be a burglar next door.","The neighbor loved his dog dearly. If he were home himself, the dog shouldn’t have been screaming like that. After she knocked several times without hearing a bark, she feared the dog might already have been killed by the intruder.","For safety, she invoked the property management to intimidate whoever was inside.","After she called out, she heard clear footsteps approaching the door from inside.","Jiang Cheng gripped her bat tighter. She had a plan: if a stranger opened the door, she would pretend to have the wrong apartment, acting like she mistook them for the neighbor, to keep herself safe.","If it really was a bad guy, she’d have to wait for the property staff and police to handle it.","Just as she was strategizing, there was a sudden bang against the door, as if something had slammed violently into it, startling her.","Jiang Cheng tightened her hold on the bat, staring at the door. “Hello? Are you okay?”","From inside came frantic pounding, mixed with scraping sounds, like both hitting and clawing.","Then, the doorknob moved.","Not enough to open the door, but it moved again.","Jiang Cheng’s internal alarm blared. Instinctively, she stepped back two paces.","The doorknob moved a third time, and the door creaked open.","Seeing half a face in the gap—it was the neighbor she’d met a few times—Jiang Cheng let out a breath. “What happened, you—”","Her voice cut off abruptly as she took in the neighbor’s eyes: pitch black, with no white visible.","In that instant, the “neighbor” lunged at her!","Jiang Cheng reflexively raised her bat to block, just managing to stop the outstretched arms. But the force of the lunge was shockingly strong, pushing her backward.","The momentum drove her back several rapid steps until bang, her back slammed into the door of the neighbor across the hall.","Quick-thinking, the moment her back hit something solid, she let go of the bat and slid down, slipping out from under the attacker.","The “neighbor,” slower to react, kept charging forward even after losing its target, crashing loudly into the door across the hall.","The bat clattered to the floor.","Jiang Cheng scrambled up and turned to look. The “neighbor” turned its head to stare back at her.","Those eyes had no white—completely black.","Drool dripped from its mouth.","A guttural whimper came from its throat.","Then, with a hoarse roar, it opened its mouth wide, exhaling a foul, stinking breath.","Jiang Cheng ran.","“Help!” she screamed as she fled. “Someone, help!”","Shouting for help when a single woman is in danger is the right thing to do. The last time she encountered a pervert, her cries had summoned many kind neighbors.","But this time, the empty hallway was met with not a single open door.","Only her sharp screams echoed back at her.","Jiang Cheng didn’t realize that she and the neighbor were among the first to wake up.","The tragedy was that she had woken up still human, while her neighbor had become something inhuman.","She now understood what had happened to the dog next door. Though she had only been shoved against the door briefly, she had glimpsed the flesh and fur in the neighbor’s mouth, and the large crimson stain on its T-shirt.","What she couldn’t understand was why.","She remembered that on Wednesday, when she came home, she had run into the neighbor heading out to walk his dog. Everything was normal then. How had he become something so terrifying?","Behind her came the sound of heavy thumping footsteps, along with hoarse roars, chasing her.","Her mind racing, she had already reached the end of the hallway.","Running too fast, she nearly crashed into the fire door leading to the stairwell. Jiang Cheng slammed to a halt, yanked the fire door open, slipped inside, and immediately pulled it shut, holding it tight.","The next second, she heard a loud thwack as the “neighbor,” unable to stop its momentum, slammed into the door.","Jiang Cheng even heard what sounded like bones breaking.","The stairwell fire door opened outward from the other side, unlike the apartment doors, which swung inward.","The neighbor, stretching its arms like a zombie, had been chasing her, and the sound of snapping was likely its wrist or arm hitting the fire door and breaking.","Jiang Cheng bet that in his current state, he wouldn't open that door.","A sound like a body slamming into the door rang out—","Jiang Cheng's bet paid off.","Her neighbor, clearly lacking coordination, couldn't manage the motion of pulling the door open.","But Jiang Cheng didn't linger. A fire door that couldn't lock didn't offer her any safety. She turned and ran downstairs.","She had chosen a lower floor because she thought it would be easier to escape in case of a fire or something similar. What was happening now wasn't a fire, but the \"easy escape\" had certainly proven true.","The first-floor lobby had a security guard on duty 24 hours a day.","Jiang Cheng pushed open the ground-floor fire door, about to call for help, when she immediately spotted the familiar-looking security guard lying motionless on the floor, face down.","Her cry for help caught in her throat. She ran over and turned the guard over. \"Hey? Hey? Are you okay? Wake up? Wake up!\"","The guard's body was still warm, or rather, the heat hadn't yet faded entirely.","But his face was an ashen gray.","Jiang Cheng felt that her neighbor's face earlier had also had that same ashen quality, a kind of dark green.","Everything upstairs had happened so fast. In her brief exchange of looks with the neighbor, her gaze had been caught entirely by his pitch-black, pupil-less eyes and his drooling, bloodied mouth.","Recalling it now, the rest was blurry, but his face had indeed been a dull grayish-black, even more green than the guard's.","Jiang Cheng reached out and felt the guard's nose. Her heart went cold—no breath.","The warmth of his body was indeed just residual heat.","The guard was already dead.","Jiang Cheng clenched her teeth, her breathing rapid and heavy.","Thankfully, she still kept her wits. She grabbed the walkie-talkie on the floor. \"Hey? Anyone there? Anyone? Hey! Hey!\"","But the walkie-talkie, just like the silent stairwell, got no response.","Realizing this, Jiang Cheng didn't hesitate. She dropped the walkie-talkie and stood up, planning to head straight to the property management office.","Because the office had security guards, and a few things that looked like stun batons, and even that big fork with the half-moon-shaped head.","Best-case scenario, she'd find people. Even if she didn't, she could at least find a usable weapon.","Jiang Cheng pushed open the glass door of the building and stepped out.","But there was a huge crash from above, like a thunderclap. Broken glass rained down like a shower, and with a heavy thud, a \"person\" fell from the midair onto the empty ground below the stairs leading to the building entrance.","The \"person\" didn't groan or cry out in pain. Instead, it lifted its head.","Pitch-black eyes.","Still holding the glass door handle, Jiang Cheng froze completely.","The thing that had fallen onto the steps wasn't any \"person\"—it was the neighbor she had just locked out on the stairwell with the fire door.","He had smashed through the glass window at the end of the hallway, and followed her by jumping down from upstairs.","Or maybe not jumping. It was more like a \"fall.\"","His feet were clearly injured from the fall. One ankle was bent at a 90-degree angle, and the other leg was twisted from the knee. When he saw Jiang Cheng on the building steps, he tried to stand up but failed. Then he started crawling upward, clawing at the ground.","His wrists and arms had already been broken upstairs from slamming into the wall without braking.","He crawled in a grotesque, misshapen way.","It was even more horrifying to watch.","Jiang Cheng took a step back and closed the front door of the building. Through the glass, she watched the monster neighbor slowly crawling toward her.","All she could hear was her own labored breathing.","Don't panic, she told herself. You can't panic.","She had already experienced the neighbor's monstrous strength. She knew that even with his damaged wrists and arms, this glass door might not be able to hold him back.","She couldn't just wait to die.","Heaven helps those who help themselves.","Jiang Cheng quickly scanned the first-floor lobby and saw the cleaning supplies the janitor had left in the corner.","She spotted an old-fashioned cloth mop.","The mop handle was a sturdy wooden stick.","Jiang Cheng grabbed the mop and swung it. The heavy, cloth-woven mop head seriously affected her ability to generate force.","She rushed over, pulled open the security guard's desk drawer, found no scissors, but spotted a set of keys inside. She glanced back through the glass door—the monster neighbor was still crawling upward.","While twisting her head to keep watch, she used the jagged edges of the keys to cut the rope holding the mop head.","Thank the property management's stinginess for never buying the janitors new mops. This one was already old and tattered, and the binding rope was already heavily worn.","After a few cuts, Jiang Cheng severed the rope, removed the mop head, and was left with a smooth, bare wooden stick.","She turned her head to look again. The neighbor's head and shoulders had already crawled past the highest step. His broken arms flailed against the glass door.","Jiang Cheng gripped the wooden stick tightly, took a deep breath, and suddenly pushed open the glass door, charging out. Mimicking what she'd seen in TV shows, she raised the stick high and slammed it down viciously onto the monster's skull.","The sound of a skull cracking was not pleasant to hear.","It even set her teeth on edge.","But those pitch-black eyes made Jiang Cheng starkly aware that the person in front of her was no longer a \"person,\" but a monster mutated by some unknown cause.","Suppressing all her discomfort, she clenched her teeth and struck a second time!","Attacking the head was effective!","The monster's movements clearly stalled.","Jiang Cheng gritted her teeth and brought the stick down again and again, until the monster's head was cracked open, and disgusting liquid and bits of solid debris splashed onto the steps.","She had killed someone.","So what.","When facing a monster, you have to protect yourself first.","When the police came, she would say exactly that.","The muscles in her arms were cramping slightly from the burst of strength.","Jiang Cheng stood there, panting, holding the stick smeared with disgusting fluid.","She thought she'd at least get half a minute to rest and feel safe, but then a sharp, piercing screech came from the bottom of the steps.","Jiang Cheng immediately shifted into a defensive posture and looked down.","This time, it wasn't a human, but a very familiar black cat.","Its eyes were an eerie, glowing green in the darkness.","Its fur was bristled, and it let out a piercing scream at her, as if it were a challenge or a declaration of war.","Jiang Cheng breathed heavily, gripping the stick tightly, and aimed it at the cat at the foot of the stairs. \"...Mo Li?\"","Even the cat had turned into a monster?","Jiang Cheng clenched her jaw.","Mo Li let out a harsh cry, turned into a black streak, and with incredible speed and leaping ability, lunged straight at her!","Jiang Cheng felt her heart tighten, as if an electric current had passed through her, a wave of danger—or maybe murderous intent—washing over her.","She gritted her teeth, swung the stick, and struck hard—"]},{"number":5,"title":"Chapter 5","paragraphs":["Cats are the upper limit of what felines can reach in size when kept as pets by humans.","Among animals of the same size, cats rank high in combat ability.","A human simply cannot match a cat's speed.","Jiang Cheng swung a stick, feeling her hand sink as something flashed before her eyes.","Mo Li stepped on the stick for leverage, then shot past her face like lightning toward something behind her.","A thud, crash, and a guttural roar came from behind.","Jiang Cheng turned in horror.","Pinned to the ground by Mo Li was a security guard who had somehow come out of the building and was standing right behind her!","She had rushed out and left the glass door open—the door was wide open.","But hadn't the security guard just been dead?","Jiang Cheng suddenly understood. The killing intent she had sensed from Mo Li earlier wasn't aimed at her.","That little black cat had been trying to save her!","The security guard let out a hoarse, rasping roar just like the mutated neighbor, rolled over, and sat up on his knees. He grabbed the black cat with both hands and bit down!","The composure Jiang Cheng had maintained since first seeing the mutated neighbor finally cracked. She screamed, \"No—!\"","The security guard turned his head toward her. His eyes were pitch black, and his skin had an eerie, bluish-gray pallor.","Bits of Mo Li's fur, skin, and flesh dripped from his mouth.","Jiang Cheng felt a chill run through her entire body.","This wasn't an isolated case of mutation.","Her mind flashed back to the hallway where no one had responded to her cries for help, the unanswered calls to the police and property management, the silent road.","And she herself had just woken from a feverish, semi-conscious sleep.","A terrible realization dawned on her. Something horrifying was happening, and people hadn't fully awakened yet.","But what was waking up wasn't always human anymore.","She had just killed one monster, and another new one had already been born in its place.","Even though both creatures were still warm-blooded beings, Jiang Cheng was a living, breathing human radiating the sweet scent of flesh and blood. That made that little black cat far less appealing to the security guard than she was.","The guard flung Mo Li aside and tried to stand up.","These thoughts raced through Jiang Cheng's mind in just a few seconds.","The guard had fallen, grabbed Mo Li, bitten her, thrown her away, and was now trying to stand—all within those few seconds.","From the building's glass door to the first step of the stoop was only five or six paces. With a long enough arm, someone could lean forward and reach all the way to Jiang Cheng.","So Jiang Cheng truly had no time to hesitate. The moment she realized Mo Li wasn't attacking her but saving her, the moment she saw the guard had turned into a monster, she swung the stick without a second thought—like swinging a bat—aiming straight for his head!","But she miscalculated.","The neighbor had only been killed because his limbs and bones were already broken from his fall. The security guard was physically whole.","The guard snatched the stick with his teeth as it came at him, grabbed it with both hands, and yanked. Jiang Cheng felt an immense force drag her forward. She was standing at the edge of the steps, and the ground was slippery with the neighbor's brains. The stick was torn from her grip, she stumbled backward, missed her footing, and tumbled from the steps down to the ground.","Luckily, the stoop had only six steps and wasn't steep. The fall hurt, but she wasn't incapacitated.","Gritting her teeth against the pain, Jiang Cheng scrambled over. When she looked up, the guard was still holding the mop handle in his mouth.","His teeth had actually embedded themselves into the wood. With a hard yank, he pulled the stick out of his mouth, dragging out several teeth along with it. He tossed it away, and the stick spun through the air with a whistling sound before landing somewhere in the distance.","The guard's pitch-black eyes were fixed on Jiang Cheng from the top of the steps as he stepped forward twice.","After mutation, these monsters gained tremendous strength, but their bodies were no longer very agile. The neighbor had broken his own wrist and arm because he charged too fast and couldn't stop in time.","The guard tried to walk down the stairs but lost his balance and pitched forward, tumbling down the steps.","Jiang Cheng was already on her feet, sprinting for her life. Without a weapon, she—a defenseless girl—stood no chance against a mutated monster bare-handed.","She ran toward where the stick had landed. The moment she picked it up, calm and courage flowed back into her.","She turned around. The guard was staggering toward her, his gait as unsteady as the neighbor's.","Jiang Cheng gripped the stick and stood her ground, muscles tensed.","The moment the guard lunged at her, she dodged nimbly to the side and swung the stick hard, landing a vicious blow to the back of his head!","The guard crashed to the ground. Jiang Cheng stepped forward and hammered him again and again on the back of his head!","Even then, the guard tried to push himself up from the ground, completely unlike a normal human, who would have been stunned after a single blow to the skull.","Luckily, there was nothing funny about \"emergency strength.\"","With a few more whacks, each blow knocked the guard back down as he tried to rise.","After several hits, his skull finally cracked. As his hand grabbed Jiang Cheng's ankle, she gripped the stick in both hands, cocked it upright, and drove it into his skull. She twisted!","At last, the monster listlessly fell to the ground as a lifeless corpse.","Jiang Cheng pressed her foot on the guard's head and yanked the stick out.","His dead hand was still clenching her ankle like a vise. She had to crouch down and struggle for a moment to pry his fingers loose before pulling free.","At this point, she abandoned any thought of going to the property management office.","She now realized that a terrifying wave of mutation had spread over an alarming area. Her neighbors, the property staff, maybe even the entire city, had been affected. Mutated monsters could be anywhere, including the management building.","Nowhere outside was safe.","She decided to go back. In this situation, her best bet for safety was to lock herself inside her own apartment.","And there was Mo Li. She had to go back and check on the little black cat.","That little black cat had saved her life.","If Mo Li hadn't lunged at the guard, he would have been standing just a few paces behind her without a sound, and all he would have needed to do was pounce and bite her to death.","Please, little black cat. Don't be dead!","But just then, she heard a girl's scream. \"Help! Somebody, please help! Aaaaaaah!\"","Jiang Cheng stopped mid-stride back toward the building.","She couldn't ignore a girl's cry for help. The youth apartment complex had more male residents than females, but the building was marketed as a community for young people. Most of the tenants were around her age.","Jiang Cheng sprinted toward the sound, heading into the complex garden.","Under the streetlamp light, she saw a man pinning a girl to the ground. At first glance, it seemed like an assault.","But it wasn't.","He was tearing into her with his teeth!","A mutated monster!","Jiang Cheng cracked her stick across him, knocking him off the girl. Without even checking the mauled victim, she swung the stick again and again at the man's skull until she heard the crunch of his head cracking.","That sound was like music to her ears.","It meant she had put down another monster.","A few more whacks, and as the skull splintered and brains spilled everywhere, the monster finally stopped moving.","But Jiang Cheng couldn't afford to relax. Just because it was dead now didn't mean it might not come back. In horror movies, some monsters kept reviving and couldn't be killed.","She mustered every ounce of her strength for one last, brutal blow.","CRACK—the stick snapped in two. The broken piece flew back, nearly hitting her.","The mop handle wasn't made from good wood, but it wasn't thin either. In the past, Jiang Cheng would never have believed she had the strength to snap a mop handle like that.","Come to think of it, a human skull shouldn't crack so easily either.","Was her strength greater now, or had the bones of those turned into monsters become brittle?","There was no time to dwell on that. She dropped the broken stick and rushed to check on the girl on the ground.","The girl's shoulder was torn and bloody, chewed raw. She trembled with pain and terror, gasping between sobs.","\"Can you get up?\" Jiang Cheng tried to haul her to her feet.","But the girl couldn't seem to move. She gasped frantically and begged: \"Call an ambulance! An ambulance! Save me!\"","Yet the surroundings remained eerily quiet. No sound of cars on the road.","It meant Jiang Cheng, the three mutated monsters, and this injured girl were among the earliest to wake. Most people were still unconscious.","The world was still silent, brewing.","No one knew whether the next person to open their eyes would be human or monster. The longer she stayed outside, the greater the danger.","She let go of the girl.","The girl screamed: \"Don't go! Don't leave me! Help me!\"","Driven by the terror of abandonment, the girl somehow forced herself upright into a sitting position.","But Jiang Cheng wasn't abandoning her. She walked over to the monster she'd just killed and crouched down to strip the clothes from its corpse.","The man had been wearing a shirt. Jiang Cheng yanked it open, popping the buttons off, then pulled it free from the body. She folded it into a long strip, went back to the girl, and crouched: \"Lift your arm.\"","Seeing the girl crying, tears and snot streaming, Jiang Cheng simply took her arm, threaded the shirt under her armpit, and tied it tightly around the wound to stop the bleeding.","The shoulder was mangled from bites. Jiang Cheng knew it would hurt, but the girl wouldn't die immediately. Stopping the bleeding was urgent—she was losing too much blood.","The girl flinched in panic, also from pain and fear: \"What are you doing! No! What about infection! Call me an ambulance! Please, call an ambulance!\"","\"Shut up and listen!\" Jiang Cheng cut off her cries. \"I don't know what's happening, but everyone's passed out. I tried calling the police and the property management—no one answered. Everyone must be unconscious. Listen—there's not even a single car on the road.\"","\"You and I woke up early. But not everyone who wakes up is still human. Some turn into these monsters.\"","Black eyes, grayish-blue skin, immense strength.","But poor balance—as if they hadn't mastered their new bodies yet.","\"This is the third monster I've killed!\"","\"There are still many people unconscious. We don't know if they'll turn into monsters when they wake!\"","\"Right now, we have to get back inside a building immediately. Out here, anything could happen—someone might wake up and mutate. We need to get inside right now!\"","The girl was stunned into silence.","Yes, she had seen it with her own eyes—the person who had attacked her like a wild beast really did have altered eyes and skin.","And she herself had just woken up after collapsing in the garden at night.","Everything Jiang Cheng said was true.","\"Then... then...\" the girl stammered.","Jiang Cheng finished tying the knot, stopping the bleeding: \"I'm heading back. You need to get up and go home yourself. Be careful.\"","The girl grabbed her sleeve: \"I can't get up... help me, please.\"","She wasn't faking it. The pain was excruciating. Where she'd been lying, there were shreds of flesh from the monster's savage biting—it was horrible to look at. Terrifying and revolting.","Her shoulder bone was exposed, and the blood loss made her dizzy.","Jiang Cheng put the girl's uninjured arm over her shoulder and pulled her upright.","But the girl, weak from injury and fear, trembled and could barely stand. She begged: \"Can you walk me back?\"","Jiang Cheng asked: \"Which building are you in?\"","The girl told her the building number.","But it wasn't the same one as Jiang Cheng's, and the garden lay between them. Right now, the garden felt like a nest of unknown monsters—any shadow could hide a creature ready to attack.","Jiang Cheng thought for a second and made a decision: \"Come with me. To my place.\"","She lifted the girl's other arm, ducked under it, and propped the girl's weight on her shoulders as they headed toward her building: \"Going to yours and coming back is too dangerous. First, come to mine. Forget everything else—we both need to get inside right now.\"","The girl understood the urgency: \"Okay. Let's go to yours!\"","But even with Jiang Cheng supporting her, every step jostled the wound, making her hiss with pain, her body shaking and legs buckling.","Jiang Cheng dragged her toward her own building.","There, a little black cat lay, alive or dead unknown.","Please don't die!"]},{"number":6,"title":"Chapter 6","paragraphs":["My name is Jiang Cheng.","Hiss—my name is Shen Wei.","Do you live alone?","I live with my boyfriend. Oh, I hiss—I forgot my bag. Hiss—","Don't worry about it, talk about it when we're safe.","Okay.","Jiang Cheng felt that Shen Wei was surprisingly light, much lighter than she had estimated based on her height and build. This was abnormal.","Jiang Cheng had basically confirmed that her strength had really increased compared to before she passed out.","But it seemed like she hadn't increased as much as the monsters had. Luckily, the monsters weren't very agile. If a monster could control its limbs and balance like a normal person, she would have been dead long ago.","Ah! Shen Wei gasped quietly.","She saw the security guard's body.","Did you kill him? Her voice trembled. Did the security guard turn into a monster too?","Turning into a monster doesn't discriminate by identity or profession, Jiang Cheng said.","Shen Wei fell silent.","As they walked further, they arrived in front of the building and saw the body of a neighbor.","Not only was the neighbor's head shattered, but his arms and legs were also broken and twisted out of shape. His death was even more gruesome than the security guard's or the male homeowner's in the garden.","Shen Wei felt both nauseous and terrified. She took one look and dared not look again.","Jiang Cheng said, \"It's a good thing you didn't go back. There were other people in your house, and you can't be sure they won't mutate. This is my next-door neighbor. He should have been the earliest to wake up in the whole complex. He probably bit his dog to death. The dog’s barking woke me up. Sit here for a moment.\"","She set Shen Wei down on the raised platform beside the steps, then quickly climbed the stairs herself.","Under the porch, the black cat lay still, a large pool of blood beneath it.","The cat had been bitten in the belly by the security guard, who had ripped off a chunk of fur and flesh.","Jiang Cheng started crying.","She had come to this city just to get away from her greedy relatives who wanted to inherit everything, and also because it was easier to find a job in a big city.","But she had never really fit in; all her relationships were superficial.","She had actually always been lonely.","Although she couldn't tell if this feeling of \"loneliness\" truly belonged to her or to the original \"Jiang Cheng\" whose body she had taken over, whenever she thought about it, a sour ache gripped her heart.","Just yesterday, she had finally ceased to be lonely. She had gained a companion—Mo Li.","The somewhat aloof little black cat didn't seem to want to be kept as a pet. He had run away, but he had rushed back at the critical moment and bravely sacrificed himself to save her life.","In the little cat's heart, she must have been special.","He must have accepted her as a companion.","He must have been lonely too.","Jiang Cheng's tears fell, splashing onto Mo Li's wound. Suddenly, the cat twitched.","Not dead yet! Still alive!","Jiang Cheng wiped away her tears in one swift motion, gently probing with her finger. Sure enough, the heart was still beating—much faster than a human’s, thump-thump-thump.","Jiang Cheng looked back at the steps where Shen Wei was watching her intently.","Shen Wei was trembling with pain. For a young girl to endure such agony without crying out was pretty impressive. If she had to walk on her own, she could, but she would be slower than an old man or woman.","After thinking for a moment, Jiang Cheng carefully cradled Mo Li, lifted the hem of her T-shirt, and wrapped it around the cat. She pinched the left, right, and middle parts of the T-shirt hem together and bit down on them firmly with her mouth.","Her entire belly and waist were exposed, even her underwear was showing, but Mo Li was secured in front of her chest using the shirt, leaving her hands free.","She walked down the steps, then propped up Shen Wei's arm. \"Goh!\" (Go!)","With Jiang Cheng's help, Shen Wei endured the agonizing pain and climbed the steps. The two of them entered the building.","Jiang Cheng looked back and kicked the building door shut with her foot. It was just a useless glass door, but she felt that without the lure of living human flesh and blood, the monsters wouldn’t actively try to break things.","The neighbor had chased her out of his apartment, then chased her again, breaking the stairwell window and jumping down—his target had been her, a living person.","The man in the garden had also gone after Shen Wei’s flesh and blood.","Without a living person to lure them, closing the door might prevent the monster in the garden from coming in.","Shen Wei seemed on the verge of passing out from the pain.","She was really holding up well. After the initial fear and panic, she could at least cooperate without crying or making a fuss.","But having her take the stairs was out of the question. Jiang Cheng chose the elevator.","One elevator was already waiting on the first floor. She pressed the button, and it opened immediately. Jiang Cheng deliberately kept her distance from the elevator doors to make sure nothing was inside.","Luckily, the elevator was empty. The eerie white light shone on the brushed metal walls, making it look like a scene from a ghost movie.","One benefit of living on a low floor was that it took only a few seconds to arrive.","When the elevator doors opened, Shen Wei felt that Jiang Cheng's whole body was tense. Even with her dizziness, she could feel Jiang Cheng's tension.","Fortunately, there were no other monsters in the hallway.","Jiang Cheng helped Shen Wei towards her own apartment.","As they passed one of the doors, they heard a voice from inside: \"Ziqing! Ziqing, what are you doing? It's me! Ziqing, you're crazy! Let go of me! Li Ziqing! Ah—\"","\"Ahhh—!\" A man's voice turned shrill. \"Help! Help! Ahhhhhh—!\"","Startled, Shen Wei opened her eyes and glanced at Jiang Cheng.","Jiang Cheng's steps faltered for a moment, but she clenched the shirt hem in her teeth and continued forward without stopping, still supporting Shen Wei.","Shen Wei bit her lip and hung her head.","Both of them knew what was happening in that room—two people in a small apartment had woken up. One was still human, the other had turned into a monster.","In such a tiny apartment, with the other person being someone close to her, she probably hadn't been able to react in time to grab a weapon and defend herself. She wasn't as lucky as Shen Wei, who had Jiang Cheng to rescue her.","Monsters were very strong. Once they pinned you down and started biting, it was basically...","But Jiang Cheng and Shen Wei weren't superheroes. They were just two ordinary girls. Their top priority was to save themselves first.","Now there was an injured person and an injured cat.","One was dying, the other on the verge of passing out.","Jiang Cheng spotted a baseball bat lying on the ground in front of the door opposite the neighbor's apartment. It was a good weapon—perfect for dealing with monsters whose heads were brittle and bodies uncoordinated.","Jiang Cheng hooked it with her foot, kicked it once, and sent her baseball bat back to her own doorstep.","Her apartment door was still wide open. She had left it ajar earlier when she went out to check on the neighbor.","Next door, the neighbor's apartment door was also open. Sneaking a glance in the dim hallway light, she vaguely saw blood on the floor and the remains of the dog.","Jiang Cheng pushed her own door wide open with her foot. The small apartment was visible at a single glance; it was safe.","She kicked the baseball bat inside, then helped Shen Wei in, and closed the door behind them.","The lock clicked into place with a snap, signaling that Jiang Cheng had finally returned to a temporarily safe space.","Using her last bit of strength, Jiang Cheng helped Shen Wei to the bed and laid her down.","Shen Wei couldn't hold on any longer. She opened her eyes to look at Jiang Cheng once, then closed them.","The white shirt tied around the wound was completely soaked red. Jiang Cheng hadn't used very professional techniques; she had been in a hurry, and Shen Wei's wound was large. Plus, with all the walking, the shirt couldn't fully cover the injury, and the exposed parts kept bleeding.","With her hands finally free, Jiang Cheng quickly released her mouth and gently placed Mo Li, who was still wrapped in her shirt, onto the bed.","She couldn’t let her guard down yet. Gritting her teeth, she quickly grabbed the family first-aid kit. The kit was small, containing only some basic medicine.","rummaging through it, she pulled out a bottle of iodophor, unscrewed the cap, and poured some directly over the wound on Mo Li’s belly.","It must have hurt badly—all four of Mo Li’s limbs twitched.","Then she used scissors to cut open the white shirt Shen Wei had tied around herself. The wound was too large, so Jiang Cheng poured the rest of the iodophor into the gash on Shen Wei’s shoulder.","Shen Wei had already closed her eyes, unconscious from the pain, but the sudden sting jolted her awake. She couldn’t even scream, only letting out a hissing breath.","Jiang Cheng pulled out gauze pads and bandages, wrapping them around Mo Li’s belly a few times before tying them off.","There wasn’t enough bandage left for Shen Wei. She pressed a few gauze pads onto the wound to stop the bleeding, wrapped what bandage remained around it, then went to the wardrobe to grab a T-shirt. Cutting it open, she finally bound Shen Wei’s wound tightly.","Shen Wei passed out from the pain again. Better that way—less suffering.","Both the woman and the cat were bandaged now. The supplies were limited, and her methods were crude, but Jiang Cheng had done everything she could.","Finally, drained of energy, she collapsed onto the floor by the bed, leaning her back against the bed frame and letting her head fall back onto the mattress.","As the adrenaline faded, an indescribable weakness spread through her body.","She lay there, face upturned and eyes closed, taking several deep breaths before she felt a little better.","Then she opened her eyes again—the noise was gone. The man who had been shouting “Li Ziqing” in the hallway had stopped.","Having seen those neighbors on the same floor a few times, Jiang Cheng could roughly guess which couple it was. Like Shen Wei, they were cohabiting lovers.","Living alone as a single woman was often considered unsafe.","But today, those living alone were the lucky ones. Because you could never guarantee the person beside you would still be human when they woke up.","Most people couldn’t assess the situation in time, nor could they steel themselves to strike down someone they were close to. In a cramped apartment, once you lost the initiative, your chances of survival dropped sharply.","Jiang Cheng closed her eyes again.","But just as she was about to rest for a moment, voices echoed from the hallway once more—","“What’s going on?” came a loud banging on a door, followed by, sounding close, banging on Li Ziqing’s door. “You okay? What’s happening in there? Is this some kind of game, or is something wrong? Say something if it’s just messing around.”","Jiang Cheng opened her eyes again. With no choice but to catch her breath, she stood up and walked toward the door.","First, she checked through the peephole. Confirming nothing looked amiss, she cracked the door open and peeked out.","The man banging on Li Ziqing’s door was also familiar to Jiang Cheng. He was a male neighbor on their floor. She didn’t know the neighbors’ names, but she’d given them nicknames in her head.","For example, Li Ziqing and her partner were always all over each other in the hallway and elevator, so Jiang Cheng had mentally dubbed them the “Lovebirds.”","The man now knocking was large—clearly a fitness enthusiast, with broad shoulders, huge pectorals and biceps, and his neck had thickened noticeably.","Jiang Cheng called him “Big Guy” in her head.","Big Guy had once tried to flirt with her, but she wasn’t into that exaggerated, bulging muscular type and hadn’t responded.","He hadn’t pushed it. Occasionally, they’d nod at each other when crossing paths.","“Go back!” she shouted. “Go back! Back inside your room! Someone’s turned into a monster—it bites! Get back inside!”","But without seeing a supernatural phenomenon firsthand, who would easily believe someone claiming there were monsters? Big Guy looked baffled. “Huh? What the hell? No, what are you talking about?”","Jiang Cheng was about to shout again when the door next to Li Ziqing’s abruptly made a loud bang.","Then another bang.","Just like earlier with her next-door neighbor.","Jiang Cheng’s pupils contracted sharply."]},{"number":7,"title":"Chapter 7","paragraphs":["The Big Guy was startled by the sound of the door being banged on, muttering as he walked over, \"What now over here?\"","One apartment had screams, another had a door being pounded on. What was wrong with all his neighbors on this floor?","Jiang Cheng immediately yelled to stop him, \"Don't go over there! Go back to your own place! Now!\"","The Big Guy looked at her, \"Huh?\"","The mutated monster in this apartment got to the door handle even earlier than Jiang Cheng's neighbor had. The force and angle happened to be just right—unlike Jiang Cheng's neighbor, who fumbled a few times before pressing the handle down, this monster succeeded on the first try.","The door creaked open.","The Big Guy was standing right outside the door.","The monster stood inside.","A pair of normal eyes met a pair of pitch-black eyes.","Saliva dripped.","The Big Guy was speechless.","\"Run—!\" Jiang Cheng shouted.","The monster opened its mouth, letting out a hoarse roar from its throat, and lunged out with its hands outstretched.","The Big Guy let out a yelp, spun around, and bolted, \"Help! There's a ghost!\"","The Big Guy might have muscles bulging everywhere, with broad, thick shoulders and arms so developed they couldn't lie flat against his sides, looking like a hulking brute. But he had a timid heart.","He wasn't afraid of the living, but spirits scared him.","What kind of monster was this? He was about to pee his pants!","Mom!","The baseball bat was right by the door, and Jiang Cheng grabbed it as she sprinted out.","The Big Guy's position was quite far from her, near the other end of the hallway, close to the dead end. He didn't run many steps before hitting the wall.","Turning his head, he saw the monster with black eyes and drooling, slobbering—it was actually a neighbor he usually recognized. But now, the neighbor was radiating a kind of deathly aura.","The hands spread out like claws, coming at him.","The Big Guy's soul nearly fled his body as he dropped to a crouch instinctively, just like Jiang Cheng when she first encountered her neighbor monster. It was a reflex of evasion.","This neighbor monster also hit the wall. But since they were so close to the end of the hallway and hadn't built up much speed in those few steps, this neighbor didn't crash into the fire door with enough force to break an arm like Jiang Cheng's next-door neighbor had.","The monster's outstretched hand touched the wall, stopping its momentum, and it turned its head.","The Big Guy dodged that strike, scrambled on all fours for a few steps, got up, and also turned to look.","Their eyes met again.","The monster roared.","The Big Guy sprinted toward Jiang Cheng's direction, \"Ahhh run! Why are you coming over here?!\"","Jiang Cheng charged forward, yelling, \"Move—!\"","She gripped the bat tightly.","The Big Guy sidestepped nimbly, clearing the space, revealing the monster chasing him behind.","Jiang Cheng, using the momentum of her run, swung the bat in a full arc!","The Big Guy twisted to look behind him and saw it happen—","Teeth, slime, and blood burst forth.","The monster's body flew backward through the air.","The silhouette of the girl gripping the bat looked more powerful than any man pumping iron at the gym.","Everything seemed like a slow-motion scene in a movie, as if the world had frozen for an instant.","Then, with a thud, the monster crashed down, landing on its back.","In one fluid motion, Jiang Cheng stopped, turned around, and before the monster could get up, she viciously struck it again and again with the bat.","She could hear banging coming from Li Ziqing's door. She had to finish this quickly—if Li Ziqing also came out, she'd have to deal with two monsters at once.","The bat was thicker at the top and thinner and lighter near the bottom, making it great for swinging with force. It was way better than a mop handle.","Jiang Cheng's strength had indeed increased since she fainted. With a proper weapon in hand, she smashed the monster's head to pieces in a few blows.","The walls on either side of the hallway were splattered with red, white, and sticky stuff.","The Big Guy clenched his glutes, pressing himself flat against the hallway wall, staring in horror as a slender female neighbor beat a normally familiar neighbor to death with a string of strikes.","Jiang Cheng paused, resting the bat on the ground to catch her breath. She straightened up and nodded toward the Big Guy's apartment, \"Go back inside and lock the door!\"","The Big Guy stammered, \"He! You! Me!\"","The banging on Li Ziqing's door continued.","\"Don't touch that door, go back. She's about to come out,\" Jiang Cheng strode past him. \"There might be others turning into monsters too. Head back now and talk on the owners' forum!\"","The Big Guy was glued to the wall like a gecko, watching Jiang Cheng as she dashed back toward her place, then looking at the neighbor's corpse lying horribly on the ground.","He glanced at Jiang Cheng again.","She was already jogging back to her own door, stepping inside, and slamming it shut behind her with a bang.","Meanwhile, the neighbor directly opposite from the Big Guy had just woken up. Still groggy, he heard shouts in the hallway.","A man screamed \"ghost,\" a woman yelled \"go back,\" then more shouting: \"Help!\" and \"Move!\"","Then came a bunch of messy noises.","This neighbor rubbed his temples, recovering his senses enough to get up and open the door to check. \"What's all the racket? What's going on?\"","He looked up and locked eyes with the Big Guy still plastered against the wall opposite.","The Big Guy glanced at this neighbor with normal eyes, then at the monster's corpse on the ground.","The neighbor followed his gaze and saw the body and the gruesome scene.","The two normal—or alive—people stared at each other in silence.","The Big Guy wanted to say, \"It wasn't me,\" but he opened his mouth, unsure how to explain.","The neighbor stared at this muscular man for one second... then yanked his door shut with force, frantically locking it.","The Big Guy jolted, then sprinted and leaped over the corpse, shouting, \"Check the owners' forum!\"","After yelling, he scrambled into his own apartment and slammed the door shut too.","The banging from Li Ziqing's door continued to echo.","But fortunately, Li Ziqing wasn't lucky enough to hit the door handle and open it. She thumped and scratched inside, but after the Big Guy escaped into his place, the hallway fell silent, and Li Ziqing gradually quieted down, no longer making noise.","Back inside her house, Jiang Cheng set the bat upright by the door, ready to grab on her way out.","Shen Wei and Mo Li were lying on the bed. Across from the foot of the bed, against the wall, was Jiang Cheng's dressing table that also served as a computer desk. Jiang Cheng pulled out the chair, sat down, opened her laptop, logged into the owners' forum, started a new thread, and typed rapidly:","[!!!! Attention! Those Who Just Woke Up! Some People Turn Into Monsters When They Wake Up!!!!]","She used several exclamation marks in the title to grab attention.","In the body, she wrote: [Attention everyone! Some people wake up with black eyes and blue-gray skin! Those who mutate into this state completely lose their reason and attack anyone or anything like wild animals, using their teeth to tear flesh! Everyone must stay alert and find a nearby weapon to defend yourself! The head is the weakness of the mutated ones—attack their heads until they lose their ability to move!]","What \"lose their ability to move\" really meant was to beat them until they were dead.","But Jiang Cheng couldn't write it that directly.","Back in the safety of her house, she realized she had already killed four people today.","Of course, these four people were twisted monsters—she was just defending herself. But what happens next is still unknown. They definitely wouldn’t write something as blatant as “kill” directly. Still, it doesn’t matter. When people attack in self-defense out of fear, they don’t stop so easily. Once you’re face-to-face with a monster, it’s kill or be killed.","All she had to do was tell everyone the monsters’ weaknesses.","[Variants have poor coordination in their limbs. You can outrun them by sprinting and making sharp turns. You can also attack their knees, ankles, or other lower body parts to make them fall, then go for the head.]","[Both the police hotline and property management phone lines are unanswered. The affected area might be huge. It’s not safe outside right now. Someone was passed out in the garden, and who knows if they’ll still be human when they wake up. I suggest everyone stay indoors and observe for now.]","After posting, Jiang Cheng refreshed the forum page and saw two new threads.","Thread One: [Are you there?! It’s me, it’s me! I’m 0320! Contact me!!! Please!]","Thread Two: [There’s a murder!! Someone’s been killed on the third floor of Building 2!!!]","0320 was the Big Guy. Jiang Cheng clicked on his thread.","Big Guy: [My phone number is xxxxxxxx. Call me! Please!]","Jiang Cheng picked up her phone and dialed the number. “Hello?”","Big Guy’s voice trembled. “Is that you? The one from 0306?”","“It’s me.” Jiang Cheng moved the mouse and opened the second thread. “Check out my latest post.”","“I’m reading it! Is this real?”","The big man sounded like he was about to cry. Jiang Cheng felt helpless. “Didn’t you see it with your own eyes just now?”","Big Guy muttered, “How did this happen?”","“How would I know?” Jiang Cheng told him. “My neighbor in 0308 turned into a mutated monster too. He bit his dog to death and chased me downstairs. The security guard downstairs was the same, and I ran into another mutant in the garden.”","“0308?!” Big Guy’s voice shot up. “Are you talking about Little White and Little White’s Dad?”","The dog next door was indeed covered in white fur. Jiang Cheng had heard other dog-owning neighbors call out to it: “Little White.”","She confirmed, “Yes.”","Big Guy asked, “What about Little White’s Dad?”","Jiang Cheng stayed silent and didn’t answer.","Hearing the silence on the phone, Big Guy understood.","He wanted to cry. “Am I dreaming? Maybe I should just go back to sleep.”","Jiang Cheng understood exactly how he felt. Since she woke up barely forty minutes ago, she’d had a strong sense of unreality too.","But she said softly, “This isn’t a dream. It’s real. Some people are turning into monsters, and plenty of others haven’t even woken up yet. We have no idea how many people are going to turn. That man from 0317 was probably bitten dead by his girlfriend. If that girl can get the door open, she’ll run out too.”","Heavy breathing came through the phone.","Fortunately, the man on the other end was an adult after all. Big Guy pulled himself together, sniffled, and asked, “So what about the security guard and the one in the garden? You...?”","Jiang Cheng hummed in acknowledgment.","“Badass! I never would’ve guessed it in normal times.” Big Guy admired her with genuine respect. He’d seen Jiang Cheng plenty of times before— she was quite pretty and seemed harmless. Who would’ve thought she’d go on the offensive in a crisis?","“My name is Li Jiangbing,” he said. “What’s yours?”","“Jiang Cheng.”","“Jiang Cheng, what do we do now?”","Why was he asking her? Jiang Cheng wasn’t responsible for him.","“Right now, a lot of people haven’t woken up or just have. I’m choosing to stay indoors and observe for now.”","“Alright, alright! I’ll stay inside too. Let’s wait until daylight tomorrow at least.”","“Yeah. Find yourself a weapon.”","“Got it. I’ve got a ton of stuff here. I have nunchucks, a tactical baton, a collapsible baton. Want me to give you one?”","“No need for now,” Jiang Cheng said. “I have a baseball bat. It works well.”","Big Guy said, “Okay, let’s leave it at that for now. Hang up first. Keep in touch.”","Jiang Cheng replied, “Got it. Keep an eye on the forum.”","After hanging up, Jiang Cheng heard screams from the hallway again: “Hey—someone come! There’s a dead body!”","She heard Li Jiangbing open his door and shout, “Get back inside! Lock your door! Check the owner’s forum!”","Though Li Jiangbing crumbled under pressure in a crisis, in normal times, that big frame of his was intimidating. Right after, two doors slammed in succession—he’d actually yelled that neighbor back inside.","But Jiang Cheng knew that more and more people were gradually waking up.","Some would open their eyes and still be human.","Others would open their eyes and no longer be human."]},{"number":8,"title":"Chapter 8","paragraphs":["The second post Jiang Cheng opened was made by the neighbor who had exchanged a glance with Li Jiangbing when the door opened earlier. That neighbor had gone home and posted it.","Both he and Li Jiangbing had posted quickly with fewer words, so they got done before Jiang Cheng.","There wasn’t much content—just screams that she had seen a neighbor kill someone, and that it was probably that big-bodied gym guy on the same floor. No one answered when she called the police, and the property management office’s phone went unanswered too.","Below, Li Jiangbing had already replied: 【It wasn’t me!!!!!!!! Go check the post from 0306! The one with lots of exclamation marks! I’ve pinned it to the top! It’s at the very top!】","Not bad—it felt like Li Jiangbing, that guy, had already moved past his initial panic and fear.","Only then did Jiang Cheng realize she hadn’t even taken a sip of water since earlier. Her throat was dry and sore, probably from yelling too hard at Li Jiangbing.","She went to get a glass of water, sat down on the sofa, and gulped it down.","Turning to glance at the bed, she saw both the person and the cat still unconscious.","She tried calling the police again, even dialed for an ambulance, but regretfully, no one answered. So now, no one could help the person or the cat—they’d have to tough it out with just the medicine she’d applied.","Just then, her stomach rumbled. It wasn’t just thirst that hit her as she relaxed; hunger came too.","Jiang Cheng made a bowl of instant noodles and ate the leftover braised meat from yesterday’s fridge.","While she ate, the silence around her began to break.","Out on the street, there were sounds of car wheels and horns, all chaotic.","Someone in the community garden was screaming—more than one person—their voices echoing in the night. From various apartment buildings came shouts, screams, even cries of pain.","In the hallway outside her door, there were noises too—doors opening, startled cries, then panicked slamming shut.","The neighbors were gradually waking up.","Whenever someone yelled, “Someone’s dead, call the police!” Li Jiangbing would open his door and bellow back, “Get back inside! Lock your door! Check the top post on the owners’ forum!”","His build was intimidating, and his voice was loud. Every neighbor he shouted at ended up backing off.","But the noise in the hallway startled Li Ziqing again. This time, Li Ziqing finally found the door handle, and after a few tries, opened the door and stepped out.","Li Jiangbing was still leaning out his door and saw it. He shouted, “Holy shit,” then yanked himself back inside and slammed the door shut.","But by then, Li Jiangbing had gotten past his initial terror of seeing a ghost. He’d also learned from Jiang Cheng’s post that the mutated monsters had a weak point in the head, and he’d watched how Jiang Cheng had taken one down herself.","Now he was itching for a fight.","He looked through his various weapons at home, passed on the nunchucks and the telescopic baton, and finally grabbed his pair of all-steel tonfa sticks.","Taking a few deep breaths, he peeked through the peephole—to see Li Ziqing, having lost her target, drifting like a ghost slowly through the hallway.","Perfect.","Li Jiangbing gave himself a mental pep talk, then yanked the door open and charged out with a roar.","His muscles weren’t built for nothing, and the weapon felt good in his hands.","He dispatched Li Ziqing quickly.","When he charged out and started fighting, he was brave and full of spirit. But once he’d smashed in the skull of that neighbor he’d seen every day, and he stopped to take another look, a wave of nausea hit him.","Li Jiangbing leaned against the wall and threw up a huge mess, emptying his stomach completely.","Wiping his mouth afterward, he knew that by now, plenty of people would be peeking at him through their door peepholes.","So he shouted repeatedly in the hallway: “There’s a dead body in the hallway! Don’t come out! Go check the owners’ forum!”","He repeated it several times before going back into his apartment and closing the door.","The sounds in the hallway were clear to Jiang Cheng. She just lowered her eyes and noisily slurped her noodles, alternating between a sip of noodles and a bite of braised meat.","Fighting monsters took strength, so she needed to eat her fill.","From outside in the garden, screams, cries for help, and weeping turned into hysterical shrieks of agony, rising and falling before fading away.","Jiang Cheng was arguably the most experienced person in the entire community when it came to dealing with these monsters. But she wasn’t a superhero. If she could help, she would, but what was happening outside right now—this large-scale catastrophe spreading across the whole city—wasn’t something she could change on her own.","Saving one Shen Wei had taken everything she had.","It was the weekend. The temperature was cool that evening. She had no idea how many owners had been unconscious in the garden, killed, or turned into hidden murderers.","Right now, the absolute best thing to do was what Jiang Cheng had said in her post: stay indoors with the door locked.","Just then, it seemed like someone a few floors above yelled out an open window: “What’s going on? Someone come quickly! What’s down there?”","And then she heard Li Jiangbing’s familiar voice again. He was yelling out his window too: “Eve-ry-one—go check—the own-ers’—for-um! Eve-ry-one—go check—the own-ers’—for-um!”","He had such a loud voice and huge lung capacity, stretching his syllables into a long echo. It bounced around outside.","Good. That meant a lot of people in the community probably heard him now.","Li Jiangbing really was useful.","But not long after, Li Jiangbing was shouting toward the garden again: “Stop fucking calling me! Don’t call! It’s useless calling me! If you need something, post in the forum!!!”","No guesses needed—he must have gotten flooded with calls from people who had read the post where Li Jiangbing had left his phone number for Jiang Cheng, craving advice and information.","Jiang Cheng didn’t let outside distractions bother her. She focused on eating. She drank all the broth too, and only then did her weary body feel recharged with strength.","She cleared away the small table and walked over to the bed to check.","First, she gently stroked the black cat’s head and softly called, “Mo Li... Mo Li...”","Please don’t die.","Mo Li’s limbs twitched.","Good. Still alive.","But it didn’t look good. Jiang Cheng pressed her palm against Mo Li’s back. Was a cat’s temperature this high? She remembered reading on a pet forum that cats ran hotter than humans, but... this high?","It felt almost scalding.","Jiang Cheng had a gut feeling things were dire.","But there was nothing she could do.","She hadn’t even thanked him yet for saving her life.","Little cat, hang in there!","Because she was so upset, Jiang Cheng didn’t notice that when she silently thought “Hang in there!”, Mo Li’s body twitched ever so slightly.","As if a small electric shock had gone through him.","Jiang Cheng wiped her eyes and moved to the other side of the bed to check on Shen Wei.","Shen Wei looked terrible too. Her face was pale and lifeless, as if she had lost a lot of blood. She didn’t have a fever, though—her forehead felt slightly cool.","Jiang Cheng called to her softly, hoping she’d open her eyes. But Shen Wei fared even worse than Mo Li—she showed no reaction at all. She was completely unconscious.","Even if a dead mutated monster ended up in her own apartment, Jiang Cheng would be okay—she would just be thankful she had survived again.","But she really didn’t want to see a girl who had talked to her earlier, who had bravely kept calm and clear-headed through her pain, die right in front of her.","She didn’t have much hope, but Jiang Cheng still dialed for an ambulance one more time, praying for a miracle.","And the miracle happened—the call actually went through!","Jiang Cheng’s heart skipped a beat.","Yet before she could speak, a chaotic and violent noise erupted from the phone—","Ringing phones, rising and falling in waves.","The sound of collisions.","The screams of many women.","“Pin her down! Pin Xiao Song down!”","“Ahh, she bit me! Pry her mouth open! Ahhh, pry her mouth open, she bit me!”","“Go easy! That’s Xiao Song!”","“Can’t you see she’s not human anymore! She’s crazy! She’s a monster!”","Screams, wails, cries for help, and arguments intertwined with the jumble of phone rings, hammering at the heart.","In the sealed telephone duty room, the female operators on shift faced a mutated colleague.","It was a colleague they’d spent days with, so they couldn’t bring themselves to strike hard from the start.","But the mutated one was ferocious, bloodthirsty, and once she bit down, she wouldn’t let go.","“What are you doing, Sister Wang?!”","“Ahhh, murder! Sister Wang’s killing someone!”","“Shut up! Xiao Song isn’t human anymore!”","Everyone was hysterical—helplessness, panic, and terror spilled out of the receiver, flooding into Jiang Cheng’s ears.","Jiang Cheng listened for a moment, then hung up the phone.","Outside, the noise was still faintly chaotic. The building had a calm, insane feel to it.","Helpless. No one could be counted on.","Jiang Cheng had felt this way once before—when her parents died suddenly.","But she had gotten through it alone then.","She could do it again this time.","Back at the computer, she opened the forum. New posts had appeared, more and more people waking up.","Her own post sat at the top, pinned by an admin. In the time it took to cook a bowl of instant noodles, it had already amassed hundreds of replies:","“My neighbor got bitten to death! The biter is also a resident!”","“There was one on our floor. We all worked together to kill it. Will we go to jail?”","“No one’s picking up the emergency line!”","Most of the residents and tenants in the youth apartment complex were young, so the community forum was usually very active.","Now it was like an explosion. A single refresh brought up new towering threads.","“From what OP says in the post, the affected area is huge. The cops probably ended up like us too. Some of them might’ve turned into monsters.”","“Is what OP says even true? How would she know?”","“For sure, they’re human too. It’s not like being a cop gives you job immunity.”","“What’s going on? Is this some kind of virus infection?”","“Everyone, turn on your TVs and wait for the news. If the situation’s serious, there’ll definitely be bulletins and announcements. Keep the TV on to receive updates.”","That last suggestion was a good one, a correct one.","Jiang Cheng turned on the TV and cycled through several channels, but obviously the government hadn’t reacted yet. All the programs were prerecorded.","She turned the TV off.","Pacing back and forth in her cramped apartment, she thought.","Some cause led to everyone’s collective unconsciousness. The “cause” was unknown—maybe a virus, maybe radiation. Among them, some underwent mutation.","If what happened in the youth apartment complex was happening indiscriminately across the city, or even farther, then the police who maintained order would have lost some personnel first. Doctors too. Same for every other sector, because it had nothing to do with profession—it probably covered all jobs equally.","In this situation, though, police and doctors were the most needed professions.","That meant order might not be restored until tomorrow or even the day after. At least the next day or two wouldn’t be safe to go out. People would be stuck at home.","Jiang Cheng quickly checked her supplies.","Lucky for her, living alone meant she couldn’t afford the embarrassment of “finishing in the bathroom and realizing there’s no toilet paper.” She kept a small stock of daily essentials at home.","She always followed the principle of “use one, keep one in reserve.”","For staple food, she had one bag of rice (5kg, two-thirds left) and another unopened bag (5kg).","Eggs: four, plus an unopened carton.","Canned luncheon meat: six cans, usually for fried rice.","Pickled vegetables: one big pack containing 12 small packets.","Frozen meat: several large pieces, she couldn’t say the exact weight.","Vegetables: a small amount.","The rest: two big tubs of chocolate, four boxes of various flavored pies, and two types of cookies.","Snacks—beef jerky, nuts, chips, and a few bags of puffed food.","Even if she ran out of non-staples, the rice alone (one and a half bags) could keep her going for twenty days. Food was adequate for now.","Toilet paper was also sufficient.","The water dispenser had half a bucket. At home, she had another full bucket saved. That would last a long time.","But the antiseptic solution in her small medicine cabinet had been used up all at once by Shen Wei and Mo Li. Given the situation, wound care supplies would likely be badly needed in the coming days.","This needed replenishing.","After checking everything, Jiang Cheng turned on the TV again. Still no emergency news. It seemed at least tomorrow before the government reacted.","She logged back into the community forum. More posts had appeared.","Her thread was still pinned, but with too many replies now to read conveniently. Others had started new threads.","From what she scanned, most people showed a certain level of fear, panic, and anxiety, but basically everyone agreed that staying put in their homes was the safest move.","By now, the courtyard outside had gone almost completely quiet. Looking down from the window, she could see a few ghostly figures moving slowly.","There were fewer screams and shrieks from the building too.","The first wave of encounters between ordinary people and the mutated monsters had ended in a short burst.","Those who ran slowly, had little strength, or panicked—without rescue—had probably already died.","As for the others, they were mostly now holed up in their homes, safe for the moment, actively contacting others, going online, and gathering information.","After that initial chaos, an eerie silence had settled once more over the complex.","Only the cars on the road were getting louder.","The community was gated, and residents had apartments to hide in.","She wondered what it was like outside a closed community like this.","Someone, it turned out, had the same thought. Another forum user had reposted external information: “It’s not just our complex! It’s everywhere! The whole of S City! And C City, N City, L City... this might be nationwide today!”","Even though she had suspected it, Jiang Cheng felt a weight sink in her heart when she saw this."]},{"number":9,"title":"Chapter 9","paragraphs":["Before the government had made any response at all, netizens had already begun spontaneously pooling information. It was at times like this that the power of the internet became apparent.","Jiang Cheng closed the homeowners’ forum and opened several major national online forums to check the latest firsthand accounts.","Information from all over the country gathered here, and she kept browsing the web until the middle of the night. Sure enough, it wasn’t just S City—this event covered the entire country.","What could cover such a vast area all at once?","A virus? Or radiation?","Jiang Cheng recalled the moment that afternoon when she had felt dizzy while feeding the cats in the garden, and the sky had taken on a strange purple hue. She had looked up then, thinking it was just an unusually early sunset—it was still clearly mid-afternoon.","That night she had developed a fever, taken some medicine, and fallen into a deep sleep.","Now that she thought about it, that hadn’t been ordinary sleep—it had clearly been unconsciousness.","The situation across the country was mostly the same: people waking up gradually, chaos and panic first. Then the unlucky ones died, while the lucky ones survived by beating to death the mutated monsters.","Some people were injured, and many described the mutated creatures as “biting people like mad dogs.”","That was vivid—that was exactly what Jiang Cheng had felt when she first saw the monster in the garden tearing into Shen Wei.","Most people had also reached a consensus by now: stay home, lock the doors, and wait for the government’s instructions tomorrow.","Jiang Cheng closed her laptop and got up again to check on Mo Li and Shen Wei.","Mo Li was burning hot; Shen Wei was icy cold. One cat and one person, both bitten by mutated monsters, yet their conditions were completely different.","Jiang Cheng wasn’t a doctor, but she took a cooling patch from the fridge and applied it to Mo Li to bring down the fever, then shook out a blanket and covered Shen Wei to keep her warm.","She made a silent prayer that she hadn’t mixed up the two treatments.","It was then that she heard a faint siren in the distance. She couldn’t tell if it was a police car, a fire truck, or an ambulance.","But the sound was thrilling.","It meant the government’s forces, after the initial chaos, were able to regroup effectively and were already mobilizing.","Jiang Cheng looked out the window and saw silhouettes in every window where lights were still on. Clearly, everyone shared the same feeling—a relieved, joyful sense of “finally, they’re coming” and “we’re saved.”","Let’s hope so.","Jiang Cheng checked the door again, confirmed it was locked. She left the hallway light on, turned off the main lights, and then, holding the baseball bat against her chest, lay down on the sofa and fell asleep.","Many people at this time were nowhere near falling asleep. Just moments ago, she’d seen that most houses still had their lights on—because many people, after waking up from unconsciousness and realizing something was wrong, never left their homes at all. They’d only peered out the windows at the terrifying scenes in the garden below, then sensibly stayed put in their safe houses.","Their minds were a tangle of chaos—how could anyone possibly sleep?","Jiang Cheng was probably the person in the entire neighborhood who had expended the most physical energy that night.","She even felt hungry again just before sleeping, ate a few biscuits to settle her stomach, and then lay down. She fell asleep quickly.","The moon hung high over the city, pale and stark.","Jiang Cheng slept deeply.","She had no idea that the one cat and one person occupying her bed were undergoing silent, cataclysmic changes—blood, cells, gene strands all transforming beyond recognition.","Mo Li’s paw pads flowered open many times and then closed again; his body twitched slightly in small spasms.","As for Shen Wei, her skin, pale and grayish, was gradually turning a sickly green. If she had changed to this color before Jiang Cheng fell asleep, and Jiang Cheng had seen it, she would have been alarmed—because the mutated monsters she’d encountered had lost the normal color of human skin, which had turned a dark blue-black.","But sadly, right up until Jiang Cheng fell asleep, Shen Wei’s skin had only looked like someone who had lost too much blood.","Jiang Cheng never realized the danger.","Shen Wei’s skin changed little by little—similar to the mutated creatures they’d encountered earlier, but not exactly the same. Her skin was altogether greener, a pale gray-green lighter than the dark blue-black of the others.","Her complexion changed too, gradually losing the texture of human flesh and taking on the appearance of green artificial leather.","This transformation happened without a sound, until Shen Wei’s eyes snapped open.","Her eyes no longer had any whites—they were pitch black entirely!","Humans truly do possess something called “the sixth sense.”","In her sleep, Jiang Cheng’s heart suddenly constricted. She shot her eyes open and immediately met a pair of pitch-black eyes.","Shen Wei stood before the sofa, bent over “gazing” at her, nose nearly touching nose.","Jiang Cheng didn’t know how long she had slept, but the sky was still dark. Moonlight streaming through the floor-to-ceiling window cast Shen Wei’s long shadow across the floor and the sofa.","Her green skin gave off a look of dense, thickened toughness.","Her black eyes looked like something straight out of a science fiction film about aliens.","Jiang Cheng held her breath, not daring to move a single muscle.","Strangely, though Shen Wei had already mutated into a monster, she didn’t immediately attack or bite her. Shen Wei seemed to be “staring” at her. After a moment, her face drifted slowly from Jiang Cheng’s nose down toward her chest, over her heart.","Jiang Cheng couldn’t tell if Shen Wei was actually “looking” at her, or “smelling” her, or even... “listening” to her?","Just then, the neighbor upstairs got up to use the bathroom and pressed the flush button. The loud, gurgling rush of water suddenly echoed overhead.","Shen Wei snapped her head up, staring toward the ceiling.","Now!","Jiang Cheng hurriedly sat up and shoved Shen Wei away! Then she sprang to her feet and swung the baseball bat over her head with full force!","Shen Wei stumbled backward, and as the bat whistled toward her, she dropped her center of gravity in an instant, narrowly dodging the blow.","Jiang Cheng’s swing hit empty air, and her balance wavered—she stumbled a step sideways before steadying herself, gripping the bat tightly and staring at Shen Wei in shock—that dodge just now had been so precise, so swift and agile that most normal living humans couldn’t have pulled it off.","Shouldn’t a person who mutates be uncoordinated and unstable?","The hallway light wasn’t very bright—a soft, warm yellow that only reached a small area near the entrance.","Jiang Cheng had deliberately not drawn the curtain before sleeping, so moonlight and the lights from outside filtered in as well.","You could make out faces, but the overall room was still dim.","In that split second, the bat had swept across the crown of Shen Wei’s head, and she had dodged by crouching low—but then she didn’t stand back up, the way a human would.","Instead, Shen Wei remained in that half-crouched pose, her black eyes locked on Jiang Cheng.","Jiang Cheng, white-knuckled around the bat, also held her position, afraid to move.","Through the dim light she could now clearly see that Shen Wei’s skin differed from the four variants she had encountered before.","In that instant, Jiang Cheng realized that Shen Wei was a more advanced existence than the earlier mutated creatures. Her limbs were coordinated and agile—something the four monsters Jiang Cheng had killed were nowhere near matching.","One person, one monster—locked in a standoff inside the dimly lit room.","Jiang Cheng felt sweat begin to bead on the back of her neck, gathering into a drop that slid along the dip of her spine down toward her waist.","Shen Wei stayed in that half-crouch as if it cost her no effort at all. But Jiang Cheng, holding her baseball bat, found she couldn’t stay completely still for any length of time.","Whenever Jiang Cheng shifted slightly, Shen Wei’s face tracked her movement.","When Jiang Cheng froze again, Shen Wei would too. But she seemed to grow irritated by this, and suddenly she opened her mouth and let out a sharp hiss of air.","It looked like the prelude to a cat fight.","But when that breath was exhaled by a “person,” it was enough to make one’s skin crawl. The hairs on Jiang Cheng’s arms stood on end.","Jiang Cheng suspected that Shen Wei couldn’t actually see her clearly. She seemed to be relying on her hearing to pinpoint Jiang Cheng’s location.","Jiang Cheng lowered her gaze to the floor. The trash can was right at her feet.","She slowly shifted her foot, ever so gently, until the tip of her shoe touched the trash can. In the next instant, she pushed off with her foot and sent the trash can skidding out. Or rather, it couldn’t really be called a “kick”—she essentially used her foot to “shove” it forward.","The advantage of this was that the sound produced at the moment she applied force was minimal, far quieter than the sound of the trash can hitting the ground a split second later.","Sure enough, Shen Wei lunged in the direction where the trash can landed.","The moment Shen Wei moved, Jiang Cheng moved too, swinging the baseball bat in a whistling arc aimed at the back of Shen Wei’s head.","Amazingly, Shen Wei dodged again with startling agility, twisting her body and leaping straight at Jiang Cheng.","But Jiang Cheng had already anticipated this outcome when she swung. The moment her bat met empty air, she didn’t hesitate—she swung again, striking at the air in front of her.","Her prediction was right! Shen Wei, mid-pounce, seemed to slam straight into the bat as if she had thrown herself onto it. She was knocked off course by the blow and missed her target.","Shen Wei turned and lunged back, but Jiang Cheng’s bat never stopped. Blow after blow, she beat Shen Wei back.","Thankfully, although Shen Wei was more agile and flexible than the previous mutants, she didn’t have any “surprise tactics.” As long as she could locate Jiang Cheng, she would simply keep attacking in straight lines.","So for Jiang Cheng, reading her trajectory wasn’t difficult—every strike could land on Shen Wei. But Shen Wei’s strength was simply overwhelming.","When Jiang Cheng had faced the four earlier mutants, their uncoordinated limbs had allowed her to dodge flexibly and use her technique during both attack and defense. In truth, Jiang Cheng had never engaged in prolonged strength-based struggles with those four.","But now, in this cramped space, as Shen Wei launched one straight-line assault after another, every swing of Jiang Cheng’s bat was a contest of pure power.","Shen Wei’s coordination and agility were both greater than the earlier mutants, but she hadn’t lost that “raw strength” trait either. She even used her arms to block the bat and protect her head.","She knew her head was a vital spot.","In the brief span of a few moments, the two women engaged in a simple yet fierce life-and-death struggle within the small space.","Although Jiang Cheng’s physical stamina had been enhanced after her high fever, it was clear that the mutant’s strength had increased even more. Every clash was a high-intensity drain on her energy, and after just a few rounds of attack and defense, she could feel her arms going numb and her stamina flagging.","Her breathing had become ragged, and the back of her T-shirt was soaked through with sweat.","Shen Wei had now completely lost her human habits. Whenever she squared off against Jiang Cheng, she would crouch with her knees half-bent, body slightly hunched, both hands spread out in front of her like ghost claws.","She’d had long, beautiful manicured nails, but in this situation they looked like nothing short of lethal weapons.","And she had blocked the bat with her arms several times—Jiang Cheng could feel that her bone density seemed to have been enhanced beyond that of the four she’d killed earlier.","Shen Wei fixed her pitch-black eyes on Jiang Cheng, opened her mouth, and let out another breath. Her teeth shone pale white.","To be honest, the living aren’t frightening, and the dead aren’t frightening either. But something that was neither alive nor dead—that was truly unsettling to the core.","That exhaling sound was utterly inhuman. A fresh wave of goosebumps broke out on Jiang Cheng’s back, and she couldn’t help but shrug her shoulders.","That single instant of distraction was all Shen Wei needed. She pounced.","Jiang Cheng reacted quickly and swung the bat down hard. But this time, Shen Wei caught the bat!","Jiang Cheng knew immediately that something was wrong. The thought barely flashed through her mind before she was flung through the air by an enormous force, the bat flying from her hands, her body crashing into the sofa.","She opened her eyes and saw Shen Wei above her, mouth wide open, leaping down at her. There was nowhere to dodge, nowhere to hide.","Jiang Cheng’s pupils contracted sharply.","Was she going to die here?","Time’s fast and slow defied description.","Shen Wei seemed to hang in the air, frozen, as she lunged.","But the next instant, she vanished from Jiang Cheng’s field of vision—she disappeared so fast that Jiang Cheng couldn’t even see it, only hearing the massive crash against the sideboard and an extremely clear sound of bones shattering.","Shen Wei hadn’t “vanished”—she had been knocked aside the very instant she lunged at Jiang Cheng.","Jiang Cheng propped herself up, trembling, and stared at the creature that had knocked Shen Wei away and bitten through her neck—","Completely black, with long, sleek limbs, its body larger than a big dog, almost like a leopard.","Was it what she thought it was?","Normally, that would be impossible. But if humans could turn into monsters, what was impossible anymore?","After gazing at the pitch-black creature for a long time, Jiang Cheng tested a name: “...Mo Li?”","The black creature turned its head. Its eyes were a piercing green, still blazing with murderous intent.","It had Shen Wei’s neck clamped in its jaws.","Shen Wei’s head now hung at a right angle. Though some flesh and blood still connected it to her body, the main connection was clearly severed. Her limbs had gone limp—she was well and truly dead.","The leopard-like creature released its grip, let go of Shen Wei, and walked toward Jiang Cheng.","With every step it took, its body shrank a little more.","Jiang Cheng sat on the sofa, watching as the beast that could easily kill a mutant shrank back into the familiar black cat. It jumped lightly onto her lap and looked up at her with green eyes.","A faint electric current ran through her heart.","This had happened before—back then it had felt like someone had lightly poked her heart, giving Jiang Cheng a feeling of being “stirred inside.”","Now she felt it again.","It wasn’t language, but it reached her heart directly—subtle, faint, unmistakable.","“I...” Jiang Cheng stared at Mo Li and answered instinctively. “I’m fine.”"]},{"number":10,"title":"Chapter 10","paragraphs":["“I’m fine,” Jiang Cheng replied, but couldn’t help raising her hand.","Mo Li didn’t flinch. Her fingertips gently landed on top of Mo Li’s head.","So fluffy.","A fluffy little head.","Jiang Cheng moved cautiously, her palm slowly coming down to rest on Mo Li’s back—a bit bigger than the first time she’d seen him a week ago, but still a normal-sized cat.","So different from that beastly form from moments ago.","Just now, in that sealed, confined space: agile, vicious mutants. She’d truly escaped with her life—more dangerous than facing those four before.","And Mo Li had snapped the mutant’s neck with a single pounce. What incredible fighting strength.","Though she couldn’t explain what she’d just witnessed, Jiang Cheng finally managed to calm down. She took a deep breath, scooped the black cat into her arms, and pressed her cheek against him.","“Thank you!”","“You saved me again.”","Her back was soaked through—all from the lingering terror.","Mo Li didn’t struggle at all. His body was soft and warm.","So warm it burned.","Jiang Cheng opened her eyes and looked down—the little black cat had closed its eyes again, as if asleep.","She carefully set Mo Li down on the sofa.","She knelt beside him, lifting his leg to examine the wound on his belly. The bandage from before had probably snapped during the transformation. The bite wound from the security guard had looked so horrifying, but now, under the sleek black fur, there was no trace of injury.","She thought about Mo Li’s transformation earlier. It was surreal. But from a scientific standpoint, that kind of physical change would require massive amounts of metabolism, and during that process, wounds could indeed be repaired by new cells.","But he’d collapsed again, which meant he probably hadn’t fully recovered his strength.","He’d thrown himself into danger to save her.","Jiang Cheng held Mo Li’s paw, unable to speak.","Ever since her parents died and her relatives fought over the inheritance, no one in this world had ever been willing to do something “without regard for their own safety” for her, the way her parents had.","Jiang Cheng felt, in that moment, that she had family again—even if Mo Li was just a cat.","She gently stroked Mo Li’s fur. His body had no wounds now, but he was still scorching hot.","When a person runs a high fever, dehydration can be fatal. Mo Li’s body temperature was far higher than even a human fever.","Jiang Cheng thought for a moment, stepped over the chaotic mess on the floor, brought some water, and fed it to Mo Li drop by drop with a small spoon.","Mo Li swallowed. So he did need fluids.","She fed him several spoonfuls until he stopped swallowing.","There was only so much she could do. Mo Li would also need food to regain energy, but he was in a drowsy state, and he wasn’t a kitten who could drink milk—she couldn’t feed him right now.","So she gently carried him back to the bed, hoping he’d recover and wake up on his own.","For now, she had things she still needed to do.","She walked to Shen Wei’s body, crouched down, and examined her carefully.","Shen Wei’s skin was grayish-blue, with a tough texture, like thick leather.","Completely different from human skin.","Her neck was almost entirely torn through. A cat’s bite force was nothing to scoff at—among same-sized animals, they’re top-tier fighters. And that was before Mo Li had grown enormous.","When she’d finished examining everything, Jiang Cheng dragged Shen Wei’s body to the door. She checked the hallway through the peephole, saw nothing out of the ordinary, then quickly opened the door and dragged the body out into the corridor.","Now there were three bodies in the hallway on this floor.","Jiang Cheng locked the door, wiped her hands clean, and didn’t bother tidying up the messy living room. She opened her laptop and posted on the residents’ forum:","【!!!WARNING! People bitten by mutants will also turn into mutants!!!】","In the body of the post, she objectively described what she had observed.","【Transformation occurs about six hours after being bitten. This is only one observed case so far; the transformation time may not be universal.】","【Vision is weak; relies on smell and hearing—mainly hearing—to determine direction. But the influence of lighting can’t be ruled out; the room was very dark at the time.】","【Limb coordination is good, movements are agile. Hard to deal with.】","After posting, Jiang Cheng copied the content and shared it on various other forums as well.","Then she finally had time to browse the forum pages.","She’d gone to sleep just after midnight. Now it was between four and five in the morning. In the four hours she’d been asleep, the forum had been flooded with posts.","Jiang Cheng skimmed through them quickly and realized she wasn’t the first to warn people. There were already a few others who had encountered situations like Shen Wei’s.","She found every relevant post she could and jotted down times on paper.","Sure enough, Shen Wei was just one case—her transformation time wasn’t universal. Of the cases Jiang Cheng recorded, the fastest one transformed within half an hour.","Compared to a youth apartment building like this one, where single owners and renters gathered, each shut away in their own isolated unit, ordinary residential communities were actually more prone to situations like Shen Wei’s.","Because most families lived together in regular communities. One unit might have a mom, dad, kids, even grandparents—several people under one roof.","If just one person transformed, it became a humanitarian disaster.","Jiang Cheng also noticed that not everyone fell into a coma like Shen Wei did. Shen Wei’s state might have been caused by excessive blood loss. Some people transformed without any symptoms at all.","One post described two people working together to kill a mutant. One of them got bitten on the arm—a minor injury. After they fled back into their apartment, both were exhausted, so the other person went to the kitchen to cook some noodles.","In the time it took to boil those noodles, the bitten one transformed.","In the past couple of years, broadband had spread to cities, but it hadn’t yet reached towns and villages. Compared to the total population, the number of people who could access the internet was still small. And among those who survived such horrifying encounters, only a small fraction would even think to post warnings for others.","So the actual number of cases was likely far higher than what appeared online.","As of now, Shen Wei’s transformation time was the longest among known cases. She had practically woken up the fastest—and the timing was calculated from when she woke. So that didn’t mean there weren’t longer incubation periods.","If someone received a minor injury and showed no obvious symptoms like unconsciousness, wouldn’t they easily be able to hide among the crowd?","Jiang Cheng cupped her chin, staring at the screen, these thoughts racing through her mind.","But thinking about that now was still too far off.","Jiang Cheng closed her laptop, stood up, and looked at the living room.","The dining table was overturned, chairs lying on the floor. The glass in the sideboard was shattered, mugs and glasses had fallen and smashed, and shards of glass littered the floor.","Jiang Cheng righted the table and chairs, swept all the glass bits into the trash can.","She looked up at the floor-to-ceiling window—the sky outside was beginning to brighten. Dawn was breaking.","Putting away the broom, she went to the bed to check on Mo Li.","Mo Li’s eyes were closed, but his breathing was steady. His temperature was still high. When she gently touched him, he’d open his eyes for a moment, then close them again—looking very weak.","Jiang Cheng rinsed the rice and put the porridge on to cook, then soaked a small bowl of cat food in warm water. She carried it over and gently shook Mo Li: \"Eat something.\"","All living things need food to replenish their energy, and a mystical transformation like Mo Li's must consume far more energy than usual. He was so weak right now—there was no way he didn't need to replenish.","Jiang Cheng tried tucking a softened piece of cat food into Mo Li's mouth, and sure enough, he swallowed it. She had guessed right.","Mo Li couldn't move at all right now. Jiang Cheng tested it and found that feeding him three or four pieces at a time was the fastest to swallow. Fewer pieces wasted efficiency; more pieces meant he had to lift his neck, which seemed very difficult for him in his current, utterly weakened state.","So Jiang Cheng fed him four pieces at a time. Mo Li cooperated well—once four pieces were in his mouth, he swallowed once, without even opening his eyes.","Not until he had finished the entire bowl of cat food did he close his eyes again and drift back to sleep, snoring softly.","Jiang Cheng worried he might relieve himself on the bed, so she found an old pillowcase, folded it several times, and tucked it under Mo Li.","Mo Li kept his eyes closed and didn't open them, letting her fuss over him however she liked.","The porridge was done. Jiang Cheng had a simple breakfast.","As she ate, she opened the owners' forum online and saw someone posting that they had no food at home, asking what to do. A kind neighbor had already replied offering to share some.","Below, someone asked: \"So when can we go outside?\"","Another asked: \"Are we still going to work on Monday?\"","These two questions sparked a lively discussion. Many people wanted to know what to do about Monday's commute and whether the monsters on the road would bite them.","Jiang Cheng spooned a mouthful of porridge into her mouth.","Scrolling further down, she saw someone saying they planned to go out and check things in \"tomorrow's daylight.\" Since the post was made in the middle of the night, that so-called \"tomorrow\" meant today.","After breakfast, Jiang Cheng cleaned up and turned on the television. Still no news or government announcements.","She lowered the volume but didn't turn the TV off, planning to leave it on in case there was a temporary government notice she could catch in time.","Before long, it was seven or eight in the morning. Jiang Cheng gave Mo Li some water again.","By then, sounds began to stir in the hallway. Not the mutated ones—ordinary neighbors. In the end, people can't bear to turn their own homes into prison cells; someone was bound to crack.","Three bodies lay in the hallway, but that didn't stop someone from finally working up the nerve to step out and take a look.","With the first, a second and third soon opened their doors. Before long, the neighbors were all out, gathered around the bodies, chattering quietly.","Li Jiangbing came out too, bragging to the others about how he had killed Li Ziqing: \"I saw her wandering around in the hallway, and that just wouldn't do—what if she bit somebody? So I went back inside, grabbed my weapon, and came out...\"","Even now, he held a baton in each hand, and with his hefty build, he cut an imposing figure to the neighbors.","Especially since no one else besides Jiang Cheng had seen his cowardly side yesterday. The neighbor who had woken up later also assumed the one Jiang Cheng killed was actually the one he had taken down.","Everyone praised him: \"Thank god you were here.\"","\"I looked through the peephole and it scared me half to death.\"","\"Same here. I didn't even know what was going on. I thought it was a murder.\"","\"So, uh... does this count as murder?\"","\"...Can't be, right?\"","Li Jiangbing said, \"I don't think it does. If the police saw one of these things with their own eyes, they'd know it had to be killed. Go look at her place—her boyfriend got bitten to death by her.\"","Li Ziqing's door was still wide open, and everyone couldn't resist poking their heads in for a look.","The apartment was tiny, visible at a glance. Li Ziqing's boyfriend's death was brutal—his neck had been chewed completely through.","Someone gagged.","Someone's voice trembled: \"They're fucking eating people?\"","Li Jiangbing let out a grunt and said, \"The police ought to give me a bravery award. If they call this murder, there's no justice in the world.\"","Li Jiangbing wasn't too worried.","He had come face to face with a mutant, and he knew they couldn't be considered \"people\" at all anymore. The police would certainly understand.","Besides, during the large-scale awakening last night, many people and mutants had died together. He himself had stayed online until the early hours, and from what he saw online, this was happening everywhere. He wasn't worried.","Deep down, he felt there was safety in numbers.","But he was puzzled: \"When did another one show up?\"","There should have been just two mutated corpses in the hallway—Li Ziqing and the neighbor next to her. But now there were three.","Li Jiangbing's voice boomed: \"Who's this one? Never seen him before. He's not from this floor, right?\""]},{"number":11,"title":"Chapter 11","paragraphs":["Jiang Cheng had been pressing against the door, peering through the peephole ever since she heard the commotion in the hallway. When she heard Li Jiangbing's voice, she pulled the door open. \"She's not one of them.\"","Everyone turned to look at her.","The girl leaned against the doorframe, bare-faced, no makeup. She looked a little haggard, probably from lack of sleep.","When a person looks haggard, they tend to come across as cold. Like when you've worked overtime too long and you're too exhausted to talk to anyone on your way home.","\"She's someone I rescued in the garden last night,\" Jiang Cheng said. \"At that hour, we couldn't find any police or ambulance. To take her home—she lives in Building 6—we'd have had to cross the garden. We didn't dare. So I took her in at my place. She was bitten. She mutated later in the night.\"","Li Jiangbing understood. \"She's the one you wrote about in your post!\"","The neighbors had an \"aha\" moment. \"You're the owner who posted that stickied thread!\"","Everyone had seen Jiang Cheng's two posts, but on the owners' forum everyone used screen names, so nobody knew which unit the poster was from. But hearing the exchange between Li Jiangbing and Jiang Cheng, they now knew.","So she was the first person in the complex to encounter a mutant, warn everyone, and post about it!","They looked at Jiang Cheng again and noticed that although she leaned against the doorframe with a tired, casual air, there was a baseball bat in the hand hanging at her side.","Her eyes were dark, clear, and bright. No panic, no frantic energy. Completely calm.","Last night, everyone had seen through their windows that some of the people who woke up in the garden were killed on the spot the moment they ran into the mutants. And she—being the first one to wake up and run into a mutant—had survived without a scratch.","Jiang Cheng said, \"Take a look at her. Doesn't she seem different from the other two?\"","Jiang Cheng also wanted someone else to confirm whether her own observation was off.","The neighbors had been looking for a while and all nodded. \"Yeah!\"","\"Just like you described in your post.\"","\"So she's really stronger?\"","Jiang Cheng nodded. \"A lot stronger. I almost died.\"","She briefly explained again the difference between an Original Mutant and an Infected Mutant.","Among the neighbors on the same floor, only she and Li Jiangbing had come into direct contact with the Original Mutant, and only she had come into contact with the Infected Mutant. Even Li Jiangbing listened intently.","\"I think...\" Jiang Cheng said, \"it feels like evolution.\"","Everyone exchanged glances.","A younger male neighbor said, \"Sounds like the virus is iterating.\"","Jiang Cheng sighed. \"Yeah. That's exactly the feeling.\"","Li Jiangbing said in admiration, \"You're pretty damn tough.\"","Without Mo Li, she'd probably be dead. Jiang Cheng gave a slight shake of her head and said to Li Jiangbing, \"Since everyone's here now, let's get the bodies cleaned up. Can't just leave them lying in the hallway forever.\"","Li Jiangbing asked, \"How do we handle it?\"","Jiang Cheng said, \"The ones from 0315 and 0317 go back to their own apartments. As for mine, can you take it into 0308?\"","Last night, Jiang Cheng had essentially saved Li Jiangbing's life, so it came naturally for her to delegate tasks to him, and he also naturally agreed. \"Okay.\"","And then it also came naturally to Li Jiangbing to delegate tasks to others. \"You two, take the one from 0315 back. You two, take the one from 0317 back. Does anyone know which unit each one belongs to? Doesn't matter. If you get it wrong, you get it wrong. The police can sort it out later. Go, go, go, move it! Be men about it! You wouldn't make the girls do this, would you?\"","Li Jiangbing held a tactical baton in each hand, tall, burly, loud-voiced. Last night, several neighbors had watched through their peepholes as he killed Li Ziqing. When he barked orders, no one dared to argue. The male neighbors he pointed at all moved, dragging the bodies by the ankles into the units.","People have a natural curiosity. Everyone followed to watch.","Li Jiangbing dragged Shen Wei into 0308, which was next to Jiang Cheng's place.","\"Little White got it bad, huh.\" He dumped the body in 0308, then came out and said with a sigh.","The dog was pitiful, too—bitten to death by its own owner, its throat practically chewed through.","But Jiang Cheng's gaze swept across his hands—","Li Jiangbing had his baton tucked under his armpit, both hands free, clutching a few packs of instant noodles and a bag of chips.","\"I don't have much food at home,\" he quickly explained. \"I usually eat meal-prep for fat loss at the gym. I'm afraid if I keep food in the house, I won't be able to control myself. I never stock up. All I have at home is protein powder.\"","So seeing food at Little White's place, he'd grabbed some on a whim.","Jiang Cheng didn't call him out for \"borrowing\" without asking. She just said, \"That won't keep you full. You should see if he has rice or flour.\"","Li Jiangbing said, \"I don't know how to cook. I only know how to boil chicken breast. I figured I'd survive on instant noodles for the next couple of days.\"","\"And then?\" Jiang Cheng asked.","Li Jiangbing said, \"When things get back to normal in a few days...\"","Jiang Cheng's eyes were clear and bright, reflecting his burly figure.","Li Jiangbing couldn't finish his sentence. A thin sweat broke out on his forehead.","\"It'll be fine, right?\" he asked in a lower voice. \"The police will take over soon, right? The government has to do something, right? They can't just leave us hanging?\"","\"How would I know?\" Jiang Cheng's voice was also quiet.","It sounded like the common type of gentle, polite, soft-spoken young woman. In fact, that had always been Li Jiangbing's impression of her. He'd even once thought about trying to hit on her.","But last night, Jiang Cheng had completely shattered that impression.","\"Still, if you don't have food reserves, I'd suggest you take whatever you can from 0308,\" she said.","Li Jiangbing didn't dare to think too deeply about it. Cold sweat on his forehead: \"Right. I'll go find a bag—no wait, I'll look for one in his place.\"","He turned and dove back into 0308.","Jiang Cheng glanced down the hallway. The neighbors dragging the bodies had also taken things from 0315 and 0317. Unsurprisingly, all of it was food.","Someone protested: \"How can you just take other people's stuff?!\";","Someone defended themselves: \"I don't have any food at home.\"","Jiang Cheng didn't listen any further. She stepped back into her own apartment and closed the door.","Faint arguments drifted in from outside—about whether it was right to take things from other people's homes. The debate only ended when everyone saw Li Jiangbing taking things too.","Li Jiangbing said, \"If I don't take it, I'll starve, won't I? Fine—if the family comes to collect the body later, I'll pay them back in full.\"","Obviously, everyone was a bit intimidated by Li Jiangbing now. When he said that, the other men who had taken items from the dead chimed in loudly: \"That's right, that's right!\"","The rest of them stayed quiet.","For now, they could still call it \"taking.\" But what about later? Jiang Cheng thought behind the door.","Mo Li was on the bed. He'd open his eyes whenever he heard a sound, look at Jiang Cheng, then close them again. Which meant he wasn't unconscious or in a coma. He was just weak.","Jiang Cheng went over and stroked the black cat's head.","He kept his eyes closed, motionless.","Jiang Cheng refreshed the owners' forum.","Everyone was awake now. Some people, like her, had experienced a terrifying night. Others, while safely hiding in their own homes, had watched the horror unfold down in the garden from their windows.","But even under these circumstances, on Sunday morning, more and more posts in the forum were asking: \"Is work tomorrow still on or not?\"","This question struck a chord with many people, and forums across the board were abuzz with people asking and discussing what to do about Monday.","The residents of the youth apartment complex were mostly young men. As everyone knows, when three single men get together, they automatically spawn one idea guy.","Soon, Jiang Cheng saw someone post on the youth apartment owners' forum: 【Screw it, let's go out and take a look.】","More than one person echoed: 【Yeah, let's go check it out. We can't just suffocate in our rooms either.】","【Anyone got weapons?】","【I've got a hammer. Not insulting anyone—I literally have a hammer, and I've also got a wrench.】","【I've got a length of steel rod.】","【How the hell do you have that at home?】","【Passed by a construction site next door, saw this perfectly straight piece, had an itch to pick it up.】","The group was passionately brainstorming in the forum.","Half an hour later, Jiang Cheng stood by the floor-to-ceiling window and looked out. From the various buildings, several male residents emerged—they had agreed on a time to head out together.","Each of them carried a weapon—hammers, wrenches, a length of steel rod, dumbbells, nunchucks, mops, kitchen knives, and all sorts of other things.","A few had even put on motorcycle helmets.","Almost every building responded to the call with at least four or five people coming out, and one building even sent out eleven men.","After the first wave of skirmishes in the garden during the mass awakening last night, the ones who were doomed had already died, and the survivors had fled back into their buildings. There were no more living people in the garden. The mutants drifted like boats that had lost their power in the water, wandering slowly and aimlessly.","Dozens of young men, pumped up with adrenaline, took the initiative to strike out, and the garden immediately became a frenzy of chaos.","Jiang Cheng watched from upstairs as the male residents encountered the mutants. For this group, who were armed and had done their homework on mutant characteristics, the hardest hurdle was actually swinging their weapons at the mutants.","In the end, they still had human forms. Deep down, many people still thought of them as \"people.\"","Everyone was law-abiding citizens, good-hearted regular folks. Suddenly having to strike hard, to strike to kill, at a \"person\"—it wasn't nearly as easy as they had imagined.","Several people charged out with bravado, only to find when they came face-to-face with a mutant that they simply couldn't bring themselves to do it. They just couldn't get past that mental barrier.","Just within Jiang Cheng's line of sight, he could already see three or four people turning around and running back into their buildings.","Fortunately, among this group were a few who had already clashed with mutants last night, whose hands were already stained with blood.","These people who had experienced life-and-death situations didn't hesitate at all. They swung hard at the heads.","When someone took the lead, others followed, and adding a hammer or wrench hit to a mutant's head didn't feel like such a huge psychological hurdle anymore.","As soon as they personally killed their first mutant, the initial mental barrier was passed.","Jiang Cheng watched their movements go from hesitant and timid to aggressive and bold.","After killing their first mutant, they seemed to be suddenly endowed with courage. They shouted and charged at the next mutant.","But everyone had seriously underestimated the number of mutants in the garden.","Yesterday was Saturday, and at that time on a summer evening, far too many people had been out in the garden—some just returning home, some heading out.","Last night, people upstairs had only seen what they could see. Many who woke up later had only heard some distant noises, and the first wave of battle was already over. The ones that happened behind trees, in unlit shadows, couldn't be seen at all.","But now, under the clear bright sky, with the blazing sun, everything was perfectly visible.","As the excited young men shouted and yelled, mutant after mutant was drawn out from the greenery, emerging into everyone's view.","One after another.","Another.","Another.","The beautiful plan of \"picking them off one by one\" fell apart because the number of mutants far exceeded expectations.","The young men, who had just been pumped up, began to feel the strain. Just as they took down one, another would roar and lunge at them.","At that moment, many residents watching from their own floor-to-ceiling windows saw several figures among the mutants down there that stood out—fast, steady, moving in straight lines toward the young men.","Instinctively, many residents slapped their own window glass and shouted in alarm: \"Watch out——!\""]},{"number":12,"title":"Chapter 12","paragraphs":["Compared to the original mutants, the infected mutants were an entirely different class of being.","Stronger, faster, and more agile in their limbs.","The first one to tackle a person was an infected mutant.","The person who was brought down let out a loud scream, which quickly turned into a shrill cry of agony. His companions immediately rushed to help, swinging hammers and wrenches at the back of the infected mutant's head.","The mutant was beaten to death on the spot.","But when they pulled the mutant off the fallen man, they saw that his face had been chewed to a bloody pulp. The pain had him writhing and gasping.","No wonder he'd screamed so horribly.","Someone grabbed him and pulled him up: \"Get up!\"","Lying there wasn't an option—with that many mutants around, you'd be waiting to die.","The wounded man knew it too. Gritting his teeth against the agony, he scrambled to his feet, let out two muffled grunts, and ran toward the building entrance. Everyone understood he was heading back inside.","Someone blurted out, \"Don't let him back in! He'll turn into an infected mutant too!\"","Everyone who heard paused mid-motion and couldn't help glancing over. The wounded man clearly heard it as well, because he immediately quickened his pace into a sprint, terrified someone might stop him.","A few people let out an \"Hey!\" but there was nothing they could do—they couldn't abandon the mutants right in front of them to chase after a man who was wounded but not yet turned.","More mutants kept lunging at them, so everyone had to refocus on the immediate threat.","An original mutant could be handled by one person alone, though the sheer numbers made it exhausting. An infected mutant was harder to take down solo, but with several people ganging up on it, it became much more manageable.","The commotion in the garden was so loud that nearly every household had people standing at their floor-to-ceiling windows, watching.","Jiang Cheng noticed that those who hadn't joined the forum-organized activity at the very start were now trickling out of the buildings one after another, carrying all sorts of weapons.","The pressure in the garden eased up.","Jiang Cheng thought it over, stood up, patted Mo Li's head, grabbed her baseball bat, and headed out the door too.","Just as she pulled the door shut, she heard a \"bang\" from farther off in the same direction. Turning her head, she saw the big guy Li Jiangbing stepping out, tucking his baton under his arm.","\"Hey?\" Li Jiangbing was delighted to see her and called out across the distance, \"You're heading downstairs too?\"","There were elevator lobbies at both ends of the building, and Li Jiangbing was closer to his side. Jiang Cheng walked over: \"Everyone should pitch in, right? I can't just stand by and watch.\"","Li Jiangbing said, \"Exactly, that's what I was thinking. I went to bed too late last night and woke up late, just saw it now—otherwise I'd have gone down earlier.\"","People tend to over-explain when they feel guilty.","Jiang Cheng didn't call him out on it. Because she herself hadn't been among the first to join in either—she'd let others take the lead first, observed the situation, and only then decided to participate.","A perfectly understandable mindset, a very human impulse.","The two of them went downstairs together.","It was Li Jiangbing's first time going down since he'd woken up from his coma on Saturday. On the steps outside the building entrance lay the guard's body, and at the bottom of the steps lay another body—probably kicked down by someone coming out, since leaving it sprawled on the steps would have been too much of a blocker.","Li Jiangbing took a couple of looks and recognized him, letting out a sigh: \"Little White's Dad.\"","Little White's Dad had died an awful death.","Li Jiangbing couldn't help but give Jiang Cheng a somewhat odd look.","Jiang Cheng stated the facts plainly: \"The wrist got snapped when he chased me through the hallway and slammed into the wall himself. The legs were broken when he jumped straight out of the third-floor window and landed badly.\"","Li Jiangbing's face lit up with understanding: \"So that's what happened.\"","Jiang Cheng summarized, \"It seems like they keep chasing after sounds or living things.\"","\"Be careful in a bit,\" she added. \"From upstairs, I noticed that the infected mutants seem to see better during the day than at night. It's like they can actually see—they're probably sensitive to light.\"","Li Jiangbing gripped a tactical baton in each hand and said boldly, \"Got it.\"","Ever since he killed Li Ziqing with his own hands, it was as if he had crossed some threshold—he'd overcome his fear psychologically.","The first wave of suicide squads from each building kept making noise, and by now the mutants had been drawn into a tight cluster around them.","Groups had gathered near every building.","Jiang Cheng and Li Jiangbing tightened their grip on their weapons and made a beeline for the nearest group. The ones surrounded in this group were also neighbors from their own building.","A baseball bat is designed for swinging with force, and the grip feels especially good in the hand.","Jiang Cheng stepped forward and swung from behind, knocking one mutant flat on the ground. She followed up with several heavy strikes, and the mutant stopped moving.","Li Jiangbing whistled in admiration. \"Whoa!\"","He wasn't just standing around, either—his tactical baton was swinging too.","Even though he worked out, he'd only ever trained in boxing; he'd never really practiced with weapons. His tactical batons, nunchucks, and the like were mostly for show—pure entertainment.","Using a tactical baton like a fire poker didn't give him as much leverage as a bat. But luckily, brute force worked wonders—Li Jiangbing's muscles weren't for nothing; he had real strength.","He swung his baton around and took down a mutant in just a few hits.","Jiang Cheng kept her eyes on everyone's movements, occasionally glancing over at Li Jiangbing.","\"I think I got stronger after I woke up yesterday,\" she said. \"I mainly came down to test that out. What about you? Do you feel anything?\"","\"Huh? That's a thing?\" Li Jiangbing swung his baton as he spoke. \"Nope, I don't. Feels the same as before.\"","A muscle-head like Li Jiangbing wasn't a good frame of reference.","Jiang Cheng took down another mutant. She observed that the male neighbors from her building seemed to have roughly the same strength as her—maybe even less.","The way they smashed open mutant skulls looked much more laborious than how she and Li Jiangbing did it.","So the \"strength boost\" wasn't a benefit everyone got—it seemed to apply only to her and the mutants.","Jiang Cheng nodded, said no more, and just reminded him, \"Let's not split up. Be careful they don't bite you.\"","There were too many mutants. Even if they weren't that agile, the sheer numbers meant that with one careless moment, they could get you from the side or behind and you'd be infected.","Jiang Cheng did not want to turn into one of them.","With two heavy hitters like Jiang Cheng and Li Jiangbing joining the fight, the pressure on their building's group lightened considerably.","At first, only six people had come out from their building. Now, counting Jiang Cheng and Li Jiangbing, the squad had grown to twelve. After clearing out the mutants gathered in their area, they teamed up and went to help the other buildings.","More and more residents were coming out of their buildings.","By around 10:30 in the morning, the mutants in the garden had been completely cleared. Everyone from all six buildings gathered in the central square, and a rough headcount put them at nearly three hundred people.","The crowd buzzed with chatter.","\"Work\" and \"does this count as us killing people\" were the two phrases Jiang Cheng heard the most.","All law-abiding citizens, and in such a bizarre situation, the two things everyone was most worried about were those. Jiang Cheng didn’t know why she found it ridiculous—she was just another wage slave among the corporate drones, and she too should have been worried about work.","Someone asked, “What do we do now? We can’t just leave the bodies lying around, can we?”","Many people echoed that. With this many bodies in summer, if they weren’t dealt with, it could trigger an epidemic.","Li Jiangbing agreed too, and he was about to chime in when Jiang Cheng suddenly stepped forward and raised her voice: “This isn’t the most urgent thing. The most urgent thing is to immediately put the injured under watch, to prevent them from turning into infected mutants.”","The crowd went quiet and looked at her.","The girl had fair skin and looked quite refined, holding a baseball bat covered in blood and some sticky substance.","“A normal person bitten by a mutant becomes an infected mutant, and they’re tougher than the ones that turned yesterday. Everyone should have seen that,” she said. “I came down late—when I was upstairs, I saw someone injured and run back into the building. There must be others who are hurt. Let’s assume it spreads like rabies, through blood. Anyone bleeding could turn. So my question is—does anyone know the injured person who ran back? Which floor, which unit?”","The crowd buzzed with discussion.","Someone from Building 2 said, “From our building, I only know he’s on the eleventh floor, I see him in the elevator all the time. But I don’t know the exact unit.”","Jiang Cheng nodded and asked, “Are there any injured people here right now? Don’t hide it.”","Everyone looked at each other.","Li Jiangbing shouted loudly, “If you’re hurt, speak up!”","His arms were thick with muscle, propped out on either side of his tall frame, and standing behind Jiang Cheng backing her up, he was quite intimidating.","Someone asked, “And what do we do with the injured? We can’t just... you know.”","Killing mutants didn’t carry the same psychological weight, mainly because the changes in their appearance gave you a strong sense of “not human.” You knew clearly that person could no longer be called a person—they were a monster.","But the injured, as long as they hadn’t turned yet, still looked entirely human.","Kill them? That was hard to stomach.","Jiang Cheng said, “Look, we can’t be sure that being injured definitely means infection. But we have to take precautions. The best way is to put them under restraint first, and if they really do turn, then we deal with it then.”","Everyone agreed with that: “That’s right.”","“Makes sense.”","“If they don’t turn, they’re human; if they turn, we deal with it then. Lock them up first—that’s correct.”","Jiang Cheng had gained the crowd’s support, and swept her gaze over them: “Alright then, everyone here, check each other next to you—see if anyone is bleeding or injured.”","As she spoke, she set the bat on the ground and pulled at her collar herself, letting those around her see her neck.","Her snow-white neck was spotless.","Then she lifted the hem of her pants—her ankles were clean too.","She lifted the bottom of her shirt a little, her belly and lower back were clean, no injuries anywhere.","She set the example, and the two or three hundred people in the square began checking each other. In no time, they found a dozen or so with injuries.","One guy tried to sneak away quietly, but someone grabbed him.","He shouted, “I just scraped my skin! Just a little scrape!”","There were scratches on his ankle, bleeding. They had been made by the fingernails of a mutant that had fallen but wasn't dead yet.","The injured person had been found. So what came next?","Everyone naturally turned their gaze toward Jiang Cheng.","The girl wasn't especially tall, nor did she look particularly strong, but her eyes, clear and sharp as black and white, made people feel she was the one they could rely on."]},{"number":13,"title":"Chapter 13","paragraphs":["“I’m the owner of Unit 0306, Building 2. I was the first person to post on the owners’ forum. I’m probably also the first person in this community to have dealt with a Mutant.” Jiang Cheng said. “I have a bit more experience than the rest of you.”","In reality, she only had a little more. Because after that battle just now, everyone had faced plenty of Mutants. When it came to practical combat experience, they had all caught up—there wasn’t really much of a gap left.","But most people were willing to cooperate with the group and follow orders, yet they themselves weren’t the kind to plan things out or give commands. It was like how the owners’ committee usually had just a few people taking the lead and doing the actual work, while everyone else just signed their names on the agreement forms.","When a large group gathered, people hoped someone would step forward and tell them what to do next.","“My suggestion,” Jiang Cheng said, “is that the injured should bear with it for now and have their freedom restricted. I think the property management’s conference room is a good spot. Settle them there and have someone guard them.”","The crowd buzzed again.","A man whose arm had been bitten was the first to agree: “Fine, I don’t mind. If I really do turn, I don’t want to hurt anyone either. Just put me down directly if it comes to that.”","This man was one of the initiators of this operation on the owners’ forum and the leader for their particular building. He had already built some authority in the fight just now. With him agreeing, others didn’t have much credibility in objecting. So many eyes were watching, and everyone had weapons. The will of the majority took on very real meaning in times like this.","All they could ask was: “Then how long are we locked up for?”","Jiang Cheng said: “Let’s do 24 hours for now. If there’s no problem by this time tomorrow, we’ll release them.”","Li Jiangbing spoke up in agreement: “Fine, that works for me.”","One by one, others voiced approval. The injured few looked uneasy, but they were sensible enough not to cause a fuss.","Jiang Cheng said: “With things as they are, we need to get organized. We can’t just stay in chaos. We have six buildings total. Let’s pick a few liaison people for each building to handle the work and stay in contact, instead of becoming a tangled mess.”","She first volunteered herself: “Building 2 has me, Jiang Cheng. This is my neighbor, Li Jiangbing. Who else from our building is stepping up?”","Li Jiangbing, having been singled out by name, didn’t object and simply stood behind her. Two more people from Building 2 voluntarily stepped forward, and the four of them formed a core team with Jiang Cheng as the lead.","The other buildings also gathered in groups and quickly found their own representatives.","While the others stepped back, those who had voluntarily stepped up stood at the center.","Jiang Cheng nodded: “No need to exchange numbers one by one. When we get back, let’s open a thread on the forum and share contact info there.”","“For now, each building will send one person to walk the injured to the property management office and stay with them there. Let’s get this done first—it’s the most urgent.”","Those willing to stand at the center were usually the ones willing to take charge. Each building assigned one person, so six people in total “escorted” the dozen or so injured to the property office.","Jiang Cheng instructed: “The office has computers that can log onto the owners’ forum. Keep an eye on it. We’ll post our contact info there soon, so stay in touch if anything comes up.”","She also had them give their building reps their unit numbers before sending them off.","The crowd parted to let them through, then closed up again once they had walked off.","The dozen or so people at the center started discussing: “What do we do now? What about the bodies? We can’t just leave them lying here, can we?”","But Jiang Cheng said: “Right now, we have something more important than the bodies.”","Everyone looked at her.","Jiang Cheng said: “A bit earlier, from upstairs, I saw injured people running back into the buildings.”","Li Jiangbing let out a curse: “Damn.”","Everyone’s faces turned grim.","“They should be easy enough to find,” Jiang Cheng said. “There weren’t that many people at that point—just those who had signed up on the forum at first. And when you signed up, you all filled in your unit numbers. Seven, eight, maybe nine or ten people. Shouldn’t be hard to narrow them down.”","She stressed: “We have to find them and get them to the property office.”","This was the most urgent task—they were afraid those who ran back would turn, bite someone else, and lead to more infections. That would be endless trouble, wouldn’t it?","They confirmed on-site that only Buildings 2 and 5 had wounded running back inside. Then they double-checked the unit numbers of the earliest participants. Li Jiangbing led the team for Building 2, and one person from Building 5 also stepped up to lead, raising their voices and rallying five or six people to head back into the buildings.","They would first cross-check against the forum list to see which units those people belonged to, then go and grab them.","Once this group left too, someone asked Jiang Cheng: “How about the bodies? We have to deal with them, right?”","In just a short time, it had become natural to ask Jiang Cheng about arrangements first, seeking her opinion before anything else.","Jiang Cheng said: “For now, pile them all in the central plaza. That’s the furthest point from every building, and it’s spacious around it. If we end up having to burn them, it’ll be safer there.”","Someone hesitated: “Burn them?”","“Ever since midnight last night, I’ve been hearing police sirens and ambulance sounds,” Jiang Cheng said. “But as everyone knows now, this isn’t just our community or our city—it’s basically nationwide. Even if the government gets running again, there’s no way they can handle a volume of bodies this size in a short time. Even if crematoriums ran 24/7, it wouldn’t be fast enough.”","“Given this temperature, if we leave them lying around for a few days, we’ll have a plague on our hands.”","“My take is this: pile them here for now, then contact the police and see what they say. If they’re available to take care of it, great. But if they can’t, we burn them ourselves. We can’t just watch the corpses rot and spread disease.”","“Did anyone bring a phone? Call the police right now.”","Everyone fumbled in their pockets. One man pulled out his phone, flipped it open, and dialed the emergency number in front of the group.","Nothing went through.","“No go,” the man said, closing his phone. “Constant busy signal. It just keeps ringing engaged.”","Jiang Cheng nodded. “Then let’s clean up for now.”","Led by Jiang Cheng and the others, the owners began clearing the battleground.","Almost nobody slacked off. This was their own courtyard—if they didn’t take care of the bodies, they’d be the ones to suffer.","In the end, all the bodies were stacked in the central plaza. Killing hadn’t really registered at the time, but looking at them now came with shock and a lingering fear.","“They look pretty different from humans.”","“Yeah, look at the skin color. A living person wouldn’t have this shade.”","“Look at that one—that’s the infected Mutant type. See how its skin tone is different from the others?”","“God, that one’s really creepy. I almost didn’t dodge it in time.”","“That one was my neighbor from the same building... ugh.”","Everyone stared at the bodies, remarking on how “inhuman” the Mutants were.","Just then, someone upstairs threw open a window and shouted down toward the center of the courtyard: “There’s news—on now! Quick, watch the news broadcast—!”","Several people ran to the foot of their buildings, craning their necks to call up: “What does it say? Has the government issued a notice? What’s the word?”","Several people upstairs poked their heads out, chiming in all at once: \"They say it's a large-scale virus.\"","\"Told us to stay safe, and that we can use force to fight back if necessary.\"","\"Told us to stay home as much as possible and not run around.\"","\"Called on police, doctors, and firefighters to stay at their posts.\"","A person downstairs put his hands on his hips and asked, \"Did they say anything about work tomorrow?\"","The reply from upstairs came: \"N—o.\"","Jiang Cheng exchanged glances with a few of the leaders among the group.","She said to the one who had a phone, \"Try calling again.\"","The man pulled out his phone, flipped it open with a snap, and dialed again. This time, on the fifth try, they were lucky enough to get through.","\"Can't come?\" the man said to the operator. \"So what do we do on our end? There are a lot of bodies here.\"","\"Huh? Oh... got it.\"","\"Alright then.\"","He hung up and told everyone: \"They said unless it's a fire or an explosion needing emergency rescue, don't call about mutants—handle it ourselves. Said they don't have enough police.\"","\"Of course,\" Jiang Cheng said. \"How many cops does a city have compared to residents? And if it's a virus, cops aren't immune either—they've lost people too.\"","She added, \"Given how widespread this virus is, at least in the short term, we can't count on the government.\"","Someone muttered, \"Then isn't everything going to fall into chaos?\"","Jiang Cheng didn't answer. She just glanced at the pile of corpses, taller than a person, and then at the one who had spoken.","The sun was blazing, but everyone still felt cold.","Jiang Cheng said, \"Let's burn them now. No point waiting for them to stink.\"","She asked everyone, \"Does anyone have anything flammable? Gasoline? Alcohol or the like?\"","A man in a property management uniform said, \"There's disinfectant alcohol, gasoline, and diesel in the utility shed. Some of each. We use them for the lawnmower.\"","So several people went to fetch the fuel.","Jiang Cheng discussed shift rotations for the property security staff with the leaders from the other buildings: \"Eat lunch first, then swap in new people, then switch again in the evening.\"","\"By the way, I'm Jiang Cheng.\"","Everyone exchanged names.","There were quite a few people, and not everyone could remember everyone else, but they all remembered Jiang Cheng.","\"You're really strong,\" someone said.","They had all seen how she swung the bat and cracked open a mutant's skull. A few swings and the mutant stopped moving. They had realized right away that she was extremely strong.","Because when they used blunt weapons to beat a mutant to death, they generally needed more swings and more time.","No one had actually counted in the moment, but the speed of the kill was immediately obvious.","After observing all morning, Jiang Cheng had basically confirmed that no one else had experienced the same \"increase in strength\" she had.","She kept her composure: \"I've been strong since I was a kid. No man can beat me in a fight.\"","Her self-set image was accepted right away.","In fact, it was one of the reasons these people were willing to listen to her when she stepped up to take charge.","At that moment, noise came from the direction of Building Two.","Li Jiangbing came back with his group, his face stone-gray.","Jiang Cheng knew right away something had gone wrong: \"Already mutated?\"","\"Yeah,\" Li Jiangbing said, his expression grim. \"We killed it. But we lost two of our people.\"","He turned and gestured.","Everyone saw that behind him, among those who had gone to capture the injured person, two were clearly wounded.","Everyone's faces turned grim.","Someone asked, \"It mutated that fast?\"","Li Jiangbing nodded: \"We matched up the online registration with the apartment numbers and found it. We went to knock on the door, and the knock startled it—it opened the door and lunged out. We weren't ready, and two of us got cut and bled.\"","Infected mutants had agile, coordinated limbs; \"opening a door\" was hard for a primary mutant, but not at all for an infected one.","That was where Li Jiangbing's group got caught out. They had no experience dealing with an infected mutant and hadn't expected the mutation to happen so fast.","Jiang Cheng's gaze settled on the two behind him: \"Then send them to the property office too.\"","The two men's faces went pale as death.","It was almost certain that anyone wounded and bleeding from a mutant would turn a hundred percent. Going there likely meant death—just like the mutant they had just killed.","Both of them still clutched their weapons—one a cleaver, the other a hammer.","The one holding the cleaver tightened his grip, the veins on the back of his hand bulging."]},{"number":14,"title":"Chapter 14","paragraphs":["Before anyone else could react, Jiang Cheng had already shifted the bat from a resting hold in her hands to a two-handed grip, angled slightly over her shoulder. The stance was ready to swing at any moment. \"No need to bring weapons over there. Li Jiangbing, could you hold onto their weapons for them for now?\"","Her wording was polite, her tone gentle, but the meaning behind her words was anything but.","A faint trace of blood still hung in the air, along with a rank, sickly stench. Everyone found it hard to breathe.","When the first wave of injured had been sent to the property management office, the mood hadn't been this grim. Deep down, people had still clung to the idea that maybe the mutation was only a matter of probability, that hope still existed.","But the case right in front of them had shattered that hope in an instant.","Everyone followed Jiang Cheng's lead and tightened their grips on their weapons. The atmosphere froze solid.","The two of them stood surrounded in the center of the crowd.","These people were, in theory, law-abiding citizens. Apart from a few who shared cramped rentals, most of those who'd chosen this young professionals' apartment complex were young, held respectable jobs, and had a certain standard for quality of life.","But today, every single one of them had picked up a weapon and piled up a mountain of bodies in the central plaza of the garden.","One more corpse or two on that pile wouldn't make a difference.","The two men slumped in defeat, handing their cleaver and hammer to the people beside them, and muttered flatly, \"Let's go.\"","The one holding the hammer was already on the verge of tears.","A second later, the tears came: \"I need to call my mom...\"","Everyone, including Li Jiangbing, looked to Jiang Cheng. She gave a slight nod, her voice very soft: \"Call her. Tell her not to worry.\"","The man pulled out his phone, sniffing as he dialed the home landline number.","No one answered.","He murmured, \"That's weird. Sunday, they should both be home.\"","The rhythmic \"beep—beep—beep—\" of the unanswered ring was faintly audible to those standing closest.","Many people had already guessed what it might mean. Their lips moved, but no words came out.","The man on the phone slowly grew dazed.","Li Jiangbing looked left, then right, reluctant to rush him. But he'd just witnessed a case of infection and mutation that happened in a very short span of time, and he was extremely wary of anyone carrying wounds. Not getting them locked up immediately made him uneasy.","Finally, he looked at Jiang Cheng.","Jiang Cheng said, \"Maybe they've just gone into hiding. It's too chaotic right now; hiding is safer. Look, all those people upstairs are hiding too.\"","The man looked up. The young professionals' apartments featured floor-to-ceiling glass windows, and in a single glance he could see many of those who hadn't dared come down to help, pressing their hands against the glass and peering downward.","\"Oh...\" He clicked his phone shut and looked up at Jiang Cheng.","He'd left the scene fairly early, back when Jiang Cheng had just stepped forward to speak confidently and assign tasks. But in this short amount of time, he could feel that Jiang Cheng had already become the center of this group.","\"Then you...\" He hesitated, then held his phone out toward her. \"Could you hold onto my phone for me? If my parents call, please let them know I'm safe. The last number dialed is my home number.\"","Jiang Cheng took the phone without any hesitation, agreeing: \"Okay.\"","She said, \"I'll go with you.\"","She shot a meaningful glance at the people around her.","The representatives from each building who had stepped up to take charge were all sharp-minded people. Catching Jiang Cheng's cue, the leader from Building Four chimed in first: \"Let's go, let's go, we'll all go along together.\"","Everyone exchanged glances and filed out in a large group toward the property management office, a far bigger procession than when they'd escorted the previous dozen or so people.","That earlier group had been docile enough that they hadn't even confiscated their weapons.","On the way, they ran into the people carrying fuel back to the central plaza. At the head was the person in the property management uniform. They weren't just carrying fuel—they were also hauling two corpses, both in property management uniforms. These must have been the staff on night duty yesterday.","So that's why the property office's phone had gone unanswered.","\"What's going on?\" they asked.","The others told them: \"One of them mutated. These two are injured, we're escorting them over.\"","Jiang Cheng asked, \"Is the meeting room area still all right?\"","The person in uniform glanced at the crowd flooding past and shrank back slightly: \"It's fine. They're keeping an eye on them.\"","Jiang Cheng nodded: \"We'll take them over. You two go ahead and start the burn. Be careful—move any flammable materials away first.\"","The person in uniform worked for the property company itself, so he nodded: \"Don't worry. There's a fire hydrant in the garden.\"","Jiang Cheng gave a slight nod, and the large group escorted the two injured men to the property management office.","The office was located in the basement of one of the buildings. The people on guard duty looked surprised to see so many crowding in: \"What's wrong?\"","The situation was explained briefly, the guards exchanged looks, and their expressions grew graver.","The meeting room had double doors, secured with a U-shaped padlock. But the room had a surveillance camera, and the feed could be viewed on the computer at the reception desk of the property office.","The dozen or so people inside were behaving themselves. Some sat, some had simply lain down on the big conference table, looking utterly bored.","The guard unlocked the U-shaped padlock and pulled the door open.","The people inside, whether sitting or lying down, all stood up: \"What's going on?\"","Jiang Cheng didn't tell them that someone had already been infected and mutated. She only said, \"More people were injured, we're sending them over too.\"","Li Jiangbing and the leader from Building Four each gave a light push, and the man stepped inside reluctantly. The door was immediately shut behind him, the U-lock snapping into place with a click.","But no one left. Including Jiang Cheng, they all stood surrounding the meeting room door, staring at it.","So many people crammed into the hallway that they could barely turn around, yet the silence was terrifying.","Until Jiang Cheng said, \"Come on, let's talk in the lobby.\"","They filed back through the corridor to the property management lobby, still silent.","Jiang Cheng broke the quiet first: \"Our community is lucky.\"","\"Everyone here has their own place.\"","\"In other neighborhoods—the big-unit ones where three generations of five or six people live under one roof—I can't even imagine what's happening there right now.\"","But it was still grim. Everyone knew in their hearts that the people in that meeting room were as good as dead.","Some worried about whether that door could actually hold a person who'd mutated. Those who'd been infected before mutating were far stronger than the original mutants.","A few even harbored the thought of \"dealing with\" those people right now. But they didn't dare say it aloud, restrained by the baseline of social morality.","Jiang Cheng changed the subject and told the guards about the shift rotation they'd agreed on: \"We'll come eat and then take over for you. You go home and have your meals yourselves.\"","For now, \"having a meal\" still meant going back to your own place. Whether you stewed ribs or had instant noodles depended on how much you'd stocked up.","Given the current circumstances, the fact that Jiang Cheng could organize the manpower and get them to follow her direction was already a feat. So far, no one in this community had any ability to mobilize supplies.","Jiang Cheng noticed another person in a property management uniform in the lobby. She asked, \"Is there any food here? We can't just not feed them either.\"","The property management staff member said, \"I think there might be some. Let me look.\"","She rummaged while muttering, \"I remember that person just bought a box of ham sausages... and that one has instant noodles over there...\"","Sure enough, she pulled out an unopened box of ham sausages and a few packs of instant noodles from a colleague's desk cabinet.","Seeing these things, someone's stomach growled at an inopportune moment.","Everyone turned to look — it was the big burly guy from Building Two.","Jiang Cheng understood exactly why Li Jiangbing's stomach was rumbling — he had no supplies at home. What he'd scavenged from Room 0308 yesterday wasn't much, and it clearly couldn't match his massive frame. It wasn't nearly enough to fill his stomach.","Jiang Cheng picked up the box cutter on the table and sliced open the ham sausage carton, then casually grabbed a handful of sausages and held them out to everyone: \"You're all hungry, right? Have something to tide you over.\"","One by one, people reached out and took a sausage from her hand — one each.","When only three were left, Jiang Cheng shoved them all into Li Jiangbing's hands. He and she exchanged a knowing glance, and as everyone else was busy peeling off the red plastic wrappers, he slipped the sausages into his pocket.","Of course, not everyone missed it. Someone couldn't help but glance at him. But given Li Jiangbing's sheer size, those who noticed had enough sense not to question \"why does he get more\" at that moment.","Jiang Cheng patted the remaining half box: \"These are for the meeting...\"","Her voice cut off abruptly. \"What's that?\" she asked.","Everyone followed her gaze. The reception counter was higher on the outside and lower on the inside, like a front desk in a company. Because someone had been looking for scissors to open their sausage wrapper and created a gap, Jiang Cheng caught sight of what was piled up on the inner side of the counter.","One of the guards said, \"We figured since they were going inside for observation, we'd have them leave all their things here first.\"","Stacked behind the counter were clubs, cleavers, and hardware tools. They were the weapons of the first group locked inside — confiscated by the guards.","Everyone felt that was exactly as it should be.","But Jiang Cheng rested her chin in her hand.","The room was filled with the sound of chewing. Everyone had fought hard all morning, burning through their energy, and they were all hungry.","As they ate, Jiang Cheng spoke up: \"Send these in too.\"","She singled out the cleavers and the serrated knives, pushing them aside, leaving the blunt objects — \"these\" being what she meant.","\"It's unlikely they'd all mutate at once,\" she said. \"This way, if one of them changes, the others can handle it themselves without us having to go back in and risk danger.\"","The chewing in the room suddenly stopped.","Li Jiangbing had just crammed an entire sausage into his mouth, his cheeks puffed out, and even he froze at those words.","If that happened, what would the meeting room become? Just imagining it sent a chill of cold sweat down the back of everyone's neck.","But the girl who'd made this decision didn't seem to realize she was tossing desperate worms into a doomed jar of fighting crickets.","Her eyes were black and white, clear and bright: \"Our first principle is to protect the normal people who haven't been infected or mutated.\"","Who could argue with that?","Everyone also wanted to protect themselves. They were exactly the \"normal people who hadn't been infected or mutated.\"","No one spoke out against it. Many silently lowered their eyes and resumed chewing, only the artificial flavoring of the ham sausages now hitting so strong it killed their appetite.","It almost made them want to vomit."]},{"number":15,"title":"Chapter 15","paragraphs":["The knives and other blades weren't sent in, partly for fear that they'd break the door open from the inside. And partly because if anything went wrong, the normal people on their side might get hurt.","As for water, there was no need to worry—there was a water dispenser in the meeting room.","The bathroom issue had been resolved from the very beginning. When the first batch of injured had been escorted over, they'd asked, \"How are we supposed to use the toilet?\"","It was also the property management girl who'd found two large plastic buckets for them.","Everyone had filled their stomachs with ham sausages for now, but Jiang Cheng was looking at the surveillance feed of the meeting room on her computer. She watched for a moment, then raised her head: \"When we send things in later, we need to be on full alert.\"","\"They're too quiet,\" she said. \"Once those two go in and explain the situation, once everyone knows what's what, there's no way they'd all stay this calm.\"","\"This isn't right. Something's off.\"","Li Jiangbing forced down the meat in his mouth and said, \"Whatever you say.\"","Following Jiang Cheng's arrangement, when they unlocked the U-shaped lock and opened the door, a circle of people stood in a semi-arc around the meeting room entrance. Their various \"weapons\" were all pointed at the door.","Some people inwardly grumbled about whether it was really necessary. But then the door opened—and the people inside charged out!","Li Jiangbing was ready. He swung his baton hard, cracking it across the man's shoulder, then drove it straight into his chest, and finally kicked him back in!","These moves were one fluid motion, done in an instant, completely squashing the plan of those inside to break out.","The two sides faced off—","\"Let us out! Let us out!\"","\"I don't want to die!\"","\"Back off! Back off!\"","\"If you don't back off, I'll hit someone!\"","Men's shouting filled both sides of the door, deafening in the narrow corridor.","Weapons were thrust out toward the doorway, ready to stop anyone from charging again.","At that moment, everyone thought: Jiang Cheng from Building 2 really had called it.","Jiang Cheng stood in the middle. Li Jiangbing stepped aside, revealing her.","She locked eyes with the man Li Jiangbing had kicked back in. She'd guessed it was him—he was one of the leaders from Building 6, and he'd been bitten on the arm. Earlier in the square, when Jiang Cheng had demanded that all the injured be kept together under supervision, he'd been the first among the injured to speak up in support.","Back then he'd said: \"If I do end up turning, I don't want to hurt anyone. You can just put me down directly.\"","When he'd said that, he probably still believed there was a way out. But when you're truly confirmed to have only one ending, people's minds shift.","A creature's instinct is to survive—even if it means \"surviving\" in another form.","The unnatural calm in the meeting room told Jiang Cheng that someone was controlling the situation, persuading the others to stay low and wait for their chance.","He was a man in his twenties, well-groomed hair, handsome face, great physique, and good fashion sense. His clothes were brand-name.","He looked like a well-paid white-collar professional with a respectable job. In daily life, probably a charismatic man.","But none of that mattered. The wound on his arm was already bandaged, but he was doomed to die.","Jiang Cheng's voice cut through the shouting.","\"Step back,\" she said. \"We're here to bring you food.\"","\"You have two choices: take the food and close the door.\"","\"Or we shut the door right now.\"","Back in the square, this girl had stepped up on her own initiative. Now, she appeared to have fully taken command.","The man from Building 6 gritted his teeth and stared at her, his face ugly.","Behind him, someone was already crying, fidgeting in frustration.","Then the girl from Building 2 began to count down: \"Three... two...\"","\"Fine!\" he barked just before she reached one. \"We'll take it. Bring it in.\"","Things had deteriorated to this point—neighbors at each other's throats. No one wanted to \"go in.\" They said some AIDS patients went around sticking people with needles—who knew whether these people might also out of resentment bite someone just to spread it? If you got bitten, you'd be stuck in there with them.","\"Back behind the table, or we're closing the door now,\" Jiang Cheng said.","The way out was sealed—no telling how many people were crammed into the corridor, everyone armed, all of them having killed mutants that day.","There was no way out. But they couldn't starve either. After a hard morning and nothing but water in that room, they really were hungry.","Nobody wanted to die on an empty stomach either. The people inside slumped back behind the meeting table, heads hung low.","The ham sausages and instant noodles were thrown in. They clattered onto the table, sausages scattering everywhere, some rolling to the floor.","The people inside scrambled frantically—over the table, onto the floor—to grab them.","Morale was broken, the scene was chaos, and the man from Building 6 got shoved aside by the crush. He reached out to steady himself against the wall.","He turned to glance back at the door, only to see the people outside toss a few things in with a clatter, landing on the floor on that side of the meeting table.","Then the meeting room door was slammed shut, and the U-shaped lock clicked into place quickly.","From outside came a voice: \"Move that cabinet from the hall over here...\"","Inside, a man bit into a ham sausage and asked curiously: \"Why'd they give our weapons back?\"","Scattered on the floor near the door were the weapons that had been confiscated from them earlier.","Outside, the sound of moving large furniture and the bump of it against the door began.","The man from Building 6 stared at those weapons for a long time. Then he gave a bitter smile.","A group of people walked out of the property management center. It was already midday—the sun was strong and the temperature had risen.","Yet there was a chill in everyone's hearts. Even with the blazing sun at their backs, it felt cold.","The girl walking in the lead had glossy black hair that shimmered in the sunlight. She was beautiful too, conventionally attractive.","But she... wasn't exactly \"conventional.\"","Li Jiangbing rubbed his neck, as if to brush away that subtle discomfort. He glanced to the side and noticed that everyone had either naturally or deliberately let Jiang Cheng take the center position.","But their expressions weren't entirely natural.","Someone let out a sigh: \"That guy lives on my floor.\"","Killing the mutants hadn't felt like this. But locking what still looked like perfectly human people inside that meeting room—that was hard to stomach.","Li Jiangbing stole a glance at Jiang Cheng's profile. She seemed unmoved.","Someone else chimed in: \"What else can you do? There are so many people in this complex. If you don't contain it, one bites another, one infects another, and everyone's done for.\"","Li Jiangbing saw Jiang Cheng turn slightly to look at the person who said that.","It wasn't someone else—it was the leader from Building 4. A tall young man, sharp and alert, handsome as well. Earlier in the square, when Jiang Cheng had given him a look, he'd picked it up immediately.","They'd exchanged names before—his was Song Jingshuo.","Li Jiangbing saw approval flicker in Jiang Cheng's eyes, but then she turned back, as if lost in thought.","What was she thinking about?","The square was already burning. Flames shot into the sky, and even from a distance, they could feel the wave of heat.","Fire... it was a truly terrifying thing.","The number of people in the square didn't shrink; it grew. Those who had been watching from their homes, seeing that the mutated individuals in the neighborhood had mostly been cleared, now felt bold enough to come downstairs.","People who had been in the garden all along and those who had just emerged from their buildings were exchanging information with one another.","One side was telling the other about the precautions for killing the mutated, while the other side was sharing what the broadcast news had said and what new updates had appeared online.","Many people were coming downstairs now because they were afraid that if they didn't join the group in the garden, they'd be left behind—unable to get timely information, easily marginalized when something happened.","Humans are, after all, social animals. Herd animals.","The fire burned fiercely. These were all neighbors. Many had been seen and encountered in the neighborhood before. They'd shared elevators, some had worked in the same area or even the same office building, and some had even formed carpool groups together.","Now familiar faces were being incinerated. Their families had no idea that they had already died here.","Someone couldn't hold back their tears.","Men and women alike.","This community was mainly made up of young people who had left home to fend for themselves. Seeing their neighbors being burned, many felt as if they were looking at themselves.","Li Jiangbing let out a sigh and, out of habit, turned to look at Jiang Cheng. But he saw her gathered with Song Jingshuo and the leaders of the other buildings, talking about something.","Li Jiangbing snapped to attention and hurried over to eavesdrop.","\"This has to be the priority. It's the most urgent thing right now. Everything else can wait,\" Jiang Cheng said firmly. \"This afternoon is crucial. Tomorrow won't work.\"","Li Jiangbing didn't dare interrupt to ask what it was about; he just pricked up his ears and listened.","Song Jingshuo said, \"What if they haven't opened the doors?\"","Jiang Cheng said, \"We have numbers, and we have tools. Breaking down a door isn't hard.\"","Someone let out an \"ah\" sound, tinged with hesitation.","Jiang Cheng's gaze shot over. Li Jiangbing could swear her eyes seemed to say, \"You've already killed people, so what's a little more?\"","But Jiang Cheng didn't say it outright. Instead, she said, \"Everything happening now falls under the principle of emergency necessity.\"","Apartment residents in this young-people's complex tended to be young and, on the whole, well educated.","Someone like Song Jingshuo, or the former leader from Building 6 who had been locked in the meeting room and tried to lead a charge out—these were clearly people with good education and sharp minds.","When Jiang Cheng mentioned \"the principle of emergency necessity,\" the building leaders all accepted the idea and nodded in agreement.","But not everyone was highly educated. Unfortunately, Li Jiangbing happened to be the one dragging down the average educational level of the neighborhood.","He had no idea what \"the principle of emergency necessity\" meant. He scratched his head in frustration and finally couldn't hold back, blurting out, \"What are you talking about?\"","Jiang Cheng turned to see him and raised an eyebrow. \"Perfect timing. I have something to say to everyone. Jiangbing, help me shout a few lines and get everyone's attention.\"","Oh, she orders him around like it's second nature.","Li Jiangbing felt oddly reassured, cheerfully agreeing: \"Alright.\"","The large crowd of residents in the central plaza was immersed in restless unease and an oppressive, unspoken gloom when suddenly a booming voice like a copper gong roared out: \"Over here—! Everyone come over—! There's something important to announce—!\"","Everyone turned their heads and saw the building leaders gathered under the vine-covered pergola beside the central plaza.","The girl from Building 2, Jiang Cheng, stood on a bench in the pavilion, tall and poised, sweeping her gaze over the crowd.","\"I'm Jiang Cheng from Building 2, the main contact person for our community's interim owners' committee,\" she said.","She deliberately avoided a title like \"leader\" that might invite challenges, choosing instead to call herself the \"contact person.\" Song Jingshuo and Li Jiangbing both glanced at her.","\"...There's a lot to do,\" Jiang Cheng said from her elevated spot. \"Sealing the various entrances to the complex, dealing with the corpses in the buildings, sweeping each floor door to door to root out any mutated that slipped through—these are all urgent.\"","\"But there's one thing that's the most urgent of all, and it must be done right now.\"","\"Our community needs to organize itself immediately and use this afternoon to go to the Duoduo Supermarket and stock up on emergency supplies!\"","\"Rice, flour, oil, salt, sugar! Toilet paper! These essential things!\"","\"Only this afternoon—it absolutely has to be this afternoon!\"","Sure enough, voices of doubt rose from the crowd: \"Why?\"","Jiang Cheng's gaze landed on them. \"Because this is our community's greatest advantage.\"","\"Our community,\" she raised her hand and began counting off on her fingers one by one for everyone, \"is young, well-educated, quick to rally, strong in action, and can use the internet to communicate information. Also, most of us live alone, so we have room for individual isolation, which means the rate of secondary infection from attacks by the mutated is extremely low!\"","\"Think about those communities where three generations live under one roof, with five or six people in a single household. There's no way they could clear out their mutated and create a safe environment the way our community did in one morning.\"","\"I estimate that most communities won't be able to do it until tonight at the earliest.\"","\"That means this afternoon, a lot of people simply can't leave their own neighborhoods. This afternoon is time that our community's residents earned by using our own strengths.\"","\"By tomorrow, when large numbers of people start coming out to stock up, our advantage will be gone.\"","\"So it has to be today—this very afternoon—that we, the residents of this young-people's apartment complex, organize ourselves and go out to buy supplies!\""]},{"number":16,"title":"Chapter 16","paragraphs":["Someone spoke up hesitantly: \"Do we really have to go?\"","The community had been cleared, but no one knew what was outside. The owners who came down later had heard from those who'd fought about how the injured were dealt with, and they couldn't help feeling afraid.","Many of those who came down later didn't have the same nerve as the first batch.","\"Didn't the government say to stay indoors as much as possible?\"","\"Nobody's forcing you. It's completely voluntary,\" Jiang Cheng said. \"But I'm going, even if it's just me alone.\"","She pointed: \"Turn around and look, everyone.\"","They all turned their heads. Behind them, roaring flames consumed the bodies of their neighbors. It looked like something straight out of a disaster movie.","\"In the past, major natural disasters were regional. The nation could immediately mobilize forces and supplies from other areas to converge for relief,\" Jiang Cheng said. \"But this time it's not just nationwide—it's a virus.\"","\"Viruses don't care if you're a cop, a soldier, or a truck driver hauling supplies. Once you're infected, you turn into a mindless monster, and the people around you have no choice but to kill you to stay alive.\"","\"Take the military—huge numbers of people packed into confined spaces living in high density. In a situation like this, those places are bound to become disaster zones.\"","Jiang Cheng said: \"Of course I believe the government isn't going to just abandon us. Last night in the middle of the night I already heard police sirens and ambulances. So I know plenty of remarkable people are still holding the line.\"","\"But when every profession, every region is losing people across the board, how many days is it going to take for government rescue to reach us this time?\"","\"How many days can the food in your home last?\"","She stared down at the person who'd spoken and demanded: \"Tell me, how many days can you last?\"","The owners buzzed with murmuring.","\"My home doesn't have any food at all. I finished all the potato chips yesterday.\"","\"All I have is instant noodles and frozen dumplings, and they're almost gone after this morning.\"","\"She's right.\"","In a community full of single young people, very few cooked for themselves regularly. Most just boiled some dumplings or made instant noodles.","Nobody had surplus food.","Jiang Cheng said: \"The news said to stay home as much as possible, and a lot of people will listen. If we don't take advantage of this window to stock up first, by the time everyone else catches on and swarms the supermarkets—this big a city, this many people—do you think the stores' stock will be enough to go around?\"","\"But supply chains will definitely be affected. At least for the next few days, until the nation can effectively mobilize manpower and resources, our city is going to be running on whatever inventory is left.\"","\"We're not forcing anyone. We're just putting the call out.\"","\"To all owners willing to join the supply run: arm yourselves appropriately, take precautions, bring weapons and bags or handcarts. Assemble at the east gate open area at 2 PM.\"","\"We leave at 2 sharp. No waiting for latecomers.\"","With that, Jiang Cheng hopped down from the bench and let the crowd discuss and debate among themselves.","She conferred with Song Jingshuo about the practical details—as she said, there really was plenty to handle.","Luckily, the property management worker who'd led them to move fuel from the office had joined them, and with him around, a lot of things became much easier.","Song Jingshuo praised him: \"The fact that you can still show up for work—that's pretty impressive.\"","The community had two main gates, east and west. According to him, the security guards on both sides were still on duty.","He was a middle-aged man in his forties, wearing a blue short-sleeved work uniform. His surname was Luo. Jiang Cheng recognized him—she often saw him carrying a toolbox around the neighborhood, always moving in quick little trots.","He seemed to fill several roles at once: he'd changed a light switch in her apartment and unclogged the drain for her too. A very capable handyman.","Master Luo said: \"Well, the leadership never said we could skip work.\"","Without an official word saying you didn't have to come, what if you didn't show and they docked your pay later? Who dared take that risk?","The property management had dorms. They used the basement level of one of the buildings, and the dorms were there too. Last night, they'd been lucky: the person on shift mutated, but nobody in the dorms did.","\"What about your boss?\" Jiang Cheng asked.","\"Nowhere to be seen. Phones ring, nobody picks up.\" Master Luo sighed.","The boss didn't live in the dorms—he had his own home and came to work every day. But if they still couldn't reach him now...","Most likely, it wasn't good news.","Master Luo said: \"The customer service supervisor can still be reached. She's at home—says the area outside her building is full of mutants and she can't get out. I'm in charge of the engineering department, and me and the security captain both lived in the dorms. But he was on duty last night and mutated. Sigh...\"","So the body dragged out of the property office was the security captain.","\"Master Luo, that makes you the only person left in charge at the property office. You need to take it over,\" Jiang Cheng said. \"I remember your office has a kitchen, right?\"","She'd seen property staff packing hot meals in lunchboxes—freshly cooked, not cold boxed meals delivered from outside.","Master Luo nodded: \"We do. My wife is the cook.\"","Jiang Cheng asked: \"How long can the kitchen's food supply last?\"","Master Luo said: \"We have rice and flour. Vegetables are delivered by the market every other day—they didn't deliver today. Meat is fine; we have some in the freezer.\"","Jiang Cheng paused for a moment: \"Master Luo, there are two things you need to take responsibility for.\"","\"Go on.\"","\"First, you need to make sure the property staff get fed.\"","\"Mmm, of course. No one should go hungry.\"","\"Second, you and your wife need to figure out how many days the kitchen's rice and flour will last. If it's less than five days, I suggest your department send someone to join us on the supermarket run this afternoon.\"","Master Luo agreed and left a few people to watch the fire, then hurried off to find his wife.","Jiang Cheng and Song Jingshuo then worked out the details: first eat, then send people to relieve the ones on duty at the property office, and arrange for the building reps to buy supplies for the people stuck in the meeting room.","These were the kind of concrete, nitty-gritty arrangements. Li Jiangbing hated tedious details like this. But he was afraid of being left behind by this group, so he just kept hovering, squeezing in next to Jiang Cheng to listen.","Jiang Cheng had noticed him long before, but she said nothing.","When everything that needed to be said had been said, everyone went back to their own buildings. Jiang Cheng rode the elevator with a few people from Building 2, and she and Li Jiangbing got off on the third floor.","As the elevator door closed and it rose again, she said to Li Jiangbing: \"The guy who mutated, and the two who got injured later—you can check their apartments for food. If there's nothing, come by my place. I still have a bit to spare.\"","Li Jiangbing had actually been thinking about food just then—what he'd scavenged from apartment 0308 yesterday was long gone. The fact that Jiang Cheng was still looking out for him made him happy.","Li Jiangbing didn't have much education, but he had plenty of street smarts, and he understood well the principle of staying close to the core group during major events.","What was interesting was that his female neighbor on the same floor had gotten herself into—dominated, even—the core circle from the very start. She understood that principle better than he did.","\"I saw that guy's place—he's got quite a bit of stuff. I'm heading over now. He's on the fifth floor. Better not let someone else get there first.\"","\"Good. Stay in touch by phone.\"","Li Jiangbing walked a few steps before something felt off. He turned around to look. Jiang Cheng was standing behind him, staring at the fire hydrant on the wall.","\"What are you doing?\"","The words had barely left Li Jiangbing's mouth when he saw Jiang Cheng raise the baseball bat in her hand and smash the glass of the fire hydrant case with a single swing. Shards clattered to the ground.","Jiang Cheng reached inside, pulled out the fire axe, and weighed it in her hand. She set down the bat, gripped the axe with both hands, and gave it a few practice swings. She nodded in satisfaction: \"This is good.\"","There were two axes in the case. She handed one to Li Jiangbing: \"For you.\"","Then she took out the other for herself.","\"I've been observing. As long as you crush the head or sever the neck, the mutated ones die. Sharp weapons work better than blunt ones. We should upgrade our gear.\" Jiang Cheng told Li Jiangbing.","Li Jiangbing's paired batons looked cool, but if you didn't know the proper forms and were just swinging them around like fire pokers, they didn't have the same striking power as Jiang Cheng's baseball bat.","Li Jiangbing happily gripped the fire axe: \"You're right. I was just thinking about finding a kitchen knife.\"","An inch shorter, an inch more danger; an inch longer, an inch more strength. This was even better than a knife.","They reached the door of Jiang Cheng's home. She had already pulled out her keys and unlocked the door, one foot already stepping inside, when Li Jiangbing suddenly asked, \"Jiang Cheng, you're a manager at your company, aren't you?\"","Jiang Cheng paused, turned her head to look at him, and answered vaguely: \"Mm, just a small supervisor.\"","\"I knew it. You've got the look of someone used to being in charge.\"","\"Go on, hurry up.\"","\"Alright. I'll call you later.\"","\"Okay.\"","Jiang Cheng went back into her own home and closed the door.","The mirror behind the door had shattered during last night's struggle with Shen Wei, with only a small piece still clinging to the door.","Jiang Cheng looked at herself in the mirror.","She had lied.","\"Jiang Cheng\" was just an ordinary employee at the company. Her income wasn't substantial—enough to get by, nothing more. She bought this apartment with her parents' inheritance. She wasn't like Song Jingshuo from Building Four or the injured person from Building Six, who you could tell at a glance were elite types.","So who was it that loved being in charge so much, whose first instinct was to take control?","The mirror reflected half a face.","Was it \"me\"?","A transmigrator?","Jiang Cheng stared at that half face for a moment, then locked the door. She went to check on Mo Li by the bed first.","Mo Li was motionless, like he was dead.","Jiang Cheng carefully touched him. He was ice cold.","In that instant, Jiang Cheng's heart felt ice cold too.","Thankfully, it was only for that one instant. The next second, Mo Li opened his eyes! Still alive!","Why was he so cold? A cat's body temperature should be higher than a human's.","Jiang Cheng hurried to get some warm water and fed it to Mo Li. He swallowed it all down. Then she soaked his cat food in warm water and fed him that too. He ate it.","But Mo Li's body temperature wouldn't go up. Not at all like before, when he had been burning hot with fever.","It was as if all his energy had been drained.","She used a hair dryer to blow his fur warm, but the moment she turned it off, he quickly cooled down again.","What could she do?","Jiang Cheng remembered seeing in period dramas how northerners used their own body heat to warm up people suffering from hypothermia, continuously transferring warmth.","Jiang Cheng opened the wardrobe and found a long-sleeved shirt. She took off her t-shirt, looped the sleeves of the shirt diagonally across one armpit and over the opposite shoulder, fashioning a simple baby sling. She carefully placed Mo Li against her chest, his soft, black fur pressed against her bare skin, using her own body to keep transferring heat to the little cat.","She carried Mo Li this way while posting a contact thread on the forum, and she ate a simple meal with him nestled against her.","After eating, she checked the thread again. The contact person from each building had replied, registering their building number, apartment number, messaging app ID, and phone number.","Jiang Cheng entered all their phone numbers into her contacts.","As it happened, this year, the communication app everyone commonly used had rolled out a \"group\" feature. It was still in beta, but all you had to do was update the version and you could use it. It was perfectly timed.","Jiang Cheng created a group in the app and pulled these people in.","Once everyone was in, the first message she sent was: 【Each building should create its own group. This group is for main contacts only.】","Every building had three to four contacts. Everyone replied in succession:","【Okay.】","【On it now.】","【I'm ready to head downstairs. How about you all?】","Jiang Cheng glanced at the time: 【I'm getting ready to head down too.】","Jiang Cheng found her biggest backpack, and also pulled out her shopping cart. With Mo Li still strapped to her chest, she pulled her t-shirt back on directly over him, wrapping him inside the fabric.","Luckily, the t-shirt had some stretch to it, so it could accommodate the lump.","The door suddenly knocked: \"Jiang Cheng, Jiang Cheng, you going down?\"","It was Li Jiangbing's voice.","Jiang Cheng replied with an \"Coming,\" tucked the fire axe into her waistband at the back, then shouldered her backpack and went to open the door.","Li Jiangbing looked at her, dumbfounded: \"What's that?\"","Jiang Cheng patted the bulging bundle on her chest: \"My cat.\"","It was working. Kept in constant contact, Mo Li's body wasn't so cold anymore.","The little cat should make it."]},{"number":17,"title":"Chapter 17","paragraphs":["Through the contact list posted on the owners' forum, the contacts from each building had exchanged personal information and contact details, and joined the group chat.","By the time they regrouped in the afternoon, everyone had already grown familiar with one another.","Jiang Cheng's getup was utterly ridiculous, but under the current circumstances, laughter was hardly appropriate—the pile of corpses in the square still hadn't been burned away, still billowing smoke and reeking.","No one actually laughed anyway. Song Jingshuo asked, speechless: \"What is that?\"","The backpack, the hand cart, and the fire axe at her waist were all understandable, but whatever was bulging inside her clothes was anyone's guess.","Jiang Cheng had to explain: \"My cat got spooked and went into stress. I have to keep him with me, or he might get scared to death.\"","Cat owners knew full well how easily cats could suffer from stress. But Song Jingshuo gave Jiang Cheng a look.","Jiang Cheng: \"What?\"","Song Jingshuo shook his head and said, \"That doesn't seem like your style.\"","Jiang Cheng tugged at the corner of her mouth: \"We've known each other for less than six hours.\"","At that, everyone suddenly realized she was right. They had only known each other for a few hours. Fewer than half of them could remember each other's names.","Yet everyone could say Jiang Cheng's name, everyone knew she lived in Building 2, Unit 0306.","And when Song Jingshuo said \"that doesn't seem like your style,\" everyone silently agreed. Because in their minds, Jiang Cheng was different from the other neighbors whose faces and personalities were still vague—her image was too clear.","The coldness of using a gentle voice to tell people to put down their weapons and go wait for death in the property management conference room, contrasted with her refusal to abandon a pet—the contrast was simply too stark.","Jiang Cheng patted Mo Li through her clothes, mixing truth with lies: \"My parents passed away. He's my only family.\"","Everyone nodded in understanding, accepting the explanation.","But someone hesitated, then still asked Jiang Cheng: \"Are you sure it's just stress? Couldn't he have been infected by the virus like the others?\"","Jiang Cheng's heart tightened.","Bitten, transformed, enlarged—Jiang Cheng was already fairly certain Mo Li had been infected, but his mutation direction was different from humans.","After mutating, not only had his physiological parameters strengthened, but he also retained his sanity.","From last night until now, Jiang Cheng had never observed mutants attacking other mutants. This suggested that mutants recognized each other through some means—maybe scent, maybe something else—but Mo Li and Shen Wei did not recognize each other. They each refused to accept the other as their own kind.","Mo Li's mutation was an entirely different kind of mutation.","One could even call it evolution.","But under the current circumstances, with everyone on edge and seeing threats everywhere, speaking up wouldn't necessarily win trust. They might treat him like those people in the conference room.","For humans who still retained their sanity and hadn't started mutating, people could still allow them observation time.","But if the subject was a cat, there was no reason to grant such treatment. If Jiang Cheng herself were in that situation without knowing the full story, she would rather kill by mistake than let one get away.","\"Of course not.\" Jiang Cheng looked the person straight in the eye. \"Last night, an injured person I was helping mutated in my apartment. I fought her off, and it scared the cat.\"","From morning till now, everything she said hit the mark and carried conviction.","Everyone nodded, believing her.","The owners gathered one by one.","Master Luo also arrived, brows furrowed: \"My wife said the cafeteria's food storage is only enough for the rest of us for one day. We were supposed to do a restock today, but all this delayed it.\"","Jiang Cheng said, \"Then arrange a few people to go with us for supplies.\"","Sure enough, Master Luo looked troubled: \"Well, we don't have money...\"","Jiang Cheng had already anticipated this.","Master Luo said, \"The manager can't be reached, and the accountant didn't come in today—she said she didn't dare go out.\"","Jiang Cheng said, \"No problem. Tell everyone that I'll cover the cost of food and supplies for the property staff.\"","Master Luo was overjoyed: \"Oh, really? How about that—how could we...\"","Whoever's bowl you eat from, you listen to their words.","Jiang Cheng had her calculations.","But others understood that logic too, and had their own calculations.","Song Jingshuo cut in: \"It's not appropriate for you to do it alone. How about this, Master Luo—tell everyone that the cost for the property supplies will be covered jointly by Song Jingshuo from Building 4 and Jiang Cheng from Building 2, each paying half.\"","Everything about Song Jingshuo screamed brand name, from his belt to his whole bearing—the epitome of a young elite, the kind who spoke in a way that made people feel at ease. He looked like someone with excellent education who had entered a major corporation at a young age as a promising talent.","After returning home today, he had reviewed what had happened and realized that anything Jiang Cheng could think of, he could think of too, and any decision Jiang Cheng could steel herself to make, he could make as well.","But he had been one step behind Jiang Cheng at every turn. Jiang Cheng was always the first to think of something and the first to make the right call without hesitation, and by noon, everything had revolved around Jiang Cheng as the core and leader.","Yet when the first wave came down from the buildings to bravely clear the garden, she hadn't even been there.","The pace had been set by her the entire time. It was only when he got home and reviewed things that Song Jingshuo felt the frustration.","Because he too was someone who liked to take the initiative, who didn't enjoy following someone else's lead.","Jiang Cheng glanced at Song Jingshuo, and their eyes met with mutual understanding. Similar people understand each other better.","Jiang Cheng gave a slight smile: \"Fine, then the two of us will cover it together.\"","There was nothing to fight over at the moment. No actual interests were at stake yet—just the authority to coordinate and lead. No need to compete; cooperation was the priority.","Song Jingshuo nodded slightly. Cooperation first.","Master Luo happily went off, called two young security guards, dragged out the property management's flatbed cart—three people in total, including himself, enough.","By around 2 PM, the east gate was packed with a surging crowd of owners, easily over a thousand. Though some had questioned earlier, Jiang Cheng had hit the key point: many single young people had no habit of stocking up, and at home their food supplies truly couldn't last.","If they didn't seize this organized large-scale group trip to stock up now, they wouldn't dare go alone later.","So even those who were reluctant didn't dare not show up.","Naturally, some still hadn't come. The whole complex shouldn't have only this many people.","Master Luo handed Jiang Cheng a megaphone, and she stood on a high point and began to speak:","\"Right now we don't know the situation on the streets. Everyone, stay close and keep pace with the group. Those of you with protective gear, try to stay on the outer perimeter and stay alert at all times.\"","\"None of us knows how long this situation will last. Personally, I suggest not buying snacks or the like. Our carrying capacity is limited, so focus on survival supplies—rice, flour, oil, salt, sugar, toilet paper, and so on.\"","\"If you don't have a hand cart, buy one first thing after entering the supermarket.\"","She only hit the key points without rambling. As she jumped down and steadied herself, Song Jingshuo reached out and took the megaphone: \"Everyone, be considerate. Keep the female owners toward the middle.\"","Jiang Cheng glanced back at him.","Someone objected: \"Why should we? My life matters too.\"","Song Jingshuo didn't argue with him either, only smiling with a hint of sarcasm: \"You can walk in the middle, too.\"","A chorus of boos rose from the crowd.","Li Jiangbing jumped up and cursed: \"Are you a real man? Look at you, all cowardly!\"","The man muttered and shuffled two steps back, disappearing into the crowd.","At 2 o'clock sharp, the young residents of the apartment complex stood ready to go.","After a morning of fighting, many people had gained experience and made as much protection as they could.","Some used tape to bind magazines to their forearms as makeshift bracers, so that if a mutant charged and tried to bite, they could block it. Paper isn't so easy to bite through, after all.","Some wore motorcycle helmets to protect their necks and faces.","There were even a few in ice hockey gear, which seemed incredibly practical for the current situation — the kind of thing that made everyone envious. But those were rare cases; a city wouldn't have many people who played ice hockey.","The security guard opened the main gate and even cheered them on: \"Go early, come back safe, stay alert!\"","Regardless of whether they'd agreed with this plan before, when a large group of people gathered to do something together, it was impossible not to feel one's blood run hot.","Many people raised clubs, cleavers, and hammers, letting out wild whoops, full of morale as they set off.","Song Jingshuo called out: \"Jiang Cheng, you should walk in the middle.\"","His voice was loud, and everyone knew Jiang Cheng anyway, so a lot of people looked over.","Jiang Cheng had Mo Li tucked in her arms, a backpack on her back, a hand cart trailing from her left hand, and with her right hand she reached behind her waist, pulled the fire axe from her belt, and swung it in an X-shaped arc through the air.","\"I don't need it,\" she said.","The two swings she made whistled with force. The fire axe looked light in her hands.","What a strong girl, many people thought. No wonder she dared to be so brave.","Li Jiangbing pressed close to Jiang Cheng: \"It's fine, I'm right here.\"","He'd also switched his weapon to a fire axe, and on his left arm he wore a small shield that looked like some kind of merchandise from a game or movie — unclear whether it would actually offer any real protection. But with an axe in one hand, a shield on the other, tall and muscular, his silhouette was genuinely intimidating.","Standing next to Jiang Cheng, he looked like her bodyguard.","Song Jingshuo couldn't figure out how Jiang Cheng had managed to win over such a big man. The protectiveness he showed toward her was unmistakable.","Wherever he appeared, he always stayed close to Jiang Cheng, standing right by her side. Jiang Cheng also casually called him by the last two characters of his name, and while the two didn't look like a couple, they were clearly closer than anyone else here.","Could he be trying to court Jiang Cheng?","Song Jingshuo thought contemptuously. Women always have that advantage.","Watching Song Jingshuo walk off with the others, Li Jiangbing leaned in close to Jiang Cheng and whispered sneakily: \"Why does he always have such an attitude with you? Is he trying to chase you?\"","But Jiang Cheng understood someone like Song Jingshuo more deeply than Li Jiangbing ever could. Because she was the same kind of person. Even though Song Jingshuo looked tall, handsome, and well-off, Jiang Cheng felt not the slightest tinge of attraction toward him. Her mind was entirely focused on grasping the situation at hand and securing her own safety.","She glanced sideways at Li Jiangbing: \"I think he thinks you're trying to chase me.\"","That was a bit of a mouthful. Li Jiangbing took a second to process it, then exclaimed in shock: \"I don't mean that at all.\"","Absolutely not.","He liked soft, cute girls. Before, when he'd run into Jiang Cheng in the hallway, he'd thought she looked sweet and pretty, which was why he'd wanted to strike up a conversation.","But now, what was burned into his mind was the image from last night in the hallway — Jiang Cheng shouting \"Clear the way!\" as she gripped her bat and charged forward, smashing the mutant to the ground with one hit.","That silhouette of hers left too deep an impression on him.","He absolutely had no intention of courting her. He just wanted to stick with her."]},{"number":18,"title":"Chapter 18","paragraphs":["Aduo Duo was a large warehouse-style supermarket, the biggest one in this newly developed economic zone where the youth apartment complex was located, about eight to nine hundred meters away from the apartments.","Given the sheer number of people in front, by the time the ones at the head entered the supermarket, the ones at the back were only just leaving the residential compound.","After exiting the east gate of the complex, there was a street running between two neighborhoods called Jixiang West Street. Walk along Jixiang West Street for about two to three hundred meters, make a turn, then continue straight on the main road for another five to six hundred meters, and you'd roughly arrive.","The situation outside the complex was far worse than inside. The moment the security guard opened the gate, the people at the front spotted mutant creatures roaming on Jixiang West Street.","Right off the bat, one infected mutant came charging straight at them!","Walking in the front were all fearless fighters—people who had already gained ample experience from the morning's battle, mastered the skills for killing, and had the guts to do it.","Everyone called them the \"Daredevil Squad.\"","That name wasn't coined by Jiang Cheng or Song Jingshuo. It came about when the first squad's volunteers were being recruited—people just started joking and shouting the name out on their own.","The sign-up turnout could even be described as enthusiastic.","Jiang Cheng genuinely felt grateful to be living in a community where the majority were young, educated people.","Youth often means hot blood. Good education means stronger collective spirit and discipline, making people easier to organize.","Jiang Cheng had imagined: if this were an ordinary neighborhood full of families with elderly and children—people with parents to care for and kids to raise—it would probably be really hard to get so many people to move together like this.","As people grow older, they lose that fire. Once they have families, they hesitate and look before they leap, afraid to charge forward.","Jiang Cheng also walked near the front, just slightly behind the Daredevil Squad.","There were plenty of mutants on the street. Actually, anything still moving on the street was a mutant. Yesterday was Saturday—a pleasant summer evening—and way too many people had been out and about.","A lurching first-stage mutant stumbled toward her. Jiang Cheng swung her axe and sliced halfway through the mutant's neck. The head flopped to one side, but since half the neck was still attached, it stumbled, fell over, and then got back up again.","Li Jiangbing stepped in and hacked through the remaining half with his own axe. The mutant's body crumpled to the ground, and the head rolled with a thud toward the crowd behind.","Jiang Cheng heard screams and retching from the rear.","Compared to the massive number of residents, those who had come out to fight in the morning were actually a minority. Although more residents gradually joined in afterward, the vast majority only emerged after the burning mound of corpses.","There was a big difference between seeing already-immobile bodies lying on the ground and watching a living, breathing \"person\" get decapitated right before your eyes.","Some people needed time to adapt.","The Daredevil Squad cleared the path up front, and whenever they got tired, they'd shout for people at the back to move up and take over.","Young people tend to get carried away by adrenaline. Even those who started out tense and nauseated gradually adjusted and began itching for a turn.","By the time they emerged from the side street, the front ranks had already rotated in new faces.","The main road had no living people either. Occasionally a car would race past before the road fell back into silence.","Several cars had crashed into curbs or collided with each other; some had burned down to charred black shells. Inside, you could still see scorched skeletons slumped in the driver's seats.","Seeing scenes like that stirred a desolate feeling in everyone's hearts, as if they were in a disaster movie.","Some first-stage mutants were trapped inside their cars, pounding and roaring as they spotted the massive procession of residents, desperate to get out. Mutants feel no pain, and they've been given boosted strength. They don't know how to open doors, so they battered their heads against the glass until it shattered. But the moment one poked its head out, the residents immediately smashed its skull in.","The young residents of the youth apartment complex cleared the road all the way, and by the time they reached Aduo Duo supermarket, even the people who'd been screaming and gagging at first had started to get used to it.","Partly that was because, although there were plenty of mutants on the road, there were even more residents—it was essentially a steamroll. Those in the front had also taken precautions with protective gear.","Or maybe one person would flounder alone against a mutant, but right beside them, several clubs, hammers, and cleavers would already swing in unison.","Along the way, Jiang Cheng didn't hear of anyone getting hurt.","Eight hundred meters felt like marching with a mighty army.","When the group arrived at the supermarket entrance, they found the doors shut.","Everyone exchanged uneasy looks. \"What do we do?\"","They all turned to look at Jiang Cheng. But this time, Song Jingshuo stepped forward first and said firmly, \"Knock. See if anyone's inside. If someone's there, have them open up. If not, we smash the doors.\"","The entrance was made of thick, heavy glass doors. Thick, admittedly, but still glass. With this many people, they could still break through. A few people glanced at Jiang Cheng, while others slapped the doors hard. \"Anyone in there? Anyone?\"","Lots of voices shouted together, the sound penetrating deep into the building.","Soon, a few workers in supermarket uniforms cautiously peeked out.","Residents spotted them instantly. \"People! People!\"","\"Open up! We want to buy things!\"","\"Open up! We want to spend money!\"","The workers saw that the crowd outside was all living people, not mutants, and hurried over to unlock the floor locks. \"Is it safe out there?\"","The doors opened, and everyone swarmed inside, voices overlapping: \"Are you open for business?\"","Since the customers were already here, how could they not be open? The workers nodded in a daze. \"Y-yes, open.\"","Residents flooded through the entrance, making the workers step aside in surprise.","Jiang Cheng didn't go in right away. She also stepped aside and asked one of the workers, \"Are you all working a normal shift today? Did you come from home?\"","\"I didn't—I live in employee housing, right here in the building.\" The person she asked gestured to someone next to him. \"He's the one who came from home today, rode a motorcycle all the way chased the whole time. Pretty badass.\"","Even Jiang Cheng was taken aback. \"Came from home?\"","The man replied irritably, \"What else am I supposed to do? Can't exactly skip work.\"","As it turned out, his wife had taken the kids to the grandparents' place yesterday, and he'd been home alone having a few drinks, then slept straight through until morning. He'd missed the initial chaos of the night. In the early dawn, the streets were dead quiet, and he had no idea what had happened.","It wasn't until he got on his motorcycle and the engine roar attracted the undead that this guy realized something was wrong. Thanks to his bike's nimble speed and handling, he managed to shake off those half-dead creatures as they chased him.","He went to work.","A strange thought rose in Jiang Cheng's mind: Why couldn't someone just not go to work?","Is going to work more important than living?","The word \"work\" had been floating around her ears since morning. People kept asking over and over, \"Are we really going to work tomorrow?\"","During the day, there were so many urgent, chaotic, tedious matters that Jiang Cheng couldn't spare a moment to think deeply about it. But deep down, she'd been feeling something odd.","Everyone seemed so fixated on \"work.\"","But she wasn't.","\"Work\" wasn't even within the scope of what she was thinking about. Ever since last night, everything she'd thought about was life, safety, and survival.","She understood that fixation, of course. But she felt a strong sense of detachment—like watching a play. You understand the characters and the plot, but there's still a stage separating you from the actors.","Maybe because this wasn't \"Jiang Cheng,\" it was \"me.\"","—The thought flashed through her mind. Li Jiangbing called out to her: \"Jiang Cheng, hurry up.\"","Jiang Cheng said no more and followed the crowd streaming into the supermarket.","Fortunately, the warehouse-style supermarket was big enough that over a thousand people flooding in didn't feel especially cramped. And besides the residents of the youth apartment complex, there really were no other customers.","The shopping carts here were bigger than the ordinary ones in regular supermarkets. Li Jiangbing grabbed two carts—one for himself, one for Jiang Cheng.","Jiang Cheng tucked her handcart underneath the supermarket cart: \"Let's go.\"","The two headed straight for the rice, flour, and cooking oil section.","Many people had taken Jiang Cheng's advice and also made a beeline for the grain and oil aisles. That area took up two full rows of shelving, but it was still packed shoulder-to-shoulder with residents.","Li Jiangbing tried to shove his way deeper in, but Jiang Cheng pulled him back: \"Follow me.\"","She led him to the canned goods section first: \"For fresh meat, buy just a little. Frozen meat is better. But my freezer isn't that big, so it's not worth it. Canned food isn't tasty, but it keeps well.\"","Li Jiangbing was now fully persuaded by her, and what she said made sense.","Just now, walking from the complex to the Buyduo Supermarket, he'd witnessed the situation firsthand. The trip went smoothly only because there were so many of them—there were too many factors of luck, timing, and numbers at play. Otherwise, why didn't other neighborhoods organize a crowd of a thousand to go out?","Without such a large organization, anyone going it alone probably wouldn't have made it through that stretch of road.","The two of them headed straight for the canned goods aisle.","Luncheon meat, corned beef, braised pork, and fish in cans. Not delicious, but the traditional tin-can process contains no preservatives, so it's not actually that bad. In times like these, it's a solid choice.","Then they went to the seasonings aisle for salt and sugar. Fermented bean curd and pickled vegetables—those go well with rice.","Li Jiangbing was a little worried: \"What if they run out of rice later?\"","\"Relax,\" Jiang Cheng said. \"A warehouse this big—they've got enough stock that it won't be cleaned out by just the people in our complex.\"","They also grabbed sanitary pads, shampoo, bar soap, and other daily necessities.","Figuring they had about everything they needed, Jiang Cheng went straight up to a supermarket staff member: \"Open the storage room for us. We're here for the rice, flour, and oil—you can see how many people we have. What's on the shelves won't be enough.\"","In the short time since, the rice, flour, and oil shelves were already nearly bare.","Everyone had grabbed at least one bag of rice.","A big crowd of young people who never cooked at home stared at each other blankly:","\"How long does one bag last?\"","\"I don't know either—let me call my mom and ask.\"","\"What do I do if I don't know how to cook rice?\"","\"Forget whether you can cook it—first tell me, do you have a rice cooker?\"","\"Ah! No! Where do they sell rice cookers? I need to go grab one right now!\"","The supermarket staff were in a situation similar to the property management workers like Uncle Luo at the complex. Some of the staff lived in the dormitory, right in the building itself. Most of them were stock clerks and security guards, along with a few cashiers.","But the managers, administrative staff, and accountants were all locals. Given today's situation, most of them hadn't shown up—only the little supervisor on the motorcycle had come in.","The remaining frontline employees had first banded together to take down their mutated colleagues, then huddled in fear, not daring to open the doors or leave—until the youth apartment residents stormed in like a swarm of bandits.","Seeing so many people, the supermarket staff, who had lost their backbone, suddenly steadied themselves.","Wasn't this just a normal weekend scene? Big crowds of customers, busy work. When people were busy, it brought an inexplicable sense of peace.","As soon as Jiang Cheng approached the staff, they promptly and cooperatively opened the storage room.","Forklifts brought out the rice, flour, and oil.","No need to even stock the shelves—everyone swarmed straight for the pallets and loaded up their carts.","With food in hand, the heart is at ease."]},{"number":19,"title":"Chapter 19","paragraphs":["Jiang Cheng moved quickly because she knew exactly what she needed, unlike many people who scurried around like headless flies. She and Li Jiangbing finished their shopping pretty fast.","They had originally planned to wait by the checkout counters for Master Luo, but surprisingly, Master Luo and his group were already there waiting for her.","The flatbed cart Master Luo’s group brought had bags of rice packed tight and solid. The rest of their haul was mostly pickled vegetables, salted duck eggs, and canned goods. That was the suggestion Jiang Cheng had made, and Master Luo fully agreed, following through on all of it—toilet paper included.","Even though these were all necessities, and those two young folks Jiang Cheng and Song Jingshuo had given their word, Master Luo still worried they might have bought too much.","The white-collar workers living in the complex earned much higher salaries than he and his crew did, but at the end of the day, those people were the ones fronting the money. He was afraid that buying too much would make them resentful.","But the first thing Jiang Cheng said when she walked over was: \"Is that enough? With as many people as you’ve got, maybe you should haul over a bit more.\"","Master Luo’s worries eased, and he nodded repeatedly: \"It’s enough, it’s enough. My wife did the math—this will last us two weeks.\"","Everyone’s expectation for the situation ahead was the same: things might be chaotic for a few days, then the government would step in, just like in every disaster before, and turn things around swiftly.","The current shopping spree was just to get through that \"first few chaotic days.\"","It was his wife who said: \"To be safe, buy enough for half a month.\"","Jiang Cheng glanced over what they’d bought. It was clear Master Luo was a man who took advice well—or at least he agreed with her reasoning. Either way, it gave Jiang Cheng a sense of relief.","\"Let’s wait for Song Jingshuo,\" Jiang Cheng said. \"We agreed to meet up with him.\"","Her expression was light, and there was nothing unusual in her tone or manner when she mentioned Song Jingshuo. It gave everyone the impression that the two of them were simply splitting the financial burden, nothing more.","In truth, Jiang Cheng didn’t need the help.","After using her parents’ inheritance to buy the apartment in the youth complex, she still had a sum left over. She had stashed that money away untouched, reserving it for emergencies.","Since last night, she’d known an emergency had arrived.","She wasn’t afraid of having to dip into those funds. Compared to money, some other things mattered far more.","A person had to know what took priority.","Because the supermarket was short on staff, a few people who weren’t cashiers were manning the registers, and fewer checkout lanes were open, so the lines moved slowly.","The first batch of owners who paid for their items didn’t dare head out alone either. Though the 800 meters of road outside had already been cleared of mutants, who could guarantee that one or two wouldn’t suddenly appear from somewhere else?","The original mutants were one thing, but it was the infected ones you had to worry about. Infected mutants moved quickly and were agile. If you weren’t careful and one bit you, you’d be locked up in the property management conference room.","Everyone knew by now that those who’d been bitten by mutants were locked in there to wait for death.","That woman from Building 2—the one who looked all sweet and pretty—her behavior really didn’t match her face, did it.","But the hesitant mumbling and mutual questions of \"What do we do?\" and \"Should we go back together?\" were overheard by that woman from Building 2.","Jiang Cheng shouted toward the people outside the checkout area: \"Whenever you gather a group big enough, head back—don’t wait for everyone. Pack in as many people as you can, and stay safe!\"","A lot of people answered: \"Okay, got it.\"","Those who checked out first waited until seventy or eighty, even close to a hundred people had gathered, then left in groups together.","People were still queuing up behind.","Everyone had a handcart. Word was that the carts had been restocked from the warehouse.","Many young people had always turned their noses up at those handcarts—those were things middle-aged aunties and uncles used. They never thought they’d end up buying one for themselves. Turns out they were actually super convenient.","Song Jingshuo finished his shopping too.","When he walked over and saw Jiang Cheng already standing with Master Luo, his heart gave a slight lurch. But Jiang Cheng spotted him and waved first: \"There you are. Let’s split it half and half.\"","Song Jingshuo relaxed, came over, and split the cost of the property staff’s food supplies with Jiang Cheng.","Jiang Cheng said: \"Let them go first. We’ll cover the rear.\"","Song Jingshuo nodded: \"Same thought.\"","They were the ones who had organized everyone to come out; they had to make sure the main group got back safely. They couldn’t leave people behind.","And so, groups of a few dozen at a time, they retreated.","The core members of the temporary owners’ committee and the suicide squad stayed behind to cover the rear. When they finally had a staff member broadcast over the intercom three times to confirm there were no owners left behind in the supermarket, the last group of a few dozen, including Jiang Cheng, was ready to leave.","A dozen or so staff members from BuyDuo Supermarket watched them with longing in their eyes: \"You guys are really leaving just like that...\"","Reluctant to see them go.","After all the bustle, silence suddenly descended. Out on the road outside, biting monsters were still roaming.","Jiang Cheng noticed one of the staff members was the person she had struck up a conversation with earlier—that tough guy who had ridden his motorcycle all the way to get to work. He seemed to be some kind of shift supervisor.","Jiang Cheng asked him: \"Are you going back home?\"","The man said speechlessly: \"I’m not an idiot.\"","That morning, he had left the house completely unaware of what was happening. Only after stepping out did he learn there were monsters on the streets. He’d survived purely thanks to his motorcycle. But at the time, his mind had been locked onto one track—he never considered just turning back home. He only thought about charging through those monsters to get to work.","One one-way trip like that was enough. He wasn’t about to make the return journey.","\"I’ll just stay here for now,\" he said. \"There are beds in the dorms.\"","And there were even beds and mattresses on sale in the store, already made up with bedding, so they could sleep on those directly.","\"You guys,\" Jiang Cheng reminded him, \"count how many of you there are and set aside enough food for yourselves.\"","\"Don’t stand guard over a giant warehouse and end up starving yourselves.\"","Her words left them exchanging glances.","The supervisor thought it over, his expression growing more and more grim, and he nodded firmly: \"Got it.\"","Jiang Cheng turned to catch up with the main group, and the man shouted after her: \"Hey—thanks!\"","Jiang Cheng twisted her head and gave a small chin-up gesture in reply.","Several dozen people dragged and carried their supplies out of the supermarket.","The staff immediately locked the doors behind them. Then they stood together behind the glass door, watching the group from the youth complex disappear from sight.","The feeling of \"everything seems normal\" faded, and deep inside they felt adrift and uneasy again.","Song Jingshuo walked along the road, glancing over at Jiang Cheng.","Song Jingshuo had a double-strap backpack on his back. He didn’t have that kind of middle-aged lady’s shopping cart—instead, he dragged a large business travel suitcase he’d brought to the supermarket for hauling goods.","Jiang Cheng pulled a handcart and shouldered a big athletic backpack, stuffed until it bulged.","Song Jingshuo felt the urge to show that a man could be more capable than a woman by offering to carry her things or lift the heavy stuff. But that backpack of Jiang Cheng’s clearly weighed a ton. Song Jingshuo compromised: \"Jiang Cheng, put your bag on top of my suitcase.\"","Jiang Cheng refused: \"No need. I can carry it fine.\"","Li Jiangbing chuckled: \"Don’t let Jiang Cheng fool you—she’s slim, but she’s got serious strength.\"","The people nearby nodded, and one said: \"Yeah, no kidding. Today I saw a mutant, and she swung her bat at it—one hit and its head exploded.\"","Jiang Cheng thought back. It must have been during that stretch where she’d taken down several mutants in a row. Her body had warmed up, the bat had felt natural in her hands, and that swing had gone exceptionally well—one clean shot, instant headshot.","At this moment, she didn't want to be modest, nor could she afford to be. Instead, she said with a touch of bravado, \"That's right, I really am that strong.\"","Everyone acknowledged it.","Song Jingshuo's little bit of cunning had backfired, and he gritted his teeth slightly, no longer wasting words.","Jiang Cheng glanced at Song Jingshuo.","It wasn't that Song Jingshuo bore any real ill will, but someone like him was clearly accustomed to office politics, and used to being the one in control. In everything he did, he wanted to fight for the lead.","Just an elite white-collar worker used to workplace competition.","They took a turn, veering off the main road onto a street running between residential compounds.","Jiang Cheng kept looking back. Song Jingshuo, now paying close attention to her, asked, \"What's wrong?\"","Jiang Cheng said, \"I'm thinking about whether we should seal off the entrances at both ends of this street...\"","That way, they could reduce the possibility of mutants from outside the block getting in.","Everyone looked at her.","But she immediately dismissed the idea herself: \"Forget it, let's not think about that for now.\"","There was no usable material. There was also another compound's gate on this street, and who knew how many mutants were lurking inside that compound.","Besides, the project was far too large. Jiang Cheng knew very well that she didn't have the ability to command or mobilize so many residents to do such labor.","Although she had successfully organized the collective purchase for all the residents, precisely because of that, the neighbors' most urgent needs had already been met, and the corpses in the compound had even been burned. Moving forward, for everyone, it was clearly easier and safer to just stay put inside their homes and wait for the government's rescue.","Moreover, the compound was originally a gated community. As long as the gates were kept shut, the mutants outside couldn't get in anyway.","That was more than enough for the residents.","Everything else was just Jiang Cheng thinking too much, too far, too big.","But Song Jingshuo understood in an instant what she was thinking, and also why she gave up.","Song Jingshuo suddenly felt a bit deflated—while he'd been playing his little tricks, Jiang Cheng was considering expanding their defense perimeter.","How could that not make a person feel ashamed?","\"Let's leave it as is,\" he said softly. \"What we have now is already good enough.\"","We've done our best.","Jiang Cheng nodded. \"You're right.\"","It was comforting to have someone whose thoughts could sync with hers.","Just as the compound's gate came into view, Jiang Cheng's phone vibrated.","Jiang Cheng tucked the axe into her belt, pulled out her phone, glanced at it, and said with a slight tightening of her expression, \"Li Yuan of Building 3—isn't he on duty at the property management office?\"","Immediately, the person in charge of Building 3 replied, \"Yes! We helped him buy rice and flour.\"","Jiang Cheng answered the call, listened, and said, \"Okay, got it. We're almost at the compound. We'll drop off the supplies and head over right away.\"","After hanging up, everyone looked at her. She said, \"Someone in the meeting room has mutated.\"","\"The people in the meeting room handled it themselves.\"","Using the weapons she'd left them.","\"We'll go check it out later.\"","Meeting room headcount: minus one.","The good mood that everyone had been in after the successful collective purchase suddenly sank. In silence, they walked together toward the compound gate.","The security guard was waiting anxiously inside the gate. \"You're finally back. Is there anyone else behind you?\"","\"No, we're the last group.\"","\"Old Luo said to lock the gate as soon as you all got back.\"","\"Lock it. Thanks for your hard work.\"","The compound's main gate used an electric sliding gate for vehicles, and an electromagnetic lock gate for pedestrians.","The security guard added a chain lock to the electromagnetic lock gate, because if the power went out or there was a malfunction, the electric gate wouldn't open on its own—but the electromagnetic lock would demagnetize and fail, leaving the gate open.","With the chain lock in place, everyone felt much safer.","Turning back to look at the compound, though it was separated from the outside by just this one iron gate, a sense of security welled up inside them."]},{"number":20,"title":"Chapter 20","paragraphs":["Everyone first split up to take their purchased items home.","Yin Shi returned to her own place, set her backpack down on the floor, and first lifted up her shirt to check on Mo Li.","Mo Li was still curled up like a baby, pressed tightly against her body. He didn't feel as cold to the touch as before—actually starting to warm up. Jiang Cheng's body was continuously supplying him with heat.","But at this current temperature, if she set him down, he might get cold again.","Jiang Cheng decided to keep carrying Mo Li with her.","The members of the interim owners' committee dropped off their things at home and quickly regrouped downstairs, then headed together to the property management office.","Master Luo and the others were already there too. When they saw the group arrive, everyone moved aside from the computer monitors: \"Take a look yourselves.\"","They watched the surveillance playback.","After they had left at noon, the people in the conference room were in rough shape. Someone was pounding on the door and cursing, someone was crying inside, someone was throwing things.","Among them, one person looked unwell—paced around a couple of times, then huddled in a corner, sitting with knees drawn up. Everyone else was caught up in their own emotions, nobody paid him any attention.","He buried his face in his knees, like he was resting. He stayed in that position until just before Jiang Cheng's group was almost back to the complex—the ones bringing up the rear. Then that person suddenly lifted his head, eyes pitch black.","He had mutated.","It was clear to see that a mutated individual's physical capabilities were enhanced. This one didn't even bother standing up first—he practically \"sprang\" from his seated knees-drawn position, lunging at the nearest person.","That person was caught completely off guard and tackled to the ground.","Everyone watching the surveillance footage instinctively flinched backward—the common reaction when watching a horror movie. But then they all realized that the people inside were already potential infectees who had open wounds.","The guy from Building 6 reacted fastest. He grabbed a sledgehammer and bashed the mutated individual right in the back of the skull. The others snapped out of it and grabbed whatever they could to help.","Working together, they took the mutant down in a few blows.","But when they rolled the mutant off, Jiang Cheng and the others saw that the person who'd been pinned and bitten had half his face and neck torn to shreds, convulsing on the ground.","The surveillance footage seemed to freeze for a moment.","But it hadn't actually frozen—the wounded person on the floor was clearly twitching. It was the people surrounding him who had gone still.","Even through the screen, you could feel the helplessness.","They all knew they too would mutate, or had been bitten badly by the first one to turn, and were as good as dead.","The basement had no windows. The door was not only locked but also blocked. There was no escape.","Despair filled the room.","The surveillance camera was installed in a corner of the ceiling, so what Jiang Cheng and the others saw was the backs of these people.","But then the man from Building 6 suddenly turned around—through the screen, he glared at them with venom.","Even Jiang Cheng felt the hairs on the back of her neck stand up for a split second.","The man from Building 6 dragged a chair over, climbed up onto it, and swung his hammer at the people outside the screen.","The image vanished. The screen filled with static, flickering wildly.","Everyone exchanged stunned looks.","Song Jingshuo said, \"This is trouble.\"","Li Jiangbing: \"Huh?\"","Jiang Cheng explained: \"If any exposed wound means a hundred percent mutation rate, then at the very least, one mutant would remain in that conference room at the end. If several people mutated simultaneously and the others failed to take them out in time and got taken out themselves instead, and mutants can recognize each other and won't attack each other—then there could be multiple mutants left in that room.\"","Song Jingshuo continued: \"That bastard smashed the camera, so we can't know exactly how many mutants are in there. If we open that door without being prepared...\"","Everyone understood.","Someone sighed: \"What was he thinking?\"","It was just harming others without any benefit.","Actually, there was a way to understand it. His mind had snapped, and he wanted to take his revenge on society. The other residents in this complex without exposed wounds—mainly Jiang Cheng, Song Jingshuo, and their group—were the \"society\" standing right in front of him.","Jiang Cheng sighed faintly and said, \"We're not opening that door.\"","That was a complete rejection of the possibility that there might be survivors—a full death sentence.","No one said a word. The atmosphere in the property management office was heavy.","Then someone said: \"The news!\"","Everyone turned.","There was a TV mounted on the wall, left on the whole time. Earlier, because everyone was watching the surveillance footage, someone had muted it.","Now the TV was cutting to another final bulletin.","They quickly turned the sound back up.","[...extremely dangerous. We urge all citizens to arm themselves in self-defense. If you encounter a mutated individual, kill them immediately.]","Everyone in the office fell silent, watching the government's second broadcast.","Compared to the morning, it was different. In the morning, they had advised citizens to \"stay at home as much as possible\" and only \"use force to fight back if necessary.\"","By the afternoon, the guidance had changed.","What had happened between the morning and the afternoon?","\"Everyone, brace yourselves. There's no rescue coming,\" Jiang Cheng said softly. \"The military is probably done for.\"","Everyone stared at her in shock.","Master Luo said frantically, \"Miss Jiang, don't say such things.\"","Jiang Cheng's gaze swept over, her eyes dark and deep.","\"I've said before, not every place is as lucky as our complex. The vast majority are people living alone, quietly isolated in their homes.\"","\"Those high-density, concentrated-living places are absolute disaster zones. College dorms, prisons, and the military.\"","\"In military barracks, one room could house a dozen or even dozens of people. That's ultra-high-density accommodation, and their areas of activity are also highly concentrated—mess halls, parade grounds.\"","\"Even in our own complex, open spaces like the garden were disaster zones. But our population density can't compare to the military's.\"","So many people concentrated in one place, all collapsing together, producing the first wave of original mutants. And when ordinary people encountered the mutants for the first time, how many more would be wounded and exposed before they knew what was happening?","Even if they managed to control the first violent encounter, the next thing would be the wounded starting to mutate.","The agility of an infected mutant wasn't something an original mutant could compare to.","\"Military personnel are physically on a level ordinary people can't match. If the degree of enhancement is proportional to their baseline stats, then infected mutants from the military would be far stronger than those made from ordinary civilians.\"","\"Soldiers are the ones who can climb walls, dive into water, and fight.\"","Just imagining those already powerful bodies being enhanced further... people's faces started going pale.","Fear came from that overwhelming sense of losing control.","Yes—loss of control.","The military's open spaces were too vast, the density of people too high. By the time the upper echelons realized that the wounded would become even more terrifying infected mutants, the situation would already be out of hand.","The sense of security they felt when they returned to the complex had come from the iron gate blocking external mutants out, from the fact that their own internal mutant problem was cleared, from the fact that their supplies would last through the first chaotic days.","Then, they would wait for the government to sort everything out.","But now, being told \"no one is coming\"—that newly built sense of security shattered in an instant.","The property management office fell into a terrifying silence.","Fortunately, everyone gathered there was part of the interim owners' committee, all of whom had been among the first—or at least among the earlier—respondents to the call to go downstairs and eliminate the mutants.","Compared to other residents, the people on the interim committee were clearly braver or more decisive, and relatively calmer in the face of crisis.","The property management staff, by contrast, showed obvious signs of panic.","\"It can't be...\" Master Luo muttered. \"It can't be...\"","One of the younger property employees asked in a daze, \"Then... what do we do now?\"","Song Jingshuo's mind was also in a whirl. The situation had developed beyond what he'd expected, and he too was still thinking, \"What do we do next?\"","That was when Jiang Cheng spoke up.","\"First,\" she said, \"Master Luo, until the property manager can return to his post, you need to take charge of the property staff.\"","\"We've already stocked up enough food for the property team for half a month. At least for now, things are stable—no need to panic. What matters right now is to guard the main gate well. We worked hard to clear all the mutants inside the compound together; we can't let the ones from the streets outside come back in.\"","\"Master Luo, can you handle managing the property team?\"","Jiang Cheng looked straight into Master Luo's eyes, her gaze filled with expectation.","People who work office jobs have a strange trait: when you're running around like a headless chicken and lose all sense of direction, if someone gives you a clear task to do, the working person calms down instead—they even feel like they've grabbed hold of something solid.","Master Luo's panic was pressed down by Jiang Cheng's gaze, and he looked composed again.","He didn't agree right away. He thought for a moment, then nodded firmly. \"Yes! Leave the property stuff to me. I've already told the gate crew—they're locking everything up.\"","Jiang Cheng praised him. \"You're thoughtful.\"","She added, \"But I don't think the gate should be manned by just one person. There should be at least two there at the same time. If something happens and one goes down, the other can still raise the alarm. Can you arrange that?\"","This time Master Luo agreed immediately. \"Sure. You're right.\"","Jiang Cheng's gaze turned to the others. \"Next, what we talked about this afternoon—going floor by floor through the buildings.\"","\"There must still be mutants trapped inside their own apartments. We need to clear them out.\"","\"And there are also still some bodies in the buildings that we didn't have time to deal with this morning. We'll take care of those while we sweep the floors too.\"","\"You there, what's your name?\" Jiang Cheng turned to ask one of the young female property employees.","The girl quickly replied, \"Yang Xinyan.\"","In a property company, young women usually end up in either finance or customer service. They already knew the finance person didn't live in the staff dorms and couldn't come to work today anyway. So Yang Xinyan was most likely customer service—essentially an office clerk.","Jiang Cheng assigned her a job. \"The owners' forum has a post about the interim committee, with everyone's names, apartment numbers, and phone numbers registered on it. Make a spreadsheet and put together a contact list. Does the property office have a printer? Print it out—everyone here gets a copy, and the property office puts one up too.\"","Yang Xinyan indeed did clerical work on a daily basis—this was exactly the kind of task she was good at and used to. Having been assigned a job, she immediately felt grounded.","She gave a quick \"okay\", sat down at the desk, and started moving the mouse.","Jiang Cheng turned back around.","Song Jingshuo knew she was about to assign the next tasks to everyone.","She'd taken control of the room again. How did this keep happening?","He started to reflect on where he'd gone wrong. Why did this girl always beat him to it?","His mind had just been in chaos for that brief moment. Anyone who encounters such a major situation needs half a minute or a minute to process it, right?","Everyone needs a moment to pull themselves together.","Yes—the gap between them was just that time spent pulling himself together.","Anyone faced with a sudden crisis goes through shock, acceptance, processing, calming down, and only then starts thinking of solutions.","But Jiang Cheng didn't. She skipped straight to the final step.","The reactions that ordinary people have in between—she didn't have any of them."]},{"number":21,"title":"Chapter 21","paragraphs":["The complex had six buildings, over two thousand apartment units, and over two thousand owners. Although the mutated ones in the garden had been cleaned up, there were surely still original mutated ones like Little White’s Dad and Li Ziqing trapped in their own homes, not yet emerging.","Also, today had been so busy that some of the bodies in the buildings still hadn’t been brought out and dealt with.","While the temporary homeowner’s committee members were still around, Jiang Cheng organized a meeting to nail down the details of these issues that had been brought up since noon.","She also said, “We should each building have one designated contact person. That way, people in each building can go to him, he comes to me, and I coordinate—guaranteeing that communication gets relayed in a timely manner.”","No one objected, and on the spot they elected the contact persons for each building.","Building Four was Song Jingshuo; Building Two was Li Jiangbing.","Jiang Cheng—well, of course Jiang Cheng was the overall contact for the whole complex. No one needed to nominate her; it was simply the established fact everyone had naturally accepted over the course of the day—Jiang Cheng of 0306, Building Two. She was now the organizer, the manager, the liaison for all matters concerning the Youth Apartments.","Given the unusually unanimous attitude, Song Jingshuo had no complaints and could only accept it.","Yang Xinyan was used to desk work. She quickly compiled everyone’s information from the owners’ forum into a table, printed it using the property office’s printer, and handed a copy to each person.","It was organized by building. She had thoughtfully placed each building’s contact person at the top row of that building’s table.","Jiang Cheng was at the very top.","When Song Jingshuo got his copy, he lost whatever remaining steam he had.","Jiang Cheng asked Master Luo, “How many walkie-talkies does the property have? Any spare ones we can use?”","Even though everyone had each other’s contact info, phone calls were one-on-one and inefficient. Walkie-talkies allowed one-to-many communication, which was better suited for the current situation.","“Let me think... Twelve are in use, and there are four backup units in the cabinet,” Master Luo said. “The latest batch of twenty new ones hasn’t been handed out yet—the manager said they’d be distributed next Monday.”","Jiang Cheng said plainly: “Give them out now.”","Jiang Cheng had solved the issue of meals for the property staff, so Master Luo didn’t hesitate. He went and grabbed a cardboard box: “They’re all here.”","Jiang Cheng asked, “Battery powered?”","Master Luo said, “Rechargeable.”","The property manager had indeed planned to have the staff charge the new walkie-talkies over the weekend so they’d be ready for Monday’s distribution.","Conveniently, they were now fully charged and available for the temporary committee.","Plus the four backups, that made twenty-four units in total—old and new mixed—that they could use.","Each building had seven or eight representatives, and over forty people were cramming the property hall. They definitely weren’t enough, but it was better than nothing.","“Four per building,” Jiang Cheng assigned. “The contact person takes one; the other three circulate. The contact person handles the allocation.”","Master Luo had good sense. He squeezed one out of the property’s active stock to give Jiang Cheng: “You take one too.”","That way, Jiang Cheng didn’t have to dip into Building Two’s share.","Jiang Cheng accepted it: “Perfect. Do you have enough?”","“Enough,” Master Luo said. “You keep it.”","This was precisely why Song Jingshuo loved being the one in control.","When you’re the controller of an event, you naturally get the power to distribute resources, and resources naturally tilt your way.","What was involved here was nothing more than a walkie-talkie, but the principle stood.","Everyone learned and tested how to use the walkie-talkies.","Jiang Cheng finalized the tasks ahead and emphasized, “Whatever you do, don’t split up—make sure you’re protected.”","“If anyone gets hurt during the process, lock him in his own home. Take his keys and deadbolt the door from the outside.”","The apartment doors were designed so that once locked from the outside, they couldn’t be opened from the inside.","“Mark the door, notify his neighbors nearby. Observe at regular intervals. If he mutates, then we handle it.”","Everyone agreed enthusiastically: “Got it!”","As they were about to dismiss, sounds came from the corridor. They came from the meeting room—screaming, cries for help, and the sound of collisions.","The hall suddenly went quiet, everyone listening. Moments later, the screaming and crashing in the meeting room stopped. But then someone started pounding on the door, sobbing, “Let me out, let me out!” and someone else shouted curses.","Clearly, the meeting room’s population had decreased again.","Despairing, wasn’t it? Completely hopeless.","Every mutation further proved the high probability and inescapability of the infection.","The wailing cries were hard to listen to.","“That’s it, then,” Jiang Cheng said. “Everyone grab dinner as soon as you can. Recruit as many volunteers as possible on the forum—the more people, the safer.”","“Dismissed.”","Amid the cries from the meeting room, the dozens of committee members filtered out of the property center.","It was close to 6 PM now—early evening. The sky was no longer as bright as in the afternoon, the sunlight shifting from white to gold. Shadows grew longer.","The air carried a strange smell—the odor of bodies being cremated in the square. It permeated the whole complex, lingering for a long time.","Everyone felt the grime in their nostrils.","“See you around.”","“Heading back.”","“Take care.”","Having fought together once, the dozens of people—though they might not all know each other’s names—had become familiar faces. They exchanged goodbyes and split into six groups, heading toward their respective buildings.","Jiang Cheng got on the elevator with a few people from Building Two. She and Li Jiangbing lived on the third floor, so they were the first to get off.","They said to the others, “Keep an eye on the forum and group messages later.”","“Will do.”","The elevator door closed, and Li Jiangbing glanced at her before asking, “Are you going to keep carrying that cat around all the time?”","Jiang Cheng said, “It doesn’t really hinder my movements.”","That was true—on the way to the supermarket, she’d had a big lump on her chest, but she still swung her axe just fine.","What Li Jiangbing had really meant was “We’re in an emergency, and you’re still worrying about a cat.” But the cat hadn’t stopped Jiang Cheng from cleaving open a mutated one’s skull, and it hadn’t stopped her from thinking clearly and organizing everything with sharp logic.","Li Jiangbing clicked his tongue and decided against making a tactless comment.","Jiang Cheng reminded him, “You’re in charge of posting the volunteer recruitment thread for our building.”","A person couldn’t do everything single-handedly, especially the overall leader. If she tried to do all the work herself, she’d exhaust herself to death.","Li Jiangbing was the contact for Building Two—this was his job.","He gave a thumbs-up: “Don’t worry.”","Jiang Cheng returned home, hung up her keys, and lifted her shirt.","Mo Li had been tucked against her chest for hours. His body was warm now, as if gradually recovering. That was good.","Because of the situation in the meeting room, the supplies bought from the supermarket hadn’t been unpacked yet.","She put him back on the bed, first pulling out the new hot water bottle she’d bought that afternoon. She filled it with hot water, wrapped it in a towel, and had Mo Li hug it with all four limbs. Then she covered him with a thin blanket.","After that, Jiang Cheng rinsed the rice, put it in the rice cooker, sliced some preserved sausage over the rice, added a couple of greens, closed the lid, and pressed the switch.","Only after starting the rice did she dry her hands and begin unpacking and sorting the supplies.","The handcart had limited space, but she managed to squeeze two bags of rice into it anyway.","People couldn't survive without their staple food, and she didn't think that was enough, so she stuffed another bag into her hiking backpack. Three bags totaling fifteen kilos of rice.","Next came the canned goods—luncheon meat, tuna, and various other meat cans, thirty tins in all. Two large bundles of pickled vegetables, each containing several smaller packs. And fermented bean curd, that incredibly salty condiment perfect for eating with rice.","Thirty salted duck eggs.","Compared to fresh eggs, salted duck eggs clearly kept much longer, and shelf life was a major factor in her food choices.","They still had plenty of toilet paper at home, so she skipped grabbing any this time—it took up too much space. But she did restock sanitary pads, soap, shampoo, and other daily essentials, since they were nearly out at home. There was no way around that.","The reason her backpack was so heavy, though, was that on top of that one bag of rice, she'd also packed a large bag of cat food. Those two items alone were enough to weigh anyone down.","She couldn't ignore Mo Li's existence. When she'd first gotten the cat, she'd only bought small bags of food, and if grocery runs became inconvenient from now on, that definitely wouldn't last.","Jiang Cheng organized and stowed everything away, then opened her computer to take a look.","Every building's contact person had posted a call for volunteers to sweep their floors. Clicking into any of them, she saw loads of people signing up enthusiastically. One nice thing about a community full of young people—they were passionate and quick to act.","Li Jiangbing had posted his own notice too, with already over twenty responses. They were set to gather in the first-floor lobby at seven-thirty in the evening for a coordinated effort.","In the afternoon, everyone had gone to the supermarket on a group shopping run, and even those who hadn't joined the morning's garden cleanup now had some experience under their belts.","People were having heated discussions on the forum about how to protect their vital areas.","Some were even itching for action, proposing that the community respond to the government's second notice and mobilize to clear out the mutants from the nearby streets.","Jiang Cheng took a look at the owner forums for other nearby neighborhoods, and the tone there was completely different—nothing like the enthusiasm back home.","Gloom and mourning were the norm, the real deal.","The community across the street from the east gate of the youth apartment complex was the \"normal\" case—so many people grieving, terrified, lost, even hopeless over the deaths of family members.","The youth apartment complex was just too unusual: almost everyone lived alone, young, with no family right there with them.","Sure, some people had relatives they couldn't get in touch with and were worried sick. But still, unlike the neighboring complex—where people watched loved ones die horribly right outside the building and didn't dare go save them, or where a family member had turned and was locked in a room by the rest of the household but no one could bring themselves to deal with it—this was different.","Completely different circumstances.","The youth apartment complex was truly exceptional, one could even say extraordinarily lucky.","Jiang Cheng clicked into the forums of several nearby residential compounds and saw tons of desperate pleas for help.","There were people trying to organize residents to fight for themselves, but it was nearly impossible. The elderly wouldn't leave, children were terrified and clutching their parents' legs, crying, \"Don't go!\" They were scattered like loose sand, impossible to rally.","Jiang Cheng even noticed people in the neighboring complex's forum talking about today's panic buying at the youth apartments. Residents of other buildings had spotted it from their high-rise windows.","\"How did they manage to organize like that?\"","\"Are there really no mutants left in their complex?\"","\"I saw them clear out the mutants on the street too. I want to go out and buy stuff, my rice is almost gone. But there are still so many mutants in our compound, there's no way to even get downstairs!\"","\"Their complex is all young people, not like ours, sigh...\"","The aroma of claypot rice began to fill the room.","Jiang Cheng clicked into a few major forums and saw fresh content.","\"Zombies.\"","\"Let's just call them zombies.\"","\"It's from a foreign sci-fi horror movie, I think the mutants look a lot like that.\"","That was a new film from overseas this year, a horror flick with a fresh, original concept—practically a new genre of its own.","It had premiered in March, at least in theaters abroad. Apparently, there were plans to bring it to China domestically next year.","Right now, only a very small number of people the country had seen it overseas or watched a pirated version online. The pirated copies had only just started circulating, and they were all cam rips. Based on past patterns, a proper clear version wouldn't be hitting the streets for at least another month.","Someone had uploaded a few seconds of footage from the movie as an animated GIF to the forum.","The way those \"zombies\" in the film moved—that lurching gait, how they chased and tore at their victims—really did resemble what people were seeing with the mutants right now.","The only real difference was the skin. Mutants had grayish-blue skin. The original ones were a deep, mottled blue, while the infected ones were slightly lighter, a grey-blue.","That thread had gone up in the afternoon. By the time Jiang Cheng saw it, there were already hundreds of pages of replies.","It had spread to other forums by now, and it seemed everyone was adopting the term.","And so, whether they were original mutants or infected ones, they all got a single new name—","\"Zombies.\"","But what about Mo Li?","What exactly was Mo Li?"]},{"number":22,"title":"Chapter 22","paragraphs":["Jiang Cheng finished eating, and then gave Mo Li water and cat food.","Mo Li swallowed more easily than at noon this time, and ate more than he had at noon as well. But for a human, the little bit of food a kitten eats still seemed like the appetite of a tiny bird.","Jiang Cheng was therefore very worried.","How could that little bit of cat food provide enough energy to support Mo Li’s astonishing transformation?","According to the law of conservation of energy in the universe, theoretically speaking, he should need a large amount of energy. If that energy came from food, then he should need a large amount of food.","It was about time. A voice came through the walkie-talkie: \"Jiang Cheng, come downstairs.\"","Jiang Cheng replied, \"Okay, coming right now.\"","Jiang Cheng felt the hot water bottle and found that its temperature had dropped considerably.","The heat had clearly been sucked out of it.","The heat in a hot water bottle was fixed. It wasn’t like the human body, which continuously generates new heat through digestion, absorption, and breakdown to maintain the body’s normal temperature.","Jiang Cheng replaced the hot water in the bottle with fresh hot water. Then she opened the wardrobe, took out a winter down jacket, and swapped it for the towel blanket.","\"I’m going out to take care of something,\" she said, gently smoothing the fur on Mo Li’s forehead. \"I’ll be back soon. You sleep well.\"","Mo Li opened his eyes and glanced at her, letting out a soft \"meow.\"","That was great—he looked much better than he did at noon.","Jiang Cheng was so happy that she couldn’t help but kiss Mo Li on the forehead. \"Good kitty~\"","She stood up, picked up the axe from the sofa, grabbed her keys, clipped the walkie-talkie to her waist, and opened the door to head out.","Mo Li didn’t have the strength to move right now. He kept his eyes open, gazing at Jiang Cheng’s receding back until she disappeared.","About twenty or so people had gathered in the lobby.","By now, everyone knew who Jiang Cheng was. When she arrived, Li Jiangbing was just telling them about how Jiang Cheng had single-handedly taken down four mutants last night.","When they saw her, they all called out, \"Jiang Cheng’s here.\"","Li Jiangbing said cheerfully, \"Jiang Cheng, check out our gear!\"","Everyone had come well prepared, mainly in terms of protection, each with their own clever ideas.","Li Jiangbing still had his arm shield and fire axe.","Someone had brought a pot lid, someone had a chair, and someone had pried a cabinet door off its hinges.","A young mind was definitely a good thing.","Jiang Cheng’s eyes lit up. \"Great. We take the elevator to the top floor and sweep downward floor by floor.\"","Everyone gave a shout of agreement and piled into several elevators.","Sure enough, everyone had picked up the term \"zombies\" too. Now all they talked about, morning and night, was \"killing zombies.\"","Li Jiangbing glanced at Jiang Cheng. \"How’s the cat?\"","\"Better,\" Jiang Cheng said. \"Left him at home.\"","Li Jiangbing thought Jiang Cheng was great in every way. Pretty, quick-witted, strong, and brave. It was just... something about the way she was with that cat.","It was a bit like those idiots in foreign movies who, at a critical moment, still go back to save the cat or the dog. That was a bit hard to take.","The elevator dinged—they were at the top floor.","Everyone gripped their weapons tightly and filed out, tense but a little excited, all looking at Jiang Cheng and Li Jiangbing. \"Shall we start?\"","Jiang Cheng thought for a moment. \"Let’s make some noise first to notify the neighbors on this floor. Tell everyone we’re knocking on doors one by one, and if their homes are fine, they should just answer.\"","Li Jiangbing said, \"I’ll handle that.\"","Li Jiangbing had the guy with the pot lid bang on something loudly a few times first, then he shouted at the top of his lungs: \"Neighbors, the neighborhood committee is here to clear the floor! The neighborhood committee is here to clear the floor! If we knock on your door, you call out! If we knock and there’s no answer, we’re breaking the door down!\"","His voice echoed down the hallway. Several households cracked open their doors, peeking out: \"I’m fine here.\"","\"My place is fine too.\"","\"Same here.\"","The clearing team started from one end of the hallway, knocking on doors one after another. The neighbors had all heard Li Jiangbing’s voice earlier. Some opened their doors and poked their heads out, while others didn’t want to open up and simply answered from inside.","One person cracked the door just wide enough and waved eagerly: \"Hey, hey—across from me, you guys check my neighbor across the hall. I heard something off over there.\"","They all hurried over. And seeing so many people around, the man got a little braver, opening his door a bit wider: \"When I went out in the afternoon to grab some stuff, I never saw him open his door. He must be home. Friday I got in the elevator with him, and we even said hello. Then all of us passed out. I haven’t seen him once since I woke up.\"","Li Jiangbing gripped his axe, stepped forward, and carefully knocked. \"Anyone there? Anyone home?\"","And sure enough, with the sound of chaotic, uneven footsteps approaching, the steel door let out a loud \"BANG.\"","Confirmed—they had a job to do!","The group formed a semicircle around the door.","Those with the strongest protection were at the front. The cabinet door, the pot lid, and the chair were all in front, just waiting for the mutant inside—sorry, waiting for the zombie inside to come out on its own.","Why was the term \"zombie\" so easily accepted? Because it carries a sense of \"not human.\"","A corpse. The corpse of a body.","You hear it, right? Already not a person anymore, right? I mean the ones we killed this morning.","Yeah, yeah, not people anymore. And that makes it okay for us to kill them.","Not people, just corpses. Even the government said \"eliminate immediately.\"","So there’s no reason to feel guilty.","But whether the zombie opened the door was a matter of chance. Because the original zombies had very uncoordinated limbs and clearly no capacity for thought, driven purely by instinct. They didn’t have the mental logic of \"press down on the doorknob to open the door.\"","That door was slammed countless times, but the clumsy zombie never managed to get it open.","Everyone waited patiently for a moment, and then—well, the patience ran out. They looked at each other. \"What do we do? Break it down?\"","How though? The doors in these newer apartments built over the last few years were all national standard level-4 steel doors.","Jiang Cheng patted the person in front of her on the shoulder, and that person stepped aside. Jiang Cheng slipped into the center of the circle.","She stood next to the door, back pressed against the wall, one hand holding the axe, the other reaching into her trouser pocket for her keys.","Her keychain had several cartoon keychains hanging off it. She grabbed the keyring and reached out, dangling the jingling bunch near the doorknob, making noise.","It worked.","The banging on the door stopped. Clearly, the zombie had been drawn to the sound.","The zombie began fumbling with the doorknob.","After a few tries, the door swung open. The fresh, living scent of more than twenty young people out there drove the zombie into a roar as it lunged forward.","The door panel, the pot lid, and the chair all shot out at once to hold it in place.","The moment the door opened, Jiang Cheng pulled back her hand, shoved the keys back into her pocket, and gripped the fire axe with both hands.","The instant the zombie was held in place, Jiang Cheng swung the axe down in a diagonal arc, striking it right on the side of the neck. The head went askew immediately.","The guy holding the door panel found himself facing the zombie nose to nose, and nearly vomited on the spot.","Li Jiangbing finished it off with another axe swing! The zombie’s head rolled to the floor.","Jiang Cheng and Li Jiangbing’s two axes had handled it cleanly in no time—no one else had even needed to get involved.","A chorus of \"Whoa—\" went up from the group.","Even the neighbor across the hall, who had been peeking through the crack the whole time, let out a \"Whoa—\" of his own.","It was gross, sure. But the fear and the tension quickly drained away.","Zombies weren’t such a big deal. They had numbers, they had weapons, and they worked together.","Li Jiangbing was strutting around, full of himself, and even made a show of extending his fist toward Jiang Cheng in a cocky gesture.","Everyone was watching, so Jiang Cheng played along and bumped her fist against his.","Li Jiangbing was beaming with pride.","It was a bit theatrical, but it did boost morale. Everyone looked even more fired up than before.","They cleared the entire floor, and that one apartment on the top floor had been the only one with a mutated.","Li Jiangbing asked, \"What do we do with the body?\"","Jiang Cheng said, \"Put it in the elevator for now.\"","Two people dragged the corpse by its arms into the elevator, while others, grimacing with disgust, carried the severed head inside as well.","Everyone took the stairs down one floor together.","Some defended, some attacked, and they had even learned from Jiang Cheng how to create noise on the door handles to lure the zombies into opening the doors themselves. They made it down to the fifth floor without any trouble.","Just when it seemed like they were about to wrap things up smoothly, something went wrong on the fifth floor.","Because there were so many people, not everyone was actually pulling their weight.","Jiang Cheng was a girl, and the young men were so pumped up they were howling with enthusiasm, so she and the other two girls hung back, letting the excited, hot-blooded bunch take the lead.","No one expected there to be two zombies in that room.","The first one to come out was a regular zombie, and everyone had gotten used to working together, blocking it first before killing it. But just as they managed to hold the first one in place, a second one came out, using the first zombie's back as a stepping stone and leaping into the air.","A dark shadow loomed overhead.","Jiang Cheng's pupils contracted sharply.","It was a second-generation zombie, infected from a bite by an original zombie!","Li Jiangbing was a big guy and had been at the front the whole time. He had trained in combat, so his reflexes were lightning fast. He swung his axe straight up at the thing.","The zombie landed, and Jiang Cheng followed up with a chop of her own axe. Then hammers, baseball bats, and kitchen knives came rushing in from everyone else. With all those weapons piling on at once, even a second-generation zombie as agile as this had no room to dodge—they basically smashed its brain to pulp in a chaotic flurry.","But even so, when the zombie had come down, it had still knocked one person to the ground and bitten him.","Now the zombie was dead, but this man was covered in blood. It had torn a piece of scalp off his head, and blood was streaming down his face.","The hallway fell dead silent. The fiery enthusiasm and raucous yelling from moments ago were gone.","Everyone seemed to snap back to reality from that game-like, absurd excitement.","No one spoke.","\"I...\" the injured man sat on the ground, blood covering his face, stammering, \"I scratched myself, I, I really—I panicked just now and accidentally put my face against someone's kitchen knife, I...\"","But everyone's eyes were on him, and not a single pair believed him.","They stared at him, and in their eyes, wariness was already creeping in.","Jiang Cheng turned her head and quietly said to the person beside her, \"Get him a towel.\"","The quick-witted person hurried into the room, grabbed a towel from the bathroom, and came right back.","Jiang Cheng took the towel, folded it, walked over, and crouched down to press it against his head to stop the bleeding, saying softly, \"I know. But we still need to keep an eye on things, just in case...\"","\"How about this,\" she said. \"I live in 0306, and the room next to me, 0308, is empty right now. You can go stay there. We'll observe for one night and talk again tomorrow. Maybe by tomorrow it'll be nothing.\"","Her voice was gentle, but every face around was tense.","Because most of these people had been in the square during the day, and they all knew that back then, she had used that same soft voice to send the two people from Building 2 into the property management office's conference room.","They also knew what was happening in that conference room now.","\"I... I didn't...\" the injured man's teeth were chattering from fear. \"I really...\"","Tears started streaming down his face.","Locked up. He would definitely die.","He instinctively tried to grip his weapon only to find nothing in his hand.","He looked down—his weapon was already in Jiang Cheng's grip.","He looked up.","Jiang Cheng's eyes locked with his for a single second. Both of their expressions shifted.","The next instant, the young man struck like lightning, reaching out to snatch his weapon back. But Jiang Cheng had already sprung backward, retreating before his hand could close!","She lost her balance, falling backward, and the people behind her reached out in unison to catch her.","But one thing was for sure: he didn't get his weapon back.","The young man lunged forward, trying to pounce, but everyone raised whatever they were holding and pointed it at him: \"Hold it!\"","\"What the hell are you doing?\"","\"Don't take another step! Stop!\"","Both sides were locked in a standoff.","Li Jiangbing tightened his grip on his axe. \"Brother, calm down. We're—\"","\"Don't touch me!\" the young man shouted, face drenched in blood, features twisted, no longer wanting to hear any of it.","He had been on their side a moment ago, but he knew that from the second he got bitten, in their eyes, he was already a zombie.","The veins on the back of his hand bulged as he pointed at the people around him: \"Don't touch me!\"","\"Whoever fucking touches me, I'll bite them!\"","\"You hear me?! I'll bite you all to death!\"","\"I'm infected, and none of you are walking out of this alive!\"","His desperate, hysterical screams echoed through the corridor."]},{"number":23,"title":"Chapter 23: The 023","paragraphs":["The atmosphere in the corridor froze.","At that moment, Jiang Cheng's gaze shifted to the person behind him.","Most people had taken a step or two back when the incident happened, forming a semicircle around the man.","But behind him, a girl who had initially helped him up hadn't managed to retreat into the crowd. She was now pressed against the wall directly behind the man, who had lost his composure and was about to snap. She didn't dare move.","Jiang Cheng's eyes landed on her.","She looked back at Jiang Cheng.","Jiang Cheng gave her a look.","The girl's lips moved slightly.","Jiang Cheng stared at her steadily.","She knew she could do it. This girl had also taken part in the garden siege during the day, and she'd been nearby all the way to the supermarket. Jiang Cheng had already become familiar with her face.","She had also asked her name. Her name was Su Yu.","Su Yu had been brave in attacking the zombies during the day and had actively volunteered for the floor-sweeping operation. She just couldn't get over the mental block that the man hadn't turned yet—he was still human.","Jiang Cheng's gaze was very calm, and it calmed Su Yu down as well.","Su Yu pressed her lips together tightly and gripped her weapon—a frying pan.","She was someone who earned her own living and loved cooking. She had kitchen knives at home too, but the feeling of a blade cutting into human flesh was too unbearable; so she had chosen a frying pan as her weapon. Against zombies, whose \"death\" only came when the head was crushed, it worked pretty well.","The hysterical man was on high alert, tears and snot running down his face. He pointed his two fingers at both directions, his gaze darting frantically between left and right, terrified that these people would rush in and subdue him the moment he let his guard down.","He never expected a fish to slip through the net behind him.","Under everyone's watchful eyes, Su Yu gritted her teeth, swung her frying pan, and brought it down on the back of his head.","Bang. The man dropped to the ground.","A crowd surged forward and piled on top of him, pinning him down.","Jiang Cheng said, \"Check the room for something like a belt.\"","This man had been too traumatized; he wouldn't stay put willingly. His movements had to be restrained. They needed to tie him up.","Someone went into the room to search the owner's wardrobe, hoping to find a belt or a tie, but instead they turned up a bunch of sex toys—whips, handcuffs, ball gags, and the like.","The two zombies had been a boyfriend-girlfriend couple.","The handcuffs and ball gag fit this man perfectly, since he'd said himself that he would bite.","In normal times, people would've laughed at the sight of these things. But no one could laugh now.","There was a kind of darkly ironic sense of fate.","So many people in the hallway, yet it was quiet enough to clearly hear the \"click\" of the handcuffs locking, and even the rustle of clothes as everyone moved.","After they locked the handcuffs and fastened the ball gag, everyone turned to Jiang Cheng and asked, \"Where do we put him?\"","The property management's meeting room could no longer be opened.","Jiang Cheng had originally planned to coax this man into 0308 next door to her for quarantine, but now there was no need for that.","\"Just leave him in this room. Find the key to this apartment.\"","The key was found quickly on the shoe cabinet by the door.","They threw the man onto the bed. The door was locked from the outside.","Many owners on this floor were watching from their open doorways.","\"You, you, you, and you.\" Jiang Cheng called over several owners from the neighboring units and the unit across the hall. She handed the key to the one across the hall—the same person who had first suggested everyone check this apartment, so he was clearly fairly meticulous.","\"You all keep an eye on him. If he starts turning, call me or Li Jiangbing. All the temp committee members' contact info is in the pinned post on the forum.\"","Jiang Cheng and Li Jiangbing always carried walkie-talkies on them; the other three were circulating. Contacting her or Li Jiangbing directly would be faster and more convenient for reaching others.","Jiang Cheng assigned this task to the owners on the same floor.","This was ultimately a matter that concerned everyone's safety. People couldn't rely on the temp committee for everything; everyone had to do their part.","Jiang Cheng let everyone continue the floor-by-floor sweep, and she turned her walkie-talkie to the all-channel frequency to report what had just happened and how they'd handled it to the temp committee.","\"One reminder,\" she said. \"No need to send food. People won't die from going hungry for a day or two.\"","If he still hadn't turned after two or three days, they could consider letting him out.","Song Jingshuo's voice crackled with static: \"Understood.\"","Each building responded in turn: \"Got it.\"","The call ended, and Song Jingshuo clipped his walkie-talkie back onto his belt.","He was also leading Building Four's sweep, reminding everyone, \"Stay careful.\"","They all nodded in agreement.","Someone asked, \"This Jiang Cheng... what does she do?\"","Song Jingshuo said, \"Li Jiangbing said she's a company manager.\"","Jiang Cheng had lied to Li Jiangbing, calling herself a \"junior manager,\" but when Li Jiangbing bragged to others, he dropped the \"junior\" and just said \"Jiang Cheng? She's a manager, pretty impressive.\"","Others nodded: \"She does look like someone who can take charge.\"","Now, people said, \"That Jiang Cheng...\"","What about Jiang Cheng? Jiang Cheng hadn't done anything wrong.","But some would rub their noses and say, \"Wouldn't dare date a girl like that.\"","No matter how pretty she was. Too intimidating.","Pathetic.","Song Jingshuo sneered inwardly.","Mercy cannot command troops, righteousness cannot amass wealth, kindness cannot hold office, sentiment cannot accomplish deeds.","Those with iron hearts who could make tough calls and hard decisions were indeed frightening.","But right now, they needed exactly the kind of people like him and Jiang Cheng.","Jiang Cheng also ended her call and clipped her walkie-talkie to her belt. Turning around, she saw Su Yu holding her frying pan, back against the wall, staring blankly at the floor with unfocused eyes.","Jiang Cheng walked up to her and, just like Li Jiangbing had done, extended her fist to her.","Su Yu looked up at her, her eyes clearing, and extended her own fist to bump against Jiang Cheng's.","But she asked, \"Jiang Cheng, in the future... I mean later, will we be held accountable?\"","Jiang Cheng said, \"If we can be held accountable in the future, I'd say that's something worth being happy about.\"","She said, \"Come on. Let's keep going.\"","Su Yu nodded, gripping her frying pan tight.","The two of them caught up with the rest of the group.","It was already past 11:30 by the time the entire building was fully cleared.","Everyone came down to the first floor and pressed the elevator button. When the elevator arrived and the doors opened, it was full of corpses.","\"It's too risky to go outside at night,\" Jiang Cheng said. \"Stack them in the lobby for now. We'll burn them tomorrow.\"","Although the gardens had been swept during the day, it was still safer not to go out at night.","Among them were a few corpses of people who had been bitten to death by their cohabiting zombie partners. There was a common thread among those killed in the first wave by their own partners: their necks had been broken.","Li Ziqing's boyfriend was the same way.","Everyone stacked the bodies in the lobby and even pushed the security desk over to block the glass doors.","After this day, people had learned a lot more about zombies. Zombies had poor vision. Without living people or sounds to attract them, zombies would wander slowly and aimlessly, and they wouldn't actively damage the environment around them, like doors or windows.","They chased after flesh and blood and noise.","Jiang Cheng communicated over the walkie-talkie: \"Building Two is clear.\"","\"Building Six is clear too.\"","\"Almost there. Building One—we're just about done.\"","\"Building 4 is cleared.\"","\"Building 3 has one injured, already under control. Hands and feet tied, mouth gagged, others on the same floor keeping an eye on it.\"","\"Building 5 also has an injured one, uh...\" The person in charge of Building 5 paused briefly. \"Dealt with on the spot.\"","The person in Building 2 had only threatened to bite. The one in Building 5 actually went through with it. Luckily, the person who got bitten had protection—a magazine wrapped in tape around the arm. A conflict broke out, and the would-be biter died in the scuffle before he even turned.","After the Building 5 liaison finished briefing everyone, the lobby of Building 2 fell silent, and so did the walkie-talkie channel.","They had been killing zombies all day, but this was the first time a living person—one who hadn't turned yet—had been killed.","\"Good work.\" Jiang Cheng raised her walkie-talkie, breaking the silence. \"Next time, please try to capture them alive and isolate them if at all possible. Let's try to avoid a repeat of this.\"","In times like these, the ones who stepped up to take charge, who willingly became leaders, were usually clear-headed and sharp-minded. The voice on the other end replied, \"Understood. I didn't control the situation well. It won't happen again.\"","Song Jingshuo's voice chimed in to smooth things over: \"We're all doing this for the first time—it's inevitable. We'll have more experience next time.\"","Jiang Cheng: \"Yes, everyone's worked hard. Experience comes from going through it. Rest up early, and stay in contact if anything comes up.\"","She cut off the walkie-talkie and swept her gaze across the people in the Building 2 lobby. \"Good work, everyone. Get some rest—head back now.\"","Everyone seemed to let out a sigh of relief, murmuring \"Good work, good work\" to one another as they filed toward the elevator lobby.","But Jiang Cheng called out to Su Yu: \"Su Yu.\"","Su Yu stopped in her tracks.","Li Jiangbing glanced at them, figured they might have something to discuss between the two women, and wisely didn't stick around. The lobby was now left with just Jiang Cheng and Su Yu.","Jiang Cheng gave Su Yu an appraising look.","In most big cities, if a girl's family lives locally, her parents usually won't allow her to move out and live alone. Although young adults' apartments tended to have more men than women, most of the women living there, like Jiang Cheng, lived by themselves.","They were all women who had come to S City from elsewhere to make a living.","Girls like that were usually capable and independent.","Su Yu seemed like a textbook example of that kind of girl.","\"What's up?\" Su Yu asked.","Jiang Cheng said, \"If you know any other women in the neighborhood—no, even if you don't, it doesn't matter. In short, if you run into other girls, try to encourage them to participate in the things the homeowners' committee organizes as much as possible.\"","\"This neighborhood has more men than women,\" she said. \"It's too easy for us to get pushed to the margins. You know what I mean.\"","Su Yu's eyes widened slightly—she clearly did know.","At a company, if you don't fight for yourself, you get sidelined. A girl like her, coming to a big city alone and fighting her way through, understood that all too well.","Being marginalized in a corporate setting gets you passed over at most. But in a situation like the current one—what would happen if they got pushed aside?","Su Yu remembered what Jiang Cheng had said upstairs earlier: \"If in the future there's actually someone to hold us accountable, I'd consider that a good thing.\"","You needed a government, laws, and institutions with enforcement power for there to be accountability.","In other words, given the current situation, it was possible that in the future no one would be around to hold anyone accountable, which meant—","Su Yu still felt conflicted. \"It won't get to that point, right?\"","Floods and earthquakes in the past hadn't gotten to that point.","Jiang Cheng said, \"Who knows? Up until yesterday, who would have thought people could turn into monsters?\"","She continued: \"All I know is that in ancient times, when war or disaster struck, the first things to be sold were wives and daughters. When famine hit and people resorted to cannibalism, women were the first to be eaten.\"","Why had Su Yu been so proactive in volunteering for all this, despite it being dirty, disgusting, and dangerous?","Because her instinct told her that if she didn't participate actively and put something on the line, then when things got worse, she stood to lose something.","She just hadn't turned that gut feeling into clear logic yet.","\"When people don't take on responsibility and duty, what they lose in return is power.\"","Jiang Cheng's voice was soft, as if she didn't want the men in the elevator lobby to hear.","But to Su Yu, the words rang like a bell."]},{"number":24,"title":"Chapter 24","paragraphs":["Jiang Cheng returned to her own home, feeling exhausted.","Actually, many people had joined in the floor-by-floor sweep. Residents from every level had tagged along out of curiosity, and anyone wanting to take a swing at the zombies had to push to the front. She'd barely lifted a hand the whole time, just followed along without spending much energy.","But she hadn't rested properly since Saturday night. She'd been running on high alert the entire time.","Back home, she checked on Mo Li first. The hot water bottle had gone cold, but Mo Li's body temperature seemed a bit better. Things were looking up.","When she came back and touched his head, Mo Li even managed to lift it and let out a soft \"meow.\"","He nuzzled his head against Jiang Cheng's palm.","The soft feel of it sent what felt like a faint electric current from her palm straight to her heart—","The little cat was lonely.","How strange. No post on the pet forum had ever mentioned that a person and their small companion could share a psychic connection. How was it that the moment her heart got that tiny jolt, she understood completely what the little cat meant?","Jiang Cheng leaned down and gently rubbed her cheek against the kitten's fluffy head. \"Don't be afraid. I'm back. I'm here with you.\"","She said softly, \"You're not going to die. And you didn't turn into a monster. You and I—we just got stronger, that's all.\"","\"Don't be scared.\"","Mo Li said nothing. Mo Li just kept rubbing his head against her. When she lifted her head, he strained to raise his own, chasing after her.","Jiang Cheng saw him try to push himself up with his front legs, only to fail. Clearly he was still in a weakened state.","\"Want something to eat? Oh, no, that's not it.\" Jiang Cheng understood what Mo Li wanted. \"Wait for me. I'll be right back.\"","She washed up quickly and changed into pajamas.","She opened the down jacket and took a look. Mo Li hadn't relieved himself at all. She was a little worried.","\"Need to pee or poop?\" She slid her hand down to the base of his tail.","Mo Li sensed her intention and, as if using every last ounce of strength, tucked his tail over his rear and his little bells to cover them, letting out a short \"meow.\"","Jiang Cheng decided against lifting his tail to check. She'd respect the little cat. A cat this intelligent—a little cat that could transform into a handsome big cat—would surely never soil the bed, right?","Mo Li gave a firm \"Meow!\"","As if to say: Never!","Jiang Cheng chose to trust Mo Li.","She carefully wrapped Mo Li up in the down jacket, lay down, and cradled the little \"bundle\" in her arms. \"Sleep. We don't know what tomorrow will bring. Let's rest early.\"","Mo Li, held against her, seemed to curl up into a ball inside the jacket.","So soft. Jiang Cheng fell asleep quickly.","But Sunday night was destined for restless sleep.","In the middle of the night, the walkie-talkie went off first. The person on night duty from the property management reported: \"The conference room is stirring again. It's been handled now.\"","There was a two-second pause, and then the duty person couldn't help but add: \"People are crying in there. Damn, it's rough.\"","Jiang Cheng had just woken and couldn't get up right away. She picked up the walkie-talkie from her pillow, took a deep breath to reply, when Song Jingshuo's voice cut in first: \"Received. Just don't let them out. All of you—don't let it get to you. Once you're infected, no one can save you. Absolutely do not open that door.\"","The duty person's mood was low, clearly already affected. He answered gloomily, \"Understood. Don't worry.\"","She'd been beaten to it. Jiang Cheng wasn't angry. After all, she'd been the one stepping ahead of Song Jingshuo all along.","She steadied her breathing and pressed the talk button too. \"Thanks for the hard work.\"","She put the walkie-talkie down and tried to sleep again, but then the phone rang. An unknown number.","Her head was pounding terribly. She took a few deep breaths and forced herself to pick up. \"Hello? This is Jiang Cheng.\"","The voice on the other end said, \"Jiang Cheng, we're on the fifth floor. That person—uh, that guy, I don't know his name, the one you left with us to watch—he's turned.\"","Jiang Cheng asked, \"Can you deal with it?\"","The caller hesitated for a moment, and Jiang Cheng said, \"Got it. I'm coming up now.\"","Jiang Cheng climbed out of bed and grabbed the clothes she'd worn during the day. They were splattered with blood and other fluids. She put them back on.","The moment she stepped out the door, she heard a door open somewhere in the distance. She turned and saw Li Jiangbing stepping out too.","Spotting her, Li Jiangbing waved from afar. They met in the middle, and Li Jiangbing swore, \"What's wrong with these fifth-floor folks? If someone turns, just take care of it themselves.\"","Apparently, the people on the fifth floor had called both of them simultaneously. The call to Jiang Cheng had been on speakerphone, and Li Jiangbing had heard her say she was heading up, so he had no choice but to drag himself out of bed too.","\"Let's go.\" Jiang Cheng yawned widely. \"Let's go see.\"","They lived on the third floor. No point taking the elevator; they took the stairs up.","The hallway on the fifth floor had gathered a crowd. They were clustered around the door of that room, craning their necks to peek inside.","Li Jiangbing went over and complained, \"What's going on? Didn't we already kill zombies during the day?\"","A fifth-floor resident sighed, another scratched his head and said, \"It's just... we watched him change...\"","\"And he was tied up...\"","Most ordinary, normal people—as long as they aren't sociopaths—don't have particularly strong aggressive instincts. Everyone here was a law-abiding decent citizen.","Killing zombies during the day was different: those zombies bared bloody maws and lunged at you. It was self-defense.","But this man was handcuffed, his feet bound with a necktie, and even wearing a ball gag in his mouth. Despite turning, he couldn't get up to attack anyone.","When no one is under attack, good citizens find it very hard to initiate violence.","There was a mental barrier.","As everyone was chatting, a loud sound suddenly rang out!","They all turned in shock. While they'd been wasting time, Jiang Cheng had somehow slipped into the room and had already split open this second-generation zombie's head with one swing of her axe.","Jiang Cheng stood upright, closed her eyes, and let out a long breath. Her head really hurt. She hated not getting enough sleep, being woken up or forced out of bed. It was awful.","\"Jiangbing, take care of this.\" Jiang Cheng could barely keep her eyes open, wandering out like she was sleepwalking. \"I'm done. I can't hold on anymore.\"","The thing was, she hadn't slept well since Saturday night. She'd been running nonstop for two nights and a day now.","Everyone's mouths hung open. They instinctively stepped back to clear a path for her.","Jiang Cheng turned left.","Li Jiangbing stepped over, grabbed her shoulder, and spun her 180 degrees. \"This way!\"","Jiang Cheng went, \"Oh.\" Then said, \"I'll leave it to you.\"","\"Go on, go on.\" Li Jiangbing said considerately. \"Go catch up on your sleep.\"","Everyone watched her head toward the stairwell and vanish behind the fire door before they finally looked away.","Back to the room.","The unlucky young man had been left on the bed. The residents nearby hadn't dared relax. They'd set an alarm, and when it went off, they'd go in pairs to check on him.","When she looked again a moment ago, she saw that it had already mutated. But because its hands and feet were restrained, the person was flopping and squirming on the ground like a carp. Sensing the fresh blood and vital energy of living humans, it became even more frantic in its attempt to get closer to them. Unfortunately, the ball gag prevented it from moving its mouth — all that could be seen was a torrent of drool pouring out, dripping and splattering onto the floor. Absolutely disgusting.","Of course, it was even more disgusting now — brains splattered everywhere, with plenty of chunks and fragments scattered around.","Li Jiangbing’s mental fortitude was already well-honed by this point. He rested the axe on his shoulder, walked in, grabbed the corpse by the ankle with one hand, and dragged it out: “Alright, go back to sleep, everyone. The building’s clean now.”","“And hey, if you notice anyone acting off, report immediately.”","He muttered to himself as he dragged the body toward the elevator.","The residents of the fifth floor looked at one another, then at the vacant room with its sticky, grimy floor.","“Sleep. Time to sleep.”","“Exhausted.”","“Finally, we can get some proper rest.”","One by one, everyone returned to their own apartments and shut their doors.","At least by now, no one was asking “are we going to work tomorrow” anymore.","Like hell they were.","Jiang Cheng, nursing a throbbing headache, made it back home. At the entrance, she stripped off her filth-covered clothes and dropped them right on the floor. Too tired to bother changing into pajamas, she went straight to bed, scooped up Mo Li, hugged him to her chest, and fell asleep with her eyes shut.","In her dream, it felt like a small tongue with tiny barbs gently licked the tip of her nose.","Jiang Cheng woke up because sunlight hit her face. When she’d come back from clearing the building last night, it was already close to eleven, and she’d been too exhausted to close the curtains.","She still felt like she hadn’t slept enough. Turning over to face away from the window, she dozed off again for who knows how long before gradually coming to her senses.","She reached out a hand — the bed was empty.","Jiang Cheng rubbed her eyes and sat up: “Mo Li?”","A soft “meow” came from beside the floor-to-ceiling window.","The morning light was a bit blinding. Jiang Cheng raised a hand to shield her eyes and looked over.","The black cat lifted its head from the bean bag chair by the window.","The morning sunlight traced a golden outline around his glossy black fur. His ears stood upright, his limbs long and sleek — he looked both agile and powerful.","For a cat, Jiang Cheng thought Mo Li’s silhouette was nearly perfect.","Jiang Cheng got out of bed and stretched toward the morning light.","Mo Li watched from the bean bag.","Last night, Jiang Cheng had been so worn out that she’d come home, kicked off her dirty clothes, skipped pajamas entirely, and flopped straight onto the bed — wearing only a tank-top bra and underwear.","Standing up to stretch, her skin gleamed white in the early light.","The black cat’s eyes gleamed green, fixed on her.","When Jiang Cheng finished stretching and walked toward him, Mo Li seemed to spook — as if trying to jump down from the bean bag.","But... his legs gave out, and he tumbled onto the floor.","He’d forgotten he still hadn’t recovered. This morning, just to get some sun, he’d struggled to move from the bed to the bean bag. It had drained almost all his energy.","Jiang Cheng hurried over and scooped him up: “You okay?”","Mo Li was held like a baby, belly up, all four paws pointing at the ceiling.","He tried to kick his legs, realized it was completely futile, and finally gave up. He sank limply into Jiang Cheng’s arms.","“You haven’t recovered yet. Don’t go running around,” she said softly, gently rubbing his belly. She glanced at the bean bag and it clicked: “You want to sunbathe, right?”","She patted the bean bag into a suitable shape, like a little nest, and placed Mo Li in the middle of it. “Get your sun, then. I’ll make breakfast.”","Breakfast was simple — there was still a bowl of congee left from yesterday. She just had to heat it up and add a salted duck egg.","Jiang Cheng lit the stove and put the congee on to warm. She glanced at her phone and saw a text from Li Jiangbing: [Are you up? More news — they said no work.]","Jiang Cheng quickly turned on the TV. Since yesterday, the government’s news announcements had been on a loop. The announcement from yesterday evening had been replaced with a new one, playing over and over:","[S City has entered temporary control status.]","[Except for units essential to the city’s basic operations, such as medical institutions and emergency support, all enterprises, public institutions, schools, and kindergartens are to suspend business and classes.]","[Police forces are being concentrated to eliminate the mutated. Residents are urged not to go out unless necessary.]","[Residents are permitted to use force to defend themselves against the mutated. Anyone suspected of infection must be immediately restrained and isolated.]","[...Remain vigilant at all times.]","Online, everyone was already calling them “zombies,” though the authorities still used the term “the mutated.”","In any case, the question everyone had been agonizing over all day — “Do we still have to go to work on Monday?” — finally had an answer.","The congee in the pot began to bubble, but Jiang Cheng paid it no mind.","She rested her chin on her hand, staring at the scrolling announcements, lost in thought.","She turned and opened her laptop, starting to search for “S City police strength” and “S City total population.”","How many police were available in S City?","After the initial mutation of the virus, how many were left?","After the unprepared first encounters with the zombies, how many more were lost?","Could she still count on others now?"]},{"number":25,"title":"Chapter 25","paragraphs":["The porridge was burnt and thick. In the past, Jiang Cheng would have dumped it out and made a new pot. But now Jiang Cheng wouldn't waste food like that. Though supplies were still plentiful for the moment, she had a strong sense of impending crisis.","She forced down the burnt porridge with a salted duck egg.","After she was full, she fed Mo Li.","Things were much better now—Mo Li was fully capable of eating on his own. She tossed a handful of cat kibble into the \"nest\" on the beanbag sofa, and he crunched away by himself. He wasn't fast, but he was completely independent when it came to eating.","He still hadn't used the litter box, though. Jiang Cheng had checked—the box was clean, with no trace of use at all. That worried her a little.","Her phone suddenly buzzed, just one short ring, then cut off—a sneaky sort of sound.","She picked it up. Li Jiangbing.","She called back: \"I'm awake.\"","\"Did you sleep well?\" Li Jiangbing asked. \"You looked pretty wiped out yesterday.\"","\"Not bad. I've basically recovered my strength. The main issue was that I didn't sleep well the night before last either,\" Jiang Cheng said. \"I've already had breakfast. Have you eaten?\"","Li Jiangbing had eaten too.","Good, Jiang Cheng said. \"Let's get to work.\"","They had to move early in the morning.","The bodies in the first-floor lobby needed to be dealt with.","Jiang Cheng and Li Jiangbing roused the members of the interim homeowners' committee from Building Two, and some of the building's residents also came to help. Together, they dragged all the corpses stacked in the lobby to the central garden plaza.","After all, this was where they lived—nobody wanted to leave a pile of corpses sitting in their own lobby.","Su Yu was there too, along with the other girl from last night. Each of them had also brought along another girl.","Everyone was busy, so Jiang Cheng didn't talk much with them—a nod here and there was enough of a greeting.","Master Luo was already hard at work in the plaza.","When he saw Jiang Cheng, he said: \"I swung by the office this morning and took a look. That conference room was making a racket again early today, but now it's gone quiet. They didn't call you all again anyway. They're keeping an eye on it.\"","That conference room was like some kind of cocoon now—nobody knew what would finally emerge from inside.","Anyway, the door was locked tight and would never be opened. There were no windows in the basement, so they couldn't get out.","People from every building were moving. The zombie corpses killed during last night's building-to-building sweep were all being dragged out for centralized disposal now.","The paths between the buildings and the garden were bustling with people coming and going, looking like a hive of industrious worker bees. There was an oddly vibrant, lively feeling to it.","What a strange contrast.","The corpse pyre from yesterday had truly become a \"heap.\"","A lot of people assume that burning corpses means reducing them to ash—but it really doesn't work that way. At a place like the Youth Apartment, with no professional crematorium equipment, open-air burning never produces \"ashes.\" In the end, it just produces a \"heap.\" You could even make out clearly defined human remains in that pile.","Fresh bodies were dragged onto the heap to keep burning. There was still plenty of fuel, more than enough.","Quite a few people had come to help.","But some people weren't there to help—they were there with cameras, snapping photos. There were traditional cameras with long telephoto lenses, and the newer compact digital cameras that could slip right into a pocket.","\"How often does a person get to witness something like this in a lifetime? We've got to document it—maybe someday this will go into the history books,\" they said. \"Cameras were invented for moments like this.\"","That almost sounded reasonable.","The fire blazed up, and waves of heat rolled over everyone as they kept a safe distance and watched.","The photographers moved in and out, searching for the perfect angles, near and far.","The scene was both frozen and in motion.","Just then, someone came running over: \"The neighborhood next door has organized too!\"","By \"next door,\" they meant the residential complex across the street from the east gate—a place called Lucky Harmony Gardens.","On Sunday afternoon, when the residents of Youth Apartment marched out through the east gate in force toward the BuyDuoDuo Supermarket, they'd passed right by Lucky Harmony Gardens. That street was called Lucky West Street.","At the time, many residents of Lucky Harmony Gardens had watched them pass from their windows, and a few had even shouted questions from across the way.","And just as Jiang Cheng had been browsing property forums of other complexes and other big forums, plenty of outsiders had been browsing Youth Apartment's owner forum.","At this moment, the internet had real meaning—information was flowing.","Among the outsiders visiting the Youth Apartment forum, the vast majority were from Lucky Harmony Gardens next door. Because they had witnessed that waves of group shopping on Sunday afternoon, they were desperate to know what was happening on this side, and they flooded into Youth Apartment's forum.","From there, they got a rough picture of what had occurred.","Back on their own forum, the residents of Lucky Harmony Gardens plunged into heated discussion:","[We can't just sit around waiting for death!]","[We're out of food at home.]","[The baby's formula is nearly gone!]","[We need to organize too.]","Lucky Harmony Gardens had everything from studio apartments to four-bedroom places, from small children to elderly people, and even plenty of domestic helpers. Demographically, it was basically a complete cross-section of society. Unlike Youth Apartment, which had a narrow resident base—mostly young, highly educated singles.","Now, Lucky Harmony Gardens had finally put together a team, going down to clear out the zombies wandering in their compound.","It had been far harder for them to organize than for Youth Apartment.","Some people were even fully armed and ready to head downstairs when their elderly parents sobbed and clutched at them, refusing to let them go: \"Let someone else go! Let someone else go! You're my only son!\"","It was so hard.","But as the forum posts said, they couldn't just sit and wait to die. Especially since Sunday evening, when the government's new announcement shifted its tone and clearly began encouraging citizens to save themselves.","They'd argued all night, and finally, this morning, some people had taken the lead to go downstairs. One. Two. Three. More and more. Eventually they'd managed to organize.","But though the neighborhood had a larger total population, it had far fewer able-bodied young men than Youth Apartment did.","Couples with children—the mothers basically stayed home. But some young couples without kids, holding cleavers and rolling pins, summoned their courage and went down together.","Some families had elders grabbing their only sons to stop them from risking their lives. But other families had the older generation holding the young people back, saying: \"You're still young, stay put—I'll go.\"","After understanding the situation, Jiang Cheng paused to think, then urged everyone: \"Let's go help them.\"","\"This isn't the time for looking after only our own doorstep. If they collapse, we'll just be facing more zombies.\"","\"At a time like this, we're all one and the same community. Not just neighborhood and neighborhood, city and city.\"","\"Actually, right now—humanity is one community.\"","Zombies don't stay put in one place, after all. Zombies have legs. They walk. Next door, the population skewed heavily toward the elderly, women, and children. Imagine if they were left to fend for themselves and the whole complex fell to infection—would they one day have to face infant zombies crawling on the floor with baby bottles?","That's too nightmarish!","Even horror movies wouldn't dare film that.","The two complexes were far too close together. Youth Apartment's east gate almost faced Lucky Harmony Gardens' west gate directly. If one fell, the other would be next—lips and teeth.","If JiXiang Garden fell, it would essentially turn the area outside the East Gate into a zombie nest, and once those zombies started moving and spreading outward, the Youth Apartment would be the first to suffer.","Jiang Cheng's rallying cry got a response from everyone: \"She's right!\"","By now, everyone basically kept their weapons on them at all times. People like Jiang Cheng and Li Jiangbing would carry axes tucked directly into their waistbands, ready to draw at any moment.","But everyone still went upstairs to do some quick protective prep before regrouping downstairs.","The strong and able-bodied team surged toward the East Gate in full force.","When the two security guards at the East Gate heard what was happening, their blood ran hot, and they wanted to join in too.","Jiang Cheng stopped them: \"You two are way too important! The safety of our compound depends on you two! You absolutely have to hold your posts. This place can't do without you.\"","That sounded pretty inspiring too. The two guards gave their word: \"Miss Jiang, don't worry! We've got the gate covered!\"","Because of a lack of organization, JiXiang Garden's main gate was still wide open, never having been shut down and locked up like Youth Apartment's had been.","Only two vehicle barrier arms blocked the entrance, and the people from Youth Apartment ducked right under them. The young folks, hot-blooded and fired up, shouted as they charged in: \"Youth Apartment's here to back you up——!\"","\"Youth Apartment's here to help——!\"","\"We've arrived——!\"","JiXiang Garden had only mustered a small number of people, but the zombies in their garden were far more numerous than those at Youth Apartment.","On Saturday night, too many families had been out enjoying the cool air in the garden. Unlike Youth Apartment, where lots of young people had been inside playing video games and were, fortunately, sealed off in their own units.","The JiXiang Garden people were stuck in a hard-fought battle when Youth Apartment's massive team appeared like troops dropping from the sky.","This huge swarm of young people stormed in with shouts, swinging without a moment's hesitation, unafraid at the sight of blood, and neither fainting nor retching at severed hands or shattered skulls.","Their combat power was fierce, and the moment the main force arrived, the tide of battle turned instantly.","They only showed a flicker of reluctance when they encountered child zombies or baby zombies, but they still swung their iron rods and brought down their axes without mercy, taking out those zombies with no room for hesitation.","Around just past ten o'clock, the fight was basically over.","Everyone fanned out across the garden with their various weapons, sweeping through and checking every corner, terrified of missing anything.","Those baby zombies could suddenly crawl out of the bushes or even spring up from the ground to lunge and bite — they were pure nightmare fuel.","For the people of JiXiang Garden, this was their first face-to-face battle with zombies, and the psychological shock hit hard. Most of them felt completely drained, plopping down wherever they were, catching their breath as they watched those energetic young folks from Youth Apartment finish up the cleanup.","Jiang Cheng and a few other core members of the interim committee had just gathered when a man who looked to be in his forties walked over and asked: \"Thank you so much! I know your compound has already set up a temporary committee — are you the people on it?\"","He switched his cleaver to his left hand and extended his right.","Among the group, Song Jingshuo stood out — tall, with a sharp, elite bearing. The man made straight for him.","Song Jingshuo almost instinctively reached out to shake his hand, clearly having muscle memory for that gesture from years of habit. He exchanged pleasantries: \"Yes, we're the heads of the Youth Apartment interim committee. My surname is Song. And you, sir?\"","The man said: \"My surname is Huang. I'm one of the organizers here in this compound. Honestly, thank you from the bottom of my heart. We never imagined anyone would come to help us.\"","Mr. Huang's eyes were a little moist — he genuinely was moved close to tears.","Song Jingshuo was about to keep talking, but Jiang Cheng cut in: \"Hey, big brother, does the cleaver work well? Is the cleaver better or the axe? I've been wondering whether I should switch to a cleaver too.\"","Mr. Huang found this girl utterly clueless — seriously lacking in social awareness.","If she were one of his subordinates, she'd never get a promotion.","He answered dismissively: \"Either works.\"","But the girl was even more dense than he'd thought, as if she had no idea at all that this was a moment for the heads of two compounds to be having a proper exchange. She just stuck her hand out: \"Here, give me the knife — let me try it.\"","Mr. Huang couldn't really refuse, and just like that, his cleaver ended up in this girl's hands.","Furious, he was about to say something when he saw that girl take a step back and hand the cleaver to a huge, muscle-bound guy beside her.","Her voice turned cold: \"He's injured.\"","Everyone followed her gaze. Mr. Huang himself looked down.","He was wearing summer shorts, and on his calf — several scratch marks. Small ones, like the claws of a small animal... or the hands of a very small child.","\"It's nothing,\" Mr. Huang said. \"Just a scrape. A band-aid will do.\"","But the young man from Youth Apartment who'd been shaking his hand had already pulled his hand back. He'd even taken a step back, standing together with that girl.","Mr. Huang froze.","He saw that clueless girl from Youth Apartment pull a walkie-talkie off her belt.","\"Call all our people over,\" she said. \"Screening the wounded — now.\"","Word spread from person to person, rallying calls going out in every direction, and soon everyone knew: this was an order from Jiang Cheng of the interim committee.","The people of Youth Apartment had already been through this before — they all knew exactly what it meant.","The people of JiXiang Garden were still sitting on the ground, breathless and spent, when suddenly shadows fell over them.","They looked up. Those warm-hearted, brave young people from Youth Apartment had tightened their grips on their weapons, faces grim, forming a tight circle.","Step by step, they advanced — closing in and surrounding them."]},{"number":26,"title":"Chapter 26","paragraphs":["The main functions of a keypad phone were making calls and sending texts. Some advanced new models could even play music.","The internet consisted mainly of portal sites and forums, plus some shared resources.","Starting Saturday night, internet forums became an important channel for citizens to get information. Especially those owner community forums that were usually dead quiet with hardly any posts suddenly became a hive of activity.","But these were all things for young people; many middle-aged folks couldn't quite navigate them.","The man named Huang was indeed one of the main organizers of this zombie-clearing operation in Jixiang Jiayuan, but his communication with others on the forum was all done with the help of his middle-school-aged son. He was a traditional middle-aged man who wasn't familiar with the internet.","There was some information he hadn't looked into deeply.","For example, zombies were divided into original zombies and second-generation infected mutants.","For example, up to this point, infection after injury was almost one hundred percent certain.","It was also because the discussion about infection on the Youth Apartment owner forum had already surged during the day on Sunday, and the people from Youth Apartment had basically all witnessed the temporary committee dealing with the injured. There was no longer any need to discuss that information on the forum.","Too many posts had pushed the infection-related posts down; if you didn't dig deep, you'd never find them.","Old Huang's son, Little Huang, missed out on that information because of this.","Missing information can sometimes change fate.","At this moment, Old Huang frowned at the young people from Youth Apartment whose attitudes had suddenly changed, and asked in confusion, \"What's going on?\"","But neither Jiang Cheng nor Song Jingshuo answered him. Their gazes skipped over him to look behind him.","Jiang Cheng asked, \"Does your community have anyone else who can take charge?\"","A man who looked to be in his thirties jogged over: \"What's wrong?\"","Things were fine just a moment ago; why did the atmosphere suddenly turn tense?","Jiang Cheng asked him, \"Can you organize the people in your community?\"","\"Ah, well, I think so,\" the man answered with that middle-aged slickness of not committing fully, \"Do we have a situation?\"","Having learned from past mistakes, Song Jingshuo couldn't afford to be careless again. He asked directly, \"Are you injured?\"","The man said, \"No, I'm fine. Who's injured?\"","He even turned to look at Old Huang, but before he knew it, Song Jingshuo, Li Jiangbing, and several others had moved in and were roughly pulling at him, checking his neck and arms, and even pulling up his pant legs to inspect his calves.","There were child and even infant zombies in this community; because of their height, they might inflict wounds on a person's legs.","After quickly confirming that this man indeed had no injuries, Jiang Cheng tilted her chin: \"Brother, can we step aside for a word?\"","The man frowned and followed her and Song Jingshuo a few steps away.","Old Huang tried to follow, but Li Jiangbing, with a bear-sized hand, held him back: \"Brother, hold on. Let them finish talking first.\"","Old Huang already had a vague sense that something was wrong. He demanded, \"What is there that I can't hear? Today's matter, I'm the main organizer. I work at the municipal directly affiliated agency; I have rich organizational experience.\"","No wonder he had a bit of a leadership aura about him.","Li Jiangbing just laughed it off: \"Alright, alright, just wait a moment.\"","Li Jiangbing had tattoos. In normal times, Old Huang wouldn't even talk to a person like that.","But Li Jiangbing was tall and burly, carrying both an axe and a cleaver. Not only that, but he was also surrounded by many young men who formed a human wall, blocking him and cutting him off from the young man and woman who were clearly in charge.","He shouldn't have dismissed that young woman earlier.","Old Huang had already figured it out—that young woman might actually have even more say than the tall young man he'd shaken hands with. Many of these young people were acting on her cues.","Especially this tattooed gym guy who stayed right by her side like a bodyguard or secretary.","Before long, the second man finished talking with Jiang Cheng and Song Jingshuo, and the three of them came back together.","The man had introduced himself to Jiang Cheng and the others; his surname was Zhou, Zhou Wang, thirty-something, also a middle-aged man.","His expression was grim.","Old Huang kept his composure: \"Say, Old Zhou, is it? What did they say?\"","They weren't familiar with each other either; they'd only connected through the owner forum, at the level of barely matching faces to surnames.","Zhou Wang licked his lips to ease the tension and said, \"Youth Apartment's suggestion for us is to first see if there are any injured people...\"","Jiang Cheng and Song Jingshuo and the others didn't interfere; they just watched from the side.","Anyone who could step up to organize at a time like this had to have some ability. They had called Zhou Wang aside to communicate, and now Zhou Wang understood the situation and knew Youth Apartment's approach.","He could host and take the lead himself.","Jixiang Jiayuan needed its own leader; it couldn't rely on Youth Apartment for everything.","Zhou Wang did have some ability and decisiveness, but when the injured found out they were going to be locked up in isolation, conflict inevitably broke out.","The community became noisy and chaotic, and Zhou Wang struggled to keep things under control.","Although they had briefly fought together, they were still just unfamiliar neighbors. Many of them were sturdy men in their thirties or forties with rich life experience; they weren't about to obey just because someone said so.","Another reason was that the proportion of injured people in Jixiang Jiayuan was actually higher than those uninjured.","Many people had initially ignored the child and infant zombies. Since they were few in number, while fighting the adult zombies, people would suddenly get scratched or bitten on the legs.","Now everyone knew how serious things were. Those who were uninjured naturally wanted to control the injured, but they were outnumbered and couldn't manage the situation.","Luckily, people from Youth Apartment had already quietly surrounded them.","Those who refused to be locked up in isolation found they couldn't get away no matter what.","Zhou Wang cast a pleading look at Jiang Cheng and Song Jingshuo.","Jiang Cheng raised her hand and made a gesture—both palms pressing inward.","The people from Youth Apartment had already developed a tacit understanding through a whole day of fighting and cooperation. Jiang Cheng didn't say a word; everyone saw the gesture and understood.","The encirclement began to tighten.","They were all young people holding sharp weapons. These young people might carry some sympathy, but no one would go soft. Because what Jixiang Jiayuan was about to go through, they had already gone through.","People's minds and character can be forged through experience.","Before Saturday, they were vibrant, optimistic, promising young people.","Now, they could swiftly split open a zombie's skull.","Some of them could even grit their teeth and swing their weapons at people who were infected but hadn't yet turned.","Youth's growth and maturity can sometimes take years, and sometimes it can happen in a single weekend.","The shouting injured from Jixiang Jiayuan quieted down and began to back away.","The pressure of the shrinking encirclement was too great.","But there were those who refused to accept it. One person suddenly made a dash outward. And he aimed his escape at a girl, charging straight at her.","He had assumed, based on first impressions, that the girl would be the weak point in the encirclement.","But luck was not on his side—the girl was none other than Su Yu, who lived in the same building as Jiang Cheng.","Before the young men nearby even had to lift a finger, a loud clang rang out as Su Yu slammed a frying pan straight into the face of the man who was trying to break through!","The blow landed hard, catching him dead center on the bridge of his nose. Even the young men watching couldn't help but wince, then they gave Su Yu enthusiastic thumbs-ups.","The man spit out two teeth, his face covered in blood, and collapsed to the ground, unable to get back up.","The residents of the youth apartment complex had come well-prepared. Someone pulled out rolls of duct tape from their backpack and immediately bound the man's hands.","They also planned to tape his mouth shut—mainly out of fear that he might bite someone out of desperation and cause further infection.","Zhou Wang ran over in a sweat, holding up his hand to stop them: \"Go easy! Go easy!\"","Two people dragged the man back to the open space in the middle.","The injured residents of Ji Xiang Jia Yuan looked grim.","\"Brother Zhou,\" Jiang Cheng called out to him, \"why don't we handle this? We're a bit more experienced over here.\"","\"Little Jiang, hold on!\" Beads of sweat kept forming on Zhou Wang's forehead, one layer after another. \"Our situation is different from yours—you need to think about that.\"","\"Your complex, I know, is all single young people.\"","\"Over here, we've got families with kids and elderly parents to look after.\"","If so many people were to be locked up, Zhou Wang knew, there would immediately be four to five times as many family members showing up to make a scene.","At that moment, the people from the youth apartment complex once again understood just how special and fortunate their own situation was.","They also felt the hesitation and overthinking of the middle-aged residents, which was frankly irritating.","Jiang Cheng didn't hesitate for a second. Every decision she made was quick and decisive.","Suddenly, a hoarse voice rang out from among the injured: \"Self-quarantine at home.\"","Everyone turned to look.","The one who made this suggestion was none other than Old Huang. Clenching his teeth, he offered his idea: \"Everyone goes home, locks themselves in a separate room, and is watched over by their own family members. We also need to set up a temporary management team—someone in charge of communications, someone to patrol, keeping records, and maintaining open lines of contact. If anyone turns, the patrol team will stop by and handle it.\"","His mind was sharp and his thinking quick, clearly someone with organizational and managerial experience. He must have been a leader at some level—you could tell he had ability.","If he hadn't been injured himself, a man with his competence would have been the one in charge of Ji Xiang Jia Yuan, not Zhou Wang.","He stared straight at Jiang Cheng.","By now, he had fully grasped the situation—all these big strong young men... they were all taking orders from this young woman.","Turns out she was the real boss of the youth apartment complex all along."]},{"number":27,"title":"Chapter 27","paragraphs":["Everyone also looked toward Jiang Cheng.","Many people could offer suggestions, but the decisions came with responsibility—and facing blame after failure. Those who could make decisions always stood out from the crowd.","Zhou Wang looked at Jiang Cheng along with everyone else.","Jiang Cheng and Song Jingshuo exchanged a quick glance and understood each other perfectly.","“Alright,” Jiang Cheng answered.","Zhou Wang let out a quiet sigh of relief.","“People from our complex will assist you,” Jiang Cheng added.","One of the injured gritted their teeth. “This is a matter for our own complex!”","If not for those young people from the apartment building, they’d all be home by now. They were the bravest and most caring people in the complex—the only ones who dared to go downstairs and fight the zombies. Why did good people get no good reward?","The young people from the apartment building weren’t about to take that lying down. They shot back immediately: “If we hadn’t come to help, half of you would already be dead.”","“Still drawing territorial lines?” Jiang Cheng said. “The two complexes are separated by a road a few meters wide, and your main gate is hanging wide open. Go home, turn your wife and kids into zombies by biting them, and then think—are you sure they won’t stumble into our complex?”","“The virus doesn’t care which complex you’re from. Zombies bite whoever they see. Sir, if you go home, bite your wife and kids into zombies, and they come running into our complex, nobody here will show any mercy.”","This wasn’t just for the people from Jixiang Jiayuan—it was also for the people from the apartment building. With this level of contagion, there was no such thing as just minding your own business.","“There are too few of you. Our people will keep an eye on things, make sure everyone is registered, and send them back to their own homes to quarantine.”","“Old Zhou,” Old Huang said, “let’s do it that way. I’ll call my son down to help with the registry.”","He pulled out his phone from his shorts pocket and called his son.","While that was happening, the young people from the apartment building confiscated all the weapons from the injured.","A boy who looked to be in his early teens came running over with a pen and a notebook. “Dad! Dad—!”","Old Huang had fully calmed down by now. He briefly explained the situation to his son and said, “You help with the registration.”","Little Huang looked like a middle school student—a wiry, thin kid, his face ashen, his eyes filling with tears he tried hard to hold back.","He was the one who had helped Old Huang contact the other homeowners on the forum the whole time. He had wanted to come downstairs and fight zombies too, but both his dad and mom wouldn’t let him, so only his dad went down.","Why did it have to turn out like this? Wasn’t his dad supposed to come back home a hero?","The tense atmosphere between the two groups softened because of this father and son. The young people from the apartment building let out sighs too and stopped wanting to argue with the injured from Jixiang Jiayuan.","At the same time, they felt that being single had its benefits—when you died, you died. The apartment building had lost so many people already; they’d all been burned directly, no fuss made.","But seeing this—the young and the old, a family with responsibilities—it made people’s eyes sting.","Old Huang said nothing and gave his son a pat on the shoulder.","Little Huang wiped his eyes, glanced around, chose a spot by the flower bed, placed the notebook on it, and crouched down to start registering people.","With the help of the apartment building crew, they organized the people by building. After one building was fully registered, the uninjured residents of that building led the way, while a group of apartment building people escorted that building’s injured back to their homes.","Once they got to each unit, they not only explained the situation to the family members, but also knocked on the neighbors’ doors and called everyone out to explain the whole thing as well.","The families’ worlds collapsed.","The neighbors were also uneasy.","The people from the Youth Apartment said, \"Lock them in, you have to lock them in. If they turn, notify the person in charge of your complex—the specific contact info is on your owners' forum. They'll come handle it.\"","\"Don't ignore this,\" the Youth Apartment people warned. \"If you get bitten, you could turn. If you don't quarantine properly, the whole family's done for.\"","They also told the neighbors, \"You need to keep an eye on each other. If anything happens, contact us right away.\"","\"Door to door, balcony to balcony. If you don't watch out, the whole floor will be in trouble.\"","During this process, there was also an unexpected incident.","Not really unexpected—at this point it was practically the norm. It was someone from the same floor reporting that a certain unit seemed off.","They went over, knocked on the door, pressed an ear to it, and sure enough, something was wrong. There was that hissing gasp and hoarse throaty sound.","\"Damn,\" the Youth Apartment people said, already experienced. \"Probably the whole family turned together.\"","First they asked how many people were in the unit, then the young people put their heads together and used the same method Jiang Cheng had used before—making noise on the doorknob to lure the zombies into opening the door themselves.","But the zombies inside fumbled around for a long time, snarling the whole while, and just couldn't get the door open.","The next-door neighbor kept peeking through a crack in their door and saw what they were trying to do. \"Uh... our building's door locks—you have to do it like this, twist this part here to open it...\"","He even showed them his own lock.","The lock was different—not the kind you could open by pressing down on the handle. It had a twist mechanism you had to turn first.","The Youth Apartment people: \"...Why didn't you say so earlier?\"","They ended up breaking the door down by force.","Inside was a family of four: a young couple, a kindergartner, and a grandmother who helped take care of the kid.","Three of them were second-generation zombies, quick and agile.","Luckily, the Youth Apartment people were already well-versed in this. The young people had even devised a formation: the well-protected ones with shields stood in front to draw the zombies' attention, while the main damage dealers flanked them. People also had to be positioned right next to the door on both sides, to avoid the scenario that had happened at the Youth Apartment—\"the front zombies were held off, but the back zombies weren't protected.\"","In short, the young people were already skilled and experienced at fighting zombies. They positioned themselves rationally and coordinated seamlessly, taking down the entire family in a very short time.","The people of Ji Xiang Jia Yuan watched, stunned.","Among them, the father, mother, and grandmother were all second-generation zombies.","The original zombie was the little kid.","After it was all done, nobody felt any sense of accomplishment from killing zombies. Everyone was a bit gloomy and didn't want to talk.","They were about to leave when the neighbor got anxious: \"You're just leaving? What about these bodies? You can't just leave them lying in front of my door.\"","Everyone rolled their eyes in unison.","\"The bodies in your complex are your own problem.\"","\"We came to help, not to be your servants.\"","In the courtyard of Ji Xiang Jia Yuan, Zhou Wang pulled two more people aside—the three of them serving as the main organizers on this side—to listen as the Youth Apartment people shared the experience they'd accumulated over the past day.","This included quarantine, cremation of bodies, sweeping the buildings, and so on.","The young people from the Youth Apartment were one step ahead, and all this experience was now invaluable.","Only after doing all of this could a complex be completely cleaned out and restored to a level where residents could freely come and go downstairs.","Otherwise, everyone would have no choice but to hide trembling in their homes, and that would mean being trapped with no way out.","The reason some people in Jixiang Jiayuan had finally taken the lead to organize was that several households had already run out of food.","When Jiang Cheng was explaining the plan to sweep the buildings, a middle-aged man casually added, \"There's also the underground parking garage.\"","Jiang Cheng froze for a moment.","Right — the underground garage! How could she have overlooked that?","She shot a quick glance at Song Jingshuo, but he didn't look surprised or as if he'd just remembered. He seemed perfectly calm.","Suppressing her reaction, Jiang Cheng continued explaining to the Jixiang Jiayuan residents what they had already done and the lessons they'd learned from it.","Honestly, Jiang Cheng didn't think much of Zhou Wang. She could see too much hesitation in this middle-aged man's eyes. But the other two were even worse than him. At least Zhou Wang had been willing to step forward just now.","These middle-aged men were sluggish, dragging their feet, always second-guessing themselves, and slickly trying to dodge responsibility. But the office politics approach would cost lives in a situation like this.","Compared to them, the young people from Song Jingshuo and Li Jiangbing's youth apartment building gave off a refreshing sense of efficiency and decisiveness.","Anyway, Jiang Cheng finished passing on everything that needed to be said.","\"You have to be careful,\" she said. \"If you slip up even once, getting infected means death.\"","The middle-aged men sighed. \"Yeah, you're right.\"","No sooner had the words left their mouths than Zhou Wang's phone rang. An unknown number.","He answered. After a few seconds, his face turned grim. \"Got it. We'll come deal with it right away. Don't let him out. And you and your family need to be careful too.\"","Zhou Wang folded his phone shut, and everyone looked at him.","His expression was dark. \"It's Little Huang. Old Huang... has turned.\"","The other two gasped, shocked. \"That fast?\"","\"Some turn faster than others,\" Jiang Cheng said, glancing at the time. \"About the same. The fastest case we saw in our complex turned around one to two hours after being injured. But we've also seen ones that hadn't turned even after 24 hours.\"","Someone asked with a faint trace of hope, \"So could it be that they don't turn at all? Like, become immune?\"","Jiang Cheng replied, \"We can't be sure. Rabies can have an incubation period of years. And we're not doctors.\"","Disappointment played across the other person's face. He muttered, \"How do we deal with this... How...\"","Jiang Cheng didn't want to get tangled up with these older guys.","When the youth apartment people came back from sweeping the buildings, they decided it was time to head out.","Zhou Wang pressed his palms together and bowed in all directions. \"We're forever grateful. On behalf of Jixiang Jiayuan, thank you all!\"","But the young people were thinking about what they'd seen in the buildings — the old folks wailing in despair, the wives whose worlds had collapsed, the blank stares of the children...","The youth apartment residents had arrived buzzing with energy and heroism, but on the way back, they were unanimously subdued and silent.","Truth was, some of them had already lost touch with their families yesterday, and they'd already braced themselves for the worst. It was just that they'd been so busy — first surviving themselves — that they'd set their families aside. Their emotions had been carried along with the group the whole time.","Now the worry came flooding back. Someone made a call as they walked.","\"What's going on?\" the person on the phone muttered.","Someone beside them asked, \"What happened?\"","The person calling said, \"It was ringing with no answer earlier. Suddenly it just said not in service. We spoke yesterday.\"","Several people turned their heads at the same time to look at him.","\"What's going on?\" he asked, bewildered. He looked just like the middle-aged men from Lucky Garden.","The young people in the youth apartment weren't born from stones either—they had parents who raised them, just like everyone else.","In fact, everyone had probably already figured it out.","If you yank the battery out of a phone without turning it off first, the caller hears: \"The subscriber you are trying to reach is out of service.\"","Zombies are sensitive to sound.","What happens when a phone keeps ringing? The zombies wouldn't flip the phone open to answer—would they smash it with one swat, or knock it to the ground and send the battery flying?","Only then would the ringing, unanswered call turn into \"out of service.\"","Everyone understood.","It seemed that only this person, who was calling his mom and dad, didn't get it. All the way back to the youth apartment, he clutched his phone, head lowered, muttering, \"What's going on...\""]},{"number":28,"title":"Chapter 28","paragraphs":["Jiang Cheng asked Song Jingshuo, \"Do you have a car?\"","Jiang Cheng didn't have a car—or rather, \"Jiang Cheng\" didn't. So in the cognition Jiang Cheng received from the original \"Jiang Cheng,\" she wasn't familiar with underground parking garages at all. That's why Jiang Cheng overlooked the underground garage when making arrangements.","That should be it... probably.","Song Jingshuo answered as expected: \"Yes.\"","So Song Jingshuo clearly hadn't forgotten the underground garage the way she had.","Jiang Cheng said, \"I don't have a car, and yesterday I didn't think about the underground garage. Let's clean it up today.\"","\"Also, if there's any information I've missed, please, if you think of it, don't hesitate to bring it up.\"","Song Jingshuo glanced at her.","Earlier, when Old Huang had suggested home isolation, Jiang Cheng had used her eyes to seek his opinion.","Jiang Cheng wasn't someone who made decisions arbitrarily. An outstanding person not only knows how to listen to advice and suggestions but also knows how to collaborate.","He was the same.","Song Jingshuo admitted openly that he had indeed thought of it: \"I meant to bring it up today. I was too busy and didn't get the chance.\"","There wasn't much to fault there. Yesterday, Sunday, had been tense from morning to night—a whole day of sudden situations and too much to handle.","Whether someone had overlooked something or thought of it but didn't have time to say so, it was all understandable.","Jiang Cheng nodded. She took a couple of steps, then couldn't help saying, \"None of the others brought it up either? Not a single person thought of it?\"","She couldn't quite wrap her head around that. Whether Song Jingshuo had been intentional or not, he wasn't the only one on the provisional committee. Forget the committee—the whole estate had that many people. Was there really no one who thought the underground garage also needed cleaning?","Song Jingshuo's lips curved slightly—half mockery, half amusement.","Jiang Cheng raised an eyebrow.","Song Jingshuo explained, \"Someone must have thought of it. They're just waiting for you to arrange it.\"","Jiang Cheng had a sudden realization.","In just one day and one night, the youth apartment had already become a collective.","Once everyone had integrated into the collective—especially when the management group or the leaders had shown reliable management and leadership—people naturally and comfortably started waiting to follow instructions.","They all felt that Jiang Cheng and the provisional committee must have arrangements in place. Things had to be done one at a time. Even though they hadn't mentioned cleaning the garage yet, maybe after they finished the current tasks, they'd bring it up next.","So, why should I be clever and offer suggestions? I'll just wait for orders and follow the arrangements.","Compliance. Conformity.","That definitely had pros and cons. But Jiang Cheng weighed it up—for now, the pros far outweighed the cons.","The compliance, unity, and tacit coordination of the youth apartment, when compared to Jixiang Jiayuan, were clearly visible as being incredibly useful—exactly what was needed at the moment.","So let it be.","The walkie-talkie at her waist crackled. It was the person guarding the meeting room: \"There was a big commotion in the meeting room just now—sounded a bit scary. It's very quiet now. Not sure if inside... um...\"","Jiang Cheng thought for a moment and said, \"Make some noise. If it's still very quiet inside, then there's a living person.\"","If it were zombies—even though the second-generation zombies seemed considerably more agile than the original ones—they were still driven by some primal instinct craving flesh and blood. If they heard sounds or caught the scent of blood and flesh, they'd be unable to resist panting or letting out low growls.","If it was perfectly quiet, it could only be a living person.","The living didn’t want to make a sound.","The living shut inside, waiting to turn and die, didn’t want to answer the living outside.","The voice on the walkie-talkie went “Oh” and said, “Alright, we’ll try.”","But Jiang Cheng felt there was no point wasting manpower guarding the meeting room anymore.","“Master Luo, Master Luo,” she called.","Master Luo’s voice crackled back over the walkie-talkie: “Here, I’m here. Go ahead.”","“Does the property office have a welding torch?”","“Yes. What do you need welded?”","Jiang Cheng said, “Weld the meeting room door shut. Then block it up as well. Double insurance. Once that’s done, the interim committee members can pull out of the property office—no need to keep guarding the meeting room.”","Was that, in effect, pronouncing a death sentence on the people in there?","The interim committee members all paused mid-step, listening to her communicate with Master Luo.","A sigh from Master Luo came through the walkie-talkie, mixed with electrical static. But he didn’t object. He agreed: “Alright, we’ll get on it right away.”","Jiang Cheng instructed, “While welding, make sure people are on guard at the door—don’t let them rush out if they get the chance.”","She clicked off the walkie-talkie and lifted her eyelids. The people around her had stopped or slowed, waiting for her.","Jiang Cheng swept her gaze across them. Some met her eyes calmly; a few looked away.","But no one raised an objection.","That was good. The interim committee had been up for almost twenty-four hours now, and so far no one had openly opposed any of her decisions.","Even if some felt a weight on their conscience, they chose silence.","They also understood that certain decisions were for everyone’s good—as long as their own interests weren’t harmed, keeping quiet was the way to go.","Besides, most of them were single young people who hadn’t known each other before, just vaguely familiar strangers at best.","No families wailing, clinging, or throwing tantrums to block things, like in Jixiang Jiayuan.","Jiang Cheng skipped past the meeting room and jumped straight to the next topic: “There are two things now: one, we need to clear out the underground parking garage. But that’s not urgent, so we’ll set it aside for now.”","“The other, which I think is more pressing: I want to organize another supply run today.” Jiang Cheng checked the time—it was close to noon. “Let’s do it in the afternoon.”","“But we just did a supply run yesterday,” someone finally raised an objection. “Is it really necessary?”","Jiang Cheng knew someone would think that.","It was only too normal. That was how a lot of people were—as long as they could call the moment “safe,” that was safe enough.","They’d already snapped up enough food to last a week or two, so they figured that was enough, that was fine. Was it really necessary?","But Jiang Cheng couldn’t explain why she couldn’t bring herself to feel that kind of “safe.”","Ever since she woke up two nights ago and faced the first zombie of 0308—Little White’s Dad—she had entered a completely different state from before.","Or rather, she believed that this world had entered a completely different state.","This wasn’t like a flood, where the water would recede later.","It wasn’t like a typhoon, where the wind would stop eventually.","No. The world was simply different now. But it seemed not everyone could grasp that. They seemed to be waiting for the flood to recede, for the typhoon to stop.","Jiang Cheng stood on the residential street, and in that moment, it hit her like a bolt of clarity—the reason she had transmigrated here wasn’t to live out some dull nine-to-five ordinary day-to-day life.","【She had transmigrated precisely to meet a world like this!】","It had already been a week since that afternoon when Jiang Cheng realized she was a transmigrator.","But it wasn’t until this moment—bright sunlight at noon, surrounded and encircled by the crowd—that she fully shed the shell of “Jiang Cheng.”","She didn’t know who she was or what world she came from, but she understood her sole purpose now: to survive in this mutated world.","Song Jingshuo noticed for the first time that Jiang Cheng had paused for so long. She was usually quick to react.","He was about to smooth things over when he caught a faint flicker of expression on Jiang Cheng’s radiant face amid the dappled sunlight filtering through the trees.","Song Jingshuo was a master at reading people, but the change vanished in an instant—he didn’t have time to study it.","Looking again, she was still the same young, pretty, and composed girl, wearing a gentle smile as she patiently explained: “It’s not mandatory. Just a suggestion. The thing is, we need quite a lot of stuff, but we can only carry so much. Yesterday I filled both my handcart and my backpack, and I still couldn’t get everything.”","“Also, the municipal government has issued three official notices now. I think everyone can sense it—so far they still haven’t organized an effective response, which means the current situation might last longer than we initially expected.”","“I still think we should buy more supplies to feel more secure. Of course, no pressure—just a proposal.”","“I’m going to arrange another shopping run, mainly because there’s safety in numbers. Whoever wants to come, come along.”","The other person was convinced too: “Fair enough—I still have stuff I didn’t buy either.”","At the time, they had prioritized the most essential food items; the less important things were left behind, after all, a person only has two hands and one pair of shoulders.","Many people hadn’t managed to grab handcarts—they’d gone for supplies first, and by the time they checked on the carts, those were already snatched up. They had to lug everything home on their backs and in their arms.","The clever ones used suitcases, but back then, a lot of people hadn’t thought of that.","The members of the interim committee finalized the plan as they walked.","They posted the notice on the owners’ forum.","The property management had a megaphone, so they had someone carry it around to each building and shout the announcement.","Then each building was subdivided by floor; every building had several committee members, each responsible for a few floors, going up to those floors to spread the word.","No need to knock on every door—in a situation like this, yelling was the main method. Yell in the stairwell; stairwells carry sound well, and everyone could hear.","If someone was sleeping too deeply to hear, or missed the forum notice—well, tough luck for them.","The concrete execution plan was settled, and Jiang Cheng turned around to find Su Yu had been following her the whole time, trailing behind Li Jiangbing, sticking close to the committee members. Clearly, Su Yu had listened to the entire discussion.","“Ah, Su Yu,” Jiang Cheng greeted her. “This is Su Yu from Building 2. Su Yu, why don’t you join the committee too? There’s too much work and not enough hands.”","Su Yu had been sticking close precisely waiting for that invitation.","Yesterday afternoon, when the committee was first formed, she had hesitated and missed her chance to join. After Jiang Cheng woke her up to it last night, she regretted it. Today, she’d been looking for an opportunity to bring it up with Jiang Cheng.","She nodded immediately: “Okay.”","Jiang Cheng said, “You have a messaging app, right? Go back and join the group chat.”","“Oh, and add Master Luo as well. The property staff need to be part of the committee too.”","\"We shouldn't call ourselves the interim owners' committee. We should call ourselves the interim emergency response committee.\"","No one objected.","In fact, even during all the chaos yesterday, people were still contacting the property management about burnt-out light bulbs, blown fuses, clogged toilets, and the like. Someone had to deal with these things.","The property management office currently had no leader, so they couldn't just leave things unattended.","Jiang Cheng immediately used the walkie-talkie to communicate with Master Luo.","Master Luo was getting on in years, and his understanding of how society worked was actually deeper than that of the younger folks. He had realized yesterday just how significant and influential the interim committee's existence would be. Although the property management staff who were still stuck in the residential complex all listened to him now, and Master Luo himself was the head of the engineering department, he was really just a man used to keeping his head down and doing his work. Being \"head of the engineering department\" merely meant assigning tasks like, \"You go fix the electricity meter in Building 4, and you go unclog the toilet in Building 6.\"","Bringing the property management staff under the interim committee's umbrella actually suited Master Luo just fine.","In the face of a crisis that no one could handle alone, anyone with a clear head was afraid of being pushed to the sidelines."]},{"number":29,"title":"Chapter 29","paragraphs":["But Master Luo didn't have the messaging app everyone else used. He didn't even know how to use the internet.","That wasn't a problem though—Master Luo was just the property manager's representative. As long as the property office could stay in touch with the interim committee, things would be fine.","The girl from the property office, Yang Xinyan, had the messaging app. She joined the group chat on Master Luo's behalf. And if anything urgent came up, they could just use the walkie-talkie to call him directly.","Jiang Cheng asked Su Yu, \"Want to post the recruiting thread for the afternoon supermarket run?\"","Su Yu understood—Jiang Cheng was helping her stay visible in the group.","Su Yu agreed immediately. \"Sure.\"","They nailed down the time and details, got everything arranged, and everyone dispersed.","The young people had left with high spirits and fiery determination, but they came back much quieter. Some of them seemed to have aged a little over the course of a single morning.","Jiang Cheng also returned to her apartment.","Mo Li was still lounging in the beanbag chair, soaking up the sun. When he heard the sound of the door opening and closing, he lifted his head slightly.","He watched the girl step around the bed, pass the desk, and walk up to the beanbag chair.","She looked down at him.","Animals are more sensitive to certain things than humans. It was the same person, but something felt different.","Mo Li, of course, had no way of knowing that the old Jiang Cheng had actually been Jiang Cheng plus \"Jiang Cheng,\" while the Jiang Cheng standing before him now was simply Jiang Cheng and nothing more.","She had broken free of \"Jiang Cheng.\"","So she looked down at the black cat in front of her, and she was thinking—","Were those feelings of loneliness and the need for companionship truly hers, or were they leftovers from \"Jiang Cheng\"?","Because \"Jiang Cheng\" was the one who had lost both parents, had no relatives left, and had come alone to the big city—a lonely girl.","The transmigrated Jiang Cheng was not that person.","The transmigrated Jiang Cheng refused to be swayed by any memories or emotions left behind by \"Jiang Cheng.\"","If this had been the same peaceful life as before, she might have been able to accept and inherit \"Jiang Cheng.\" But now the world had suddenly changed beyond recognition. She felt she should just be herself.","Jiang Cheng crouched down, leveling her gaze with the black cat.","Mo Li let out a confused \"Meow?\"","Jiang Cheng tentatively reached out and touched the top of his head.","A fuzzy little head—soft, sending an indescribable sensation through her palm.","Jiang Cheng closed her eyes and savored it. When she opened them again, she was smiling.","It was her. It was really her.","She loved this feeling—fuzzy, soft, warm.","A little living creature, keeping her company.","This creature was so simple and pure. In front of him, she could completely let her guard down.","\"I'm a transmigrator,\" she said, rubbing his little head. \"Outside, there are zombies.\"","\"And what about you?\"","A little cat that could transform.","\"What are you?\"","Mo Li, of course, couldn't answer. Compared to humans, his skull was really quite small. How could such a tiny brain possibly process such a complicated question?","He couldn't give Jiang Cheng an answer.","He couldn't even understand Jiang Cheng's language.","But his emerald-green eyes were clear and beautiful.","Jiang Cheng touched her nose to his. \"You and me—from now on, we'll keep each other company.\"","There was no new announcement on TV. Just the same loop playing over and over.","There weren't even new news reports anymore—only pre-recorded dramas and variety shows.","Work stopped. Businesses closed. Transportation halted. Production ceased. Schools shut down. That included the jobs of people like reporters.","Flipping through channels, watching different dramas, gave the feeling that the entire city had ground to a halt.","Su Yu posted a new procurement recruitment thread on the owners' forum.","The interim committee members for each building divided up the work and made the rounds, floor by floor.","The property staff used megaphones and shouted at the base of every building.","It was a full three-dimensional notice system at this point—nothing left to chance.","The time was set for one in the afternoon, but surprisingly, the people from Jixiang Jiayuan headed out before they did.","The latest message to hit the owners' forum read: 【The people from Jixiang Jiayuan are out—a lot of them, looks like they're heading to Duoduo.】","The person who posted lived in a unit facing east, with a window overlooking the street beyond the east gate and also the west gate of Jixiang Jiayuan. The moment they saw it, they jumped onto the forum to post.","Not surprising—the people from Jixiang Jiayuan had been forced out in the first place because their supplies at home had run out and they had to brave the zombies to stock up.","The zombies inside their compound had been cleared out. Someone had taken the lead, and the main force was on the move.","Except for the children, almost all the adults had come out—plenty of them elderly men and women. Carrying backpacks, hauling bags, each person dragging a handcart.","But by then, it was already close to one.","Jiang Cheng heard the news over the walkie-talkie and said, \"It's fine. We got the jump on them once already. Everyone has basic supplies at home now. This trip is just to top up. However you look at it, we're still better off than them.\"","Mo Li had basked in the sun all morning, and he had visibly recovered a great deal.","He could stand up and jump to the ground now—though his legs gave out as he landed, sending him stumbling and rolling with a good bit of embarrassment.","But the little black cat immediately got up as if nothing had happened and walked over to his food bowl to eat and drink.","This filled Jiang Cheng with relief.","But when Jiang Cheng, dragging her handcart and wearing her backpack, was ready to head out, Mo Li clamped his teeth onto the hem of her pants.","Jiang Cheng looked down. Mo Li was looking up, snout protruding, emerald eyes squeezed up toward his forehead, staring at her.","\"Let go, good boy,\" Jiang Cheng said. \"I have things to do.\"","Mo Li did let go—but then he started scrambling up Jiang Cheng's pant leg, his claws piercing through the fabric and pricking her skin slightly.","\"Huh?\"","Jiang Cheng didn't resist. She let him climb, even extending her arm to give him support.","Mo Li stepped on her arm and climbed up to her shoulder, and then... settled down there.","Jiang Cheng was a little surprised. \"You want to come outside with me?\"","Mo Li: \"Meow!\"","If Mo Li had been an ordinary house cat, Jiang Cheng would have peeled him off her shoulder and set him back on the ground right then.","But Mo Li was a cat that could transform.","He had saved her life twice.","And one of those times was even before he could transform—when he was just an ordinary little black cat, he threw himself fearlessly at the security guard who had turned into a zombie, bravely saving her.","He nearly lost his own life in the process.","Mo Li was no ordinary cat.","He had mostly regained his mobility now, and he was clearly expressing his desire to go out with her. Jiang Cheng hesitated for just a moment, then agreed. \"Alright.\"","But having him lying on one shoulder made her load unbalanced. If she ran into zombies, she might not react fast enough.","Jiang Cheng first removed her backpack, then took a casual cloth crossbody bag from the rack by the door and slung it across her body. She opened the mouth of the bag. \"Come in here.\"","She tucked Mo Li into the crossbody bag. Mo Li didn't resist at all—he sat down inside obediently.","Jiang Cheng didn't bother zipping it up. She left it open, so Mo Li could either duck completely inside or poke his head out, whatever he pleased.","Good. And so, Jiang Cheng headed out with Mo Li in tow.","One o'clock, they gathered.","Sure enough, fewer people came than yesterday. There would inevitably be those who thought, \"We've got enough already—no need to risk it, just stay home and wait for rescue.\"","But still, more showed up than expected.","\"Let's go, let's go—don't let the Jixiang Jiayuan folks clean out the store.\"","\"We can't out-hustle those old folks anyway.\"","Under these circumstances, everyone actually managed to laugh.","\"Let's move, let's move.\"","Compared to the youth apartment, the organization was clearly much stronger.","First of all, the notification was well done. Whether you decided to go or not, everyone received the notice from the interim committee. Everyone knew what was happening, and knew the gathering time and place.","They were supposed to set out at one o'clock. Most people had already arrived by twelve fifty. They set off right on time at one.","So the group was dense and compact.","The Jixiang Jiayuan group stretched out long and thin, straggling along.","Jiang Cheng had already received the message before leaving that \"Jixiang Jiayuan is also going to BuyDuoDuo.\" By the time the youth apartment group set out, many residents of Jixiang Jiayuan were just coming out of their compound.","Their interim committee's notification was not up to par. Many people heard the commotion downstairs, opened their windows, saw everyone heading out, and only then realized the neighborhood was organizing a shopping trip. They scrambled to find their handcarts and rushed downstairs.","Some had received the notice, but their family members were hesitating: \"Let them go scout the road first. Once we know it's safe, then we'll go?\"","\"But we have to go together to be safe. If we wait until they're all back, do we really go by ourselves? Wouldn't that be even more dangerous?\"","\"That's true, but...\"","Time was wasted in this tug-of-war of hesitation.","The group gathering downstairs had already set off, and these people still hadn't even come down.","The only lucky thing was that the street they shared with the youth apartment—Jixiang West Street—had already been swept through by the young people on Saturday.","That street was now visibly safe. The zombies lay dead on the ground or dead inside cars parked along the road.","Severed heads rolled in the middle of the street. Shattered brains and brain matter splattered everywhere.","There were also many popped-out eyeballs. If you accidentally stepped on one, the feeling underfoot was something else.","Sickening, slippery, and with a strangely bizarre thrill.","Someone deliberately stepped on eyeballs and only stopped, disgruntled, after being scolded by others.","That was a bit twisted.","In short, Jixiang Jiayuan's group lacked organization. There was no concept of a vanguard or a rear guard, and no concentrated, well-protected escort team.","But thanks to the path the youth apartment had already cleared, they could still safely make it from their compound to BuyDuoDuo.","They even got nervous when they saw the youth apartment's main force coming out in full formation: \"Hurry, hurry! Walk faster! They're coming out too.\"","These were the same old folks used to fighting over discounted eggs. Unbelievable.","These people had no sense of gratitude at all.","In the morning, those young people had just helped them clear the zombies from their courtyard. Without the youth apartment's timely help, those uncles probably wouldn't have made it out in one piece—they'd all be injured.","If they were injured and then went home and bit their family members, the whole household would have been zombie-fied together.","The young people at the youth apartment felt quite displeased with the attitude of the Jixiang Jiayuan residents.","Someone in the owners' committee let out a snort.","Someone else swore.","Jiang Cheng said flatly: \"Don't bother with them. We're not doing this for them. We're doing it so our neighborhood won't become a zombie nest. As long as we achieve that, that's enough.\"","When Jiang Cheng put it that way, everyone felt much better immediately.","\"That's right. They're our neighbors. If they all got infected, in the end it'd be us who'd have to deal with it.\"","\"That's true.\"","\"Hey, what's going on up ahead? Why is it jammed up?\"","When they reached the street corner and turned east, there were people everywhere ahead, and they could faintly hear arguing coming from further up.","What's going on?","Jiang Cheng took the axe from her back waist and gripped it in her hand, then called out: \"Jiangbing!\"","Li Jiangbing was now perfectly in sync with her. He also pulled the fire axe from his belt, and his booming voice carried: \"Move aside, move aside! We're the youth apartment interim committee! What's going on up ahead? Move aside, we're going through to take a look!\"","The young men from the interim committee beside Jiang Cheng all raised their weapons—kitchen knives, baseball bats, iron rods, all sorts.","Su Yu also tightened her grip on her frying pan.","The people ahead were mostly from Jixiang Jiayuan. They turned around, saw this group that clearly looked ready for a fight, and silently parted to either side to make way.","Earlier they had quickened their pace, trying to get ahead of them.","Now that a problem had arisen, they moved aside to let the others head to the front and deal with it.","Ha."]},{"number":30,"title":"Chapter 30","paragraphs":["The group from Jixiang Jiayuan, led by Zhou Wang and his people, was already at the front, but they hadn't managed to solve the problem—the employees inside the Buyduoduo supermarket refused to open the door.","\"We're closed! We told you we're closed! Not happy about it? Go complain to the government! The news already said nobody has to work!\"","\"There's not a single grain of rice left in our homes! If you don't open up, what are we supposed to eat?\"","\"That's not our problem! Figure it out yourselves!\"","\"We've got elderly and kids to feed! Have you got any conscience at all?\"","Li Jiangbing and his men brandished their weapons, shouting as they shoved their way forward behind Jiang Cheng.","The Jixiang Jiayuan folks did step aside, but some grumbled: \"Yesterday when the people from Youth Apartments came, they opened up. Why won't they open for us today?\"","Zhou Wang and the others at the very front turned around at the sound of voices, and their faces lit up when they saw them: \"Xiao Jiang! You guys came too!\"","Someone immediately started complaining to Jiang Cheng: \"The supermarket folks won't open the door!\"","As if Jiang Cheng were some sort of leader of Jixiang Jiayuan.","Li Jiangbing found it downright ridiculous.","The people turned and cleared a path, and Jiang Cheng could now see directly through the glass door to the supermarket staff inside.","They were all holding weapons now too—neat, brand-new iron hammers, clearly fresh from the shelves.","Jiang Cheng walked up to the glass door. \"What's going on?\"","She recognized the man shouting from inside the glass door—the same brave soul who had ridden his motorcycle through a street full of zombies just to get to work.","From the looks of it, he hadn't gone home since yesterday.","The staff living in the supermarket dormitory were all lower-level employees, and he seemed to be the only supervisor. Yesterday those employees had listened to him quite a bit.","She remembered this young supervisor, and he remembered her too.","\"Oh, it's you,\" the young supervisor said. \"We're closed today. No business.\"","He held the hammer against his chest, his gaze locking with Jiang Cheng's.","Earlier, she'd heard him—he'd said the government had announced a shutdown of work and business.","That was true enough, no denying it.","But as she met his eyes, she saw something else in them.","Yesterday, before leaving, Jiang Cheng had reminded him to keep enough supplies for his own people too.","He'd taken that to heart.","But back then, everyone was only buying out of unease and immediate need. No one had expected that after a whole night, the rescue they'd hoped for wouldn't come, and the government would instead tell everyone to fend for themselves.","That meant the residents would have to survive on their own for much longer, with no support.","Supplies had become even more important.","It was clear this man had fully grasped the situation and thought it through.","The faint glint in his eyes plainly told Jiang Cheng the real reason he wouldn't open the door: he wanted to protect—or rather, hoard—the remaining supplies in the supermarket.","Given the current state of things, the store wouldn't be getting any restock either. Whoever held the supplies would be the one to last longer.","If this had been yesterday, Jiang Cheng might even have supported him. Because yesterday she too was still gauging things and hoping for rescue. But today, the situation was clearly worse than expected, and what he was doing now put him in direct conflict with her interests.","\"That's not going to work,\" she said. \"Everyone needs supplies. A lot of folks in Jixiang Jiayuan have no food left at home. You saw the news—there's no rescue coming. People have to go out and stock up themselves, or they won't survive.\"","The young supervisor waved his hand dismissively. \"That's not something I can handle. We're just a supermarket—a private business. It's not our responsibility. We don't have enough staff, and you people are disorderly. Our higher-ups told us not to open. If I opened and something went wrong, who's going to take responsibility?\"","This was the same man who'd braved a zombie-filled street just to clock in. His employee mindset was truly intact, still talking about \"who takes responsibility\" at a time like this.","Jiang Cheng couldn't help but smile.","She hadn't smiled in front of anyone these past few days. This was the first time.","Outside the glass, in the sunlight, the girl's smile revealed a row of snowy-white, even teeth.","The young supervisor was taken aback for a moment.","Then the girl took a step back.","\"Back up,\" Jiang Cheng said.","The ones packed at the front were all core members from the two residential complexes. The Youth Apartments people were already used to following Jiang Cheng's lead, and the Jixiang Jiayuan folks had seen today just how much weight her words carried. At her command, everyone at the front instinctively took a step back.","Trouble? What kind of \"trouble\" could there be? Locking out a crowd of people who had no food left—and expecting nothing to happen? That was the real trouble.","Jiang Cheng swung her fire axe.","A deafening crash—cracks spread across the glass door like a spider's web!","The young supervisor's pupils shrank. He shouted in alarm: \"What are you doing?! What are you doing?!\"","Jiang Cheng acted as if she hadn't heard. A second swing—the web expanded, and small fragments of broken glass tumbled down.","On the third swing, a second axe joined hers on the tempered glass.","Li Jiangbing's axe.","Right behind him came crowbars, hammers, kitchen knives, frying pans, baseball bats... all kinds of weapons rained down on the glass, producing a chaotic, ear-splitting clamor!","Some were from Youth Apartments, some from Jixiang Jiayuan.","Law-abiding citizens, no matter how many of them gather, will never have a second person make a move until someone makes the first one.","But once the first move is made, the second, third, fourth, fifth, sixth will follow right along.","Jiang Cheng was the one who broke that ice.","The supermarket had two glass doors at the entrance. Only the first door had a floor lock on it.","They were tempered glass, but with so many people working together, it broke quickly. Li Jiangbing delivered a heavy kick, snapping the crack-riddled glass—still clinging together like broken bones connected by sinew—right off the frame.","The young supervisor shouted curses: \"You're all insane! This is illegal!\"","At the same time, he called to his staff: \"Stop them! Stop them! Don't let them in!\"","He and the supermarket employees stretched out their arms, trying to block the crowd.","It was like a mantis trying to stop a chariot—utterly futile. Li Jiangbing alone could push two of them aside with ease.","He was big, but he had a little sense to him. When he shoved, he grabbed the front of their clothes so they wouldn't actually fall to the ground. Otherwise, with all those people surging in behind him, they'd get trampled.","That would be real \"trouble.\"","Only the outer door had been locked. The employees were pushed aside by the influx of people, pressed against either side of the small space between the outer and inner doors, their faces pale as they watched the unstoppable crowd.","Some were simply shoved right through the inner door.","People flooded in with a roar.","The young supervisor got squeezed against the side of the small vestibule between the two doors, his face a bitter grey as he watched the tide of people surge past him. Every single one of them was rushing, terrified of falling behind and missing out on the goods.","The girl with the axe had the weapon slung over her shoulder, pulling her handcart behind her. As she walked in, she glanced sideways at him.","Just yesterday she'd seemed like such a kind young woman—he'd even been grateful to her. Who would've thought he'd misjudged her so completely.","The young supervisor seethed with resentment.","One of the employees whispered to him: \"Brother Dong, what do we do now?\"","What else could they do? The supervisor, surnamed Dong, ground out between clenched teeth: \"Let it go cold!\"","There was no stopping it now—even more people flooded in, forcing them to shrink back again, terrified of being trampled in the crush.","Fortunately, one of the employees muttered quietly, “Good thing we moved some stuff into the dorms.”","The day before, thanks to Jiang Cheng’s warning, he’d told the staff to haul grain, canned goods, bottled water, and other essentials into the dormitory. The rooms were now packed to the ceiling.","Thank goodness they’d taken that step. No slacking off.","Actually, when he thought about it, they owed that girl a thank-you.","Sigh.","Yesterday, people from the Youth Apartments had still shopped in an orderly fashion—hurried, sure, but still like a normal supermarket run: grab your items, queue up, pay, leave.","Today, it was complete chaos.","For starters, the main grain shelves were empty. Supervisor Dong had taken his people the day before to strip the place, and he had no intention of opening for business today—no restocking at all. So people stormed straight into the warehouse, hauling things out directly.","Li Jiangbing and Song Jingshuo had known from the moment Jiang Cheng smashed that glass door that the broken order wouldn’t stop at just one door.","But the loss of control still exceeded what they’d expected.","The elderly weren’t as disciplined as the younger crowd. The store employees, still dazed from the break-in, hadn’t manned the registers. So the word “shop” had devolved into just “take.”","Some old folks even abandoned their little hand-pulled carts and shoved fully loaded shopping carts straight out the door.","Once one person did it, everyone followed suit.","The Jixiang Jiayuan residents had set the example, and though the Youth Apartments folks were a bit more civil, they caved after a moment’s hesitation. After all, there was no one at the cashiers.","“Brother Dong, is this okay?” one employee asked.","A few people had actually thought about manning the registers—they’d done it yesterday. But Brother Dong had told them not to.","Brother Dong let out a low chuckle. “If everyone paid up honestly, we’d be on the hook for that broken glass. But...”","But if this became a full-scale group looting, that glass door would be nothing. There was no way a handful of them could have stopped a crime of this collective scale. They could wipe their hands clean of any responsibility.","The more chaotic it got, the less blame fell on them. Let it be.","The shopping carts certainly had more capacity.","Jiang Cheng tucked her hand-pulled cart under a shopping cart and loaded everything she needed into it.","When Li Jiangbing saw her again, he was speechless: “Cat food again?”","Because ever since she’d made that unforgettable first impression two nights ago, she’d always struck him as calm and rational.","But every time it came to that cat of hers, she suddenly seemed to have nothing to do with words like “calm” or “rational.” She was actually wasting precious cart space on cat food.","He’d seen her grab a bag of cat food yesterday too. A bag of cat food took up even more room than a bag of rice.","“Me first, then the cat,” Jiang Cheng said, patting the satchel at her waist. “I don’t eat much anyway, and besides, this time it’s mostly human food, right?”","A dark, lumpy shape in the satchel suddenly blinked open two green eyes, making Li Jiangbing jump. “You brought it? I thought you left it at home today.”","Fair enough—Jiang Cheng doted on her cat way too much, but she had indeed prioritized her own needs yesterday. Today, her cart was mostly rice and canned goods. Not like those crazy foreign movies, at least.","When the shopping cart was full, Jiang Cheng pulled the hand-cart out from underneath and kept loading. She found some plastic rope at the service desk and tied the hand-cart to the shopping cart.","As she knelt down to tie the rope, she couldn’t help thinking how pathetic her carrying capacity was.","One person could only haul so much.","【If only I had storage space.】","Jiang Cheng froze.","What was that thought that had just flashed through her mind?","It felt like she’d said something in her own head, gone in a flash, and she couldn’t quite grasp what it had been.","Li Jiangbing called out, “You done yet?”","Jiang Cheng quickly finished the knot and stood up. “Done. Let’s go.”","Jiang Cheng and the others didn’t pay either. There was no one at the cash registers—nobody was paying. And everyone was just rolling the supermarket carts straight out the door.","It was a full-on robbery.","The store was in shambles, and from the direction of the warehouse, shouts and curses were still echoing.","Bad news: the rice was all gone.","Rice was the staple grain, the most important thing.","Because rice only needed water and heat—even if it didn’t cook into proper rice, it could become porridge. But flour? Half the people had no idea how to turn flour into food.","Yesterday, Jiang Cheng had said the Youth Apartments should stock up ahead of time, and that advice had fully paid off. The Youth Apartments residents had done two rounds of shopping and basically everyone had what they needed.","Not everyone from Jixiang Jiayuan, who’d only come today, got what they needed.","Song Jingshuo’s face was grim when they regrouped.","Jiang Cheng knew exactly what was on his mind.","The collapse of civilized order was terrifying.","What was even scarier was the snowball effect."]},{"number":31,"title":"Chapter 31","paragraphs":["“We can’t control what goes on outside,” Jiang Cheng said as she pushed her shopping cart down the road. “But inside the compound, we absolutely have to hold things together.”","The core members of the interim committee were used to sticking together—even those who had already filled their carts wouldn’t leave first; they’d wait for the group.","Song Jingshuo and Li Jiangbing walked on either side of Jiang Cheng, pushing three carts in a row.","Occasionally a car passed on the main road.","Someone muttered: “Who even goes out in weather like this?”","Where would they go, and for what? Wasn’t staying holed up at home the best option?","Yesterday you could still hear fire engines in the distance, and ambulances too. Today, both sounds were gone.","Combined with the news begging residents to fend for themselves, it left people silent.","But think about it—a fire scene that was already dangerous, you rush in to save someone, and the flickering shadow you see isn’t afraid of flames, doesn’t feel pain, doesn’t fear death—a zombie.","No matter how brave the firefighters were, they’d be walking into a death trap.","Or an ambulance picks up a patient, and halfway there, the patient’s eyes suddenly snap open—pitch black, no whites at all.","In that tiny space, blood splatters across the windows.","The more you imagine it, the heavier it gets. People’s hearts sank, and even their footsteps grew heavier.","Song Jingshuo wholeheartedly agreed with Jiang Cheng: “Right, we can’t let our compound fall into chaos.”","The supermarket earlier had been pure madness.","People were fighting over supplies.","Because the youth apartment had already done a bulk shopping run yesterday—over a thousand people—and Brother Dong’s group hadn’t restocked in time, some shelves of daily necessities were nearly empty, which sparked the scramble.","To be fair, it wasn’t the youth apartment people who threw the first punch—it was the old men and women from Jixiang Jiayuan.","In normal times, when the elderly were unreasonable, most young people really could only swallow their anger.","First, because after decades of education in this country, young people’s manners were genuinely a cut above the older generation’s. Second, because once you reached a certain age, even the cops couldn’t do anything to you, and prisons wouldn’t take you.","But these were not “normal times.”","That very morning, they’d helped clear zombies for those same Jixiang Jiayuan folks, and not a shred of gratitude did they show—instead, they acted like the young people were trying to steal the supermarket goods from them.","The youth apartment crowd was already simmering with pent-up rage, and then these old geezers dared to throw the first punch.","Did they still think these young people were the same as before?","They’d chopped off heads. They’d smashed in brains. They’d gone through the gut-wrenching necessity of escorting injured neighbors they had just fought alongside into quarantine.","The murderous anger had been bottled up for two days, and when the old man shoved them with petty arrogance, it exploded.","The young man hit back.","“Old bastard!” His eyes completely changed, and he threw a punch.","Everyone heard a clear, sharp crack.","The old man collapsed with a broken bone.","The old man groaned loudly; the old lady jumped up and down screeching curses.","“Keep cursing! I’ll hit you too!” The young man’s forehead bulged with veins as he pointed at the old lady and roared. “Think this is still the old days?! I’ve killed before! I’ve chopped off heads! Go ahead, call the cops if you can!”","The sheer, overwhelming violence in his rage stunned the old pair into silence. The groaning stopped, the cursing stopped—they just froze.","The young man turned away in fury and loaded things off the shelf into his cart. None of the surrounding old folks dared to contest him again.","A couple of other young men nearby watched with cold eyes.","If anyone else tried to throw hands, they would have stepped in. Who would they help? That was clear as day—their own people.","Watching these fierce, strapping young men, the old folks—who were used to spitting, smoking, cutting in line, and grabbing freebies—finally realized with a jolt that the world had changed.","That girl from the youth apartment had smashed a glass door with an axe, like shattering a seal and releasing some terrible monster.","A shadow loomed over those who weren’t young or strong enough.","Scenes like this—Jiang Cheng, Song Jingshuo, and the others had witnessed several of them in the supermarket just now.","The youth apartment, as a closed community, had remained orderly up until this morning. Everyone had been able to keep up a normal facade.","But after stepping outside and coming into direct contact with the Jixiang Jiayuan residents, something had subtly shifted.","And it wasn’t fair to say the Jixiang Jiayuan people had “infected” them.","Everything that had happened from the night before last to now was enough to drive anyone mad and break them. It was just that the youth apartment had been effectively organized from the very start—that sense of “collective” had kept the negative stuff in check, preventing it from boiling over.","Everyone had felt that “order” still existed.","Until now.","“We have to keep it under control.”","“Toward outsiders, we don’t have to hold back—but inside the compound, there has to be order.”","That was the consensus the core members of the youth apartment’s interim committee reached on their way back with the shopping carts.","The youth apartment had almost no elderly or children—the vast majority were young people. If rescue didn’t come soon, it was easy to predict things would only get worse than today.","Today, fights were just shoves and punches. Tomorrow, it might be knives.","So far, no one had killed or injured a normal person. The chopped heads and shattered brains had all belonged to zombies or the infected.","No one had yet turned a weapon against a healthy, uninfected living human.","But that might not last.","When it got to that point, the youth apartment—full of able-bodied young people—could become the most formidable fighting force in the area if they organized and managed themselves effectively.","At the thought, reactions among the core members varied.","Some were worried, deeply unsettled.","Others felt a small flame ignite inside them, stealing a glance at Jiang Cheng’s back as she walked ahead.","Song Jingshuo’s brows were knitted tight.","He had graduated from a top university, was highly capable in every way—a quintessential young urban elite. Elites like him could only rise higher by standing on the foundation of a rule-of-law society.","The more civilized and prosperous this society was, the more room people like him had to grow.","He had already bought a large flat this year, planned to finish the renovation by autumn, and move out of the youth apartment by year’s end.","Chaos was the last thing he wanted.","The more he thought about it, the heavier his heart grew.","He couldn’t help but glance sideways at Jiang Cheng. This girl had a strange, uncanny calm—talking to her gave you a kind of inner peace.","But Jiang Cheng stopped walking.","The moment she stopped, Song Jingshuo and Li Jiangbing stopped too, and everyone behind them had no choice but to halt.","Before anyone could ask “What’s wrong?”, Jiang Cheng had already let go of her cart’s handle, pulled her fire axe from the back of her waist, and strode straight toward a street-level shop along the road.","The perimeter of the youth apartment had a ring of commercial storefronts.","This area had high population density and heavy foot traffic, so the shops all managed to stay in business. There were small restaurants, fast food joints, hair salons, and more.","Of course, the shops were all closed now. Most had glass doors secured with U-locks; some had rolling shutters.","Jiang Cheng went directly for one of the glass-door shops with a U-lock.","Without a word, she swung the axe and shattered the glass door.","Everyone was stunned.","But Song Jingshuo said, “You all watch the carts,” then called out, “Jiangbing, let’s go.” He headed for the same shop.","Li Jiangbing followed without hesitation.","“It’s a pharmacy,” someone finally realized.","Someone grumbled, \"Why are those two the ones giving orders?\"","Someone shot back, \"If you're so good, you do it. If you can handle it, we'll listen to you too.\"","The first guy shut his mouth, looking sheepish.","\"But the pharmacy—are we not paying for that either?\" Su Yu asked hesitantly.","Everyone looked at her, then at the three of them.","Not paying at the Buy More supermarket had been following the crowd—those people from Jixiang Jiayuan all grabbed stuff and ran, so their Youth Apartment crew couldn't just stand there like fools and pull out their wallets. Mostly it was because the scene was already chaos, and the supermarket staff weren't even manning the registers, just watching.","So everyone had slipped into a sort of collective unconsciousness.","Following the herd.","But now...","Before anyone could finish looking, Jiang Cheng was already coming out with her arms stacked full of medicine boxes.","Right behind her, Li Jiangbing and Song Jingshuo emerged too, carrying just as many boxes.","The moment they'd gone inside, Jiang Cheng had said, \"Mainly grab fever reducers, respiratory meds, stomach and gut stuff, anti-inflammatories, and antibiotics—oh, and painkillers. Anything else you personally need, take it yourself.\"","The three of them walked out clutching bundles.","Jiang Cheng led the way, and she didn't head for her own car—she headed for their companions' shopping carts: \"Load it onto your own vehicles, no need to sort, just stuff it in, as much as you can fit. We'll coordinate rations later if anyone needs something specific.\"","Everyone swarmed, grabbing boxes from her arms and cramming them into whatever gaps they could find in their carts. The carts were already packed full, so they jammed boxes sideways and vertically—a few shoved between bags of rice and flour, and for the big rolls of toilet paper, they tore the plastic wrap and squeezed pills into the cardboard core.","Most medicine boxes were small enough that anywhere with a tiny bit of room, they forced them in.","Song Jingshuo and Li Jiangbing followed her example, not loading their own vehicles but distributing to everyone else.","The three of them handed out their hauls, then turned and went back in.","The second trip, they still shared with the others, but also started stuffing some into their own cars.","By the time they went back a third time, other people wanted to go in too.","In fact, from the moment Jiang Cheng had smashed the pharmacy's glass door with her axe, people had been watching.","The Youth Apartment's temporary committee had a habit of leading from the front during supply runs and covering the rear on the way back. That was exactly why so many able-bodied young people were willing to follow their commands—because they actually shouldered responsibility, carried the weight, and gave everyone a backbone.","So they were already the last group from Youth Apartment walking down the street.","Strung out behind them were all the Jixiang Jiayuan folks. Many of the elderly moved slowly, and after the big crowd left, they'd lingered with a \"picking through leftovers\" mentality. So they'd actually left the supermarket even later than the young ones.","From a distance, they spotted the Youth Apartment kids gathered outside a shopfront. They muttered, \"What are they doing now?\"","They shuffled closer, watched for a moment, and understood: after robbing the supermarket, now they were robbing the pharmacy.","The old people almost slapped their thighs. \"We need to stock up on meds too!\"","Old age came with a hundred aches and ailments—they needed medicine far more desperately than the young.","One old man lifted his foot to climb the steps and follow inside.","Just then, Jiang Cheng and the other two were coming back out to the doorway. The old man tried to squeeze past.","Jiang Cheng swung her axe in a sharp arc through the air, freezing the old men and women in place at the bottom of the steps.","\"Us first.\" She pointed the axe at the people below, her voice icy. \"We finish, then you go in.\""]},{"number":32,"title":"Chapter 32","paragraphs":["An elderly woman, frustrated by Jiang Cheng's obstruction, snapped, \"Young lady, how can you be like this? We are old people. We have many illnesses. We need our medicine.\"","\"I know, we're saving some for you, but we're taking ours first,\" Jiang Cheng said.","The old woman cursed, \"Young lady, how can you be so selfish!\"","She tried to push her way in.","She was somewhat afraid of the able-bodied men, but Jiang Cheng was just a young woman. And a pretty one at that. Pretty girls have thin skin; the prettier they are, the more they fear losing face.","Middle-aged and elderly women fear nothing more than young girls.","The old woman didn't dare push against the men. She assumed the young woman would be the easiest to break through. She pressed her chest against Jiang Cheng's axe and tried to climb the steps.","But Jiang Cheng was not like the young women she had dealt with before.","Jiang Cheng shoved her axe forward hard, sending the old woman stumbling backward. Had the old man behind her not caught her in time, she might have landed flat on her bottom and shattered her tailbone.","\"You—\" The old woman couldn't believe it.","More and more people were taking notice of the pharmacy, craning their necks, itching to make a move. Jiang Cheng didn't bother arguing with her. She just called out, \"Jiangbing!\"","Li Jiangbing stood on the steps, brows furrowed with rage, holding an axe.","He was the most effective one. The moment he stood there—big frame, bulging muscles, like a door god—no one dared step forward anymore.","Jiang Cheng called again, \"Su Yu! Peng Ze! Come help.\"","Su Yu lived in the same building as her. Peng Ze was someone among the people she'd interacted with over the past couple of days who was most convinced by her words.","Peng Ze was the one who had rolled his eyes and talked back to the other person earlier.","Hearing Jiang Cheng call for help, Su Yu immediately went over. Peng Ze, however, cast one more glance at the man who had muttered, \"Why should we listen to them?\"","Why?","Now they knew, didn't they?","Li Jiangbing guarded the entrance, and no one dared approach.","The rest of the group, without making a fuss, either pulled weapons out of their shopping carts or from their belts, gripping them in their hands.","Some also pulled the shopping carts of the people who had gone to grab medicine closer inward. Everyone held their weapons, spreading out in a circle around the carts to guard them.","Because it was true—some people's eyes kept drifting toward their shopping carts.","They were the rear guard, at the very back of the main group.","But the ones from Jixiang Jiayuan who lagged behind were some of the old, weak, sick, and disabled—slow-moving, slow-handed—which was why they were in the back. Some hadn't managed to grab the scarce supplies they needed. Their eyes on Jiang Cheng's group's overloaded carts carried a hint of intent.","The moment everyone pulled out their weapons and formed a protective circle around the carts, those people looked away.","When Su Yu entered the pharmacy, she saw it was a tiny community convenience pharmacy, not big at all. Jiang Cheng and the others had cleared the shelves of needed medicine and even kicked open the storeroom door, hauling everything straight out of the back.","\"Use plastic bags,\" Su Yu said, pulling a big stack of plastic bags from behind the counter.","Jiang Cheng explained the priorities for which medicines to grab to Su Yu and Peng Ze.","Su Yu happened to be standing in front of the heart medication shelf, and casually asked, \"What about heart medicine?\"","\"Heart medicine? No need,\" Jiang Cheng replied.","\"In times like these, heart conditions...\" she said coldly, \"what would be the point.\"","The pharmacy went silent for a moment.","Song Jingshuo's hands paused mid-motion as he was packing medicine. He turned his head to look at Jiang Cheng.","Heart patients can't run or jump, can't even take a fright.","Luckily, the youth apartment community had mostly young people, so the chances of heart conditions existing were low.","Song Jingshuo thought he was already quite survival-of-the-fittest. But Jiang Cheng... Jiang Cheng seemed even more ruthless than that.","Su Yu let out a low \"oh\" and continued packing medicine into the plastic bags.","Song Jingshuo turned back around as well.","They filled the plastic bags with medicine, carried them out bag by bag, and tied them to the rails of the shopping carts.","People needed so many supplies, yet their carrying capacity was so poor. If the situation worsened in the future, this would really be a deadly problem.","Jiang Cheng thought about this as she tied plastic bags to the cart rails.","[If only I had a storage space.]","The moment this thought flashed through her mind again, Jiang Cheng's pupils dilated.","This time, she caught a glimpse of the fleeting information in her mind!","[Storage space]?","And this time, she clearly felt a strange sensation—like an extremely faint electric current racing through her body and brain.","She had felt this before, a week ago. On that Saturday afternoon, she had suddenly awakened to the realization that she was a transmigrator. It was the same feeling. Only this time, it was much lighter.","A week ago, she had awakened to the awareness that she was not originally from this world, that she wasn't \"Jiang Cheng.\" But information like \"who am I\" and \"where do I come from\" was completely absent.","As if her memories were locked away.","Now, it was like a sliver of information had leaked out through a crack.","What was a \"storage space\"? Jiang Cheng felt like she knew but couldn't say.","The people from Jixiang Jiayuan watched helplessly as every shopping cart was covered in hanging plastic bags.","\"Leave some for us,\" some old men and women said, with tears in their voices.","Jiang Cheng stood up and looked around. Each of their carts was stuffed and hung full of medicine.","\"That should be enough,\" Jiang Cheng said. \"Let's go.\"","Everyone put their weapons away again, pushed their respective carts, and headed toward the community gate.","Li Jiangbing also tucked his axe into his belt, walked down the steps, and pushed his own cart.","The old men and women surged into the pharmacy in a flood.","Jiang Cheng and the others had only walked a few steps ahead when they heard shouts and curses erupt from the pharmacy behind them.","In the old days, if there was drama to watch, people would stop and linger over it.","Now, no one cared. They walked steadily, heading straight back into their own community.","They were the rear guard. Once they entered, the security guard locked the gate.","A full sense of safety.","The security guard seemed to be in a good mood too, and even asked, \"I heard you didn't pay?\"","Master Luo and the others had gone to Duoduo Supermarket too. This time, without Jiang Cheng and Song Jingshuo footing the bill, they were bolder and grabbed freely. They brought back way more than last time. Not for themselves—for the entire property management staff.","\"Yeah,\" everyone said. \"No other choice. We'll deal with it later.\"","The security guard didn't have their level of moral scruples, thinking that these college-educated people were still talking about paying back later—too book-smart for their own good.","Regardless, more supplies meant the security guard felt more at ease.","He was lucky to be a security guard at this youth apartment. He knew the guard across the street at Jixiang Jiayuan, and it seemed he was already dead.","Sigh.","The courtyard of the community still carried the lingering stench of burning corpses.","But there weren't many people around—they had all just finished gathering supplies and had gone home to put things away.","They stopped: \"Jiang Cheng, these medicines...\"","In theory, as the provisional committee, they had taken these medicines on behalf of the whole community.","Jiang Cheng said, \"If we pool them all together, the responsibility of looking after them would be too great. It would also be easy for trouble to arise. Let's do it this way—we split up, each person takes their own share back. When needed, we'll coordinate.\"","People can't avoid selfishness. Especially in times like this, the more supplies you have in hand, the better.","Medicine is a unique and vital resource.","All the way back, everyone had actually been thinking about how Jiang Cheng would handle things, and whether she would make everyone hand over their supplies once they returned to the neighborhood.","But Jiang Cheng was, after all, Jiang Cheng. She gave everyone the solution that each person most wanted to see.","Even Su Yu—who considered herself a good person, an upright person, a kind person—believed that it was better for the group to each hold and jointly manage the medicine supplies.","Following closely with the temporary committee's actions had truly been the right choice.","And she had to thank Jiang Cheng for pulling her into the committee at noon, or she wouldn't have gotten a share of the spoils.","She knew—she had to stay close to the core of the group.","She had always had stomach problems, and when the pain flared up, she needed medicine.","If she couldn't hold her own medicine supply, and had to beg someone for medicine when she needed it, what if they made demands?","With luck, the other person might not be that twisted, but what if they copped a feel while handing you the pills, or cracked a dirty joke? What would you do then?","Would you curse them or not? Would you take the medicine or not?","Su Yu had been out in the real world for a few years now. Once a girl leaves campus and strikes out on her own in the working world, she stops being naive.","In those years alone, she'd already run into plenty of crap—both the obvious and the subtle kind.","From the very beginning, Jiang Cheng had been handing out medicine to everyone, grabbing a handful for you and a handful for me. That had worked out perfectly—each category of medicine was evenly distributed, so the \"inner circle\" of the committee wouldn't get into conflicts over resource gaps.","\"Everyone's got around the same amount. The amounts per building are about the same too,\" she instructed. \"Each building manages its own floor. When people in your building need help, do your best to provide it. If we can't be of any help at all, then what's the committee even for?\"","Everyone nodded in agreement. \"Yeah.\"","But then she added, \"Still, don't go around acting like you're scattering alms to the poor. These meds look like a lot, but think about how many households and how many people are in one building, and then think about how many people are in the whole neighborhood. Keep a tight grip on them.\"","Everyone understood. \"Got it.\"","They agreed to take care of cleaning out the underground garage later, and the group split into six parties, each heading toward one of the six buildings.","Entering Building 2, a few of them waited for the elevator together. Each person was pushing a shopping cart, so at most two people could squeeze into one elevator.","Someone went in first and called over to Su Yu, but Su Yu said, \"I'm going up with Jiang Cheng.\"","Everyone could tell Su Yu had something to say to Jiang Cheng. Li Jiangbing went up ahead instead. \"See you tonight.\"","In the elevator lobby, only Jiang Cheng and Su Yu were left. Jiang Cheng turned to look at Su Yu. \"What's up?\"","Su Yu bit her lip.","Jiang Cheng said, \"Go ahead.\"","\"I feel really uneasy, deep down,\" Su Yu confessed. \"Jiang Cheng, I've been thinking the whole way back. Maybe we shouldn't have broken down the front door of Buydodo Sushi.\"","Jiang Cheng understood.","Actually, she'd felt it on the road earlier—Song Jingshuo had wanted to bring this up with her too. He'd looked at her several times, hesitating, but never found the opening to start the conversation.","Because the \"shouldn't have done it\" part was Jiang Cheng's own doing. You couldn't raise a criticism of Jiang Cheng in front of everyone—it had to be hashed out in private.","Jiang Cheng had a strange feeling about it.","Su Yu and Song Jingshuo—people like them—were clearly still bound by the world's laws and morality. Of course, these weren't iron rules. Give them more time, and they might break through them on their own. Or, like today, with her taking the lead, they followed.","But the restraint was definitely there for them, needing to be overcome.","Not for her, though.","No matter which world she had come from, as long as human civilization and society existed, no society could be without morality and law.","But that thing couldn't restrain her for even a second.","Why was that?"]},{"number":33,"title":"Chapter 33","paragraphs":["Was she some kind of lawless outlaw?","Since awakening, Jiang Cheng had always felt that just getting through the present was enough. Later, when the zombies broke out, she figured survival was her immediate goal.","She had zero interest in \"who I am,\" \"where I come from,\" or \"what kind of person I used to be.\"","Because those were all \"the past.\" Her eyes were fixed only on \"now\" and \"the future.\"","The \"past\" was over and done with—not worth the time to look back at.","But now, she found herself mildly curious about what kind of person she had been.","These thoughts flickered through her mind and passed in an instant. Pulling back to the present, she saw Su Yu standing before her, looking slightly uneasy and lost.","[Companions are meant to be filtered.]","This idea popped into her head unbidden—","Useful to me, or useless to me.","Of great use to me, or of little use to me.","In comparison, if it were Li Jiangbing standing there in confusion, Jiang Cheng would break through his haze and drag his rationality back to the same understanding she had.","Li Jiangbing's strength could do the work of two men, and his build and appearance were imposing. He only had to stand at the pharmacy door, and the old men and women wouldn't dare come forward. It saved tremendous effort.","If it were Song Jingshuo, Jiang Cheng would also have plenty of motivation.","Because among the building leaders, Song Jingshuo's organizational and mobilizational abilities were clearly a cut above the rest.","He was also very useful.","Compared to Su Yu, those two had more \"value\" to Jiang Cheng.","Su Yu had shown bravery and composure last night, and Jiang Cheng thought more highly of her for it, willing to give her a hand and a push.","But when she showed a moment of weakness, Jiang Cheng found herself losing interest.","Yet a rational person can't make decisions based on interest alone.","Suppressing her feelings, Jiang Cheng comforted her: \"In extraordinary circumstances, we can't cling to the old rules.\"","\"If we're not the ones to break down the door first, someone else will. And then the say-so won't be in our hands.\"","Jiang Cheng's comfort to Su Yu was extremely simple. She had a feeling that every extra word cost her a huge amount of energy.","Su Yu seemed to have more she wanted to say, but just then the elevator arrived.","Jiang Cheng said, \"The elevator's here. Let's go.\"","She took the lead and pushed her cart on. Su Yu quickly followed.","Jiang Cheng lived on the third floor, and the elevator climbed for just a few seconds before stopping. Jiang Cheng said, \"See you tonight.\"","Su Yu also said, \"See you tonight.\"","Jiang Cheng pushed her cart out of the elevator.","Su Yu went silently up to her own floor alone.","Back in her apartment, she didn't rush to tidy up. Normally she was a girl who loved things clean and orderly, who enjoyed organizing and cooking. But now, with her clothes stained by all kinds of disgusting fluids, maybe even carrying some residual bits of organic tissue, she felt nothing.","A whole cart of things sat by the door, and whether to organize them or not didn't matter at all.","Just like Jiang Cheng, she peeled off her \"combat clothes\" at the entrance, changed into loungewear, and went inside. She opened the fridge, grabbed a carbonated drink, and a big mouthful of cool fizz went down—she couldn't help but let out a satisfied sigh.","She sat at her computer desk, turned on the computer and messaging app, and pinged another girl from the neighborhood.","They hadn't known each other before—only met in the last couple of days. They had fought together and scavenged together. She was also a brave, independent girl who shared her temperament, so they had exchanged messaging IDs.","That girl had returned to the neighborhood a bit earlier and was in her place tidying up today's haul.","[I grabbed four jars of fermented bean curd!] the girl messaged. [I'm telling you, this stuff goes great with rice. Pairs with mantou, congee, even plain rice. I think we won't be cooking like we used to in the coming days.]","Su Yu agreed with her, then told her about how the neighborhood committee had ransacked the pharmacy.","Girl: [The neighborhood committee is badass! That's exactly what should be done!]","Su Yu: [Jiang Cheng said the committee members in each building have roughly the same supply of meds. People from each building should first go to their own building's committee, and cross-building swaps can happen when needed. But I also have some on hand. If you ever get harassed by the men in your building, come straight to me.]","After a pause, she added: [Or Jiang Cheng.]","The girl replied: [Thank you! So glad we have you both! The moment you mentioned it, I thought of that. Ugh, having fewer women really makes you worry about this stuff. Some men really do take advantage of the situation. Good thing Jiang Cheng is a woman.]","Su Yu paused for a moment.","In truth, Su Yu didn't really have much say in things. She had even been trying to stay close to the core of the neighborhood committee out of fear of being sidelined.","But that didn't stop her from understanding and accepting Jiang Cheng's comfort.","But neither did it stop her from finely and sensitively sensing Jiang Cheng's perfunctory attitude toward her just now.","Last night, when they were sweeping the buildings, Jiang Cheng had trusted her to help in that moment, and she had delivered. When Jiang Cheng offered her fist afterward and Su Yu bumped it, her heart had felt warm and blazing.","Today, Jiang Cheng had even pulled her into the committee.","Unconsciously, she had drawn closer to Jiang Cheng.","But just now, Jiang Cheng had shown her coldness.","That coldness was exactly like the indifference she displayed in the pharmacy when she said heart disease had no point in being treated.","Su Yu felt uneasy inside.","She couldn't help typing: [Don't you feel like Jiang Cheng is...]","The other girl, tidying things up while occasionally glancing at the screen to see if she needed to reply, turned her head and saw the chat box displaying \"typing...\" below.","She waited a moment, but the prompt disappeared—Su Yu hadn't sent the new message.","After a bit, the prompt appeared again, and Su Yu sent: [Yeah. Fortunately.]","In Building 2, Su Yu sat at home biting her finger joints.","She hadn't sent that sentence—she had deleted it.","It's probably not Jiang Cheng's problem, she thought. It's probably mine.","Yeah, it must be my problem.","I shouldn't have said those things, right? Jiang Cheng must think I'm being a hypocrite.","Su Yu felt she should reflect on herself.","Because she had been watching Jiang Cheng since yesterday morning. Every step Jiang Cheng took, she admired.","Last night, when that injured man was hysterical and trying to take everyone down with him, if it hadn't been for Jiang Cheng's look of trust and encouragement, she might not have found the courage to strike a living person who hadn't yet turned.","Today, Jiang Cheng had even brought her into the committee.","How could she question Jiang Cheng?","So the reason fewer people step up is because the ones who do have to endure this kind of backlash and doubt face-first.","Thinking about how she had almost sent a message questioning Jiang Cheng to someone else, Su Yu couldn't help feeling guilty.","Little did Su Yu know, at nearly the same moment, Jiang Cheng was also reflecting on her own perfunctory behavior.","Jiang Cheng got home, closed the door, and a half-cracked mirror on the doorstep reflected her face.","Jiang Cheng stared into her own eyes in the mirror—","What kind of person were you before?","No matter who you were before, in this world right now, you're just an ordinary person. No power, no resources.","This attitude of looking down on others can't continue.","[That's the mindset of someone who holds power and resources at the top. You're not that. You don't have it.]","Peng Ze wasn’t in the same building as Song Jingshuo, so he split off and headed home to his own building.","Song Jingshuo walked back to the elevator lobby of Building 4 with the rest of the people from that building.","Everyone was chatting casually when suddenly someone laughed and said, “Jingshuo, I’ve been thinking—how is it that our interim committee is full of grown men, yet we let a woman take charge? I think it should’ve been you.”","The elevator lobby went quiet, and everyone turned to look at the speaker.","This was the same guy who had muttered in front of the pharmacy, “Why are the two of them calling the shots?” and had gotten a cold glare from Peng Ze.","His name was Wang Haotian. Before that, Song Jingshuo had run into him on the stairs—just a familiar face, a neighbor. Now that they had both joined the provisional committee, after only a day and a half they were already on familiar terms and could call each other by name.","But that day and a half had been so hectic that there hadn’t been time to really get to know the people around them.","At this moment, though, a single sentence laid bare a person’s character.","Song Jingshuo lifted his eyelids and gave him a glance.","He remembered that last night, it had been Wang Haotian who joked, “You wouldn’t want a girlfriend like Jiang Cheng.”","Yesterday, he’d had some competitive intent against Jiang Cheng, sure—and it wasn’t surprising that others had picked up on it.","But now, Song Jingshuo genuinely regretted it.","Because Jiang Cheng must have seen it too. How had she looked at him back then? Was it the same way he was now looking at Wang Haotian—like he was some kind of idiot?","When it came to office politics, he wasn’t afraid of anyone. Guys at Wang Haotian’s level were no match for him. This kind of petty provocation was child’s play.","But what time was this? Playing politics now?","Had Jiang Cheng been just as speechless facing him yesterday?","The moment Song Jingshuo thought about that, shame and irritation burned through him.","It wasn’t that he feared stupid people failing to understand him.","But being looked down on by someone equally sharp-witted—that was genuinely hard to take.","“What does gender have to do with it at a time like this?” Song Jingshuo said lightly. “You’re a man too—how come your dick didn’t make you the leader?”","When no women are present, men have no trouble saying the names of their genitalia, even using the crudest vocabulary. Even the ones who usually look polite and well-mannered in public.","Everyone burst into loud laughter.","Wang Haotian forced a couple of dry laughs, thinking to himself: Wasn’t it you who deliberately pointed out Jiang Cheng was a woman yesterday? Wasn’t it you who fought her to win over the property management staff?","And now you’re pretending to be the righteous one?","But then his mind turned to Jiang Cheng’s pretty face. Even though he’d joked “you wouldn’t want a girlfriend like that,” he couldn’t deny Jiang Cheng’s beauty.","The group split up into different elevators.","Inside his elevator, Wang Haotian said to the people riding with him, “Song Jingshuo did a complete 180—you don’t think he’s got a thing for Jiang Cheng, do you?”","The other person: “Huh? Does it seem like that?”","“Why else would he suddenly start backing her up?” Wang Haotian said. “Look, I was originally sticking up for him, and now I’m caught in the middle feeling like I’m the bad guy.”","The other guy snickered and only said, “Jiang Cheng is pretty, that’s for sure,” and didn’t say more.","That evening after dinner, everyone gathered at the entrance to the underground parking garage as arranged.","Jiang Cheng wore her crossbody bag, one hand still slipped inside it.","Song Jingshuo knew immediately: “You brought your cat again?”","Everything about Jiang Cheng looked good to him now. Pretty face, sharp mind, strong decision-making.","It was just this habit of bringing her cat everywhere that was a bit of a flaw.","But then he remembered: she’d said yesterday that both her parents had passed away, and the cat was her only family. At the time, he hadn’t paid attention—his mind had been solely focused on competing with her to win over the property staff.","Now that he recalled it, he saw Jiang Cheng smile gently, her hand stroking the cat’s head inside the bag, saying, “It won’t slow me down.”","Even as an adult, without parents, she was an orphan in a way.","Lonely enough that she couldn’t bear to be apart from her cat.","Song Jingshuo felt a sudden softness in his chest. He was about to say something comforting when Jiang Cheng pulled an axe from behind her waist, swung an X-shaped arc through the air, and said, “Let’s go!”","She led the way down into the parking garage.","Song Jingshuo had no choice but to hurry after her.","The recruited suicide squad followed along.","There were quite a few of them—an impressive, sprawling crowd."]},{"number":34,"title":"Chapter 34","paragraphs":["Clearing out the garage wasn’t about charging in blindly. In fact, after the past two days, the young residents of the apartment complex had basically figured out the traits of both the original zombies and the second-generation infected ones, so they had a battle plan.","Master Luo grabbed two rolls of barrier tape from the property storage room.","Everyone stretched the tape across the downward ramp entrance of the underground garage, two strips spaced about four or five meters apart, positioned at shin height.","Both ends were held firmly by people, using the tape as trip ropes.","Once ready, someone tossed a cooking pot down the ramp.","The pot clattered and banged its way down, rousing the zombies inside the garage.","Because there were no living people in the garage and it was fairly soundproofed from the outside, these zombies had been drifting around slowly, some even standing almost still in place. They looked like NPCs in a game that hadn’t been triggered yet.","But with all that racket, the zombies stirred and moved toward the source of the noise.","The people outside the entrance watched as the zombies gradually gathered along the path the pot had rolled, and then they started banging on the pot lid with a loud clang.","The zombies turned toward the ramp entrance and came shambling up.","This was when the difference between the second-generation infected zombies and the original ones became crystal clear — the ones leading the charge were all second-generation zombies.","The second-generation ones moved way faster than the original zombies, who stumbled and lurched with uncoordinated limbs!","They watched as those few pulled further and further ahead of the rest, getting closer and closer.","The young people tensed up, gripping their weapons tightly. “Here they come, here they come!”","“Hold the ropes!”","At that, everyone pulling the trip ropes clenched the barrier tape even harder to keep from letting go.","The next second, a massive force yanked at the ropes!","The plan worked. The leading second-generation zombie was tripped and sent flying. It was moving so fast that it even soared over the second trip rope before hitting the ground.","The moment it landed, a barrage of assorted weapons smashed its skull in.","Second-generation zombies had coordinated limbs and quick agility, but their vision was poor in dim light. They were also completely driven by instinct — their craving for flesh and blood being their only motivation — and they lacked any ability to think.","For them, if there was an obstacle on the direct path toward flesh, they would rely on their jumping ability to leap over it.","Last night, the reason the team clearing the fifth floor of Building Two got hurt was that a second-generation zombie in that room had stepped directly on an original zombie in front of it and jumped out.","But at dusk like this, trying to spot trip ropes at their feet was too much to ask of them.","The two trip ropes ensured that even if a zombie happened to avoid the first one, it couldn’t avoid the second. As long as they tripped and hit the ground, they were either bashed in the skull with a hammer or had their necks chopped by a cleaver.","There weren’t many second-generation zombies — only eight came charging out, and they were all dealt with quickly.","What followed were the original zombies. Because of their poor coordination, the steep ramp slowed them down, and many fell and ended up crawling.","They had already been left behind by the second-generation ones, and now the gap only widened. That gave the suicide squad more time to adjust and prepare.","It almost got a bit leisurely.","They just waited for the rest of the zombies to stagger up or crawl up, then took them out one by one.","After smashing one with a hammer, someone said, “This is kind of like whack-a-mole.”","Was that finding humor in misery? It was a disgusting, terrifying scene, after all.","But somehow, cracking jokes like that made it less disgusting, less terrifying, and less oppressive.","Everyone cheered in response. “One comes, one dies!”","A lot of volunteers had signed up for this mission. The apartment complex was just stacked with manpower. Whether it was fighting or doing work, there was no shortage of people.","Of course, with a few thousand people in the neighborhood, there were bound to be the self-serving types who never lifted a finger. But those people hid in their rooms or buried themselves deep in the crowd, so no one really knew them.","The people everyone recognized were the ones who had been fighting side by side over the last two days.","Because there were so many people, Jiang Cheng and Song Jingshuo, along with the other core members, didn’t even need to push to the front — not even Li Jiangbing.","But Su Yu was right up at the front.","Her frying pan was good quality — not one of those thin, cheap ones. It was thick and heavy, a bit of a weight to swing.","But its striking power was excellent. Perfect for smashing the back of a skull.","She got the hang of it and found her rhythm. One zombie that got tripped had its head completely crushed after just two hits from her, drawing a round of cheers.","Su Yu wiped the sweat off her forehead.","She had a lot of fashion and film magazines at home, and she had wrapped them around her arms as makeshift armor. It was a sweltering summer evening, and after all that heavy physical exertion, sweat was beading on her forehead.","She couldn’t help glancing back.","Jiang Cheng was standing further back, holding an axe, talking to that Song Jingshuo guy. He wasn’t looking at her.","The girl next to her nudged her with an elbow and praised, “You’re pretty impressive.”","Su Yu turned and smiled at her.","This was the girl who had chatted with her on the app after the supermarket run. Like Su Yu, she was one of the brave girls who stood out during group operations.","She also glanced back at Jiang Cheng.","She wasn’t resentful that Jiang Cheng wasn’t fighting at the front. Quite the opposite — she and Su Yu exchanged a look, understanding each other perfectly. They were both glad to have Jiang Cheng on the temporary committee.","The girl said a bit regretfully, “I should have joined the temporary committee too.”","Su Yu reassured her, “It’s fine. Just actively participate when there’s something to do.”","Get closer to the core, get familiar, and you’ll naturally fit in.","“Yeah!”","They both tightened their grips on their weapons.","Jiang Cheng handled the thinking for the committee on the inside; they could fight on the front lines. Even though it drained their energy, there was a sense of security in finding their place within the organization.","Besides, Su Yu genuinely felt that facing zombies was actually easier than facing living people.","When a zombie came at you, you just hit it hard.","But the people she had run into today at Jixiang Jiayuan, the Maiduoduo Supermarket, and the pharmacy left her feeling irritated and helpless.","She would rather face zombies.","One comes, one dies.","All the zombies at the garage entrance had been killed. After banging on the pot lid for a while longer and throwing more clattering items down, no more zombies came out.","But the garage was huge, so there was no guarantee it was fully cleared.","“Let’s go down,” Jiang Cheng said. “We have to make sure not a single zombie is hiding in any corner of the neighborhood.”","Once every zombie in the area was eliminated and the main gate was locked, the apartment complex would become something like a safe zone.","Everyone had had enough of living in tension and fear for the past two days. They all wanted the neighborhood to return to a safe, relaxed state.","“Let’s go! Let’s go!”","The young men hollered, waving all sorts of weapons.","People with their heads, necks, arms, and legs fully armored led the way using U-shaped forks they had gotten from the property office. The rest followed behind, advancing slowly.","There was a long stretch of road ahead with no incidents at all. The zombies that had been there earlier had just been lured out of the entrance by the noise they'd made.","As they went deeper, there were indeed some that had slipped through the net. They came out and were killed on sight. Farther ahead, there were likely more, so they used the noise method again, luring out a few and dealing with them all.","But the underground parking garage was too large. They couldn't all stay bunched together the whole time—that would be too inefficient.","So everyone spread out again, forming teams in formation. Some watched the front, some watched the left, some watched the right, and some were responsible for making noise, sweeping the area like a carpet.","Overall, there weren't as many zombies in the garage as in the garden.","The incident had happened on a Saturday night. More people had been in the garden at the time. Those who happened to be in the garage at that moment were far fewer.","Cleaning it up was actually much easier than Sunday's big garden battle.","Using the noise method to lure zombies out also let them see them with the naked eye from a distance. The formations had both offense and defense, and other squads would come over to help.","A little past eight, the entire garage was cleared.","Everyone fanned out to different areas of the garage, making noise to confirm no more zombies were coming out.","Dealing with the corpses now felt routine.","They all worked together to drag them to the central plaza and stack them up. Master Luo had prepared the fuel and was squatting there, waiting for everyone to start the fire.","They'd burned a batch on Sunday at noon—that time had the most bodies and the biggest fire.","Then another batch on Monday morning, burning what they'd swept up from the building on Sunday night.","Now they were burning again.","As the flames rose, the moon had climbed higher.","The heat hit them in waves.","At this point, the Youth Apartment complex had achieved zero zombies inside the buildings, in the courtyard, and in the underground garage.","On the third night after the zombie virus outbreak, the Youth Apartment had become a sealed safe zone.","Someone suddenly lost control of their emotions and raised the hammer in their hand, letting out a fierce shout.","That shout acted like a catalyst. The pent-up emotions everyone had held back for two days finally burst loose, and they all started shouting—","\"No more zombies!\"","\"No more zombies in the complex!\"","\"Everyone can come down and wander around now!\"","\"Aw aw aw aw aw aw aw aw!\"","Many people upstairs opened their windows: \"Really?\"","\"That's great!\"","\"Thank you, you've worked so hard!\"","Some people upstairs also started shouting.","Cheers rose and fell, echoing through the Youth Apartment community.","Uplifting. Enough to make you cry.","Su Yu felt heat rushing through her veins, her emotions flooding.","She wiped the tears from her face and, almost instinctively, looked over at Jiang Cheng again.","She saw Song Jingshuo from Building Four also turn to look at Jiang Cheng beside him.","In the firelight, orange light flickered across Jiang Cheng's face, but her expression stayed still, calmly gazing at the burning pile of bodies.","All the pain, the urge to cry, the joy, the fierce emotions—they seemed to have nothing to do with her.","While everyone gathered around the fire, high-fiving, bumping fists, encouraging each other, celebrating passionately, she only lowered her head, gently stroking the small fuzzy head poking out of her messenger bag."]},{"number":35,"title":"Chapter 35","paragraphs":["When the gathering broke up, the temporary committee had also arranged for someone to stay and watch the fire pit.","Master Luo was personally on duty there. He didn't really trust these young homeowners, even though the young men were brave enough, when it came to putting out fires and preventing them, it took trained property staff like them to put people's minds at ease.","Anyway, with Master Luo standing guard there, Jiang Cheng felt reassured.","Everyone dispersed and headed home.","Jiang Cheng returned to her apartment, set Mo Li down on the bed, and hurried to take a hot shower.","She was now carrying the responsibility of leading the temporary emergency committee for the youth apartment building, and there was no telling when some emergency would come up that needed her, so even her shower was quick.","Sure enough, she had barely finished drying her damp hair and stepped out of the bathroom—just after finally tossing her \"battle uniform\" of two and a half days into the washing machine—when the walkie-talkie crackled:","\"Miss Jiang, Miss Jiang. This is the west gate. A few homeowners want to drive out. Should we open the gate?\"","Jiang Cheng was a bit surprised. She picked up the walkie-talkie and said, \"Ask them if they're going out for errands temporarily, or if they're leaving the complex for good?\"","The security guard went to ask, then came back: \"They say they're leaving to go elsewhere, and at least won't be back for a few days.\"","Jiang Cheng understood. \"Take a look outside the gate—are there any zombies around?\"","The guard replied, \"I don't see any right now by the gate. A couple wandered by during the day, and we stabbed them through the neck through the iron fence.\"","\"Let them through,\" Jiang Cheng said. \"Everyone remember: people inside the complex are free to leave. We don't have the right to stop anyone from leaving.\"","\"But people from outside are not allowed in.\"","\"The youth apartment must be completely sealed off from the outside—no people, no zombies get in.\"","Their call was on the full channel, so everyone could hear.","This time, not just the west gate guard, but the east gate guard, Master Luo, a few property staff holding walkie-talkies, and even Song Jingshuo and all the building block leaders replied in unison: \"Understood!\"","Sealed off. No zombies. Every homeowner had a certain stockpile of food and supplies.","Given that the entire city was overrun with zombies and most people had been trapped in their homes for two days already, everyone understood just how precious the current state of the youth apartment was.","And for it, they'd lost more than twenty homeowners.","Some had been locked in their own homes; more had been locked in the property management meeting room in the basement. The door to that room had been welded shut, the surveillance cameras destroyed—no one knew what was happening in there now.","They were all brave, kind-hearted, responsible homeowners.","These were terrible, painful costs.","This safe zone—so stable, so united—had been hard won.","This was their own home! They had to defend it!","Someone couldn't help but say, \"What are they thinking? Leaving at a time like this?\"","Everywhere out there was unsafe, not even the roads were safe.","Someone replied, \"Maybe they're worried about their parents?\"","At that, everyone suddenly understood.","\"Ah, that's true. Sigh...\"","\"Is everyone here local?\"","\"I am. I called home—my family is safe. So I'm not worried.\"","\"I'm not local.\"","\"Me neither. But I talked to my family—they're fine.\"","Seeing that there was a danger of starting a group chat over the walkie-talkie, Song Jingshuo stepped in: \"That's enough. If you want to chat, go to the group chat online. Don't waste the walkie-talkie battery.\"","The walkie-talkies ran on rechargeable batteries, and there were only a few chargers, all kept at the property office where you had to take the device to recharge.","It was a bit of a hassle.","Everyone clicked off their walkie-talkies right away, afraid of draining the power.","Song Jingshuo was truly useful.","He wasn't afraid to manage people. He didn't hem and haw; when something needed to be said, he said it.","And because he hit the nail on the head, the people being spoken to were willing to listen, or at least couldn't argue.","Jiang Cheng blow-dried her hair, thinking, not bad—she liked this person.","A useful person.","After her shower, she felt light and easy.","She reached out to touch Mo Li. During the day, his body had felt warm, but by evening the temperature seemed to have dropped again. He looked listless too.","When she put her hand on him, he only gave her a glance without even a single \"meow.\"","It was like he ran out of battery the moment the sun went down.","\"What's going on with you.\" Jiang Cheng had no choice, so she tucked Mo Li into her chest to keep him warm.","With Mo Li tucked inside her clothes, she sat down at her computer desk and went online.","The forum was buzzing. The posts had a kind of crying-for-joy feeling to them. With the complex cleaned up, everyone seemed to have relaxed.","Just now in the courtyard, had the fire not been burning corpses, some people might have been ready to dance around the bonfire.","Beyond the forum, the group chats were buzzing too.","This was just the temporary committee's communication group. You could imagine how many groups had already been formed across the whole complex through the homeowner forum.","Right now, no one in the complex was asleep. They were all online, chatting heatedly.","People could be so short-sighted, settling into the comfort of the moment.","In reality, beyond the youth apartment, the whole city—or the whole country—had no good news to report at all.","The TV was still looping the old announcements.","There was nothing new on the major forums across the country either.","Things like \"went out,\" \"grabbed rice from the supermarket,\" \"kicked the door in\" were everywhere. The same things were playing out in different places starting Monday.","But the youth apartment was ahead of all that—they'd already stocked up on Sunday.","Apart from those households that had hoarded supplies beforehand, if everyone else only went out to find supplies when they ran out of food, then with the current situation outside, they'd only search near where they lived. No one would go far. Crossing into another district to hit a big supermarket was too risky.","Nor was every neighborhood so lucky as to have a big supermarket like BuyDuDu nearby.","So for now, the youth apartment's hoard should surpass everyone else's—they were among the most well-supplied people around.","Suddenly, someone in the temporary committee group said: [The neighboring complex is stirring up trouble again.]","There were several residential complexes near the youth apartment, but when someone said \"the neighbor\" without any prefix, it always meant Jixiang Jiayuan.","Everyone asked: [What now?]","[I read their forum. Turns out someone who was supposed to be isolating at home didn't isolate properly—no idea how they got out—and then they turned and bit several neighbors on the same floor.]","[The turned one was beaten to death, and then the newly injured had to be quarantined. Family members started fighting over it, and some people ended up killed—living people.]","[Uninfected ones.]","The group went silent.","Killing zombies was fine. Even killing an infected person who hadn't turned yet was becoming acceptable.","But killing an uninfected, perfectly normal living person...","Every single person in every room—every member of the temporary committee sitting at their own computer—stared at their screens in silence.","No one wanted to admit or face it: the bottom line was being broken through, layer by layer.","How long had it been? The zombies broke out Saturday night, and it was only now—Monday night.","Just forty-eight hours.","The ordinary homeowners were still online celebrating with neighbors they'd gotten friendly with over the past two days that the youth apartment had become a safe zone.","But the members of the temporary committee felt nothing but grief and dread at the news they'd just received.","A new message popped up in the group.","Jiang Cheng: 【Everyone, get some rest early. These past two days have been too exhausting. Tomorrow at 9:30 AM, all members of the interim committee should meet up for a discussion on what to do next.】","Everyone's spirits lifted.","Right—although the area outside the compound looked bleak, their youth apartment had a backbone.","There was still an organization. Still strength.","Over a thousand able-bodied young people. In ancient times, that would have been enough to raise a rebellion and start a kingdom.","【Got it!】","【Received!】","【Sleep time, sleep time.]","Although the stench of burned corpses still hung thick in the air, that night they slept more soundly than on Sunday evening.","On Sunday night, everyone had still been on edge, terrified that a zombie might leap out from some corner of the compound. They slept lightly, even plagued by nightmares.","After being told by the interim committee that the entire compound had been cleared out, many people finally slipped back into deep sleep.","Jiang Cheng also fell asleep holding Mo Li.","During the day, Mo Li had thought he was recovering, because in the sunlight he could feel energy accumulating. But come nightfall, the energy gathered in his body stopped increasing—it wasn't even enough to sustain this body's consumption.","Luckily, there was still cat food to eat, offering a small supplement.","Then the girl held him close as they slept together.","Her body was warm, and energy seeped through her skin into him.","Mo Li fell asleep in Jiang Cheng's arms too.","...","The sun rose.","Jiang Cheng had drawn the curtains before sleeping, and sunlight couldn't penetrate the blackout curtains. But even so, the moment sunlight hit the other side of the curtains, Mo Li's eyes snapped open.","In the darkened room, his pupils were large and round.","He lifted his neck and turned to look at the window.","It had been the same yesterday morning—that pull toward energy, a craving from deep within his fur, his blood vessels, his very cells.","Mo Li slipped quietly off the bed.","The floor-to-ceiling window was a protruding bay window. The bean bag sofa sat in that protruding space.","Last night, before sleeping, Jiang Cheng had drawn the curtains, sealing the bean bag sofa on the other side.","Mo Li pushed through the curtains and slipped inside.","The moment sunlight fell on him, it felt like every strand of fur unfurled.","Energy seeped through those open hairs into his skin, and his whole body basked in comfort.","The little cat's small mind couldn't process much, only quietly feeling his body slowly mend, waiting for the girl on the bed to wake in the morning.","When Jiang Cheng woke up and found Mo Li gone again, she rubbed her eyes, walked over, and pulled back the curtains. Sure enough, the black cat was curled up on the bean bag sofa, soaking in the sun in an extremely contented pose.","\"You really love sunbathing, huh.\" Jiang Cheng stroked Mo Li and found his body temperature much better than last night. \"So it really comes down to sunbathing. It actually works.\"","Just one session in the sun and his temperature was back up.","Jiang Cheng thought about leaving Mo Li at home to sunbathe, but by the time she got ready and was about to head out, the little cat bit at her again.","Wherever she went, he had to follow.","Jiang Cheng still put him into her crossbody bag.","That bag was his designated seat.","Tuesday morning, the interim committee members gathered for a meeting.","Since the property management's meeting room was already occupied and welded shut, the meeting was held in the vine-covered pavilion by the small plaza. That way, everyone had somewhere to sit.","The air still carried the stench of corpses, but the sunlight was great, and this was the most relaxed everyone had felt since Saturday night.","Even on Sunday and Monday, meetings had been tense affairs, with Jiang Cheng, Song Jingshuo, and others rapidly discussing, arranging, and assigning tasks. Everyone was wound tight, grabbing their assignments and rushing off.","Now, finally, they could sit down and discuss things at a leisurely pace.","Everyone felt like they were finally seeing daylight again."]},{"number":36,"title":"Chapter 36","paragraphs":["“Have you managed to get in touch with your families? Is everyone safe?”","Jiang Cheng’s words snapped everyone out of their daze. Safe? How could they be, when things next door were still in such chaos?","Even if they had food in hand for now, as long as they hadn’t seen government rescue, they knew the day they’d finally see the light was still far off.","In the pavilion, those standing, sitting, and leaning all let out sighs.","Some even shed tears.","Jiang Cheng’s expression showed she was completely unaffected by these emotions.","Li Jiangbing and Song Jingshuo couldn’t help but think—maybe it was because her parents had both passed away, leaving her with no ties or worries.","Jiang Cheng continued:","“Someone left last night. Given the current situation outside, the policy is: exit allowed, entry denied.”","“Non-residents of this compound are not permitted to enter.”","“Any resident who leaves and wants to come back must undergo a full-body check.”","“Anyone returning from outside must also be examined to ensure they’re not carrying injuries.”","Everyone nodded—no one disagreed.","“Master Luo.” Jiang Cheng turned and called out.","This meeting had also notified Master Luo and his crew. Master Luo responded.","Jiang Cheng said to him earnestly, “Given what’s going on outside, the truth is none of us can really leave. The property management staff will, of course, have to stick it out with us.”","“I hope that until this virus is completely resolved, we can keep up the daily maintenance of the compound,” she said.","Master Luo looked a bit troubled: “There are only three of us in the maintenance department, including me.”","The other maintenance workers’ wives also worked in this city as migrant laborers, but unlike Master Luo, whose wife worked in the same place and could live with him in the dorms, the others spent weekends at their rented rooms with their wives. Now they couldn’t come back either.","What remained in the compound were mostly elderly cleaners and young security guards, along with a young office clerk named Yang Xinyan.","Things like clogged toilets or burned-out light bulbs might seem trivial, but in practice they could cause tremendous inconvenience in a person’s daily life.","Then there was the sanitation issue.","Just these past two days, without regular cleaning, the compound had visibly deteriorated. Because people generated trash every single day.","This was a serious problem. A community of several thousand people produced an astonishing amount of garbage daily.","But the current problem was: even if the property staff could resume cleaning services, how would the collected trash be disposed of?","Right now, all city public services had shut down. The fact that they still had running water, electricity, and internet was mainly thanks to automated modern systems and a handful of dedicated staff still on duty.","But garbage—that relied on sanitation workers driving garbage trucks around the city every day to pick up from each community, then delivering to waste stations for sorting, burial, or incineration.","No one was doing that anymore.","Jiang Cheng had called this meeting today precisely to solve the practical problems at hand.","What were the practical problems?","Food, water, and waste.","The moment the trash issue came up, everyone turned serious.","Zombies were a big deal, but garbage wasn’t a small matter either. It affected everyone’s everyday life.","These past two days, every household had piled up several bags of trash. Some young men with poor hygiene habits hadn’t changed their trash bags in time, and their homes were already smelling bad and had little black flies.","Mixed with the stench of corpses drifting in through the windows—don’t even get started.","Even the slobs themselves couldn’t stand it anymore.","No wonder Jiang Cheng had called the meeting today. Repairs and upkeep weren’t minor concerns.","The young people who chose these single-apartment units over shared rentals generally had some standards for quality of life. According to Maslow’s hierarchy of needs, once basic safety and food concerns were met, people’s needs moved up a level.","But Master Luo’s concerns were also very real: first, not enough hands for repairs. Second, no way to transport trash out.","The interim committee now had dozens of members, and they launched into a heated discussion on the topic.","Residents kept drifting over to watch and couldn’t help but chime in. Since it affected their own interests, everyone wanted to hear and offer suggestions.","Eventually, people crowded around in layers, several deep.","After all the noise and debate, they somehow managed to reach a conclusion.","First, for repairs: the property office had tools, but were short-staffed, so they’d need volunteers. But while some might volunteer to change light bulbs, getting people to unclog toilets or drains would be a tough sell.","In the end, they decided to assign duties.","The specifics—whether by drawing lots or by assigning according to unit numbers—would be left to each building to decide.","For now, the six building leaders, now called “building captains,” had all shown credible organizational skills and a spirit of stepping up, and they carried some weight in the community.","Within their own buildings, they could rally eight or nine people, sometimes a dozen, to help out, and they could keep things under control.","Everyone believed they could handle it.","If they couldn’t, they’d be replaced. Whoever had what it takes would take over.","Whenever humans gather in groups, capable people always emerge.","The real headache was the trash problem. With a community this large, the waste station only had to miss a single day of collections for the compound to be overflowing.","After much discussion, they finally decided to commandeer the clubhouse swimming pool as a temporary trash staging area.","The community clubhouse was outsourced, and after the zombie outbreak on Saturday night, the staff hadn’t come to work. The clubhouse was empty now.","First, they’d have to drain the pool.","One advantage of this singles apartment complex: most owners had at least a bachelor’s degree, and there were a particular number of engineering-minded men.","The moment the call went out, there was no need to search the whole compound—right among the onlookers, several engineers stepped forward on their own.","Perfect.","Though Jiang Cheng had initially deflated their spirits, seeing this crowd of eager volunteers gave everyone a morale boost and a sense of security again.","Those who arrived later heard from the early birds that the interim committee had decided to strictly prohibit outsiders from entering the compound, and they felt even more at ease.","In just two days, the interim committee had already earned a lot of trust.","Some people followed the group to the clubhouse to deal with the pool. The rest continued discussing the garbage and the follow-up issues it raised.","“We need to make another trip to BuyDuoDuo supermarket,” Jiang Cheng declared.","The previous two large-scale shopping trips for the compound had mainly focused on personal essentials—food, toilet paper, and the like. Because people’s carrying capacity was limited, everyone had to skip non-essentials.","No one had thought to grab anything for the community itself.","“Disinfectant, bleach... anything that can sanitize,” Jiang Cheng said. “And whatever else they still have—if we can carry it, we take it.”","If the trash was just piled up and didn’t get processed, the consequences were unthinkable.","This time, there was no need for a full mobilization—just the people present were enough. On the spot, they organized a team of over forty.","Those who didn’t sign up also pitched in, helping find shopping carts.","People had already wheeled back a lot of shopping carts from the supermarket. The carts at that store were big—great for hauling, but they took up space too.","Apart from a few buildings in the youth apartment complex that had slightly larger duplex layouts, most people's units were quite small. After moving their belongings, many people left their carts in the hallways, or in the building lobbies, and some even pushed them out into the courtyard.","It didn't take long to find more than enough shopping carts.","Everything needed had already been made clear, so Jiang Cheng didn't have to go herself. Li Jiangbing led that trip.","The street between the youth apartment complex and Jixiang Jiayuan had been completely cleared—no zombies in sight.","Buy Duoduo faced the main road, and while it had been cleaned up, the occasional distant zombie would still be drawn over by the noise. But they posed no real threat.","Everyone had plenty of combat experience by now.","\"Leave it to me,\" Li Jiangbing said. \"Brothers, follow me!\"","A crowd of people noisily pushed their carts off.","\"Disperse, disperse,\" Jiang Cheng said to the onlookers.","She raised her hand.","Mo Li wanted to sunbathe, but with so many people around, Jiang Cheng was afraid he'd get stepped on, so she simply placed him on top of the pavilion roof.","The meeting had gone on for over an hour, and Mo Li had basked in the sun for just as long.","Jiang Cheng reached up and lifted him down, setting him back in her shoulder bag. She gently stroked his fur and felt the warmth in her palm—completely different from his body temperature at night.","Was sunbathing really that effective? Then she'd have to let the little cat get more sun.","\"Su Yu,\" Jiang Cheng called. \"Organize those two things we just discussed and post them online.\"","Su Yu immediately took the task: \"Got it.\"","Jiang Cheng turned to the building heads and asked, \"Want to go take a look at the clubhouse?\"","All the building heads nodded. \"Sure, let's go check it out.\"","Su Yu went home to post the announcement.","The building heads, along with a few people who were especially active in various activities—like Peng Ze—and Yang Xinyan from the property management, all headed to the clubhouse together.","On the way, Song Jingshuo walked beside Jiang Cheng and said in a low voice, \"Next time we have a meeting, we need to find an enclosed space.\"","There were too many onlookers, and people kept butting in.","Even though the topics discussed that day weren't really sensitive to interruption, Song Jingshuo still didn't like it.","Jiang Cheng felt the same way and agreed. \"Okay.\"","She thought to ask Yang Xinyan, \"How are things with the conference room?\"","Yang Xinyan's expression darkened. \"No sound. Not a single peep.\"","She was a clerical worker who spent all day in the office answering phones and checking group messages, separated from the conference room by only a short hallway.","Although others had been with her in the property management center, the young woman had watched, from the very beginning, as so many people were locked in that conference room. She'd watched the monitors as people mutated, watched someone from Building 4 destroy the camera, and then, as time went on, she'd heard the periodic commotion, the welded-shut door, and finally—utter silence.","The girl felt that these past two days had been longer than the rest of her life put together.","In no time, they arrived at the clubhouse.","The clubhouse used to be a sales center, but it had been built with the intention of becoming a clubhouse. The interior was well planned, with a swimming pool, a gym, and a small coffee bar.","The first group to arrive was already draining the swimming pool, though very slowly.","Master Luo said, \"This can't be rushed; the water only flows at this speed.\"","He added, \"Good thing these guys showed up. Otherwise, I wouldn't have known how to handle these machines.\"","A young man came over to tell them, \"This pool is a non-standard 25-meter pool. I calculated that if we assume all our garbage is unsorted mixed waste, the density is roughly estimated at 0.15 to 0.3 tons per cubic meter. So filling the pool should hold about 200 to 380 tons.\"","\"A community like ours generates about 3 tons of waste per day. This pool should support about 65 to 120 days.\"","\"Of course, this is directly related to how compacted the waste is. If we can compact it to some degree, that number can be pushed even higher.\"","He wore a plaid shirt and thick-framed glasses, practically with the words \"tech nerd\" written all over his face.","He liked to support his statements with data.","Jiang Cheng and Song Jingshuo both liked tech nerds like him—these were the real workhorses who got things done."]},{"number":37,"title":"Chapter 37","paragraphs":["\"What about sorting the garbage?\" Jiang Cheng asked. \"What if we only pile up the non-burnable stuff here and burn the rest? Would that make it last longer?\"","The engineering guy didn't answer right away. After a pause, he said hesitantly, \"...Would it really go on that long?\"","\"How would I know?\" Jiang Cheng said. \"Just asking.\"","Jiang Cheng had been speaking with such authority these past two days that everything she said was taken seriously by everyone.","Hearing that, the engineering guy breathed a sigh of relief.","But he added, \"If you burn it without any filtering or treatment, it releases a lot of toxic substances.\"","Jiang Cheng thought for a moment, then asked, \"Which is more toxic—that, or burning corpses?\"","The engineering guy froze for a second, then said, \"Well... burning corpses is... more severe, I'd say.\"","He continued, \"Burning bodies is basically an 'enhanced version' of burning trash. Most of the toxins from burning garbage are there, but human bodies naturally contain chlorine. When it incompletely combusts with fats and proteins, it's the perfect breeding ground for dioxins. Plus there are even more complex toxic heavy metals.\"","\"And most importantly,\" he said, \"there's the risk of pathogen aerosols. That's the one unique danger specific to cremation.\"","\"Take the zombie virus—we don't understand it at all right now. It could attach itself to soot particles and spread with the wind, causing a second wave of plague.\"","This was something Jiang Cheng hadn't known.","She pondered for a moment, then asked, \"But we've already been burning for two days. So far, the later mutations in the neighborhood have all been caused by exposure through open wounds. If the zombie virus spread the way you describe, we should be seeing mutations in people without any injuries. But that hasn't happened. Can we rule out that possibility?\"","The engineering guy thought it over and nodded. \"Personally, I think we can.\"","Everyone breathed a sigh of relief.","Song Jingshuo suggested, \"Separate paper products and plastics into their own piles. No need to burn them yet either. The clubhouse is spacious enough to store quite a bit. Only use the swimming pool for non-burnable items. We'll deal with the rest later.\" Jiang Cheng sensed that Song Jingshuo's attitude had changed.","It sounded simple enough, but in reality, mobilizing a community of several thousand people was bound to bring endless trouble and resistance.","Yet Song Jingshuo chose the more difficult path, supporting the idea of extending the usage time of the pool as much as possible.","The mindset he'd had before—hoping the government would come rescue them tomorrow—was gone.","Jiang Cheng's instincts were right.","Ever since Monday, when Jiang Cheng led everyone to smash the glass doors of the Buy Duo Duo supermarket and the crowd ransacked the place, Song Jingshuo had gone home and thought all night. He'd finally come to terms with the fact that \"things were different now.\"","He'd started agreeing with Jiang Cheng's view that the current situation could last a long time.","Jiang Cheng adopted Song Jingshuo's suggestion. \"Good idea. Spread the word as soon as possible.\"","After two days of supermarket raiding, everyone was bound to have a lot of packaging to tear open, which would generate plenty of cardboard boxes and cartons—bulky things that took up lots of space.","The small apartments weren't big, so everyone would definitely toss them out as garbage.","Jiang Cheng immediately pulled out her phone and called Su Yu to fill her in: \"...Tell everyone not to mix cardboard boxes and packaging like that, or plastic bottles, with the rest of the trash. They should be piled up together in the small plaza downstairs.\"","Doing one big centralized collection was actually more convenient than dealing with it piecemeal every day.","She also talked with Master Luo, arranging for the cleaning workers to go collect those items from the plaza.","Paper products needed to be tied up in bundles to save storage space. Jiang Cheng had \"Jiang Cheng's\" memories and had seen how the cleaning workers neatly tied up cardboard to sell as scrap.","She said, \"Once this is all over, these are for the workers to sell as scrap.\"","Jiang Cheng was young, but she understood people well. Song Jingshuo glanced at her, thinking to himself.","But from his experience, the women he knew like that were usually the commanding, alpha-female types. Jiang Cheng could project an intimidating sharpness at times. Yet if none of this had happened—no zombies, no chaos—and you ran into her in the neighborhood, she'd come across as nothing more than a refined, bookish girl.","Was this what they meant by \"times forge the man\"?","Under extraordinary circumstances, ordinary-looking people sometimes rose to the occasion.","Without this special situation, they might have lived their whole lives in obscurity.","Master Luo used his walkie-talkie to assign the cleaning crew their tasks. When they heard that the recyclables would be theirs once everything was over, they were clearly delighted.","Jiang Cheng said to Yang Xinyan, \"Xinyan, go keep an eye on things. Tell them to haul it this way.\"","Yang Xinyan nodded and set off with light footsteps.","Everyone had grown accustomed to taking instructions from Jiang Cheng.","Su Yu moved quickly. She wrote up the notice, posted it to the forum immediately, and then contacted other people.","The members of the provisional committee then went floor by floor shouting: \"Check the forum! Check the post about trash disposal!\"","Su Yu called Jiang Cheng to report the progress.","They'd fully shifted into corporate work mode now.","After hanging up, Jiang Cheng sighed. \"The only problem is communications.\"","If they relied on the property management's loudspeakers to announce things at each building, the people on the side facing away from the garden might not hear.","But announcing everything by shouting was way too primitive.","She said, \"If only there were some way to notify everyone all at once. That would be so much more convenient.\"","The engineering guy went, \"Huh? Actually...\"","Jiang Cheng looked up at him.","He pushed up his glasses. \"Actually, there are broadcast speakers in the hallways. I think we could use those.\"","\"Huh?\" Jiang Cheng was surprised. \"There are?\"","\"Is it the fire alarm thing?\" Li Jiangbing chimed in. \"I remember they tested it one day during daytime, playing music. But that was on a workday, so you would've been at the office.\"","The last part was directed at Jiang Cheng.","Master Luo, however, waved his hand dismissively. \"No, that won't work. I don't know how to operate that. The person in charge of it doesn't live in the neighborhood.\"","Master Luo and the other two workers were just electricians and handymen. But that broadcast system was connected to a computer system. The engineering department specifically had one person who managed the surveillance and broadcast system. His salary was much higher than theirs.","That guy didn't live in the staff dorm, so he wasn't in the neighborhood now either. No one else knew how to do it.","Once that was explained, the engineering guy said, \"That's easy.\"","He turned his head and cupped his hands around his mouth to yell: \"Gao Yuxuan! Gao Yuxuan! Come here!\"","From the swimming pool area, a young man came jogging over. \"What's up?\"","The engineering guy told him, \"We want to get the building broadcast system working. The engineer isn't around. Can you get it fixed up?\"","Gao Yuxuan didn't hesitate: \"Easy!\"","Gao Yuxuan was clearly also an engineering type.","The engineering guys were too handy.","Gao Yuxuan went off without another word.","Jiang Cheng asked the engineering guy, \"What's your name again?\"","It was obvious the engineering guy wasn't great at socializing with pretty women. He'd been perfectly fluent when explaining technical things a moment ago, but the moment it became about small talk, he tensed up: \"Zhao... Zhao Yi.\"","Jiang Cheng's eyes curved into a bright smile. \"It's such a relief to have you guys around.\"","Zhao Yi's ears visibly turned red.","Jiang Cheng said, \"Then I'll leave the club matters to you. I need you to make a plan, ensure the road for garbage transportation is smooth, and also arrange space for the rest of the trash piles.\"","Zhao Yi nodded firmly. \"Okay, leave it to me.\"","Song Jingshuo glanced at Jiang Cheng, a bit surprised.","Compared to Zhao Yi, who was clearly still an innocent, pure-hearted young guy, Song Jingshuo was far more experienced. He could obviously tell that Jiang Cheng had Zhao Yi wrapped around her finger with ease.","But this broke the impression Jiang Cheng had given him over the past two days.","In the past two days, Jiang Cheng had shown herself to be completely calm and rational, detached from any sense of gender.","He had thought she was the type of girl who deliberately separates her ability from her gender in the workplace.","He had worked with many women in his career—some weaponized their beauty, while others did the exact opposite, believing that having their gender noticed at work was an insult to their capability, and strove to project a genderless image.","He had assumed Jiang Cheng was the latter, but now he saw she wasn't.","So she was the kind of person who didn't care whether she wielded beauty or competence, but instead chose the most effective solution based on the situation and the person.","Someone like that would succeed at anything she did.","He was exactly that kind of person himself.","Yang Xinyan left the club to gather the cleaning staff.","The young homeowners who stayed home without having to work kept an eye on the forum at all times. And the members of the interim committee had also notified people floor by floor.","Everyone had seen the post Su Yu had made. Coincidentally, many of the items they had panic-bought over the past two days were still unopened in their packaging, taking up space at home. Everyone started getting to work.","Before long, Yang Xinyan saw homeowners coming downstairs one after another, arms full of cardboard boxes and cartons.","\"Over here, put them over here,\" Yang Xinyan waved to them. \"You can leave them here, we'll handle the rest.\"","She was a young girl, and the homeowners were generally friendly toward her, even polite: \"Thanks for your hard work.\"","Yang Xinyan responded courteously, \"It's my duty.\"","The homeowners' mood and state right now were the best they'd been since Saturday night. Most of them were decent people and politely said thank you.","Yang Xinyan found dealing with the homeowners to be relaxed and pleasant.","Among the cleaners, one younger guy—who had been watching her interact with the homeowners the whole time—turned his head and let out a \"tch.\"","The older cleaners were actually quite happy. Master Luo had told them that once things settled down, all these cardboard boxes, cartons, and plastic bottles would be theirs to sell for money.","But this younger guy, who wasn't even forty yet and was usually lazy and never proactive, said, \"And what if things never settle down?\"","The older ones said, \"Huh?\"","The middle-aged male cleaner continued, \"What if it never gets better, and it stays this chaotic, with monsters everywhere? Then these broken cardboard boxes are worthless—no one's buying them. What's the point?\"","One of the cleaning ladies said, \"That can't be.\"","\"Why not?\" the middle-aged cleaner scoffed. \"You see the government coming to rescue us yet? Even in the worst floods, the whole country never shut down like this. Have you ever seen anything like this?\"","They really hadn't. Whether it was earthquakes, floods, or typhoons, it was always localized disasters.","When one region was in trouble, help came from all directions.","But now, zombies were in every direction.","Even the interim committee folks had said that this time even the military probably couldn't handle it—the army couldn't fight a virus with willpower alone.","If things really fell apart...","\"My great-grandmother survived famine before,\" the middle-aged cleaner said. \"In times like that, cash is just waste paper—only good for wiping your ass.\"","\"Besides, if everything really collapses, not only can't we sell cardboard, but our wages won't be paid either...\"","As he spoke, his expression gradually shifted, as if something had suddenly clicked in his mind.","\"So then, why the hell should we keep working for them!\""]},{"number":38,"title":"Chapter 38","paragraphs":["Li Jiangbing led a few dozen people pushing dozens of shopping carts, heading straight for BuyDuoDuo again.","The small street east of the gate was already clean, completely free of zombies. As they turned onto the main road, they spotted two feral zombies shuffling in from somewhere in the distance.","Without hesitation, they charged forward with the carts, knocked the zombies to the ground, and smashed their heads in within seconds.","Arriving at BuyDuoDuo's entrance, the broken glass door area from before was now empty, the shattered glass cleaned up.","The supermarket staff had placed a table horizontally across the opening, stacking flood-control sandbags on top and underneath, sealing off the doorless entrance.","Everyone pushed the sandbags over, shoved the table aside, and moved into the space between the two sets of doors.","The inner glass door had no floor lock; instead, a chain lock hung from the handle.","Li Jiangbing bellowed at full volume: \"Anyone there—! Anyone there—! If no one comes, we're smashing the glass—!\"","Hearing the commotion, Brother Dong rushed out with his employees, furious: \"Why are you back again! Rice and flour are gone! Noodles are gone! Canned goods, salted eggs, fermented bean curd—all gone! Everything is cleaned out! What more do you want?\"","Li Jiangbing: \"We've got other things to grab. Can you talk nicely or not?\"","Robbers now complaining about being spoken to rudely—was there no justice left? Brother Dong was so angry he could've twisted his own nose off.","But circumstances dictated terms. Compared to the previous two visits, this group was much smaller, but still two to three times their numbers.","And it was the people from the Young Professionals Apartments—the ones Brother Dong hated the most.","The folks from Jixiang Jiayuan had stood at the door arguing for ages without daring to smash anything.","That girl from the apartment complex, though—she'd come straight up and put an axe through the glass door without a second word.","That rundown apartment building was all strong young men. In peacetime, Brother Dong feared old folks more; now, in chaos, the old-timers had become paper tigers.","The organized, disciplined young people from that apartment complex were the ones truly to be wary of.","\"I won't waste words with you. You decide for yourself.\" Li Jiangbing used his height to look down at Brother Dong and his crew.","Brother Dong gritted his teeth and swallowed his pride. Grumbling, he unlocked the door.","Li Jiangbing led everyone rushing in noisily.","They hadn't been the last to leave yesterday, so they hadn't seen the final state of things.","Looking around today, many shelves were bare. Even a large supermarket, without daily restocking, could easily be stripped clean by two residential communities.","Those old folks had apparently fought over things in some chaos—much of it knocked over and scattered.","Clearly, the supermarket staff saw no point in cleaning up and had just left it. Now, a single glance showed utter ruin, like a place that had just been ransacked.","Li Jiangbing led everyone straight to the household goods section. Barrel after barrel of disinfectant and bleach went onto the carts.","\"Hand soap and bar soap too!\"","\"Don't forget the insecticide!\"","\"There's medical alcohol over here! Want it?\"","\"Yes! Useful, useful! Don't be rigid, everyone—grab whatever seems useful!\"","\"Ohoh!\"","\"Then I also need a new pot.\"","Brother Dong stood off to the side, arms crossed, watching coldly for a while before finally asking: \"What exactly are you planning to do?\"","Everyone kept working, but among them were some chatty ones who, while hauling goods, explained the garbage disposal plan in their community.","Brother Dong was silent for a moment, then asked: \"What about the other communities?\"","Then again: \"Did you burn the bodies in your compound?\"","Someone from the apartment complex answered: \"Yes. Do you have bodies here? How did you handle them?\"","Brother Dong's gaze wavered slightly, but he answered: \"We put them in the cold storage.\"","Everyone paused.","\"Damn! Is it the cold storage where they keep raw meat?\"","\"I took frozen meat the day before yesterday! Was it already in there by then?\"","Brother Dong chuckled: \"Put them in early Sunday morning.\"","That day, the employees had no idea what to do, and he just happened to come in—the only supervisor around. Back then, he'd still been thinking of \"waiting\" for the police to deal with things, so he'd directed the bodies to be stored in the cold room first.","A collective groan went up from everyone.","Brother Dong pulled the conversation back: \"I'm asking you—what about the other communities?\"","Irritated now, they rolled their eyes at him: \"What do other communities have to do with us? Can we control everyone else? Look at those people from Jixiang Jiayuan—yesterday morning, we risked our lives to go over and help them fight zombies. Apart from a few of the leaders who show basic decency, did anyone else even say thank you? Damn them.\"","Brother Dong asked: \"Have other communities burned their dead?\"","Someone said: \"How should we know?\"","Another said: \"Jixiang Jiayuan burned theirs, we helped with that. Don't know about the rest.\"","Brother Dong felt worried.","He now deeply regretted his single-minded drive to go to work on Sunday morning.","His family had originally been suburban farmers, but over time they'd bought an apartment in the city, while still keeping their old house out in the countryside. If only he'd had a clear head on Sunday, he could've just headed straight to the village.","His parents, wife, and kids were all over there.","Many villagers had moved into the city, leaving lots of empty courtyards. Population density would be much lower, which meant fewer zombies.","Now he was trapped between several massive residential areas, with extremely high population density. He didn't dare risk the trip back home. It was a bitter pill to swallow.","As someone who worked in a large supermarket, he had a strong sense of \"scale\" and \"volume.\" Just thinking briefly about how much garbage these densely packed communities would generate each day made him see black in front of his eyes.","And the unclaimed corpses on the streets outside—already swarming with flies.","Brother Dong could clearly sense that this area—no, not just this area, but the entire city—was about to deteriorate at an alarming rate.","He felt that things would get worse and worse, yet he was powerless to change it.","At that moment, he envied the Young Professionals Apartments.","That impressive young woman had brought together several seemingly resourceful, capable people to manage the entire community.","He didn't know if their approach would work, but at least it inspired hope.","Unlike him, hiding out in a supermarket with a few colleagues, with no end in sight.","The more he thought, the more agitated he grew.","Li Jiangbing and his dozens of people swept through the nearly emptied supermarket once more.","Looking around now, the only food left was mainly snacks that wouldn't fill anyone up and had little nutritional value. High-calorie items like chocolate, which were good for emergencies, were all gone.","The emptiest shelves were the rice, flour, and cooking oil ones.","The toilet paper shelves were bare too.","The apartment people filled every cart they'd brought and even jammed odds and ends into the gaps between bottles and boxes.","No sense in leaving empty-handed.","With a clatter, they pushed their carts out.","Li Jiangbing even waved at Brother Dong: \"We're off.\"","Brother Dong had no fight left in him.","After they left, he gathered his employees and relayed the latest plan from the apartment complex, saying: \"There are capable people in that place. None of us even thought of this.\"","\"We'll need these disinfectants too. Go check the back storeroom now and move out whatever we need.\"","Someone asked: \"Brother Dong, why do we need to move things?\"","Brother Dong's face was grim as he laid it out for everyone: \"Youth Apartments, Lucky Homestead, Royal Scenery Gardens, Elegant Hills, Deqing Lane, Peaceful Homes... so far only Youth Apartments and Lucky Homestead have shown up. None of those other neighborhoods have come yet, and I'm telling you, they will eventually.\"","Once people come, they won't come empty-handed. Especially those who haven't shown up yet—the longer they delay, the more depleted their supplies at home become, and the more desperate they get.","If the shelves are empty, they won't just leave satisfied. They'll definitely try to storm the warehouse.","There's no law and order anymore. At least in the days before the government can mount an effective response, there's definitely no law and order.","The useful supplies need to be moved ahead of time. They all had to survive too—they had their own consumption needs.","Everyone understood the gravity of it and went off to carry out the orders with worried expressions.","Li Jiangbing and his group were heading back, loaded with supplies, when suddenly someone called out: \"Li, Li, hold on a second!\"","Jiang Cheng was petite and called Li Jiangbing directly by his given name, \"Jiangbing,\" and Li Jiangbing would come running happily to her side.","Nobody else dared call him that. These past couple of days, everyone just addressed him as \"Li.\"","Nowadays, who's the big brother and who's the little brother isn't determined by age—you can tell just by height and build.","\"Li.\" The man who called out pointed to a shop on the outskirts of the neighborhood. \"There's a hardware store over there. I think we should check it out.\"","Around the outside of the neighborhood was a row of small shops, including the convenience pharmacy that Jiang Cheng had led people to break into earlier. This man had just turned his head and suddenly spotted the four characters for \"hardware and renovations.\"","For a big group of men, did they need a reason to go to a hardware store?","No.","It was like spotting a perfectly straight stick on the road—you had to bring it home. No reason needed.","As soon as he mentioned it, Li Jiangbing agreed immediately: \"Let's go.\"","Dozens of people shuffled over in a hurry.","The hardware store had a rolling shutter door. The men pried it open with a bit of effort—it was easy.","Once they squeezed inside, everyone's eyes lit up: \"Oh wow, so much good stuff!\"","Back in Youth Apartments, Yang Xinyan ran into the clubhouse to find Jiang Cheng: \"Miss Jiang!\"","She was a bit flustered: \"They refuse to work anymore!\"","Her shout echoed through the swimming pool area, and everyone turned to look at her.","\"Who?\" Jiang Cheng asked.","Yang Xinyan ran up, her face flushed, panting: \"The cleaning staff!\"","\"They said, since they're not getting paid, why should they work. They're just not doing it anymore.\"","\"I tried to talk to them, but they wouldn't listen.\"","Jiang Cheng asked directly: \"Who's the one leading this?\"","Many situations need that one person to step up first before others dare to follow. Without that \"first person,\" many people would just keep complaining and enduring.","Master Luo guessed right away: \"Is it Liu Hongwang?\"","Yang Xinyan nodded: \"Yes! That's him!\"","It was safe to assume the guy was usually a troublemaker or a slacker. Otherwise, Master Luo wouldn't have figured it out so quickly.","Sure enough, Master Luo said: \"He's no good at work anyway, always getting complaints. The manager told me before that as soon as we hired someone new, he'd be fired. We hadn't hired anyone yet, and now this happens.\"","The people turned into zombies, and suddenly everything fell into chaos. The manager was stuck at home and couldn't come in either.","Jiang Cheng exchanged glances with Song Jingshuo and a few others.","Jiang Cheng: \"Let's go take a look.\"","The provisional committee followed her out.","People always look out for their own interests. With a neighborhood this big, housing thousands of people, if the property management staff threw in the towel, the environment would deteriorate fast.","In the end, they couldn't just leave everything undone—it would all be pushed onto the homeowners anyway.","Once these necessary, unavoidable tasks were assigned, everyone would have no choice but to shoulder them. But you're the property management staff—serving the residents is your job. What right do you have to refuse?"]},{"number":39,"title":"Chapter 39","paragraphs":["“Why should we work for you? You don't even pay us!” Liu Hongwang craned his neck and shouted.","Just as Jiang Cheng had anticipated, there was always a ringleader in these situations. The other cleaners, mostly in their forties or even fifties, inwardly hoped Liu Hongwang could fight for their interests or even call a strike. They followed him in downing tools, but none dared to step forward themselves, each shrinking back in silence.","The security guards had been drawn over too, whispering among themselves in low voices.","Morale was wavering.","“The property company’s funds come from the property fees paid by the residents, including your wages,” Song Jingshuo said with a grim face. “The property company exists to serve the community and its residents.”","“The situation is special right now. You’re not the only ones whose pay has been suspended. We’re in the same boat. It’s the same across the city, across the whole country—everything has come to a standstill.”","“There’s no way around it. This is force majeure. But once the current crisis is resolved, everything will return to normal. The property company will make up your wages.”","“If the property company tries to shortchange you, the interim committee will definitely protect your rights and help you get your pay back.”","Everyone chimed in: “Yeah, yeah.”","“You few who’ve kept working—we can all vouch for that.”","“Don’t worry about it. If they dare dock your pay, with our numbers, we can get it back even if we have to resort to strong-arm tactics.”","But Liu Hongwang wasn’t buying it.","He planted his hands on his hips: “You keep saying production has stopped, but why won’t you say work has stopped too? I’ve watched the news—they broadcast it a dozen times a day, and they’re still airing it now. Who do you think you’re fooling? You college kids think you can bully us because we’re uneducated, huh?”","He thrust his hand out, jabbing at the air with his fingers: “Right now, the whole country is shut down. Nobody’s working. Look at you all—every one of you lounging comfortably at home. Why should we still be working?”","“We’ve still got to collect the trash, Old Luo still has to work, and them—” Liu Hongwang swept his hand through the air, pulling the curious security guards into the conversation, “—they still have to man the gates and do night shifts.”","Compared to the cleaners, the security guards were younger—the oldest was just past thirty.","Liu Hongwang felt a pang of regret that the security captain had turned into a zombie on Saturday night. The captain was a sturdy guy—if he were still around, he’d surely have led them in revolt. Why should they keep working when the whole country had shut down?","He wanted to lie around comfortably too.","Ever since Sunday, when everyone had worked together to wipe out the zombies in the community garden, the residents of the Youth Apartment—both owners and property staff—had shown strong solidarity. They’d been united, cooperative, and obedient to orders.","But now, all of that had suddenly developed a crack.","Song Jingshuo noticed that several of the security guards’ expressions and glances had shifted subtly.","The unity was falling apart.","Yet he truly felt he couldn’t refute Liu Hongwang’s argument.","Indeed, everyone had stopped working. On the surface, it really did look like the residents were exploiting and oppressing the property workers.","Song Jingshuo’s thoughts were in turmoil; he felt like the situation really was what Liu Hongwang described. He couldn’t think of a solution, so he instinctively looked at Jiang Cheng.","A faint smile played at the corner of Jiang Cheng’s lips—cold, chilly.","Song Jingshuo paused.","He knew Jiang Cheng definitely had a solution.","But at the same time, he sensed that her solution would inevitably trample on certain lines that most people—or ordinary public morality—would consider inviolable.","It had only been three days, and he already understood her that well.","Jiang Cheng stepped forward.","Before she even spoke, the mere act of stepping up silenced the crowd.","Jiang Cheng now carried that kind of authority in the Youth Apartment. The moment she stood forward, everyone instinctively shut their mouths and waited for her to speak.","Every time, she never let them down.","“Liu Hongwang,” she called out his name, giving him one last chance. “I’ll ask you one more time—are you sure you no longer wish to continue working as a cleaner?”","Liu Hongwang had seen her several times over the past two days, always at the center of a crowd.","He was somewhat wary of her.","But just now, even a man as polished as Song Jingshuo couldn’t handle him, which proved he was in the right.","A man like Song Jingshuo—normally dressed in a suit and tie, looking every bit the elite, striding past with a laptop bag and not even glancing his way—had still been left speechless by him. Why? Because the world had gone mad, monsters were everywhere, and there was no law anymore.","In the past, the residents were kings and he was the lowly servant—but from now on, that might no longer be the case.","Liu Hongwang’s boldness swelled.","The big bruiser who usually stayed close to Jiang Cheng happened to be absent right then, which made Liu Hongwang bolder still.","“That’s right! I quit!” He hurled the bundle of string he used for bundling cardboard to the ground and shouted, “Forget it—I’m done!”","Song Jingshuo saw Jiang Cheng smile faintly.","The same kind of smile as before.","Jiang Cheng said, “Fine.”","“I respect your decision,” she said. “But the property company is employed by the residents, and you are employed by the property company.”","“Given the extraordinary circumstances, I, on behalf of the interim committee, hereby terminate your labor relationship with the Youth Apartment community. You no longer need to work.”","So “making a fuss” did work—look, all it took was a protest and you didn’t have to work anymore.","The other cleaners’ faces brightened with anticipation.","The residents watching began to murmur amongst themselves.","Liu Hongwang had won a complete victory. But before the corners of his mouth could even curl up, he heard Jiang Cheng continue: “You are no longer a staff member of the Youth Apartment. I’m giving you half an hour. Pack your things and leave our community.”","The open outdoor space suddenly became so quiet you could hear a pin drop.","Dozens, even hundreds of gazes fixed on Jiang Cheng.","Everyone had heard last night what happened at the neighboring Jixiang Jiayuan—a live person, a normal, uninfected, healthy person, had been beaten to death.","But that hadn’t happened in the Youth Apartment yet.","Up until now, the only people forcibly detained in the Youth Apartment had been the infected who had sustained injuries.","What would happen to an ordinary healthy man like Liu Hongwang if he left a safe zone like the Youth Apartment?","Nobody knew.","But the chance of dying wasn’t negligible—in fact, it was high.","A lone adult male could, theoretically, pick off zombies one by one like whack-a-mole. But if several surrounded him at once, or if even a single second-generation zombie showed up, the odds of death would skyrocket immediately. Sending Liu Hongwang out of the Youth Apartment was effectively sending him to his death.","Song Jingshuo closed his eyes briefly. He wasn’t surprised in the slightest.","This was exactly her style.","In fact, at that moment, Song Jingshuo wasn’t the only one who felt this way. Quite a few people shared the same sentiment, especially the backbone members of the interim committee.","Liu Hongwang’s face changed.","“Why should I—” He swung his arms trying to argue, but Jiang Cheng cut him off coldly: “Because we paid our own money to buy the apartments here, and because we are the residents and owners of this community.”","“The only reason you can stay in this complex is that you work for us residents.”","“Now that you no longer wish to do that work, we respect your choice.”","\"But you need to respect us too. Someone who has no connection to this neighborhood has no business being in our homes.\"","\"Song Jingshuo.\" With Li Jiangbing gone, Jiang Cheng began calling names. \"Zhang Tao, Peng Ze, Wu Jiancheng, Nie Kuizhang.\"","The men she named were all the taller or more robust-looking members of the interim committee.","She said, \"You all go supervise him packing his things right now. He has half an hour to leave our neighborhood.\"","She meant it.","Every property staff member's face changed color.","Master Luo and Yang Xinyan both turned pale.","\"Miss—Miss Jiang...\" Yang Xinyan called out weakly, trying to plead for mercy.","Even though she had always disliked Liu Hongwang among the cleaning staff—he was lazy at work, and whenever he looked at people, he'd sneak glances at their chests, waists, and legs—he was still a colleague in the end.","The fox grieves for the hare when the hunter comes.","But Jiang Cheng acted as if she hadn't heard her.","Jiang Cheng's gaze didn't flinch. She met the stares of a hundred pairs of eyes in the plaza with perfect composure.","With Li Jiangbing absent, Song Jingshuo stepped forward first.","He didn't disappoint Jiang Cheng's expectations of him.","\"Let's go,\" he said calmly to Liu Hongwang. \"Head to the dormitory and pack your things.\"","They were serious.","Liu Hongwang panicked. He didn't care about saving face; he could bend when needed. He hurriedly said, \"I was wrong, I was wrong. I'll work hard, I promise.\"","Would Jiang Cheng forgive him? Song Jingshuo wondered. He thought... no.","He turned to look at Jiang Cheng.","Jiang Cheng's expression didn't waver. \"Make him leave.\"","Song Jingshuo actually felt a small sense of satisfaction at having guessed right.","Within the company team, if there's a dissenting element, kicking that person out is the cleanest solution for the sake of management.","It wasn't that he couldn't have thought of it himself. It was just that he couldn't cross the line of ordering someone's ruin.","But now, Jiang Cheng was asking him to send this man to his doom, and he felt no urge to object—only the will to carry it out.","Song Jingshuo could feel his own heart growing harder.","Maybe it was because he had shattered a skull, severed a neck before.","There was no going back.","He still longed for the zombies to disappear, for the city, the country, the world to return to how it was before.","But even if they did return to the rule of law, he knew he could never go back.","Before Jiang Cheng's words even faded, Song Jingshuo reached out and grabbed Liu Hongwang's arm. \"Let's go.\"","Liu Hongwang wasn't about to surrender without a fight. He shoved Song Jingshuo. \"What are you doing! I already said I'd work!\"","But Peng Ze had already strode over. Zhang Tao, Wu Jiancheng, Nie Kuizhang—even members of the interim committee who hadn't been named by Jiang Cheng—all came forward.","They all reached out their hands.","The residents listened to Liu Hongwang shout, curse, grovel, and beg for mercy—all in vain.","They watched as the interim committee subdued him, arms twisted behind his back, shoulders forced down.","One person could never resist a crowd.","\"Master Luo.\" Jiang Cheng's tone was gentle. She turned to him. \"If you'd be so kind as to go along as well, keep an eye on him while he packs. Make sure he doesn't mess with anyone else's belongings.\"","Yang Xinyan squeezed the hem of her work shirt, watching Master Luo nervously.","Master Luo sighed and nodded. \"All right.\"","To Song Jingshuo and the others, he said, \"Follow me.\"","The group escorted Liu Hongwang away, following Master Luo.","Jiang Cheng's gaze swept over the other cleaners.","No one dared meet her eyes.","The security guards looked away as well.","Yang Xinyan twisted the corner of her shirt and stared only at the ground.","\"If there's anyone who doesn't want to keep working in this neighborhood, they can also come to us voluntarily to resign,\" Jiang Cheng said. \"As for unpaid wages, once things return to normal, we'll help you settle it with the property company properly—no need to worry about that.\"","\"This is not a prison. You all have the freedom to leave.\"","\"But let me make this clear again: in this neighborhood, people can leave, but no one new comes in.\"","\"Xinyan, sorry for the trouble—please keep an eye on the work here,\" she said.","To Master Luo, to Yang Xinyan—no, in fact, with everyone on the property staff, her tone had always been this gentle and courteous.","Being called out, Yang Xinyan quickly nodded. \"Yes, yes.\"","\"Miss Jiang.\""]},{"number":40,"title":"Chapter 40","paragraphs":["The square started buzzing again.","The residents had come downstairs solely to comply with the interim committee's request—to dump their cardboard boxes, plastic shells, and bottles. When they'd been watching the commotion earlier, they'd still been holding all these things.","Now they were moving again.","Except before, everyone had just tossed things down and left, and the cleaners had sorted and bundled them.","Now many people deliberately stacked them neatly as they set them down, and some even helped organize, which lightened the cleaners' workload when it came time to bundle.","People also said \"thank you\" and \"appreciate your work\" to the cleaners.","The cleaners nodded with little \"mmm\"s.","The security guards had also dispersed, each returning to their post.","Actually, everyone could feel it—after this whole stir was over, the cleaners' and guards' eyes had cleared up.","So the idea of \"why should we still be working\" wasn't just held by that middle-aged male cleaner from earlier.","This was good too. Once things were said out in the open, people's hearts settled.","When Li Jiangbing and the others came back, they happened to run into Liu Hongwang banging his head on the ground in front of Song Jingshuo in the open space inside the main gate.","Li Jiangbing and the others were stunned: \"What's going on here?\"","Peng Ze moved closer and told him: \"He said he wouldn't work without pay. Jiang Cheng, on behalf of the interim committee, fired him. Now he's not an employee of the property company, so he's not a resident of our compound. They told him to leave. Now he regrets it.\"","Liu Hongwang was a mess of snot and tears: \"Brother! Mr. Song! I was wrong! I really was wrong! Where am I supposed to go if I leave? You're sentencing me to death.\"","Li Jiangbing and the others exchanged glances.","Song Jingshuo's expression was indifferent.","He turned and said something in a low voice to the people beside him, and a few young men went over and hoisted Liu Hongwang up.","Li Jiangbing and the others quickly pushed their carts aside to clear the way.","The men ignored Liu Hongwang's wailing, carried him to the gate, and shoved him out.","They pushed his bicycle out too.","Actually, everyone felt a bit of pity inside, and they were all diligent young people—someone had already helped tie Liu Hongwang's personal belongings onto his bicycle.","They even gave him a stick: \"Take this. For self-defense.\"","Then they stuffed a few magazines and a roll of tape into his hands, telling him: \"Wrap these around your arm. Protection against bites.\"","Liu Hongwang's face was ashen, watching the compound gate close in front of him. A familiar guard locked it from the inside.","Song Jingshuo walked to the gate and said through the gap: \"Find a place to stay while it's still daylight. It's much more dangerous at night.\"","Liu Hongwang gritted his teeth, his face twisted.","In the end, he turned his head away, tucked the stick into his luggage, got on his bicycle, and rode off.","At Jiang Cheng's request, both the east and west main gates of the compound now had two people on duty.","Song Jingshuo asked the two guards: \"Do you both know him?\"","The two guards looked at each other, then just went \"mmm.\"","\"Even if you know him, you can't let him in,\" Song Jingshuo said. \"His home is gone now; this place is your home. You're just like us—eat, drink, and sleep all happen here. If you let him in, he holds a grudge, cuts a wire, damages a pipe—you'll be affected too.\"","\"Think clearly. You've got nowhere else to go either. Right now, the compound is your home.\"","\"Guard your own home.\"","This guy's speaking skills weren't any worse than Jiang Cheng's, Li Jiangbing thought to himself with a silent whistle.","The guards nodded repeatedly: \"Understood, understood.\"","The lingering discontent in their hearts had been talked through by Jiang Cheng.","The compound belonged to the residents; they weren't residents, so they needed to work for the residents, exchanging their labor for the right to stay in the compound.","The heavens were unfair in creating such gaps between people, but there was nothing to be done about it.","Whatever thoughts remained, push them down for now and just focus on staying here safely.","In the surrounding area, this youth apartment complex was the most reliable and safest option.","Song Jingshuo walked over to Li Jiangbing and looked at their carts, each one piled high and full.","\"Good haul?\"","\"Mission accomplished. Where's Jiang Cheng?\"","\"In the square.\"","\"Let's go, let's go—find Jiang Cheng.\"","A group of them pushed the shopping carts clattering and banging toward the small square. Sure enough, Jiang Cheng was there.","\"Jiang Cheng! Look what we found!\" Li Jiangbing shouted from a distance in his booming voice.","The hardware store was a real treasure trove.","Li Jiangbing and the others had found more than twenty bags of quicklime in the hardware store.","\"This is good,\" someone said. \"Perfect for disinfecting the garden.\"","Corpses couldn't be completely burned to ash—even a crematorium's high-temperature furnace left bone fragments. And for this open-air burning in the youth apartment complex, the temperature couldn't even come close. After burning, there was a big \"pile\" of remains.","There were also many places that had left behind liquids or residue. The entire compound needed a thorough disinfection.","But there would still be a huge amount of daily waste to handle. The disinfectant and sterilizing solutions they'd hauled back this time—plenty as it seemed—might not be enough in the long run.","\"And there's this.\" Li Jiangbing had everyone bring out the items. \"Take a look.\"","\"Whoa, so many steel pipes? Where'd you get these?\"","\"From that hardware store on the street.\"","\"Hardware store, huh. Figures.\"","Jiang Cheng took a steel pipe and tested its weight, gesturing: \"If it's this long, you can really put some force behind it.\"","Right—as long as these were cut to the right length, as weapons for hitting zombies, the weight, hardness, and thickness were all perfect.","\"Can you cut them?\" Jiang Cheng asked the property staff.","Yang Xinyan said: \"Probably. The engineering department has a cutter. Master Luo and the others can handle it.\"","Everyone got busy again.","The disinfectant supplies were all sent to the clubhouse for storage.","Jiang Cheng had already designated Zhao Yi as the person in charge of that area. He had a background in environmental engineering—perfect fit.","Cutting the steel pipes didn't even need Master Luo. A bunch of engineering types among the residents eagerly volunteered: \"I can do it! I'm in!\"","They even argued over exactly what length the ideal pipe should be cut to.","The square was noisy and bustling, which actually eased Yang Xinyan's uncomfortable feeling from earlier.","It was then that Su Yu came downstairs.","She was responsible for posting on the forum and then chatting in the group chat afterward. She was also meticulous about packing up her stuff, so she didn't come down with her cardboard boxes until she'd finished everything—and then she saw how lively the square was.","A lot of people were crowded around Jiang Cheng. Su Yu didn't want to squeeze through, so she went over to greet Yang Xinyan instead.","In the compound, there were more men than women, so the women naturally gravitated toward one another and banded together, forming their own group. One by one, they pulled each other into the group.","But no one pulled Jiang Cheng in.","It wasn't that they were excluding her—it was that everyone independently felt... Jiang Cheng must be extremely busy.","Even Su Yu felt that way. And since she'd joined the interim committee and was in its group, if any of the women had special needs, she could relay them.","Or they could just go talk to Jiang Cheng directly.","Yang Xinyan had already joined the female residents' group and wasn't a stranger to Su Yu and the others. Seeing Su Yu, she immediately gave her the lowdown on what had just happened—","A cleaner who'd tried to strike had been expelled.","\"Miss Jiang is...\" Yang Xinyan was a bit in awe. \"Something else.\"","Here, \"something else\" wasn't a casual phrase; it was a full assessment.","Su Yu understood that word and that feeling very well.","This was the third time, following the smashing of Maiduo's glass door and the pharmacy.","“Otherwise, they'd be hard to manage...” she began making excuses for Jiang Cheng.","It was only then that the two of them realized the opposition of their positions—one was a homeowner, the other a property management staff member. In this incident, their stances were actually different.","Both of them felt awkward.","Yang Xinyan quickly said, “I understand, I understand.”","Now the community's above-ground and underground areas had all been cleaned up, and many homeowners could safely come downstairs to stroll around.","Of course, many people still carried “weapons” with them when they went out.","One bite from a zombie and that person was done for. Even if you didn't turn, the interim committee wouldn't let you off. So it was safer to carry a weapon while walking around.","Many homeowners who had never known each other before, lone wolves, now suddenly had a desire for social interaction.","They greeted each other when they met, proactively asked for names, exchanged contact info, and added each other to group chats.","Strangers who were neighbors turned into comrades-in-arms. Some had battlefield bonds from fighting back-to-back; some even owed each other their lives.","The atmosphere in the community had changed from before—it was almost like a giant mixer.","After Li Jiangbing handed over those disinfectant supplies to Zhao Yi, he washed his hands of that whole affair.","Apart from someone like Zhao Yi, who worked in environmental engineering, who would be interested in dealing with garbage? Li Jiangbing was even less interested.","Now the community was bustling and lively, but nothing major was going on. There was no need for him to stay by Jiang Cheng's side at all times. So he went to the property management office to watch the engineering guys cut steel pipes.","On the way, he spotted Su Yu.","He liked gentle, sweet girls. He'd misjudged Jiang Cheng on that front, but he felt he wouldn't misjudge Su Yu—she was much more gentle, the real deal inside and out.","Ahem, not that he was saying Jiang Cheng wasn't genuine inside and out. No, no.","He called out to Su Yu: “Want to go check it out?”","Su Yu had been using a frying pan as her weapon. It was a bit heavy, and not so convenient to carry around when something happened. But she had always resisted using a cleaver.","Even now, seeing her companions hack through zombie necks and chop off zombie heads still made her feel a bit sick.","With a frying pan, at least there was a full corpse.","So she followed Li Jiangbing to the property office.","The property office was very crowded. Lots of people had heard about the steel pipes and came over wanting one. Compared to chair legs or mops, steel pipes were certainly much better to use.","The cutting machine was in the engineering department, and the room couldn't hold that many people. Everyone was crammed in the hallway.","Some people got pressed against the wall or a door. When they turned their heads, they were startled to find that door welded shut: “What's going on with this?”","Someone in the know said, “That's the meeting room.”","The person in front looked up and sure enough, there was a sign reading “Meeting Room” on the door: “Ah, that one...?”","“Yeah!”","“Are those people still alive?”","“Who knows.”","“Why was it welded shut?”","“They say the people inside lost their minds and destroyed the surveillance camera. That way no one outside could see what was happening inside. So the interim committee just sealed the door shut.”","“Oh man...”","People are always curious. Someone couldn't help leaning over and pressing an ear to the door.","After listening for a moment, his expression suddenly changed drastically. He jerked upright and backed away two steps, stepping on the person behind him, who yelped in pain: “Hey! Watch it!”","Others asked, “What's wrong?”","That person said, “Listen for yourself.”","Several people couldn't help but lean in and listen too. Even the guy whose foot got stepped on couldn't resist pressing his ear to the door.","...","The sound of exhalation.","Not normal breathing.","It was the sound of someone forcefully exhaling, right by their ears.","That scared several people into straightening up. They looked at each other in silence.","“You heard it, right?”","“You heard it too?”","Everyone verified with each other.","Think about it—even if they'd killed each other, in theory, there should still be one last survivor left, right?","“Why isn't he banging on the door?”","Whether they were first-generation zombies or second-generation, they all followed instinct to attack living humans. When they encountered obstacles, they'd charge headfirst into them too.","This one was clearly standing right behind the door. So why wasn't it mindlessly banging on it?","“Is it because it knows it's useless? So...”","“But wouldn't that mean it has intelligence?”","They squeezed out a tiny bit of space. Others saw them and asked, “What's wrong?”","They replied, “There should still be one zombie in there.”","Others said, “Forget it. It's welded shut anyway.”","That made sense—just don't worry about it.","But those few exchanged glances and, in the jam-packed hallway, suddenly felt goosebumps rise.","They subtly shifted their positions, trying not to lean against that door.","Li Jiangbing came down with Su Yu. As soon as they got there, they saw it was packed with people. He called out loudly, “How's it going? Let me take a look! Make way, make way!”","Everyone made way for him, and he brought Su Yu inside.","The first batch had already cut several pipes of different lengths. Many people who'd come to watch were taking turns swinging them around to try.","Li Jiangbing didn't lack a weapon himself, but he shoved others aside: “Let the girl try first. Let the girl try first.”","He pushed Su Yu forward.","Su Yu tried several pipes and found that one of them felt especially good in her hands.","Li Jiangbing waved his hand grandly: “That one's yours. Take it.”","No one objected, and Su Yu gripped that pipe in her hand: “Thanks.”","Actually, a lot of people didn't have proper weapons and wanted a steel pipe. That was why so many people were crammed in there—they all wanted to grab one. There simply weren't enough to go around.","But when Li Jiangbing spoke, nobody dared to say a word, so Su Yu got first pick.","Su Yu thanked Li Jiangbing and squeezed out holding her new steel pipe.","The property office was in the basement of one of the buildings. The air wasn't exactly fresh to begin with, and with so many people packed in, it got even worse.","Su Yu squeezed out, came up from the basement, and immediately pulled out her phone to draft a text message:","[They brought back steel pipes and are cutting them at the property office. A ton of people are crowded there waiting. If you don't have a decent weapon, come quick. I already got one—these are really good.]","She was planning to send it to a few girls she knew well. Texts cost per message, so it wasn't the cheapest option, but it was quicker than calling each person one by one.","She thought for a moment and added: [If you can't grab one, try asking Li Jiangbing. What he says carries weight.]","After editing, she sent it out as a group message.","Jiang Cheng, Song Jingshuo, and Li Jiangbing had formed a triangle.","A triangle was stable.","And the triangle formed by these three people gave Su Yu a sense of security.","This was fine just like this.","Let nothing more change.","The youth apartment was busy and lively, chaotic but orderly.","In the afternoon, on the third day since the zombie outbreak began, the government announcement that had been looping on repeat finally updated."]},{"number":41,"title":"Chapter 41","paragraphs":["From Saturday night when the zombie virus broke out until now, Tuesday, three days had already passed.","The S City Emergency Management Command had finally released a new announcement.","This time, the citizens who had been trapped for days and steeped in fear finally heard the words \"rescue.\"","【To all citizens:】(Note)","【By order of the Central Emergency Committee, the garrison forces of the Eastern Region have overcome numerous difficulties, completed reorganization, assembly, and supply allocation, and formed the first batch of rescue troops. According to unified deployment, they will depart at 18:00 today for S City to carry out cleanup of the mutated and municipal rescue operations.】","【Water, electricity, gas, communications, and networks—all critical infrastructure has been taken over by the government, with professionals remaining at their posts to ensure the operation and stability of all system hubs.】","【We are deeply aware that every moment of waiting is agony, and every second of perseverance is hope. Citizens are asked to remain calm and take all necessary measures to ensure their own safety.】","【Through wind and rain, racing against time, we will never abandon a single citizen.】","【You are not fighting alone! All rescue personnel will do their utmost to open the channels of life and rebuild the order of survival!】","A STEM-oriented guy named Gao Yuxuan had already hacked the property management's broadcast system.","He connected the TV news to the system, and the government spokesperson's voice floated throughout the entire residential complex—everyone could hear it.","At first, cheers even broke out in the complex. But as the announcement went into detailed explanation of the specific rescue arrangements, the cheers died down.","The rescue forces were to enter from the southern edge of the city, advancing zone by zone. But the Youth Apartment complex was in the new tech development zone in the northern part of the city—very far north.","S City was a megacity with a population of over ten million. How long would it take the troops to advance from the south to the north?","Everyone fell silent.","Someone even posted on a forum, saying: 【Comparing public data from disaster relief in past years, the number of troops sent to rescue S City doesn't even reach one-eighth of what was deployed for a single flood relief in the past.】","People replied one after another: 【Is it because this time it's nationwide? Before, all forces were concentrated on one disaster zone; now it's like the whole country is a disaster zone. We can't just save S City and ignore the surrounding cities, right?】","【The military itself also lost a lot of personnel, right? I mean, with the zombie thing.】","【Jiang Cheng said it before—military living quarters are so densely packed, even more high-risk than ordinary neighborhoods. She was right.】","【But no matter what, since government rescue has begun, it'll get better eventually, right? Right?】","【Should... be, right?】","【It should be, just don't know how long it'll take for them to clear their way up to us.】","【Initial estimate—a week?】","【Damn, that long?】","【Think about how big S City is—a city with a population of over ten million!】","【Did you all know that some owners from Royal View Garden came out and got bitten to death?】","【Huh? What happened?】","【When did that happen?】","【Just today. People from Lucky Gardens saw it from upstairs, on Lucky East Street.】","Royal View Garden and the Youth Apartment are separated by Lucky Gardens.","Lucky Gardens is to the east of Youth Apartment, with Lucky West Street between the two complexes.","Royal View Garden is to the east of Lucky Gardens, with Lucky East Street between the two complexes.","【What happened?】","【They ran out of food and came out to look for some. But there are a lot of zombies over there.】","【Why didn't they clear them out first?】","【What \"clear them out\"? Think everyone's like our complex—organized, disciplined, and capable of fighting. Hell, Lucky Gardens has been leeching off us. Lucky West Street all the way to Maiduoduo—that stretch was cleared by us! The zombies in their complex were also killed by us. If it weren't for us, they wouldn't even dare come down from their buildings.】","【Exactly.】","【True.】","【Shit, people from Lucky Gardens are badmouthing our complex!】","【???】","【???】","【Where?】","【On their owners' forum.】","Everyone went over to check.","It turned out that Li Jiangbing had led dozens of people to Maiduoduo to stock up on disinfectant supplies, and people from Lucky Gardens had seen them.","The street between Lucky Gardens and the east gate of Youth Apartment is Lucky West Street. Although it had been cleared by Youth Apartment residents more than once, it was ultimately an open road, not an enclosed one, so stray zombies from farther off were bound to wander in.","Lucky Gardens couldn't organize their own people—individual households were too small and too scared to go out. Suddenly they saw a team from Youth Apartment pushing carts back and forth.","When the team from Youth Apartment made that round trip, any stray zombies on the road were inevitably taken care of as they went.","Some people from Lucky Gardens dithered and hesitated, then finally mustered the courage to go out—pure freeloading.","But when they got back, they started cursing on the forum, saying the supermarket shelves were empty of food. They seemed to have forgotten that just yesterday, they themselves had gone out and grabbed a haul. Anyway, they blamed it all on Youth Apartment, saying that trip after trip from Youth Apartment had stripped Maiduoduo bare.","Damn it!","The Youth Apartment residents were furious. Everyone flooded over to the Lucky Gardens forum to trade insults.","At first, a few people tried to argue back, but honestly, Lucky Gardens was completely in the wrong, and not many were willing to step up and defend their own complex—they soon went quiet.","In a short time, the front page of Lucky Gardens' forum was flooded by Youth Apartment residents.","Jiang Cheng only skimmed through all this quickly.","She checked the owners' forums of the nearby communities. By today, a few complexes had finally managed to organize themselves, but there were also communities where no one took the lead and everyone remained scattered.","Many posts were crying out that their homes had no food left, that their babies had no formula.","Switching to a major well-known forum, the hot topic was \"What exactly is the zombie virus?\" Many experts in biology and medicine were voicing their opinions, questioning the biological characteristics of \"zombies\" and denying from a biological standpoint the possibility of such a thing existing. Yet this thing was really there, right downstairs or next door in every home, lunging at the scent of flesh and blood.","All kinds of viewpoints were muddled into a chaotic mess.","Everyone's understanding of zombies had also been updated. Previously, they had thought that people bitten to death by zombies were simply dead. Now they discovered that only those whose necks had been chewed completely through actually died. As long as the neck was intact and the head was whole—even if the person lay on the ground in a pool of blood looking \"dead\"—after a while, they would sit up and turn into a zombie.","Jiang Cheng suddenly understood. No wonder the corpses dragged out of the double room earlier all had their necks gnawed through.","In that small room, with the environment quiet, the zombie's biting was undisturbed—it just kept biting and biting, until it chewed through the neck completely and finished the person off for real.","Li Ziqing's boyfriend, who was on the same floor as Jiang Cheng, had his neck broken that way.","Then a small number of those infected, for reasons unknown, whose necks weren't broken, mutated into second-generation zombies—like that one on the fifth floor that stepped on the back of a first-generation zombie and leaped out to bite someone.","The first encounter in the garden happened at night, and back then no one dared go downstairs, so this phenomenon hadn't been observed.","With this new information, Jiang Cheng realized the transmissibility of the zombie virus was stronger than she had previously thought.","The situation they were facing was more severe than expected.","Another hot topic on the forum was that major cities like S City had finally received rescue, with some people optimistic and others pessimistic.","The central government had established an emergency command headquarters, but the specific rescue efforts were managed and directed by local emergency command centers. Resources across cities were highly uneven.","The phrase \"rebuilding the order of survival\" in S City's government announcement was interpreted in various ways.","Residents of slightly smaller cities were furious that rescue priority went to the big cities, feeling their right to life was being ignored.","People in even smaller places, such as rural areas, had no voice at all.","Broadband had only been developed for a few years? Only in a metropolis like S City could most households have broadband. In many small cities, broadband penetration was still low, and rural areas were essentially silent zones.","Other issues, such as power outages, water cuts, gas shutoffs, and even fires, had occurred on a small scale in many places.","S City was a major metropolis. After the initial panic, surviving government personnel established a temporary emergency command department. Professionals risked their lives to break through zombies, rushed to key posts, and stood by their duties.","But not every place could be like S City.","With current technology, water plants and power plants could basically operate automatically for long periods without obstruction. But that didn't mean malfunctions wouldn't happen.","And when it came down to the user end—water pipes, wires, electrical boxes—failures were completely normal.","In normal times, someone would come to fix them immediately, and they'd be back in service quickly. The downtime was so short that residents never even felt the inconvenience.","But now, these failures couldn't be repaired in time. Broken meant broken. Shut off meant it never came back.","Residents were in complete despair.","Even fires that received firefighter rescue were a minority.","City fire departments were arguably the first government force to mobilize after the zombie virus outbreak. Yet they were simultaneously caught between two dangers: massive fires and zombies.","In the past two days, the death rate among brave and steadfast firefighters had been extremely high. Most died at the jaws of zombies within the fires.","That was why, even though fire truck sirens were heard on Sunday, they had all disappeared over the past two days.","In fact, any area where no lines or pipes were damaged, and no fires or explosions had occurred at all, was extremely lucky.","Jiang Cheng had actually interpreted and analyzed S City's new announcement today too. But thinking about it in the abstract was useless—she'd have to wait until tomorrow to see the actual situation to know what was really going on.","What Jiang Cheng was thinking about now was another question. She clicked the X to close the browser, and her chair spun 180 degrees to face the bed.","Mo Li was lying at the foot of the bed.","Jiang Cheng could reach him just by scooting her chair forward.","His fur was jet black and glossy, with an incredible texture.","Mo Li opened his eyes, jade green, with Jiang Cheng's reflection in them.","Jiang Cheng gently scratched his fluffy little head with her fingers. Mo Li stretched his neck back in pleasure, chin tilted high toward the ceiling.","Jiang Cheng observed him, paused her fingers, and asked softly, \"Mo Li... do you... need to bask in the sun?\"","Mo Li now appeared to be in a basically healthy state. \"Basically\" meant he could walk on his own, go eat cat food, and drink water on his own.","Although it was strange that the litter box remained so clean that not a single grain of litter had even been disturbed, Mo Li had clearly recovered his basic mobility.","But Jiang Cheng wouldn't be fooled by such simple appearances. She could observe subtler issues.","From body temperature, mental state, and energy levels, Mo Li displayed completely different states between day and night.","Once the sun went down, Mo Li appeared to be in a state of running low on power, lying still for long periods. This was completely different from when Jiang Cheng first encountered him a week ago.","But during the day, when sunlight could reach him, he seemed to recharge like a battery.","Others might not notice the difference, but Jiang Cheng could perceive it.","Mo Li's jade green eyes simply looked at her, unable to understand what she was saying.","Jiang Cheng decided to try an experiment. She cupped both hands together and wrapped them around Mo Li's head.","A week ago, she had awakened to the fact that she was a transmigrator. Back then, she still wanted to continue her current peaceful, uneventful life, so some of the strange phenomena from her first encounter with Mo Li had been overlooked.","But over the past two days, information from before her transmigration had been leaking into her mind like seepage through cracks.","And so she remembered those things she'd ignored—","A faint electric current flowing through her heart.","A sense of telepathic understanding that seemed to grasp what the kitten meant.","And it had happened more than once.","[Mo Li, Mo Li.]","Cupping her hands around Mo Li's fuzzy little head, Jiang Cheng stared into his eyes and attempted to communicate through consciousness.","[Mo Li, do you need to bask in the sun to regain energy?]","[Do you need to bask in the sun?]","[The sun?]","Suddenly, an unusual sensation flowed through her heart for a brief instant.","At the same time, Mo Li lifted his head slightly: \"Meow.\"","[Yes.]","It worked! She could actually communicate with Mo Li!","Jiang Cheng held her breath, focusing her mind: [Can you transform again?]","\"Meow.\"","[%¥#]","The meaning was unclear. It seemed Mo Li himself didn't know the answer.","Jiang Cheng changed the question: [Besides basking in the sun and eating cat food, do you need me to do anything else?]","But this question seemed too complex for Mo Li. He let out a soft \"meow,\" this time without any meaning—pure confusion.","For a kitten, this question was too complicated.","He might understand \"basking in the sun\" and \"eating cat food,\" but he couldn't grasp the meaning of the entire sentence.","Jiang Cheng released her hands. Mo Li's clear green eyes looked at her.","Jiang Cheng looked back at him.","So, this communication—was it her ability? Or his ability?","Did it have anything to do with the infection mutation?","No, no, no.","Her first electric connection with Mo Li had happened when she encountered the flasher in Building Four.","That had nothing to do with the zombie virus at all. It had happened days before the zombie virus even appeared.","It was only about her and Mo Li.","Or maybe only about her?","Why was this happening?"]},{"number":42,"title":"Chapter 42","paragraphs":["After the night passed, many people woke up late on Wednesday.","They didn’t have to go to work anyway, and there was nothing else to do. Plus, a lot of people had stayed up late surfing the internet the night before, so Wednesday morning found most people getting up late.","Jiang Cheng was one of the early risers. She took Mo Li downstairs bright and early.","Although the charred wreckage was still piled up in the central plaza, the neighborhood seemed especially clean today compared to yesterday.","Jiang Cheng pulled Mo Li out of her shoulder bag and held him up. Mo Li stepped lightly on her palm, then leaped gracefully onto the beam of the pavilion, stretching his neck as if he were thoroughly enjoying the morning sunlight.","“You enjoy the sun here, then,” she told him.","Whether Mo Li could actually understand her when she spoke to him directly like that—who knew. It didn’t matter. Mo Li was special; he obviously wasn’t going to run off on his own. Almost everyone in the neighborhood knew this black cat belonged to her. No one would mistake him for a stray and take him away.","Besides, no one had the heart to adopt stray cats right now anyway.","“I’m going to work out. I’ll come back and get you in a bit.”","Jiang Cheng headed to the community clubhouse.","She stopped by the swimming pool first. Zhao Yi had worked hard all day yesterday, laying down a layer of quicklime on the pool floor. Yesterday, the property management’s cleaning staff had already begun collecting trash from the neighborhood and dumping it there.","Large quantities of cardboard boxes, paper scraps, and plastic bottles collected yesterday were also neatly stacked in one of the clubhouse rooms.","This was why the neighborhood felt so refreshed today.","Thanks to everyone’s efforts, the community was functioning again.","Zhao Yi had called her last night to report on the progress. Today Jiang Cheng took a look herself, and she was satisfied.","She went to the gym and got on the treadmill first.","She’d barely worked up a sweat when Song Jingshuo walked in. He had gotten up early too.","That morning, Song Jingshuo had woken up and turned on his computer first thing. He saw that in several group chats, people had still been sending messages at three or four in the morning—staying up late.","There wasn’t much you could do at night anyway. The interim committee had also asked residents to try not to go downstairs after dark.","Even though the neighborhood had been cleaned up, no one could guarantee there wasn’t something hiding somewhere, or that someone injured or infected hadn’t gone unnoticed.","In short, nights were dangerous, so staying downstairs was to be avoided.","That meant daytime had to be used even more effectively, and staying up late served no purpose or benefit.","Song Jingshuo noticed Jiang Cheng had good routines and had even come to work out early in the morning as if they’d read each other’s minds. It was both surprising and not surprising.","People like them—the first essential quality was self-discipline.","You had to have a certain strength of will to be truly self-disciplined. Those who lacked it could only mark time and drift with the current.","“Morning,” he greeted her, stepping onto the treadmill next to hers.","Jiang Cheng replied, “Morning.”","That was it.","Song Jingshuo’s fingertip hovered over the start button for a moment, then pulled back and rested on the handrail as he watched Jiang Cheng run and sweat.","Jiang Cheng caught him looking from the corner of her eye, turned her head to glance at him, and pressed the stop button.","The belt slowed and gradually came to a halt.","Jiang Cheng asked, “Something on your mind?”","Her cheeks had turned rosy from exercising, her young skin firm and elastic. She really was a beautiful woman.","But her expression was detached, even a bit severe, without a hint of softness.","Song Jingshuo felt a bit aggrieved. “Jiang Cheng, is the way you treat me vs. the way you treat Zhao Yi really that different?”","They’d spent these past days shoulder to shoulder working together under intense pressure—shouldn’t that have brought them closer?","Jiang Cheng treated him with nothing but business formality, yet with Zhao Yi, that nerdy engineer type, she’d smile and be all sweet. It was too much.","Song Jingshuo had never been one to take a loss lying down. And besides, he no longer had any rivalry with Jiang Cheng—only appreciation. They were on the same team now.","He had to push back a little.","Jiang Cheng narrowed her eyes at him.","Song Jingshuo was tall and lean, handsome. In a dress shirt he had that crisp professional look; in workout gear, he had an athletic edge. In romantic matters, he was the kind of man who came out on top wherever he went.","She let her gaze size him up. He was thoroughly confident.","Jiang Cheng explained seriously: “The government’s rescue teams have arrived now. Things haven’t deteriorated to that level.”","“...” Song Jingshuo asked, “What level?”","Jiang Cheng: “To the level where people need sex to relieve and soothe the psychological pressure brought on by the threat of death.”","Song Jingshuo: “...”","Song Jingshuo now shared the same thought as Li Jiangbing—","He’d misjudged her.","Song Jingshuo rubbed his temple, about to say something, but Jiang Cheng continued explaining: “Communication with you is completely smooth. No auxiliary tricks needed—straight talk gets the job done. But with others, adjusting communication methods to each person’s personality to spark everyone’s initiative and efficiency—that’s what we should be doing right now.”","The two locked eyes.","Song Jingshuo’s eyes lit up.","She said “we.”","“Once this is over and life gets back to normal, let’s have a meal together,” he extended the invitation.","Jiang Cheng nodded. “Sure.”","She pressed the start button on her treadmill again. “But whether things can get back to normal—the assessment comes after today.”","Song Jingshuo’s face turned serious. “You don’t have confidence in the government’s rescue efforts?”","“We’re short on key, effective information right now. Only after today ends can we say whether we can have confidence,” Jiang Cheng said.","What was key, effective information? Naturally, the scale and speed of the rescue.","The government certainly had plenty of disaster-relief experience. But that was flood-rescue experience, earthquake-rescue experience. Zombies were something no one had ever heard of—the government was facing the same thing for the first time.","You had to wait and see how far the rescue forces advanced today before making an objective assessment and setting proper expectations.","“Until then, let’s just focus on staying in shape. Even if things really do return to normal in the future, it won’t hurt.”","She used the phrases “even if” and “really do.”","Was she really that pessimistic?","The morning sun was bright. The gym’s treadmills faced floor-to-ceiling windows overlooking the community garden.","Bright sunlight streamed in through them.","Song Jingshuo’s rare sense of ease from these past days dissipated once again, and he felt even heavier in his chest than he had in the previous few days.","He also pressed the start button on his treadmill as the belt slowly began to speed up.","“Jiang Cheng, what do you do for a living?”","“Events and exhibitions. You?”","“Finance.”","“No more talking.”","“Alright.”","The two of them ran.","At the gate, the security guards changed shifts.","The two guards who had been on night duty all night, rubbing their shoulders and lower backs, returned to the dormitory.","Back in the dormitory, where no residents could hear them, they finally dared to speak.","One guard said: “Once the military sorts this thing out, we should sue that Jiang Cheng.”","“...For what?”","“She drove Old Liu out like that—that’s basically murder! We’ll sue her, make her do time!”","“Old Liu brought it on himself.”","“Are you stupid? Whose side are you on, can’t you tell? Old Liu was one of us. If it weren’t for that Jiang Cheng, maybe with Old Liu’s lead we wouldn’t have had to work at all by now—we could’ve been lying in the dorm all comfortable like the residents.”","“But Miss Jiang said...”","“Pah!” The guard spat, almost hitting his coworker square in the face. “What makes them so special? They’re all people, aren’t they? Just because they’ve got a few stinking bucks! So what if we’re not homeowners?! Those who aren’t homeowners have to be their servants?! Spending the whole night on duty feels good to you, huh? Your back doesn’t ache, your shoulders aren’t sore, you don’t wanna be lying in bed just like them?! How dumb are you.”","He was fuming.","He’d had enough of watching these homeowners get all comfortable a long time ago.","All of them, in their suits and ties and high heels, looking all high and mighty, wouldn't even glance at them when passing through the gates every day.","What's so noble about that?","Especially that Jiang Cheng—a woman, a mere girl, the kind who wouldn't even be allowed at the dinner table back in their village—yet she bosses around a whole bunch of grown men. What a joke.","Women like that are clearly trouble. In their village, no one would ever marry one.","And the worst part is, she's actually pretty damned good-looking. Pah!","By ten o'clock, the sun was high, and residents began drifting downstairs to stroll around the complex.","Many of them were the type who, after work, would stay cooped up at home playing games on weekdays, who could go the entire weekend without stepping outside—yet here they were, coming down in droves, soaking up the sun, exchanging greetings with familiar neighbors.","Choosing not to go downstairs and not being able to go downstairs are two very different things.","Now, being able to freely go downstairs and safely wander around had somehow become something that stirred emotion and gratitude in people's hearts.","If you've never known the fear of not daring to step out the door, how can you cherish the freedom you once took for granted?","Some residents brought down pets that hadn't been walked in days. Mostly dogs.","Jiang Cheng came back from the gym, showered at home, and saw several people walking dogs in the garden from her window.","Mo Li was still basking on the beam of the pavilion. Jiang Cheng filled a small bowl with cat food and went downstairs to see Mo Li.","\"Come down and eat,\" she called to him.","Mo Li looked at her.","Words alone wouldn't do it. Jiang Cheng stared into Mo Li's eyes, concentrated, and communicated through thought: [Eat.]","She tried to keep the message as simple as possible—the simpler, the better for Mo Li to understand.","But Mo Li refused: [Sunlight.]","Jiang Cheng: \"Huh?\"","Mo Li seemed to worry she hadn't understood, and emphasized again: [Sunlight.]","He lifted his head toward the sky, letting the sun wash over his entire body. He had only eaten cat food once after dark yesterday, to replenish energy for the night.","But now, he felt no hunger at all. Sunlight pierced through his fur, and energy radiated into his cells.","His body was not just repairing itself—it was storing up.","Jiang Cheng watched Mo Li for a while.","Some things couldn't be formed into clear language; the transmission of thought was vague and hazy, but she could vaguely understand.","It was hard to believe.","A little cat saying he didn't need to eat food, that sunlight alone was enough.","But zombies were hard to believe too—how could people turn into monsters?","And a little black cat could turn into a great black panther.","There was even telepathy.","And then there was her, a transmigrator from another world.","So maybe solar charging didn't sound all that far-fetched.","In fact, if it were true, it would be absolutely wonderful. It meant an endless supply of energy at zero cost.","\"Jiang Cheng—\"","Someone called her from a distance. Jiang Cheng turned and saw Su Yu walking over with another girl. They were walking a small dog.","They came up to greet Jiang Cheng.","They also spotted Mo Li on top of the pavilion: \"Taking your cat out to sunbathe?\"","By now, pretty much everyone recognized Jiang Cheng's cat, which she carried with her everywhere.","Never mind what was going on outside the complex—whether there were still plenty of people without food supplies, worrying about empty stomachs or afraid to go out. For now, with the apartment complex locked up tight, everyone had food and drink at home, just waiting for government rescue.","The mood was light at the moment. The girls chatted with Jiang Cheng, chattering away, full of rosy hopes that \"this whole thing will blow over in a few days.\"","Jiang Cheng didn't pour cold water on them either. Some things, some concerns, she only shared with people like Song Jingshuo. She'd wait until today's update before saying anything more.","She crouched down to look at the little dog. \"So cute.\"","The dog belonged to the other girl, who said, \"His name is Fu Duoduo.\"","Jiang Cheng cupped the little dog's head with her hand. \"Fu Duoduo, hello there.\"","She gazed into the dog's eyes.","After a moment, she released her hand.","\"Cute,\" she said with a smile.","Nothing happened.","Telepathy was limited to her and Mo Li alone."]},{"number":43,"title":"Chapter 43","paragraphs":["Mo Li showed no sign of wanting to go back inside.","Direct sunlight outdoors was far more effective than sun through a window indoors.","And within his range of perception, there was no sense of danger either.","Jiang Cheng now recalled how Mo Li had tugged at the hem of her clothes earlier, insisting on coming out with her. He must have sensed something.","Now that the youth apartment complex, the adjacent Jixiang Jiayuan, and the Jixiang West Street between them were all clean, Mo Li no longer had that tense feeling.","He now looked like an ordinary little cat, lounging lazily in the sun, as if all was well with the world.","Since that was the case, Jiang Cheng didn't push it. She went home by herself.","Turning on her computer, she picked a few major forums and posted the same thread: [Has anyone seen cases of animal infections?]","To avoid causing panic, she added: [Just curious. So many people keep cats and dogs—have any cats or dogs been infected with the zombie virus?]","After posting, she turned on the TV.","As it happened, there was fresh content on the news: [A reporter from our station at the Emergency Management Command brings word: rescue forces have advanced into the S city urban area, currently reaching the Chaoqing District, where intense cleanup operations are underway.]","[The first batch of relief supplies is following close behind.]","[The on-site emergency command has stated they will adopt a \"district-by-district sweep, not missing a single household\" approach, going all out to ensure the safety of the people's lives.]","[Please firmly believe that the nation stands with you, sharing the same breath and the same fate.]","[Stay confident, and be sure to take shelter and self-rescue measures.]","[We will surely get through this together and rebuild our homes!]","Intense cleanup operations.","Usually, the word that follows \"intense\" is \"battle.\" Using \"intense\" with \"cleanup\" felt a bit odd.","But you could read between the lines: although the authorities still hadn't used the term \"zombie\" and continued to refer to them as \"mutants,\" they clearly no longer regarded them as human.","If they were still human, it would have been called a battle.","It was because they were no longer human that it was called cleanup.","Jiang Cheng watched the segment several times on a loop, then opened the forums again.","The major internet companies that were well known had already come under the leadership of the government's emergency committee. In the past couple of days, every major forum had set up local sections for netizens to coordinate and share information by region. The internet company employees were still coming into work, or possibly working remotely. Either way, they had adapted to the times, giving people exactly what they needed—it was indeed very convenient.","Jiang Cheng opened the S city section of a major forum, and sure enough, many people were already analyzing the new announcements.","[When they said yesterday they would rebuild the order of life, I already felt pessimistic. Today they mentioned \"ensuring the safety of lives\"—in past earthquakes and floods, they always said \"ensuring the safety of lives and property.\" The tone is clearly different. Sigh.]","[It basically means \"as long as you're alive, that's enough,\" right?]","[Starting from Chaoqing District—that's far from us. When will they get to Guangxiu District?]","[From Chaoqing heading north, the next stop will definitely be Gaotang District. You're still far from Guangxiu.]","[Does \"district-by-district sweep\" mean administrative districts or residential complexes?]","[I was wondering about that too. Then he said \"not missing a single household,\" so the unit is the household. That means the \"district\" mentioned earlier refers to residential complexes. That makes much more sense.]","[The person above has a point. You have to treat zombies like an infectious disease or a virus to understand it. If you want to clean up a virus, you have to thoroughly clean an entire area. Otherwise, if you leave a few spots unclean, won't it multiply and spread rapidly? Don't forget the zombie virus is infectious. And now everyone knows that getting scratched or bitten means infection and mutation. There are bound to be people who got infected and stay silent, trying to hide. Then they silently turn, come out, and bite a bunch of people. Even if each zombie bites three people, and those three turn and each bite three more... then you see the point clearly. So not cleaning up completely is the same as not cleaning at all.]","Jiang Cheng switched to her own residential complex's owners' forum, and true to form, someone had already copied over the discussions from the big forums.","The festive mood from yesterday when they first heard the government was launching rescue operations had faded.","Now it was all worries about \"how long until they get to the new development area over here?\"","As noon approached, when Jiang Cheng was about to start making lunch, the walkie-talkie crackled: \"Miss Jiang? Miss Jiang, can you hear me? The interim committee?\"","Jiang Cheng immediately grabbed the walkie-talkie: \"Copy, this is Jiang Cheng. Who is this?\"","The other side said: \"This is the east gate. A dozen or so people have shown up, saying they're from Maiduoduo Supermarket, and they're looking for you. Hold on, he wants to talk to you.\"","The voice on the walkie-talkie changed, this time a man: \"Miss Jiang, right? My surname is Dong, I'm the guy from Maiduoduo, we've met several times, it's me.\"","Jiang Cheng recognized the voice right away—it was the guy at Maiduoduo called Brother Dong, the little supervisor: \"I know you, I remember. What's the matter?\"","Yang Xinyan usually stayed at the property management center, because she was the one responsible for communicating with the residents.","The walkie-talkie was on the all-channel frequency, so she had heard the conversation between the east gate guard and Jiang Cheng.","Jiang Cheng suddenly called out: \"Property management center, is anyone at the property management center?\"","Yang Xinyan quickly replied: \"I'm here, I'm here!\"","Jiang Cheng: \"Xinyan, broadcast over the loudspeaker for the interim committee members to gather at the east gate.\"","Wednesday morning counted as one of the rare relaxed moments these past few days. Some people were lying in bed, playing games; others were strolling in the garden or sunbathing. Suddenly the loudspeaker crackled to life, and the property girl's voice rang out: [Interim committee members, gather at the east gate. Interim committee members, gather at the east gate. Right now, immediately. I'll repeat: interim committee...]","Clearly, something was up. Interim committee members who had been lying down got up, those playing games pushed away their keyboards, and the ones strolling downstairs turned and started running.","Not just the interim committee—many residents in the garden also followed along to the east gate to see what was happening.","Jiang Cheng met Brother Dong at the east gate.","Brother Dong had brought his supermarket employees to beg for medicine.","Jiang Cheng confirmed once more: \"You're sure it's not the zombie virus?\"","\"Positive,\" Brother Dong cursed. \"It was the people from Yujing Xiangyuan who did it.\"","East of Jixiang Jiayuan was Yujing Xiangyuan.","The people at the youth apartment complex looked down on Jixiang Jiayuan, but at least Jixiang Jiayuan had someone step up to organize them, even if the organization was loose—it was still something.","Yujing Xiangyuan had gotten nothing organized at all. Some residents had run out of supplies at home and couldn't just hide inside and starve, so they had to risk their lives going downstairs.","Some were bitten to death on the way, but others managed to make it to Maiduoduo Supermarket.","They had risked their lives to sprint to the supermarket, only to find the food shelves completely empty. Even the food section in the warehouse was cleaned out.","That was absolutely devastating.","Brother Dong told them: \"Everything was emptied out by the people from the youth apartment and Jixiang Jiayuan. Look at the front door—they smashed it. It's all gone. Nothing left. Take a look around and grab whatever you need.\"","He was trying to shoo them away.","But some people were quick on the uptake. Looking across the supermarket, there were roughly a dozen or so staff members, and none of them looked panicked.","Why weren't they panicking? Because they must have food stocked up!","Those who saw through this demanded that Brother Dong and his crew share some of the food. Their families couldn't hold out any longer—there were kids and elderly at home, all with stomachs growling from hunger.","But Brother Dong and his people had witnessed firsthand how the folks from Jixiang Jiayuan and the Youth Apartment had stripped this very supermarket bare. They'd seen with their own eyes how people brawled over a single bag of rice.","They knew all too well how vital food was in these extraordinary times.","So naturally, they flat-out denied having anything.","Nobody believed them. Not a single person in front of them looked like they were starving—everyone seemed well-fed and full.","These people had crossed through life-and-death situations to get here for their families. Their emotions were already teetering on the edge of collapse, ready to ignite at the slightest spark.","Not to mention they were armed. They'd already bashed in skulls and sliced through necks.","Seeing the supermarket staff's evasive glances and perfunctory words, anger rose from the depths of their hearts, and vicious thoughts surged from their guts.","The two sides clashed.","Fortunately, the people from Yujing Xiangyuan had come in scattered groups and weren't united. The Maiduoduo side was solidly united in protecting their food, and their weapons were handy, too. In the end, they drove off the Yujing Xiangyuan people.","There were injuries on both sides. Some had black eyes and swollen faces; others were bloody and battered.","The bloody ones had suffered external wounds. A bunch of rough men weren't too careful about such things, and their wounds weren't properly treated.","By nightfall, they started running fevers. This morning, when everyone discovered it, the fevers were already high. If this continued, they'd be in trouble—they needed medicine.","Everyone basically knew that a few pharmacies were scattered around the supermarket area. The nearest and safest one was the shop on Jixiang West Street.","Why was it safe? Because that street had been swept back and forth by the Youth Apartment people multiple times, cleared out thoroughly.","It was probably the safest stretch of road in the vicinity.","After assessing the risks, Brother Dong still decided to lead people out to get medicine. When they arrived at the small pharmacy's door and saw the smashed-in entrance, they knew it was bad. Going inside, they found it completely empty.","Jiang Cheng and her people had taken a good chunk of the important categorized medicines. The old men and women who went in after they'd left grabbed whatever was left, not caring about categories at all—they hauled everything away.","Only birth control pills and male enhancement pills remained. Even the health supplements were gone.","There were other pharmacies, but getting to them wasn't as safe—there would definitely be zombies on the road.","One bite, and it was death.","Though they had some camaraderie with their colleagues, that bond wasn't strong enough to die for them. Nobody was willing.","But Brother Dong could figure it out: \"Those bastards from the Youth Apartment are sharp as foxes—it must have been them.\"","It was also a young woman from the Youth Apartment who'd been the first to smash open the supermarket's main gate. Brother Dong had a gut feeling that this pharmacy had a high chance of being busted open by her too.","That young woman definitely had medicine on her. Even if she didn't, since she was a leader at the Youth Apartment, she'd surely find a way to get some.","So Brother Dong came knocking on their door.","And since he was already here—a bit late, but still—Brother Dong and his crew had finally realized they needed to stock up on some medicine too. So they also wanted to get some other meds.","He stated his purpose. Jiang Cheng spoke into the walkie-talkie: \"We've only got a little medicine here, and there are so many people in our compound. We can't just give it to you for free.\"","Brother Dong thought to himself, See? Called it. A young thing, but sharp as a tack.","The two negotiated over the walkie-talkie. Brother Dong took his people back to the supermarket once, and now, they were back again.","This time, they weren't empty-handed. They pushed several carts full of drinks: \"Come on, let's trade.\""]},{"number":44,"title":"Chapter 44","paragraphs":["Jiang Cheng had made it clear to Brother Dong over the walkie-talkie: medicine—yes, they had it—but it wasn’t going to be free.","She asked Brother Dong what was left in the supermarket.","Brother Dong rattled off a bunch of pots, pans, slippers, brooms, stools, chairs, plastic goods—nothing of any value. Jiang Cheng didn’t want any of that.","Brother Dong said, “Food’s gone, not even fermented bean curd left. Just some drinks.”","Those drinks sat deep in the warehouse. The people who’d gone in after them only wanted rice and flour, ignoring the sugary stuff.","Jiang Cheng heard him out and made the call: “Drinks it is.”","That was how the East Gate deal came about.","Several cartloads of high-sugar drinks traded for a few small boxes of medicine.","Brother Dong: “That’s steep.”","Jiang Cheng: “Fine, then the deal’s off.”","Brother Dong: “Fine, fine, deal!”","The neighborhood committee members heard the broadcast and came ready for something serious, weapons in hand. Under Li Jiangbing’s direction, many had already been issued the new batch of steel pipes—there weren’t that many, so priority naturally went to the committee members, especially the suicide squad. They were the block’s main fighting force.","The uniformity gave them real presence.","Turned out they were there to pick up sugar water.","The BuyDuoDuo crew had uniform weapons too—all hammers—but in terms of sheer presence, they came up short.","The two sides conducted a cordial and friendly exchange.","“Jiangbing,” Jiang Cheng said. “Take it to the plaza and hand it out to everyone.”","Li Jiangbing was uniquely suited for this sort of thing. Under him, order prevailed.","“On it!” Li Jiangbing directed the others to push shopping carts toward the plaza, grinning. “Drinks are being distributed!”","A crowd of onlookers followed along to the small plaza to claim their bottles.","Normally, who would miss a bottle of soda? But over the past few days, most homes had run dry. Anyone who’d been to the supermarket twice wasn’t about to lug heavy drinks back. Of course, rice and flour came first—even toilet paper beat drinks in priority.","The old folks of Jixiang Jiayuan didn’t bother with that either. People were grabbing baby formula, not soda.","It was a bit of a sideshow, but on a Wednesday morning, it felt just right.","The sun was bright, the grass was green, and sipping a sweet drink—as long as you kept your eyes off the charred remains in the plaza—almost felt like slipping back into normal life.","Just waiting for the government’s rescue effort, waiting for everything to return to business as usual.","Jiang Cheng and Song Jingshuo stood at the East Gate talking to Brother Dong.","Brother Dong pulled out a cigarette, handed one to Song Jingshuo, and grumbled to Jiang Cheng: “That’s rough.”","Jiang Cheng only smiled.","Song Jingshuo explained for her: “Technically, that stuff belongs to the community. We really can’t just give it away.”","Ever since Monday afternoon, when Su Yu posted the notice informing everyone that the committee had medicine, they’d been fielding requests for it from early evening onward.","People with diarrhea, stomach aches, all kinds of ailments.","The committee needed to prove its value to people if it wanted them to follow its orders.","Li Jiangbing was at the plaza handing out drinks, one bottle per person. And he’d held back two cases.","When someone asked why, Li Jiangbing said: “Saving some for Little Zhao and his guys. They’re at the community center dealing with waste disinfection—stinking to high heaven. If you want to go take over for them, I’ll give you one too.”","That shut everyone up.","It was something Jiang Cheng had reminded Li Jiangbing about yesterday, when he’d come up with all those steel pipes: “Whatever you’ve got, prioritize the committee, especially the suicide squad and the volunteers. Whatever it is, don’t shortchange those people.”","Li Jiangbing heartily agreed and carried it out to the letter.","The plaza buzzed with noise, but it carried an air of ease and cheer.","From the East Gate, Brother Dong could pick up traces of it and was moved to remark: “No other block in the area is doing as well as yours.”","Song Jingshuo had stuck around there specifically to ask about the surrounding area: “What’s the situation over at Yujing Xiangyuan?”","Other supermarket workers chimed in with complaints:","“They’ve lost it.”","“Eyes all bloodshot.”","“Hell, it’s a good thing we’re manual laborers—we’re not afraid of them.”","People who worked in physical jobs for years, even the wiry ones, had strength far beyond the average person. In a fight, both sides took hits, but BuyDuoDuo didn’t come off worse.","“We only held back because they looked so pathetic.”","“A few people from Shanshui Yayuan, Deqingli, and Lekang Jiayuan came over too. Deqingli has its own convenience store in the compound—apparently it’s already emptied out.”","“Lekang Jiayuan sent some of their people to Haoneighbour. They’re closer to Haoneighbour.”","Haoneighbour was a small neighborhood convenience store.","Song Jingshuo nodded: “That’s something, at least. As long as they’ve got food.”","But having been through two rounds of panic-buying, even looting, Song Jingshuo knew a single Haoneighbour couldn’t feed an entire compound’s population.","Thank God the youth apartment had struck early.","He couldn’t help but glance at Jiang Cheng again. She was listening to the conversation too, but clearly nothing about any of this surprised her.","Of course—someone who’d mobilized everyone to charge out and raid supermarkets within the first moments had seen this coming.","Jiang Cheng said: “You’d better stash the food somewhere secure. People are going to keep coming.”","BuyDuoDuo was a prime target.","When people nearby finally dared—or were forced—to step outside to scavenge, almost every one of them would think of BuyDuoDuo first.","Brother Dong said: “But the government’s already started relief.”","Jiang Cheng said: “They’re down south. Let’s see how far they get today. Do the math on the distance from here to the south side, and you’ll know when they’ll reach us.”","The BuyDuoDuo crew fell silent, faces grim.","They took the few boxes of medicine the deal had earned them and headed back.","The youth apartment’s gate closed and locked again.","Zhao Yi and his crew were called out from the community center to get their drinks.","By now, he was a name in the compound, a familiar face. “That Zhao Yi, the environmental engineering guy,” people would say.","When everything had been orderly and running smoothly, he hadn’t felt especially valuable. But with all public services grinding to a halt, people suddenly realized they couldn’t survive without people like him.","Waste management was no joke. Humans produced an absurd amount of garbage.","When Song Jingshuo and Jiang Cheng strolled over, the central plaza was crowded with people sipping their drinks.","Somebody was under the pavilion going “pspspsps” at the black cat on the roof.","Cozy, practically a tea party.","Li Jiangbing had stashed two bottles for them. He wouldn’t have forgotten Jiang Cheng’s even if he forgot everyone else’s.","Mo Li spotted Jiang Cheng and lifted his head.","Jiang Cheng could feel his irritation. All that pspspsps from below—it genuinely pissed him off.","Jiang Cheng raised her hand, and Mo Li stepped onto her palm, climbed up to her shoulder, and settled there.","She sipped her drink and patted Mo Li absently to soothe him.","Song Jingshuo was chatting with Li Jiangbing and some others, relaying what he’d heard from Brother Dong.","The block had it so good that people sometimes forgot just how rough things were outside. Hearing Song Jingshuo talk, it hit them anew.","Jiang Cheng squinted for a moment, then asked Zhao Yi: “Can that pile be dealt with?”","She nodded toward the charred remains.","Zhao Yi said: “Already handled. Neutralized.”","\"No, I mean,\" Jiang Cheng said, \"we handle it here. Can we move it to the swimming pool?\"","Zhao Yi was silent for a moment: \"It's not out of the question...\"","But that would be treating a dead person like garbage.","They hadn't touched it before, because this was a person... they'd kept thinking that maybe after things \"ended,\" the police would need to run DNA tests, confirm an identity, or something.","\"The living matter more,\" Jiang Cheng said. \"Better deal with it.\"","Everyone supported this.","It wasn't just about the flies. More importantly, sometimes when you accidentally let your gaze drift over, your heart would lurch.","Like some beautiful illusion had shattered. Uncomfortable.","The temporary committee called in the cleaning crews, along with Zhao Yi and the others, organized volunteers, and finally got rid of that pile of \"stuff\" in the small square that made everyone feel awful to look at.","Some people's shoulders relaxed, with a sigh: \"Even the air feels fresher.\"","The central courtyard's small square became a social hub, and the hot topic of conversation was, of course, the ongoing rescue efforts.","Many people saw Jiang Cheng around and couldn't help but crowd over to ask her what she thought, ask how long she thought it would take to reach the new district.","Song Jingshuo was talking to someone else nearby, but was half-listening to the conversation around Jiang Cheng, inwardly sneering.","They were treating Jiang Cheng like some kind of oracle.","A drink wouldn't last long, and besides, it was nearly noon — time for lunch, really.","But many people had woken up late, eaten breakfast late, so it wasn't quite lunch time yet. Jiang Cheng wasn't like that; she'd gotten up early: \"I'll go make lunch.\"","She made her escape.","Mo Li still didn't want to go back. Jiang Cheng found a quiet spot, put him down, and let him find somewhere to keep sunning himself.","It wasn't until evening, when she saw the sunlight outside slanting and dimming, that she came downstairs and called out a few times. Mo Li appeared quickly and hopped onto her shoulder as they headed home together.","The post Jiang Cheng had put up on the big forum had some replies now.","Very consistent — everyone saying they hadn't seen any animals infected or mutated yet. Some people got worried because of that: \"If animals can mutate, that'd be terrible.\"","Others replied that some animals had been bitten to death.","For example: \"A dog in our complex was so protective of its owner. It's thanks to him that his owner escaped. But the dog lost so much blood and died.\"","There were several cases of pet dogs protecting their owners, but none had mutated.","Looking at it that way, Mo Li was also an exception.","At eight in the evening, when the sky had gone completely dark, the follow-up report the whole city had been waiting for all day finally came:","\"A reporter from this station at the temporary emergency command site: the area from X Street to X Street, and X Road to X Road in Chaoyang District is now under solid control of the rescue forces.\"","\"X Garden, X Court, X Li, X Yuan... all residential complexes have been fully cleared.\"","\"The first batch of supplies has been delivered to residents.\"","Along with the crisp, standard broadcasting voice, footage from the front lines played on screen. Residents were jostling to the front of the military trucks, scrambling for supplies, while soldiers tried to maintain order.","In theory, this should have been encouraging news, but no one felt encouraged.","Because the TV also showed a map, with the controlled area shaded green.","That small patch of green relative to the entire city of S City? It was just too small.","Inside the Buyduoduo supermarket, Brother Dong turned his head and said: \"Get a map over here!\"","Someone immediately ran to the books-and-stationery aisle and brought back a map.","Brother Dong unfolded the map, circled the controlled zone according to the broadcast, then spread his hand and measured with the width of his thumb.","Just like Jiang Cheng had said — divide the distance, and you could roughly estimate.","The estimate was despairing.","Someone looked ready to cry: \"That's not half a month of waiting...?\"","Brother Dong stared at the map for a long time, then cursed: \"Damn it.\""]},{"number":45,"title":"Chapter 45","paragraphs":["The atmosphere in the Youth Apartment was oppressive too.","During the day, people had been relaxing with sodas and chatting, and the zombie remains in the courtyard had been cleaned up, giving things a fresh start.","But as soon as the evening news broadcast came on—after a whole day of rescue efforts, only a tiny patch on the map of S City had been lit up.","Reality set in right away.","Most people didn't have maps on hand. Many found themselves standing in front of the TV, tracing their fingers over the map to estimate their progress.","Once they finished their estimates, they all fell silent.","Just then, the speakers in the hallway crackled to life: [Testing, testing, testing? Can everyone hear me?]","There was also the sound of walkie-talkie chatter: [Can you guys hear this over there? Oh, you all can? Great.]","Then: [Alright.]","After that, the microphone clearly changed hands, and Jiang Cheng's voice came through: [Good evening, everyone.]","The speakers were in the corridors, and lots of people had their doors open, leaning against the doorframes or crouching in the hallways to listen more clearly.","Jiang Cheng's voice rang out across all six buildings in the complex: [You've all seen the news. It's not looking good.]","[It's even worse than I expected.]","[Given the current situation, our chances of going out as a group are pretty slim. With the government already launching rescue operations, staying put and waiting is the safer option.]","[After this broadcast, I want everyone to take stock of your supplies, especially food. The buy-more store has been completely cleaned out by both of our complexes. They basically have nothing edible left over there.]","[This means our original plan for food rationing may have been too optimistic. And now, whatever you have on hand needs to last until rescue arrives.]","[First, take a count. Then plan your daily consumption. I'd suggest setting up a reasonable diet schedule.]","[Based on feedback from Zhao Yi, we're still finding a lot of kitchen waste in the trash collected the past two days. I strongly urge everyone to stop doing that.]","[The situation has changed. I recommend changing your old eating habits and treasuring the food we have.]","[Keep in mind—many of our neighbors are going hungry.]","[Jixiang Jiayuan has already had a violent incident. In extreme situations, once something like that starts, it can spread as supplies run out.]","[Apart from eliminating food waste, the interim committee will also hold a meeting tomorrow to discuss security issues in the complex.]","[Until national rescue and supplies arrive,]","[I hope everyone can take care of themselves.]","[The interim committee will also do its best to maintain order.]","[Good night.]","The broadcast went silent.","In the corridors, people looked at each other. No one was in a cheerful mood—brows were furrowed.","Several sighs rang out at once.","One by one, everyone returned to their rooms to recount their remaining food, calculate exactly how much they needed per day, and figure out how many days their stockpiles would last.","At the property management center, Gao Yuxuan was a bit nervous. He asked Jiang Cheng, \"Are we going to have a famine?\"","\"We shouldn't. Our food supply is still relatively plentiful. We should be able to make it safely until the rescue troops arrive,\" Jiang Cheng replied. \"But it's better to keep some pressure on everyone. Zhao Yi said that this morning, they found a failed baked cake in the trash.\"","The cake hadn't risen—it had collapsed, so it was thrown away.","That's probably how things used to be.","But this isn't how things used to be.","Hearing that, Gao Yuxuan relaxed.","Jiang Cheng patted the microphone. \"This thing is really useful.\"","In the current situation, having a broadcast system that can reach every household in the complex was far better than making phone calls or sending out group notifications.","Jiang Cheng complimented without reservation: \"You and Zhao Yi and the rest of you—you've been a huge help.\"","When she praised someone, her dark, bright eyes looked straight at them, carrying full appreciation and genuine sincerity.","Gao Yuxuan happily rubbed the back of his neck and said, \"It's just what we're trained for—nothing special.\"","Jiang Cheng gave a small smile.","If Song Jingshuo, the finance guy, was the face of the elite type, then Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan were the classic hands-on tech nerds.","Li Jiangbing, the personal trainer, was your obvious social networker.","And then there was someone like Su Yu—a girl a bit kind, a bit brave.","Jiang Cheng found that she really enjoyed observing these people. Even the cleaning lady with the surname Liu, whom she had expelled from the complex.","Interesting. Every single person was interesting. And putting them all together and watching them interact was even more interesting.","Just as Jiang Cheng had said, the residents of the Youth Apartment didn't actually face an immediate food shortage, at least not yet.","Jiang Cheng had already inventoried her own stash. The most important thing was rice—the staple food.","She originally had one and a half bags at home, each 5 kg.","On the first trip to the buy-more store on Sunday, she had a backpack and a rolling cart. Her carrying capacity was very limited, so she only brought back three bags of rice.","But on the second trip on Monday, she grabbed a shopping cart, and her carrying capacity doubled. She snagged five bags of rice.","Now she had a bit more than nine bags of rice in total.","She didn't have a big appetite. With side dishes, she consumed only about 300-350 grams per day. In theory, one bag of rice would last her half a month.","But now with fewer side dishes—no fresh vegetables at all, just canned goods, jerky, salted eggs, meat sauce, and pickles—her rice consumption had gone up slightly.","Even so, she could still last at least three months.","But not everyone was like her.","Despite her repeated emphasis on prioritizing staples and canned goods when raiding the supermarket, and despite the limited carrying capacity, there were still people whose carts contained snacks like chips and preserved plums.","Also, men eat more than women. Jiang Cheng couldn't estimate how long each person's hoard would last—they'd have to do the math themselves.","But because there had been two opportunities to stock up, the Youth Apartment as a whole shouldn't face a food crisis before rescue arrived.","Even Mo Li wasn't short on food.","On both shopping trips, Jiang Cheng had gritted her teeth and sacrificed some carrying capacity to bring back cat food for Mo Li.","Now, Mo Li's body had mysteriously evolved to the point where, during the day, just basking in the sun meant she didn't need to eat.","Mo Li only ate one meal before bed at night, and not much at that—like the small appetite of a tiny ordinary kitten. With two bags of cat food plus the supply already at home, at this rate, Mo Li could easily last several months.","With food in hand, the heart doesn't panic.","Jiang Cheng posted in the group: [Let's meet up tomorrow for a meeting. Where's there a closed-off space in the complex we can use?]","The earlier meeting in the plaza had been crowded with residents watching and listening, even butting in.","Some topics shouldn't be directly deliberated by the residents. They should first reach a consensus within the interim committee, then announce the decision publicly. So Jiang Cheng wanted an enclosed space.","In the end, Song Jingshuo said: [Come to my place. My unit is a bit bigger.]","He gave his building and unit number.","Turned out he lived in the duplex unit of Building 4.","Most of the Youth Apartment comprised small single-person units, ranging from about 30 to 50 square meters, with 30 and 40 square meters being the most common.","Jiang Cheng's place was a 40-square-meter studio.","From the perspective of the house, it was small.","But for a single person living alone, it had a living room, a kitchen, a bathroom, and a bedroom—every function covered, more than enough.","The only unit with a bit more space was in Building 4, the one Song Jingshuo had bought. It was 60 square meters, spread over two floors.","[Okay.] Jiang Cheng arranged it. [10 a.m. tomorrow.]","She could wake up early, of course, and so could Song Jingshuo. But others might not. There was no need to drag people out of bed at the crack of dawn and make their lives miserable—it wasn't a workday.","Keeping order and maintaining everyone's mental state over the coming days was exactly what Jiang Cheng planned to discuss with the neighborhood committee tomorrow.","Finding a closed space to meet was about coordinating with the committee before facing the residents.","So, waiting at the clubhouse gym on Thursday morning was about coordinating with Song Jingshuo before facing the committee.","Song Jingshuo was excellent at communication and organization—a highly charismatic figure.","If it weren't for Jiang Cheng, an outsider who had transmigrated here, he would have been the soul of the Youth Apartment neighborhood committee.","But now, even he agreed that the soul of that committee was Jiang Cheng.","Jiang Cheng had guessed that a disciplined person like Song Jingshuo would definitely hit the gym in the morning. There was nowhere else to go, nothing else to do.","Someone like him wouldn't let himself sink into listlessness. The more he saw others' dark circles from staying up late and waking late, the more disciplined he became.","Sure enough, Song Jingshuo appeared in the gym, draped in the morning light.","\"Jingshuo,\" Jiang Cheng called out.","It wasn't the first time she'd called him by just his given name. Whenever she did, it meant she needed something from him.","Song Jingshuo paused, then let out a sigh.","Jiang Cheng: \"...\"","Song Jingshuo draped the towel around his neck and walked over to her: \"Didn't you say that communicating with me doesn't require any tricks?\"","Jiang Cheng smiled, her eyes curving into crescents.","Sunlight streamed through the floor-to-ceiling glass, falling on her shoulders. Her hair was dark and glossy.","Song Jingshuo had no fight left in him: \"Go ahead. Just say it straight.\"","\"Rescue won't arrive for half a month,\" Jiang Cheng said. \"Several thousand people are going to be locked inside this compound for half a month.\"","Song Jingshuo's expression turned grim.","He said, \"I was thinking about this all night last night.\"","Anyone who had ever managed people understood: wherever there are people, there is trouble. Where public order is weak, crime breeds.","Several thousand able-bodied young people locked in one compound with nothing to do—mostly men, at that.","Most people wouldn't even think about this, but Song Jingshuo had stayed up until the early hours mulling it over.","Of course, that was also because he was a core member of the neighborhood committee. His responsibility demanded he think more deeply than others.","She started the thought, and Song Jingshuo immediately got it.","He said, \"Don't worry. You and I—we'll stay in lockstep.\"","His tone was firm.","Seeing Jiang Cheng already waiting here in the morning to discuss this with him was beyond reassuring. In times like these, having a reliable partner was more comforting than anything else.","\"You, me,\" he said. \"And Jiangbing. The three of us have to stay on the same page.\"","Truly on the same wavelength—Jiang Cheng didn't even need to waste a single extra sentence.","This was exactly what she had wanted to hear from him.","\"Jiangbing's no problem,\" she said. She raised her hand to her chest, thumb up, chin tilted. \"Come on, let's hit the treadmill.\"","At 10 a.m., the neighborhood committee gathered at Song Jingshuo's place.","His home was indeed the largest unit in the Youth Apartment—60 square meters on a single floor. But the committee now had quite a few members, and the place was packed.","The sofa and coffee table were full, and since they were all young people, they weren't shy about it—some just sat right on the floor.","\"The government's announcements never waste a word,\" Jiang Cheng said from her seat on the dining table, higher than everyone else. \"'Survival order'—the moment I heard those two words, my heart skipped a beat.\"","\"And before that, there's 'rebuilding.'\""]},{"number":46,"title":"Chapter 46","paragraphs":["Text released by the government must be read word by word, every single character picked apart.","A lot of people don’t understand that.","Someone in the interim committee did, and nodded.","“Rebuilding” placed in an announcement like that definitely isn’t filler.","“The information we’ve gathered over the past few days has only come from a few forums. All we know is that people were beaten to death over in Jixiang Jiayuan.”","“The government has far more information than what we’ve seen.”","“City surveillance cameras are everywhere.”","“And the emergency hotline is back up.”","The municipal government could essentially monitor the whole city. They’d seen and knew far more.","“The staff at Mai Duoduo, mostly shelf-stockers, do heavy lifting all day. Whatever their height, they’ve got plenty of strength.”","“If that weren’t the case, they’d have walked away with more than just injuries.”","“Most likely, their hoarded food is as good as gone.”","Jiang Cheng paused.","A wave of murmurs swept through the room. Everyone had experienced that chaotic frenzy of Monday morning, fighting alongside the people from Jixiang Jiayuan to grab supplies at Mai Duoduo. They could all vividly recall that sense of losing control.","Song Jingshuo leaned against the cabinet with his arms crossed, scanning the sea of heads, then glanced at Jiang Cheng.","Jiang Cheng let them whisper among themselves, letting the tension properly ferment.","Once it quieted down, she spoke again: “Over the past few days, the interim committee has done an excellent job—that’s plain for every homeowner to see. Of course, we’ve also had some help from the contrast with our neighbors.”","That last line drew a few laughs, a few “tch” sounds. But everyone agreed with her point.","“Until government rescue reaches our new district, until life returns to normal, the interim committee will not disband.” Jiang Cheng asked, “For now, our compound doesn’t have a food crisis. Did everyone take stock yesterday? Half a month, a month—is that enough?”","Everyone nodded in turn: “Yeah, enough.”","“No problem.”","“We can hold out.”","That Monday trip, with everyone pushing a shopping cart, had doubled their carrying capacity—it had really solved a huge problem. That’s why they could feel so secure, why they could sit here and laugh.","“Then the food topic can be skipped,” Jiang Cheng said. “The main topic I want to discuss with everyone today is—order.”","“Split into two parts: internal and external.”","“Internally, the interim committee must ensure that everyone in the compound abides by the law.”","Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan were both there. They’d been part of the interim committee from the start—the first group to head downstairs and fight the zombies. They just hadn’t stood out in the crowd until they’d stepped up on Tuesday and started leaving an impression.","The homebodies, upon hearing this, exchanged glances and saw a flicker of surprise and confusion in each other’s eyes. Was there really someone who wouldn’t obey the law?","“I’m not saying something is definitely going to happen,” Jiang Cheng said. “But I want everyone to understand: even if the police can’t come out right now, even if the government is in trouble, the law is still the foundation of everyone’s safety. Only when every person follows the law can we build an environment where everyone can live in peace.”","“So until government rescue arrives, until the national system recovers, any illegal act by anyone in this compound—the interim committee will step in without hesitation to stop it, manage it, and when necessary, punish it.”","The girl sat on the dining table and spoke at length.","Her voice wasn’t particularly loud or forceful, but every word was clear to everyone.","When she said “punish,” no one laughed. Everyone remembered how she’d fired and expelled a cleaner. Under the current circumstances, expulsion was essentially murder.","Many had been present at the time, and almost no one had objected. Because everyone stood on the same side as she did—the homeowners’ side. From that standpoint, that cleaner had been harming all their interests. And if he’d succeeded, if the rest of the staff—other cleaners, security guards, maintenance workers—had all gone on strike, the damage to the homeowners would have been even worse.","And so, everyone had supported that murder.","Now, they all understood her reasoning. They just couldn’t help secretly wondering what methods she’d use if such a situation ever arose.","...","They couldn’t imagine it.","But they supported it.","“Anyone opposed?” Jiang Cheng said. “If there are any opinions or suggestions, now’s the time to speak up. We’re meeting here today precisely to make this clear.”","She said, “We need to get our own people on the same page first.”","“Our own people”—those words made everyone in the room feel good. But no one voluntarily jumped in to give their opinion.","Song Jingshuo’s gaze swept across, and he called out: “Zhao Yi, what’s your take?”","The homebody was startled, stammered for a second, then said, “No, no objection. Whatever Jiang Cheng said, I agree.”","Jiang Cheng smiled and asked, “And Yuxuan?”","Gao Yuxuan quickly said, “Agree.”","Jiang Cheng’s gaze continued sweeping around, and everyone she looked at said, “No objection,” “Agree.”","That topic was passed.","Jiang Cheng: “Next, the external side. I think we need to strengthen the compound’s defenses. My prediction is that in the days ahead, we might get targeted.”","Everyone was sitting on the floor—some cross-legged, some hugging their knees—and when they heard that, they all unconsciously craned their necks, straightened their backs, and perked up their ears.","“Right now, there’s no resupply,” Jiang Cheng said. “Jixiang Jiayuan is still okay—they followed us on that supply run. The other neighboring compounds are probably nearing the end of their resources.”","“Did anyone check their homeowners’ forums this morning? It wasn’t just Shanshui Yayuan—Yujing Xiangyuan, Deqingli, and Lekang Jiayuan all went out on their own volition over the past couple of days.”","Someone couldn’t help but say, “Volition? They’ve run out of food. They finally decided to leave the house and try their luck.”","“They’re even worse off than Jixiang Jiayuan.”","“In the vicinity, it’s only us and Jixiang Jiayuan. The rest can’t manage.”","But Jiang Cheng had met with Brother Dong and his crew from Mai Duoduo yesterday—only people from Yujing Xiangyuan and Deqingli had made it to Mai Duoduo.","People guessed: “Must be because of the restaurant street.”","Jiang Cheng nodded. “I think so too. They probably couldn’t get past it.”","The other two compounds had to cross a strip of restaurants and nightlife to reach Mai Duoduo. That street wasn’t just restaurants—there were bars and coffee shops too.","Remember, the zombie virus broke out on a Saturday night, and it was summer.","Who knows how many people were on that street at that time of night. A decently popular restaurant would have a waitlist of dozens, even over a hundred people.","“Jesus.” Someone pictured it and involuntarily rubbed their arms, feeling the hairs stand on end.","“But even for Jixiang Jiayuan, they didn’t get nearly as many supplies from that run as we did,” Jiang Cheng said. “And their average household size is bigger than ours. Also, take Yujing Xiangyuan—if someone from there cuts through Jixiang Jiayuan, they could reach us.”","“What’s happening in our compound isn’t just visible on our forum—people on the Jixiang Jiayuan forum are talking about it too. All anyone has to do is look, and they’d see that Youth Apartment has plenty of supplies.”","\"I'm worried that under the current circumstances, some people who are starving might set their sights on us and take the risk.\"","The atmosphere in the room suddenly turned serious.","Everyone agreed with Jiang Cheng's concern: \"Could happen, it really could.\"","Jiang Cheng threw the question to the group: \"Let's discuss it.\"","When it came to making decisions, everyone tried to avoid eye contact. But when it came to concrete measures at a practical level, people got eager and lively.","The room buzzed with heated discussion.","Jiang Cheng took his own cup to the kitchen to get some water. Song Jingshuo's kitchen had a water purifier with direct drinking water, which was very convenient.","The interim committee currently only had Jiang Cheng and Su Yu—everyone else was male.","Although the first group to go downstairs and kill zombies were all men, later on, brave women like Su Yu gradually joined in as well. But the women were at a disadvantage because their awareness of power was too weak. Years of social conditioning had not given them a strong sense of initiative to actively seize and wield power.","So when the interim committee was formed, they only watched from the sidelines.","In the end, only Su Yu got pulled in by Jiang Cheng because she lived in the same building as him.","With mostly men, they were very enthusiastic about getting things done, and quickly came up with many useful suggestions.","At the beginning of the year, because of theft incidents, the community's perimeter fences had been equipped with barbed wire mesh, but the east and west gates did not have it. It needed to be installed.","That stuff was priced by the meter, and however much had been installed was all there was—there was no leftover.","But it wasn't a problem for the engineering-minded men. The tech and engineering guys especially offered a lot of feasible suggestions.","The limitation was what materials were available in the property management warehouse.","Jiang Cheng asked the man who had spoken most often and most enthusiastically: \"What's your name?\"","\"Cui Haiyang.\"","Cui Haiyang—Li Jiangbing knew him. He was the one who had done the main cutting on that batch of steel pipes.","The people on the interim committee, strangers who didn't know each other at first, were gradually becoming familiar, even close.","\"Good. Cui Haiyang.\" Jiang Cheng made the call. \"You're in charge of this.\"","\"Count on it.\"","Then they moved on to the issue of the youth apartment building's windows that didn't have security bars—the first and second floors were relatively more dangerous, and they needed to figure out how to prevent break-ins.","Master Luo gave a very practical suggestion: \"What about rat glue?\"","The property management had a batch of rat glue, and because it would be used long-term, they had stockpiled quite a lot. And it came in large sheets that needed to be cut to size.","\"Put it under the windows. That glue is strong—one step and both feet get stuck.\"","That way, an intruder couldn't stand properly and would basically end up falling flat on their face.","Others suggested making tripwire-style traps and similar small tricks.","Then the topic started to wander, went off the rails, drifted further and further, and the chatter grew even more animated.","\"Alright, alright. We'll open a dedicated thread later, and everyone can write up their suggestions and the specific methods for making them.\" Jiang Cheng had to knock on the table to pull the conversation back.","Maintaining order for survival—both internally and externally—was the main agenda item for today's meeting. Once those two issues were discussed, they moved on to other small, miscellaneous matters.","The clubhouse had been holding garbage since Tuesday, and although Zhao Yi and his team had taken various measures, under the limited conditions they couldn't completely get rid of the smell.","In fact, this morning Song Jingshuo and Jiang Cheng had already noticed that the odor was starting to drift into the gym.","Now that everyone was stuck at home, the gym was being used frequently—not just for workouts, but also for socializing.","Song Jingshuo suggested moving the exercise equipment out of the clubhouse. In the end, they decided to distribute the machines across the ground-floor lobbies of each building.","Things like that—small, trivial details.","There was also a bigger matter. Jiang Cheng said: \"The bodies on Jixiang West Street need to be dealt with. They're too close to us.\"","Jixiang West Street was the road sandwiched between the east gate of the youth apartment building and the west gate of Jixiang Jiayuan. Whenever they went to buy things from Duoduo, they'd exit through the east gate and take that road.","Jixiang Jiayuan was one of the earlier-built residential complexes in the new district, and the roads to the east and west of it were named after the community.","Jixiang West Street was right next to the youth apartment, and the bodies on that street were now badly decomposed.","Yesterday, when Jiang Cheng met with Brother Dong at the east gate, he saw the situation outside and felt it was necessary to clean it up.","Things like this required someone to bring them up—otherwise, most people would just see the problem, think it wasn't great, but wouldn't lift a finger to deal with it.","When humans live together in groups, someone has to step up and call the shots."]},{"number":47,"title":"Chapter 47","paragraphs":["But the youth apartment couldn't just go over there alone as unpaid labor—why would they? This street was shared by both residential complexes. And by now, everyone was already pretty fed up with Jixiang Jiayuan.","\"Either we all suffer together.\"","\"Or both complexes go out and do the work together.\"","\"Exactly!\"","That was everyone's opinion, remarkably unified.","The meeting was lively and ran until past one in the afternoon, when stomachs finally started grumbling and they called it adjourned.","A satisfying session, all things considered.","Many people took on tasks—small, trivial things, but having something to do gave a sense of purpose.","Some couldn't be bothered to wait for the elevator and hurried down the stairwell instead, eager to rope people into helping.","Li Jiangbing took charge of coordinating with Jixiang Jiayuan. He picked a few people, and none of them hesitated—they agreed on the spot and went with him to handle the matter.","Jiang Cheng took all of this in.","As they say, wherever there are people, there are factions. In just five or six days, several small cliques had quietly formed among the dozens of residents.","The interim committee sprang into action with enthusiasm.","For anything needing manpower or ideas, they'd post threads in the forum recruiting volunteers or brainstorming.","After lunch, many people went downstairs for a stroll and saw a crowd gathered at the east gate, discussing how to reinforce the security measures, talking a mile a minute.","Li Jiangbing replied that afternoon about the communication with Jixiang Jiayuan: \"It's settled—we'll do it together tomorrow morning.\"","Then he added: \"Old Zhou looks terrifyingly thin.\"","Friday morning, the interim committee organized a crew to clean up Jixiang West Street. When they met the Jixiang Jiayuan group again, Jiang Cheng and Song Jingshuo saw Zhou Wang—and despite Li Jiangbing's warning, they were still taken aback.","It had only been a few days, and he looked gaunt—downright skeletal.","He seemed to have aged more than ten years overnight.","When he spoke, his demeanor had changed drastically too.","Before, he'd come across as a slick, worldly middle-aged man—not like the hot-blooded young guys in the youth apartment who were willing to take responsibility. He'd had a way of wanting both power and deniability, talking in vague circles, laughing things off.","Now, when he opened his mouth, he was much harder. The people from Jixiang Jiayuan seemed more organized and obedient than they'd been a few days prior.","When he spoke, people listened.","Jiang Cheng and Song Jingshuo exchanged a glance.","There were dark circles under Zhou Wang's eyes. Even though no one had to go to work now—everyone could sleep until they naturally woke—he'd developed bags under his eyes.","Song Jingshuo said, \"Brother Zhou, you need to take care of yourself.\"","Zhou Wang nodded, then looked at them.","The girl was young and pretty; the young man was tall and handsome. Li Jiangbing, who'd come to discuss things with him yesterday afternoon, wasn't even thirty, a bit rough around the edges—what you'd call street-smart—but he was competent too.","These young people had completely taken charge of a community of several thousand people, keeping it running in good order.","His eyes were bloodshot, a little cloudy, as he stared at them.","\"Little Jiang,\" he said. \"You guys are impressive.\"","Unlike him—he couldn't sleep, no matter what.","Jiang Cheng asked, \"What else happened?\"","Zhou Wang could tell right away they'd already heard about the earlier incident where someone had been beaten to death. It was those people's fault for posting all over the forum.","He wasn't too good with the internet; he'd reacted too slowly.","He'd actually been trying to keep all these things under wraps, not let too many people know.","But Jiang Cheng and her group were different. These young people had been showing goodwill from the very start and had genuinely helped Jixiang Jiayuan.","If they hadn't brought people to help that Monday, who knew how many more might have died.","Besides, Zhou Wang had been losing sleep night after night, in real agony, and desperately wanted someone to understand him.","Not just anyone—it had to be someone in the same position as him. Otherwise, they couldn't grasp the pressure he was under.","The ones who could empathize with him most were the people right in front of him.","The middle-aged man looked off toward the street corner in the distance, seeming lost for a moment, then turned back and said, \"A lot of things.\"","\"At times like this, you see who people really are—who's decent and who's a bastard.\"","\"There are scumbags everywhere.\"","Yesterday—just yesterday—a young mother had jumped off a building with her baby in her arms.","She'd been part of a family of four. Her mother-in-law and father had both turned one after another, and she'd hidden in the bedroom with her child, surviving on baby formula. Only when Jixiang Jiayuan organized a sweep of the buildings did they discover her—they broke down the door and killed the two zombies in her home.","But she'd missed the group supermarket run, and her household supplies were completely exhausted.","She had no choice but to ask neighbors for help.","But everyone had witnessed the chaos and disorder at Pinduoduo Supermarket—they all understood that order had already collapsed to some degree. No one knew what was coming next. People were clinging tight to their own supplies, and no one was willing to lend a hand.","Finally, a male neighbor said he was willing to help her, but in return, he made inappropriate demands of the young mother.","She was shocked, furious, and terrified. She refused in panic, and of course, received no help after that.","That was Tuesday.","She rummaged through her home for food, scraping by on a few snacks. Her baby only had half a can of formula left.","Tuesday afternoon, the TV and radio announced that the government had begun rescue efforts, and she began to hope.","Wednesday night, the news broadcast the progress of the rescue.","She thought it over all night, wrote a suicide note, and at dawn on Thursday, jumped with her child.","Jiang Cheng and Song Jingshuo both fell silent.","Jiang Cheng said, \"That wasn't in the forum.\"","Zhou Wang: \"I couldn't let them talk nonsense. I had Little Huang—oh, Old Huang's son, remember him?\"","He looked around, then pointed him out to Jiang Cheng and the others: \"He's over there.\"","Jiang Cheng and Song Jingshuo both turned to look, and sure enough, they saw the teenage boy who'd earlier held back tears while helping the adults register people.","\"I've got him following me now. Old Huang's gone—it's just him and his mother left now,\" Zhou Wang said. \"The kid knows his way around the internet. I put him in charge of the forum. He's the 'moderator' now.\"","Their interaction with Old Huang had been brief, but the impression lingered. Old Huang was older, more commanding, with more presence than Zhou Wang. If he'd survived, he'd have been the one leading Jixiang Jiayuan.","Even Zhou Wang said, \"If Old Huang were still here...\"","Then maybe he wouldn't be lying awake every night—at least there'd be someone sharing the burden.","The young mother's suicide was just one of the many horrible things that had happened in the past few days. It wasn't the only thing he'd had to deal with.","He was exhausted, heart and soul. His hair was falling out, he couldn't sleep—but he'd also grown colder, harder.","Because right now, being smooth and tactful didn't solve a damned thing.","What was happening in Jixiang Jiayuan was exactly the kind of situation Jiang Cheng had discussed with Song Jingshuo beforehand—the thing they absolutely had to prevent from happening in the youth apartment.","That was disorder.","When the government talked about rebuilding \"survival order,\" those people in power saw things more clearly than anyone—they knew better what was happening and what was about to happen.","Song Jingshuo expected her to ask about the male neighbor.","He expected that a girl would naturally feel empathy for another woman—like how Su Yu from Building Two had been brought into the interim committee by her.","A girl like her—decisive, commanding, with real leadership ability—might well want to avenge the young mother, or at least teach that male neighbor a lesson.","But Jiang Cheng just nodded and said, \"Don't overthink it. We did everything we could,\" and that was the end of that topic.","Song Jingshuo wondered if he really was overthinking it.","Jixiang West Street had been cleared.","The rotting, stinking corpses, the round heads, the eyeballs rolling on the ground—all of it was piled up and burned.","Jiang Cheng used this moment to do something she had wanted to do for a while: block off the road.","Her idea was to use the cars parked along Jixiang West Street to seal off both ends of the street. That way, a vacuum-secure zone would form between the west gate of Jixiang Jiayuan and the east gate of the Youth Apartment.","Even if residents from either complex walked out of their gates and onto the street by themselves, they would be basically safe.","In the past, Zhou Wang would definitely have said things like \"Is this appropriate?\" or \"What if the car owners come after us?\"—all that shirking of responsibility. But now, the moment Jiang Cheng proposed it, he nodded in agreement.","Accountability can only be pursued against the living.","First, you have to stay alive.","The fact that people from both complexes worked together on this not only made it easy but also soothed the resentment on the Youth Apartment side.","Nobody likes being taken advantage of by their neighbors all the time. The neighbors ought to step up and do their part too.","They picked cars that were boxy vans or taller SUVs.","The able-bodied men chanted in unison as they lifted the fronts of the cars and pulled them out from the curbside. At first, they tried not to damage other people's vehicles, but later they got frustrated and just smashed the windows, released the handbrakes, and steered while pushing—much easier that way.","Whatever private property—none of it mattered much anymore.","Many hands make light work. The closed-off street Jiang Cheng wanted was completed quickly.","From a certain angle, this could be seen as connecting the Youth Apartment and Jixiang Jiayuan together.","What Jiang Cheng really wanted was to expand the safe zone.","The most basic safe zone was, of course, the Youth Apartment itself. If something happened, they would just lock the gates tight and defend to the death.","No people or zombies getting in.","But on top of that, the bigger the safe zone, the better.","Sure enough, once both ends of Jixiang West Street were sealed off, everyone felt a sense of expanded space.","The confined, suffocating feeling of being trapped inside the complex lightened considerably.","Zhou Wang also consulted Jiang Cheng on other matters.","His task for Little Huang was to check the resident forum boards of nearby complexes every day, with special attention to the Youth Apartment, and report anything noteworthy to him promptly.","Ever since the Youth Apartment had its broadcast system set up, communication on many matters had become much more convenient. Many specific arrangements were made through the group chats.","So there wasn't much discussion on the forums anymore.","But Su Yu's post about centralized disposal of recyclable waste was published before Gao Yuxuan had gotten the broadcast system up and running.","Little Huang saw it and reported it to Zhou Wang.","That was on Tuesday, and now it was already Friday. The garbage problem at Jixiang Jiayuan had become serious.","Jiang Cheng asked, \"What about your property management people?\"","It was bad. They weren't as lucky as the Youth Apartment—no one in the management dorm had turned.","Someone in the Jixiang Jiayuan management dorm had mutated, followed by second-generation zombies from later injuries. Almost all the property management staff who had been in the complex at the time were wiped out, and the few who survived weren't of much use.","Zhou Wang asked in detail how the Youth Apartment handled their garbage.","But Jixiang Jiayuan didn't have a clubhouse or a swimming pool. In the past, residents of their complex used to come to the Youth Apartment's clubhouse to swim.","Zhou Wang said, \"Could our complex's garbage also...\"","Jiang Cheng flat out refused: \"No.\"","According to Zhao Yi's calculations, the swimming pool's storage space could handle their garbage until rescue arrived—with room to spare.","But it certainly couldn't support two communities.","There was no way Jiang Cheng would agree to that.","One good thing about Zhou Wang was that he understood rejection and didn't push it. He changed his tune: \"Then could you spare the environmental engineering person to come help us? Have him consult for our complex too.\"","That wasn't out of the question.","Jiang Cheng had always kept a close eye on Jixiang Jiayuan precisely because it was right next to the Youth Apartment. Anything that happened there would inevitably affect her complex.","If the garbage wasn't dealt with, flies and mosquitoes would inevitably breed and spread.","Jiang Cheng turned to Song Jingshuo and asked, \"If we send Zhao Yi and the others over to help, what would be a fair price to charge?\"","Song Jingshuo's mouth twitched.","So now she remembers him?","Jiang Cheng smiled.","Go on, finance guy! Go haggle down to the last penny!"]},{"number":48,"title":"Chapter 48","paragraphs":["City S’s Emergency Management Command was set up in the City Operations Management Center.","It had a city surveillance hall connected to every public camera in City S, with coverage that could span nearly every street in the city.","The monitoring systems of both the police command center and the traffic command center were sub-modules of this system.","The department ran around the clock; even at night, dozens of staff were on duty.","That was exactly why, when the zombie virus broke out, it was practically wiped out.","Just as Jiang Cheng had said, when the zombie virus hit, any space where large numbers of people gathered at the same time became a disaster zone.","Government forces had run into serious trouble when they tried to retake the building — many of the zombies inside were fast, agile second-generation variants.","But no matter the cost, after paying a heavy price, the government managed to reclaim control of the building and clear out every last zombie inside, turning it into City S’s Emergency Management Command Base.","Now, presiding over the situation here was a deputy mayor surnamed Zheng.","He had originally been the fourth-ranking deputy mayor in charge of education, but all of those ranked above him had been confirmed dead on the night the zombie virus broke out. So now, Zheng was the one holding things together in City S.","Things were not looking good.","The rescue forces were advancing far slower than expected.","Because of how the virus spread, an area had to be completely cleared of zombies before it could be declared a green zone. That made rapid progress impossible.","But City S was a metropolis of over ten million people.","Vice Mayor Zheng took off his glasses, pinched the bridge of his nose, and felt utterly exhausted.","Every police officer who could be assembled in the city was already here.","Multiple fires had broken out across the city, and the firefighting units simply couldn’t keep up. Too many firefighters had been lost on Sunday and Monday.","The major hospitals had all fallen; the footage on the monitors looked like something out of a horror movie.","University students were fighting desperately to save themselves — those young people were the nation’s future, and Vice Mayor Zheng could only watch as those kids died, got infected, and turned into second-generation zombies.","Residents whose homes had run out of food were braving the streets with kitchen knives in hand, only to be surrounded and torn apart by zombies.","All of this was playing out in real time, screen after screen.","Whoever came up with the word “zombie” had nailed it — too vivid, too apt.","But all officials, by unspoken agreement, never used that term. If the authorities themselves used it, the despair would be too much to bear.","To this day, officials still used the term “mutants” — first-generation mutants, infected mutants, also called original mutants, and second-generation mutants.","Vice Mayor Zheng’s fatigue wasn’t just physical; it was mental. The pressure he was under was immense.","The secretary beside him — more accurately, the temporary secretary — well, the same could be said for most people working in the command center; nearly every title had the prefix “temporary” attached to it.","Everyone was just filling in because the person before them had died, thrust into the role under emergency orders.","The secretary reported the latest updates from several parties, then finished with one final item:","“Two residential communities in the new development district — Youth Apartments and Lucky Family Garden — their residents cleared out nearby mutants on their own and barricaded the roads together. The two communities have now merged into a single green zone.”","Amid the flood of gloom, one piece of good news. Even Vice Mayor Zheng felt a jolt of energy. He put his glasses back on. “Really? Let me see.”","The dispatch hall had a full wall of dozens of screens.","An operator pulled up the surveillance footage from Lucky West Street this morning.","A group of people gathered behind Vice Mayor Zheng, all watching.","“Looks like they’re cleaning up.”","“Seems they’d already cleared the zombies off the street before this. Look at the corpses — they’re already decomposing.”","“Looks like residents from both communities are working together.”","“Someone must have organized this. Without a leader, there’s no way they could cooperate like this.”","“There — those few people right there.”","The operator zoomed in on the spot someone had pointed out.","While everyone else was working, a handful of people stood there talking, and no one around them looked resentful or bothered.","Clearly, those were the organizers, the leaders of the two communities.","Judging by where they stood, the middle-aged man at the front of one group was clearly the head of Lucky Family Garden.","On the other side, Youth Apartments — everyone had heard of that project, marketed to young buyers, so it was easy to guess that side was a younger crowd.","And yet, standing at the very front, conversing with the middle-aged man from Lucky Family Garden, was a young woman. That surprised everyone.","No one suspected the girl was just standing there by coincidence.","Because everyone in that room was career government workers. People in the system were the most attuned to the meaning of seating arrangements and positioning.","One look told them all: she was the person in charge on the Youth Apartments side.","Even her stance and bearing carried an air of authority.","That was confusing. Such an aura was usually cultivated over years of holding power in officialdom or the business world — not something most young people could have.","Unless, of course, she was one of those second-generation rich kids born into privilege, raised from birth with a status above others — that too could produce such a presence.","But then, why would someone like that be living in Youth Apartments? That project targeted young middle-class professionals.","“Organizational ability. Decisiveness. Courage. Brains.” Vice Mayor Zheng sighed. “If only more communities were like this.”","But as soon as he said it, he fell silent.","Because across that entire wall of screens, what filled the view were more scenes of residents being chased down by zombies, tackled, and torn apart in the streets; residents on balconies, crying and cursing through tears; people in convenience stores with shattered glass doors, grappling and fighting over supplies.","All screens were muted by default. But those silent images, spreading from one screen to the next across the vast, towering wall, only made the heaviness worse.","Back at Youth Apartments, Jiang Cheng and the others, of course, had no idea someone was watching them through the surveillance cameras.","Anyway, bargaining was left to the Finance Guy — someone who clearly would never let himself take a loss — and he didn’t let Jiang Cheng down. He managed to score half a bag of rice as payment for the technie.","Zhao Yi was called over, and Jiang Cheng gave him a quick briefing.","Zhao Yi had no objections. He agreed with Jiang Cheng’s philosophy: in terms of both safety and sanitation, two communities that close together couldn’t stay isolated. Helping the neighbors was helping themselves.","Song Jingshuo, afraid Zhao Yi was too honest to ask for what he’d earned, deliberately spelled out the payment in front of Zhou Wang, then said cheerfully, “If it’s too heavy, just have Jiangbing go over and carry it back for you.”","Zhao Yi: “I can carry it myself.”","“Then that works.” Song Jingshuo patted him lightly on the shoulder.","Song Jingshuo was good with people — everyone liked him. But for some reason, Zhao Yi had always found him irritating.","After dinner, Zhao Yi went over, and by evening, he was back in the neighborhood.","The courtyard was dotted with small clusters of people — the same people who used to hide in their rooms blasting the AC and playing games now cherished every chance to come downstairs and socialize with healthy, living people. They were all down in the cool evening air, chatting.","As soon as people saw Zhao Yi, many greeted him: \"You're back.\"","Zhao Yi wasn't used to suddenly being treated like a celebrity. But everyone really did know him now, and they genuinely appreciated his contributions to the community.","Someone else said to him: \"They're over by the gazebo.\"","\"Them\" of course meant Jiang Cheng and her core team.","Zhao Yi swung the sack onto his shoulder and hurried over. From a distance, he could see that group talking under the gazebo.","Jiang Cheng was the most conspicuous — she was the only girl among the core members, and her black cat was perched on her shoulder, giving her a very anime-like vibe.","Usually in anime, that kind of pocket-sized pet would transform into a giant war beast.","Ah, getting off track.","Zhao Yi shook off those random thoughts and went over to report to Jiang Cheng: \"I'm back.\"","\"Good work,\" Jiang Cheng said. \"How did it go over there? Everything sorted? Took you this long?\"","Speaking of which, Zhao Yi had a complaint: \"Don't even get me started.\"","Because his expertise matched the job, he'd gone in full of confidence, expecting it to be like at the Youth Apartment — everyone having their roles, working together actively, even brainstorming and coming up with creative ideas.","Instead, problems popped up right from the site selection stage.","Zhao Yi: \"They didn't have anything like a swimming pool, but they had sunken gardens, so I thought we'd just pick one.\"","\"Whichever one we picked, people from the nearby buildings would rush down and kick up a fuss, saying no, pick somewhere else.\"","\"A lot of them were old men and old ladies, I didn't dare touch them.\"","Everyone gave him sympathetic looks. Jiang Cheng said: \"Brother Zhou really had it rough.\"","Then she asked: \"So where did you end up picking?\"","Zhao Yi: \"We ended up in the underground parking garage. Transportation was a real pain. Those people also made a fuss about not letting us use the elevator to move the trash down there. We had to use the vehicle ramp.\"","Just hearing about it gave everyone a headache. Zhou Wang really was something. Even Song Jingshuo felt that if it had been him, he probably would've lost his temper — only someone who'd been worn down by the world, a middle-aged man with no rough edges left, could have that kind of patience.","Song Jingshuo glanced at the sack on Zhao Yi's shoulder: \"You got paid, right?\"","It was actually a flour sack.","Flour sacks like that were rarely seen at the Youth Apartment. The young people there would buy flour from the supermarket in small paper bags.","These big flour sacks were something only old folks would buy at the market.","The sack now contained rice.","Zhao Yi opened it for everyone to see, and they said: \"Why is it mixed? Is it a grain medley?\"","It looked like several different types of rice and grains mixed together, even some beans.","Zhao Yi had a lot of respect for Zhou Wang: \"It's 'hundred-family rice.'\"","Zhou Wang naturally couldn't pay this \"fee\" out of his own pocket. Food was such a sensitive topic these days; no matter what, he couldn't be the one to take that hit himself.","A loudspeaker had been set up under each residential building, announcing the trash disposal matter and then declaring: \"The compensation for the Youth Apartment staff is to be shared by all property owners, per household.\"","He had people go door-to-door collecting from every building. Each household just contributed about a bowl's worth. Since it was spread out and each household's share was so small, no one had much to complain about, and they all gave.","But a few sneaky owners tried to cheat by offering beans, insisting: \"We only eat mixed grains in our house.\"","The collectors didn't bother arguing. It wasn't for themselves anyway — every household just needed to give a little.","In the end, they gathered half a sack of grain.","It was actually really heavy. Carrying it on the shoulder was easier than holding it in hand, so that's why he had it on his back.","It looked like something out of a famine scene — a refugee fleeing with clothes and food.","Song Jingshuo struggled to hold in a laugh.","Zhao Yi hated him even more for that.","He retied the flour sack, held it with one hand and supported it with the other, and offered it to Jiang Cheng: \"Should I hand this over to you?\"","Jiang Cheng: \"Why would you hand it to me? It's yours. You did the work, so you definitely get the reward.\"","\"Keep it,\" she said, then pulled out her phone to check the time, muttering as if to herself: \"The daily progress update should be broadcasting soon, right?\"","Song Jingshuo also raised his wrist to check the time.","Nowadays, phones had almost completely taken over. What young person still wore a watch?","Zhao Yi really hated that kind of show-off guy."]},{"number":49,"title":"Chapter 49","paragraphs":["At the Youth Apartment, a group of men were in high spirits, installing extra anti-theft measures over the main gate of the compound. The Youth Apartment had never encountered any outside intruders.","But on Friday night, someone slipped into Jixiang Jiayuan.","The Youth Apartment and Jixiang Jiayuan were the first to rush out of their buildings to clear out zombies, and they beat every other residential compound to emptying the Buyduo Supermarket.","Anyone who kept an eye on the owners' forums would know this—it wasn't a secret.","Especially since, later on, people from nearby compounds also charged out and made a dash for Buyduo Supermarket, only to find that all the food had been cleaned out, and they had to resentfully go elsewhere to scavenge for supplies.","Some of them died out there, never making it back to their compounds.","On Tuesday, employees from Buyduo Supermarket got into a clash with these people and were injured. On Wednesday, they pushed a few carts of drinks over to trade for medicine.","After they left, Brother Dong figured this couldn't go on.","Inside the supermarket there were a few small shops, including a photo studio. Brother Dong and his men smashed the glass, went in, found the camera, and took a whole bunch of photos. Then they called the studio manager. The manager listened to their situation, sighed heavily, and walked them through how to develop the film over the phone, and they printed out the photos.","After that, when people came running to Buyduo Supermarket looking for food, they saw the banner stretched across the entrance: \"All food has been cleared out. Look elsewhere!\"","And they posted many photos, all showing the interior of Buyduo Supermarket— empty shelves, an empty warehouse, and an empty cold storage room.","Some people refused to believe it and went in to check for themselves. It was exactly as shown. Those people could only leave in disappointment and stopped clashing with Brother Dong and the others.","But some got mouthy about it: \"Who told you to come so late? The Youth Apartment and Jixiang Jiayuan already grabbed everything. Go look for them.\"","This kind of talk eventually showed up on the forums of several other compounds, and plenty of people saw it.","Nearby, just about any shop that had any link to food—restaurants, convenience stores, small grocers—had been smashed open, and everything inside was empty.","Even unrelated stores, like a beauty salon, got broken into, and people combed through them, turning up the employees' personal snacks or some rice, flour, and cooking oil in the kitchen.","But the quantity was nowhere near enough to hold things together.","If people don't eat, they die, and no one wants to die, so they had to figure something out.","Friday night, after dark, someone snuck into Jixiang Jiayuan.","Why Jixiang Jiayuan? Everyone knew that the Youth Apartment people definitely had more supplies. But the Youth Apartment's gate was locked, the security booth was lit, and there was a guard on duty.","Jixiang Jiayuan's property management was gone by then—dead or scattered. Jixiang Jiayuan had no property management left at this point.","The gate was normally shut, but nobody was manning it. Unlike the Youth Apartment, there were no reinforced anti-theft measures on it either.","Jixiang Jiayuan was wide open. The two compounds were right next to each other, so when comparing them, of course one would pick Jixiang Jiayuan.","They chose the dead of night, when people were asleep.","But they weren't professional thieves, nowhere near that slick, and they still roused people.","In the middle of the night, a shrill scream of \"Thief! Catch the thief!\" rang out. It woke up other neighbors, who were about to go lend a hand—only to find thieves in their own homes too.","And it wasn't a solo act—they'd come as a group, a full gang.","By the time Zhou Wang came charging downstairs wearing two mismatched shoes, two people were already dead.","After the time they'd spent killing zombies, people in general had lost their sense of awe toward dead bodies. Food was the red line. Jixiang Jiayuan honestly didn't have as much food as the Youth Apartment residents had. And every household here had elders to care for and kids to feed—they had to feed a whole family. The moment food was involved, everyone's nerves were stretched tight.","Then there was the fear of zombies lurking in the dark. All these factors stacked together—there was no room for pulling their punches. They were swinging until they found it too late that the person wasn't moving anymore—already dead.","There were over a dozen of them in total in that group raid. Six or seven of the survivors had been captured alive. Word was a few still got away.","By the time Zhou Wang made it down, people were still beating and kicking the captured ones.","Everyone carried a heavy chip on their shoulder—men, women, old, and young. All of them.","Zhou Wang shouted for them to stop.","\"Uncle Zhou,\" Little Huang called out.","Little Huang's father, Old Huang, had been the earliest organizer of Jixiang Jiayuan. Even Zhou Wang had been organized under him.","But Old Huang had gotten injured in the very first wave of fighting. He'd been locked alone in the bedroom to quarantine, and sure enough, he turned into a zombie anyway.","Little Huang ended his father's life with a kitchen cleaver, his own hands on the handle.","That left a family of three down to a middle-aged mother and a middle-schooler. At least the boy's height now surpassed his mother's, and he could wield both a rolling pin and a cleaver.","For matters inside the compound, he used the rolling pin. For going outside, he carried the cleaver.","Zhou Wang assigned him tasks, and Little Huang's mother, seeing things clearly, told her son, \"You just stick with Uncle Zhou. Do whatever he tells you. Always stay with him.\"","Little Huang inherited his parents' sharp mind and steady, composed temperament. He listened to his mother and nodded. \"I understand.\"","In these abnormal times, he knew he had to be the \"man of the household.\" He couldn't be a \"orphan\" in some orphan-widow story.","The mother and daughter from the next building who jumped to their deaths—those were the real orphans-widow cases.","\"Uncle Zhou.\" Little Huang was holding a rolling pin with bloodstains smeared across it. He proactively reported to Zhou Wang, who had just come downstairs, \"They came to steal. We questioned them—these ones are from Yujing Xiangyuan and Deqingli.\"","They were all middle-aged men.","These men all lived nearby and had become acquainted by working out at the same gym.","If Li Jiangbing had been there, he could have named several of these people. That's right—they had worked out at the same gym where Li Jiangbing was employed, and some had even been his clients.","These people were backed into a corner too. Every street-facing store that could be looted had been basically wiped out. It was almost impossible to find food anywhere else. So they finally fixed their sights on the Youth Apartment and Jixiang Jiayuan, and after a screening, they picked Jixiang Jiayuan.","They organized online, recruited around a dozen people from several different compounds, and orchestrated the job.","The captured men were already beaten black and blue, some missing teeth.","These were men in good physical shape from long-term gym training, which is why they had the nerve. But they were on someone else's turf, and they were outnumbered by people defending their home.","When they realized some of their own had died, their faces went ashen.","Some had started begging: \"...We know we were wrong. We're sorry! We swear we'll never do it again!\"","Others played the pity card: \"There's really nothing to eat at home. My kid's only three...\"","Little Huang asked, \"Uncle Zhou, what are we going to do with them?\"","Keep them and hand them to the police later? But they'd looted Buyduo Supermarket without paying too. Everyone had looted.","And on top of that—people had been killed.","In the darkness, Zhou Wang glanced at Little Huang.","Still a young kid. But after everything he'd gone through, his eyes were no longer innocent.","Zhou Wang turned his gaze to the crowd.","Plenty of the male residents were gripping weapons.","Plenty of pairs of eyes burnt with aggression.","The people who killed those invaders—they hadn't been killed by any one person's hand. The crowd had done it, everybody together.","\"Old Zhou,\" someone called.","Zhou Wang looked over. At that man's feet lay a body.","Their eyes met in the darkness—those were sunken, scheming eyes.","There was blood on his weapon.","Even the rolling pin in Little Huang's hand had blood on it.","What should they do about it?","The earlier incident where someone was accidentally beaten to death in a conflict had already been settled, with both families agreeing to reconcile under mediation.","The woman who jumped off the building—that was her own choice.","But the body lying on the ground right now had been beaten to death by all of them together.","It was hard to pin it on anyone specific. It was everyone. It was each and every one.","“Here’s what we’ll do,” Old Zhou said, looking around. “All the women go back inside. The kids too. The men all stay. We’ll handle it together.”","When Zhou Wang said this, the women residents exchanged glances with their husbands, then gradually scattered, taking their children back into the buildings.","A few who hadn't left yet received a firm: “Go on, go on.” from Zhou Wang.","Many people could feel a shift in the atmosphere.","The men urged their wives: “Get inside now. I’ve got this here!”","Xiao Huang's mother was also present, holding a rolling pin in her hand. But she hadn’t gotten a chance to step forward, so she remained spotless.","Old Huang was a man of some standing, and his wife was someone who had seen the world. She sensed something wrong immediately and grabbed Xiao Huang by the arm: “You’re still young. Come back with me.”","But Zhou Wang cast a glance over.","Xiao Huang, who had been hesitating, stopped hesitating at that look. He pulled himself free: “You go on back. I’ve got this. I’m not a kid anymore.”","He gripped the rolling pin with both hands, holding it diagonally across his chest.","His mother caught sight of the blood on it. She remembered when her husband had turned, and the ad hoc owners’ committee had come around, but her son had refused to let anyone else kill his own father. He had insisted on ending his father’s life with his own hands.","A child had to grow up someday. And now was not the time to keep treating him like a child.","She let go of his arm and said politely to Zhou Wang: “Please keep an eye on him for me.”","Zhou Wang nodded: “Go on back, big sister. I’m here. Don’t worry.”","She looked at him, then at her young son, a flicker of reluctance in her eyes, before she steeled herself and turned away.","The elderly also retreated into the buildings. What remained in the open area beneath the residential blocks were only able-bodied young and middle-aged men.","Xiao Huang was the youngest among them.","He took in the scene—many pairs of eyes gleaming in the dark with a look that could chill you to the bone.","A few sturdy men gathered around Zhou Wang, huddling and speaking. Xiao Huang didn’t join them. Being careful of atmosphere and glances was something he had learned sharply over these days.","The tight circle that included Zhou Wang—these few men were the ones who could decide matters of consequence for Jixiang Jiayuan.","Xiao Huang knew it was precisely because he kept close to a decision-maker like Zhou Wang that he and his mother had not been bullied the way that woman who jumped with her child had been.","Stray words drifted intermittently through the night.","“Can’t...”","“Send them back...”","“Human lives...”","“Later...”","“Legal trouble...”","“Everyone will...”","Xiao Huang strained his ears, but he couldn’t catch anything clearer. The uncles were deliberately keeping their voices low.","The others around weren’t speaking either, all waiting for these choices to be made.","But their bodies were taut, alert, watching carefully over the people who sat or half-lay on the ground.","Xiao Huang saw the uncles pass out cigarettes to one another.","The air of tension around the adults seemed even heavier. It looked like a truly difficult decision.","But when they all threw their cigarettes to the ground and ground them out viciously under their shoes, it meant the decision had been made.","“They can’t be let go.” Zhou Wang’s gaze was gloomy as he announced, “They’ve already been bitten by zombies out there.”","For a moment, the air froze.","Someone cried out in alarm: “We haven’t —”","Those with quicker reflexes sprang up, trying to bolt away to save themselves.","But quick as they were, they were no match for a plan already laid.","The cleaver swung into a neck. Blood splattered outward, spraying into Xiao Huang’s open, startled mouth.","Hot. Salty. The blood of the living."]},{"number":50,"title":"Chapter 50","paragraphs":["People from the buildings near that spot went back home and heard some noises outside.","Some couldn't help but shiver.","A child, curious, tried to climb up to the window to look, but was yanked back by an adult: \"Go to sleep!\"","The noises stopped quickly.","Many didn't sleep. After a long while, a fire appeared in the central open area of the complex.","Someone glanced outside, then drew the curtains and let out a faint sigh.","Little Huang's mother waited a long time at home before he finally came back.","When Little Huang got home, his face was expressionless — he didn't even ask, \"You're still up?\"","His mother spoke first and asked, \"How was it handled?\"","Little Huang was silent for a moment, then answered, \"Treated as zombies.\"","It was what she had sensed would happen. She couldn't help but take a deep breath.","\"Uncle Zhou assigned me some work,\" Little Huang said mechanically, went back to his room, and sat in front of the computer.","He posted a thread on the Jixiang Jiayuan owners' forum, using Zhou Wang's tone to inform other residents: 【During these extraordinary times, discussions of certain matters in this complex on the forum are prohibited.】","What things were prohibited from being discussed, most residents had a good idea.","Jixiang Jiayuan didn't want people outside to know what had happened. Precisely because they didn't want it known, they had disposed of the ones taken alive.","Little Huang also posted as the moderator, telling everyone: 【I can trace people through IP addresses.】","Little Huang loved playing with computers. Old Huang had always supported him, buying him many computer books and sending him to training courses.","That was one reason Zhou Wang had Little Huang manage the forum.","Another reason: managing a child who had lost his father was far easier than managing an adult.","Little Huang silently finished the work Zhou Wang had assigned, stood up, and saw his mother standing at the bedroom door watching him.","Little Huang asked softly, \"Mom, where are Dad's cigarettes?\"","Little Huang had always been a well-behaved, excellent student. He had never touched cigarettes or alcohol.","His mother said nothing. She walked over to the tea table, bent down, opened the drawer, took out Old Huang's unfinished pack of cigarettes and a lighter, and handed them to her son.","Little Huang sat on the sofa, pressing the lighter to light a cigarette. His hands were trembling, so the flame trembled along with them.","He had no idea how to smoke. On the first puff, he choked.","His mother said gently, \"Breathe in slowly, don't rush to exhale.\" \"Your dad said, 'Breathe it into your lungs.'\"","\"He said it really relieves stress.\"","But in the end, Little Huang never learned to smoke. He had always been a good kid and had always urged his father to quit.","Watching him choke again, coughing until he couldn't catch his breath, his mother sighed faintly, lifted her hand, and gently stroked the top of his head.","Little Huang's cigarette fell to the floor.","Someone had been begging for mercy the whole time, saying over and over, \"The kids at home are crying from hunger, I really had no choice.\"","He said his child was only five years old.","Under his mother's palm, Little Huang, suppressing his voice as hard as he could, sobbed and cried...","What happened at Jixiang Jiayuan, Jiang Cheng didn't know about.","The youth apartment complex, for now, was still fully under control. The young people there could still eat their fill — though their meals were simple, mostly staples with canned goods, pickled vegetables, salted duck eggs, or chili sauce — but they were full. Compared with what they learned about other areas online, everyone was already quite satisfied.","The young people gathered together, running, working out, playing cards, playing ball in the safe green zone, finding plenty of things to keep themselves occupied.","It effectively diffused their anxiety and aggression.","They waited for the government's rescue and supplies.","Compared with the things she could control, Jiang Cheng was more focused on what she couldn't — Mo Li.","Mo Li had fully recovered. His eyes were a deep, glossy green, with not a trace of listlessness.","Mo Li himself thought so too.","Every day, Jiang Cheng tried to communicate with Mo Li through mental telepathy, hoping to sharpen the clarity of the communication through daily practice.","Unfortunately, it didn't work.","After observation and reflection, Jiang Cheng concluded that the problem wasn't the method of telepathic communication itself, but Mo Li.","In other words, no matter what kind of incredible mutation had occurred, Mo Li was, in the end, still a cat.","His intelligence was roughly comparable to that of a human toddler. Thinking about it that way made sense — communicating with him was like communicating with a child whose thinking and language hadn't fully developed; of course it was hard to make things clear and precise.","Most messages were short and direct.","Mo Li was incapable of expressing complex thoughts or emotions.","Jiang Cheng felt a bit disappointed.","She wasn't sure what she had expected, exactly, but she still felt disappointed.","\"If only you were a bit smarter,\" she murmured, rubbing Mo Li's head.","Even without deliberately focusing her mind to use telepathy, a faint current still carried vague meanings into Mo Li's brain.","Mo Li looked at Jiang Cheng with some confusion, then rubbed his head against her palm.","She was unhappy.","In Mo Li's understanding, showing her his belly and rubbing his head against her were ways to make her happy, so he did that.","The thought behind his action was vaguely received by Jiang Cheng.","She laughed softly, caught off guard.","\"Alright, alright, thank you.\"","She held him in her arms.","\"Time to sleep. Good night.\"","The residents of the youth apartment complex spent that night the same as the previous few — some up late playing games, some worrying about distant family, some sleeping soundly because of the temporary safety around them.","No one knew what had happened next door at Jixiang Jiayuan.","But the next day, Saturday, Su Yu came knocking on Jiang Cheng's door with another girl. At that time, Jiang Cheng had just taken a shower.","Because the swimming pool in the clubhouse was storing garbage and smelled awful, the fitness equipment had, as agreed, been moved out and placed in the lobbies of various buildings.","Each building got one treadmill, with one extra left over. The other equipment was assigned randomly. That way, people who wanted to work out could basically use the equipment in their own building's lobby. If their building didn't have a particular piece, they could visit other buildings to use it.","Jiang Cheng had just come back from a workout, sweaty and freshly showered, when she heard Su Yu knocking.","She opened the door and saw that Su Yu had brought along another girl — the one who had a dog she often walked. Jiang Cheng remembered her. Her name was He Tian.","\"He Tian got molested,\" Su Yu said, her expression grave.","This had happened on Friday night.","He Tian's stomach wasn't feeling well, so following the list on the forum, she contacted a person in her building to ask for some stomach medicine.","\"He told me on the phone to come to his place to get it,\" He Tian said. \"When I got there, he said he had to look for it and asked me to come inside. I was pretty stupid — I thought since he was a responsible volunteer, he must be decent, so I actually went in.\"","The people who were now serving as responsible leaders or core members of the interim committee were mostly the ones with some sense of duty, some capability, and some charisma.","During these past days, everyone had fought zombies together, rushed to grab supplies, participated together in all sorts of complex-organized activities — everyone had shown their good side, their brave side, their willingness to follow organizational discipline.","It had given people a beautiful illusion.","But when a young girl is alone with one of those men in a confined space that isn't very large, all those feelings of collectivity, solidarity, the courage, passion, and hot-bloodedness unique to youth simply dissipate like smoke.","In that house, at that moment, those two people were just a man and a woman, nothing more.","\"Disgusting!\" He Tian still felt like she wanted to vomit just thinking about it.","Disgusting!","That disgust wasn't only from the physical contact, the groping of her body. It was also a kind of disillusionment on a spiritual level.","All the beauty that had been keeping people's spirits up over these past few days had been shattered.","\"Fucking disgusting!\"","Even a sunny, cheerful girl couldn't help but curse, unconsciously rubbing her arm with her hand.","Whether it was goosebumps from disgust or because that place had been touched, she couldn't say.","Su Yu had already heard her tell the story once before, but listening a second time, she could still strongly empathize with her revulsion.","But she turned her gaze and saw Jiang Cheng listening intently, very serious, very patient.","But it was only listening. Su Yu couldn't detect a trace of empathy in her eyes or her expression.","Su Yu was slightly stunned.","\"Alright. I understand the situation,\" Jiang Cheng said. \"Now, did you get the medicine?\"","Su Yu: \"I gave it to her last night.\"","Jiang Cheng asked He Tian, \"Are you feeling better now?\"","He Tian nodded: \"I'm fine now.\"","The incident happened last night. He Tian had slapped that man in the face, angrily rebuked him, and run off without getting the medicine.","Back at her own place, she posted about it in the female residents' group chat.","Everyone was furious when they heard about it. Girls empathize most easily with these kinds of things—if it happens to one girl, it means it could happen to all of them.","Su Yu immediately brought her the medicine.","The two of them discussed it with the other girls in the group for a while and concluded that they couldn't just leave it alone; they needed to go to Jiang Cheng.","Why Jiang Cheng? Of course, because Jiang Cheng was the universally recognized de facto leader of the provisional committee.","But also because, since last night, all the male members of the provisional committee had suddenly become untrustworthy to the girls.","The man He Tian had gone to see was even a building captain. Just like Li Jiangbing and Song Jingshuo.","At a time like this, everyone felt so relieved that the provisional committee still had Jiang Cheng and Su Yu.","\"You two go back for now,\" Jiang Cheng said. \"I'll handle this.\"","Su Yu and He Tian both nodded and left room 0306.","They went upstairs to Su Yu's place. They had been nothing more than neighbors in the same complex who didn't know each other before, but after this week, they had become very close friends.","\"What's wrong with you?\" He Tian asked.","She felt like Su Yu seemed a bit off.","Then Su Yu said, \"Don't you think Jiang Cheng... seems a bit off?\"","He Tian: \"Huh?\"","Su Yu's face flushed hot, and she quickly waved her hands: \"I'm just talking nonsense. I've been overthinking lately.\"","Really, how could she say something like that out loud.","But Su Yu genuinely felt like Jiang Cheng had changed.","First impressions matter a lot. The \"first impression\" Jiang Cheng left on Su Yu wasn't actually when she stood in the middle of the crowd convincing everyone to do something—it was the look she gave Su Yu last Sunday night when they were clearing out zombies from the building. A young man had been injured and, refusing to accept his fate, was keeping everyone at bay by saying \"Whoever comes near, I'll bite.\"","At that moment, Su Yu was actually extremely nervous and scared. Because everyone was on the opposite side, and she was the only one behind that man.","But that look from Jiang Cheng carried encouragement and trust, which gave her the courage to surge forward.","Then Jiang Cheng privately hinted to her to be careful about the girls being marginalized and suggested that the girls participate as much as possible in the things organized by the provisional committee.","That night, Jiang Cheng established an image in Su Yu's heart.","Everyone in the whole complex knew that Li Jiangbing, the big guy from Building 2, was Jiang Cheng's loyal follower, always by her side like a shadow. If Jiang Cheng's instructions were carried out effectively, Li Jiangbing definitely deserved credit for it.","Privately, some people joked that Li Jiangbing had a crush on Jiang Cheng.","Su Yu knew that wasn't it. She didn't know what had happened between Li Jiangbing and Jiang Cheng, but something must have happened.","She could especially understand Li Jiangbing.","But in the last few days, she had a vague feeling that this Jiang Cheng seemed to have undergone a subtle change or deviation from the Jiang Cheng in her mind.","Was her initial impression just wrong?","Su Yu didn't know that Jiang Cheng had already broken free from being \"Jiang Cheng.\"","A girl's keen sixth sense allowed her to feel it, even if she couldn't understand it, leaving her mired in confusion."]},{"number":51,"title":"Chapter 51","paragraphs":["Jiang Cheng called Li Jiangbing first: “Jiangbing, where are you?”","“Yeah, got something going on. Come with me to find Jingshuo.”","“Okay, see you downstairs.”","Jiang Cheng hung up and called Song Jingshuo.","“What’s up?” Song Jingshuo asked.","The two of them used to meet every morning at the clubhouse gym. After the equipment was moved to the lobby of each building, they hadn’t seen each other these past two mornings. They only met in the afternoon now.","The interim committee would gather around noon each day, mainly to oversee the operations of sanitation, repairs, and a few other matters in the compound.","That was a group meeting, not a private one.","Jiang Cheng briefly explained and said: “Jiangbing and I are heading over to you now. Let’s discuss how to handle it.”","Song Jingshuo: “Okay.”","He added: “Talk it through first before doing anything.”","Was he worried she might be too furious and lose her temper on the spot?","Jiang Cheng hung up. Before leaving, she habitually glanced at the mirror. The cracked mirror could only reflect half a face.","How could that be?","This kind of thing couldn’t even stir the slightest emotion in her.","She met Li Jiangbing downstairs. He was working out in the lobby, drenched in sweat.","He saw Jiang Cheng come down, stood up, and wiped his sweat: “What’s up?”","There were other people working out in the lobby, so Jiang Cheng said: “Let’s talk outside.”","On the way, she gave Li Jiangbing a brief rundown.","Li Jiangbing cursed: “What a damn idiot.”","Jiang Cheng observed him.","Even though Li Jiangbing cursed the guy, it was purely because he thought the man and the act were stupid, so that’s why he swore.","As for feelings of anger or disgust, the emotions Su Yu would empathize with, he had none.","He was a man.","Song Jingshuo was also a man.","Jiang Cheng was well aware of this. At Song Jingshuo’s place, she said: “When order collapses, it doesn’t collapse in just one direction.”","It wasn’t that if someone bullied a girl today, that would be the only kind of incident and nothing else would happen.","Quite the opposite: when a building manager uses whatever little privilege he has to get something he wants, the targets he faces wouldn’t be limited to just female residents.","Where there are people, there’s scheming.","Song Jingshuo had a clear head and fully understood what Jiang Cheng meant.","Actually, the meeting they’d had before was themed around “order.”","The government said they needed to rebuild the order of survival. The youth apartment didn’t need “rebuilding”; it just needed maintenance. The interim committee’s responsibility was to keep order from deteriorating to the point where “rebuilding” became necessary.","“Nie Kuizhang from Building Three, right?” Song Jingshuo took the matter off her hands. “We’ll handle it. Don’t get involved.”","Li Jiangbing nodded in agreement: “The two of us will go.”","Li Jiangbing wasn’t a college graduate like Song Jingshuo and the others, but his practical street smarts far surpassed people like Zhao Yi, a shut-in.","In fact, he’d already thought on the way over that it was best for Jiang Cheng not to show her face. Song Jingshuo had the same thought.","The reason Jiang Cheng brought Li Jiangbing to see Song Jingshuo was exactly for this reason.","She had no intention of stepping in.","“Alright,” she nodded. “I’ll leave it to you two.”","She also made no demands about what should happen to the guy. How exactly to “resolve” the matter was up to Song Jingshuo and Li Jiangbing to decide.","Song Jingshuo asked for He Tian’s phone number. Jiang Cheng gave it to him and went back to her own place.","Passing the pavilion, she didn’t see Mo Li. Mo Li was sunbathing on top of the pavilion, but people always tried to pet him, so he’d found a new spot to soak up the sun.","Jiang Cheng didn’t know where he was, but she focused and sent a telepathic signal, receiving a faint jolt of feedback in return, knowing he was nearby. That was enough.","About an hour later, Su Yu came knocking.","“He Tian asked me to come thank you,” she said.","If she were truly grateful, why didn’t she come thank Jiang Cheng herself? No one had work or school. Everyone had more time than they knew what to do with these days, all bored out of their minds.","Jiang Cheng asked: “She’s not satisfied with the outcome?”","Su Yu bit her lip slightly, eyes cast down.","Jiang Cheng asked: “How did they handle it?”","“They made the guy apologize to He Tian, admit his mistake, and promise not to do it again. Then they took half of his medicine supply.”","“But you’re still not satisfied?” Jiang Cheng said.","Su Yu kept her eyes down and didn’t deny it. Not denying was admitting it. That meant they weren’t satisfied.","Jiang Cheng asked: “What kind of resolution were you hoping for?”","Su Yu raised her eyes: “I thought you would step in.”","He Tian had received a call from Song Jingshuo asking her to come over.","The girl, still sensitive after what happened yesterday, was wary of all men now. She asked if Jiang Cheng would be there too, and Song Jingshuo said she wouldn’t.","So He Tian called Su Yu, and Su Yu went with her.","All men were at Nie Kuizhang’s place.","The interim committee had seven key members: Jiang Cheng plus six building managers. Besides Jiang Cheng, all six building managers were there.","Clearly, the outcome was agreed upon by all six men.","These guys were all tall, or heavily built.","Before last night, Su Yu and He Tian would have felt a strong sense of safety around these people. But just now, in Nie Kuizhang’s home, the feeling was completely inverted.","It felt like two little lambs wandering into a den of wolves.","Of course they were deeply unsatisfied with the outcome.","But all the men, even Nie Kuizhang himself, though his face was grim, accepted it. Everyone felt this was “good enough” and “not bad.”","Neither of them could voice their dissatisfaction out loud.","They swallowed the grievance, accepted the apology and two bottles of stomach medicine as compensation, and were told the matter ended there.","When the elevator doors closed, they both felt a sense of “we escaped.”","He Tian didn’t actually ask Su Yu to thank Jiang Cheng on her behalf. In fact, she asked: “Is that it?”","Su Yu was also very disappointed, so she said: “I’ll go ask Jiang Cheng.”","“You seem to have misunderstood,” Jiang Cheng said.","“From the zombie virus outbreak last Saturday to today, one week, I’ve done my best to keep our compound under control,” she said. “Maybe that gave you the impression that I’m capable of anything, invincible?”","Su Yu’s lips moved slightly.","“Invincible” might have been overstating it, but in Su Yu’s heart, Jiang Cheng truly could solve a lot of things.","She thought Jiang Cheng could resolve this matter effortlessly as well.","But in reality, Song Jingshuo was the one running the show. She hadn’t expected Jiang Cheng to hand this off to him. She had lost trust in all these men now.","She just wanted Jiang Cheng to deal with this, to be their anchor.","“You’re wrong about that,” Jiang Cheng said. “I’m no different from you or He Tian. I’m just an ordinary female resident of this compound.”","She cut straight to the point: “You want Nie Kuizhang removed from his position as building manager, don’t you?”","Su Yu blurted out: “Why should he get to be a building manager!”","That kind of scumbag, what right did he have!","Jiang Cheng smiled: “Exactly. Tell me, what gave him that right?”","What gave him that right?","A scene suddenly flashed in Su Yu’s mind: just now, at Nie Kuizhang’s place in Building Three.","They knocked on the door. Li Jiangbing opened it. He was exceptionally burly, with bulging muscles, and one person alone could block the entire entryway.","Inside, all six men stood up.","The pressure hit her immediately.","Both she and He Tian were unhappy with the outcome, but neither dared to challenge or question it out loud.","They even felt a sense of relief leaving the place.","Su Yu became dazed.","Jiang Cheng could see from her expression that she had probably figured it out.","\"We don't have the power to revoke the building captains' status,\" she explained more explicitly, more thoroughly, \"because the building captains are not titles or positions granted by the interim committee.\"","In reality, the building captains were chosen from among the people in each building who went downstairs to kill zombies—the tallest or the strongest, the toughest or the fiercest, the boldest or the most ruthless.","Li Jiangbing was an obvious case; he used to be a personal trainer.","Song Jingshuo looked refined and lean, but in reality, he was fit with obvious signs of muscle built from working out, and he was one of the earliest organizers.","The thug Nie Kuizhang was plump and burly—his muscle couldn't compare with Li Jiangbing's, but his sheer bulk made him someone you didn't want to mess with.","So standing among these men, Su Yu and He Tian felt like sheep entering a pack of wolves.","\"We actually don't have that authority,\" Jiang Cheng said. \"Can the three of us—me, you, He Tian—really stand in front of them and tell Nie Kuizhang he's no longer allowed to be building captain? Would he listen? Would anyone else support that?\"","\"Right now, with this outcome, aside from us, no one else is objecting, right?\" she asked.","\"We\" and \"others\"—the words clearly divided people by gender.","Su Yu hesitated: \"They...\"","\"They are all men,\" Jiang Cheng said. \"People used to overlook my gender. Because my interests had always aligned with everyone's. Everyone seemed willing to listen to my suggestions, but in reality, they were following the suggestion itself, not me.\"","\"But this time, if I stepped forward, the rest of the interim committee would realize that my interests don't align with theirs.\"","\"If I had the power to remove one building captain, it would mean I could remove any building captain.\"","And with that, Jiang Cheng would be standing on the opposite side from the six male building captains, not on the same side.","\"I'm not some irreplaceable figure. Anyone on the interim committee could replace me. Li Jiangbing could, Song Jingshuo could, even Nie Kuizhang could.\"","\"There would definitely be someone happy to take my place, no doubt about that.\"","Of the seven core members of the interim committee, only Jiang Cheng was a woman.","She could easily be pushed out.","Because when it came to gender, men are especially quick to band together.","The outcome that Su Yu and He Tian were unsatisfied with was one that the other six men were all satisfied with.","They genuinely believed this matter was bad, but handling it this way was good enough. It would never occur to them to have He Tian's mindset of \"I want to beat this bastard to death.\"","They believed Nie Kuizhang had already paid the price—admitted fault, apologized, and had half his medication confiscated.","That was good enough. Six men, or at least five of them, were very satisfied with this outcome.","Su Yu returned home and opened the female residents' group chat, finding it buzzing with discussion. They were talking about this very matter.","He Tian had posted many angry remarks.","Everyone was comforting her and expressing disappointment toward the handling of the matter and toward Jiang Cheng.","He Tian: Su Yu went to see her, she'll come back and see what she says.","Su Yu saw that message, paused for a moment, then typed: I'm back, I've finished talking with Jiang Cheng.","What did Jiang Cheng say?","Why didn't she step in and leave everything to the men?","They should throw that fat bastard out of the building! Didn't they kick out that janitor before? Kick him out too!","They men always cover for each other, didn't Jiang Cheng think of that?","That was exactly why Jiang Cheng didn't step in.","Su Yu relayed her conversation with Jiang Cheng succinctly to the group.","The chat fell silent.","After a long while, someone said: What she said... does make sense...","Su Yu continued typing: Jiang Cheng asked me why the building captains are building captains, and then I thought, what made me believe I could have Nie Kuizhang's captaincy revoked?","It was \"morality\" and \"law.\"","When I figured it out, I suddenly realized that right now, in this current stage, whether it's morality or law, they seem...","They're both useless.","The chat fell silent again for a long time.","Someone said pessimistically: \"Are we falling into some primitive society where the strongest devour the weak?\"","Someone tried to console: \"It's not that extreme.\"","But \"not that extreme\" is not an outright denial—it's a partial denial, or in other words, a partial admission.","So the screen stayed still for a long time.","No one said anything.","Su Yu sat at her computer, unable to resist biting her knuckles.","Jiang Cheng had said: \"I'll do my best to maintain order and make sure our building doesn't fall apart to an irreversible degree.\"","\"Look at me—I'm just an ordinary girl like you.\"","\"I don't have any special ability to control anyone.\"","\"So I have to hold on to my say in the interim committee first. I can't let them team up and kick me out.\"","Su Yu knew everything Jiang Cheng said was right, but she still felt terrible.","That terrible feeling started from the back of her neck and went down, all the way to the last vertebra.","It ached."]},{"number":52,"title":"Chapter 52","paragraphs":["The chat group interface on the screen suddenly refreshed.","“Once this is over!”","“Once everything gets back to normal!”","“We’ll go to the police and get that scumbag arrested!”","A few sparse responses like “Right” and “Exactly” trickled in.","But more people stayed silent.","When would the zombie virus pass? When would everything return to how it was before?","The progress of government rescue efforts gave little reason for optimism.","Everyone felt lost.","At the same time, the troops sent to rescue City S were clearing out a residential complex in the southern district.","The captain of the second squad had a grim look on his face.","The team members threw a middle-aged man and woman onto the ground: “Captain! It’s them!”","The team members gritted their teeth in hatred.","Among them, one team member looked ashen, with a bloody, torn wound on his neck and obvious bite marks.","So far, no case had been reported where an infected person did not mutate. All infected would eventually turn. The time varied, but in the end, everyone became a zombie.","None of the soldiers had expected that someone would keep a zombie at home, or even lie to them to protect it — resulting in one soldier getting infected.","The team members were furious! Every pair of eyes was bloodshot.","“That’s not a monster, that’s my son — ”","The middle-aged woman collapsed to the ground, wailing.","“You killed him! You killed my son!”","She sobbed hysterically.","Her husband stared blankly at the ground — a middle-aged man who had lost his son, as if his soul had left him.","A young soldier, veins bulging on his neck, couldn’t hold back and raised his rifle, shouting: “Your son died long ago!”","From the moment a person was infected with the virus, they were already dead.","Just like his comrade at this very moment.","The captain reached out and pressed down on his rifle, barking: “Lower your weapon!”","The young soldier gritted his teeth, obeyed the order, and lowered his rifle.","The captain was furious too, of course.","Their current unit was a temporary formation — when the zombie virus broke out, places like military camps, densely packed with people, were hit hardest. They had already lost too many comrades on Saturday night.","Only after the survivors regrouped did their current unit take shape.","And now this soldier who was bitten and infected — he had originally been the captain’s own man.","The captain had no patience for these two despicable middle-aged people.","He looked at his soldier and said in a low voice: “Xiao Xu, you first...”","Although everyone knew that infection meant inevitable mutation, regulations required that before mutation, the person should still be treated as a “human” — kept under supervision until mutation, at which point they could be “dealt with.”","“No need to bother, Captain.” Xiao Xu gave a bitter smile, refusing to submit to supervision. He drew his sidearm and pressed the muzzle against his temple.","“Xiao Xu!”","“Brother Xu!”","“Xu Gang!”","Xiao Xu looked around at everyone.","Many faces here he hadn’t known before Wednesday, because they hadn’t been in the same unit. But over the past few days, they had become brothers who would die for one another.","“Too bad I can’t treat you all to my kid’s first-birthday banquet.” He said, “Captain, when my child grows up, help me tell them...”","“Your dad wasn’t a coward.”","Bang — !","Everyone closed their eyes.","They had faced original zombies and second-generation zombies without blinking, but at this moment, they couldn’t bear to watch.","Xiao Xu’s body fell at the captain’s feet.","His child was about to turn one. Before the virus outbreak, he had said he was going to hold a birthday party.","He would never attend his own child’s first birthday.","The captain clenched his fists so hard the veins on his hands stood out.","He ground his teeth, turned, and kicked the kneeling man rolling across the ground.","The woman screamed loudly.","The captain paid them no more attention. He gave the order: “Keep clearing.”","“Zombies — kill on sight.”","In the southern part of City S, the rescue forces advanced slowly.","Meanwhile, at the Youth Apartments in the tech district, Su Yu had barely left when Li Jiangbing and Song Jingshuo arrived right after.","Jiang Cheng invited the two of them to sit inside.","Actually, the apartment layouts here were mostly the same; Jiang Cheng’s unit was exactly the same as Li Jiangbing’s.","But the two still couldn’t help glancing around — not out of curiosity about the layout, but about a girl’s home.","Song Jingshuo was surprised: “What happened here?”","The mirror behind the door was shattered, only a few shards still hanging from the frame.","The spots on the sideboard where glass should have been were empty — clearly the broken glass had already been cleaned up. One cabinet door had also fallen off and was now hanging on haphazardly.","There were cracks on the TV, but it was still on and barely working.","There were three dining chairs. The fourth one had fallen apart; it hadn’t been thrown out yet, just stacked in the corner.","The place was actually cleaned up quite neatly — like a battlefield tidied up after a fight.","Li Jiangbing knew: “Don’t you remember? The first person in our complex to encounter a zombie was Jiang Cheng. She was also the one who killed the first second-generation zombie.”","Song Jingshuo suddenly understood.","He remembered now — he had seen it on the forum. Jiang Cheng had shared it.","Later, when Jiang Cheng stepped up and took on a leading voice, he learned she was the girl on the forum who had shared tips on killing zombies. At the time, he’d thought, “No wonder.”","Jiang Cheng pulled up a chair across from the sofa, and the three sat down.","Li Jiangbing told Jiang Cheng how Nie Kuizhang had been dealt with. He and Song Jingshuo both subtly watched her reaction.","Jiang Cheng’s reaction was — no reaction at all.","She didn’t even need Su Yu to have informed her of the outcome in advance. Whatever result Li Jiangbing and the others told her, she would have accepted it.","Rather than standing against the six male building leaders and cutting ties with their position, she had handed the matter over to Song Jingshuo and Li Jiangbing — turning a gender conflict into an internal male conflict. Jiang Cheng had already gotten what she wanted.","She had no complaints.","The female residents, of course, were dissatisfied.","But all the female residents combined, even with Jiang Cheng, still had no real power to restrain the male residents.","As Su Yu had said, morality and law seemed to still exist on the surface, but in reality, they had quietly lost their force.","It was precisely Jiang Cheng and the Interim Committee that maintained the inertia of order, keeping things “seeming” to still exist.","If the conflict were forced to escalate, it would pierce through this thin layer of paper — making everyone suddenly realize that what “seemed” to exist was actually already gone.","“We’ve all communicated, and things like this are strictly prohibited from happening again.” Song Jingshuo promised. “The survival order covers all residents — regardless of gender, everyone should be protected under that order.”","Li Jiangbing held out two large bags: “And this — confiscated from Nie Kuizhang. All for you.”","Jiang Cheng took them. Sure enough, it was the half of the medicine that had been taken away.","“Alright, then that settles it.” Jiang Cheng said.","The matter was done.","Li Jiangbing and Song Jingshuo’s shoulders relaxed. They stood up to leave.","Jiang Cheng stood up as well.","“We just need to hold out until government rescue arrives,” she said as she walked them out.","Song Jingshuo and Li Jiangbing reached the door and turned to look at her.","She leaned against the doorframe, smiling. \"I should remind everyone—we're all just ordinary citizens. Just because we helped out with some organization and coordination during a special time doesn't mean we've earned any special privileges or become some kind of big shots.\"","\"When all this is over,\" Jiang Cheng pushed her hair back, \"we go back to work, back to our lives. People in my line of work—event planning—might go hungry for a while, but you finance guys should be fine. Gyms should do okay too. Everyone's lives are about to get back on track.\"","Hearing Jiang Cheng say this, even Song Jingshuo felt a momentary daze.","Not to mention Li Jiangbing.","Li Jiangbing was a fitness coach. For all his imposing, intimidating build, his job meant putting on a smile every day, hustling for clients, bowing and scraping to get people to sign up or renew memberships.","But for the past week, Li Jiangbing had been strutting around like he owned the place. He'd started to see himself as some kind of street boss.","When Jiang Cheng said \"get back on track,\" somewhere inside him, he actually felt a pang of reluctance.","Li Jiangbing quickly caught himself and let out a sigh. \"Ain't that right—we're all just regular folks.\"","Jiang Cheng gave a faint nod and a smile, then stepped back and closed the door.","Song Jingshuo headed for the elevator. Li Jiangbing followed him, only snapping out of it when they reached the elevator lobby. \"Why am I following you? My place is the other way.\"","He turned and headed back toward his own unit.","Song Jingshuo let out a quiet laugh.","He stepped into the elevator alone and faced the doors.","The stainless-steel mirrored door reflected his image.","Song Jingshuo ran a hand through his hair, too. He hadn't bothered much with grooming these past days—not as polished as he used to be.","Better to get back to ordinary life sooner rather than later.","Any normal person would want to return to normalcy.","Unfortunately, they'd all be disappointed.","Saturday evening's broadcast: the rescue teams were still advancing at a frustratingly slow pace.","After the progress report, it was supposed to loop like the previous days. But today there was new content.","[......Citizens are encouraged to actively carry out self-rescue operations and establish safe blocks. All streets, residential communities, property management offices, and homeowners' committees are to take the lead in organizing......]","The moment this guiding principle aired, the city of S exploded.","Wails and cries rang out across the city.","Some people started cursing: \"What do they mean by this?! What do they mean?! Are they telling us to go get ourselves killed?\"","Even at the youth apartment building, Jiang Cheng could hear someone throw open a window and shout and swear at the garden below.","Another window opened, someone trying to calm things down: \"Stop yelling. Yelling won't help anything.\"","Another voice: \"It's not over yet! There's more! Get back inside and watch!\"","[......Armored vehicles leading the way, supply trucks will break through all obstacles and drop supplies along the main thoroughfares first. Offering the strongest possible support to the citizens.]","The rescue forces had to thoroughly clear every area they passed through. Otherwise, even one zombie left behind could bite a few people, and those few would mutate and infect even more.","That was why the rescue forces were advancing so slowly. But the civilians couldn't wait any longer—they were on the brink of starvation.","So the logistics units pushed forward first. Armored vehicles took point, speeding along the city's ring roads and tossing supplies as they went.","But according to the city surveillance system, the zombie numbers inside the urban area were massive. And with government combat personnel stretched thin, the supply convoys couldn't afford to stop or take side roads—otherwise, they'd risk getting surrounded.","They could only drop supplies along the main roads.","Then it was up to the citizens to collect.","That was what the emergency command center meant by \"self-rescue.\"","Jiang Cheng turned and rummaged through the drawer of her computer desk, pulling out a map of S City.","When she'd first come to S City alone, not knowing where anything was, she'd deliberately bought a paper map. Now it finally came in handy.","She spread the map across the desk and bent over to study it closely.","Her phone rang—unsurprisingly, it was Song Jingshuo: \"Jiang Cheng, what do you think?\"","\"Nothing good,\" Jiang Cheng said. \"Brace yourself.\"","Civilized society was, for now, coming to an end. S City was about to enter full-on survival mode."]},{"number":53,"title":"Chapter 53","paragraphs":["S city had a total of five ring roads.","Youth Apartments was located in the development zone. Relative to the downtown area, it counted as a new district, just outside the North Fifth Ring Road, not far from the Fifth Ring itself.","It was a bit far from the city center, but the company Jiang Cheng worked for sat between the North Fourth Ring and the North Fifth Ring, so her commute wasn't actually that bad.","The closest ring road to the development zone was, of course, the North Fifth Ring. Fortunately, the first wave of the supply convoy was scheduled to travel along the Fifth Ring first.","One reason was that supplies entering the city from outside naturally hit the Fifth Ring first.","The other was that, with years of urban development and residents relocating outward, the areas inside and outside the Fifth Ring had become dense clusters of residential communities, with a very high population density.","The development zone was a prime example.","On Saturday night, the interim committee held an emergency meeting.","Still at Song Jingshuo's place.","A map was taped to the TV with transparent tape.","Everyone sat on the floor, and Jiang Cheng stood beside the TV.","\"Good news is, water, electricity, and natural gas — those lifelines — are already under government control. For now, there won't be any large-scale outages.\"","Water, electricity, and gas were state-owned industries to begin with, and they were highly automated. As long as there were no major malfunctions, a small team of maintenance staff could keep them running.","Provided the terminal points didn't break down.","\"Let's just hope we get lucky and there aren't any minor glitches nearby,\" Jiang Cheng said. \"Because right now, if something breaks, nobody's coming to fix it.\"","\"Same goes for people. The news bulletins these past two days haven't mentioned hospitals even once. I've been paying close attention — not a single mention. That means all hospitals have probably fallen.\"","Everyone sighed in unison. \"Yeah, hospitals of all places...\"","Open-plan spaces, packed with people.","You didn't want to think about it.","All this information had come from that night's news broadcast. And then came the most important part —","\"The supply convoy sets off from here.\" Jiang Cheng tapped a spot at the bottom of the map with her pen.","Between that starting point and the development zone outside the North Fifth Ring lay the entire urban core of S city.","\"The emergency command center says, given the difficulty residents might have in picking up supplies, the convoy will split into four groups. They'll head east and west simultaneously, not using the elevated highways. They'll stick to the service roads the whole way, and both directions of traffic will be used at the same time, dropping supplies on the inner and outer service lanes.\"","East and west — that way, people near the East Fifth Ring and West Fifth Ring would basically receive supplies at the same time.","And by using both directions, one convoy going with traffic and one going against, residents on both the inner and outer sides of the loop would also get supplies simultaneously.","Because the main ring roads in S city were wide roads, crossing a ring road was itself a danger for residents. And there were residential areas on both sides of the ring roads too — dropping supplies on only one side would be unfair to the residents on the other.","So the question facing Youth Apartments now was: \"How many vehicles do we have? How many people can drive?\"","Jiang Cheng said, \"Before the meeting, Jingshuo, Jiangbing, and I took a trip down to the underground garage to scout things out. Didn't look too promising.\"","Youth Apartments had the lowest parking space ratio of any nearby community, at 1:0.4.","Jixiang Jiayuan, which was built much earlier than Youth Apartments, still managed 1:0.8. Word had it that Yujingxiangyuan had the best parking ratio in the area, at 1:1.","Shanshui Yayuan was a villa complex, which was a different story.","Youth Apartments had been designed from the start as \"a young person's first home.\" The developer's thinking was that young people would be less likely to own private cars.","Unfortunately for them, and coincidentally matching the developer's assumption, the cars Jiang Cheng and the others saw in the underground garage were predominantly compact models. There were also plenty of hatchbacks, which had very limited trunk space.","There were even a few ultra-mini cars with just a single row of seats.","The hauling capacity of all these vehicles was just too poor.","\"Route 535 express bus.\"","Jiang Cheng wanted to slam her pen down hard on the map to give her words more punch. But behind the map was Song Jingshuo's expensive flat-screen TV, so she held back.","She pointed with her pen to a spot that was a short distance from Youth Apartments: \"This is the terminal station for the Route 535 express bus. It's three stops away from us.\"","Song Jingshuo was truly impressed by Jiang Cheng at this point.","When he'd finished watching the news and realized the government's rescue efforts were likely to be even more helpless than they'd anticipated, his heart had gone cold. And he'd also realized what kind of scene this supply distribution method might lead to, so he'd called Jiang Cheng.","At the time, his mind had been in chaos.","But Jiang Cheng's voice on the other end had been calm, and he knew immediately that she already had a plan.","He'd asked, \"What are you thinking?\"","Jiang Cheng had simply had the property management staff on duty broadcast over the building intercom, calling all interim committee members to an emergency meeting at Song Jingshuo's place an hour later.","And she herself had called up Li Jiangbing and Song Jingshuo to take a head start going down to the underground garage. They'd surveyed the vehicles and confirmed that the owners' private cars really weren't up to the task.","On the way back, she'd shared her idea with the two of them.","\"I'm not an expert on vehicles, but that Route 535 bus really does look tougher than a regular bus. It's taller and longer, and it always drives fast — I reckon it could plow through zombies on the road without any problem.\"","Everyone laughed.","The development zone was outside the Fifth Ring, far from the city center. The government had planned express bus routes in these residential areas to handle the rapid flow of large crowds during rush hour.","The development zone also had a metro line planned, but word was it wouldn't be open for another five or six years. Many residents without private cars commuted into the city every day on the 535. They called it \"heading downtown.\"","Jiang Cheng's proposal passed without any resistance.","The residents, who'd been nervously holed up at home after watching the news bulletin, heard the building intercom announcement and felt a sudden wave of relief — the interim committee was holding an emergency meeting. They'd come up with something good, right?","That Jiang Cheng, she'd have a plan, right?","Just wait for instructions.","Sure enough, before bedtime, the intercom crackled to life again:","[Tomorrow morning, the interim committee will set out early to find vehicles for supply pickup.]","[Recruiting drivers who can handle large vehicles. License doesn't matter — just guts.]","[Recruiting scavenging team members.]","[Forum recruitment post is up. Sign up fast.]","[Notice to all residents: Use abbreviations for all event names on the forum. Absolutely no discussing tomorrow's plans on the forum, to prevent neighboring communities from copying, competing, or beating us to the punch.]","[These are extraordinary times. Maintain operational security.]","[For my community, and my community for me.]","Words like \"vehicles\" and \"scavenging\" weren't used much in everyday life, but the younger residents understood immediately — these were game terms.","Since they weren't allowed to discuss it on the forum, everyone chatted in their own building's group chats instead:","[We're guarding against Jixiang Jiayuan next door, right?]","[We have to. Look at the situation we're in.]","A girl asked: [I didn't quite catch that. What was that about... vehicles? What's scavenging?]","The young men who played games eagerly explained it all to her.","[Ohh, I get it now! That makes sense. Honestly that's a perfect way to put it — I understood it instantly.]","[Hahahahahahahahahaha.]","“Um... do we really have to go? I calculated that my staple food supply is enough for three months. We already have quite a lot of supplies, is it necessary to risk another raid? There should still be plenty of people going hungry right now...”","The barrage of messages in the group chat suddenly paused for a moment, as if everyone had lost their internet connection at once.","Then the insults came flooding back:","“Saint!”","“God, what a bleeding heart!”","“In times of chaos, kill the saints first!”","“What if the rescue takes four months to arrive? Are you going to starve for that extra month?”","“Wait, why assume it’s a saintess? What if it’s a saint?”","“Then kill both saint and saintess first—kill them all!”","That person was so badly flamed that they didn’t dare speak again.","Su Yu had been watching the group chat scroll by the whole time without joining in. Because she actually kind of agreed with the person who got scolded.","Am I too much of a bleeding heart? she wondered, conflicted.","But when she went to other forums, she did see some truly distressing help-seeking posts. The situations described in those were genuinely pitiful, enough to tug at anyone’s heartstrings.","Su Yu sighed and closed the group chat.","She needed to sleep early—she had to be at Terminal 535 early the next morning.","On Sunday morning, Su Yu woke up very early. She had set the rice cooker on a timer the night before, and by the time she got up, a full pot of rice was already done.","Eating rice for breakfast wasn’t common; lately, most mornings were porridge. But today she made steamed rice because today’s mission required bringing a packed meal.","Su Yu ate a third of the rice, then seasoned the rest with furikake and pork floss, shaping it into rice balls to take as her midday ration.","She got herself ready, packed the rice balls into her backpack, and found two magazines, taping one around each forearm with duct tape.","Practice had proven that this trick was incredibly effective. Lots of people would raise their forearms to block whenever a zombie lunged at them suddenly. The magazines were hard to bite through, and in a critical moment, they really could save your life.","She glanced at the wall clock—6:05. The meeting time was 6:15.","She slung on her backpack and grabbed a steel pipe.","This pipe was something Li Jiangbing and the others had fetched from a hardware store. It was excellent—much lighter than a frying pan, yet easy to swing with force.","It was also easy to carry, just tucked casually into her belt.","It gave off a sort of ancient swordsman vibe.","The committee members gathered on time at the entrance to the underground parking garage, along with some recruited car-owning residents.","Every car was packed as full as possible to maximize transport efficiency.","When the convoy drove out of the garage, many residents were already up, leaning out of their windows to watch: “They’re leaving, they’re leaving!”","“Go get ’em!”","“We’ll be waiting for your return!”","The atmosphere was charged with excitement.","A lot of people couldn’t help rolling down their windows and waving up at the buildings.","The road outside the east gate, Jixiang West Street, had already been blocked off, so the convoy exited through the west gate. Over a dozen cars rolled out in full force, quite a sight.","Ever since Saturday night of last week, everyone’s range of movement had been restricted. The farthest they’d reached was Buyduoduo, 800 meters away. On normal days, they couldn’t even do more than step out of the east gate onto Jixiang West Street.","After a week away, seeing the street-side park and familiar buildings from the west gate gave everyone a sense of having been apart for ages.","A few original zombies staggered toward them from up ahead. The lead driver said, “Hold tight!”","He floored the gas pedal and plowed straight through them!","The convoy roared forward, smashing and crushing its way toward the destination!","Leaving a trail of zombie remains behind them."]},{"number":54,"title":"Chapter 54","paragraphs":["On the way, they’d long since lost count of how many zombies they’d smashed or crushed. As long as the head wasn’t broken and was still attached to the body, even if the lower half was gone, the upper half could still crawl along.","This was the first time they’d seen anything like it.","Before, they’d always walked on foot out of the neighborhood, taking down zombies with blows to the back of the skull or the neck, killing them outright. They’d never made half-zombies like this.","It was disgusting and terrifying at once.","Someone couldn’t help but curse: “What the hell kind of twisted virus is this?”","On the big forums, students of medicine and biology had already debated fiercely, insisting that according to everything they’d learned, this thing shouldn’t exist.","But it did exist, right outside the window, downstairs, in the streets. Nobody could deny it.","At the Route 535 terminal station, there weren’t many zombies.","Because this route was mostly used by migrant workers commuting between the new development district and the city center. The zombie virus had broken out last Saturday, at night, so there was hardly anyone around.","The few zombies in the bus depot were probably the on-duty staff. They were still in their uniforms.","If you thought about it too closely, it stung. These were hardworking laborers just doing their jobs—but there was nothing for it. Everyone had to put them down.","The depot had about thirty buses, and the keys were all in the dispatch office.","The Route 535 express buses weren’t the same model as the ones in the city center. They were especially tall, and Jiang Cheng was right—they looked seriously sturdy.","“Whoa!” Li Jiangbing planted his hands on his hips in amazement.","It gave him that “it’s all ours now” feeling of plenty.","The core members huddled up to discuss: “Three? Four?”","They were figuring out how many to take to be enough.","Jiang Cheng sighed. “If only we could take them all.”","Someone couldn’t help laughing. “You’re way too greedy. Like a little hamster, stuffing everything into your cheeks.”","Jiang Cheng happily admitted to being greedy. “That’s exactly how hamsters survive the winter.”","There was no real criticism in their laughter. By now, after a week had passed, nearly the entire provisional committee had come to accept Jiang Cheng’s particular sense of crisis.","It was exactly that crisis awareness that always kept them one step ahead.","In the end, after considering all the factors, they drove away four buses with full tanks.","Four big, towering buses. None of the four drivers had any experience with vehicles that large—the biggest thing any of them had driven was a seven-seater. They were running on pure guts. As soon as they climbed up, it was all “holy shit, look at this view,” and then two of the buses scraped the pillars at the depot gate as they drove out.","The people on the buses heard the grinding sound of metal against concrete and winced right down to their molars.","Four giant buses and a dozen or so cars formed an even bigger convoy, heading back to Youth Apartments to pick people up.","At Youth Apartments, the volunteers had already gathered on Jixiang West Street, waiting for the buses to arrive. Since there were so many people, it drew the attention of residents in Fortune Garden. Someone opened a window and shouted down: “Are you guys going to pick up supplies?”","A lot of people also came down to watch out of curiosity, because the Fortune Garden residents had also planned to scavenge supplies at the Fifth Ring Road that day, and plenty of people were already standing in the courtyard.","Zhou Wang heard the commotion and brought people over to check. He asked: “Where’s Little Jiang? And Xiao Song? Where are they?”","The Youth Apartments residents hedged: “They went driving.”","Zhou Wang was an old hand. He could tell just by looking at these young people that they weren’t telling the whole truth.","But they had also stayed up all night planning, making a ton of arrangements for today. He figured Youth Apartments would be doing the same thing as his group—mobilizing residents with cars, coordinating families without them, neighbors helping neighbors.","So he didn’t push. If people don’t want to tell you something, pressing them won’t help.","But when the four 535 buses came rumbling down and pulled up to stop on the main road, Zhou Wang realized he’d underestimated these young folks from Youth Apartments yet again.","The cars all pulled into the underground garage. The four big buses stopped and swung open their doors. Li Jiangbing bellowed: “We’re moving out!”","The volunteers traveled light: each with a single pouch holding a day’s rations and water, basic protective gear, and a weapon in hand.","The towering buses fired up everyone’s spirits. They howled and scrambled over the cars blocking the intersection at Jixiang West Street, full of energy.","“Here they come!”","“Let’s go!”","“Everyone onboard!”","The people of Fortune Garden stared in astonishment. “So that’s how you do it.”","Zhou Wang watched the receding figures and suddenly let out a sigh.","He felt like he’d been playing by the old rules too long. Deep down, he was still obeying the social norms of the past. But the truth now was that survival was the first principle, and under that principle, you could ignore a lot of laws—like private property, or public property.","Young people’s brains worked better after all.","The Fortune Garden residents were envious of those four big buses, even a little tempted: “Brother Zhou, what if we...”","Zhou Wang glanced at his watch. “No time. Let’s stick to the plan and head out.”","The people felt a little disappointed.","But in last night’s news bulletin, the temporary emergency command had predicted the arrival times of the supply convoy at each drop-off point. If you went too late, you’d lose out.","Even though time seemed to still be ample, there was always the fear of crowding, everyone wanting to get a spot early.","Zhou Wang: “Let’s go. We need to move too.”","Fortune Garden rolled out a long convoy from their east gate. All private cars—they’d pulled nearly every driver they could mobilize.","They soon caught up to the Youth Apartments convoy. Anyone watching would have thought they were one big group.","But the Fortune Garden people weren’t satisfied with always coming second to Youth Apartments, and they certainly didn’t want the Youth Apartments group reaching the drop-off zone first. So more than one sedan floored the gas and overtook the big buses.","The Youth Apartments drivers didn’t dare to speed—mostly because they weren’t used to driving the large vehicles and were afraid of crashing. Cursing under their breath, they trailed along behind these cars.","But the Fortune Garden folks quickly regretted their decision. When they’d been behind the buses, even though they’d seen zombies from their windows being drawn by the noise and chasing the convoy, the ride had felt pretty smooth.","But once the smaller cars got out in front, the experience was totally different.","Zombies came charging directly from the front and the sides! Slamming into the windows! The glass was already cracking!","The driver swore, “Why are there so many of them?!” and gritted his teeth as he floored the gas pedal, crashing straight into them.","On a lucky hit, zombies were sent flying.","But sometimes luck ran out, because zombies felt no pain and feared no death. When there were too many, you could knock out a few, but one unlucky slip and a zombie would land on the hood, scramble a bit, and end up clinging to the windshield, grabbing hold of the wiper blade.","The road completely disappeared from view.","“Damn it!”","“Whip the wheel! Shake him off!”","The passengers inside were screaming.","Jiang Cheng and the others were in the lead bus. It was tall with a good view, so they could clearly see a private car ahead starting to swerve in an S-pattern. It hadn’t gone two curves before it lunged up onto the sidewalk and slammed into a roadside flower bed.","The car flipped over, its doors popped open.","A pack of zombies flooded toward it.","A second-generation zombie leaped, bouncing off a primeval zombie, and landed with a bang on top of the overturned vehicle.","The zombie bent down, upside down, and plunged its upper body into the car.","From inside came screams and shrieks.","No one came to the rescue.","There were too many zombies on the road, all drawn in by the noise of the convoy. A lot of them looked like second-generation zombies, too.","Who would dare stop and get out to help? What if you were the only one to stop, and no other car pulled over? That would be walking straight into death!","A bit of neighborly goodwill wasn't enough to make anyone volunteer to die.","But the cars up ahead were slowing down, pulling aside to clear the inner lane.","The four big buses proudly rolled back to the front. Against vehicles that big, even zombies looked small—they charged in and got knocked flat and crushed under the wheels, the sound of bones cracking deeply satisfying.","No small car dared to overtake anymore. They all obediently lined up behind the four big vehicles from the youth apartment complex.","Meanwhile, Zhou Wang got a call from Jiang Cheng: \"Which drop-off point are you heading to?\"","Zhou Wang: \"Wanzhuang Bridge is the closest one.\"","Like Jiang Cheng, he was holding a map with supply drop points circled in pen.","Of course you'd head to the closest drop point to you.","Last night's announcement of these drop points, when mapped out, showed they all corresponded to large dense residential areas. Wanzhuang Bridge, Sishui Bridge, and Liujiabao Bridge were clearly meant for the newly developed districts.","Of them, Wanzhuang Bridge was the nearest to them.","Going to a farther one made no sense—people from neighborhoods closer to those points would be going there anyway. Overall, the population distribution across the drop points was fairly even.","Jiang Cheng said: \"We're taking the outside.\"","\"Good,\" Zhou Wang said. \"Then we'll take the inside.\"","That meant the inner ring of the Fifth Ring Road versus the outer ring.","No need to think about it—there was bound to be a scramble.","For the past week, the youth apartment complex and Jixiang Jiayuan had been semi-allied, neighbors separated by just one street, with many faces familiar to each other.","Either way, they were going to be fighting for supplies. There was no point in getting into a conflict with people they knew. Both sides of the ring road had drop points—they'd split up and fight strangers instead.","The moment Jiang Cheng hung up, someone in the same bus suddenly started heaving. Everyone turned to look: \"What's wrong?\"","The lead bus had been barreling through and crushing zombies all the way, splattering sticky, disgusting gunk across the windshield. But it had been a week since the zombie outbreak. They'd seen brains split open, eyeballs stepped on, necks chopped through. Their nerves were already tempered.","So why was someone puking?","\"Eating... eating people... ugh...\" The man gagged as he explained. \"Dogs! Cats! ... Eating people... ugh!\"","There had been corpses all along the road. Left out in the summer heat for a week, they were already rotting, flies buzzing around in swarms.","Crows were pecking at them too.","But cats and dogs were a different kind of animal entirely. Not the same as crows.","Of course, there were stray cats and dogs in the city—more of them after the outbreak. Some had lost their owners; others had been thrown out when homes ran out of food.","Cats and dogs eat meat. With no food to find, they gnawed on corpses. For carnivores, a dead person was no different from a dead rat or dead bird—just a bigger chunk of meat. Totally normal.","Just his bad luck that he happened to look over at the wrong moment.","Someone leaned toward the window to peer out: \"Where?\"","But the bus had already driven past; it was out of sight now.","Someone muttered from their seat: \"What kind of world is this...\"","Even cats and dogs were eating people now.","Someone couldn't help but glance at the familiar sling bag Jiang Cheng wore, zipper open, revealing a dark hollow inside.","As the gaze landed, a pair of emerald-green eyes like jewels lit up in the darkness, glowing eerily as if sensing the stare and staring back.","The looker flinched and quickly looked away.","The traffic on the road was getting heavier—clearly, residents from the new development districts were all heading for the government supply drop-offs. Everyone was mixed in together now, all private cars, impossible to tell who was from Jixiang Jiayuan and who wasn't.","But those four number 535 public buses stood out unmistakably.","Some sharp-eyed drivers, seeing so many private cars tailing the big buses, decided to follow along too.","If this were a game, the public buses were the tankiest tanks up front.","When the convoy finally turned onto a service road off the ring road, things got noticeably cleaner—the Fifth Ring Road and the areas inside and outside it were separated by greenbelts, and it wasn't city streets anyway. There were almost no zombies on either side, just a sparse handful here and there, probably drivers who had pulled over last Saturday night.","The big buses simply crushed them outright.","The convoy began to split. The four buses turned directly onto the outer service road, while the Jixiang Jiayuan convoy passed straight through under the bridge and entered the inner side of the ring road.","Many drivers watched the dividing traffic ahead, momentarily unsure which side to follow.","The previously orderly convoy suddenly fell into chaos."]},{"number":55,"title":"Chapter 55","paragraphs":["They had reached their destination. In particular, after the Jixiang Jiayuan convoy crossed the overpass and went to the inner side of the ring road, the people in the other cars that had been following along had no idea what was going on with these four Route 535 buses.","The Fifth Ring Road was a suburban express loop, with no residential buildings on either side. On the outer side, the area separated by the green belt consisted of companies and factory buildings.","As a result, there were almost no zombies on this stretch of road.","Some cars couldn't wait to overtake, eager to grab a good spot.","In truth, nobody actually knew which spot counted as a \"good spot,\" but that's how it gets when there are crowds—someone always inexplicably wants to get ahead, to take the lead.","The driver of the lead bus from the Youth Apartment turned his head and asked, \"What do we do? Overtake or not?\"","Everyone looked at Jiang Cheng.","Jiang Cheng said, \"Keep driving forward.\"","The four buses continued ahead. The cars behind gradually pulled over and stopped, but the big buses kept going.","Because Jiang Cheng hadn't said to stop.","It wasn't until Jiang Cheng finally said, \"Stop here.\"","\"There are no trees here—it's all open and clearly visible, so it's safer,\" Jiang Cheng said.","The area they had just passed featured urban green belts, also known as the city’s green lungs—large stretches of planted forest along the ring road that blocked visibility.","The place Jiang Cheng chose was beyond the artificial forest area. Along the roadside were already companies and factories. Iron fences enclosed the building complexes and spacious courtyards, where a few zombies could be clearly seen.","\"Honk the horn,\" Jiang Cheng said. \"Clear them out.\"","The buses' horns suddenly blared, startling the cars behind that were hesitating about whether to follow.","\"What the hell!\"","The cursing came to an abrupt halt when zombies came climbing over the fence: \"Holy crap!\"","The Youth Apartment people, on the other hand, went \"Ooh!\"","When there were a lot of people around, basic zombies weren't scary—you could basically just overpower them with numbers.","It was the second-generation zombies that were the problem. They were too fast, too agile—you worried that if you didn't spot one, it would ambush you.","But now, under the bright sun, with an unobstructed view, using the horn to lure out the second-generation zombies wasn't a problem—just go at them.","Everyone was howling with battle fervor. Jiang Cheng said, \"Wait a little longer. Don't be in a hurry to open the doors.\"","The core team was all in the lead bus, and the three buses behind all followed the lead bus. If the lead bus didn't open its doors, they didn't either.","They watched as that second-generation zombie made a beeline for the lead bus, jumped up, and thwacked its palm flat against the glass. Luckily, it hit right in the center of the window—loud enough to make you jump, but the bus window withstood the blow at its center and didn't crack.","The lead bus kept honking, piercingly sharp. But \"waiting\" really did pay off—there was more than one second-generation zombie. Three more came running out.","The basic zombies were also attracted by the horn, but they were blocked by the factory's iron fence, gray-blue arms reaching through the bars, letting out harsh, grating roars.","But the second-generation zombies were different. They jumped, stepping on the backs of the ordinary zombies in front, and climbed over the fence. Their movements were as nimble as monkeys.","Several second-generation zombies leaped and attacked the lead bus. One struck the glass near the corner edge—thud—and a web of radiating cracks spread across the window.","A second-generation zombie's combat power was far greater than a basic zombie's, and not by a small margin.","Jiang Cheng made everyone stay in the bus and kept blasting the horn to create noise, specifically to deal with the second-generation zombies.","When it seemed about right, and no more second-generation zombies appeared to have been lured out, Jiang Cheng raised the walkie-talkie: \"Buses behind us, help us clean these up.\"","The second-generation zombies were too agile. Jiang Cheng didn't dare open the doors directly—what if, instead of them charging out, the zombies charged in? In the cramped bus space, someone could end up hurt or infected.","The doors of the three buses behind all opened.","This time, the recruited volunteers weren't called the \"daredevil squad\" anymore—they were called the \"scavenger squad.\"","Young people together always liked to come up with that sort of thing—finding joy in misery.","Whatever they called themselves, though, dozens of members with rich combat experience and fully equipped protective gear weren't afraid of just four second-generation zombies. The people from the three rear buses swarmed out, gang-beat the four zombies with no honor whatsoever, and beheaded all of them.","The cars following behind watched in stunned disbelief.","This group fought in formation—several of them crowded together, working in sync, guarding front, back, left, and right.","Who were these people?","Those at the back didn't know. The young people from the Youth Apartment didn't have to work and didn't lack food—they had nothing but time on their hands. Every day, they'd swarm downstairs to hang around in groups.","When guys got together in a group, they started making trouble.","Especially when facing a survival issue—they really had to do something.","They kept studying the various behavioral traits of zombies, found neighbors they got along with and liked talking to, and then formed small teams. After eating, they'd go downstairs together to practice their \"formation\" for coordinated killing.","Too bad that by the time they were doing all this, you could hardly even see a zombie on Jixiang West Street anymore. And the provisional committee didn't recommend going out without permission.","Anyone who went out without permission had to undergo a full-body check when they came back.","If they had even a tiny scrape or nick, they couldn't explain it away, and they'd be locked up for quarantine observation.","Everyone practiced their \"battle formation\" more and more smoothly, waiting for real combat.","Once they actually engaged in real combat, they immediately saw both their strengths and their shortcomings. They'd have to improve based on real battle experience.","But how were the people in the cars behind supposed to know any of this? They started guessing: \"Are they soldiers?\"","\"Doesn't look like it—soldiers walk and eat in sync, and these people don't seem like that. Definitely not.\"","\"Are they college students? They all seem pretty young.\"","\"...Well, not that young.\"","\"Then... employees of the same company?\"","The main thing was, the age range was too concentrated. It didn't really feel like people from the same residential community.","\"Which community has a mix of men and women, old and young? There's no way it's this uniform.\"","\"Hey—actually, there is!\"","Someone actually guessed it right: \"Youth Apartment! It has to be the Youth Apartment!\"","\"I heard they're the ones who cleaned out the Buyduoduo supermarket!\"","\"Damn, no wonder they could clean out a supermarket. They're really strong.\"","\"Don't get into a conflict with them later—just stay out of their way.\"","The people in the lead bus got off too.","Jiang Cheng pushed her sling bag to her back, bracing it with her hip against Mo Li, and stood with her hands on her hips, looking up at the cracked glass.","\"Jiangbing,\" she turned her head and asked, \"could you crack glass like that with just your bare fist?\"","Li Jiangbing bragged: \"I definitely could... probably?\"","His voice trailed off with less certainty. He'd never actually tried it. He knew in his heart how much of his muscle came from chugging protein powder and nutritional supplements.","The government's supply convoy was still quite a while from arriving at the estimated time. As for the zombies you could see in the open, a few had run out from the woods and had already been crushed by cars. Aside from that, there were the ones trapped behind the factory's iron fence.","Since a group of people couldn't stand to be idle, and the factory was close—just across a patch of lawn—they went over to the fence and stabbed the zombies through the bars with their blades.","Basic zombies were the dumbest. Even if you hacked off their arms or stuck a knife through their bodies, they had no idea how to dodge, and they didn't \"die\" anyway.","To actually kill them, you had to smash their brains or sever the connection between head and body.","Some people guessed that the brain was the central control. When the brain was destroyed, they died. When the neck was severed, the central nervous system was broken—the central control lost command of the body—and that counted as death too.","But there were also doctors in the neighborhood who insisted they had examined the zombies' bodies, and none of this held up.","This stuff just wasn't scientific! This stuff just couldn't exist! It violated too many principles of biology.","Yet there it was, right in front of them, possibly even an acquaintance or a family member.","You ask the doctor to explain, and the doctor tears at his hair, on the verge of losing his mind.","\"These things really are...\" everyone said while poking at the zombies, \"...kind of stupid.\"","The basic zombies didn't dodge; they just roared and lunged, trying to bite. But they were blocked by the railing, their grayish-blue faces desperately trying to squeeze through the bars, pressing until their features warped.","People used steel pipes to stab straight into their eye sockets and churn up their brains.","One zombie hadn't been stabbed yet, and it pushed too hard. With the sound of cracking bone, its deformed skull actually wrenched itself through, scaring everyone.","Unfortunately, even with its skull shattered, it wasn't dead yet, its head misshapen, screeching horribly, especially grotesque.","People quickly chopped its head off. The headless body hung on the railing and went still.","The core members of the neighborhood committee didn't join in the chaos; they were handling the real business.","Peng Ze climbed onto the roof of a car. He had binoculars and had brought them along this time. Standing up high, he looked through them for a while, then climbed down: \"Nothing. I don't see anything.\"","No official supplies in sight yet.","Jiang Cheng nodded.","Peng Ze looked around, a bit worried: \"Isn't our car a little far from the supply point?\"","The announcement said Wan'an Bridge was a supply point, and he always thought it should be right under the bridge, the center point of the bridge.","Their four cars had gone a bit too far. He worried that when the government dropped the supplies, they'd all land there, making it hard for them to grab any.","\"Supplies are for 'people,'\" Jiang Cheng said casually. \"Wherever there are people, that's where they'll drop.\"","They had a lot of people and big cars; as soon as the logistics convoy arrived, they'd see them at a glance.","Song Jingshuo also got out of the car. He took off his designer sports backpack, opened it, and pulled out a bunch of purple cloth strips: \"Come on, everyone, tie these on so we can recognize each other. Don't want any fighting later.\"","With more than two thousand people in the neighborhood, not everyone knew each other. They were afraid of conflicts breaking out among their own.","The neighborhood committee had thought of even this.","Everyone went over to grab a cloth strip.","Some tied them around their arms, some right across their foreheads. The atmosphere immediately picked up.","Only Jiang Cheng held one in his hand, stared at it for a moment, then looked up: \"A bedsheet?\"","Song Jingshuo froze for a second.","Li Jiangbing burst out laughing: \"Old Song, you have a bedsheet in a color this flashy? Never would've guessed, never would've guessed!\"","Song Jingshuo rubbed his forehead helplessly: \"My mom bought it. She bought it when she came to visit me. I never slept on it.\"","That color, in a single guy's bedroom, was way too flashy. He'd always found it annoying, but in the end it was his mother's gesture, so he never threw it out, just left it stuffed in a drawer, unused.","Now he had the perfect excuse to \"put it to good use\" with full justification.","Li Jiangbing laughed until he snorted.","Peng Ze also tied a strip around his forehead, then climbed back up onto the car roof to serve as lookout.","Jiang Cheng handed him the crossbody bag holding Mo Li, and Peng Ze took Mo Li up onto the roof too, letting him out to enjoy the sun.","An hour later, Peng Ze suddenly jumped up: \"They're here, they're here!\""]},{"number":56,"title":"Chapter 56","paragraphs":["When a group of people band together, they start to feel a sense of power, thinking themselves invincible.","But when the nation flexes its might—when armored vehicles roll in, caked in blood and dragging mangled limbs, when the supply convoys follow in orderly, silent, solemn formation—everyone present can't help but feel utterly insignificant.","The fronts of the armored vehicles were coated in dark brown—zombies do have blood in their bodies, but it's not bright red; it's a very deep, very dark brown.","There were severed limbs caught in the tracks. One arm was wedged in the tread gap, rotating with the track, slapping the ground with every revolution. Slap. Slap. Slap.","Even if the Fifth Ring Road had fewer zombies, that didn't mean there were none. The Fifth Ring Road stretched 110 kilometers in total, and to get from the south of the city to the north, one had to pass through the southern, eastern, and western sections before reaching the northern arc. It was impossible to imagine how many zombies that lead convoy had crushed along the way.","The vehicles didn't stop. Ignoring the crowd gathered at Wanzhuang Bridge, they pressed forward with grim determination.","A few people grew frantic, jumping up to chase after them, but were held back by those nearby, who scolded them: \"Didn't you read the government notice yesterday? Echelon advancement.\"","Echelon advancement meant the lead vehicles had to go to the farthest destination.","The supply convoys had entered the Fifth Ring Road from the south, moving in both eastbound and westbound lanes, and would converge at a point on the northern Fifth Ring Road. That point was the true terminus of this supply run.","Wanzhuang Bridge was still some distance from that point.","The destination of this lead truck convoy was not Wanzhuang Bridge.","Another half hour passed, and two more convoys rolled through in the meantime. Many people were growing anxious: \"When is it our turn?!\"","Someone even suggested a bad idea: \"Let's set up roadblocks and stop the vehicles. They're giving supplies to the people anyway—what does it matter who gets it? We're the people too!\"","To everyone's surprise, some actually voiced agreement.","But when it came to who would drive their own car into the middle of the road as a barricade, no one volunteered.","In the end, they dragged some traffic barriers (water-filled barricades) into the middle of the road.","Peng Ze, perched on top of a vehicle, saw what was happening. \"Some people are trying to block the convoy!\"","He said, \"According to the notice, the next two convoys aren't for Wanzhuang Bridge. It's the one after that.\"","He stayed on the roof, craning his neck, and asked, \"What do we do?\"","Peng Ze was a somewhat naive, hot-blooded young man. He didn't have many ideas of his own, but he had complete faith in Jiang Cheng. Whenever Jiang Cheng spoke, he followed without hesitation.","He thought blocking the road was a bit immoral, but if it worked, they could get their supplies sooner. He couldn't exactly blame those people either—many of them were probably starving and desperate.","Because he could understand them, he found himself conflicted.","Jiang Cheng said, \"All we need to do is get our supplies. Nothing else matters.\"","No need to worry about what others did, and no need to worry about whether this batch of vehicles was meant for them.","Peng Ze let out an \"Mm!\" and stopped agonizing over it.","He was actually curious, though—could a few flimsy traffic barriers really stop an armored convoy? And if they did manage to stop them, what then?","After another ten-plus minutes, another convoy arrived.","Every convoy was led by armored vehicles up front. But this time, the armor looked much cleaner—less zombie blood, and no severed limbs visibly hanging off the tracks.","The convoy drove closer.","Everyone's mindset was more or less the same: blocking the convoy was wrong, sure, but in times like these, \"right\" and \"wrong\" didn't matter as much. If the convoy could be stopped, they'd rush in and grab supplies.","No harm in trying.","With that mindset, all eyes were fixed on the lead armored vehicles.","Unfortunately, the armored vehicles didn't slow down at all. In fact, they sped up and plowed straight through the traffic barriers, sending them flying.","One barrier was knocked over and crushed under the tracks—probably exactly how the zombies got flattened. The crowd heard the sickening crunch of breaking plastic and debris scattering, and those standing too close scrambled behind cars in panic.","The convoy still didn't stop. Their destination wasn't Wanzhuang Bridge. They rumbled onward, engines roaring.","Li Jiangbing happened to turn his head, about to make a joke about those fools, when he caught sight of Jiang Cheng watching the convoy disappear into the distance, a faint smile curling at the corners of her mouth.","Li Jiangbing turned to look—the vehicles were already gone.","He asked, \"What are you staring at?\"","Jiang Cheng pulled her gaze back and let out a soft sigh. \"Beautiful.\"","Li Jiangbing was confused. \"Huh?\"","Jiang Cheng's eyes gleamed with appreciation. \"The armored vehicles.\"","Li Jiangbing: \"Oh, you're a military buff?\"","Jiang Cheng: \"Not really. I just... like them. Maybe because of the times we're in.\"","The decisiveness and ruthlessness of the tracks rolling over everything in their path. The silent, solemn march of the entire convoy.","[An iron tide.]","Those were the four words that came to Jiang Cheng's mind.","A bit of a liking. A strong liking. An overwhelming liking.","Li Jiangbing mimed gripping a steering wheel. \"Who doesn't love that? Sitting inside, rolling straight over everything—vroom, vroom, badass. Who's afraid of zombies then?\"","But what Jiang Cheng felt went beyond mere \"liking.\"","[I want to possess them.]","She didn't know where that thought came from. Something like that wasn't something an individual could theoretically own.","But that \"theoretically\" belonged to the \"Jiang Cheng\" who existed before.","Not the Jiang Cheng of now.","The convoy for the Wanzhuang Bridge distribution point had finally arrived!","As Jiang Cheng had said, the supplies were meant for \"the people.\" So although the four buses from the Youth Apartments were parked a bit far from the crowd, the moment they saw the convoy, they waved their arms frantically and shouted.","Sure enough, the lead armored vehicle slowed down, and the trucks behind it slowed too.","The first truck passed by. The second truck passed by... Then the last truck, before it even reached the four buses, raised its cargo bed, and cardboard boxes and sacks tumbled out, thudding onto the road.","There were a lot of people waiting for supplies. Even though the four buses from the Youth Apartments had positioned themselves at the farthest possible spot, there were still other vehicles and people crowded close to them.","The moment the boxes and sacks hit the asphalt, people surged forward.","But the Youth Apartments group had planned this out in advance—they had even rehearsed during the wait. Everyone knew exactly what to do.","A dozen or so physically imposing men—whether broad, burly, or tall, as long as they looked intimidating—formed a human wall in a single line, blocking the surging crowd.","Loud shouts rang out: \"Back off!\"","\"Go get yours over there!\"","\"This side is ours!\"","Li Jiangbing, a formidable giant of a man, and Nie Kuizhang, a big, heavyset man, were both in the human wall.","Naturally, some people wanted to angrily demand, \"Why?!\"","But facing a wall of toughs, each holding a steel pipe of identical size, thickness, and length—","And wearing cloth bands of the same color tied around their arms or foreheads—","Such unity made the scattered, disorganized crowd lose their nerve. That \"Why?!\" got swallowed back, and they turned to chase after the trucks instead!","The trucks in the same convoy also unloaded in echelon fashion. The rear trucks unloaded first, the front trucks unloaded later. The supplies were dropped in the slow lane, and once a truck finished unloading, it merged into the fast lane to keep moving.","The human wall from the Youth Apartments held back anyone who tried to rush in for the goods.","The rest of the crew shifted into full gear, hauling as fast as they could.","They had brought four shopping carts from the Buy More supermarket, one for each bus. Beyond that, the younger men carried boxes and sacks in their arms and over their shoulders, running trip after trip, loading everything onto the buses.","There were too many people, and it was complete chaos.","Those who had been waiting for a long time swarmed forward to grab things the moment the unloading trucks merged into the fast lane.","By the time the convoy disappeared, many people had already broken into fights.","Not all who came were men, nor were they all young. All kinds of curses, shrieks, and even sobs rang out. The scene was utter pandemonium.","On the other side of the human wall of people tied with purple cloth strips, however, everything was orderly.","But that group had taken way too much of the supplies!","When the goods on the slow lane vanished at an alarming rate while the people behind the purple-cloth wall were still methodically hauling things away, those who had failed to grab anything finally lost their fear and tried to break through the human wall.","“You guys still have so much!”","“This was distributed by the government! Why should it all go to you!”","It was actually pitiful—their frustration was understandable.","So Li Jiangbing merely shouted as he shoved people back with hands as big as bear paws: “Step back! Step back! Didn’t you hear me! Keep pushing and I’ll get rough—”","But before he could finish, Nie Kuizhang had already kicked someone!","Su Yu had just picked up a cardboard box and turned her head just in time to see it—","Nie Kuizhang was tall and fat, a man of considerable bulk, and when he kicked out, that person flew backward and crashed several meters away, landing with a heavy thud.","Those who had been lurking, quietly planning to take advantage of the confusion to break through the human wall, all backed off. They realized these people with the purple cloth strips were not joking—they were a genuine organized group, seizing and occupying supplies.","A inexplicable despondency settled over the crowd. No one had time to figure out why they felt that way, but the feeling flooded over them nonetheless.","It was a sense of powerlessness.","In truth, Young Apartment wasn’t the only community that was organized.","But the other organized communities didn’t tie colored cloth strips around their arms and foreheads like Young Apartment did, making members instantly recognizable and preventing internal conflict.","Those other organized groups descended into chaos while grabbing supplies. After all, not every neighbor knew each other, and in the panic, who could tell whether someone was from your own community or a different one? Whoever came to grab got shoved around, and it escalated into fists, hair-pulling, and drawing weapons.","There was a lot of bloodshed.","Now, facing Young Apartment—organized, disciplined, everyone calm and unflustered—many people felt powerless.","How could an individual, or even a whole family, stand up against this many organized and able-bodied men and women?","How could anyone else get any supplies?","Su Yu held the box and watched for a few seconds.","Jiang Cheng stood right behind the human wall. Although the row of people in front were all tall and sturdy, that didn’t stop her from seeing everything.","She had positioned herself there precisely for crowd control, so she could respond quickly if anything happened.","But when Nie Kuizhang knocked the man down, Jiang Cheng didn’t react at all. She simply kept standing there.","Su Yu could only see her back, not her expression. But the fact that she didn’t move meant she believed Nie Kuizhang’s actions didn’t need to be stopped or corrected.","She thought it was the right call.","Su Yu paused only for those few seconds before turning back and carrying the box to the vehicle.","The supplies on the stretch of road that Young Apartment had cordoned off were massive. But this trip wasn’t calculated per person—it was a collective undertaking. The scavenging crew was grabbing supplies for the entire building’s residents.","In the minds of Young Apartment’s people, once things were divided equally after bringing them back, each person would actually get very little.","But in the eyes of outsiders, this group in purple cloth strips driving public buses had taken far too much.","Despicable.","One by one, private cars began to leave, and the roadside that had been as crowded as a vegetable market gradually fell into quiet.","The four large public buses also started to turn around.","By now, there were no traffic rules whatsoever. Though the traffic lights still cycled automatically, nobody obeyed them anymore. The buses drove straight up onto the sidewalks to make their turns, going against traffic.","On the road, their fleet merged once again with the one from Lucky Blessing Estates.","Li Jiangbing poked his head out the window: “Old Zhou! Old Zhou!”","Zhou Wang rolled down his car window, his head covered in blood.","Li Jiangbing: “How’d you get hurt?”","Zhou Wang said helplessly: “Too many people, too chaotic.”","Li Jiangbing grinned, then asked: “How’s the haul?”","Zhou Wang looked up at the towering bus. Through the windows, he could see stacks of cardboard boxes piled to the brim, with sacks pressed on top.","Envy rose in Zhou Wang’s heart. He replied: “Better than nothing, at least.”","Su Yu sat in the bus on the same side, up close, watching Li Jiangbing talk with Zhou Wang below in his small car.","She glanced ahead. Nie Kuizhang, because of his size, occupied a double seat all to himself—no one squeezed in next to him.","And in the row right in front of where Su Yu sat—barely an arm’s length away—sat Jiang Cheng and Song Jingshuo.","A strange thought suddenly crossed Su Yu’s mind.","She knew, of course, that Li Jiangbing was someone Jiang Cheng trusted deeply. Everyone in private conversations now said that among the core members of the interim committee, Jiang Cheng, Li Jiangbing, and Song Jingshuo formed an iron triangle.","People generally believed that Li Jiangbing and Jiang Cheng were like brothers, while Song Jingshuo and Jiang Cheng had probably already become a couple.","Nie Kuizhang was also a core member of the interim committee and a building manager, but he didn’t share that same close and special connection with Jiang Cheng.","Su Yu knew all of this.","But that strange thought still surfaced in her mind: Li Jiangbing and Nie Kuizhang were both, in terms of appearance, very intimidating people. Yet their personalities and conduct were completely different. If you set aside emotions and private relationships, set aside existing factions, and only considered the current environment and personal capability alone—who would Jiang Cheng value more?","Would it really be Li Jiangbing?"]},{"number":57,"title":"Chapter 57","paragraphs":["Jiang Cheng held Mo Li and nodded to Zhou Wang through the car window, watching Li Jiangbing lean his head out ahead of her to greet and chat with Zhou Wang.","She turned her head and saw Song Jingshuo lost in thought.","“What are you spacing out about?” Jiang Cheng asked.","Song Jingshuo snapped back to reality and let out a soft sigh.","Jiang Cheng: “What’s wrong?”","“Nothing,” Song Jingshuo said. “...Just reminded of those foreign disaster movies—when something goes down, every family stuffs luggage into their trunks and flees. It hit me somehow.”","Jiang Cheng understood what he was getting at. She said, “We have nowhere to run.”","Peng Ze and Su Yu were sitting in the row behind them and had overheard the conversation. Peng Ze chimed in: “I’ve never understood, though—in those movies, after the foreigners flee, what do they eat and drink?”","Su Yu joined in: “If it’s a regional disaster, you just escape to a place that isn’t affected. Like another city or something.”","But a zombie virus wasn’t regional. And they couldn’t just leave where they lived.","First of all, not every family had a private car. Because of their age demographic, the youth apartment complex had a lower car-ownership rate than the surrounding neighborhoods.","Second, fleeing the city meant going to the countryside. Sure, rural areas had lower population density and therefore fewer zombies. But heading to a strange place where you knew no one—how could you guarantee finding shelter? And where would a bunch of city folk who couldn’t tell scallions from wheat seedlings find food?","Even if you fled to somewhere completely uninhabited, those two problems of food and shelter still existed. Very few city dwellers had any real wilderness survival skills.","So “fleeing” wasn’t even an option worth considering.","Staying put, at least, meant having a roof over your head that could also keep the zombies out.","The property management staff worked diligently precisely because they were afraid of losing the youth apartment complex as a sanctuary, just like Liu Hongwang had.","Everyone clearly—or at least subconsciously—understood that there was nowhere to run.","So when Jiang Cheng called for action, and the provisional committee organized things, anything that benefited hunkering down and staying put was answered with unanimous enthusiasm and quickly mobilized.","But the more Song Jingshuo understood this, the heavier his heart felt.","The chaotic scene of people looting supplies on the street earlier kept flashing before his eyes. People being shoved, beaten, trampled, robbed.","Outside the youth apartment complex, “order” as a concept had already crumbled to this degree.","Song Jingshuo felt a weight in his chest. He genuinely wanted to escape all of this.","He turned his head and saw Jiang Cheng, cheeks rosy, eyes bright, looking right at him.","Clearly, she had slept well last night. Her energy was totally vibrant.","What was her deal?","Song Jingshuo had always wondered how she managed to maintain that state. He had a vague feeling that Jiang Cheng was completely unaffected by their current circumstances.","For Jiang Cheng, zombies flooding the streets and commuting to work by bus every day seemed to be no different.","Was that really the case?","Song Jingshuo’s lips moved. He really wanted to just ask Jiang Cheng directly.","Peng Ze’s head poked in from behind. “Can we open some boxes to see what’s inside?”","Jiang Cheng agreed: “Open two boxes and two sacks, see if the stuff is the same.”","Someone on the bus pulled out a small knife, cutting through the tape on the cardboard boxes and the straps on the sacks.","What was inside the boxes was pretty much the same as what was in the sacks—just a difference in size. Inside were rice, flour, milk powder, sausages, bagged pickled vegetables, and compressed biscuits.","Someone pulled out a compressed biscuit and examined it: “Whoa, this is military rations.”","Suddenly a bunch of people wanted to “try it.” Most had heard of compressed biscuits but never touched one, so they were curious.","The guy who called it “military rations” turned out to be a military enthusiast. He cracked the biscuit through the packaging first, then opened it and handed out a few crumbs to everyone.","Someone shouted, “Give more! Look at you being so stingy~”","“Idiot,” the guy said. “Eat too much and then drink water—it’ll burst your stomach! Compressed, get it? What does compressed mean? If it can be compressed, it can expand. I dare to give it, but do you dare to eat that much?”","That person backed off: “Fine.”","Everyone got a little piece, and the guy even squeezed through the gap between the stacked boxes and seats to hand some to Song Jingshuo and Jiang Cheng.","Everyone popped it into their mouths and tried it.","“Gross!”","“That’s seriously gross!”","It really was awful. Jiang Cheng held the biscuit softened in her saliva and struggled to swallow it.","The military enthusiast said, “Try drinking some water—you’ll see what I mean in a bit.”","He was right. After they drank some water, before the bus even made it back to the youth apartment complex, they learned their lesson.","That stuff really puffed up in your stomach.","“This is so uncomfortable,” Su Yu frowned, clutching her stomach.","She had brought plenty of rations that day, so she had eaten the compressed biscuit on a full stomach. Now the biscuit was expanding in her stomach, and the bloating was making her miserable.","Everyone was getting a taste of the power of compressed biscuits. They really did expand with water.","Jiang Cheng felt it too.","“This is a good thing,” she praised.","“Right!” The military enthusiast was delighted. “Jiang Cheng knows what’s good!”","By then it was close to three in the afternoon. The bus drove back to the youth apartment complex and split off from the Jixiang Jiayuan convoy near the point past Bought More.","Jixiang West Street was sealed off, so the bus couldn’t get through. The Jixiang Jiayuan vehicles had to take their own east gate, while the youth apartment complex buses took their own west gate—so they each went their separate ways.","Having witnessed the chaos of the supply-grabbing earlier, as the bus passed the intersection of Jixiang West Street, everyone looked through the windows at the “safe zone” formed by the two connected neighborhoods and couldn’t help but feel a deep sense of relief.","Many people were standing guard inside the west gate, with security guards constantly looking outward.","There were even more people in the courtyard, clustered in groups of three or five under the shade, chatting.","Suddenly, the guard at the gate shouted: “They’re back! They’re back!”","People hurriedly surged toward the west gate.","The west gate opened, and four large public buses slowly drove into the compound.","The residents lined the way, applauding. Through the windows, they could see the stacked boxes and sacks inside the buses. Clearly, the provisional committee had once again lived up to expectations—and done it beautifully.","Cheers broke out.","The authority of the provisional committee was reinforced once more.","The four public buses drove into the courtyard. These buses, from the moment Jiang Cheng came up with the idea of borrowing them, were never intended to be returned.","The buses stopped, the doors opened, and the scavenging team members got off first—they had woken up early and worked through the morning, their mission complete. Everything else was handed off to the people in the complex.","The bus was surrounded by residents, who said to the volunteers coming off: “Good work, good work!”","Some also asked: “So, went smoothly?”","The scavenging team volunteers replied: “No one dared to rob us, anyway.”","People clicked their tongues: “There were people robbing stuff?”","“You bet. People brawling until heads were cracked open, and trampling too. It was more chaotic than what happened at Bought More before.”","That was a pretty objective statement. When the youth apartment complex and Jixiang Jiayuan people had done their zero-cost grab at Bought More on Monday, it had been messy, with conflicts and shoving—but it hadn’t escalated to active violence like this.","“Yeah, that Zhou Wang from next door got his head split open—face covered in blood.”","“Who’s Zhou Wang again?”","“The guy who manages the Jixiang Jiayuan compound.”","“Oh, oh, it’s him!”","Those staying behind had their assignments ready too. As soon as the scavenging team volunteers got off the bus, others got on.","Volunteers pushing shopping carts lined up to receive the supplies. As soon as a cart was full, it was taken down to the underground garage.","These supplies were considered communal property. The youth apartment building wasn’t short on supplies yet, so everything had to be stored in one place.","The small warehouse under the first building of the property management office was nowhere near big enough.","The plan everyone came up with yesterday was to use the underground garage. The underground garage doubled as a civil defense facility, with several heavy steel doors that could withstand surface-level explosions.","Under normal conditions, these thick blast doors were left wide open, so all the spaces in the garage were connected.","However, the garage could also be divided into separate sections by closing some of the blast doors.","The chosen section had already been cleaned and disinfected by a crew organized in the morning while the scavenging team was out.","Zhao Yi was in charge of this. He had originally wanted to join the scavenging team, but Jiang Cheng had vetoed that. Now he was a very busy and important person, with lots of things in the compound depending on him. This task was also handed to him.","He followed closely behind Jiang Cheng, reporting: “We’re working with limited resources, so this is the best we can do for now.”","“We used burning alcohol to reduce the humidity in the air.”","“Some of the cardboard we collected earlier was burned into ash, and some was shredded into bits. We mixed the ash and bits together and spread them over the floor.”","“We cut the tops off some empty oil drums, making open containers, filled them with quicklime, and placed them in the corners.”","“We also made simple moisture-absorbing bags.”","Song Jingshuo stepped back to give Zhao Yi room to report to Jiang Cheng.","The core team members followed behind Jiang Cheng and Zhao Yi, listening as they went down to the underground garage and into the chosen section.","It was exactly as Zhao Yi had described.","The air was indeed dry, without the usual dampness underground.","In the corners by the walls, they could see cooking oil containers cut into open vessels filled with quicklime. Quicklime was too precious to waste on processing the trash accumulated at the clubhouse, but this space was for storing government-issued supplies, mostly food, and was even more important. Zhao Yi could only sparingly allocate some of it here.","When he mentioned the “simple moisture-absorbing bags,” everyone looked up and could see them.","Long iron wires stretched overhead, with socks hanging from them one by one.","“The socks were donated by everyone,” Zhao Yi said. “They’re filled with plant ash and shredded paper bits.”","“For safety reasons, we’ll need to come by regularly to ventilate the space and make sure moisture doesn’t build up.”","That wasn’t all—the cars originally parked in this section had all been moved out. Not only had the floor been covered with plant ash and shredded paper bits, but a row of shelving units had also appeared out of nowhere, neatly arranged.","“They were delivered before 9 a.m.,” Zhao Yi said. “Old Dong, that guy, he’s pretty reliable.”","“Old Dong” was Brother Dong, the supervisor at Maiduoduo.","Last night, at the emergency meeting of the provisional committee, the task of setting up the temporary warehouse had been given to Zhao Yi. He had pointed out that underground spaces were most prone to leaks, and that supplies should be stored off the ground rather than piled on the floor.","Someone quick-witted at the meeting had then suggested, “Maiduoduo has lots of shelving units.”","After the barter deal for medicine last time, Jiang Cheng had already exchanged phone numbers with Brother Dong, so they had each other’s contact information.","Jiang Cheng called Brother Dong directly and settled the shelving arrangement. That morning, Brother Dong and his crew had brought the shelving over using a forklift from their warehouse.","A man who got things done promptly, indeed.","Zhao Yi sighed: “We’re working with limited resources, so this is it for now. It basically meets the requirements—moisture-proof, pest-proof, no problem.”","Zhao Yi, this boy, was really handy to have around. Jiang Cheng had grown very fond of him. Whenever she spoke to him, she was especially gentle, like a spring breeze: “You’ve worked hard.”","The homebody, when nervous, always pushed up his glasses: “It’s my duty, my duty.”","One shopping cart after another carried down cardboard boxes and sacks, with people below receiving them and stacking them onto the shelves.","Everyone was busy at work.","Like worker ants in an ant colony, worker bees in a beehive.","Everything except what was set aside for Brother Dong and what was allotted as rewards for the volunteers was moved down to the underground garage.","Several strong men pushed together against the civil defense doors. The creaking of the bearings made one’s teeth ache.","With a heavy thud, the doors slammed shut."]},{"number":58,"title":"Chapter 58","paragraphs":["The originally open and connected space was cut off by a door, separating the supply storage area from the rest of the garage and turning it into an independent, sealed-off space.","Master Luo had long since become close with the engineering guys, getting along well with them. Everyone came up together and forcefully turned the ship's-wheel style locking mechanism, which let out a creaking, grinding sound, until a series of clicks rang out and the blast door was locked from the outside.","For safety's sake, they also wrapped a chain lock around the wheel and locked that too.","This way, to open the blast door, you first had to unlock the chain lock, and then at least two men were needed to turn the wheel with ease—one person alone would struggle considerably.","And you'd also need a key.","In short, once locked up, there was no need for a dedicated guard.","Jiang Cheng and the others went down into the underground garage, while the other scavenger team volunteers were still in the courtyard. A crowd of people surrounded them, asking all kinds of questions, curious about the situation at the supply drop point.","Su Yu was also surrounded by several girls, all of whom she'd gotten familiar with recently—the ones who chatted frequently in the group chat.","They crowded around Su Yu asking about everything, and Su Yu recounted what had happened at Wan'an Bridge: \"Jiang Cheng talked things over with the neighboring community, so we split up into two sides—avoided our own people fighting each other.\"","\"Our side looked organized and disciplined from the start, nobody dared to rush us.\"","\"They were grabbing stuff from each other.\"","\"Pretty rough over there.\"","Once she'd explained enough, the girls dispersed, and only two who were closer stayed behind to chat—one of them being He Tian.","Su Yu looked around and asked the two of them, \"None of you went down to the garage to help?\"","One of the other girls said, \"There are plenty of guys for that. Why go steal the heavy-lifting jobs?\"","Su Yu paused, then said, \"There are shopping carts...\"","It was just using shopping carts to push the supplies down—going down was a slope, and coming back up the cart was empty. It wasn't that tiring.","He Tian changed the subject, asking, \"What's in all those cardboard boxes?\"","Su Yu told them: \"Mostly rice and flour.\"","The content of the \"supplies\" disappointed the girls. Because over the past week, while they could eat their fill, it was only \"eat their fill.\" The vegetables and meat stockpiled in the fridge had run out in half a week.","Everyone had been living on \"staples plus pickles\" for a while now, and they were just about sick of it.","The other girl complained, \"How much longer do we have to eat like this?\"","Su Yu was about to say something, but He Tian tapped the back of her hand, and Su Yu held it in.","Once the other girl walked off, He Tian said, \"It's impressive how you guys step up and join every operation.\"","\"You guys\" referred to the girls who'd joined the scavenger team along with Su Yu. Out of the four public buses, nine girls had gone in total.","\"Zhang Lesi and Xue Yiqing also applied to be scavenger volunteers,\" He Tian said. \"But their building leaders said there were enough people and didn't let them go.\"","He Tian hadn't applied at all.","Because her building leader was Nie Kuizhang.","After he'd harassed her, he'd only been punished with an apology and had half his medication confiscated—he was still the building leader of Building 3.","All activities that the residents of Building 3 signed up for had to go through him.","Last night, He Tian had messaged Su Yu privately: 【I'm not signing up for any more operations from now on, unless I can sign up directly with Jiang Cheng's side.】","But as things stood, there was no chance. Because all operations were assigned down to each building and organized by the building leaders.","He Tian could only avoid Nie Kuizhang by not participating in any operations at all.","【So annoying,】He Tian had said. 【And I can't move out either.】","That had all been their private chat before bed last night.","Otherwise, He Tian wouldn't have skipped the scavenger team today. The reason she and Su Yu had become friends so quickly was that they had similar personalities and shared the same values.","He Tian said, \"I've got no right to tell them they have to go do labor. Because I didn't sign up myself, I've got no standing. Someone would definitely call me out on it.\"","Su Yu didn't agree with what the other girl had said earlier, and her attitude—He Tian could tell.","He Tian tried to comfort Su Yu: \"Right now we've got more people than we know what to do with. The last thing this community is short on is manpower.\"","What she said wasn't wrong.","But it didn't make Su Yu feel any better.","He Tian knew what she was worried about. Her own experience had shown her that if there weren't a few women on the interim committee, it really wouldn't work. All men—that really didn't work.","After the Nie Kuizhang incident, Su Yu had shared everything Jiang Cheng said with the girls in the group. But it was obvious that everyone understood and accepted it differently—and the direction of their thinking even differed.","\"Anyway, you just stay on the committee,\" He Tian said. \"Having you on the committee makes me feel at ease.\"","She turned around and used the Nie Kuizhang situation to reassure Su Yu: \"Even though we're not entirely satisfied, it's not like he got off scot-free. No matter what, at the end of the day this is still a society ruled by law... well, more or less, I guess.\"","\"I think it's awesome that you can think about how we women, as a minority group, could lose our rights. But don't worry too much.\"","\"You seem a bit too wound up.\"","But that wasn't originally Su Yu's idea—it had actually been Jiang Cheng who first raised it to warn Su Yu.","In that moment, Su Yu felt that the only person who could truly understand her anxiety was probably Jiang Cheng.","But the Jiang Cheng of now seemed different from the person who, on Sunday night, had warned her not to lose her rights or get pushed to the margins.","But even if she said it out loud, nobody would believe her, would they?","Brother Dong from the Buy More store arrived with his people.","Brother Dong and his crew hadn't gone to the Fifth Ring Road—first, because they had supplies hidden in their dorm and weren't that hard up at the moment, and second, because their problem was they didn't have a vehicle.","Without a car, going on foot from the development zone to the Fifth Ring Road—imagine how many zombies you'd have to fight through on the way, and whether you'd even make it back alive was a real question.","Not having a car was a huge disadvantage.","When Brother Dong saw the news, he started cursing. He immediately realized that the owners of Jixiang Jiayuan, the Youth Apartments, and the surrounding communities would definitely drive there. But what about those of them without cars?","Then he got a call from Jiang Cheng, asking for shelving racks.","He never expected shelving racks to become trade goods. But he immediately understood what Jiang Cheng needed them for.","He was envious, but there was nothing he could do—while the shelf trade was still on, he might as well exchange them for something from Jiang Cheng.","He didn't dare go home now either—stocking up as much as he could, little by little.","Jiang Cheng gave Brother Dong two cardboard boxes and one sack.","Li Jiangbing made a point of warning them: \"With the compressed biscuits, you can only eat a little bit at a time. Once those things hit your stomach and meet water, they expand—and they expand like crazy, bloating your gut.\"","Brother Dong laughed. \"I know. My little brother was in the military; he gave me some before.\"","He untied the sack and took a look—all basic survival supplies. He sighed, \"When is this life going to end?\"","The joy everyone had felt about gaining more supplies was silenced by that one sentence.","Brother Dong and his people loaded the stuff into shopping carts, and before they left, they looked at the four public buses parked in the community, full of admiration: \"Why didn't I think of that.\"","There were plenty of cars on the streets, some of them even with doors open and keys in the ignition.","It was just that people's minds were still bound by the law.","Law-abiding citizens—that's how they were.","As for the issue of \"how residents without cars can obtain supplies,\" the authorities actually weren't unaware of it.","Vice Mayor Zheng had expended tremendous effort to gather those supplies, and he spent the entire night coordinating vehicles and personnel. Since the supply convoy departed on Sunday, he had not left the monitoring command center.","His eyes were shot through with bloodshot veins.","Seeing the bloody brawls and stampedes that broke out as people fought over the supplies, he closed his eyes in grief.","Society had enjoyed a long era of peace, and people had lived in prosperity. Who would have thought that one day there would be scenes like this, people fighting over rice and grain?","But Vice Mayor Zheng had truly done everything he could.","The fact that many households did not own private cars—that had occurred to him from the very beginning, but there was simply no solution.","The only option was to deliver the supplies to residents first, then hope that redistribution and circulation could happen among the residents themselves. As for how that “distribution and circulation” would be carried out and what price would be paid, that was beyond anyone’s control.","Vice Mayor Zheng felt tormented.","But he could not hide. He had been placed in this position, and he had to face it all head-on.","His gaze swept across one screen after another, then suddenly snapped back.","On one screen, a group of people was clearly moving in an organized, disciplined manner. Similar situations were not uncommon—several residential compounds showed obvious signs of organization.","But this group had formed a human wall to block others and monopolized a stretch of supplies along the road. What caught Vice Mayor Zheng’s attention was a young woman standing with her arms crossed behind that human wall.","In front of her stood the wall of people; behind her, her companions worked busily, moving supplies like worker bees.","She stood there, clearly managing the scene.","A woman in control of a group—rare, but not unprecedented.","It was precisely because he had seen this before that Vice Mayor Zheng found her familiar.","“Zoom in on that,” he said.","Once magnified, even his secretary recognized her: “Oh—it’s that young woman from the Youth Apartment.”","Vice Mayor Zheng nodded. “Indeed, the Youth Apartment.”","Vice Mayor Zheng could not say whether he wanted more people like Jiang Cheng or fewer.","If there were more people like her, capable of organizing others, the chance of individual residents facing the zombie plague alone and dying would be lower. The Youth Apartment and the Jixiang Jiayuan community joining together to seal off connecting roads and form one continuous safe zone was a typical positive example.","But when the enemy was no longer zombies but “other people,” the situation changed.","Those unorganized individuals appeared especially vulnerable in the face of organized groups.","And human hearts naturally lean toward sympathizing with the weak.","Sure enough, his secretary frowned. “Based on our surveillance, the Youth Apartment has already emptied out the nearby Buiduo supermarket. They should not be short on supplies...”","In a time of uncertain road ahead and pervasive confusion, wanting to grab a little more and hoard a little more is only human nature.","But that directly clashed with the higher-ups’ hope that supplies would be spread as widely as possible to as many people as possible.","Vice Mayor Zheng stared at the young woman on the screen, his emotions equally complicated.","Jiang Cheng had no idea she was being watched from afar. She had turned on the public broadcast and was addressing all residents of the compound:","【The supplies acquired this time are collectively owned by the community.】","【But we must not let this acquisition lull us into complacency. Quite the opposite—when the rescue we hoped for turns into scavenging supplies, it only proves that the situation is worse than we imagined.】","【We must absolutely put an end to wasting food. As everyone has noticed over these past few days, with very few supplemental foods available, the consumption rate of staple foods is faster than we expected. In other words, the food each of you holds in your own hands is not as long-lasting as you might think.】","【Community supplies are to be used only for emergencies. Under normal circumstances, circulation of supplies among individuals is encouraged.】","【No opening of the stores unless absolutely necessary.】","The evening news announcement had now become a must-watch for everyone in S City.","In Sunday evening’s announcement, some footage was shown of civilians picking up supplies—basically only those few minutes when the supplies first hit the ground and people rushed forward to grab them.","What came after was never broadcast. Anyone who had participated in the scavenging teams knew that afterward, fights broke out, and the scenes turned ugly.","But at least the footage that was shown was still inspiring, conveying the message that “supplies have reached the hands of the people.”","For those still living within the Fourth Ring Road, the Third Ring, the Second Ring, and the First Ring, it added fuel to the nearly extinguished flame of hope.","The latest news was that the supply convoy would push forward to the Fourth Ring Road on Monday and deliver supplies there, just like today.","Everyone knew that the Fourth Ring was manageable, but starting from the Third Ring, the difficulty would escalate sharply.","Because the Fourth and Fifth Ring Roads had been built later—fully enclosed roads with wide open spaces. On both sides of the Fifth Ring Road, there were already wild tracts, and places like Wan’an Bridge were surrounded by corporate offices and industrial parks. As for the Fourth Ring, there were many office buildings and high-rises. At that time on Saturday night, most of these places were closed and relatively sparsely populated, meaning fewer mutated zombies.","But starting from the Third Ring, it was all old roads built in earlier years. The roads ran close to buildings on either side, and there were many residential areas and commercial districts. On certain stretches of the Third Ring Road, on weekend nights at nine or ten o’clock, there would even be traffic jams.","The Second Ring was much the same.","The First Ring was another story entirely—inside it lay the old city. The so-called First Ring Road was just the circular road surrounding the ancient city walls.","The Youth Apartment, located in the new tech district, was even a bit of a drive beyond the Fifth Ring Road, and the zombie situation there was already this severe.","It was unimaginable what it was like inside the Third Ring Road.","【This is an unprecedented time of hardship, and the nation and its people are bearing this heavy trial together.】","【The first batch of rescue supplies reached only some of our compatriots. For those who did not receive supplies and are hiding at home enduring hunger—your anxiety and longing, we feel with you.】","【Faced with the limits of human strength, I sincerely plead and call upon all of you: in this darkest hour, let the ancient traditional virtue of our nation and people, that of mutual aid and assistance, become the faint light that pierces the darkness. If you have surplus food at home, please extend a helping hand to those around you in need.】","【A single act of sharing, a single spark of selflessness, can gather into a formidable force.】","【Your kindness is, at this very moment, the most precious rescue supply—the backbone that upholds life and hope.】","Jiang Cheng listened with her arms crossed as Deputy Mayor Zheng gave his speech on television.","And yet, that very morning, people had been beating each other bloody, cracking skulls open, fighting over supplies."]},{"number":59,"title":"Chapter 59","paragraphs":["Although the interim committee had said these supplies were for emergencies and the warehouse shouldn't be opened unless absolutely necessary, as long as that stock of goods was sitting there, everyone felt a deep sense of security.","The next day was Monday again—no work, no need to get up early.","Most people were still asleep when the folks from BuyMore Supermarket showed up again.","But this time, Brother Dong wasn't among them.","Because Brother Dong... he'd run off.","The Youth Apartments had a busy morning ahead. Not everything from yesterday had been moved into storage; a portion had been held back.","These days, the Youth Apartments gave volunteers a cut of the goods after every group outing. Since these outings carried real risk, everyone—including those who didn't participate—agreed it was fair compensation.","So in the morning, they were tallying accounts and divvying up supplies.","That's when the BuyMore group barged in, asking directly for Jiang Cheng. They all knew who he was by now.","Jiang Cheng called together the core members of the interim committee to meet with them.","After listening to the BuyMore folks' profanity-laced account, the committee members were speechless.","—Brother Dong had actually run off.","Not only did he run, but he'd taken supplies with him!","\"He said you shouldn't put all your eggs in one basket,\" one of them explained. \"He claimed someone might break into our dorm to steal stuff, so we ought to stash some goods elsewhere.\"","Brother Dong's reasoning wasn't entirely wrong—a few people had already sniffed around their dorm in recent days, but they'd been driven off.","With a dozen or so of them camped out in the supermarket dorm around the clock, only an idiot wouldn't figure out they were hoarding supplies.","\"So he found a car on the street and told us to stash the stuff we'd brought back from your place yesterday in the trunk. The keys were still in the ignition—the owner probably turned into a zombie and got killed by you guys.\"","\"Then that night, he grabbed more rice and canned goods from the dorm, loaded up a shopping cart, and said he was putting those in the car too for safekeeping. And then... he never came back.\"","\"We thought something bad had happened to him, so we went out looking—and that's when we realized he'd taken off!\"","Brother Dong was a native of the suburbs. He owned a place in the city, but he also had a family home with a yard out in the countryside.","When the virus hit, his wife had taken the kids to visit the grandparents—luckily for them, not a single one of the five family members had turned. He, however, had been trapped in the city.","The rural outskirts had a much lower population density. He'd talked to his family by phone—zombies were far fewer out there, and his family not only had grain stored, but land to grow more. They even had vegetables planted in the yard.","The perfect refuge.","The only reason Brother Dong had been stuck at BuyMore Supermarket was his mode of transport: a motorcycle. He'd been lucky to make it from home to the supermarket alive, and he wasn't about to risk venturing out again.","Until yesterday, when he saw those big public buses that Jiang Cheng had commandeered outside the Youth Apartments. It suddenly hit him—he could just drive any of the abandoned cars on the street.","Who was going to stop him? Nobody was in charge anymore.","As for his coworkers... what about them? They were just people he happened to work with.","If this crisis blew over like past earthquakes or floods, fine—he could always find a new job afterward.","The moment Brother Dong realized he could \"commandeer\" an abandoned vehicle, he was gone.","And he'd helped himself to supplies on the way out.","The BuyMore people were livid, cursing up a storm!","Jiang Cheng asked, \"So what exactly do you want from us?\"","The group that had been hurling curses suddenly went quiet. They shut their mouths, looking at each other, then at him.","Jiang Cheng wasn’t in any hurry either. They’d gone out of their way to come here, so they had to want something, and whoever wants something is the one who’s anxious.","In the end, a dozen-odd people pushed one of their number forward—a stocky, sturdy man.","The man scratched his face and spoke on behalf of the whole group: “We... want to throw in with you folks.”","The moment those words left his mouth, several core members of the interim committee let out a puzzled “Huh?”","The man explained: “You guys lost quite a few people too, so you must have a lot of empty houses. Our place is actually pretty unsafe—there are still zombies wandering on the upper floors, and the ones outside sometimes sneak in. We can’t sleep easy. We were thinking, could we maybe move into your compound as well, and look out for each other?”","Jiang Cheng said: “We can offer shelter, a sealed-off safe community, and the benefits of group coordination. What can you offer?”","The dozen-some Maiduoduo employees exchanged glances.","An older woman cut in, sounding anxious: “We’re all capable of hard work. We can work—we can do anything!”","There were thirteen of them in total, including five women.","But male or female, they all genuinely looked like people who could work hard. People who do physical labor for a living have a look about them that conveys toughness and endurance.","Jiang Cheng turned and exchanged glances with a few of the others—she didn’t make every decision unilaterally. Quite the opposite: on many practical details, she was very willing to listen to other people’s opinions and suggestions, and she actively sought them out.","The core seven of the interim committee—Jiang Cheng, six building heads, and even Nie Kuizhang, who’d made mistakes before—had developed a working rhythm over the past week.","Her gaze met theirs briefly, and they reached a consensus.","“What kind of work did you all do?” she asked.","Mostly they were stock clerks and cleaners. The man in the lead was a maintenance worker. When asked what he could fix, he said: “Everything. Pipes, wiring, shelves... wherever something breaks, that’s my job. A supermarket that big has me running around all day.”","So he was a jack-of-all-trades.","Jiang Cheng had already formed an idea in her mind.","“You’re not property owners, so we can’t give you the same treatment as the owners,” she said. “But the interim committee can hire you as property staff.”","“We can provide you with housing, but you’ll have to follow the interim committee’s arrangements like the other property staff and provide services to the owners.”","A shortage of property staff was a major problem in the compound right now.","Things like fixing electrical circuits were relatively easy—volunteers could be found. That was vocational-school or trade-school level work, and the compound was full of engineering-minded guys; it was like using a sledgehammer to crack a nut.","But no one wanted to clean other people’s toilets or drains, or handle the compound’s garbage collection.","When the property staff couldn’t keep up, complaints piled up. When no volunteers stepped forward, the work had to be assigned by rotation. Those who got stuck with it weren’t happy either.","But if they didn’t do it that way, Master Luo would be worked to death.","The thirteen Maiduoduo people were actually just what they needed.","“Fine, fine, fine—we can do it!” The Maiduoduo folks nodded immediately.","People used to working aren’t afraid of work.","But people who can endure hardship and stay at the very bottom for a long time are often not the sharpest tools in the shed. Anyone with a bit more brains, like Brother Dong, would have worked his way up to a junior supervisor position by now.","During this period, everything they did and how they did it had been dictated by Brother Dong.","Brother Dong had abandoned them and run off, leaving them without a leader.","Fortunately, there were no zombies on the supermarket floor, but there were still some on the upper floors of the building. However, with so few people, starting from Brother Dong, no one wanted to take risks—they were all very protective of their own lives. So they had held the supermarket and the dormitory as their base, but never dealt with the upper floors of the building.","Moreover, this sort of building had too many entrances and exits. Occasionally, a zombie would wander in by mistake, which made everyone feel uneasy.","Yesterday, everyone discovered that Brother Dong had fled. They discussed it half the night and finally came up with a plan: “Why don’t we go to the Youth Apartment?”","The Youth Apartment was the safest and most reliable place in the area.","If they could stay inside that gated community, they'd be safe too.","Jiang Cheng nodded: “You have to bring your own food supplies. Old Dong couldn’t possibly have moved that much stuff by himself, right? I’m requiring each of you to bring at least five bags of rice. Anyone bringing less won’t be accepted.”","One bag of rice weighs 5 kg. People doing physical labor tend to eat more than others—let’s say about 450 grams per day. Five bags of rice would barely last them less than two months.","Food was now an extremely sensitive resource. People were spilling blood over it on the Fifth Ring Road.","Even if the Youth Apartment needed laborers, it couldn't hand out food for free.","Letting them into the Youth Apartment’s safe zone itself was the payment for their labor.","All the people from BuyDuoDuo stayed silent, all looking at the man they had chosen as their representative.","This man didn't speak either. He looked up at the sky with his eyes, used his right hand to count the fingers on his left hand, and his lips were moving slightly.","Jiang Cheng knew: he was calculating the amount of their supplies.","Sure enough, a few seconds later, he let out a sigh of relief and said, “Alright, that works. It’s enough.”","Jiang Cheng said: “Whatever else you've hidden, just bring it all over now that you're all here.”","The man thought for a moment, then nodded: “True enough.”","But he did ask: “Could you send a few people to help us? We have quite a lot of stuff.”","Jiang Cheng smiled. In the current situation, they weren't afraid of you having too many hidden supplies—what they feared was people with nothing to eat and dying of hunger.","Handling outside tasks was always Li Jiangbing’s job. He called over a bunch of people who had nothing better to do and were about to grow mold, and they all pushed shopping carts and went along with a clatter.","Jiang Cheng found Master Luo and told him: “I got you thirteen new workers.”","After hearing the whole story, Master Luo sighed: “This Brother Dong, he’s not an honest man.”","Master Luo was very glad to have more hands. He knew all the BuyDuoDuo folks—one look told him they were all capable of hard work. With thirteen more laborers, the pressure on his side had eased quite a bit.","Master Luo asked: “Are we going to let them stay in our dormitory? We don't have that many beds left—only five are free.”","Jiang Cheng said: “No need. There are a lot of empty units in the complex. Let's just requisition them.”","So many owners had died, and most of them had lived alone, so naturally their apartments were vacant now—like the unit next door to hers on floor 0308, the one that belonged to Little White's Dad.","Which rooms in which buildings were empty had already been compiled during group building sweep a week ago the Sunday before last.","Master Luo hesitated as if he wanted to say something.","Jiang Cheng, without needing him to explain, already knew and brought it up proactively: “While we're at it, let's also find better accommodations for our current maintenance staff. No matter when this zombie business ends, at least for now we should let everyone live more comfortably. No more cramming in the dorms.”","Master Luo's wife cooked for the property management staff. She shared a room with Yang Xinyan and two female cleaners, while the other male staff members slept together in a group dormitory with bunk beds.","The couple was separated.","Master Luo cheered up: \"Great, let's stay in a nice place for a change.\"","Jiang Cheng arranged things directly: \"You two can stay next door to me, so it's convenient to get in touch if anything comes up. Jiangbing will also be on the same floor as me.\"","Being able to stay close to two key members of the interim committee at once, Master Luo was more than happy: \"Sure!\"","Jiang Cheng said, \"We'll just need to clean it up a bit.\"","Master Luo replied, \"What's there to worry about.\"","Jiang Cheng called Li Jiangbing: \"I talked with Master Luo. We're moving the property staff into the empty apartments too, to improve everyone's living conditions. Grab some bedding and bring it back for everyone.\"","Li Jiangbing replied on the other end: \"What a coincidence, we're already grabbing some.\"","As the saying goes, a thief never comes back empty-handed. Since it wasn't safe to go alone outside the safe zone, anyone who made the trip had to go in a group.","Since they were already there, why go back empty?","So when Li Jiangbing called for people, a whole crowd came flooding in. Everyone figured they'd grab some extra stuff while they were at it.","Since the Maiduoduo people had already pledged to join the youth apartment, they stopped hiding things and brought out everything they'd stashed.","Rice, flour, canned meat... they really had hidden a lot of stuff.","Good thing Li Jiangbing had brought plenty of people and vehicles.","The remaining supplies in the supermarket were no longer survival necessities—like bedding, woks, and microwaves—but they were still daily necessities.","Some people needed them, and some just wanted to take advantage, but either way, they grabbed everything they could carry, hauled everything they could haul.","People even thought the shopping carts weren't big enough, so they pulled out the supermarket's flatbed carts too, and even those weren't enough.","The man who could speak up for his colleagues was surnamed Guo, named Guo Jun, an all-around repairman who claimed he could fix anything.","Guo Jun couldn't help but twitch at the corners of his mouth at the sight of this locust-swarm mentality.","But from now on, they were part of the youth apartment too, and the more they took, the better it would be for all of them.","Guo Jun planted his hands on his hips: \"Forget the flatbed carts. If you pile too much on those, you won't be able to pull them at all, and it's a long way back.\"","Li Jiangbing asked, \"Then what do we do?\"","Everyone had a nagging feeling that the current situation might last who knows how long, and they all wanted to stockpile as much as possible.","Guo Jun said, \"Wait here. I'll bring out the forklift.\""]},{"number":60,"title":"Chapter 60","paragraphs":["When the Youth Apartments and Lucky Gardens originally blocked off both ends of Lucky West Street with parked cars along the curb to join the two communities into one continuous safe zone, they made a point of leaving a compact hatchback near the Buyduoduo supermarket side.","That car was so small that Li Jiangbing could lift half the body by himself alone.","Placing that one small car among all the big vehicles was deliberate—easy to move when needed, effectively a movable access point.","No collective action by the Youth Apartments ever escaped the notice of Lucky Gardens.","Residents in the western-facing units of Lucky Gardens' western buildings could simply look out their windows and see exactly what was happening on Lucky West Street.","The rumbling clatter of dozens of shopping cart wheels couldn't possibly fail to alert the people of Lucky Gardens.","\"Youth Apartments folks are off to scavenge Buyduoduo again?\" people in Lucky Gardens muttered sourly.","Guo Jun had mobilized two forklifts. They were tiny things, looking like oversized toys, but they could carry serious weight.","Boxes stacked neatly higher than the cabs, and the two forklifts led the way.","Two forklifts, dozens of shopping carts, all heading into Lucky West Street.","Once the final cart was in, everyone worked together to push the hatchback back into place, sealing off Lucky West Street again.","They'd made a decent racket on the way out, but they made an even bigger one on the way back. People from Lucky Gardens had already come downstairs to watch the show.","When they saw the two forklifts, jaws dropped.","Once it sank in, the sourness returned: \"This is just excessive.\"","The reason for all the envy was simple—without an organized group, just one or two individuals, nobody dared leave the safe zone.","As for Lucky Gardens, they weren't at the point of starvation overall. For households in dire straits, Zhou Wang from the neighborhood committee would figure out some internal coordination for relief.","Generally, Lucky Gardens rarely organized nonessential trips outside. The latest necessary one was yesterday's run to the Fifth Ring Road for supplies, during which several people came back bloodied, though they'd managed to grab a fair amount.","But having enough overall supplies didn't mean everyone's personal needs were met. So watching the Youth Apartments rally a group of dozens time and again to raid Buyduoduo and the nearby shops stirred up all kinds of envy and resentment.","Trying to form a team in Lucky Gardens was tough—only Zhou Wang could really pull it off.","What was even left in Buyduoduo? Essential survival items like rice and flour were long gone. What remained was everyday living goods.","Look at that—the Youth Apartments folks still had a life to live.","The east gate of the Youth Apartments opened, and even the security guard was stunned: \"Damn!\"","Jiang Cheng had brought back four full-size buses; Li Jiangbing had scored two forklifts.","Jiang Cheng's four buses clearly weren't going back. Those two forklifts probably weren't either.","Once they entered the gates of the Youth Apartments, there was no way they were going back.","New joint property acquired: Forklifts x2.","Per building regulations, each returning member was checked to ensure no visible wounds before being allowed in.","A crowd had gathered inside the compound to gawk: \"What did you bring back? So much stuff.\"","Li Jiangbing: \"Eh, grabbed whatever we saw.\"","He'd originally wanted to snag two sets of new bedding for himself, but then Jiang Cheng happened to call and asked him to get bedding too—that cracked him up. He just started hauling whole boxes straight from the warehouse.","Figured it was stuff everyone could use.","Jiang Cheng, meanwhile, had already arranged housing for the thirteen new people.","\"Two per room,\" she said. \"Find rooms with double beds so they can actually fit.\"","In reality, the Youth Apartments currently had over a hundred unclaimed units sitting vacant—enough to give every property staff member their own room.","When Jiang Cheng suggested two per room, several of the core members were baffled.","\"Why though?\" someone blurted out. \"Aren't there plenty of empty rooms?\"","Jiang Cheng didn't answer right away; she glanced at Song Jingshuo first.","She didn't expect everyone to grasp her reasoning immediately, but she did hold some hope for Song Jingshuo.","And Song Jingshuo didn't disappoint—he understood. But understanding wasn't the same as accepting.","In fact, Song Jingshuo couldn't even form a complete sentence at first. His knee-jerk reaction was: \"You... oh, come on.\"","That's fine. The fact that he understood was enough for Jiang Cheng.","She could make plenty of decisions on her own, but after all, humans are social creatures. She wanted at least one person who could keep up with her thinking, share a common language, and communicate as an equal.","\"They're ultimately not property owners,\" she said. \"We need to remind them of that every step of the way. We can't have another Liu Hongwang on our hands.\"","Liu Hongwang—everyone remembered him. A cleaning staff member expelled from the Youth Apartments by Jiang Cheng.","He'd led a strike and started a disturbance, demanding the same treatment as the property owners.","So putting the property staff and the newcomers from Buyduoduo two to a room wasn't about logistics—it was a tactic: a way to suppress and to remind.","Make sure people clearly remember their place and know what they're supposed to do.","As it dawned on everyone what Jiang Cheng's arrangement meant, they also understood the words Song Jingshuo had swallowed.","The men all felt the weight of it.","Seeing that everyone now got it, Song Jingshuo could no longer hold back his half-spoken remark. He let it out with a heavy sigh: \"Jiang Cheng... you really are a born capitalist.\"","Every man present was someone who could steel his heart to swing a fist or a weapon and seize supplies from others—no soft-hearted types here.","But every one of them, including Song Jingshuo, who was the archetypal elite professional, were workers at heart. They simply didn't have that capitalist mindset. Taking supplies was one thing—that was another matter entirely. But in terms of human relations, yes, there was a division of labor and different incomes, but the core principle was that people were equal.","But Jiang Cheng...","After Song Jingshuo said that, Jiang Cheng felt something flash through her mind.","She couldn't catch it.","Every so often, bits and pieces of information from the broken barrier tended to leak through—fragments from before her transmigration. She occasionally caught one or two phrases, but most flashed by, leaving her confused.","Jiang Cheng reined in her focus and said, \"I thank you all for trusting me with the responsibility of making decisions for our community.\"","\"I can't afford to play the saint.\"","\"I hope none of you will, either.\"","\"Of course, of course!\"","\"You kill the saint first in times of chaos!\"—everyone chimed in with their approval.","Song Jingshuo let out a long breath and clarified: \"I was just venting. Honestly, with you like this, we feel even more at ease.\"","Everyone could see by now that any competition between Song Jingshuo and Jiang Cheng was long gone.","To be fair, Song Jingshuo wasn't bad either.","But everyone weighed it internally: if Song Jingshuo were the one calling the shots, each of them couldn't help feeling, \"I could do that too.\"","But when it was Jiang Cheng occupying that role, no one had that thought.","Better stick with Jiang Cheng.","The exact count of vacant units was known only to the neighborhood committee. Even Master Luo wasn't fully in the loop. The property staff hadn't participated in the door-to-door sweep last week.","None of the thirteen people that Guo Jun had brought over would have known that either. The youth apartment arranged for them to stay two per room, and they were quite pleased about it.","The dormitory at Buy Duoduo was just like the property management dormitory at the youth apartment—both had bunk beds with metal frames, where twenty or thirty people could sleep in one small room.","Now they were swapping that for a two-person apartment with its own bathroom and kitchen. The living conditions had jumped up several notches.","There was nothing to complain about.","The supplies they had brought weren't insignificant. The interim committee didn't dock them either: \"Your things are yours to divide up as you see fit.\"","The dozen or so people split the supplies evenly and each carried their share into their new \"dorm.\" Comparatively, each of them had a few extra bags of staple grains than most of the property owners, so they could hold out much longer.","Brother Dong had heard that yet another cartload of supplies had been wheedled away. His family supposedly had a courtyard home in a village on the outskirts of town, and given the current situation, that really did sound like the ideal refuge.","Most everyone here was from the city, and at that moment, they envied the countryside.","Master Luo's group had no complaints either.","The terms Jiang Cheng offered the property staff were identical to those given to Guo Jun and his people—two per room.","Everyone was happy about that, especially Master Luo and his wife, and Yang Xinyan.","Master Luo and his wife could finally share a room, right next door to Jiang Cheng in room 0308.","With two per room, of course people paired up freely, each choosing whoever they got along with best.","At Buy Duoduo, there was one extra woman, and on the property side, there was also one extra woman: Yang Xinyan. Because the older aunties paired off with each other, she ended up left on her own.","Yang Xinyan thought she'd have to share with some middle-aged woman from Buy Duoduo she didn't even know, but Jiang Cheng glanced over and gave her a private room instead.","Yang Xinyan was sharp. She didn't say a word or make a fuss—just shot Jiang Cheng a grin, showing her teeth, and happily moved her things.","Master Luo and his wife moved into Building 2, room 0308.","Little White had been bitten to death by his own father. The room was a horrible mess at the time. Later, when the bodies were cleaned up, Little White's remains were taken to the square and burned along with the rest. The bloodstains and scraps left behind in the room had since dried out.","It was pretty filthy, honestly.","But next door, 0306, was Jiang Cheng, and 0320 on the same floor was Li Jiangbing. Master Luo was old enough to see things clearly. When Jiang Cheng offered to put him next door, he agreed readily.","The couple were both hardworking people. Within less than an hour, they'd scrubbed and cleaned the place into shape.","\"This bed's really nice. Comfortable,\" said Master Luo's wife, sitting on the foot of the bed and pressing down on it hard.","Her surname was Pan, and everyone called her Aunt Pan.","She tried the sofa too. The sofa was comfortable as well.","Opening the wardrobe, she was pleasantly surprised: \"Quite a few clothes in here.\"","She pulled one out and held it up to compare: \"Whoever lived here was pretty big-built. These would fit you.\"","Master Luo tried to stop her: \"Doesn't feel right to touch other people's things.\"","Aunt Pan said, \"When a person dies, everything's gone. They gave us this house to live in.\"","\"Once this whole mess is over, we'll be moving out anyway.\"","\"Then when we leave, we'll leave them behind. We'll wash them, put them back, and not take anything. That's settled.\"","\"I'd been planning to go to that wholesale market in Yue Village that Sunday to buy you a couple of new shirts, but then the zombies showed up,\" Aunt Pan sighed. \"Don't be so particular. Wear what's there.\"","\"The dead are dead. Their family might not even be alive anymore.\"","\"Put them on, put them on. Yours are so worn out they're nearly see-through. People will laugh at you.\"","In the end, Master Luo took off his work vest and his old clothes, and put on the clothes that belonged to the original occupant of 0308.","The quality of those clothes was much better than anything from the wholesale market—nice cut, proper shape.","\"Hey, you actually look stylish now,\" Aunt Pan said happily."]},{"number":61,"title":"Chapter 61","paragraphs":["Monday brought new labor to the Monday Youth Apartment, and the living conditions of the property staff improved. Everyone currently had ample food, and order was maintained throughout the neighborhood, filled with a sense of calm.","But this day turned out to be the hardest one yet since the S City Temporary Emergency Command Center was established.","According to plan, today the supply convoy was to break through from the ring-road connector routes to the Fourth Ring Road.","In truth, things were fine on the main thoroughfares because at that time on Saturday night, there weren't that many vehicles or people on the main roads. Some zombies were simply sent flying by the armored vehicles, and the supply trucks rumbled right over them.","The zombies on the main roads were basically all original zombies—slow-moving and uncoordinated, no match for steel machinery.","The supply convoy advanced smoothly onto the Fourth Ring Road.","But there was a stadium off the Fourth Ring Road, and no one had thought to remember that there had been a concert there that Saturday night. Those who knew were either dead, or after a week had passed, simply couldn't recall.","If fully packed, that stadium could hold sixty thousand people.","Even if it wasn't sold out, an estimated forty to fifty thousand had been there.","When the supply convoy rolled over the original zombies and pushed this far, a staggering number of second-generation zombies, roused by the noise, surged in like a tide.","Second-generation zombies were far stronger and faster than the originals, and in broad daylight with plenty of sun, their vision was perfectly fine.","Most critically, there were just too many of them!","No one had ever seen this many second-generation zombies!","The first echelon, leading the way at the front, was the one that ran into this swarm that looked like a colony of ants.","Because it was the spearhead clearing the path, the first echelon had a full ten armored vehicles. Its armed personnel were also double that of the vehicles behind.","But the second-generation zombies were just too numerous!","While the original zombies were still shambling along, the second-generation zombies were already bearing down like a beast tide.","The soldiers opened fire, but zombies could only be \"killed\" with a headshot. Bullets that struck the body merely slowed them down.","And the sheer numbers of second-generation zombies were overwhelming.","The drivers roared and floored the accelerator, trying to blast through, only to plunge into a sea of zombies.","The second-generation zombies were leaping! One after another! Leaping in groups!","They grabbed onto the truck railings! Jumped onto the hoods! Snatched at the side mirrors and windshield wipers!","Soldiers who had leaned out the windows to fire were yanked out by force. Two zombies carried one of them, and together they tumbled into the crowd of undead.","The screams lasted only a few moments before they cut off abruptly, vanishing.","The rest climbed in through the windows.","The steering wheel went dead! The heavy-laden vehicle veered off its lane and crashed into the greenery alongside the road!","Blood splattered across the glass—red, thick, smeared—until nothing inside could be seen anymore.","People in the vehicles behind shouted: \"Close the windows! Close the windows!\"","The fighters ducked back into the cabs and slammed the windows shut.","But countless second-generation zombies swarmed over the outside of the cab, staring at the humans through the glass with pitch-black eyes, then raised their fists.","Punch after punch. The zombies had enormous strength and felt no pain, and every punch came without pause.","Glass that an ordinary person couldn't smash even with a hammer began to show web-like cracks.","\"The glass is breaking! The glass is breaking!!!\"","\"AAAAAHHHHHHH—\"","Roars and screams twisted together.","This was what Vice Mayor Zheng heard from the liaison equipment in the monitoring hall.","On the wall of screens, every angle showed how the supply convoy was sinking into that zombie tide.","There were too many second-generation zombies—the slow-moving originals couldn't even get a single bite.","They couldn't even squeeze in.","Of the ten armored vehicles, only four escaped with their lives.","Even if the second-generation zombies were strong, they couldn't punch through the armor plating.","But too many of them crawled under the vehicles.","Arms and legs got wedged into the gaps of the tires and tracks. One arm, one leg couldn't stop the machinery. But ten arms and ten legs? Twenty arms and twenty legs?","Zombies felt no pain; as long as their heads remained intact, their bodies kept moving.","Countless limbs and bones lodged themselves into the tires and tracks, freezing the armored vehicles in place.","More zombies flooded in.","Seen from above, it was like disciplined worker ants hauling vast prey.","Those inside suddenly felt the center of gravity shift.","\"What's happening!\"","\"It's tipping! It's tipping!\"","With a thunderous crash, the worker ants flipped one prey after another onto their sides...","The four that had made it out wanted to turn back to rescue the rest, but the commander's voice came through the communicator: \"Retreat! Retreat immediately!\"","The drivers gritted their teeth and turned around.","Their comrades cried out: \"They've opened the hatches!\"","From the overturned armored vehicles, the hatches swung open. The soldiers, rifles raised, charged out screaming, \"I'll take you bastards with me!\"","The zombies, unafraid of bullets, surged forward and swallowed them whole.","On the monitors in the temporary command center, the soldiers were no longer visible—only layer upon layer of second-generation zombies piling on for a taste of flesh.","Vice Mayor Zheng closed his eyes in agony: \"How could this happen? How could this happen?\"","They had already used the road cameras to check the route!","His secretary explained: \"When we scouted the route, it was still night, very quiet. Nothing around had been disturbed...\"","So the massive horde hadn't moved significantly. The few aimless wanderers that strolled out had been nothing.","It wasn't until the rumbling convoy disturbed the zombies in the stadium.","Vice Mayor Zheng wiped his face: \"Scout a new viable route. The supply convoy will detour! Mark the stadium zone as a red high-risk area, and announce it citywide!\"","The secretary: \"Yes, sir.\"","\"Sir! The stadium zombie horde is beginning to spread!\"","Everyone turned to look.","The four armored vehicles that hadn't been lost had already retreated at full speed. With no living flesh left on the scene, the zombies' movements slowed suddenly, and they began wandering aimlessly.","They had no single direction—tens of thousands of them naturally fanned out in every direction, drifting slowly...","The faces of everyone in the monitoring hall were pale.","But what could they do? Tell residents to evacuate?","If the residents could freely come downstairs and move about, they wouldn't have been trapped in their neighborhoods, even locked inside their buildings.","Just as Jiang Cheng and Song Jingshuo had realized yesterday while retrieving supplies on their way back—in a disaster like this, urban residents lacking wilderness survival skills could neither flee nor had anywhere to flee.","The only option was to hold their ground!","Hold the neighborhood!","Hold the building!","Or at the very least, hold the door to their own home and keep the zombies from barging in!","A suffocating atmosphere filled the hall.","On the screens, the soldiers' remains were chewed beyond recognition, just like the second-generation zombies.","The people in the hall knew that after a while, these seemingly \"dead\" people would begin to mutate.","It wasn't just the living who, after being wounded, turned into second-generation zombies. Some of the \"corpses\" that appeared to have died from zombie attacks—as long as their heads were intact and their necks not severed—would also mutate after a period of time.","The original zombies were people in a healthy state who had been infected through unknown means and then mutated, with their bodies still in complete condition.","Many second-generation zombies only mutated after being attacked and appearing to be in a death-like state, so many of them were disfigured and covered in blood and gore.","The direct visual impact was eerie, sinister, and nauseating, putting even greater psychological pressure on people.","The monitoring hall was silent and tense. The technical staff from the transportation department were on edge, working feverishly to plan new detour routes.","\"Bigger, make it bigger,\" one staff member said in a low voice to another.","This staff member was adjusting the red zone on the map, trying to designate the area around the stadium as a high-danger red zone.","But her colleague reminded her that the red zone needed to be drawn even larger, because the zombie horde emerging from the stadium was slowly spreading. The nearby residential neighborhoods would all be affected.","This area was now being detoured around by the supply convoys, and residents in the surrounding blocks could no longer receive relief supplies.","What's more, countless zombies were slowly approaching their homes.","The staff member mapping out the route held back tears as she expanded the red zone even further.","At this moment, it was only 7:39 on Monday morning.","Jiang Cheng and Song Jingshuo were jogging in the courtyard of their residential complex.","Mo Li found a spot to bask in the sun and absorb energy.","Li Jiangbing still hadn't gotten out of bed.","Su Yu and He Tian had agreed to walk their dogs together.","Those who could wake up early were all practicing running, because everyone knew second-generation zombies were fast—if you couldn't fight them off, you had to outrun them.","You didn't need to outrun the second-generation zombies; you just needed to outrun other living people.","Around this time, Guo Jun and his group, who were buying supplies, were still dawdling in their dormitory, hesitating: \"So what do we do?\"","\"Go to the Youth Apartment?\"","\"Yeah, they're the most reliable. If they're willing to take us in, then we can relax.\"","\"But will they even take us in?\"","Plenty of elderly folks in Jixiang Jiayuan had also gotten up early and wandered over to Jixiang West Street.","They couldn't enter the Youth Apartment—security was strict, and the gates were usually locked. To get in, you needed a valid reason and had to undergo a physical examination.","But that didn't stop the old folks from grabbing the iron railings and peering inside: \"Whoa, so many people out running.\"","A complex filled with young, able-bodied fighters—they could even loot more supplies than others. It was something to envy.","And so that day passed fairly peacefully for these two complexes that had managed to build their own \"green zones\" through sheer effort.","The Youth Apartment had taken in new labor, and the living conditions for the property management staff improved—there was even a bit of festive cheer in the air.","Master Luo and his wife moved into their new quarters and tried on clothes left behind by the original owners.","After Aunt Pan complimented Master Luo on looking \"fashionable,\" she checked the time: \"Time to watch the news.\"","Now, everyone made a point to watch the news on schedule.","[The area within a three-kilometer radius of Rainbow Stadium is designated as a red high-danger zone. Strictly no approaching. I repeat, strictly no approaching.]","[Other supply drop points along the Fourth Ring Road have been successfully deployed.]","[Supplies have reached residents.]","Footage of \"residents picking up supplies\" was shown—and every clip was shorter than yesterday's Fifth Ring Road clips. Jiang Cheng noticed it at a glance.","Soon after, Song Jingshuo called her.","Song Jingshuo sat on his sofa and waited for the call to connect.","He had gotten into the habit of calling Jiang Cheng whenever something came up. Talking things through with her gave him a sense of reassurance, like having a solid foundation beneath his feet.","The call connected. No pleasantries or greetings needed. Song Jingshuo said, \"Did you notice?\"","Of course Jiang Cheng had noticed: \"The fighting must have been intense.\"","Every clip was cut extremely short, precisely because the next second, a brawl was about to break out. That didn't align with the current temporary emergency command center's guiding principles—it would only sow discord and corrupt morale. So they cut all of it out, broadcasting only the few seconds when the frontmost residents grabbed their supplies before the fighting broke out.","\"Nothing we can do,\" Jiang Cheng sighed. \"The population density along the Fourth Ring Road is way higher than here.\"","Song Jingshuo couldn't even manage a sigh. \"My apartment is on the Fourth Ring Road.\"","A spacious three-bedroom place, 180 square meters. He lived there alone—roomy. Right next to a city forest park, with floor-to-ceiling windows that opened up to an unobstructed view—a proper view unit.","A snicker came through the phone. She opened her mouth to say something, but just as she formed the first syllable, the call suddenly dropped.","Song Jingshuo: \"?\"","He dialed her again—","[The number you have dialed is no longer in service.]"]},{"number":62,"title":"Chapter 62","paragraphs":["\"Jiang Cheng?\"","Both Song Jingshuo and Jiang Cheng still had walkie-talkies on them, so Song Jingshuo called Jiang Cheng directly.","Everyone who had a walkie-talkie heard it.","Song Jingshuo asked, \"What's going on?\"","Jiang Cheng herself was just as speechless. \"My phone's been cut off. Ran out of credit.\"","Several people holding walkie-talkies chuckled. After the laughter died down, they realized the problem.","Sure enough, Jiang Cheng said it first: \"This is not a small matter.\"","Because of the increasing popularity of mobile phones, the rate of landline cancellations had been rising over the past couple of years. Although every household had a phone jack pre-installed in the wall, almost no new homes applied for landlines anymore. And in older homes, many people had already cancelled their fixed-line service.","Because if you didn't cancel, you still had to pay a fixed monthly rental fee. It just wasn't worth it.","Someone cut in: \"Mine might be about to run out of credit too.\"","Jiang Cheng said, \"There must be a lot of people. Not just us.\"","Even though they had walkie-talkies, the building-wide intercom system, and messaging app groups, mobile phones were still an extremely important tool for everyone to keep in touch.","Especially for people who needed to contact their families.","Master Luo and Aunt Pan had just finished watching today's news bulletin and were talking.","\"I remember there are quite a few residential areas around Rainbow Sports Center.\"","\"Good heavens, what do we do then? Is the red zone especially serious?\"","\"Green zones are safe, yellow zones have zombies—this is the first time we've seen a red zone. Must be really serious, right?\"","The couple was in the middle of their conversation when Song Jingshuo's voice came through the walkie-talkie, and Jiang Cheng said her phone had been cut off.","The two of them looked at each other. \"Is ours...\"","\"What do we do?\"","A moment later, the loudspeaker in the hallway started broadcasting.","Master Luo opened his door and saw that everyone else had opened their doors too, poking their heads out—the speaker was mounted at the end of the hallway ceiling, and opening the door made it easier to hear.","Only Jiang Cheng next door hadn't opened her door.","[Anyone whose phone has been cut off or is about to be cut off, please register on the owners' forum.]","[Anyone whose phone has been cut off or is about to be cut off, please register on the owners' forum.]","[Anyone whose phone has been cut off or is about to be cut off, please register on the owners' forum.]","It was the person on duty at the property management center today.","Aunt Pan couldn't help but say, \"You know, this interim committee of ours really gets things done fast. If they're on it, they should be able to solve it, right?\"","Master Luo nodded. \"They definitely will.\"","Up until now, any problem the interim committee had been made aware of, they'd basically found a way to solve or at least improve.","Everyone had confidence in the interim committee.","Ever since the building-wide broadcast system had been activated, and previous operations were banned from being discussed on the forum to prevent leaks, the forum hadn't been as lively as before.","It was also because messaging groups of various sizes had been set up, along with online chat rooms.","But today it got lively again.","Quite a few people had already had their phones cut off. Some hadn't been cut off yet but were almost there.","Everyone first registered in the relevant thread, then started new posts asking: [What do we do?]","[Just wait. They asked everyone to register, so they must have a plan.]","At this time, you could pay your phone bill at the telecom company's business hall, at a bank, or by buying a top-up card.","The telecom company's top-up card was extremely popular—it wasn't just for mobile phone credit; you could also use it to directly top up some games.","You could usually find them at street newsstands, tobacconists, supermarkets, or phone repair shops. Very convenient.","If you went out from Jixiang West Street, you'd see a newsstand, and there was also a phone repair shop inside the Buyduoduo supermarket building. You could find them in any of those places. So when the interim committee held its core members meeting on Tuesday, the natural proposal was to go outside the safe zone and look for top-up cards.","The interim committee now had more and more members. When they held full meetings, Song Jingshuo's place was starting to feel too small. But not everything required a full meeting. Some things could be handled with just a core members meeting first.","That meant just Jiang Cheng and the six building captains.","As per the usual practice, everyone was free to speak their minds, brainstorm freely, and offer suggestions and opinions. Of course, the final call was Jiang Cheng's.","But this time, Jiang Cheng didn't immediately adopt the simple and easy suggestion.","She sat half-leaning on the dining table, her chin resting in her hand, partly covering her face, as if she was thinking.","Everyone looked at her.","After a few seconds, Jiang Cheng lowered her hand. \"Not enough.\"","\"Top-up cards have very small denominations, and there are too many of us. Other than Jingshuo, ninety-nine percent of people will need to top up their credit.\"","\"Huh?\" Li Jiangbing turned his head to look at Song Jingshuo. \"Why is it everyone except you?\"","Song Jingshuo answered flatly, \"I have enough credit to last a year.\"","Everyone: \"...\"","That would cost a lot of money!","Li Jiangbing's mouth twitched. He didn't feel like acknowledging this show-off any further, and asked Jiang Cheng, \"Then what do we do?\"","Jiang Cheng looked left and right. \"Where's the TV remote?\"","Song Jingshuo found the remote on the coffee table. Jiang Cheng said, \"Turn on the TV and check something.\"","Then she added, \"The news channel.\"","The S City temporary emergency committee's news broadcast was only on S City's local channel.","When the TV came on, last night's broadcast was still looping on repeat.","At the bottom of the screen was a scrolling ticker, which had the temporary emergency command center's hotline number on it.","\"This is it.\" Jiang Cheng held out her hand to Song Jingshuo. \"Give me your phone.\"","Song Jingshuo handed it over without a word.","His phone was the latest model—a black business phone, compact, with a cover that could rotate to the top. The lines were sleek and futuristic.","It was the kind of phone whose ads appeared during commercial breaks on many recorded TV programs. A high-end business phone.","It suited his image.","The hotline was constantly busy—just a continuous engaged tone.","At first everyone waited quietly. As time passed, they started chatting among themselves. Then, all of a sudden, it connected.","Everyone went quiet and listened to Jiang Cheng's call on speaker.","The operator's voice sounded a bit hoarse: \"Temporary emergency command center. Please go ahead.\"","\"We're the interim emergency committee of the Youth Apartments in the Science and Technology New District. Please report to your superiors that many people's phones have either already been cut off or are about to be due for a payment period renewal or have run out of prepaid credit. Right now no one can go out to pay their bills, and there's soon going to be a large-scale situation where phones get cut off for non-payment.\"","\"I would like,\" Jiang Cheng said, \"to request that the temporary emergency command center suspend the suspension-of-service feature as soon as possible.\"","\"Mobile phones are currently the primary means of communication in urban areas. If people—especially residents of the same residential complex—lose this method of contact, organizing collective actions will become extremely difficult.\"","\"Please, command center, make sure this problem is resolved for everyone.\"","The operator had spent day after day listening to crying, rage, pleas for help, and complaints. She was completely drained.","Suddenly, a young woman's pleasant voice—calmly reporting a problem, offering a suggestion, laying out the stakes, and expressing expectations—made the operator's spirits lift.","\"Understood. The situation you described has been noted, and I'll report it to my superiors right away!\" The operator's voice rose in pitch. \"Which residential complex did you say you're from?\"","\"Youth Apartments in the Science and Technology New District. We're the residential complex's interim emergency committee.\"","Vice Mayor Zheng was resting with his eyes closed. He was utterly exhausted.","He suddenly heard someone speaking in low voices, and snapped his eyes open, catching a glimpse of his secretary's silhouette through the half-closed door, talking to someone.","He waited, and sure enough, after the secretary finished the conversation, he poked his head in, saw that he was already awake, and walked in.","\"What's the situation?\" Vice Mayor Zheng asked.","\"Do you remember the youth apartment complex?\" the secretary said.","\"I remember,\" Vice Mayor Zheng said. \"That girl, right? What about the youth apartment?\"","\"The switchboard operator got a call that should be from that girl — a young woman's voice, by the sound of it.\"","The secretary handed over the folder in his hand.","It was a handwritten work sheet, for status reporting.","Vice Mayor Zheng glanced over it and finished reading in a second.","\"I completely forgot about that!\" he said. \"So now?\"","The emergency response team had taken over everything in a rush, with all the critical systems already being maintained — water, electricity, gas, communications. But they'd all been guided by the principle of \"keep things running.\" What they'd forgotten was that water, electricity, and gas are all billed and collected through door-to-door meter checks, whereas communications have a special quirk: the user has to proactively pay or top up themselves.","Everyone slips up sometimes. At a critical moment like this, with the temporary emergency command center just set up, everyone was carrying enormous mental pressure and working around the clock.","Everyone was exhausted.","A lapse like this was normal.","\"I've already passed it down just now. They've already started making phone calls.\"","Vice Mayor Zheng nodded, handed the work sheet back, and added: \"Report this to the central government. This should be implemented nationwide.\"","\"Yes, sir. Please get some more rest.\"","Vice Mayor Zheng nodded, closed his eyes, then suddenly opened them again: \"What's the girl's name?\"","The secretary quickly glanced at the work sheet, which had a summary of the call, and confirmed: \"It doesn't say. She must not have given it — she just identified herself as the temporary emergency residents' committee of the youth apartment.\"","Vice Mayor Zheng nodded again, and this time he closed his eyes for good: \"Let me know when that's sorted out.\"","The secretary quietly acknowledged, and left.","Over on the other side, a few of the building managers were still discussing: \"Can they handle it?\"","\"They will, right?\"","\"Hope so.\"","Everyone chatted a bit more about the issues that had been reported from their respective building units.","\"People on floors one and two in our building say the garbage smell from the clubhouse is really strong, especially at night — they can't open their windows to sleep.\"","\"We've got a few night owls in our building who sleep all day and bang around at night, disturbing people — there've already been a couple of fights. I told them if they pick up any wounds and can't explain them at the next gate check, they'll be put in isolation. That shut them up.\"","Overall, order within the complex was holding.","Various repairs and maintenance were mostly getting done — just that Master Luo was worn out. But now that there were thirteen extra pairs of hands, things should get better going forward.","Compared to all the mess in neighboring complexes, the youth apartment might as well be paradise.","But there was no way to completely avoid conflicts. In fact, the building managers had to deal with this kind of trivial nonsense every single day.","Before, everyone went to work during the day and came home to sleep at night — life was regular, and there wasn't this much time to spend together.","Now everyone was stuck at home, and all sorts of petty crap kept cropping up.","Annoying.","A few building managers gathered together to vent.","Song Jingshuo's phone suddenly rang. He glanced at the caller ID, his expression flickering with mild surprise, and answered: \"Hello?\"","\"One moment, please.\" Then, wearing an expression of \"same as expected,\" he handed the phone to Jiang Cheng. \"It's for you.\"","\"It's the command center.\""]},{"number":63,"title":"Chapter 63","paragraphs":["The house suddenly fell silent, and everyone turned to look.","Jiang Cheng took the phone and switched on the speaker. “Hello?”","A middle-aged man’s voice came through the phone. “Young person, what’s your name?”","“My name is Jiang Cheng, Vice Mayor Zheng.”","“You knew it was me?”","“Yes,” Jiang Cheng said. “I hear your voice every day.”","His voice and face appeared every day in the news broadcasts.","With manpower in such short supply, they no longer bothered with a dedicated spokesperson. Vice Mayor Zheng himself appeared on the news every day.","Vice Mayor Zheng seemed to give a soft chuckle.","He said, “The problem you reported has been resolved.”","“Thank you.”","Vice Mayor Zheng praised her. “You reported the problem in a very timely manner. It was indeed something we had overlooked. I’ve also seen the situation in your residential compound. What you young people have done is very impressive.”","Jiang Cheng did not accept the compliment. “We’re only doing everything we can to help everyone survive. You know how difficult things are now.”","Vice Mayor Zheng fell silent for a moment.","Of course, he would not call an ordinary citizen for no reason. That was precisely why Jiang Cheng did not take his praise at face value. She remained wary of anything out of the ordinary.","“Little Jiang,” Vice Mayor Zheng said, stating what he wanted. “I hope you and your residential compound can take the lead in helping other communities. I hope you young people can set an example by sharing the supplies distributed by the government with the surrounding communities.”","“Of course, this isn’t a demand or an order. It’s a plea.”","“Little Jiang, can you do that?”","Song Jingshuo’s house was so quiet that one could hear a pin drop.","Everyone’s eyes immediately turned to Jiang Cheng.","In private, the men did sometimes discuss Jiang Cheng. Although they all trusted and admired her, they would say things like, “Don’t you think Jiang Cheng is a little too calm?”","Jiang Cheng’s emotions were unusually steady, and that was a point of complaint among the men.","When a woman displayed an exceptional ability or possessed an especially conspicuous virtue, it often made certain men feel uneasy and uncomfortable.","But when Jiang Cheng’s expression actually turned grim, everyone forgot about those complaints. They really, really did not want to see her like that.","In truth, there was no obvious change in Jiang Cheng’s expression, but her complexion had clearly darkened. A person’s presence was intangible, yet somehow visible.","“Sorry, but we can’t do that,” Jiang Cheng replied decisively. “When you make a request like this, it becomes even more impossible for us to comply.”","Vice Mayor Zheng was silent for a moment before letting out a sigh.","Jiang Cheng could hear the exhaustion in his voice. This middle-aged man, who appeared on the news every day, had visibly aged at an astonishing speed over the course of just a few days.","Although she could not accept his request, Jiang Cheng respected a man like him, and she was willing to offer a little more explanation.","“Vice Mayor Zheng, if you’re not in a position, you can’t fully understand the problems of that position. You’re responsible for the entire city, but we’re only responsible for the people in our compound. If we can’t do it, the people here won’t tolerate it either.”","“We only have any influence because the people in the compound support us.”","“We don’t have the power to force anyone to obey.”","Everything she said was perfectly understandable to Vice Mayor Zheng.","He had merely been holding on to a faint hope and had been unwilling to stop trying.","Now that hope had been extinguished, everyone had to prioritize staying alive. These people were ordinary citizens. They were neither police officers nor soldiers, let alone government officials.","For the latter, sacrificing themselves for the interests of the people was considered part of their duty.","But when it came to ordinary citizens, no one could demand that they be selfless or heroic.","Jiang Cheng had no way to force the homeowners in the compound to obey. Likewise, Vice Mayor Zheng had no way to force the citizens to become saints.","Vice Mayor Zheng gave a bitter laugh. He had not held out much hope to begin with, so he was not too disappointed.","In a gentle voice, he said, “I know. I understand.”","“Then let’s each do our best at our respective posts.”","The call ended, leaving everyone with different thoughts.","Some were relieved that Jiang Cheng had withstood the pressure from the vice mayor.","Others felt a little regretful, thinking they had missed an opportunity to establish a connection with him.","That was the vice mayor, after all. They saw him on the news every day, but in reality, ordinary people like them might never meet him in person even once in their entire lives.","Jiang Cheng looked grim, and Song Jingshuo’s expression darkened along with hers.","Li Jiangbing asked cautiously, “What’s wrong?”","He was thinking that perhaps they were afraid of being retaliated against for refusing the vice mayor’s request.","Jiang Cheng’s voice was a little hard. “The situation outside may be even worse than we thought.”","Song Jingshuo nodded. “It’s already extremely serious.”","Everyone looked at the two of them.","Jiang Cheng said, “Order must be deteriorating. We’re shut inside the compound, so we can’t feel it.”","She asked, “How can the government monitor us? Through the cameras on the streets?”","“Most likely,” Song Jingshuo replied.","“What about the ones inside the compound?”","“They’re independent systems. They use videotapes.”","Jiang Cheng sighed. “Then it’s even worse.”","She voiced her deduction. “There must have been large-scale... well, clashes of some kind. If the authorities can only see the street footage, that means it’s no longer limited to conflicts within individual compounds. It may have already developed into conflicts between different compounds.”","“Most likely, people were driven to desperation by hunger. Then supplies were suddenly distributed, but only along the city’s main ring road. Some people had supplies, some didn’t. Some compounds managed to seize a lot, while others got nothing.”","“When people are starving, they’ll dare to do anything.”","Jiang Cheng’s guess was completely correct.","Everyone had been starving together, and then the government suddenly distributed supplies—but only along the city’s main ring road.","To break through the hordes of zombies blocking the roads and reach the ring road, one needed a vehicle.","At that point, the disparity in wealth between the different compounds became apparent.","Urban layouts in China were different from those in other countries.","In some foreign countries, the rich and poor were physically separated. The poor lived in slums—filthy, disorderly places with dilapidated public facilities—while the wealthy lived in neighborhoods with beautiful surroundings, good security, and every kind of amenity.","More importantly, the poor could not reach the areas where the wealthy lived.","China’s guiding principle was that such a situation must never be allowed.","All areas were broken up and mixed together.","For example, a wetland park might be located beside an upscale residential compound, perhaps even a villa development. The residents were wealthy and enjoyed the beautiful environment provided by the wetland park. They might even want to keep it for themselves.","Dream on!","A resettlement-housing compound would be built right next door, housing working-class families.","The middle class and the wealthy could simply walk downstairs to stroll through and enjoy the wetland park.","Ordinary people could do the same.","If you had money, you could go to commercial establishments for high-end consumption. You could indulge in extravagant banquets, wine, and sensual pleasures.","But all public spaces and facilities provided by the state were to be enjoyed equally by everyone, regardless of wealth.","Such arrangements made society more harmonious and fair.","But everything went wrong after the zombie virus broke out. With manpower in short supply, the government could only drop supplies along the ring roads. Residents of wealthy communities drove their cars, plowing through the zombies in the streets and forcing their way past one road after another to seize the supplies.","But most families in the resettlement communities didn’t own private cars. They had no way to get there.","When one hungry person sees a group of people with food, they usually don’t dare to act.","But when a hungry group sees another group with food, they become furious—especially when they are in the majority.","A human being’s most basic need is the need to stay alive. Hungry people gathering together can become a terrifying force.","On Sunday and Monday, the communities erupted into bloody clashes, as if two villages in ancient times had launched a massive battle to fight over a water source.","Some people had fought stubbornly to survive for an entire week. They hadn’t died in the mouths of zombies, yet they died beneath the clubs and cleavers of residents from the neighboring communities.","And this happened more than once or twice over those two days.","The relief supplies distributed by the government were like cold water dropped into a pan of boiling oil. The whole city exploded.","Vice Mayor Zheng watched from the surveillance room as law-abiding citizens, their eyes bloodshot, hacked at one another with cleavers. He felt every cell in his body ache.","The pain spread through him.","He truly wished that at least one community—just one—could take the lead in helping people from other communities and set an example for the entire city.","Sometimes, an example like that really was useful. Humans lived in groups, and they would always need spiritual guidance.","But it went against human nature.","People could only help others when they had strength to spare. If someone was already on the verge of death and was still expected to act like a saint, that simply wouldn’t work.","Jiang Cheng’s refusal was perfectly understandable and came as no surprise.","For a young woman and her companions to keep a community of more than two thousand people stable and orderly was already an extraordinary achievement. And they were all still so young.","No one could ask more of them.","Vice Mayor Zheng looked at the chaos on the screen and helplessly closed his eyes.","“Has it really gotten this bad?”","After hearing Jiang Cheng’s analysis, everyone sighed. Someone asked, “Why hasn’t anyone come to raid our community?”","“Fuck,” Li Jiangbing exclaimed, waving his bowl-sized fists. “Do they think I’m dead?”","If Jiang Cheng was the lord, then Li Jiangbing was unquestionably her great general.","Compared with all the chores inside the community, leaving the safe zone for field missions was clearly far more dangerous. By now, it had practically become an unwritten rule that Li Jiangbing would lead whenever they went out.","After going on so many missions, even the team members had gradually become a fixed group, all familiar faces.","Whenever Li Jiangbing called out, he could quickly assemble a team.","Of course, the residents didn’t go on these missions for nothing.","Although each mission was carried out on official business, with specific items to obtain, everyone would more or less keep a few things for themselves.","That, too, had become an accepted practice.","People lived together in groups, and they quickly adapted to their environment, adjusting and establishing new rules according to changing circumstances.","The Young People’s Apartments were packed with able-bodied fighters. They were especially united, organized, disciplined, and always advanced and retreated together, forming an unbreakable block.","Who would be foolish enough to raid the Young People’s Apartments?","As they were speaking, everyone’s phones suddenly chimed with a text message.","It was from the telecommunications provider in S City:","“Emergency Communications Assurance Notice:","“Dear residents,","“To ensure smooth emergency communications during the current major disaster, our company is activating its emergency communications plan effective immediately. All mobile phones, including those with overdue unpaid bills and suspended service, have automatically had calling and text messaging restored. No payment is required, and usage is unlimited.","“May we keep watch over one another in safety and get through this difficult time together.","“—S City Telecommunications Emergency Command Center”","Throughout the community, everyone picked up their phones and read the message that had just arrived.","Many people looked at one another in confusion.","“Is this a coincidence?”","The community’s temporary committee had only asked everyone to register this matter last night. Yet this morning, communications service had suddenly been restored across the entire city?","Did their temporary committee really have that kind of influence?"]},{"number":64,"title":"Chapter 64","paragraphs":["Only a few minutes after she finished muttering, another text message arrived. It was from the telecom provider again, but this time not from the city-level branch. It was from the national headquarters.","The new message was more or less the same as the one sent by the S City Emergency Command Center, except that it covered the entire country.","It was clear that S City had taken the lead, reported the matter to the central authorities, and then had the measure extended nationwide.","But last night, it had actually been the neighborhood’s temporary committee that started compiling the statistics first.","As they were speculating, everyone saw the seven members of the temporary committee emerge from the entrance of Building Four. Everyone knew that the committee had been holding its meetings at Song Jingshuo’s home in Building Four.","As the committee members approached, someone couldn’t resist stepping forward to ask, “Does this have anything to do with us?”","He held up his phone and showed the committee members the text message.","The committee members didn’t need to look. They had received the same message.","Wu Jiancheng, the building captain of Building One, smiled and said, “Of course it does. Jiang Cheng was the one who called the city emergency command center. She even spoke directly with Vice Mayor Zheng just now. The vice mayor called her personally and told her that the matter we raised has already been taken care of.”","In truth, Jiang Cheng had handled the whole thing by herself. But now that it had been accomplished, and she had even spoken with the vice mayor, the members of the temporary committee all felt honored to have been involved.","Seeing that the seven of them continued toward the east gate without showing any sign of dispersing, someone else asked, “Where are you going?”","Normally, Jiang Cheng would have picked up the conversation in a situation like this, but today she seemed to be deep in thought. Li Jiangbing, standing beside her, answered, “Paying a visit.”","He added, “Next door.”","“Next door” specifically meant Jixiang Jiayuan.","Zhou Wang had received Jiang Cheng’s call and was already waiting for them at Jixiang Jiayuan’s west gate. The two residential compounds were practically facing each other, so they spotted one another as soon as they came out.","“Brother Zhou,” Jiang Cheng greeted him.","When Zhou Wang saw her, his heart tightened slightly. “Did something happen?”","Whenever Youth Apartments was planning some kind of operation, Jiang Cheng usually spoke with a faint smile. Her smile appeared gentle, but it often concealed the confidence of someone who had everything under control and was certain of victory.","But today, her expression was much more solemn than usual, and Zhou Wang grew tense.","They found a place to sit in the garden of Jixiang Jiayuan and began talking.","Zhou Wang was surprised. “Our neighborhood?”","“Yes.” Jiang Cheng nodded. “We wanted to understand the situation here. After all, we’re neighbors, practically shoulder to shoulder. We’re too close to ignore each other.”","Jiang Cheng wanted to learn about the current state of Jixiang Jiayuan.","“You can rest easy about our neighborhood,” Zhou Wang said with a nod. “I’m here. I can’t promise absolute security, but I’ll do my best.”","“You’re right to be concerned. Order is too important.”","Once Zhou Wang got started, he opened up. “The supplies we brought back were divided among the people who went out in teams first, and the rest was placed under communal control. Some of it was distributed to people in the neighborhood who truly couldn’t get by. We’re holding on to the little that remains for now and will see how things develop.”","“Compared to you, we didn’t get nearly as much. You made quite a haul this time,” he said. “People from several nearby neighborhoods are furious whenever they mention you.”","The members of the temporary committee exchanged glances, their expressions turning grave.","But Zhou Wang immediately added, “Still, no one dares set their sights on you. Everyone knows you’re not to be trifled with.”","He did not say that no one dared set their sights on Jixiang Jiayuan.","The few who had escaped, along with the families of those who had never returned, had already spread the word.","Youth Apartments and Jixiang Jiayuan—two places no one could afford to provoke.","Zhou Wang, like Vice Mayor Zheng, had aged dramatically in the span of a single week.","But the slick, worldly air he had once carried was gone. Now he looked like a steady, respected elder.","He asked, “What happened at your neighborhood?”","Something must have happened at Youth Apartments. Otherwise, Jiang Cheng and the others would not have suddenly come over to inquire about Jixiang Jiayuan for no reason.","“Nothing happened at our neighborhood,” Jiang Cheng said.","She told Zhou Wang about calling the command center that day and receiving a return call from Vice Mayor Zheng.","“So it was you?” Zhou Wang said.","Everyone had been delighted when they received the text message about the communications support notice. None of them had expected that Jiang Cheng and the others were the ones who had brought the matter to the command center’s attention.","“The situation may be very bad.” Jiang Cheng also told him about their suspicions.","Instead of panicking, becoming anxious, or expressing surprise, Zhou Wang looked almost speechless.","“You people...”","“You really are...” Zhou Wang was too exhausted to find the words. “You’ve really shut yourselves in and lived as though everything outside was peaceful.”","“Ah...”","He let out a deep sigh.","The seven people looked at one another.","Jiang Cheng said, “Please, tell us what happened...”","Zhou Wang said, “People from Deqingli stormed into Shanshui Yayuan to seize supplies. Quite a few people died. You really didn’t know anything about it?”","Even Jiang Cheng was stunned.","The seven of them were collectively dumbfounded.","Zhou Wang was even more speechless and could only shake his head.","Shanshui Yayuan was a low-density villa compound whose residents were owners or senior executives of various companies, large and small.","Deqingli was a public-rental housing complex. Its residents were at the lower end of the working class in terms of income.","Every household in Shanshui Yayuan had at least two cars. Most of the residents of Deqingli commuted using the three rapid bus routes—535, 578, and 611. Only a minority owned cars.","In order to obtain the supplies distributed by the government, the people of Shanshui Yayuan had taken out practically every car in their homes. Anyone with a driver’s license—or even without one—had gotten behind the wheel.","There was no need to fear hitting anyone on the roads, since the only things walking around were no longer alive. And in these extraordinary circumstances, no one cared about a few scratches or dents.","The more cars there were, the more supplies they could carry.","Most of Deqingli’s residents, however, had no private vehicles and were trapped like animals in a cage.","When people were truly pushed to the brink, their eyes became bloodshot. At a moment like this, all it took was someone to raise an arm and call out—","“Come on! Let’s make Shanshui Yayuan give us a share!”","The other nearby neighborhoods were all fairly decent commercial housing complexes. Even Youth Apartments, where the residents were too young to own many private cars, had managed to obtain vehicles—and, reportedly, a considerable amount of supplies—through solidarity and cooperation.","So why choose Shanshui Yayuan?","Because the villa compound was low-density.","There were fewer people living there.","Deqingli had the highest population density in the surrounding area.","In ancient times, the strength of a tribe was directly tied to its population.","Who would dare attack a tribe filled with able-bodied adults, united and organized? Anyone who went in without knowing what they were up against might never come back.","Naturally, people chose to attack and plunder smaller tribes.","Deqingli had a large population, which also meant it had a large number of zombies. In recent days, everyone had been forced to leave their homes in search of food, and they had killed many of them.","But unlike Youth Apartments and Jixiang Jiayuan, they had never conducted a thorough, systematic sweep of the entire compound. They had not cleared it completely and turned it into a genuine safe zone.","When so many people poured out at once, they took advantage of the opportunity to clear out many of the zombies in the compound courtyard as well. Only then did the area finally become more or less fully cleared.","Deqingli and Shanshui Yayuan were adjacent, just like Youth Apartments and Jixiang Jiayuan, with only a narrow road between them.","However, they did not face each other. They stood side by side, with both compounds’ main entrances opening onto the same major road. There were still quite a few zombies on that road.","Deqingli, however, had a high population density, so the compound had four gates—one each to the east, south, west, and north.","The lane between the two residential compounds was relatively clean. A few scattered zombies had wandered over from the main road, but the large group had trampled them to death as they passed.","Shanshui Yayuan didn’t have a gate connecting it to Deqingli.","But Deqingli had a large population, with residents from all kinds of professions. Someone had brought a hydraulic cutter and cut through the key load-bearing points where the iron railings were attached to the concrete pillars. Then everyone pushed together and knocked down a section of railing.","At first, they hadn’t intended to rob anyone. They had wanted to negotiate—even begged and pleaded in tears.","Unfortunately, the bosses refused to share their supplies.","When tempers flared and a conflict broke out, blood was shed.","By then, it was too late for the bosses to regret their decision. In several households, fathers and sons had been killed together, while the women were left alive.","Life-sustaining supplies had equalized the gap between rich and poor through violence and bloodshed.","The irony was that Shanshui Yayuan had never organized an effort to clear out the zombies.","Since every house had its own courtyard, the residents only had to keep their gates shut to keep the zombies out. So the small number of zombies had continued wandering between the courtyards. In the end, it was the people from Deqingli who cleared them away.","The seven people looked at one another.","Jiang Cheng looked at Song Jingshuo, and Song Jingshuo looked back at her.","“Why haven’t any of these things been mentioned on the forums?” Song Jingshuo asked.","Zhou Wang found the question even more ridiculous.","He looked at these young people—whom he had previously considered clever and sharp-minded—as if they were idiots.","“They’re practically starving to death...” He was utterly speechless. “Who the hell still has the energy to go online every day and give you updates?”","Besides, Shanshui Yayuan was home to wealthy business owners, while Deqingli housed low-income residents in subsidized apartments. Neither group was particularly familiar with or interested in the internet to begin with.","The young people living in the Youth Apartments were the primary users of the internet. Their incomes and education levels were relatively good, and most of them had come from elsewhere. They locked the gates of their compound and relied on the internet for information.","Only now did Jiang Cheng and Song Jingshuo realize that the people who had remained active online these past few days were, in fact, those whose living conditions were still relatively stable.","Besides, killing people and taking their belongings wasn’t exactly something worth boasting about.","When the people from Deqingli had set out, they had been empty-handed except for their weapons. They had shouted and argued, making a noisy, disorderly scene.","But when they returned, carrying, embracing, hauling, and dragging supplies, they were as quiet as ghosts. Not a single person spoke on the way back.","Some of them even left a bloody footprint with every step.","Zhou Wang lit a cigarette and exhaled a cloud of white smoke as he looked at these bewildered young people, who could eat their fill every day without worrying about starvation.","Once again, he shook his head.","Jiang Cheng clasped her hands over her mouth and nose, taking some time to digest the information and calm herself. Then she lowered her hands.","“We actually came here to warn you in advance. We didn’t expect to be arriving after the fact.”","“Brother Zhou, our two compounds are the closest to each other. You have to keep things under control in your compound,” she said. “If you can’t... leave through the east gate.”","Zhou Wang was startled by Jiang Cheng once again.","He had thought she would say that they could ask the Youth Apartments for help if things got out of control. Instead, she told them to leave through the east gate.","Jixiang Jiayuan lay to the east, while the Youth Apartments lay to the west, with only Jixiang West Street between them. The west gate of Jixiang Jiayuan and the east gate of the Youth Apartments both faced Jixiang West Street, angled toward each other.","If they left through the west gate, they would be facing the Youth Apartments.","If they left through the east gate, they would be facing other residential compounds.","The young woman’s voice was calm and gentle, but her meaning was anything but gentle—","If things fell apart, don’t come and cause trouble for the Youth Apartments.","The Youth Apartments were nothing like Shanshui Yayuan.","Zhou Wang realized then that when the Youth Apartments had rushed over last Monday to help them clear out the zombies, it might not have been out of kindness.","Perhaps they simply couldn’t allow the neighboring compound to become a breeding ground for zombies.","Zhou Wang took two heavy drags on his cigarette and answered gloomily, “All right.”"]},{"number":65,"title":"Chapter 65","paragraphs":["He added, “Lekang Homeland might be finished.”","“There are too many zombies in their complex.”","“Someone couldn’t take it anymore and hanged themselves.”","“I don’t know much more about what’s happening in there. The people I knew are already dead.”","“Renxin Hospital has become a zombie nest too. Stay away from there.”","Jiang Cheng now understood why none of this information could be found online.","When things had reached this point, who would still be browsing the internet?","The internet wasn’t as widespread as people imagined, nor was it all that useful. It was still a decent tool for the people in Youth Apartment, but for everyone else, it served little purpose.","In the end, Zhou Wang said, “Our complex is actually doing pretty well.”","Then he added, “But do you realize how outrageous the current state of your complex is?”","There was enough food, the property management was still functioning, and no serious incidents had occurred.","Yet it seemed that these young people had no idea how abnormal their complex’s situation was under the current circumstances.","On the way back, everyone noticed Jiang Cheng’s silence.","Jiang Cheng was rarely this quiet. Most of the time, she appeared utterly composed. That composure gave people a sense of reliability and safety, making them trust her.","Li Jiangbing was no less familiar with her than Song Jingshuo. In fact, he had become one of Jiang Cheng’s “people” even earlier than Song Jingshuo had.","He was also the first one who couldn’t hold back any longer. He asked, “Jiang Cheng... you’ve got something on your mind, don’t you? Why don’t you tell us?”","Everyone pricked up their ears. Song Jingshuo also stopped brooding and turned to look at Jiang Cheng. The more he had thought about things along the way, the heavier his heart had felt. He, too, wanted to know what Jiang Cheng was thinking.","Jiang Cheng stopped and looked up at the clear blue sky. After taking a deep breath, she turned around.","“Then I’ll tell you...”","“If Lekang Homeland falls completely, it’ll be a disaster. It will create a large number of second-generation zombies. If something happens and those zombies are roused, drawn out, and allowed to spread, it’ll be disastrous for the entire Technology New District—especially this area of ours.”","“Our complexes are all so close to one another. To put it plainly, when one suffers, all suffer.”","“The fences around our complexes won’t be able to stop a large number of second-generation zombies.”","Second-generation zombies possessed tremendous physical strength. Even if they couldn’t clear a fence in a single leap, they could use the impact to climb over it with astonishing speed—far more nimbly than any human.","A small number of second-generation zombies wasn’t a problem. As long as there were enough people, they weren’t frightening. Because the zombies were obsessed with living flesh, their targets were clear and their movements could be predicted. With enough manpower, people could coordinate and kill them relatively easily.","But large numbers were another matter. Human skin could be ruined by even the tiniest cut that drew blood.","Song Jingshuo said gravely, “Jiang Cheng, tell us what you’re thinking. Don’t hold back.”","Jiang Cheng glanced at him.","“Actually, we all understand that instead of sitting around waiting for rescue, everyone in this area—I mean all the residents nearby—would be better off joining forces to eliminate the zombies.”","“Only after we clear out all the zombies can we return to a truly normal life.”","Over the past few days, everyone had noticed that the maps shown in the news broadcasts had begun to display scattered little green dots—small areas of safety. In the Technology New District, those areas were Youth Apartment and Jixiang Garden.","Compared with the vast expanses of yellow covering the map, these green dots were tiny and few.","But sparks could start a prairie fire. If they caught, perhaps they could spread across the entire wilderness.","“But...”","“Everyone also knows that even in our complex, given our current situation and the fact that supplies aren’t scarce, if I proposed that people leave the complex to fight zombies, how many would actually be willing to go? How many would follow?”","The six men fell silent.","This proposal was different from all their previous collective actions. Even if everyone understood that its ultimate goal was the right one, it was not like their earlier operations, which had directly involved the interests of Youth Apartment—directly eliminating danger, directly obtaining supplies, or directly creating a comfortable living environment and social order.","This proposal was too grand, too distant, and not immediate enough.","Abandoning the safety and stability they enjoyed and risking their lives to go outside and fight zombies demanded an extraordinary degree of moral courage and fighting spirit.","“Even if some people were passionate enough to volunteer, how would we convince Jixiang Garden to join us?”","“They’re so close by. Why should we be the ones doing the hard work, serving as cannon fodder and spearhead? Even I can’t answer that question.”","“If we can’t answer it, we can’t give everyone enough motivation.”","“We simply won’t be able to get everyone to charge out with us.”","Nie Kuizhang, the building head of Building Three, looked from one person to the next.","Jiang Cheng called him out directly. “Nie Kuizhang, you have something to say, don’t you?”","“That’s exactly it.” Nie Kuizhang boldly spoke his mind. “Why should we?”","Look at them: all six building heads were exceptionally capable, proactive, and even passionate people. Yet there was still someone among them who had been struck by Jiang Cheng’s words and shared precisely that kind of thinking.","Now that Nie Kuizhang had said it aloud, he wasn’t afraid anymore. Crossing his arms, he said, “I’m not afraid of dying. Everyone knows that. If we were doing this for our own complex, Jiang Cheng, you could tell me to charge, and I wouldn’t hesitate.”","“But if all the other complexes are lying low indoors and you want me to charge out there for their sake, then no. Why should I?”","The six building heads came from different professions and had different personalities, but not one of them was a coward. A coward couldn’t serve as a building head. If you didn’t lead from the front, the people in your building wouldn’t be willing to follow you.","This wasn’t an appointed position to begin with. The residents had elected them, and if they decided you weren’t up to the job, they could choose someone else.","Jiang Cheng narrowed her eyes at Nie Kuizhang. It was actually useful to have someone among her own people who thought this way. She had been wanting to ask.","“What kind of situation would make you willing to charge out? I’d like to know. I’m asking seriously.”","Nie Kuizhang waved his hand. “None. There’s no situation that would.”","Jiang Cheng showed no emotion. She merely nodded and was about to end the topic when another building head suddenly cut in.","“If the country called on us, I’d be willing.”","Jiang Cheng’s gaze snapped toward him.","The building head continued, “But if it’s just our complex getting carried away by its own enthusiasm, then I agree with Kuizhang. Why should we? It’s too unfair.”","The country?","Jiang Cheng asked, “What if the country called on us, but we were the only ones who responded, while the people in the other complexes still hid indoors?”","“Then that’s their business,” the building head said. “As long as the country calls, I’ll do it. Whether anyone else does it has nothing to do with me.”","Li Jiangbing immediately chimed in. “Right. I’ll do it too!”","Jiang Cheng was finally a little surprised to hear that from Li Jiangbing.","Li Jiangbing was a somewhat petty, street-smart, kindhearted, flawed common man who liked taking small advantages whenever he could. She hadn’t expected him to say something like that.","It was nobler than she would ever have imagined.","The other two building heads also said, “If the country calls on us, we’ll do it too.”","Finally, when Jiang Cheng’s gaze fell on Song Jingshuo, this obvious, polished self-interested elite unexpectedly nodded as well.","“I’m in.”","His tone was firm.","Even Li Jiangbing had straightened his chest when he said he would do it.","Did the word “country” carry such enormous power to rally the hearts of these native-born people?","Jiang Cheng couldn’t quite understand.","Because she was not a native of this world. She was a transmigrator from another universe.","Compared with “the nation,” she preferred the term “government.” It was much easier to understand—a group of people who did things, that was all.","But what exactly was “the nation,” and what did it mean to the natives? That was an unfamiliar concept to Jiang Cheng.","Of course, she still possessed all of Jiang Cheng’s memories. All the patriotic education she had received since childhood was still there.","But ever since her individual consciousness awakened for the second time last Sunday at noon, she had completely separated herself from “Jiang Cheng” within her mind.","Jiang Cheng’s consciousness now belonged entirely to her. All of “Jiang Cheng’s” memories and perceptions had been sealed away, like exhibits behind the glass cases of a museum: visible and clear, yet completely isolated.","At this point, even Nie Kuizhang awkwardly added, “Fine, then. If all of you are doing it, I’ll do it too.”","Nie Kuizhang had harassed He Tian. Compared with the others, he was a man with obvious moral flaws. And just now, he had clearly been unwilling. Even now, he still wasn’t particularly willing. But when everyone else was basking in the radiance of “the nation,” he seemed afraid to let himself fall behind.","“The nation” possessed more than just the power to rally people.","It also possessed the power to intimidate.","That power of intimidation naturally came from the military—or, as it could also be called, the armed forces.","In Jiang Cheng’s eyes, the military was simply another group of people: people who wielded power.","But in the minds of the natives of this world, they seemed to view the group called “the government” and the group called “the military” as a single organic entity.","No—included in that entity were the natives themselves. They considered themselves part of this organic whole as well.","The government, the military, and the natives together formed what they called “the nation.”","Jiang Cheng began to take an interest in “the nation.”","But this was not the right time. She had no intention of breaking through that layer of glass and touching “Jiang Cheng’s” perceptions just yet.","“So,” she said thoughtfully, “when all is said and done, our ability to rally people just isn’t strong enough?”","Li Jiangbing rubbed his crew cut. “We’re ordinary working-class people, after all.”","“Then if it were ‘the nation’ calling on them, would people from the other residential compounds respond?” she asked curiously. “Or would it just be you few getting carried away by patriotic fervor?”","Li Jiangbing gave a dry laugh. “Jiang Cheng, why do you sound like you never received any patriotic education? Do you really need to ask? Even if not everyone, there would definitely be plenty of Chinese people with enough backbone to answer the call.”","Jiang Cheng asked, “Then why doesn’t ‘the nation’ call on them?”","Her question sounded rather strange.","Song Jingshuo said, “The nation would obviously mobilize the military first. As long as the military is still around, there’s no need to mobilize the public. After all, this is something that could cost people their lives.”","He continued, “Isn’t the nation’s foremost responsibility to protect its people?”","[In a high-risk situation, pushing civilians forward as cannon fodder in order to preserve one’s own armed forces.]","Another wisp of such an awareness drifted through the crack in her mind. Jiang Cheng quickly suppressed it.","Because Song Jingshuo had said it with such complete certainty.","The natives all took it for granted that protecting civilians was the nation’s highest priority.","Ever since Jiang Cheng became aware that she was a transmigrator, she had already lived in this world for nearly three weeks. During those two and a half weeks, her life had been intensely concrete.","The first week had been an ordinary life of work and routine, dealing with colleagues, business partners, and clients.","The second week had plunged her into survival mode, fighting zombies. Even then, she had still been dealing with concrete individuals, or, at most, larger groups organized around residential compounds.","She had fit in perfectly throughout those two weeks.","But once the subject began to rise to the level of “the nation,” a tremendous gap emerged between the thoughts and perceptions of the transmigrator and those of the native residents."]},{"number":66,"title":"Chapter 66","paragraphs":["Jiang Cheng looked at the people before her.","They stood along the residential road just inside the east gate, with rows of trees and greenery on either side. Sunlight filtered through the leaves in tiny fragments, casting dappled shadows across their faces.","Some were handsome, some plain; some were heavyset, others thin. They were all ordinary people.","If you looked closely, each had their own personality, along with their own flaws and shortcomings.","But when the subject was elevated to this level, they suddenly seemed to become one and the same—as different people, yet believing in or placing their trust in the same thing.","Jiang Cheng would not use the word “faith” here, because she did not think this had reached the level of faith.","In fact, when she spoke with the six building captains, the memories and perceptions of “Jiang Cheng” could no longer remain completely separate from Jiang Cheng’s individual consciousness. They had already been triggered and activated.","The patriotic education. The news reports. The touching deeds. The people who had been honored.","The sacrifices and devotion.","Yet Jiang Cheng’s brain seemed to have split in two. One “her” was just like these people, while the other felt no reverence whatsoever toward words like “the nation.” Faith was out of the question. She could even clearly sense feelings of “distrust,” “wariness,” and “caution.”","Jiang Cheng had never been curious about her past.","She valued the present and the future—since I don’t know who I was before, I’ll simply live well in the here and now.","But now, for the first time, she felt curious about what kind of world she had come from and what sort of person she had been.","She could dig through the cracks in her mind and find not a single useful piece of information. But Jiang Cheng knew that her original world had to be different from this one.","Every world had nations, but the nation in her original world must never have done anything worthy of her respect or trust.","It was not the same as the “nation” here.","Beneath the sunlight falling through the gaps in the treetops, Jiang Cheng stood alone, facing everyone else.","A summer breeze stirred the air. Song Jingshuo sensed that something was wrong with Jiang Cheng’s expression. Puzzled, he called out to her, “Jiang Cheng?”","In an instant, his voice pulled Jiang Cheng back from her thoughts.","She could not be satisfied with huddling in a single residential complex, eating nothing but rice and pickles every day while waiting for rescue that might arrive at some unknown time.","This dissatisfaction flowed outward from her genes. It could not be stopped or suppressed.","This was not “Jiang Cheng.”","This was Jiang Cheng herself.","What Jiang Cheng’s eyes saw and what her mind considered had never been limited to one or two residential compounds, or one or two streets.","The map in her mind had always been fully open. It encompassed S City—and the entire country.","It was only that her personal abilities and the conditions she could currently make use of were limited to a single community.","This was not because Jiang Cheng was some selfless saint who wanted to save everyone.","It was because Jiang Cheng simply refused to accept ever being helpless or powerless in the face of any situation.","She could not accept being unable to control events, allowing events to control her instead.","This was Jiang Cheng.","This was the “self” that had become increasingly clear and fully formed as Jiang Cheng broke free from “Jiang Cheng.”","No matter what identity she had possessed in another world, she had become this kind of person.","It was just that, until a moment ago, she had not found any new power she could borrow to bring her ideas to life. And now, the few people standing before her had opened up a new line of thought.","Or rather, this line of thought happened to be a blind spot in her understanding—","The nation.","Jiang Cheng smiled at the people before her.","“Then let’s give it a try,” she said.","“...What?” Everyone failed to follow her train of thought.","In the group chat, people were complaining about the food.","They had been eating rice with canned food, salted duck eggs, or pickles for a week and a half. They were sick of it.","Su Yu typed: [I’m getting sick of it too, but when I think about it, at least we’re able to eat our fill every meal.]","The group responded with a chorus of lamentations:","[That’s true.]","[I don’t want to look at the other forums anymore. They’re terrifying.]","[Sigh...]","[I’m being spoiled. I’ll heat up another salted duck egg. No—actually, I need to ration my duck eggs too.]","[Same here. I regret eating so much canned meat last week. I can’t live without meat. If the canned meat runs out before the zombie problem is solved, I’ll cry myself to death. I should have rationed it and spread it out more evenly.]","[The broadcast is on.]","Su Yu tilted her head and listened. Sure enough, the broadcast had begun.","She hurriedly stood up and shuffled over in her slippers to open the door. That way, she could hear more clearly.","In the hallway, the neighbors opened their doors and came out one after another.","After a brief test of the audio, everyone heard the familiar voice of Jiang Cheng.","[I have some things to tell everyone—things you may not want to hear and may not want to know. But we can’t live in a vacuum. What’s happening outside is connected to our own safety.]","[If you don’t want to listen, you still have to listen.]","Jiang Cheng’s voice came through the broadcast, steady and unhurried, as she laid out the situation outside in detail.","Leaning against her doorway, Su Yu listened until she closed her eyes.","No wonder Jiang Cheng had said that even those who did not want to listen had to do so. These things were so painful that merely hearing them was enough to make the pain spread through one’s mind; there was no need to witness them in person.","She really wanted to cover her ears.","The girl in the group chat had been right. Complaining about being sick of salted duck eggs, pickles, and canned food was spoiled and ridiculous. Without food, people would truly die.","Su Yu had never been the sort of person who ignored others simply because she herself was doing well. Once her own basic survival was secured, her empathy made her feel deep pain and helplessness over the suffering of others.","But there was still a thread of hope in her heart.","She knew that Jiang Cheng would never tell them all this without a reason. Jiang Cheng must have some kind of plan.","Although Jiang Cheng occasionally made her uneasy, in Su Yu’s heart, Jiang Cheng had always seemed to possess an aura of light.","The air in the hallway seemed to grow heavy and dispirited. People’s emotions radiated like energy, affecting one another.","Everyone felt awful now.","[I want everyone to understand that calculating how many grams of rice and how many cans we consume each day, then relying on our stockpiles to last until rescue arrives, is actually an overly idealistic scenario.]","[Because those calculations fail to account for changes in the outside environment and the impact they may have.]","[In other words: “safety.”]","[If we only calculate food consumption, then the residents of Shanshui Yayuan should also be able to sleep soundly and wait for national rescue just as we are.]","[But what happened in reality? Several households in Shanshui Yayuan were slaughtered to the last person.]","[Compared with our neighbors, we do have a more united organization and greater fighting ability. But do we really want to wait until the day when the living turn against one another, when kitchen knives are hacked into other survivors?]","[If things reach that point, and the nation solves the zombie crisis and society returns to the way it was before, will those of us who have killed people still be able to return to our old lives?]","[Everyone, are we supposed to hide inside our little apartment complex and wait for all of this to happen?]","No! No!","A voice shouted inside Su Yu’s heart. She bit down hard on her lip.","Survival was certainly important, but she could never accept such an outcome.","But what could they do? Were they supposed to send everyone rushing outside to die?","But we couldn’t be the only ones in the entire community rushing out on a wave of hot-blooded courage. This wasn’t something one residential complex could solve, and no community’s residents were obligated to sacrifice themselves to save others.","This was no longer a moment when the military could fight alone. This was a war between humanity and monsters, between humanity and the zombies, and against an unknown virus.","It wasn’t about one person or one community. It was about every person, every community.","But I, Jiang Cheng, the owner of Unit 0306 in Building Two, don’t have the ability to mobilize everyone. So I intend to...","Contact the temporary emergency command center—specifically, the temporary emergency command center of S City.","On behalf of Youth Apartment, I will issue an appeal to the government.","Jiang Cheng said, “If the government accepts it, and if the government calls upon the people, I will answer that call without hesitation.”","“I also hope that, just as everyone has done in each collective action over the past week, you’ll pick up your weapons and walk out of this community with me.”","“Even if the other communities don’t respond right away, Youth Apartment will be the first community to answer the call.”","“Human beings live in groups, but most are sheep. There must be a lead wolf willing to step forward.”","Jiang Cheng asked all the residents of Youth Apartment to bear witness as she dialed the number from that morning.","The call was answered almost instantly.","Through the building’s broadcast system, everyone heard a fairly young man’s voice. “Youth Apartment? Jiang Cheng?”","Jiang Cheng had turned on the speakerphone so the residents of Youth Apartment could listen in.","“This is Jiang Cheng. Who am I speaking to?”","“I’m Vice Mayor Zheng’s temporary secretary. My surname is Sun.”","“Secretary Sun, hello. I’m calling on behalf of all the residents of Youth Apartment. I’d like to speak with Vice Mayor Zheng.”","Another man’s voice came through the phone, much deeper and more solemn. “Jiang Cheng, have you changed your mind?”","So when they saw “Youth Apartment” on the caller ID, they had also put the call on speaker.","No one could mistake that voice. Everyone had been keeping their televisions on and waiting for him to speak each day. They could all recognize it.","It really was Vice Mayor Zheng—the very man on television who now controlled the situation in S City.","Jiang Cheng could actually speak with him directly.","Her voice remained calm and unhurried. Even when speaking to a high-ranking official, she showed not the slightest trace of nervousness.","“I’m sorry, but I can’t do what you asked. If I did, the first thing we’d have to face would be resistance within the community, division, and escalating internal conflict. What I need right now is to preserve the group’s stability and build an effective fighting force.”","Vice Mayor Zheng was silent for a moment before acknowledging her point. “You’re right.”","“Then what is the purpose of your call?”","Everyone in the hallways unconsciously held their breath, as though afraid even the slightest noise might disturb the conversation.","“Vice Mayor Zheng, on behalf of all the residents of Youth Apartment, I’d like to make an appeal to the nation: it’s time to launch a people’s war.”","After Jiang Cheng spoke, silence filled both the broadcast system and the hallways.","Only after a moment did Vice Mayor Zheng’s voice slowly return, turning the phrase over in his mind.","“A people’s war...”","“Vice Mayor Zheng, the residents of our community are young people who have attended college, who have consciences, and who are well-educated.”","“They’re the kind of young people who wait for the light to turn green even when crossing the street.”","“If this drags on, the kitchen knives in their hands may soon be forced to turn against living people.”","“You understand the situation outside better than I do. By the time all of this happens, even if the zombies are eventually wiped out, these young people will never be able to return to who they were.”","“It will destroy an entire generation.”","“Mayor, don’t let this generation of young people be left with memories like that.”","“When peace and stability return, they should be able to look back with pride and say how many zombies they killed.”","“Not how many people.”","“Mayor, there’s no time left to hesitate.”","“If we regard the zombies as a natural disaster, then this disaster is unlike any that came before. It can no longer be resolved by the military alone.”","“The people must be mobilized.”"]},{"number":67,"title":"Chapter 67","paragraphs":["Su Yu’s blood was burning, and her eyes brimmed with tears.","She realized that, in truth, she had been waiting for this day ever since the zombie virus first broke out. As an individual, she was far too weak—but her faith was not.","She had been waiting for this day.","For every weak person to join together and become a powerful whole.","But Su Yu could never have imagined that Jiang Cheng, who seemed to her to be surrounded by an aura of light, actually had no sense of shared feeling with her at all.","Jiang Cheng simply had to try.","If this was the only path out of their predicament, then regardless of whether she believed in it, she had to force her way down it.","She refused to be trapped.","Everyone held their breath, but no sound came from the building’s broadcast system.","In truth, there had been no sound from the telephone.","Jiang Cheng was at the property management office, with the phone in her hand, so she could hear some faint background static coming through the receiver.","Vice Mayor Zheng remained silent.","Jiang Cheng looked down at her phone without the slightest hurry.","At last, Vice Mayor Zheng’s low voice sounded again. “Jiang Cheng... is it?”","“I understand. I’ve received your proposal.”","“But this isn’t a decision I can make. I’ll report it to the central authorities and put forward the proposal.”","“Little Jiang,” Vice Mayor Zheng said solemnly, “thank you.”","The call ended.","Su Yu stood in the doorway and listened as Jiang Cheng’s voice came over the broadcast system:","“I’ve done what I should do... and what I wanted to do.”","“From here on, we’ll see what happens.”","No one knew who started clapping first. Su Yu wiped away the tears at the corners of her eyes and began applauding as well.","Regardless of what decision the country made, as long as Jiang Cheng led the way, she would follow!","Su Yu made up her mind.","S City Emergency Command Center.","“She’s right,” Vice Mayor Zheng murmured.","His secretary did not dare say a word, waiting only for him to give an order.","Vice Mayor Zheng said, “We can’t continue looking at this situation through the lens of the past. This is completely different from anything we’ve faced before.”","It was nothing like floods, earthquakes, blizzards, or typhoons. Nothing like them at all.","“She’s right.” Vice Mayor Zheng raised his eyes. “We can’t let the people fall into the evil side of human nature as they struggle on their own.”","“That would be more serious than the deaths themselves.”","“Xiao Sun, put me through to the central authorities.”","Lively discussions broke out across the various group chats of the Youth Apartments.","As expected, someone soon declared, “I’m not going. I’ve only got one life.”","Someone immediately sneered, “I bet you’ve never helped clear out the zombies in our community, either. Whenever you went downstairs to buy supplies, you probably wedged yourself right into the middle of the crowd.”","A wave of mockery followed.","Quite a few people in the Youth Apartments had contributed to the community. Over the past few days, they had developed a sense of solidarity and cohesion. Some had displayed courage that would have been unimaginable in peacetime, breaking through their own limits and gaining an entirely new understanding of themselves.","As for those petty, selfish people who had never once gone downstairs to help, everyone looked down on them.","The man protested: “This isn’t something ordinary citizens should be doing in the first place. We should just stay put and avoid causing trouble for the country.”","Someone replied: “When the flood submerges the entire building, it won’t matter which room you hide in. You listened to what Jiang Cheng said, but you didn’t understand a word of it.”","Jiang Cheng belonged to very few group chats. She probably belonged to fewer groups than anyone else in the entire complex.","She was only in two: the management group for the provisional residents’ committee and the management group for Building Two.","But people kept forwarding her chat logs from all kinds of groups, large and small.","Song Jingshuo: “Overall, everyone seems to be pulling together now. That’s a good thing.”","“The only question is whether the government will really do this.”","Jiang Cheng typed back: “Those who have a grasp of the overall situation will make the right decision. Perhaps certain factors are preventing them from making it immediately, but sooner or later, they’ll do it. Otherwise, they don’t deserve to sit in that position.”","Song Jingshuo sat at home, looking at the words on his computer screen with a smile. He typed: “The way you talk makes you sound like some great figure who commands the winds and clouds of the world.”","Jiang Cheng smiled as well and casually replied: “Maybe I am.”","She was only joking.","That day, everyone sat in front of their televisions at the appointed time, waiting for the new announcement. But the television continued to play yesterday’s announcement on an endless loop.","“What’s going on today?” people wondered.","The residents of the Youth Apartments began speculating in their group chats:","“No way...”","“Could it be...?”","“It’s not impossible. She spoke directly with the vice mayor.”","“Does this count as taking our concerns straight to the highest authorities?”","Everyone knew that watching the government announcement each day had become a source of spiritual support for many people.","When more than twenty minutes passed without a new announcement, people began to grow anxious.","“What’s going on?”","“Are they just abandoning us?”","“Call the government hotline!”","Irritation and panic intertwined, leaving everyone restless and unable to sit still.","The ordinary people did not know that, at that very moment, in the capital’s Central Emergency Command Center, the leaders were listening to the final report from the head of the National Health Commission’s top expert panel.","“Based on the observation and dissection of four hundred samples, the genes of the infected have undergone irreversible mutations.”","“The control center is the brain. Destroying the brain or severing its connection to the body is the only way to completely eliminate an infected subject.”","“Because the infection is transmitted through highly concentrated blood exposure, second-degree exposure is sufficient to spread it.”","“This genetic mutation lies beyond our current understanding. In this field, we are essentially starting from a blank slate.”","The leader seated in the center asked, “Is it reversible?”","The expert shook his head. “We can’t do it. With our current level of technology, we can’t even understand the underlying mechanism.”","“Can we stop them on a large scale?”","The expert continued shaking his head. “None of our biochemical weapons are effective. Apart from large-scale explosions, we currently have no means of stopping them en masse. Tear gas, poisonous gas, and anesthetics are all useless. Unless an electric gun reaches a voltage capable of destroying the central nervous system, it won’t work either.”","The expert said, “You can think of them as dead people who can still move. Only destroying the brain or beheading them can stop them.”","“Dead people...” the leader sighed. “So many dead people...”","When they were alive, they had all been ordinary citizens.","The leader felt a pain that cut straight to the bone.","For someone in his position, even personal interests did not come first.","What mattered more was the kind of reputation he would leave behind in the history books.","Who wouldn’t want to leave a glorious name in history? Who would willingly make such agonizing decisions?","But someone had to make them.","The leader opened his eyes and calmly ordered, “Prepare the televised address.”","At last, more than thirty minutes late, the screen suddenly changed.","A face familiar to every person in the country appeared on the television—the Supreme Leader.","His familiar voice came through the speakers as well. It was the Supreme Leader’s first national address since the outbreak of the zombie virus.","“Fellow citizens, comrades:","“Today, I deliver this address with a heavy yet unwavering heart.","“Our country is facing an unprecedented and extraordinarily grave challenge...”","“Our family members, friends, and neighbors have been transformed by this virus into irrational, bloodthirsty monsters that prey on human flesh.”","“Following the suggestions of our citizens, we will officially name them ‘zombies.’”","For the first time, the government officially used the term “zombies.”","Jiang Cheng watched the person on television, resting her chin in her hand.","The change in terminology meant that the government had finally accepted that those who had mutated were no longer human.","【Our military, brave and fearless, has stood on the front lines, using flesh and blood to fight the zombies who have lost their humanity, sacrificing themselves without hesitation.】","【But this crisis has already exceeded the scope of what the government and military can resolve on their own.】","【It is unprecedented and unheard-of.】","【Our soldiers have already reached the limits of human courage.】","【However, to completely eliminate these threats and reclaim our living space, relying on them alone is not enough.】","【We have reached a moment that will determine the survival or destruction of our entire race.】","【This is a war between humanity and monsters for the right to survive.】","【It is everyone’s war.】","The speech played over footage of soldiers fighting on the front lines.","A soldier being tackled by a second-generation zombie.","A soldier using his own body to protect civilians.","A soldier who was bitten and infected, then took his own life with a gunshot.","While everyone complained, “Why hasn’t the rescue reached us yet?” the soldiers were risking their lives to push the boundaries of the safe zones forward.","Many people shed tears in front of their televisions, unable to hold back their sobs. Mothers hugged their children, husbands clasped their wives’ hands, and fathers rested a hand on their sons’ shoulders.","【We now call upon all citizens: tomorrow, Wednesday, June 26, at 9:00 a.m., take up your weapons and leave your homes.】","【Heaven helps those who help themselves; salvation comes to those who save themselves.】","【Our people and our nation stand as one. United, we are an impregnable fortress.】","【Victory is ours!】","The Supreme Leader’s voice echoed through the corridors of the Youth Apartments in the New Technology District.","To make things convenient for residents whose homes did not have televisions, the building’s public-address system had been connected to government broadcasts, allowing everyone to hear official announcements.","【Victory is ours!】","【Victory is ours!】","【Victory is ours—ours—】","The final note echoed through the hallway.","Inside Apartment 0306 of Building Two, Jiang Cheng’s lips curled into a smile.","Just as you wished, the nation has issued the call.","What about you? What happened to all of you who kept saying that you would rush out of your homes the moment the nation called?","Jiang Cheng opened the group chat. The messages were surging, with countless people calling for her.","【Jiang Cheng!】","【Jiang Cheng!】","【Jiang Cheng!】","【Jiang Cheng, say the word!】","Jiang Cheng smiled faintly and called Yang Xinyan in the group. As expected, Yang Xinyan was online. Who could possibly be offline at a time like this? After watching the broadcast, everyone was waiting eagerly for Jiang Cheng.","Jiang Cheng: 【Xinyan, send out a notification to everyone. Tell them to prepare protective gear and bring food. We’ll meet tomorrow at 8:30.】","Yang Xinyan: 【Got it!】","The screen was immediately flooded with messages saying 【Received!】.","When Su Yu heard the broadcast begin again, she hurried to open the door.","This time, the atmosphere in the hallway felt completely different.","One neighbor called out loudly, “So, eight-thirty tomorrow morning!”","Several people answered at once.","“Sounds good!”","“Okay!”","“It’s a deal!”","“See you tomorrow!”","Su Yu was filled with excitement. She loudly reminded the neighbors, “Don’t forget to prepare some food!”","Everyone had experience from their previous trip to the Fifth Ring Road to seize supplies. Any extended outing required them to bring their own food to replenish their strength.","The neighbors answered one after another. “I’ll go get it ready now.”","Inside Apartment 0308 of Building Two, Master Luo smoked a cigarette. When he finished, he said, “I’m going too tomorrow.”","Aunt Pan thought for a moment and said, “I’ll make some rice balls. I’ll wrap some canned meat inside.”","“Let’s bring two flasks of water as well.”","The couple had always been frugal. They each owned a water flask, so they wouldn’t have to buy drinks when they went out, saving money.","Master Luo said, “Why bring two? One is enough.”","“Then what am I supposed to drink?”","“...You’re going too?”","“I swung a hoe back in my hometown, and I swing a ladle here. I’m no weaker than you.”","“All right. We’ll go together.”"]},{"number":68,"title":"Chapter 68","paragraphs":["On the Wednesday of the second week after the zombie virus outbreak, the weather was poor. The sky was overcast, lending everything a distinctly tragic air.","Jiang Cheng went downstairs early, as she usually did. Since the crisis began, her schedule had become even stricter and more disciplined than before.","Song Jingshuo was the same.","They were the first and second people to arrive at the little garden square.","Jiang Cheng patted the head of Mo Li, who was inside her crossbody bag, then walked over and held out her fist to Song Jingshuo.","It was one of Li Jiangbing’s favorite gimmicks, though Jiang Cheng and Song Jingshuo rarely did it themselves. This time, however, Song Jingshuo didn’t hesitate. He raised his hand and bumped fists with her.","Jiang Cheng asked, “How many people do you expect will come?”","“I can’t predict that,” Song Jingshuo replied.","Jiang Cheng smiled.","People began coming downstairs.","Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan lived in different buildings, but they arrived one right after the other. The two had called each other before leaving.","Peng Ze came with a look of grim determination.","Li Jiangbing was down fairly early as well.","The building managers had all arrived ahead of time. The only one missing was Nie Kuizhang.","Many familiar faces appeared, greeting one another and asking what everyone had brought for lunch. Rice balls were by far the food mentioned most often.","Master Luo and his wife came over and greeted Jiang Cheng. “We’re going too.”","More and more people filled the square.","Su Yu came downstairs pulling a handcart piled high with magazines. “Has anyone not finished preparing their protective gear? I’ve got magazines here.”","The fashion and film magazines had once been her beloved collection. Now, in addition to their entertainment value, they had acquired a far more practical use. Taped around the arms, they had proven highly effective protection against zombie bites.","So far, no one at Youth Apartments had ever had a magazine-wrapped arm bitten through.","Paper really was an incredible thing.","When the employees of Maidouduo moved into Youth Apartments yesterday, Li Jiangbing and the others had followed the principle of taking everything they could carry and brought over a large quantity of supplies from Maidouduo. Among them was tape.","Those without protective equipment crowded around Su Yu to collect magazines and tape. Everyone helped one another wrap the magazines around their arms and legs.","Jiang Cheng didn’t need to make any further mobilizing speech. The moment people were willing to come downstairs, they had already made up their minds.","Song Jingshuo scanned the crowd and finally spotted Nie Kuizhang, the building manager of Building Three. He had come too. With that, all six building managers were present.","He glanced at his watch. It was 8:51.","At that moment, Jiang Cheng’s phone suddenly rang. She looked at the caller ID and answered. “Brother Zhou?”","The caller was Zhou Wang from Auspicious Garden.","“I saw that your community has gathered,” Zhou Wang said. “We’ve gathered too. Where are you starting? We’d like to go with you.”","“We’re planning to start outside the west gate,” Jiang Cheng replied. “We’ll clear the road circling the community first.”","The east gate of Youth Apartments led to Auspicious Garden, while the west gate opened onto a roadside park.","There were zombies in the park as well. The last time they had driven their private cars to Station 535, they had run over quite a few along the way. But since they had never cleared the park systematically, there were certainly still zombies left.","Jiang Cheng continued, “We’ll clear the road around the community first, then move on to the mixed-use building to the south.”","“Let’s do it together,” Zhou Wang said.","Jiang Cheng agreed. “All right.”","The roads were connected in any case. The communities were laid out in neat squares, with streets running through them in a grid. There was no such thing as “your road” or “our road.”","Following the instructions, the security guard at the east gate opened it and let the people from Auspicious Garden in.","They were considerably fewer in number than the residents of Youth Apartments, though that was understandable. Auspicious Garden was a standard residential community with people of all ages, and most of those who had come were able-bodied men.","Even Little Huang, a skinny middle-school student, had come along.","Applause suddenly broke out at Youth Apartments, warmly welcoming the newcomers from Auspicious Garden.","At that moment, all the previous disagreements and barriers seemed to vanish. Everyone became one—not residents of one community or another, but simply human beings who were still alive.","Jiang Cheng narrowed her eyes as she watched it all.","The core members from both sides had joined forces as well. Jiang Cheng noticed that these men—whether they were older brothers or uncles—seemed somewhat different from a week ago. But so many people had been changed over the past few days that it was hardly surprising.","Song Jingshuo checked his watch. “It’s time.”","Everyone turned to look at Jiang Cheng.","The people from Auspicious Garden were still somewhat astonished by this young girl’s ability to rally others. How could the central leader of a community of more than a thousand people be a young woman?","Jiang Cheng drew the fire axe from the small of her back and raised it high.","Everyone held their breath.","She brought the axe down through the air and announced, “Move out!”","A roar erupted from the crowd.","“Let’s go!”","“Move out!”","“We can’t go on living like this!”","“That’s right!”","Humanity was going to reclaim its living space.","Su Yu tightened her grip on her steel pipe. He Tian held a kitchen knife, while several other girls naturally clustered together.","Li Jiangbing instructed them, “Just stay behind me. Don’t get too close to the front.”","The girls whispered among themselves, “He seems pretty reliable.”","Su Yu had been looked after by Li Jiangbing more than once. She nodded. “He’s a good guy.”","He Tian said, “Yeah. Unlike some people.”","Most people had grouped up with residents from their own buildings, since they knew one another better.","He Tian had deliberately come over to join Su Yu because she didn’t want to stay near Nie Kuizhang.","The west gate opened, and the main force set out.","Meanwhile, a few stragglers from Auspicious Garden were still hurrying over through the east gate.","The security guard was speechless. “Couldn’t you all come together?”","He wasn’t taking part in the group operation, but he had grown accustomed to the order and discipline of Youth Apartments’ actions. Compared with that, the loose and scattered way Auspicious Garden operated made him feel that inferior goods should simply be discarded when compared with better ones.","But there was nothing to be done. Many people hesitated and wavered. Only after seeing so many others leave, realizing which way the crowd’s heart was turned, and being swept up in the atmosphere could they finally grit their teeth, stamp their feet, and follow.","The important thing was that they came.","The roadside park wasn’t very large. It had only been built a few years earlier, so the trees were still small and didn’t obstruct the view.","Drawn by the noise, the zombies rushed toward them. The suicide squad leading Youth Apartments’ forces worked together with practiced coordination. The U-shaped forks needed no explanation, and the cabinet doors modified by Cui Haiyang and the other engineering-minded men had been fitted with handles for easier use. They were practically rectangular shields, and they worked extremely well.","The shield bearers had the best protective gear.","With nothing to do in the community these past few days, the engineering-minded men had spent their time racking their brains over such equipment. Using the limited tools available through the property management office, they had developed all kinds of protective gear, which was now being given to the suicide squad.","Everyone had finally realized that the best way to fight zombies was through overwhelming numbers.","Fully armed and facing the charging zombies, even if one person made a mistake, the weapons of those beside them would immediately reach out. Most of the time, a single strike was enough to kill a zombie.","There were simply too many people. Before those at the back had even made it out through the west gate, the people at the front had already cleared the roadside park.","The residents of Youth Apartments and Auspicious Garden had joined forces, forming a formidable fighting force.","After setting out from the west gate of Youth Apartments and clearing the roadside park, they turned south and began moving along the small road that encircled the community.","With Jixiang Jiayuan joining the effort—and with the two residential communities already connected into one larger safe zone after the streets of Jixiang West had been blocked off—the planned route now included Jixiang Jiayuan as well.","But even so, there were still far too many people.","When they reached the turn toward South Street, the group split into two. Half of them would circle the two communities, clearing the streets around them. The other half headed for the commercial-residential building south of the communities.","Jiang Cheng, Song Jingshuo, Li Jiangbing, and Wu Jiancheng remained with the group circling the communities. Nie Kuizhang, Peng Ze, and Zhang Tao separated from them and went to the commercial-residential building.","Everyone gripped their weapons tightly, their gazes resolute as they followed the people leading the way.","Including Jiang Cheng, they all shrank into a mass of dark heads on the surveillance screens.","Vice Mayor Zheng stared at the screens. As he watched more and more people gather and organize themselves, they finally overcame their fear, selfishness, and wishful thinking under the call to action and began saving themselves.","The surveillance operators continuously relayed new information.","“People from xx Community, xx Jiayuan... Everyone in the area from xx Street to xx Street is coming out!”","“People from xx East Neighborhood and xx West Neighborhood are out too!”","“We can see people on xx Street!”","The voices rose and fell one after another.","Ordinary citizens picked up their weapons and walked out of their homes.","Even those who had once been timid, cowardly, or selfish were given strength and courage the moment they became part of a collective under the nation’s call.","And it wasn’t happening only in S City. At that very moment, the same scene was unfolding across the country.","Cities, county towns, villages, and townships!","It was like something that belonged only in the history books. No one had expected to witness it with their own eyes in their lifetime.","Vice Mayor Zheng’s eyes grew damp.","On the morning of June 27, the half of the residents led by Jiang Cheng cleared the streets surrounding the two communities.","When they reached the southeast side of Jixiang Jiayuan, they encountered the residents of Yujing Xiangyuan.","In the past, they had merely been strangers brushing past one another on the street.","In recent days, the people from Youth Apartments had sneered at Yujing Xiangyuan’s disorganized leadership, while the residents of Yujing Xiangyuan had cursed Youth Apartments and Jixiang Jiayuan for clearing out Mai Duoduo.","Yet when people from all three communities unexpectedly met at this street corner, they actually broke into cheers.","“It’s Yujing Xiangyuan!”","“Jixiang Jiayuan!”","“And Youth Apartments too!”","They had cleared less than a kilometer of street, but it felt like a momentous victory—a grand reunion of allied forces.","Jiang Cheng and Zhou Wang quickly conferred with Yujing Xiangyuan’s leader, clarifying the directions and areas each group would be responsible for clearing. Then everyone split up again and continued forward in their respective directions.","With people from Youth Apartments and Jixiang Jiayuan present, the residents of Yujing Xiangyuan no longer needed to worry about Jixiang East Street, which was shared by Yujing Xiangyuan and Jixiang Jiayuan. Jiang Cheng, Zhou Wang, and the others headed that way, while the Yujing Xiangyuan residents went in the opposite direction.","Viewed from above, one would have seen a sea of dark heads splitting off at the intersection.","The streets were open, with clear lines of sight, allowing people to gather and form an effective defensive formation. As a result, the likelihood of injury was relatively low.","Even so, people were still injured inside the commercial-residential building south of Youth Apartments.","As the name suggested, the building contained both commercial and residential spaces. Only a small portion of it was occupied by residents; most of the tenants ran small businesses. There were beauty salons, gyms, dental clinics, and all kinds of other establishments.","The interior was divided into spaces that followed no standard layout. Everything depended on how each business had chosen to renovate its unit.","In such an environment, it was impossible for a large number of people to gather and create an effective defense with virtually no blind spots.","Injuries were ultimately unavoidable.","The first person injured was someone Jiang Cheng knew well: Peng Ze from Building Three.","The head of Building Three, Nie Kuizhang, shouted, “Peng Ze—”","The few zombies already had their skulls smashed in. They were thoroughly dead.","Peng Ze covered his injured ear. When he took his hand away, his palm was covered in blood.","Peng Ze felt as though he could hear his own heartbeat.","Thump. Thump. Thump. Thump.","Each beat was clear and enormous."]},{"number":69,"title":"Chapter 69","paragraphs":["As the floor captain of Building Three, Nie Kuizhang actually rather liked Peng Ze.","Or rather, among the people on the residents’ committee who knew Peng Ze, no one disliked him.","Peng Ze wasn’t a young man with any particularly outstanding qualities. He wasn’t as handsome and capable as Song Jingshuo, who could get along with everyone and handle any situation. Nor was he as burly and forceful as Li Jiangbing or Nie Kuizhang, with their imposing presence. And unlike Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan, he didn’t have any professional skills that could directly benefit the complex.","But he was always the first to throw himself into action. He responded enthusiastically and supported every decision without hesitation.","Anyone who took part in group operations with him quickly got to know him and came away with a good impression.","He was the kind of person everyone was happy to team up with.","After the incident in which Nie Kuizhang harassed He Tian, whenever the girls in Building Three needed something, they went to Peng Ze instead. None of them sought out Nie Kuizhang anymore.","The girls all trusted Peng Ze’s character, too.","No one had expected him to be the first one injured.","Everyone in the room stood where they were, weapons in hand. No one moved.","They all knew what would happen after being bitten, and they knew how it had to be handled.","The Youth Apartments had been very secure, and even the people who frequently went out on missions had managed to avoid injury. Injury, forced quarantine, and death were things they had gone through only a little over a week ago. Yet in their memories, it all seemed so distant.","And now, suddenly, Peng Ze had been injured.","“Peng Ze...” Nie Kuizhang called.","Peng Ze looked up at him.","Nie Kuizhang’s eyes said everything. He even glanced at the people around him.","Peng Ze gave a bitter smile.","“Old Nie,” he said. “Don’t waste your breath. I won’t be going back.”","Forced quarantine in the complex was meant to prevent people from turning and injuring others—one bite becoming two, two becoming four. But they weren’t at the Youth Apartments now.","Everyone looked toward Nie Kuizhang.","Nie Kuizhang felt awful, too.","He had become the captain of Building Three because he was big, brave, and ruthless enough to command respect.","A week and a half ago, on the Sunday and Monday when the zombies had first appeared, he had been able to drive the injured to the property management office or lock them inside their own apartments with firm, merciless resolve. At that time, everyone had barely had the chance to get to know one another.","But things were different now. They had all grown so familiar.","Peng Ze was exceptionally diligent. Jiang Cheng liked him. Song Jingshuo liked him. Li Jiangbing liked him. Nie Kuizhang liked him, too.","He took part in everything, without missing a single thing. He was always busier than everyone else, and he never once complained.","As the captain of Building Three, Nie Kuizhang dealt with Peng Ze practically every day and was often by his side.","Affection grew out of time spent together.","Everyone present was from Building Three. Since they lived in the same building, they practiced formations together, fought zombies together, and joined group operations together.","So they were all very close to Peng Ze.","They looked at him, each of them struggling with the pain of it.","Nie Kuizhang’s lips moved. “You...”","Peng Ze sniffed, steadied himself, and said resolutely, “Call security. Tell them I can’t go back into the complex. Everyone from the property office knows me. They’re all familiar with me.”","That way, everyone could put their minds at ease.","Jiang Cheng and Su Yu, Li and Song...","Nie Kuizhang pulled out his phone and called the property office. “Little Yang? Notify the guards at both the east and west entrances. Peng Ze from Building Three has been injured. If they see him, don’t let him in.”","Yang Xinyan was on duty at the property office. She was stunned. “Peng Ze?”","“Yes, Peng Ze. You know him, right?”","“Y-Yes, I know him.”","“Notify the guards.” Nie Kuizhang paused, then added, “And call Jiang Cheng, too. Tell her Peng Ze isn’t coming back.”","Yang Xinyan hung up and stood there blankly for several seconds before tears began to fall.","Master Luo and Aunt Pan had gone out today, too. So many people had gone.","She had been assigned to remain at the property office.","She knew there was no way everyone could come back unharmed. It was inevitable that someone would get hurt.","But she hadn’t expected it to be someone she knew so well.","The property office had always been short-handed, and sometimes Yang Xinyan had to do physical work as well. Whenever Peng Ze saw her struggling, he would lend a hand or help out.","That was another reason the girls all had such a good impression of him.","Yang Xinyan wiped her eyes and notified the guards first.","Over the radio, the guards sighed as well. “Peng Ze...”","They all knew him.","Yang Xinyan then called Jiang Cheng.","Song Jingshuo was standing beside Jiang Cheng. When he heard her phone ring, he turned to look—and saw her expression stiffen for an instant.","“Who is it?” Jiang Cheng asked.","Yang Xinyan could only repeat what she had been told. “Peng Ze. Nie Kuizhang said Peng Ze isn’t coming back.”","It was the first time Song Jingshuo had seen Jiang Cheng reveal such a stunned expression.","Jiang Cheng was extremely good at managing both her emotions and her facial expressions, something Song Jingshuo had always admired.","But at that moment, Jiang Cheng’s emotions slipped through. Song Jingshuo suddenly felt that this was rather good, too. It made her seem more human.","He watched Jiang Cheng put away her phone. “What happened?”","Jiang Cheng slipped the phone back into her pocket. After a brief pause, she answered, “Peng Ze was injured. He isn’t coming back.”","Peng Ze?","All of Song Jingshuo’s superfluous, useless thoughts scattered at once. He understood what had caused Jiang Cheng’s expression just now.","His lips moved, and his heart was filled with pain.","In the midst of the crowd, he and Jiang Cheng met each other’s eyes for a moment.","Jiang Cheng rotated her wrist, twirling the fire ax in a flourish, then turned around. “Let’s go.”","Song Jingshuo silently followed.","Inside the commercial-residential building, Peng Ze held out the steel pipe. “I should return this, right? I won’t have any use for it anymore.”","Nie Kuizhang didn’t take it. He sighed. “Keep it. We’re not short one pipe.”","“All right.” Peng Ze pulled it back. “Then I’m leaving.”","Nie Kuizhang stepped aside.","The others stepped aside as well.","Peng Ze walked out of the office.","There were people in the corridor, too. When they saw the blood covering Peng Ze’s ear and face, they were shocked, and someone instinctively raised a weapon.","Nie Kuizhang followed him out and shouted, “Let him go! Let him go!”","The others exchanged looks, then cleared a path.","Peng Ze passed through the crowd. When he reached the stairwell, he turned back for one last look. Everyone was watching him.","“Everyone, be careful,” Peng Ze said at last. After thinking for a moment, he added, “If you run into me again, make it quick.”","He said it with a smile, trying to make one final joke.","Unfortunately, no one else laughed.","He looked a little disappointed, then turned and went downstairs.","Once he left the building, Peng Ze’s smile disappeared, leaving him only bewildered.","Where was he supposed to wait for death?","He turned and looked around. Farther south along the road, he saw several zombies.","Forget it. He might as well kill a few more before he died and save everyone else some effort.","Peng Ze gripped the steel pipe and walked south toward the zombies. His body was completely relaxed. Now that he had already been injured, he wasn’t afraid of being hurt again.","But as he approached, the zombies only swayed slowly toward him. They didn’t lunge.","Peng Ze paused, startled.","He stood still. The two were clearly ordinary zombies. They shambled right past him.","They treated him as though he were nothing more than air.","So that was it.","With a bitter smile, Peng Ze touched his wound. Now he understood.","By the time he had come downstairs, the virus had already invaded his body, even though he had not yet begun to mutate. The zombies now recognized him as one of their own.","Peng Ze turned around and smashed the heads of the two zombies.","He headed in that direction, killing any zombies he encountered along the way. The zombies did not attack him. Even two second-generation zombies left him alone. At that moment, fighting zombies was nothing more than a one-sided slaughter for him.","After walking for a while, he turned around and looked back. He was already some distance from the mixed-use building.","He sat down on the curb by the roadside and stared blankly into space for a long time, until he heard some noise. He stood up and looked into the distance, where he saw a crowd of people.","They were residents from another housing complex.","Without a second thought, Peng Ze turned and ran.","Why was he running? He could not explain it himself.","Was he afraid that he would mutate and hurt others, or was he afraid that people would see his injuries and come to eliminate him?","Perhaps it was both.","He spotted a car parked at an angle by the roadside, its door hanging open. When he went over to check, he found that the key was still in the ignition.","Peng Ze climbed inside, started the engine, and stepped on the gas.","He did not know where he was going. In any case, he decided to head away from the city center and away from the crowds.","The farther, the better.","The car left the Technology New District and headed north—north, then farther north.","By the end of the day, as dusk approached, the streets around Jixiang Jiayuan, Qingnian Apartments, Yujing Xiangyuan, and MaiduoDuo had been more or less cleared of zombies.","Jiang Cheng and Zhou Wang discussed it and decided to meet with the people in charge of Yujing Xiangyuan to work out how everyone should cooperate or divide up the work the following day.","However, they soon discovered that Yujing Xiangyuan had no single person in charge. The residents were divided into several groups, and no one knew exactly how they had organized themselves.","After considerable effort, they managed to find several representatives, and the three housing complexes sat down together to discuss what to do the next day.","“Let’s go to Lekang Jiayuan,” Zhou Wang proposed.","Everyone turned to look at him.","Zhou Wang said calmly, “Since everyone’s already willing to risk their lives, let’s save them. We’ll save as many as we can.”","Lekang Jiayuan was in the worst condition of all the nearby communities. Its residents could barely leave their apartments; in many buildings, they could not even make it downstairs.","More than one person had already committed suicide out of despair.","In the past, everyone had only looked after themselves. But now that they had answered the nation’s call and were willing to risk their lives killing zombies, they could no longer stand by and do nothing.","Several people from Jixiang Jiayuan appeared to have no objections to Zhou Wang’s proposal. It seemed that Zhou Wang now commanded considerable respect within the complex.","The few representatives from Yujing Xiangyuan exchanged glances.","Representing Qingnian Apartments were Jiang Cheng, Song Jingshuo, and Wu Jiancheng.","Jiang Cheng was somewhat surprised that Zhou Wang’s first thought had been to save people.","She actually had another plan. Saving people was not her top priority. She had already discussed it with the key members of the temporary committee in the group chat the previous night.","Jiang Cheng fell silent in thought.","“Little Jiang, what do you think?” Zhou Wang asked.","He had asked Jiang Cheng first.","After all, it was Jiang Cheng who had originally led the residents of Qingnian Apartments to help Jixiang Jiayuan. Without them, Jixiang Jiayuan might have ended up in the same state as Lekang Jiayuan.","Jiang Cheng said, “Lekang Jiayuan isn’t very large. We don’t need residents from all three complexes to go. Besides, they must be desperately short of food. If we help them clear out the zombies, what happens afterward? Are we going to give them food?”","It was a serious problem.","Food was a red line—an extremely sensitive issue.","The residents of both Jixiang Jiayuan and Yujing Xiangyuan had gone hungry before, and people had died over food.","The representatives from Yujing Xiangyuan exchanged glances again.","Zhou Wang had dealt with Jiang Cheng for quite some time and knew she was a woman with her own ideas. He asked directly, “What do you have in mind?”","Jiang Cheng did, in fact, have a plan. She pulled a map out of her shoulder bag—from beneath Mo Li, who was sitting on top of it—and spread it across a roadside flower bed.","She had already had an idea the previous night. Zhou Wang’s proposal to help Lekang Jiayuan did not interfere with it; they only needed to make a few adjustments.","“We don’t need people from all three complexes, but it wouldn’t be fair to send only one complex’s residents. I suggest that all three of us organize a team to rescue Lekang Jiayuan. As for everyone else...”","A stretch of road on the map had already been marked with a line in permanent marker.","Jiang Cheng moved her fingertip along the line. “The others can split into a vehicle convoy and a foot team. The convoy goes first, with the foot team following behind, and they clear this route. That way...”","Their shoulders pressed together and their heads crowded around the map. Now they could all see it clearly.","“It’ll connect us to the Fifth Ring Road!”"]},{"number":70,"title":"Chapter 70","paragraphs":["“The day before yesterday, every residential compound sent people out to the Fifth Ring Road to collect supplies. Quite a few vehicles took this route, so a considerable portion of it has already been cleared,” Jiang Cheng said.","But at the time, everyone’s destination had been the supply drop-off point on the Fifth Ring Road. Not a single vehicle had stopped along the way.","The zombies that could be run over had been killed. The others that had chased after the vehicles had eventually stopped when they could no longer keep up.","However, all that chasing had drawn out many of the zombies from the buildings on both sides of the road. So now, the road was filled with aimlessly wandering zombies.","“One group will deal with Lekang Garden, while another clears this road completely.”","This had been Jiang Cheng’s original plan for the route, and adding Lekang Garden to it would not be a problem.","“At the same time, we’ll contact the emergency command center and ask them to provide material support.”","“The real key to the rescue effort is still the army. We don’t have the ability to conjure supplies out of thin air. Right now, supplies have to be brought in from outside.”","The people from Yujing Xiangyuan were surprised. “Will the command center even listen to us if we contact them?”","Jiang Cheng looked up. “How will we know if we don’t try? I can get through to Vice Mayor Zheng’s secretary.”","“Huh?”","Jiang Cheng continued, “Why did the government mobilize the public in the first place? Because the army can’t push forward, or at least not quickly enough. We already know that at least the Fifth Ring Road is open. If we clear a route leading to the ring road, the army won’t need to advance slowly.”","As she spoke, Jiang Cheng placed a fingertip on the map at Nancheng’s Qing District, dragged it toward the Fifth Ring Road, then drew half a circle along the southern and northern sections of the Fifth Ring Road before moving her finger back to where they were now.","Zhou Wang was the first to speak. “I agree.”","The people from Yujing Xiangyuan remained doubtful. “You can really get through to the vice mayor’s secretary?”","Jiang Cheng’s voice was calm. “I can call him right now.”","“Little Jiang, go ahead and make the call,” Zhou Wang said. “Whether it works or not, we’ll do this with you.”","Jiang Cheng was a young woman, while Zhou Wang had already dealt with her before and understood what she was capable of. The people from Yujing Xiangyuan only knew that Youth Apartment was well organized. They still had doubts about this exceedingly young—and exceedingly beautiful—woman.","People, especially men, were often bound by stereotypes. How could a girl who was both so young and so beautiful possibly take charge on her own?","Sometimes, people simply needed to borrow the force of others’ influence.","With everyone watching, Jiang Cheng dialed Secretary Sun’s number.","The moment Secretary Sun answered, he called her by name. “Jiang Cheng?”","The background was filled with noise.","Not every matter had to be brought directly to the top official. Besides, a vice mayor’s secretary was not the sort of secretary who merely booked flights and arranged accommodations. A vice mayor’s secretary was a reserve candidate for the position of vice mayor.","“Hello, Secretary Sun.” Jiang Cheng went straight to the point. “I’m representing Youth Apartment, Jixiang Jiayuan, and Yujing Xiangyuan. I’d like to report our situation to you.”","Secretary Sun’s voice was slightly hoarse, as though he had spoken too much. “Go ahead.”","Jiang Cheng briefly explained the situation, then added, “At present, the area from Huawei Road in the east to Hongguang Road in the west, and from Beidaying Road in the north to Sitong Road in the south, is already a safe zone. At least the streets are.”","Secretary Sun asked, “How long do you estimate it will take to clear the route to the Fifth Ring Road? I require there to be no moving zombies left on the road, at minimum.”","The moment he said this, everyone realized that he truly had the authority to make such arrangements.","Jiang Cheng made a rough estimate and promised, “Before four this afternoon.”","Secretary Sun only took a few seconds to think before making his own promise. “If you can do it, I’ll send one or two supply trucks over.”","That would solve Lekang Garden’s supply problem.","Jiang Cheng was about to agree when Secretary Sun continued, “If you can keep this route open and clear out a suitable site, I can establish a supply line to your area and station a supply depot there.”","The moment Secretary Sun said this, everyone held their breath.","His voice was deep and heavy. “Jiang Cheng, we’re not short on supplies. What we’re short on is people.”","The country’s strategic grain reserves were enough to feed the entire population for two years.","The problem now was that the supplies could not be delivered into the hands of ordinary citizens.","The country had two million active-duty soldiers.","That sounded like a lot. In the past, whether dealing with an earthquake or a flood, it would have been enough to carry out rapid, efficient, large-scale disaster relief. Even if faced with an attack or invasion by another country, it would surely have been sufficient.","But this time, it was not.","Even soldiers with bodies of iron could not withstand the zombie virus. Zombies transformed from soldiers—especially second-generation zombies—were far stronger than ordinary second-generation zombies.","Military bases, where large numbers of people lived together, had become severely affected areas. The losses had been devastating.","Not to mention that this zombie crisis was nationwide. Apart from uninhabited regions, no place had been spared. Even if the million-strong army had suffered no casualties at all, spreading them across this vast land would have been like scattering mercury across the ground—it would disappear in an instant.","A number in the millions was still far too small when compared with the entire country.","In the end, they still had to rely on the people.","Thankfully, the people could be counted on.","And the request Jiang Cheng had made happened to align perfectly with the command center’s current strategy: open supply routes and deliver materials into the hands of ordinary citizens.","After ending the call, Secretary Sun closed his phone.","There was a table in the center of the hall, covered by an enormous map of S City. Vice Mayor Zheng was standing there, along with many staff members who were busy recording and reporting the day’s situation in various districts.","Secretary Sun squeezed through the crowd and placed a finger on a location in the technology development zone outside the northern section of the Fifth Ring Road. “Send them a supply truck tomorrow.”","The staff member immediately recorded it.","Vice Mayor Zheng was listening to a report when his gaze shifted over. “The technology development zone? Youth Apartment? How are they doing?”","“Quite well,” Secretary Sun replied. “Little Jiang called me to request assistance. They’re planning to rescue a nearby residential compound that has fallen. It hasn’t received any supplies so far, and they’re worried there won’t be anything to eat once they get the residents out.”","Vice Mayor Zheng was deeply pleased. “Those young people have compassion.”","As long as the younger generation still had a conscience, the country would have hope, no matter what kind of hardship it faced.","Vice Mayor Zheng did not know that he had praised the wrong people.","It was not that the young people from Youth Apartment had no conscience. But neither Jiang Cheng nor Song Jingshuo—or anyone else—had actually intended to rescue Lekang Garden in the first place. What they wanted was to connect the technology development zone to the Fifth Ring Road, thereby establishing a link to the government.","Young people had grown accustomed to living independently and were far more atomized than middle-aged people. Compared with saving others, they were more concerned with saving themselves.","“Brother Zhou...” On the way back, Song Jingshuo sighed. “I really see him differently now.”","Compared with young people, older people still had more of a sense of human warmth.","Who would have thought that he would still think of Lekang Garden?","After Secretary Sun said that a supply depot could be stationed there, no one objected to the plan anymore.","Youth Apartment, Zhou Wang, and Yujing Xiangyuan had reached a basic agreement. Now they needed to go back and arrange manpower for the next day.","Jixiang West Street was packed with people.","Because the east gate of Youth Apartments and the west gate of Auspicious Garden both opened onto this street, Auspicious Garden had adopted the same policy as Youth Apartments: everyone had to undergo a full-body inspection before entering the complex.","Likewise, with so many people returning at once, it was impossible for just a few people to search them one by one. Instead, they checked one another in pairs. Groups of four, six, eight, or ten entered together.","There were too many people at the east gate, so Jiang Cheng, Song Jingshuo, and Wu Jiancheng went around to the west gate. There was quite a crowd there too, but the area was more open. Auspicious West Street was too narrow, and being squeezed in there was uncomfortable.","“Jiang Cheng!” someone suddenly called.","Jiang Cheng looked over and saw Su Yu, He Tian, and two other girls approaching. Their eyes were all red.","Su Yu asked Jiang Cheng for confirmation. “Peng Ze was injured, wasn’t he?”","“He’s not coming back, is he?”","“What Jiang Jiangbing told us—is it true?”","Li Jiangbing had returned ahead of Jiang Cheng and the others to organize the main group’s return to the complex. He was the one who had told Su Yu about it.","To avoid Nie Kuizhang, He Tian had not stayed with the people from her own building. Instead, she had come with Su Yu.","The other girls were shocked when they heard the news as well.","Everyone knew that it was impossible for no one to be injured, but when the person was someone they knew, someone familiar and deeply fond of, it was still unbearably painful.","Song Jingshuo instinctively looked at Jiang Cheng again. He didn’t know why he was always unable to stop himself from watching her.","Perhaps it was because Jiang Cheng was simply too calm.","Of course, Jiang Cheng could laugh and joke like anyone else. But when things grew worse—when the situation deteriorated and everyone else became more panicked—she only grew calmer.","Only this time, after hearing the news about Peng Ze, her control over her emotions was not as flawless as usual.","Perhaps it was because Peng Ze’s presence had been too strong.","There was nothing particularly outstanding about him. But whenever Jiang Cheng had an important decision to discuss, she would call for Song Jingshuo. Whenever she needed someone to put in physical effort or use force, she would call for Li Jiangbing.","Other than that, the person she called most often was almost always Peng Ze.","It wasn’t even Zhao Yi. Zhao Yi was responsible for tasks that required him to be present every day. Peng Ze, on the other hand, was always with Jiang Cheng. Whenever something happened and his name was called, he would rush over immediately.","Jiang Cheng was silent for a moment before answering briefly, “Yes.”","The girls all burst into tears.","He Tian asked, “He’s really not coming back?”","Jiang Cheng did not answer.","No matter how hard He Tian tried to hold them back, her tears still fell. She wiped her face and turned to run.","The other girls chased after her.","Peng Ze was not the only one who had failed to return.","None of those who had been injured this time came back. They all knew what would happen if they returned, so there was no reason to come back.","The people who had been with them did not stop them from leaving either.","Go somewhere else. Mutate quietly. Be put down quietly by strangers.","That was still better than forcing people who knew them to take action.","They had all grown so familiar with one another. It was simply too difficult.","Jiang Cheng pushed those emotions aside. She still had plenty to do and arrangements to make.","Once everyone had returned to the complex, many people hurried to take showers and eat. The complex’s broadcasting system came to life again, and Jiang Cheng told everyone about Secretary Sun’s promise.","“A supply route?”","“A supply station?”","Everyone became excited. It was as if they had glimpsed the dawn after holding out in the darkness.","This whole nightmare with the zombies would eventually come to an end.","Eventually, everyone would return to a normal life.","Although they had paid a heavy price—for instance, the neighbor next door had not been able to return that day—from the perspective of humanity as a whole, such sacrifices were unavoidable.","“Tomorrow, we’ll split into three teams.”","Jiang Cheng’s voice rang out over the broadcast.","“The route-clearing team.”","“The rescue team.”","“The cleanup team.”","The supply station would need a suitable location. There would be people stationed there, and they could not be exposed in a completely unprotected space. They would have to take precautions against the zombies.","At first, Jiang Cheng’s instinct had been to set it up inside their own complex. If the station were located there, Youth Apartments would certainly enjoy some advantages.","But in reality, Youth Apartments had never lacked supplies. If the supply station were established there, a large number of non-residents would inevitably have to enter and leave the complex.","The disadvantages outweighed the advantages. The disadvantages outweighed the advantages. Forget it.","Jiang Cheng immediately thought of the perfect place—the Buy More Supermarket building."]},{"number":71,"title":"Chapter 71","paragraphs":["As usual, today’s news bulletin was half an hour late. This time, however, the central leader did not appear. The people appearing on the various local stations were still the top officials—or acting top officials—of each area.","In S City, naturally, it was Vice Mayor Zheng.","A respected elder who had begun his career as a rural teacher, he had spent most of his life in education. Yet at his age, he had unexpectedly been entrusted with command of a region’s fight for survival and supply operations.","Vice Mayor Zheng was having an especially hard time controlling his emotions today. He choked up before he even began speaking.","He had not actually said anything yet, but everyone in front of their television sets found themselves shedding tears.","At that moment, the whole country shared the same feelings.","No words were needed.","At such a crucial time, Vice Mayor Zheng found himself unable to produce any ornate or rousing phrases. He restrained the turmoil in his heart and gave everyone a general summary of the day’s situation in a solemn voice—sincere, concise, and to the point.","“This will surely be the turning point in this great disaster.”","He looked into the camera as though he were looking at every single person watching.","The map had been updated.","The tiny green specks from before had almost all expanded, becoming patches of green. Some of those patches had even connected with neighboring patches, forming larger expanses of green.","Even more encouraging was the supply-route and supply-point plan Vice Mayor Zheng announced.","He announced that the first batch of areas and residential compounds to receive in-depth relief on the 27th—in other words, tomorrow—had been selected.","The first on the list was the High-Tech New District.","Most of the areas receiving supply routes in the first batch were beyond the Fourth and Fifth Ring Roads. Only one was within the Third Ring Road. From the map, it was clear that the areas about to receive supplies were all relatively large green zones.","Those green patches ignited hope in people’s hearts.","The various chat groups in the Youth Apartments were buzzing with discussion.","“This is what Jiang Cheng was talking about.”","The prerequisite for opening a supply route was clearing the roads first.","The country could no longer afford further military casualties. Its soldiers were simply too precious.","Each area would have to rely on its own strength to clear a road—one that at the very least would not cause military vehicles to sink into the rubble.","“Which group is everyone joining tomorrow?”","“I signed up for road clearing.”","“I’m going to Lekang Homes. Two of my coworkers live there. Sigh...”","“I’m going to clear Buy More. Once we have a supply point, our area won’t be short of necessities anymore, right? I wonder if they’ll be able to provide fresh vegetables and meat. I really, really want to eat some greens!”","“Me too!”","“Who doesn’t?”","The group administrators in every chat reminded everyone: “Go to bed early. Get plenty of rest.”","Many people turned in early because the day had consumed so much of their physical and mental energy. After taking a shower and lying down in bed, they quickly fell asleep.","But several of the girls who were especially close to Peng Ze, including Su Yu and He Tian, did not go to bed so early.","They arranged to meet downstairs in the small plaza to hold a memorial for Peng Ze.","They had no white candles, so they used scented candles instead. The flowers were clipped from the landscaping around the residential compound.","After wiping away their tears, everyone returned to their own buildings.","Only Su Yu and He Tian remained downstairs, talking.","“Make sure you protect yourself tomorrow.”","“I will.”","“The news didn’t mention these people at all.”","“These people” referred to those like Peng Ze—people who had survived nearly two weeks of the zombie disaster, only to answer the call to courageously leave their homes that day and end up infected or losing their lives.","“There must have been quite a few.”","“Bringing it up now might hurt morale. We still have to go out again tomorrow.”","“That’s true.”","“Either way, we have to protect ourselves properly. I heard Peng Ze was bitten on the ear.”","“There wasn’t much he could do. It was too hot—he couldn’t keep his helmet on.”","Some people had also put on motorcycle helmets when they first left home that day, only to take them off once the heat became unbearable. There was no way around it in this season, at this temperature.","But if Peng Ze had been wearing a helmet, he might have escaped this fate.","Two girls’ mournful sighs drifted across the plaza.","After taking a shower, Jiang Cheng sat at home, stroking Mo Li’s fur.","Mo Li had now fully recovered, but he still ate very little, and only in the evening. On days when the sun was especially bright, he did not eat at night either.","Over the past few days, Jiang Cheng had examined his body more than once and seriously suspected that he might be some kind of advanced transforming robot. But Mo Li’s body was extremely soft and warm. He was, without a doubt, a living carbon-based creature.","He could open the window and come and go on his own. During the day, he hid somewhere in the residential compound to bask in the sun, and Jiang Cheng often could not find him.","But yesterday evening, after Jiang Cheng used their mental link to let him know that she would be leaving the next day to face the zombies, he hooked a claw into her pant leg when she went out that morning and conveyed through their mental connection: I’m coming too.","Jiang Cheng had always wanted to know whether Mo Li could transform again. She knew that if Mo Li revealed his transformation in front of everyone, it would inevitably cause a huge commotion.","But if Mo Li could still transform, then sooner or later that day would come.","Yet throughout the entire day of fighting the zombies, Mo Li had remained in Jiang Cheng’s shoulder bag.","While resting, Jiang Cheng had placed a hand on his furry little head and communicated with him. She roughly understood what was going on—Mo Li had wanted to go out with her because he was afraid she might be injured during the “hunt.”","But amid the atmosphere of so many people uniting to destroy the zombies, Mo Li had judged that the situation before him was “not dangerous.”","A cat had its own standards for what counted as dangerous.","So while everyone else was fighting and killing, splashing themselves with revolting filth, Mo Li was snoring away in the shoulder bag.","There was simply no helping it.","Jiang Cheng stroked Mo Li, secretly hoping that he would transform again.","But that would mean a true “danger” had appeared.","The people preparing to fight the next day all went to bed early that night. Vice Mayor Zheng, however, could not. He had far too much to do.","On Thursday, June 27, Vice Mayor Zheng had slept for less than four hours when he was called out of bed just after dawn.","Secretary Sun hurried in, his footsteps quick. “The helicopters have been approved. They’re sending us two for support!”","Vice Mayor Zheng’s eyes were bloodshot. They did not shine with any light of hope. In fact, they looked terribly dim.","“But today is already Thursday...”","On Monday, the relief forces had broken through to the Fourth Ring Road, only to encounter a massive number of second-generation zombies at Rainbow Stadium. They suffered heavy casualties, and the area within a three-kilometer radius of Rainbow Stadium was classified as a high-risk red zone.","Vice Mayor Zheng had immediately requested military support.","But requests for military assistance were pouring in from everywhere—not just S City. In reality, because S City was a prosperous major city, it had already received a disproportionately large share of the surrounding areas’ military forces, manpower, and supplies.","Some supplies intended for S City had even been intercepted while passing through neighboring cities.","This was an extremely dangerous signal. It meant that central control was weakening and that the government was beginning to fracture as a whole.","That was also one of the reasons the central leader had finally decided to mobilize the public.","When Vice Mayor Zheng requested support on Monday, the massive numbers of second-generation zombies at Rainbow Stadium had been slowly spreading into the surrounding areas, but they were still largely concentrated in one place.","Ground combat was too dangerous. Soldiers were now more precious than gold.","The best option was aerial combat, using bombs or artillery shells to inflict large-scale casualties.","But the problem was not merely a shortage of helicopters. There was also a severe shortage of pilots!","Just as Secretary Sun had told Jiang Cheng, there was a shortage of people—an extremely serious shortage.","The military’s losses when the zombie virus broke out were far more devastating than the public could imagine. Why were there tens of thousands of second-generation zombies at Rainbow Stadium? In such an open space packed with people, ordinary civilians had no way to fight back—and no way to escape.","Not a single person got out.","The military survived because its soldiers were tough enough to resist and even kill zombies in the midst of the crisis. Otherwise, every military camp would have become another stadium.","The pilots who had survived the outbreak had been working nonstop for the past week and a half. Even bodies made of iron could not withstand it. Pilots were human, too.","At the same time, just as dawn broke, Zhou Wang at Jixiang Jiayuan had not intended to get up so early. He had been exhausted the day before and wanted to sleep a little longer to recover his energy. After all, he was middle-aged now.","But the ringing of his phone abruptly shattered his sleep and jolted him awake.","Zhou Wang’s heart pounded. He had a bad feeling. He took several breaths before he dared answer.","After listening to the report, he knew it was exactly what the hell he had feared.","When Jiang Cheng met up with Zhou Wang, she saw that his complexion was awful—yellowed and sickly green, the unhealthy color of someone on the verge of collapse.","“Didn’t you sleep well?” Jiang Cheng asked.","Zhou Wang forced the words out through clenched teeth. “Damn it...”","The middle-aged man was usually quite well-mannered and did not swear in front of young women. The moment Jiang Cheng heard him, she asked, “What happened?”","Furious, Zhou Wang ground his teeth. “From now on, inspections for people returning to the compound have to be stricter. We need multiple people checking one another—not just two people checking each other! Your compound needs to be careful, too!”","“Oh, your compound doesn’t need to. Everyone there is single...”","Jiang Cheng and the others never would have imagined that, after nearly two weeks of facing zombies, someone would still conceal an injured person. The injured residents of the Youth Apartments had even been considerate enough not to return; they had left on their own.","But when they thought about it, it was also completely human. Family members inspected one another, only to discover that someone they loved had been injured.","At that moment, could they really call out and expose them?","They knew perfectly well that the injured person would become infected and mutate, yet they still gritted their teeth, lied to the people at the entrance, and brought them through the gates.","Then the injured person mutated in the middle of the night. Because it was not dealt with properly, the entire family ended up together in death. Their screams alerted the neighbors, who finally discovered what had happened.","Zhou Wang had not even gotten out of bed at dawn before he was forced to deal with something like this.","And while dealing with it, one of their key personnel was injured.","After hearing the full story, everyone felt so frustrated they wanted to curse, yet could not bring themselves to do it.","In the end, Nie Kuizhang was the only one who managed to spit out, “Fuck!”","Jiang Cheng said to the others, “We need multiple-person inspections, too, just in case.”","There were no families living in the Youth Apartments, but over the past several days, many close-knit bonds had formed.","For example, Jiang Cheng and Li Jiangbing; Jiang Cheng and Song Jingshuo; Su Yu and He Tian; Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan; Cui Haiyang and Master Luo.","When two or several people were always together, even fighting zombies back-to-back, it was hard for them not to develop deep feelings for one another.","Everyone nodded in agreement.","Since they were still not far from the compound and remained within signal range, Li Jiangbing immediately used the walkie-talkie to contact the property staff staying behind and explain the new rule.","After everyone met up, they split into three teams. No team was made up of people from only one compound. Each team consisted of personnel jointly sent by all three compounds.","One team headed for the Fifth Ring Road, one for Lekang Jiayuan, and one for Maiduo.","Guo Jun and his colleagues all went to Maiduo. They were Maiduo employees to begin with and knew the building’s layout better than anyone else. Ordinary shoppers only knew the supermarkets and stores. Only Maiduo’s employees knew about the staff passages, storage rooms, receiving entrances, and the other facilities.","Jiang Cheng, Li Jiangbing, and Song Jingshuo all headed for the Fifth Ring Road.","The Youth Apartments brought out four large Route 535 buses. They also brought out the few SUVs they had. As for the compact cars and hatchbacks, they were left behind. They could not withstand second-generation zombies and were too likely to cause trouble.","Jiang Cheng and Li Jiangbing were both aboard one of the large buses. Everyone had taped the windows on the inside in a cross pattern to keep zombies from smashing through them.","Su Yu and several other girls were there as well.","Someone said, “Song Jingshuo’s car is really something.”","Jiang Cheng turned at the sound of the voice.","Sure enough, outside the window was Song Jingshuo’s SUV, its chassis exceptionally high, its build rugged, and its appearance striking.","He was handsome to begin with, and the fine vehicle only made him look even more so.","Another girl said, “I heard he bought a 180-square-meter apartment west of the Fourth Ring Road. It even has a great view overlooking the Wetland Park.”","“Really? He’s seriously impressive.”","“He works in finance. Money comes quickly in that line of work.”","Song Jingshuo was a successful young man by society’s usual standards—a young elite. He had a good build and a handsome face, and he had shown himself to be responsible, composed, and financially well-off. Naturally, he drew plenty of attention from women.","Li Jiangbing made an appreciative clicking sound. “Tsk, tsk, tsk, tsk...”","Jiang Cheng smiled faintly and turned her gaze back to the road ahead.","The vehicles left the roads around the compound and merged onto a main thoroughfare.","Zombies began appearing on and beside the road.","This was the same route everyone had taken on Sunday to the Fifth Ring Road to collect supplies. They had driven it once on the way there and once on the way back, crushing and killing countless zombies beneath their wheels.","If they thoroughly cleared it again today, the Tech District would be connected to the Fifth Ring Road—and through it, to the organization and the nation.","On the highway, vehicles of every size roared forward with their accelerators pressed down.","At the compounds, the residents formed battle lines and fought the zombies.","Inside the Maiduo building, people searched and cleared the stores one by one, hallway by hallway.","Amid the thunderous chop-chop-chop of rotors tearing through the air, two helicopters flew directly from the southern part of the city to Rainbow Stadium by the Fourth Ring Road.","Looking down from the sky, a combat team member shouted to the pilot, “They’re too spread out! This won’t work! Circle around twice and herd them together!”","The military helicopters began circling. Countless second-generation zombies were drawn by the enormous noise. They raised their heads and ran after the giant birds in the sky.","The giant birds circled again and again, until the ground below was packed solid with a dark, surging mass of zombies—a sight that made one’s scalp crawl.","Small aerial bombs were launched, shrieking as they hurtled toward the ground.","Weapons with excessive destructive power could not be used in a city. The higher-ups had approved only small aerial bombs, and each of the two military helicopters carried six.","But even small bombs were terrifying to the city’s residents.","Viewed from the tops of high-rises, the enormous explosions struck the eyes first, and only afterward reached the ears.","At that moment, the same scene was unfolding in every city across the country.","An indiscriminate blanket bombardment.","That afternoon, Secretary Sun received a call from Jiang Cheng.","“The route has been cleared. The resupply point is ready. Please open a supply corridor to the Tech District.”","Secretary Sun drew in a breath and replied firmly, “All right.”"]},{"number":72,"title":"Chapter 72","paragraphs":["By dusk, when the military trucks arrived, countless people began cheering.","Everyone knew that the supplies were specifically intended for Lekang Home, not for them, but that did nothing to dampen their excitement.","Lekang Home really had suffered a terrible fate.","The rescuers had found several bodies. They had not mutated, which meant they had been killed by other humans rather than zombies.","What had happened? No one wanted to ask.","Many of the people who came downstairs wore blank expressions.","Some were frighteningly thin. They said they had eaten everything in their homes—even cutting up genuine leather belts and boiling them.","They grabbed people by the arms and asked desperately, “Do you have anything to eat? Do you have anything to eat?”","Zhou Wang said that the people in Youth Apartments had been living absurdly behind locked doors. Only now did the young residents of Youth Apartments truly understand what he had meant.","The other two communities were in better shape than Youth Apartments, though neither had suffered anything as horrific as Lekang Home.","After seeing the state of Lekang Home, no one objected to the entire truckload of supplies being given to them.","More importantly, two weeks after the zombie crisis had erupted, the government’s supply line had finally broken through the ring road and reached the residential districts!","What did that mean?","It meant a lifeline!","For the Technology New District, it meant that the area was no longer isolated beyond the Fifth Ring Road. The main artery had been opened, and a steady flow of aid had begun.","They had taken a major step toward returning to normal life.","Many people cheered and cheered until they began to cry.","The tears spread like an infection, passing from one person to the next.","Song Jingshuo’s handsome off-road vehicle led the military truck into the grounds of Lekang Home.","Order there was being maintained by people from three communities, though in practice it was mainly residents of Youth Apartments and Auspicious Jiayuan. The people of Lekang Home had eyes that seemed to glow green with hunger.","They had originally formed five lines, and under the supervision of these people, the lines had been fairly orderly.","But the moment the supply truck entered the community, all five lines fell into chaos.","“Stay in line! No pushing!” Li Jiangbing had been having a good few days lately and had not needed to shout like this in quite some time. “Anyone who causes trouble goes to the back! You’ll be the last to receive anything!”","They had plenty of experience by now. The people assigned to maintain order were all tall, burly men. Otherwise, they simply could not hold the crowd back. They really couldn’t.","Song Jingshuo stopped the vehicle, and Jiang Cheng climbed out of the passenger seat.","The military truck stopped as well. Its doors opened, and several soldiers jumped down. They wore field uniforms, their arms and necks darkened by the sun.","The details had already been communicated by phone while they were on the road, so there was no need for further discussion. The soldiers immediately began unloading the supplies, while volunteers distributed them to the five lines, which was more efficient.","The officer in charge watched as everything began operating smoothly. He stepped back, looked around, and carefully assessed the surroundings.","Some residents were clearly suffering from extreme hunger as they waited in line.","Others were obviously well fed and healthy, and were helping maintain order.","In the distance, piles of zombie corpses rose like small hills—several of them. Forklifts were moving the bodies away.","The stench was overwhelming. The people working over there were all wearing masks or wrapping scraps of cloth over their mouths and noses.","And yet they actually had forklifts.","“Captain Li.”","Someone called out from behind him.","The officer in charge was named Li Feng, a deputy company commander.","When Li Feng heard the woman’s voice, he turned around. “Jiang Cheng?”","Ever since he had accepted the assignment, he had been communicating with this voice. He already knew that the person in charge of the Youth Apartments’ interim committee was Jiang Cheng.","When Jiang Cheng saw the man step back to survey the area, she knew he was the Captain Li she had spoken with over the phone.","But when Li Feng turned around, both of them were surprised by how young the other was.","“That’s me.” Jiang Cheng extended her hand.","Li Feng shook it. “I’m Li Feng.”","Jiang Cheng asked, “Will you be staying here from now on?”","“No. I’ll be going back and forth between both locations. But you can contact me anytime, and I’ll be coming by regularly.”","Zhou Wang also came over and shook Li Feng’s hand. “I’m Zhou Wang, the person in charge of Auspicious Jiayuan.”","Several people from Yujing Xiangyuan crowded forward as well.","Who wouldn’t want to establish a connection with the person in charge of the government’s supply line? Everyone did.","But Li Feng merely nodded at them.","The command center had already made contact with the leaders of many communities. The contact information provided to them was for the people in charge, not ordinary staff.","So although he was surprised that Jiang Cheng was such a young and beautiful woman, he had clearly sensed during their phone conversations on the way that she truly was the person in charge.","Jiang Cheng did not waste a single word. “Captain Li, I’ll take you to see the supply depot. We’ve already cleared it out.”","Li Feng nodded. “All right.”","There were many volunteers maintaining order here, and they seemed to be doing an excellent job. Li Feng called two soldiers over to accompany him, since they were the ones who would be stationed here.","They got into Song Jingshuo’s vehicle.","Zhou Wang and the others each drove a car. Three cars, one from each community, headed together toward Mai Duoduo.","“Mai Duoduo is basically empty now,” Jiang Cheng explained to the three soldiers in the back seat. “Today, we cleared all the zombies out of the building.”","“I chose this place because it’s large enough to store a substantial amount of supplies.”","“It has dedicated loading and unloading entrances, as well as warehouses.”","“Its location serves most of the surrounding communities.”","“It also has employee dormitories. The former employees aren’t living there anymore, so you can requisition them.”","They arrived as she finished speaking.","After taking a quick tour, they found quite a few people still inside, sorting and cleaning.","The earlier rush to buy supplies had left the supermarket in a complete mess, with many shelves knocked over. Some of the goods had also been traded to Youth Apartments by Brother Dong.","Jiang Cheng had arranged for people to clean up the supermarket and clear space for the supply depot.","Li Feng was extremely satisfied with the choice, especially with the volunteers working there. Many of them were young, and they looked energetic and full of spirit.","So many people were working together without any disorder. Someone was clearly directing them.","That person came running over. “Jiang Cheng!”","It was Zhao Yi. He said, “What do you think? Is this arrangement all right?”","Jiang Cheng looked at Li Feng. “What do you think?”","The empty shelves had been pushed together, creating a spacious area in front.","Li Feng praised it succinctly. “Very good.”","His skin was dark from the sun, but it could not hide his strong brows and bright eyes. His features were sharp and handsome, and his shoulders, back, and waist were exceptionally straight.","He took another brief look around to familiarize himself with the surroundings, then left the other two soldiers there and followed Jiang Cheng and the others back to Lekang Home.","With strong men maintaining order, the distribution of supplies went smoothly. By the time they returned, most of the residents of Lekang Home had already received their share.","Many people simply found a spot in the garden, sat down where they were, and began eating. Because Jiang Cheng had contacted the authorities in advance and reported the situation, the first truck sent specifically to Lekang Home contained not rice, flour, cooking oil, and other staples, but bread, sausages, pickles, salted duck eggs, and other ready-to-eat foods that required no cooking.","The truck was emptied quickly. But the residents of Lekang Home had finally eaten a satisfying, filling meal.","People placed plastic stools in the shade and sat together, discussing the situation in the Technology New District.","Jiang Cheng unfolded the map she carried with her.","When Li Feng noticed the map in her hands, he also noticed that the black shape inside her shoulder bag was actually a cat.","Li Feng was caught off guard. Ever since their first phone call that afternoon, he and Jiang Cheng had communicated with remarkable ease. After meeting her in person, he was even more certain that she was organized, clear-headed, and efficient.","In a time like this, she was an outstanding partner to have.","Then he suddenly discovered that she carried a cat with her wherever she went, and his impression of her immediately took a nosedive.","“Our target tomorrow is Food Street.” Jiang Cheng had already marked it on the map with a colored pencil.","“We made contact with Deqing Li today, and they’ll be acting together with us. But the people from Shanshui Yayuan haven’t replied.”","“Deqing Li is a high-density residential community. Its population is larger than that of our several housing complexes combined.”","“If we clear out Food Street, this area, this area, and this area will all be connected. We can basically consider the whole stretch a safe zone.”","The reason she said “basically” was that the area was too large. There were too many streets, shops, and hidden corners. It was impossible to confirm in a short time that every inch of it was completely clean.","But for now, “basically” was good enough.","“The original population should have been around six thousand. We have no idea how many are left now.” Jiang Cheng had looked up the information online the day before.","She had also told Li Feng the original populations of Youth Apartments, Jixiang Jiayuan, and Yujing Xiangyuan before asking him, “Will there be fresh supplies tomorrow?”","Li Feng nodded. “We can transport a shipment of rice, flour, cooking oil, salt, and sugar tomorrow.”","The people from Youth Apartments were inevitably disappointed. They weren’t short on rice or flour, but they were sick to death of canned food and desperately wanted some fresh vegetables and meat.","The people from Jixiang Jiayuan and Yujing Xiangyuan, however, were all thrilled.","The residents of Youth Apartments didn’t want to seem inappropriate, so they restrained their expressions and maintained an appearance of calm.","Li Feng was secretly puzzled.","The people from the other two complexes were older, and those in charge were all middle-aged. But compared with them, how were these younger people from Youth Apartments so much steadier?","He didn’t know that this was simply the embodiment of the saying: With food in hand, the heart remains calm.","Jiang Cheng asked, “Can you keep the supplies coming?”","Captain Li straightened his chest. “The country has enough strategic grain reserves to feed the entire population for two years. And this year, the southern grain-producing regions had a bumper harvest in April and May, most of which has already been stored. The central wheat-growing regions completed their summer harvest earlier this month. The only area affected is the northwestern wheat-growing region, and they’re already organizing emergency harvesting efforts. The government has done far more these past few days than everyone thinks—not just killing zombies. The first thing the country thought of was ensuring food security.”","These facts had first been explained within the military, to reassure the soldiers. Now the soldiers were passing them on to the civilians, reassuring the people.","This was exactly the information Jiang Cheng wanted to know, and she was very satisfied.","Captain Li spoke clearly and acted decisively, which pleased her even more.","Her fingertip moved across the map. “From here to here...”","Everyone listened as she explained their plans for the next few days.","Li Feng gradually grew astonished. The unfavorable impression created by the cat faded away, replaced by a clear new understanding.","This girl... was planning to use the supply points as a base and turn the entire Tech New District from yellow to green, step by step.","The entire Tech New District.","No wonder. No wonder the older men were sitting quietly and listening to her.","No wonder she was the one in charge."]},{"number":73,"title":"Chapter 73","paragraphs":["Li Feng and the others would not be staying here today.","After inspecting Mai Duoduo’s facilities, the two soldiers returned as well and boarded the empty bus with Li Feng for the trip back.","The streetlights came on. Jiang Cheng said to Li Feng, “See you tomorrow.”","Jiang Cheng had originally intended to have either Zhao Yi or Li Jiangbing handle communications with the military’s supply officer. She wanted to keep the supply arrangements under her own control as well.","But the moment Li Feng arrived, she noticed an interesting phenomenon: everyone—all the native inhabitants of this world—became remarkably docile in his presence.","No one fought for authority. Every native resident simply assumed that Li Feng was in charge.","And Li Feng was only a young man who looked to be twenty-five or twenty-six.","Jiang Cheng wisely put aside some of her plans, lest she overreach and make things worse.","The vehicle set off. Li Feng glanced at the rearview mirror.","The leaders of the several residential compounds were still standing there talking. They were all gathered around that girl. The same had been true during their interactions that day. They could not exactly be called blindly obedient, but whenever something happened, they would instinctively look to that girl.","“Company Commander, what are you thinking about?” one of the soldiers in the back leaned forward and asked.","“I’m wondering whether I can apply for some protective gear for them tomorrow.”","“Did you see it, Company Commander? One of the compounds has shields they modified themselves. There are some talented people in that compound.”","“I saw them. There are only a few, and they’re not enough.”","“That’s true.”","At headquarters, Vice Mayor Zheng was listening to a work report.","The green zones were like grass pushing through the soil after a spring rain, displaying a tenacious vitality.","Two armed helicopters and twelve small aerial bombs had finally turned the area around Rainbow Stadium on the Third Ring Road from a red zone into a yellow zone.","For the first time in half a month, he felt that the weight in his heart had eased a little. The country and its people had jointly poured their vitality into his body, giving him hope.","The zombie crisis was unprecedented, something no one had ever seen or heard of before, but in the end, it could not defeat this country or its people.","Vice Mayor Zheng thought of that with relief.","While the combat units and ordinary civilians were resting, the logistics department was so busy they could barely keep their feet on the ground.","The site looked like a massive construction zone. Blinding floodlights were mounted on tall poles. People and forklifts moved back and forth as crate after crate of supplies was loaded onto heavy trucks. Everyone was working at full speed.","Li Feng had successfully secured a batch of riot shields for the area under his responsibility. Then he saw the newest type of protective armor.","He took one look and was immediately impressed. “This stuff is great!”","It was made of white plastic, smooth to the touch. When he tapped it with his knuckles, it felt solid.","Molded to fit the shape of the human shoulders, the upper-body piece resembled a cape. It extended down from the shoulders and fastened in front with a hook-and-loop closure. The neck guard rose behind the head like the shell-shaped collar worn by a princess in a foreign fairy tale, covering the back of the head and the neck.","There was one upper-arm guard, one forearm guard, and guards for both the thighs and lower legs. All of them were secured with hook-and-loop fasteners.","The design was extremely crude. It was obvious that it had been developed in a great hurry to meet an urgent need.","But its advantages were clear: the white plastic was covered in holes, making it breathable.","After all, the temperature had been reaching thirty-one or thirty-two degrees Celsius every day lately, sometimes rising as high as thirty-four. Even the slightest movement left people drenched in sweat.","Li Feng first asked, “Has it been issued to the front line?”","“Of course. The front line comes first.”","But the civilians were on the front line now too. They had never received any special training, yet they had bravely gone out carrying cleavers. The government could not let that courage go unrewarded, so protective gear had begun to be included in the supply shipments as well.","“Give me some of these. The people on my side are going to clear a restaurant street tomorrow. I’ll set out early and deliver them to them.”","“Sure. How many sets do you want?”","On Friday morning, everyone heard a broadcast from the hallway:","“All vehicle teams are to assemble at the usual time. The scheduled assembly time for everyone else has been postponed by forty minutes.”","The residents opened their doors and poked their heads out into the hallway, asking one another, “What happened?”","At the originally scheduled time, Song Jingshuo led the vehicle convoy out first.","Today’s target was the restaurant street.","The so-called “convoy” consisted of four large 535 buses.","These buses were different from ordinary city buses. They were taller and larger, and their engines were supposedly more powerful as well.","They had played a major role in opening up the route along the Fifth Ring Road the day before, and today they were once again the main fighting force.","The lead bus went first, honking continuously to attract the zombies.","It could not go too fast, or the zombies would not be able to keep up. But it could not go too slowly either, since there was a risk of second-generation zombies jumping aboard. The bus windows were fairly sturdy, but not indestructible. No one wanted to take that chance.","The drivers had all gained experience on the road the previous day.","Today, they had come up with a new strategy.","The lead bus attracted the zombies. Once it picked up speed, the zombies in front were crushed beneath its wheels, while most of the others chased after it from behind.","But the bus was too large and too long, making it difficult to maneuver in reverse. Once the zombies had gathered, the lead bus would suddenly accelerate and shake them off.","At that moment, the following bus would charge forward, smashing some of the clustered zombies aside and grinding others beneath its wheels.","The lead bus would use the opportunity to speed away from the restaurant street.","After repeating this process several times, the number of second-generation zombies on the restaurant street had fallen dramatically. At a glance, the street no longer looked quite so densely packed and terrifying.","According to plan, once the vehicle convoy had completed its main task, people were supposed to enter and conduct a thorough, building-by-building cleanup.","But today, that step had been temporarily postponed.","Jiang Cheng, Li Jiangbing, and the others who did not have vehicles had all gone to Mai Duoduo to wait for Li Feng. Li Jiangbing in particular was practically rubbing his hands together with impatience.","The reason was that Li Feng had called Jiang Cheng very late the previous night to tell her that he had secured a batch of armor for them.","He had used the word “armor.”","Li Jiangbing was dying to see what this so-called “armor” looked like.","Li Feng and his companions had taken turns supervising the loading throughout the night. They had set out early that morning so the people in the Science and Technology New District could receive the protective gear as soon as possible.","The four buses entered Mai Duoduo’s loading entrance and stopped in the unloading area.","All three compounds had sent people over, and forklifts and handcarts were ready.","Li Feng leaped nimbly from the bus and called out, “Unload the armor first!”","Everyone had been waiting for that. They surged forward all at once.","Once Li Jiangbing got his hands on a set of armor, he spent a long while examining it by touch. Puzzled, he said, “Why does this thing look so familiar? I must have seen it somewhere before.”","Li Feng immediately solved the mystery. “They requisitioned several plastic medical-equipment factories. They used to make braces for broken bones.”","Everyone suddenly understood.","No one complained about the crude design. To have produced something like this in only a few days, the mold designers must have poured their hearts and souls into it.","They put on the upper-body pieces first, then fastened the arm and leg guards into place. Everyone helped one another adjust the straps to the proper tightness.","After two weeks of fighting zombies, they immediately recognized how practical the equipment was.","It was excellent!","Jiang Cheng asked, “How many sets are there in total?”","Li Feng replied, “Four hundred.”","Jiang Cheng made the decision on the spot. “Two hundred sets for the Youth Apartments, and one hundred each for the other two compounds.”","Li Feng was taken aback and was about to say something, but then he suddenly realized that the people from Zhou Wang’s compound and Yujing Xiangyuan had not said a word.","He looked at the several older men, only to discover—much to his surprise—that they did not seem to have any intention of objecting at all.","Jiang Cheng seemed to understand his surprise and confusion. She offered a concise explanation: “Our residential compound is the main fighting force in this area.”","Zhou Wang nodded. “Yes.”","The people from Yujing Xiangyuan did not deny it either.","So it was true. Since that was the case, Li Feng did not interfere with their distribution arrangements and agreed to their plan.","In just half a month, the Tech New District had already developed its own factions.","Sure enough, wherever there were people, there was a world of rivalries.","The only two people at the scene who were unhappy were Li Jiangbing and Nie Kuizhang.","That was because the armor came in three sizes—large, medium, and small—to accommodate different body types. But the two of them had rather unusual physiques.","One was too muscular, and the other was too fat.","Li Jiangbing’s arms were so thick that the arm guards couldn’t even fit over them. Unless he strapped the leg guards onto his arms—but then someone else would have to go without leg guards.","The upper-body armor was even worse. It was only half as wide as his shoulders and couldn’t be put on at all.","Building too much muscle had its downsides.","Li Jiangbing had spent the whole morning looking forward to getting the armor, only to end up empty-handed.","All the combatants who had taken part in the battle were waiting inside the supermarket. The people from each residential compound stayed together with their own groups.","Once everyone transported the armor from the unloading area into the supermarket, it naturally caused quite a stir.","Each residential compound organized its own people to collect their supplies. There was no need for Li Feng and his people to maintain order at all, which saved them a great deal of effort.","Song Jingshuo called. “We’re almost done here. How are things on your end? How’s that armor?”","“Quite impressive,” Jiang Cheng praised. “It’s incredibly cool.”","Song Jingshuo: “...What?”","Jiang Cheng said, “We’re getting ready to leave.”","Seeing the combatants from the three residential compounds preparing to head for Food Street, Li Feng was tempted to go along as well. “Then we’ll come with—”","Jiang Cheng cut him off immediately. “No.”","“You’re in charge of the supply line. You can’t risk losing people in battle. We have more than enough combatants on our side, but we can’t take over your work.”","“Your job is extremely important. No one can replace you.”","Li Feng: “...”","Li Feng found the whole thing strange. Jiang Cheng’s tone and reasoning sounded incredibly familiar. What did it remind him of?","A leader.","Yes, that was exactly how leaders talked. As a deputy company commander, he used the same tone when speaking to his soldiers.","But Jiang Cheng was a young, beautiful woman, which made the incongruity especially striking.","Curious, Li Feng asked, “Jiang Cheng, are you a civil servant?”","Jiang Cheng denied it. “No. I’m just an ordinary resident.”","Li Feng particularly wanted to suggest that after the zombie crisis was over, she should try taking the civil service exam. He felt that she was exceptionally well suited to working within the system.","But there was no time to bring that up at the moment. He merely nodded and reminded everyone, “Be careful.”","He watched them leave, then turned back to work with the volunteers, sorting the supplies and preparing for the distribution that would follow.","He did not see Jiang Cheng again until the afternoon.","Thanks to the new armor, no one had been injured that day.","Jiang Cheng had specifically come back to find Li Feng. “Please be sure to report this to your superiors. This armor is extremely effective!”","She also made a request. “Could you send us more?”","Li Feng said, “Not for the time being. We’re already manufacturing it around the clock, but the demand is simply too high.”","Jiang Cheng offered him a bargaining chip. “Give us another two hundred suits, and we’ll take Renxin Hospital.”"]},{"number":74,"title":"Chapter 74","paragraphs":["According to the news everyone had heard, Renxin Hospital had been completely overrun. There wasn’t a single survivor left inside.","But the hospital still had medical equipment and medicine—things many people desperately needed.","There was an intern doctor who worked at Renxin Hospital living in the Youth Apartments. These past few days, she had often been treating people in the community and advising everyone on what medicine to take.","But those were all common minor ailments. There was nothing she could do for serious illnesses.","Fortunately, the people in the Youth Apartments were all young and relatively healthy. During these past two weeks, some had suffered from diarrhea, stomachaches, or gallbladder pain, but no one had developed an acute condition or serious illness that required an IV drip or surgery.","It was also thanks to Jiang Cheng, who had raided the pharmacy ahead of time and stocked the Youth Apartments with commonly used medicines.","But in other residential communities, people had died from illness over the past half month, including children.","One woman in the later stages of pregnancy had even given birth at home.","Many others were still suffering from illness. With neither doctors nor medicine available, all they could do was endure the pain.","Even though the people in the Youth Apartments were young and healthy, they couldn’t remain illness-free forever. A hospital was an absolute necessity.","Jiang Cheng’s goal was to turn the entire Technology New District into a green zone. Today, they had cleared the Food Street and successfully joined forces with the residents of Deqingli.","If distance was calculated outward from the Youth Apartments, the next closest target was the zombie nest known as Renxin Hospital.","Before today, Jiang Cheng might have stopped advancing in this direction out of consideration for the difficulty involved. She might have chosen to wait until conditions improved and let professional soldiers deal with Renxin Hospital.","But Li Feng had brought new armor. Its defensive capabilities had proven exceptionally strong during today’s operation on Food Street.","Jiang Cheng’s ambition swelled instantly.","It wasn’t an ambition for power or authority, but an ambition to win.","Jiang Cheng thought: This is the reason I came to this world.","Otherwise, why had she transmigrated here?","To work nine to five, get married, and have children?","Jiang Cheng had actually worried about whether everyone would still be willing to follow her if she continued pushing ahead at such an intense pace. If no one followed her, she couldn’t accomplish anything as a lone commander.","But when she asked for everyone’s opinion after the operation on Food Street, the local residents surprised her once again.","She had never expected so many people to respond.","There was no fear on their faces. Their eyes even shone with surging enthusiasm.","Of course, one could also say they had gotten caught up in the killing.","But when such an act had the country’s support behind it, it was no longer simply a matter of “getting carried away with killing.”","It was just. It was noble.","It brought light to people’s eyes, sent their blood racing through their veins, and multiplied their courage.","Zhou Wang said as well, “We have to take the hospital back.”","Zhou Wang had elderly family members at home, and they suffered from chronic illnesses. Fortunately, the Friday before the zombie crisis broke out, one of them had just gone to the hospital to refill their prescriptions. During the past half month, they had also been lucky enough not to catch a cold or develop a fever.","They had been very fortunate.","But luck wouldn’t last forever. With so many elderly people, children, and pregnant women, they had to reclaim the hospital.","The other communities—including Deqingli, which had just joined them—were traditional residential neighborhoods with both old people and children. Their need for a hospital was far greater than that of the mostly young, able-bodied residents of the Youth Apartments.","Jiang Cheng’s proposal immediately received everyone’s approval and support.","With the people behind her, Jiang Cheng could now bargain with the authorities.","“Give us another two hundred sets of armor,” she said. “With all six hundred people fully equipped, we’ll take Renxin Hospital.”","Li Feng and Jiang Cheng met at Duoduo Supermarket.","The people from Deqingli had come along to collect supplies as well.","Deqingli had a large population. Fortunately, most of the residents from Jixiang Garden, Lekang Garden, and Yujingxiang Garden had already come to collect supplies that morning or around noon, so the supermarket wasn’t impossibly crowded.","The people from Deqingli had been through a lot over the past two weeks, and many of them had a hardened look about them.","But the Youth Apartments and Jixiang Garden had plenty of experience by now, and the men sent over to coordinate the distribution and maintain order were all physically strong.","The scene was somewhat noisy and disorderly, but it wasn’t out of control.","Soldiers and volunteers sent by several communities were handling those tasks.","Li Feng’s more important job was to coordinate with the people in charge of the various communities, arranging and assigning responsibilities.","The main person he had to deal with was Jiang Cheng. In this area, the young woman named Jiang Cheng had practically become the sole decision-maker.","The ceiling lights shone down on her. Her bangs were slightly damp, and sweat glistened on her face and neck.","The white plastic armor she wore seemed to be a smaller size and fit her fairly well. Under the lights, it created a visual effect that was both retro and futuristic.","But what drew Li Feng’s attention were her eyes.","They were far too bright.","Li Feng had seen eyes that bright before, but they had belonged to people who had undergone specialized training. Jiang Cheng was clearly just an ordinary civilian.","While they had gone to the restroom together, he had casually asked Zhao Yi, who was helping coordinate things at the site, “What does Jiang Cheng do?”","The answer had been that she was simply an ordinary employee at an ordinary company, no different from anyone else.","But as a soldier, Li Feng could vaguely sense that Jiang Cheng was different from the others.","Those eyes were simply too bright.","“I can’t guarantee it.” Li Feng didn’t make any grand promises just because he had been swept up in the moment.","Food was no longer in short supply, but the armor was still extremely limited.","“I heard they’ve been working around the clock to produce it,” he said. “They had to meet the needs of the frontline troops first before they could start distributing it to civilians. I had a hard time getting four hundred sets yesterday.”","“You’ve worked hard,” Jiang Cheng said. “Please help us this time, no matter what.”","“There are several pregnant women in Deqingli. An elderly person in Lekang Garden is being kept alive by IV fluids, and many of the children are sick too.”","“Other than one community clinic, Renxin Hospital is the only hospital in the Technology New District.”","“There are doctors from Renxin Hospital living in our community, Jixiang Garden, and Yujingxiang Garden. Many of them bought homes here.”","“If we can take the hospital back, it may not be able to resume full operations, but at the very least, we’ll be able to save lives.”","Li Feng pinched the brim of his cap and pulled it lower.","“Understood,” he said. “I’ll try to secure them.”","Jiang Cheng said, “Whether it works or not, you must give me an answer tonight. I need to make arrangements for tomorrow. What time will you be heading back? Nine o’clock?”","Li Feng thought for a moment, then agreed. “All right.”","It wasn’t even nine that evening when Li Feng called Jiang Cheng as promised.","“Done. We got them.”","Jiang Cheng immediately called Zhou Wang and the people from Yujingxiang Garden.","She wasn’t familiar enough with the people from Deqingli yet, and they hadn’t worked together before, so for now she wouldn’t include them in the deployment. The people from Lekang Garden were still recovering and couldn’t yet form an effective fighting force.","At present, their combat strength still mainly came from the Youth Apartments, Jixiang Garden, and Yujingxiang Garden.","That was enough.","Before going to bed, the residents of the Youth Apartments heard an announcement broadcast through the hallway speakers:","“Proceed according to plan tomorrow. Target: Renxin Hospital.”","After two days of killing, many people were no longer afraid of the zombies. Some were even a little excited at the thought of tomorrow’s operation.","It was only natural to feel proud of taking part in such a major event.","Many people even thought that the things happening before their eyes—the things they were actively participating in—would one day be recorded in history books.","They were witnessing history in the making.","They were taking part in making history.","The next day was another Saturday.","The zombie virus had also broken out on a Saturday.","Two whole weeks had passed.","Looking back on those two weeks, many people felt as if they had been living in a dream. It had been bizarre, but not absurd—or at least, nothing about Youth Apartment had been absurd. It had continued to maintain the order that society was supposed to have.","But everyone could also sense that the day they woke from this dream was not far off.","That was exhilarating.","Li Jiangbing was extremely annoyed.","Li Feng had delivered another two hundred sets of armor early that morning, but there was still nothing he could wear.","The protective-gear factory was working around the clock to meet the deadline, with assembly-line production and standardized sizing. There was simply no way to custom-make a set for anyone.","What made things even more infuriating was that, compared to the armor, everyone had unanimously decided that the other methods of protection were no longer safe enough.","They had clearly managed just fine with those methods over the past few days, but now they suddenly felt that the magazines strapped to their arms and motorcycle helmets were unsafe.","Jiang Cheng had excluded both him and Nie Kuizhang from the team assigned to seize Renxin Hospital.","It was downright insulting. He was clearly one of Youth Apartment’s top-tier fighters!","Under the insistence of Li Jiangbing and several others who shared his opinion, they were ultimately allowed to join the team heading to Renxin Hospital.","Their equipment had also been upgraded.","Li Jiangbing’s movie-prop-like arm shield had been replaced with the riot shield Li Feng had delivered along with the armor the day before. The door-panel shields used by Youth Apartment had also all been replaced with riot shields.","The same was true for Jixiang Jiayuan and Yujing Xiangyuan.","In the end, the force heading to Renxin Hospital consisted of far more than six hundred people.","This time, all the girls were excluded.","There was a limited supply of armor, and riot shields were heavy. Only people with sufficient arm strength could wield them.","Su Yu and He Tian were among the stronger fighters in the group of girls. But there were certainly men who were sturdier than them and had greater strength. With the armor in short supply, it was impossible to assign it to the girls instead of the stronger men.","The only woman in the team was Jiang Cheng.","In fact, Song Jingshuo had glanced at Jiang Cheng several times, each time wanting to say something and then stopping himself.","But Jiang Cheng merely cast him a cool glance, and he abandoned the idea.","No one else had any objections to Jiang Cheng either. Everyone knew that she had “always been strong since childhood.” The past half month had already proven it. Jiang Cheng’s strength was no different from a man’s; in fact, she was even stronger than some of the thinner young men.","Moreover, deep down, everyone had already stopped paying attention to Jiang Cheng’s gender.","Song Jingshuo had not meant any harm. He had long since abandoned any thoughts of competing with Jiang Cheng.","On the contrary, it was precisely because he was so familiar with Jiang Cheng that, when the entire group was not mobilizing and fighters had to be selected, his instinct was to let Jiang Cheng, as a “girl,” stay behind and be protected.","Song Jingshuo had his own reasons. In his eyes, Jiang Cheng still had a gender.","But Jiang Cheng, of course, refused to accept that.","She had crossed over into this world to face its challenges. She would not retreat.","Li Feng watched Jiang Cheng lead several hundred people toward Renxin Hospital, his feelings complicated.","Li Feng was in a terrible mood. He was the soldier. He was the fighter.","And yet, this time, he had been assigned to the logistics team.","Li Feng desperately wanted to take part in the battle."]},{"number":75,"title":"Chapter 75","paragraphs":["The raised section at the neck of the armor wrapped almost completely around the back of the neck, the back of the head, and the ears. It made people feel especially safe.","Li Jiangbing and the others who didn’t have armor couldn’t help touching the backs of their necks whenever they saw someone else wearing it.","Li Jiangbing took a towel and wrapped it around his neck.","Everyone, whether they had armor or not, also wrapped towels around their ankles.","Even the armor only protected the legs; it couldn’t cover the ankles. But there were definitely infant zombies in the hospital, since it had both an obstetrics department and a pediatrics department.","These were all lessons learned in blood.","When they reached the hospital, they didn’t head toward the outpatient area. The virus had broken out on Saturday night, when there should have been no one in the outpatient hall.","Everyone would have been crowded into the emergency department.","So they headed straight for the emergency department.","The hospital corridors weren’t very wide, which made close-quarters combat and killing difficult.","They used more or less the same strategy they had used when clearing out the garage: luring the zombies out.","This time, they used a loudspeaker. Someone had recorded the audio in advance, though nobody knew which tone-deaf person Gao Yuxuan had found to sing a horribly off-key rendition of a pop song.","The loudspeaker was set to play on a loop. Someone in armor cautiously approached, switched it on, left it on the steps, and turned to run.","The fighters outside formed a semicircle and waited.","Sure enough, the off-key singing immediately attracted the zombies inside the building.","The entrance was much like the one at Maiduo Supermarket: a set of double glass doors.","Before long, zombies came rushing out from inside.","Smack!","Although anti-collision strips had been pasted across the glass, the zombies didn’t know what they were for. The one leading the charge was naturally a second-generation zombie. Moving at high speed, it slammed straight into the glass.","Everyone winced and sucked air through their teeth.","“Ugh...”","The original zombies had all mutated during the first wave of the virus. Generally speaking, their bodies were still intact and clean.","Second-generation zombies, however, had mutated after being bitten or scratched by original zombies. Many of them had surely been attacked by more than one original zombie at the time, perhaps several at once, so they had multiple wounds all over their bodies.","When the first one slammed into the floor-to-ceiling glass, it smeared a huge, disgusting mess across the pane.","But the second-generation zombies didn’t look for another route because of it. Their paths were always straight lines.","If something blocked the way, they jumped over it. If they couldn’t jump over it, they simply attacked it head-on.","A mass of second-generation zombies hammered against the floor-to-ceiling glass. Everyone watched as broad networks of cracks spread across it, until at last the entire pane shattered with a roar.","That was only the inner layer. The outer layer suffered the same fate.","Finally, the zombies burst out.","Under the clear blue sky, in broad daylight, the humans raised their shields and weapons and charged forward with battle cries.","The battle to seize and hold Renxin Hospital had begun!","The armor was incredibly useful. It directly raised the humans’ fighting strength by a huge margin.","After a fierce battle, the fighters eliminated all the zombies that had been lured outside.","But the hospital corridors were long, twisting left and right. Although many zombies had been drawn out just now, there were still more lurking deep within the corridors.","Someone in armor boldly went inside and made a racket, drawing out another wave of zombies before sprinting back outside. The zombies were lured out and dealt with there.","They repeated the process again and again, making trip after trip. At last, they had eliminated nearly all the zombies visible in the emergency department corridors.","Once the humans had killed all the zombies that came rushing out and entered the hospital themselves, things actually became much more comfortable.","The air-conditioning was still running.","For a hospital of Renxin’s caliber, regulations required the air-conditioning to operate twenty-four hours a day, supported by a maintenance team on duty around the clock—at least four people during the day and no fewer than two at night. They were responsible for emergency repairs as well as regular maintenance and servicing.","Clearly, Renxin Hospital had always maintained its air-conditioning system very well. Left unattended, it had continued running for half a month without breaking down.","Everyone was drenched in sweat when they entered the hospital, but they immediately cooled down.","There were no zombies visible in the corridors anymore, but they still had to search every examination room one by one, especially those with the doors closed.","Sure enough, there were survivors among the dead.","Next came the emergency pharmacy, offices, and testing rooms. The toilets and stairwells couldn’t be overlooked either.","In fact, it wasn’t hard to guess where people would have been in the hospital on Saturday night.","Several hundred people couldn’t all crowd into one place; there wouldn’t have been enough room to maneuver.","After clearing the emergency department, they passed through the connecting corridor and arrived at the deserted outpatient hall. Everyone began splitting up.","Jiang Cheng gave them a special warning. “Be careful around the maternity ward. There may be babies.”","The people assigned to the maternity ward acknowledged her warning.","Jiang Cheng had only taken two steps after turning away when Mo Li suddenly leaped out of her shoulder bag.","Song Jingshuo let out an “Ah.” “Your cat!”","Everyone felt that a kitten was nothing but a burden at a time like this.","After all, whenever this happened in a movie, the heroine would panic and run after it, getting an entire group of companions killed in the process. In the end, she would be the one to survive, clutching the cat in her arms.","Fortunately, Jiang Cheng wasn’t a movie heroine. She seemed completely unsurprised and said casually, “Don’t worry about him. He’ll be fine.”","Everyone was astonished.","Jiang Cheng loved her cat so much that she took him everywhere, and everyone was used to it. Why wasn’t she concerned about his safety now that they were in such a dangerous place?","Of course, Jiang Cheng couldn’t tell them that her little cat could transform into a black panther and finish off a second-generation zombie with a single bite.","Besides, Mo Li had only jumped down because he had communicated with her through telepathy. He was going to patrol the various areas of the hospital.","Compared with humans, Mo Li ran faster, hit harder, and had evasion maxed out. There was no need to worry about him.","In a hospital, he even had more advantages than the humans did.","Go on.","Jiang Cheng: There’s any danger, notify me.","Mo Li: Meow!","Everyone assigned to the maternity ward felt especially unlucky.","Baby and infant zombies were the last things anyone wanted to encounter.","After killing enough zombies, people gradually became numb to it. Subconsciously, they no longer regarded these human-shaped things as “people.” But whenever infant zombies appeared, that numbness suddenly shattered.","Those tiny creatures crawling across the floor because their bones were not yet strong enough to support standing and walking had once been humanity’s adorable babies.","But even though everyone had prepared themselves mentally, the horror of the hospital’s maternity ward still exceeded anything they had imagined.","The babies there were not ordinary infants. They were newborns.","Normally, mothers were allowed to remain in the hospital for only three days after giving birth. That meant every baby there had been born less than three days earlier, forever frozen in that state.","They couldn’t even crawl.","Their way of moving toward fresh flesh was by thrashing their bodies.","Like fish stranded on the shore, they were tiny, one after another, their black eyes wide open as they flopped and jerked their way toward the living.","Their bodies smacked against the floor with a steady slap, slap, slap, slap.","The men who had killed so many zombies that they believed themselves fearless were all so horrified that they stumbled backward.","Someone vomited.","But there was no way to run from it. The “little fish” wriggled closer and closer. In the end, the people could only smash them one by one.","No one knew whether they were boys or girls.","No one knew whether they had been given names.","They had heard that if a person had a name, they could be reborn as a human in their next life.","Something else happened in the maternity ward—dangerous, but not exactly dangerous.","A full-term pregnant woman zombie was killed and fell to the floor. As the people stepped over her body, a fetal zombie wriggled out between her legs, thrashing its way into the world.","Another round of terror erupted.","Fortunately, it had no offensive power, and a single blow from a staff was enough to finish it off.","After checking the entire ward area and confirming that there were no more “living” zombies, everyone retreated as quickly as if demons were chasing them.","No one had the courage to take another look.","From early morning until afternoon, thanks to the new armor, no one had been injured.","If only they had gotten this armor sooner.","Jiang Cheng led the others in clearing out the orthopedic ward. Just as they were preparing to move on, she suddenly sensed something and turned around.","Sure enough, Mo Li had appeared.","Mo Li stood in the corridor and looked at them. “Meow.”","Jiang Cheng was slightly surprised. She walked over, crouched down, and stroked his head. 【Where is it?】","Mo Li replied, “Meow~”","He turned and walked a few steps, then looked back at them.","Jiang Cheng said to everyone, “Something seems to be going on. Let’s go take a look.”","Everyone stared at her in surprise.","Li Jiangbing said, “Wait, you understand cat language?”","“Small animals are naturally attuned to people,” Jiang Cheng replied. “If you spend enough time with them, you’ll understand them.”","Li Jiangbing thought of how he used to play with Little White downstairs. Little White’s Dad had seemed to say something similar before.","He had said that small animals were basically like children who couldn’t speak.","People who raised pets seemed to treat them as their own children.","Everyone followed, half convinced and half doubtful.","After Jiang Cheng communicated telepathically with him—【Lead the way】—Mo Li stopped looking back and headed straight in one direction, leading everyone along.","“Huh?” someone said. “This is the outpatient area.”","In theory, the outpatient area should have been empty on a Saturday night. Their main focus was clearing the emergency department and the wards. Only after those key areas had been cleared would they inspect the outpatient area.","Mo Li led them directly to the stairwell beside the escalators.","The escalators in the outpatient area naturally weren’t running on a Saturday night, so they had to walk down themselves. Everyone followed Mo Li to the level below, then continued in a particular direction.","As they went, four or five zombie corpses appeared on the floor.","“Which team came through here?”","Someone even bent down to examine one of the corpses. “What did this? Its neck was snapped clean through.”","Jiang Cheng knew at a glance that Mo Li had bitten through their necks. Without changing her expression, she said, “Forget about that. Hurry up and see what’s ahead.”","The person quickly straightened up and followed the others.","Mo Li stopped outside the door of a room—a treatment room.","There were claw marks on the wooden door, and it was even cracked in places. It had clearly been attacked by zombies.","Everyone guessed that the zombies they had just seen might have been the ones responsible.","Perhaps some other team had passed by, made a noise that attracted the zombies, and cleared them out.","Jiang Cheng certainly wasn’t going to tell them that the “team” that had happened to pass by was actually Mo Li.","She raised her hand and knocked three times.","Everyone held their breath.","There was no sound from inside.","Jiang Cheng knocked three more times and called out, “Is anyone in there?”","The instant she spoke, a voice rang out from inside—urgent and excited.","“Yes! Someone’s here!”","“Are you police officers?”","“Is it safe outside? What happened to the monsters out there?”","It really was a survivor. Jiang Cheng’s cat was truly incredible. It had actually found a living person.","But how had this person survived?","Jiang Cheng said, “It’s safe outside. Open the door.”","Sounds of furniture being moved came from inside. After a while, the door opened cautiously by a crack.","Only after seeing that there really were no monsters outside did the person finally relax and open the door. He was trembling with excitement.","“Are you here to rescue me? What happened to those monsters? Are there still monsters outside? So many people turned into monsters—there were so many of them!”","He was wearing a white coat, so he was probably a doctor.","He moved excitedly toward Jiang Cheng, but he smelled terrible. Li Jiangbing discreetly raised his shield to block him.","“Is anyone else in there? Are you alone?”","Not only did the man stink—the entire room reeked as well.","It was unbearable, like feces mixed with rotting meat.","“Uh...” The man hesitated.","Jiang Cheng gave someone a meaningful look, and one of the others went inside to investigate.","It was a small treatment room. From the doorway, they could see almost everything at a glance. But there was another door inside, leading to a second room.","The person kicked the door open. The room beyond was also very small.","The first person went in. A few seconds later, he backed out.","The person beside him glanced at him in confusion, then went in to take a look as well. He came back out almost immediately and began retching against the table.","Li Jiangbing barked, “What are you doing? What’s going on?”","The first person who had gone inside kept his face taut and said nothing—or perhaps he simply couldn’t speak.","Someone else entered. A moment later, they let out a horrified cry of “Oh my God!” and staggered back out.","The person who had been dry-heaving couldn’t bring anything up. He wiped the saliva from the corner of his mouth with the back of his hand, stared at the doctor, and told everyone, “He ate people.”","That single sentence answered the question everyone had instinctively been asking: How had this man survived?","It had been two weeks.","There was a sink in the treatment room, so he could drink tap water. But no one could survive for two weeks on water alone. He had to eat.","Even if there had been snacks brought in by medical staff, a treatment room like this couldn’t have provided enough food to last two weeks.","So that was it.","He had eaten people.","Jiang Cheng and Li Jiangbing went in to take a look as well.","There was feces everywhere in the inner room. A naked corpse lay on the floor. Judging from the clothes beside it, the victim had been a hospital orderly.","All the flesh had been cut from his body, leaving only stark white bones. The portions that hadn’t been cut away had begun to rot, which explained the stench in the room.","The meat that had been cut off hadn’t all been eaten. Some of it was still in the refrigerator used to store chilled medication. But the refrigerator could only keep things cold, not freeze them, and after so long, the meat was no longer fresh.","“I had no choice. I was going to starve to death.” The doctor broke down sobbing. “There were monsters outside. Whenever we made a sound, they clawed at the door.”","“He died, and I was almost starving to death too. I really had no other option but to eat him.”","He pulled at his hair, putting on an expression of unbearable anguish, clearly hoping to arouse their sympathy.","But Jiang Cheng asked, “How did he die?”","He had prepared for this question long ago—from the moment the orderly died.","With his nose running and tears streaming down his face, he cried, “He was bitten by a monster. I tried to save him, but he’d lost too much blood. I couldn’t save him. I’m useless! I’m a doctor, but I couldn’t save someone!”","But he soon found himself unable to continue crying.","Everyone in the strange white plastic armor was staring at him expressionlessly.","They had tightened their grips on their weapons. Whether it was a steel pipe or a kitchen knife, the business end of every weapon was pointed straight at him, ready for anything.","The doctor’s sobbing abruptly stopped.","He couldn’t understand it. His performance had been flawless. Why had they seen through his lie?"]},{"number":76,"title":"Chapter 76","paragraphs":["That was the thing about information asymmetry.","Everyone knew that the only way a living person could be “bitten to death” by a zombie was if, by sheer coincidence, the zombie bit through their neck, severing the connection between the brain and the rest of the body.","Otherwise, even if someone had chunks of flesh bitten off, lost a great deal of blood, or appeared to be dead, they would still mutate into a second-generation zombie.","Everyone knew that.","Everyone except the doctor who had been locked in that small room since the zombie virus first broke out.","He had dropped his phone while fleeing for his life. There was no television in the treatment room, only a landline. He had made countless calls for help, and had finally managed to get through once—only to be told that they could only save themselves for now.","The four or five zombies that had chased him there did not leave even after things quieted down. They continued wandering outside the door.","He could not get out, and had no way to obtain information from the outside world. His understanding of zombies remained limited to those first, most obvious impressions: “man-eating monsters” that were “sensitive to sound.” He knew nothing beyond that.","He had told everyone what he thought was a flawless lie, only for them all to see through it in a second.","Li Feng spent his days in the New Technology District.","He had transported supplies there that morning, where volunteers were waiting to receive them.","Jiang Cheng had sent all the stock clerks from Mai Duoduo Supermarket over to help him, leaving only the cleaners and Guo Jun, the all-purpose repairman, behind to keep things running in the residential compound.","The stock clerks had only agreed to go work at Mai Duoduo after she promised that they could continue living in the compound.","They knew the warehouse, shelves, and equipment better than anyone. With the few of them there, everyone could stay busy without falling into chaos.","The empty trucks were put to use as well: they were sent back to haul zombies away.","There were simply too many zombie corpses now. Strangely enough, when zombies were still “alive,” their skin turned a dark bluish-green or grayish-blue, but even if their bodies were injured, they did not continue to decay.","Once they were truly killed “dead,” however, their bodies rotted rapidly just like those of dead humans, becoming infested with maggots.","If so many corpses were left unprocessed, it would not be long before an epidemic broke out. Nor could they expect to burn all those zombie bodies in the city streets. The authorities had the supply trucks bring goods over, and once they had been unloaded, the empty trucks hauled the zombies back for centralized disposal.","Several large trucks made multiple round trips every day.","Zhao Yi had been hounding Li Feng for quite some time about how the trucks were being disinfected.","Li Feng did not know much about it either, but he had gotten to know Zhao Yi over the past couple of days and had received a great deal of help from him, so he answered seriously with what he did know.","“They wear masks. First, they spray everything down with high-pressure water guns to wash off the dirt. Then they put on these big tanks and spray again. It should be some kind of disinfectant. After that, they use huge electric fans—the industrial kind—to dry everything. The trucks have to be completely dry before they can load anything onto them.”","Zhao Yi insisted on knowing what kind of disinfectant they used.","“I don’t know either,” Li Feng said. “They spray several kinds. One person finishes, then another comes along and sprays again. The tanks they carry are all the same, but the writing on them is different. One of them said something like ‘er-two’ or ‘two-er’... some kind of aldehyde?”","“Glutaraldehyde?” Zhao Yi asked.","“That’s it!”","He added, “Don’t worry. We have experts.”","Zhao Yi was only barely satisfied with the disinfection process, but he still said, “Even if they disinfect the trucks every night, they really shouldn’t be using the same vehicles for corpses and food.”","Li Feng did not like hearing that. He shot back, “Then what else are we supposed to do?”","Zhao Yi was left speechless.","Because there really was no other option. The truck drivers were working nonstop and were especially exhausted.","Zhao Yi sighed.","Just then, Jiang Cheng called Li Feng. Li Feng immediately took the opportunity to get away from Zhao Yi and stepped aside to answer.","“Hello? Jiang Cheng?”","“Are you still there?”","“Yeah.”","“You’d better wait for us. Don’t leave yet. I have someone to hand over to you.”","Renshin Hospital had been successfully secured.","When Jiang Cheng led the team back, she brought someone with her for Li Feng.","The man’s hands had been tied behind his back. After realizing that his lies had been exposed, he had tried to make a run for it, but everyone had tackled him and held him down.","Li Jiangbing pinned him to the ground and shouted, “Run? Where do you think you’re going? There are still plenty of zombies outside! If you’re not afraid of dying, then go ahead and run!”","This was the first time the male doctor had heard the term “zombie,” but he immediately understood that it referred to those mutated monsters that bit people.","He did not dare run again. But he was someone who had been willing to kill, so everyone kept his hands tied, just in case.","Jiang Cheng briefly explained the situation to Li Feng.","Li Feng fell silent.","Jiang Cheng said, “We can’t find the police right now, and we don’t want to let him go either. Take him back with you.”","Li Feng nodded. “All right.”","Then he asked, “Did everything go smoothly at the hospital?”","Jiang Cheng answered cheerfully, “Once we get everyone organized tomorrow to clean up and disinfect the hospital, and gather all the doctors from nearby, we’ll have a hospital again.”","When she spoke about these things, the girl radiated light. Even with dirt on her body and damp strands of hair plastered to her forehead with sweat, she remained dazzling.","There was not the slightest trace of fear, disgust, or revulsion toward the zombies in her expression. Her eyes were bright and full of life.","She was overflowing with vitality.","Li Feng felt that, as an official representative, he ought to say a few words of praise and commend the civilians who had performed so outstandingly.","Yet for some reason, the mouth that was usually so articulate seemed unable to open properly whenever he was in front of Jiang Cheng.","After stammering for a moment, all he could squeeze out was, “Keep it up.”","Jiang Cheng smiled and accepted his encouragement before someone called her away. She was extremely busy.","Li Feng felt like an idiot. Irritated, he tugged his cap down to cover his eyes.","But when Jiang Cheng called him over to discuss the next day’s arrangements, he hurried over with long strides.","With the supply line open, hardly anyone in the New Technology District was going hungry anymore.","Zhao Yi told Jiang Cheng and the others, “People from Shanshui Yayuan have arrived too.”","They had come to collect supplies. There were not many of them, and they stuck together, staying only with people from their own residential compound. When they saw the people from Deqingli, their expressions changed.","The people from Deqingli were equally uncomfortable when they saw them. Many of them turned their heads away.","“I saw one of them looking like he wanted to go find Li Feng,” Zhao Yi said. “The others pulled him back and talked him out of it.”","He added, “I happened to be passing by with a handcart and overheard a bit.”","They had urged the man to endure it for now and wait until later...","They really did have to wait. The supply channel had been established, but the state’s law-enforcement agencies had not yet resumed operating.","Li Feng only had a handful of people escorting the trucks.","And they were soldiers, not police officers. Criminal cases were the police’s responsibility.","More importantly, so many people from Deqingli had come to collect supplies that they vastly outnumbered the residents of Shanshui Yayuan.","The time was indeed not right yet. The people from Shanshui Yayuan had decided to swallow their anger for now.","Everyone also told Zhao Yi about the doctor they had brought back.","Zhao Yi was the sort of person who waited for the light even when crossing an empty street. He remained silent for a long time before asking, “Then... will he be punished by law?”","As he said this, his eyes could not help drifting toward the people from Deqingli who had not yet left.","Judging by the behavior of the people from Shanshui Yayuan, there had to be murderers among those from Deqingli.","Would all of them eventually face legal punishment?","Zhao Yi felt a little lost.","Because he had seen the devastation at Lekang Homeland. Humans—carbon-based life-forms—really could starve to death.","When driven by a crisis of survival, should the actions one takes be judged guilty or innocent?","Would the principle of necessity apply?","“That’s not something we should be thinking about right now. Nor is it something we can decide,” Jiang Cheng said. “Let’s talk about tomorrow’s arrangements first.”","She waved to Li Feng and called out, “Li Feng, come over here and help us figure out tomorrow’s schedule.”","Li Feng strode over.","That day, Li Feng took the male doctor with him.","When he came back on Sunday, one of the four vehicles was loaded entirely with disinfecting supplies. After the other three vehicles unloaded their supplies at Maiduo, all four followed the volunteers to Renxin Hospital.","The moment they met, Li Jiangbing asked Li Feng about the man from the previous day. “What are we going to do with him?”","“He hasn’t been dealt with yet,” Li Feng said. “But he’s been interrogated.”","The man and a nursing aide had been chased by zombies and fled for their lives, eventually taking refuge in a treatment room in the outpatient wing. Several zombies had blocked the way out.","Unable to contact anyone for rescue, the man grew desperate after going hungry for several days and killed the nursing aide for meat.","“He confessed to everything,” Li Feng said. “The interrogator told me he suffered a mental breakdown afterward and seems to have gone a little crazy. We don’t have time to deal with him right now, so we’ve locked him up for the moment. We’ll figure out what to do with him later.”","Everyone was far too busy at the moment.","All the people who came today were volunteers.","Although no zombies had appeared by the end of the previous day, even after they used a loudspeaker to draw them out, they still proceeded cautiously. On each floor, combat personnel in protective armor checked every room first. Only after confirming that it was safe did the volunteers begin disinfecting with the solution they had received from Li Feng.","Zhao Yi took charge of the practical arrangements. There was a young woman in the residential compound who was an intern at Renxin Hospital, and she worked alongside him. The two of them discussed everything together.","All the corpses were loaded onto the vehicles and taken back for the government to handle collectively.","Jiang Cheng told Li Feng, “Yesterday, we contacted and confirmed the identities of twenty-two medical workers.”","They were incredibly lucky that so many doctors had chosen to buy homes in the Science and Technology New District for the sake of being close to work. Every department was represented.","“Once we finish cleaning up the hospital today, it can open and start treating patients tomorrow.”","Li Feng stood in the open, square-shaped corridor, hands braced on his hips as he looked up and down.","People were busy everywhere, both upstairs and downstairs.","After such a staggering number of deaths, what the survivors had shown instead was this astonishing vitality.","“All right,” he said. “I’ll include everything in my report when I get back.”","Jiang Cheng raised an eyebrow. “You still have to write a report?”","“They haven’t ordered us to yet.” Li Feng bared his teeth in a grin. “But once this is all over, they definitely will.”","Like the other soldiers, his skin had been darkened by the sun, which made his bright white teeth stand out even more.","From Thursday to Sunday, he had already become completely familiar with many of the key people here.","Conditions in the Science and Technology New District were improving steadily as well. Almost the entire main residential area had become a safe zone, and now even Renxin Hospital had been reclaimed.","People’s spirits were no longer so heavy. They could even talk with smiles on their faces.","After Song Jingshuo finished sweeping the buildings with his team, he met up with Li Jiangbing, and the two went to look for Jiang Cheng.","As soon as they reached the floor, they spotted Li Feng in the distance, grinning foolishly at Jiang Cheng.","Look at that stance—with his hands planted on his hips, showing off both his chest and biceps. What a shameless poser.","Li Jiangbing covertly stole a glance at Song Jingshuo."]},{"number":77,"title":"Chapter 77","paragraphs":["Rumors had been circulating throughout the residential compounds that Jiang Cheng and Song Jingshuo were already a couple.","After being cooped up in the community for half a month, it was only natural that this large group of young people would end up producing a few couples. Some had even moved in together.","A lot of people were curious about Jiang Cheng and Song Jingshuo. Some had even gone so far as to ask Li Jiangbing about them.","After all, Li Jiangbing should have been the person who knew the most about those two. The three of them were often together.","Whenever Jiang Cheng had something to discuss, she would usually talk it over with the two of them first before calling a meeting of all seven members.","None of this was a secret.","The fact that a young woman had taken the position of leader during a crisis like this naturally meant that some people wanted to push her out. They simply lacked the ability to win over the other committee members.","Jiang Cheng was not the only one who inspired people’s trust. Although Li Jiangbing and Song Jingshuo had completely different styles, each had his own circle of friends and supporters.","Jiang Cheng’s position on the interim committee was rock solid.","After she had publicly called Vice Mayor Zheng and proposed mobilizing the masses to fight the battle, no one in the Youth Apartment could shake her position anymore.","As for her private life... Li Jiangbing, who had been quietly questioned by many people about it, actually knew very well that Jiang Cheng and Song Jingshuo were not a couple.","Li Jiangbing even felt that, in Jiang Cheng’s heart, he ranked slightly higher than Song Jingshuo. Jiang Cheng placed a great deal of trust in him.","At the same time, Li Jiangbing knew perfectly well that Song Jingshuo definitely had feelings for her.","Although Li Jiangbing had a very good relationship with Song Jingshuo, he was still an ordinary man at heart and rather enjoyed watching the drama unfold.","Unfortunately, Song Jingshuo disappointed him.","Song Jingshuo showed no unusual reaction whatsoever. He simply walked over and spoke calmly with the two of them.","Li Jiangbing was so anxious he scratched his head.","Still, Song Jingshuo did share a certain quality with Jiang Cheng. Even when facing someone who might be a potential rival in love, he could remain calm and speak evenly. That particular air about him was very much like Jiang Cheng’s.","From that perspective, the two of them really did have the bearing of a couple.","Li Jiangbing suddenly realized that this might be the reason Jiang Cheng valued Song Jingshuo as well.","Li Jiangbing had a great deal of self-awareness. He knew that his education was limited and that he lacked the ability to make brilliant decisions when it came to major matters. But he had a knack for minor cleverness. His particular talent was sticking close to people with good brains.","On the interim committee, he believed the two smartest people were Jiang Cheng and Song Jingshuo. Fortunately, the two of them never came into conflict, so he did not have to choose sides.","The three of them made the perfect iron triangle.","Monday marked the beginning of July, and the Tech New District took on an entirely new look.","First of all, Renxin Hospital reopened on July 1.","Seventeen doctors and five nurses were keeping Renxin Hospital running.","At the same time, Bus Route 535 began operating.","The route’s stationmaster lived in Deqing Li.","After Vice Mayor Zheng called on people in the Green Zones to restore as many basic services as possible, the stationmaster had gone to find Li Feng the day before and identified himself.","Li Feng immediately introduced him to Jiang Cheng and the others.","Deqing Li was home not only to a bus stationmaster, but also to several bus drivers.","Jiang Cheng’s eyes lit up.","“We need a route like this right now,” she had told the stationmaster the day before. “It should cover all the residential compounds, take people to Mai Duoduo, and bring them back afterward. It also needs to cover Renxin Hospital, since the hospital is reopening tomorrow. Ideally, there should be several runs a day.”","This was the stationmaster’s livelihood—his area of expertise.","Besides, Deqing Li had relatively few private vehicles and was a little farther from Mai Duoduo. Unlike Jixiang Jiayuan and the Youth Apartment, which were only a ten-minute walk away, residents there had to travel a greater distance to collect supplies.","Their need for transportation was therefore even stronger.","The stationmaster directly drew a circle on the map, connecting all the locations she had mentioned. He planned an inner loop through the residential area of the Tech New District.","It was exactly what Jiang Cheng wanted.","However, when the stationmaster tried to get her to return the four Route 535 buses, she refused.","Jiang Cheng said, “We’ll return them once all the zombies have been cleared out.”","The stationmaster was not being unreasonable. He simply had to mention it as part of his duty. He nodded and agreed.","Although Deqing Li had not yet formed a deep partnership with Jiang Cheng, its residents already knew that the largest force of ordinary people in the Tech New District was led by the young woman from the Youth Apartment.","Jixiang Jiayuan and Yujing Xiangyuan were already following her orders.","And so, on July 1, Renxin Hospital reopened, and Route 535 began operating its loop through the Tech New District.","There were ten runs a day.","Since the route was genuinely very short, each bus was required to make two circuits after leaving the station before returning.","In practice, that meant it could be regarded as twenty runs.","Every residential compound had notified its residents.","As soon as the loop began operating, people immediately started taking the bus to Renxin Hospital. Many others drove there themselves.","Renxin Hospital was fairly large, with eight floors, each covering a considerable area. The various departments were spread across the different floors.","But with only a handful of doctors working there, there was no need to make things difficult for everyone. Tables were simply set up in the outpatient lobby. Rows of chairs were brought down from the corridors, with a long line of seats placed in front of each table.","Volunteers handled registration at the scene, and everyone waited in line according to their number.","Plastic chairs were placed at the front of each line. People sat down until all the chairs were filled, and only then did those farther back have to stand.","When the person at the front finished seeing the doctor and left, the next person stepped forward. Everyone behind them only needed to shift forward one chair in turn.","The chairs also effectively prevented people from cutting in line. After all, no one could sit on someone else’s lap and insist that they had been sitting there all along.","The doctors tried to order as few tests as possible. Most tests could not be performed under the current circumstances, since there was no one available to operate the necessary equipment.","Bloodwork was the only option. Even that was kept to a minimum, because there was only one doctor working in the laboratory. Ordering too many tests might work him to death.","This meant that the doctors had to rely almost entirely on their experience to make diagnoses, which raised the difficulty by more than one level.","There was no pharmacist, so the young female doctor who had been an intern at the Youth Apartment was temporarily assigned to the pharmacy.","Everything was extremely rudimentary, but people felt more secure than ever.","Because everything was moving in a positive direction.","On the map released by the authorities the previous night, the Green Zones had continued to expand. Several places in S City had already reached a state similar to the Tech New District, where basic operations had more or less resumed within a certain area.","On July 2, something happened that filled Zhao Yi with excitement:","The garbage truck arrived!","At last, they no longer had to use supply trucks to transport bodies! The corpses had nearly all been cleared away, and the garbage trucks had begun collecting trash as well.","Before the outbreak, no one had realized how important garbage disposal really was. Now everyone understood.","The Youth Apartment organized volunteers to carry the trash that had accumulated in the swimming pool for two weeks into the garbage truck.","The sanitation workers saw piles of cardboard boxes stacked neatly together.","“There’s quite a lot of it,” one of them exclaimed, reaching out to haul it away.","Several cleaners from the Youth Apartment rushed over and spread their arms to block him.","“This isn’t trash. It belongs to us!”","Things were getting better and better. Even the aunties who worked as cleaners knew that normal social order would eventually be restored.","When that happened, all those cardboard boxes could be sold for a tidy sum.","How could they possibly let someone else take them away?","The sanitation worker let out a dry laugh and walked away.","Among the supplies delivered that day, there were vegetables for the first time. They were only potatoes and eggplants, with not a single leafy green in sight, but to people who hadn’t eaten vegetables in half a month, they were a feast fit for kings.","For the first time, the lines at Mai Duoduo nearly spiraled out of control.","It happened because the distribution lines had been orderly these past few days, so everyone had let their guard down. There were also countless other tasks to handle, and the strong men had been reassigned to jobs that required more physical labor elsewhere.","Nearly.","Even Li Feng couldn’t keep things under control. There were simply too few of them.","Besides, although they were carrying guns, soldiers used their guns to deal with enemies and zombies. How could they point them at civilians?","Li Feng’s combat uniform was torn to shreds. One of the soldiers even had his shoe trampled off.","They were in an especially sorry state.","Fortunately, the volunteers who had stayed behind to maintain order finally lost their tempers.","By now, everyone was used to carrying weapons with them—even when they came to Mai Duoduo to volunteer.","So the volunteers pulled steel pipes from behind their waists! Smack, smack, smack—they brought them down on the people pushing hardest at the front!","Screams rang out, and at last the chaos came to an end.","“Let’s see any of you try pushing forward again!” a volunteer roared, pointing his steel pipe at the crowd. “Come on, if you’ve got the guts!”","The volunteers, who had seemed so amiable and polite just moments ago, now had bulging veins, wide eyes, and vicious expressions.","They really would hit people!","Those really were steel pipes!","And that really was blood!","...Everyone fell silent and behaved.","They had only dared to act up because today’s volunteers didn’t look as big and intimidating as the ones from the previous few days.","After this, they shrank right back into place.","Even the most unreasonable old men and women didn’t dare complain or shove their way forward.","Because they all knew things were different now.","These people had smashed in human skulls, severed human necks, and crushed eyeballs beneath their feet.","Things were different. There was no going back.","They shouldn’t push these people too far.","Everyone had seen what happened when people were driven to the breaking point over the past half month.","Li Feng’s mood was incredibly complicated.","He felt that order had been lost.","And yet, it was precisely this disorder that was preserving order.","Violence was preserving civilization.","At that moment, Li Feng deeply understood how correct the central government had been to mobilize the masses in a people’s war against the zombie crisis.","If this disaster didn’t end soon, who knew what people would become?","It had to end as quickly as possible. Society had to return to the civilized, law-governed world it had once been!","Li Feng took the initiative to approach Jiang Cheng and submit a request. “The distribution point still needs a few more people. It would be best if Li Jiangbing could come.”","Yes, he was submitting a request.","Because all personnel assignments in the Technology New District were now under Jiang Cheng’s control.","The residential area of the Technology New District was basically fully operational now. The industrial park was a long way from the residential area, and Jiang Cheng had no intention of touching it for the time being.","For now, the work consisted mostly of odd jobs and heavy labor, and there was no immediate need for combat personnel.","So Jiang Cheng assigned Li Jiangbing and Nie Kuizhang to Li Feng to help maintain order. The volunteers working in shifts were also instructed to be as tall, broad, and intimidating as possible.","As soon as these three imposing guardians took over, order at Mai Duoduo immediately returned to normal.","Everyone put on the manner of law-abiding citizens.","But Li Feng could never again look at these people the way he had before.","That was because Li Jiangbing was a talkative man. Whenever he was stationed there to keep watch, he liked to chat with Li Feng.","Through Li Jiangbing, Li Feng learned about many of the things that had happened over the past two weeks—such as the blood feud between Deqingli and Shanshui Yayuan.","At last, he understood the strange things he had noticed while distributing supplies these past few days.","The more he understood, the heavier his heart became.","On July 3, a new announcement suddenly aired on television during the day.","Vice Mayor Zheng delivered a speech that morning.","“Part of the supply chain has been restored, but it has not yet been fully restored.”","“Volunteer militias are now being recruited.”","“Supplies are limited. Leafy greens and fresh meat will be distributed to militia members as a priority.”","Leafy greens! Fresh meat!","People who had been eating nothing but rice and canned food every day for half a month began salivating at the mere sound of those two words!"]},{"number":78,"title":"Chapter 78","paragraphs":["Rice and flour didn’t need to be collected very often. A single bag was enough to last for many days.","Most people came for the nonstaple foods. These took up far more space than the staple grains and consumed much faster, too.","The nonstaple foods available at the moment were mostly canned goods, and it was obvious at a glance that they were all from old stock.","The only newly added items were potatoes and eggplants—vegetables that had been chosen because they could be stored for a longer time.","But the vegetables shown on the news were green. Everyone had gone far too long without seeing green vegetables.","They said that some elderly women and housewives in Auspicious Garden had started growing vegetables on their balconies. Some even sold them for money or traded them for other goods. The prices were nearly as high as gold, yet people still bought them.","After all, they were expensive, but no one ate them every day. When the craving became unbearable, people would buy some just to satisfy it.","Once Vice Mayor Zheng’s notice about “recruiting militia members” was released, the entire Youth Apartment was abuzz with discussion.","It probably wasn’t just the Youth Apartment. The entire Technology New District—even the whole of S City—was talking about it.","The priority distribution of fresh vegetables and meat to militia members was merely an additional benefit. Militia members weren’t volunteers; they were paid on a daily basis.","If they died, they would be treated as martyrs. They themselves would never get to enjoy the benefits, of course, but their families and children would receive support in the future. Vice Mayor Zheng had promised that the children of martyrs would have priority admission through special channels for kindergarten, primary school, and junior high.","They would also receive extra points for the high school and college entrance examinations.","For those who weren’t registered residents of S City, their children could even obtain S City household registration.","In reality, for ordinary people, it was difficult to keep their blood burning for very long.","When the nation called upon them, ordinary citizens had gone out without hesitation, armed with kitchen knives and iron rods, carving out a place to survive for themselves so they wouldn’t have to sit at home and wait to starve to death.","But once that space was large enough, once national supplies began arriving, once even garbage trucks started appearing and hospitals began operating again—once the basic systems needed to sustain daily life had started functioning again—their hot blood returned to a normal temperature.","They wanted to retreat into their homes and live a stable, peaceful, and safe life.","But the militia might have to go to places very far away, perhaps the city center or the other side of the city. Leaving their own residential districts meant making sacrifices for the sake of others. Without tangible benefits, slogans and emotional appeals alone wouldn’t be enough to motivate them.","Ordinary people couldn’t be held to the standards of saints.","They had to be offered benefits that could truly move them.","The militia’s daily wage amounted to the average monthly salary in S City after just six days of work.","That was the average salary, meaning it included both the lowest- and highest-paid workers.","For many low-income earners, in fact, two days of daily wages would equal what they used to earn in an entire month.","That couldn’t possibly move a high-income group like Song Jingshuo, but Master Luo was immediately tempted.","Everything was urgent, leaving people no time to deliberate. The news aired in the morning, and registration began that afternoon.","The registration point was at the supply station. Anyone interested could simply register with the person in charge.","That afternoon, Jiang Cheng watched through Maiduo Duo as people arrived one after another to sign up. Li Feng and his companions were so busy they could barely keep up, and they had to drag Zhao Yi over to help with the registration.","Jiang Cheng couldn’t sign up because of the gender requirement. The notice explicitly stated that only men were eligible.","And no one objected to the gender restriction—not the men, and not the women.","Jiang Cheng herself had no intention of joining, either.","In the Technology New District, she had to be the first to put herself on the front line because they needed victory, control, and leadership.","But joining the militia and putting herself on the front line would mean nothing more than being the first into battle. She wouldn’t be the one in control or the one giving orders.","Combat wasn’t a hobby, much less a goal.","It was merely a means—a process.","Zhou Wang came over to take a look, then said to Jiang Cheng, “There are quite a lot of people.”","Jiang Cheng had already been observing for some time. She told him, “Most of them are from Deqingli and our residential complex.”","Zhou Wang was silent for a moment before asking, “What’s going on with the people from your complex?”","He didn’t ask about Deqingli.","The people of Deqingli generally had lower incomes, so the militia’s benefits were highly attractive to them.","But many of the young people in the Youth Apartment had decent incomes. They were white-collar workers who sat in offices and enjoyed air-conditioning.","Jiang Cheng smiled. “They’re young.”","The young could keep their blood hot for longer.","The young were also more willing to take risks.","Auspicious Garden and Imperial View Garden were both home to people with elderly parents above them and young children below them. Once they had carved out a sufficient space to survive, they weren’t willing to risk their lives for short-term benefits anymore.","Of course, there were some exceptions.","Some people had simply become addicted to killing.","Jiang Cheng had noticed long ago that some people had fallen into a kind of excitement, as though they were playing a live-action game. They seemed to be becoming fascinated with it.","Jiang Cheng suddenly raised an eyebrow.","Zhou Wang followed her gaze. “Well, look at that.”","A large, heavily built man had squeezed his way toward Li Feng to register. He was impossible to miss.","Li Feng was now extremely familiar with Li Jiangbing, and was delighted to see him come to sign up. “You’re exactly the kind of person we need!”","The higher-ups had given instructions to screen applicants not only by gender, but also by age and physical strength.","Master Luo had come to register as well, but Li Feng rejected him when he saw his age and slightly stooped back.","They only wanted the strong and fit.","There was no room for dead weight in combat. A weak person would not only put himself in danger, but might also endanger his comrades.","Some of the young men from Deqingli had a fierceness in their eyes, and Li Feng accepted them on the spot.","As for the applicants from the Youth Apartment, he was much more selective. Anyone too thin, too short, or wearing thick glasses was rejected.","People like Li Jiangbing—strong and rich in combat experience—were exactly what he wanted.","Li Jiangbing successfully registered. When he pushed his way out of the crowd, he saw Jiang Cheng and Zhou Wang both watching him.","Li Jiangbing paused, looking a little guilty, then went over to greet Jiang Cheng.","The first thing Jiang Cheng asked was, “Do they have armor that fits you?”","The official notice stated that armor and weapons would be provided. People were also allowed to bring their own weapons. After all, everyone had spent the past few days using weapons they were comfortable with, and they might not adapt well to unfamiliar ones.","But when it came to armor, the equipment provided by the authorities was certainly better than anything people could prepare themselves.","Li Jiangbing let out a sigh of relief and told her, “I asked specifically before signing up. The militia’s armor is all newly made, and they have extra-large sizes. I can wear one.”","Li Jiangbing and Nie Kuizhang were both exceptionally capable fighters, yet neither of them could fit into the standard-sized armor from before. Li Jiangbing had been particularly resentful about it at the time, repeatedly grumbling that Li Feng needed to report the issue to his superiors.","Li Feng really had reported it.","And it wasn’t a problem unique to his registration point. After all, a man’s physique was often directly proportional to his strength—and therefore to his combat ability.","The Emergency Command Center was responsible for responding rapidly to every possible situation, so the feedback was immediately passed on to the factories, which made the necessary adjustments.","The new batch of armor included larger sizes.","Jiang Cheng said, “That’s good. Be careful and stay safe. Don’t charge too far ahead.”","Only then did Li Jiangbing fully relax.","Joining the militia meant leaving the Youth Apartment and the interim committee. It meant leaving Jiang Cheng.","Jiang Cheng’s gaze passed over him and settled on the people signing up. She said, “Things will keep getting better. Once all the zombies have been wiped out, everyone’s lives will return to normal. When that day comes, we’ll look back on this time and remember how neighbors who didn’t even know one another formed the interim committee and led everyone in solving one problem after another, all pulling together through the crisis. We’ll definitely miss it, won’t we?”","The way she put it made Li Jiangbing start reminiscing on the spot.","Because it was plain to see that humanity had reclaimed its living space. Everything was gradually returning to normal, and there was less and less for the Interim Committee to do.","In a few more days, once all the zombies had been wiped out, the Interim Committee would be disbanded too.","Li Jiangbing, meanwhile, would be leaving ahead of schedule.","He strolled back to the residential compound with Jiang Cheng and said, “I really want to get my hands on one of those suits of armor. Just wait and see—I’m definitely bringing one back.”","Jiang Cheng laughed.","That evening, the buses arrived and the militia assembled.","Li Jiangbing tucked his fire axe behind his waist and followed Li Feng onto the bus.","Quite a few people from the Youth Apartments had signed up to join, and many familiar faces came out to see them off.","“Be careful!”","“Good luck!”","Everyone watched as they departed.","Li Jiangbing was gone for four days.","He returned on the fifth day, knocked on Jiang Cheng’s door, and handed her a plastic bag filled with fresh vegetables and meat. “Put the meat in the fridge right away. It was pretty hot on the way back, and I’m worried it’ll spoil.”","Then he patted another bag in his hand. “I’ve got more here. I’m taking it to Jingshuo.”","“Wait,” Jiang Cheng said. “I’ll go with you.”","She put the food in the refrigerator and went out with Li Jiangbing.","“Where’s your cat?” Li Jiangbing asked.","“He’s out all day. He hardly ever stays home.”","She called Song Jingshuo on the way.","When they arrived at Song Jingshuo’s place, he didn’t thank them either. The relationship between Jiang Cheng, Song Jingshuo, and Li Jiangbing had long since reached the point where none of them needed to say thank you.","He only said, “You’re back. That’s good. I was worried you wouldn’t make it back.”","Li Jiangbing laughed and lightly punched him on the shoulder.","Food was no longer scarce.","“Have you had lunch?” Song Jingshuo asked. “Stay and eat with me.”","This was Song Jingshuo’s home, and Song Jingshuo was the chef, with Jiang Cheng helping him prepare the meal. Li Jiangbing couldn’t cook, so he simply waited to eat.","Song Jingshuo’s apartment was one of the largest units in the Youth Apartments. It even had a proper kitchen, complete with walls and a door.","Li Jiangbing dragged over a chair, straddled it backward at the kitchen entrance, and rested his arms on the backrest as he told them about the militia team.","That was precisely why Jiang Cheng had come along—to hear about it too.","“The main target was the university town.”","“We went to the University of Science and Technology first. Oh man, it was a disaster. There were so many zombies—so, so many.”","“The soldiers led the operation and issued us protective armor. Our main weapons were machetes and spiked clubs.”","“We also had remote-controlled cars. I don’t know who came up with that idea, but it worked great.”","They strapped explosives to the remote-controlled cars, played music through them, and sent them squealing and blaring down the road while a huge horde of zombies chased after them.","“At first, the captain said we should run the cars in spirals, circling the zombies into one big cluster before blowing them up. It sounded like a good plan to us too. But once we tried it in a real operation, we found out it didn’t work.”","“Zombies don’t circle around with you. They just walk in a straight line, heading straight for the sound.”","“Anyway, after a lot of trial and error, we slowly figured out how to do it. Get the zombies to gather in one place, then blow them up. One blast could take out a whole group.”","“And there was that thing you carry on your shoulder. I thought it was called a rocket launcher, but it turns out it’s called a rocket-propelled grenade launcher.”","“Whoosh—one shot, and another whole group was gone.”","“Once we finished off the ones that had gathered together, the scattered ones were dealt with using gunfire. Biubiubiu~”","He even imitated the sound effects.","“But the moment we opened fire, wow, they came charging straight at us.”","“Once they got close, that was when we went in.”","“Of course, the soldiers joined us too. First, they had to put their guns away. After that, they used knives just like we did.”","“Do you know why? Because once it turns into close-quarters combat, you can’t use guns anymore. It’s too easy to hit your own people.”","Li Jiangbing recounted the events of the past few days with animated enthusiasm.","Song Jingshuo’s cooking was unexpectedly good. He was a man with very high standards when it came to the quality of his life—including his food.","Of course, it might also have been because they had gone far too long without eating a single plate of stir-fried vegetables and meat.","Li Jiangbing took one bite, and tears nearly sprang to his eyes.","“Oh my god. This is what it means to be alive.”","He would never restrict his diet again!"]},{"number":79,"title":"Chapter 79","paragraphs":["\"Fortunately, there were whole cases of instant noodles, ham sausages, and lots of snacks stockpiled in the dormitory. Those students managed to survive on these. It was really not easy.\"","\"Then, do you know what other places were hard - hit areas?\" Li Jiangbing counted on his fingers. \"Universities, hospitals, and hotels! Hotels were a bit better. Many people were locked in their rooms. Anyway, we'll just have to clear them room by room.\"","\"Have you heard about what happened on those trains?\"","\"Haven't heard? Well, forget it then. I won't tell you. It was extremely tragic. The trains were full of people.\"","Song Jingshuo and Jiang Cheng listened very attentively.","Everyone knew that such days were numbered.","There was a sense of the end approaching.","Song Jingshuo asked, \"How much meat and vegetables did you get? You brought me so much.\"","Li Jiangbing waved his hand. \"I'm taking a day off today. I'll leave again early tomorrow. I divided the supplies into two parts, one for you and one for Jiang Cheng.\"","Jiang Cheng and Song Jingshuo glanced at each other and then looked at Li Jiangbing together. \"Leaving again tomorrow?\"","\"Yeah~\" Li Jiangbing replied. \"I'm just back for one day of rest. I'll go again tomorrow. I need to have a good sleep. These days, I just slept wherever I could. It was so uncomfortable. It's still good to be at my own home.\"","Song Jingshuo still wanted to persuade Li Jiangbing.","Song Jingshuo's way of doing things had always been rather self - centered, just like the people in his circle.","If it were someone else, Song Jingshuo wouldn't even have bothered to say anything and would have just respected their choice. But Li Jiangbing was not just anyone; he was one of his own.","However, Li Jiangbing politely declined. He had his own reasons. \"I reckon it's going to be tough in the following days. I'm taking this opportunity to earn more money.\"","But Jiang Cheng propped his chin up and looked at him, suddenly asking, \"Jiangbing, do you actually like doing this?\"","\"Huh?\" Li Jiangbing paused. \"Um—\"","Sometimes, not denying is actually admitting.","\"Well, how should I put it,\" he said. \"Anyway, it's more interesting than going to work.\"","The pay was good, there were no complicated interpersonal relationships, and he didn't have to bow and scrape. If being a militiaman to kill zombies could be called a \"job\", he was willing to take it.","The only downside was the risk of death.","\"What on earth are we living for? I've been thinking about this question a lot lately,\" the strong - built man said in a confused tone. \"I just can't figure it out.\"","He still remembered the feeling of almost soiling his pants when he first saw a zombie on that Saturday night.","But now, his body had developed a muscle memory. The moment he saw a zombie, his whole body would tense up with power, and the next moment, the axe would swing out.","The movement was smooth, the aim was accurate, and the feeling of killing was really exhilarating.","Li Jiangbing thought he might be a bit of a psycho. He really liked this feeling and enjoyed doing this.","\"To earn more money, seek a higher social status, and possess more social resources,\" Song Jingshuo answered him without a moment's hesitation. \"Simply put, it's to strive to be at the top of the social ladder.\"","Li Jiangbing clicked his tongue. \"Tsk tsk tsk~\"","Then he looked at Jiang Cheng. \"What about you, Jiang Cheng?\"","Jiang Cheng smiled. \"I decline to answer.\"","Li Jiangbing clicked his tongue again. \"Tsk~\"","Jiang Cheng just smiled without saying a word.","Finally, the three of them clinked their glasses.","There was water in the glasses. The beverages and alcohol in the Maiduoduo Supermarket had mysteriously disappeared later.","Not only beverages and alcohol, but also things like brooms, mops, bedding, bowls, dishes, pots, shovels, and basins, as long as they were not too big and difficult to move, had all mysteriously disappeared during this period, leaving only empty shelves.","Li Feng didn't deliver beverages and alcohol when sending supplies either. Now, everyone could only use water instead of wine.","Song Jingshuo wanted to say a toast. He just started with \"When you...\", but Li Jiangbing spread his five fingers and waved them in front of him. \"Don't say it! Don't say it!\"","\"Definitely don't wait for me!\" he said in a panicked voice. \"In movies, anyone who says such lines never comes back!\"","Jiang Cheng burst out laughing.","This meal of stir - fried vegetables and meat was just an ordinary home - cooked dish in the past. But it was the best meal they'd had in the past three weeks.","Li Jiangbing gave his house key to Jiang Cheng. \"If there's a water leak or something when I'm not home, please help me deal with it.\"","The next day, he left again on the coach.","There were many fewer people leaving this time compared to the first batch. But there were still a lot of people like Li Jiangbing who, either for money or for some other reasons, continued to participate in the militia's operations.","The green areas on the map were expanding day by day and connecting with each other. Every day there were inspiring news.","On July 15th, Li Feng finally brought fresh green vegetables and fresh meat. He informed Jiang Cheng in advance, and Jiang Cheng arranged the manpower accordingly.","Although there were suddenly a large number of people in Maiduoduo, the order was well - maintained.","The residents in the community were also willing to be volunteers. Even a military man like Li Feng knew that \"if the water is too clear, there will be no fish\". Volunteers could get a little more than others.","July 20th was Li Feng's last day in charge of the supply point in the Science and Technology New Area.","He said goodbye to everyone one by one.","Zhao Yi gave him a big bear hug. They were quite familiar with each other.","Zhao Yi said, \"It's a pity that Jiangbing isn't here today.\"","Li Feng also felt regretful. \"Yeah, it is.\"","He was also very familiar with Li Jiangbing.","They might not see each other again in the future. Sometimes, the fate between people was just a short journey together.","Song Jingshuo's farewell was decent and business - like. \"May your future be as bright as brocade and your career be smooth.\"","Li Feng was not an ordinary conscript. He graduated from the National Defense University and became a junior officer upon graduation. He was going to pursue a career in the military.","Li Feng replied politely, \"Same to you. May you earn a fortune every day.\"","Zhao Yi turned his face away in disgust. He didn't want to see these two being so pretentious.","Finally, Li Feng said goodbye to Jiang Cheng. He seemed to have a lot to say but hesitated. In the end, he only said, \"Keep in touch.\"","Jiang Cheng smiled and said, \"Okay.\"","The military vehicle completed its last supply mission. The officers and soldiers got on the vehicle and left under the farewell of thousands of people in the Science and Technology New Area.","An old woman even cried. \"When they're gone, I feel so empty inside.\"","Another old woman comforted her. \"You're thinking wrong. They left because everything is okay now.\"","The old woman wiped her tears. \"You're right. It's all over.\"","\"He was so close to confessing his love in public. I saw the way he looked at her. It was so obvious. I thought he was going to pull out a rose from the back of his collar and confess,\" Zhao Yi complained to Gao Yuxuan. \"I got my hopes up for nothing. He's just a coward.\"","Gao Yuxuan was playing games with Zhao Yi at his home. Each of them held a game controller, and the battle was intense.","Gao Yuxuan said, \"Impossible. There were so many people there. What if Jiang Cheng rejected him? How embarrassing would that be?\"","Everyone could clearly tell that Li Feng had feelings for Jiang Cheng.","Speaking of which, Zhao Yi was really annoyed when Song Jingshuo got close to Jiang Cheng.","But he wasn't annoyed when Li Feng got close to Jiang Cheng.","Zhao Yi said, \"If I could choose for Jiang Cheng, I'd choose Li Feng.\"","Gao Yuxuan said, \"Huh?\"","Gao Yuxuan said, \"I'm sure Li Feng appreciates your kindness. But who do you think you are? \"","How dare he make decisions for Jiang Cheng.","Zhao Yi said, \"Okay, fine.\"","\"Jiang Cheng...\" Zhao Yi sighed.","Gao Yuxuan said, \"Huh?\"","Gao Yuxuan said, \"Don't tell me you also have feelings for Jiang Cheng?\"","Zhao Yi said, \"I don't have feelings for Jiang Cheng, but I like the combination of Jiang Cheng and Mo Li. Do you understand?\"","As a fellow otaku, Gao Yuxuan's voice went up a notch. \"Understood!\"","A pretty girl often had a little black cat sitting on her left shoulder.","Why the left shoulder? Because the right hand has more things to do, so it can't press on the right shoulder and hinder the movement of the right hand.","But when the girl is talking to someone, sometimes her right hand will subconsciously twirl the tip of the little black cat's hanging tail or pinch its little paw.","Especially when she is outdoors and the sun shines down.","How could such a scene appear in real life! This should clearly be a scene from the second dimension!","[No one knows that the seemingly gentle little black cat is actually a soul - reaper from hell...]","\"Stop stop stop!\" Zhao Yi interrupted Gao Yuxuan's fantasy. \"What bullshit soul - reaper. It must be a summoned beast!\"","In Zhao Yi's fantasy, when danger occurs, the moment the little black cat jumps down from the girl's shoulder, it transforms into a giant beast, covered in black flames. Its roar makes the ground tremble as it loyally guards the girl.","Gao Yuxuan: \"... How vulgar.\"","Zhao Yi: \"You're not any better.\"","The two otakus had a fierce argument over the divergence in their fantasy routes.","After the argument, Gao Yuxuan suddenly remembered: \"What did you want to say about Jiang Cheng just now?\"","Zhao Yi paused for a moment and pushed his glasses: \"Jiang Cheng... She misnamed me that day...\"","Gao Yuxuan: \"?\"","\"It was too busy that day,\" Zhao Yi said. \"I was beside her. When she called me, she called me 'Peng Ze'.\"","Suddenly, the room fell silent.","The characters on the TV also stopped, and only the background music was playing chaotically.","Gao Yuxuan sighed.","Zhao Yi still remembered that day when Jiang Cheng turned her head and saw that it was him, not Peng Ze. There was a moment of stunnedness on her face, and then she quickly adjusted her expression.","It was that moment that Zhao Yi couldn't forget.","Otaku are not good at expressing themselves and socializing, but they have delicate perception.","When the men in the community gather together to chat, someone often says that Jiang Cheng is not suitable to be a girlfriend.","She's so heartless.","What do these hooligans know? They just talk about which girl has long legs and which girl has a big chest all day long.","Zhao Yi despised them.","But Zhao Yi didn't know that in despising these people, he was on the same wavelength as Song Jingshuo, the person he hated the most.","On July 21st, a rumbling convoy of large trucks drove into the science and technology new area and entered the purchasing channel of Mai Duoduo.","This time, they were no longer military vehicles. The logistics chain had been unblocked, and this was a replenishment for Mai Duoduo Supermarket.","All the surviving employees had returned, and the number of deceased employees still needed to be counted. But these things would be dealt with later. The government's instruction was to replenish the goods first and resume business first.","First, let the people's lives return to normal.","Guo Jun and the others went to see Jiang Cheng.","Because they received a call from the manager asking them to go back to work. If they went back to work, theoretically, they should move back to the dormitory.","Then they couldn't work here anymore, and they couldn't live in the apartment.","Everyone was quite reluctant.","Jiang Cheng no longer cared about these things: \"I don't know. The house isn't mine either. The Provisional Committee has been dissolved. From now on, the property management will take care of these things.\"","\"It's over,\" she said. \"It's all over.\"","The words \"It's over\" gave people an inexplicable feeling of being in a different world.","But it was really over.","So Guo Jun and the others went to see Master Luo.","But Master Luo didn't make decisions anymore because the property manager had returned.","Master Luo was reporting his work to the manager. When Guo Jun and the others came and told him about the situation.","Manager: \"Ah? You've all been living in the apartment?\"","Master Luo nodded and told the situation at that time.","The manager rolled his eyes: \"How many empty houses are there in our community?\"","Master Luo said: \"The statistical table is with Yang Xinyan.\"","Originally, it was in the hands of the Provisional Committee. Now that the Provisional Committee no longer had any meaning to exist, Jiang Cheng gave the statistical table to Yang Xinyan.","The manager called out to Yang Xinyan: \"Little Yang!\"","Guo Jun and the others were anxious: \"Manager, we...\"","The manager raised his hand to stop him: \"Don't worry. Let me take a look first.\"","Yang Xinyan handed over the form. The manager took a quick look and gasped: \"So many!\"","Master Luo sighed: \"Yes, so many people died.\"","What the manager was thinking about was not the fact that so many people had died. He was thinking that now he had so many sets of unclaimed empty houses at his disposal."]},{"number":80,"title":"Chapter 80","paragraphs":["There were far too many empty apartments with no one to claim them.","Of course, the owners’ families might come to deal with them later. If any relatives showed up, they would hand over the keys.","But it was already clear that quite a few of the apartments might not have any family left to claim them.","Wait. There were too many things to deal with right now. They could worry about that later.","The property manager asked Guo Jun, “What exactly are you people planning to do?”","Guo Jun explained what they wanted. The property manager understood: Guo Jun and the others were reluctant to move out.","By now, everyone knew that these apartments were “ownerless,” and most people had entertained the idea of taking advantage of the situation.","The property manager understood better than anyone, because he had ideas of his own.","There were too many empty apartments. Guo Jun and the others had only occupied seven, and the property staff hadn’t taken many either. Compared with the total number of vacant units, it was nothing.","Besides, the property management office was desperately short-handed.","Everywhere was short of workers now, in every industry and every position. Too many people had died.","In the end, the property manager and Guo Jun’s group reached an agreement: they would work part-time for the property management office in exchange for rent.","After Guo Jun and the others left, Master Luo asked, “What about us...?”","The manager said, “Stay here.”","There were plenty of residential complexes where the property management companies had moved into vacant apartments without notifying the owners.","An owner might buy an apartment and leave it unfinished for a year before finally preparing to renovate it. Then, upon opening the door with the key, they would find a dozen metal bunk beds inside—the place had become a dormitory for thirty people.","That was standard practice for property management companies.","The manager said, “We’ll deal with it when the family comes looking.”","The zombie crisis had dragged on for more than a month. Work and production had ground to a halt, and now that they were suddenly resuming, there was far too much to do.","The manager asked, “What’s going on with the meeting room?”","Why had the door been welded shut?","Master Luo explained what had happened.","The manager clicked his tongue in shock.","“That Miss Jiang is ruthless.” The manager asked, “Who is she?”","Guo Jun and the others had mentioned “Miss Jiang” earlier, and when Yang Xinyan handed over the forms, she had also said that they were from “Miss Jiang.”","Miss Jiang this, Miss Jiang that—everyone kept talking about “Miss Jiang.”","Who was she?","Master Luo said, “She lives in Building Two, Apartment 0306. I’m in 0308 now, right next door to her.”","The property manager had no memory of the female owner in Building Two, Apartment 0306.","There were over a thousand people in the complex. How could he remember every one of them?","But the meeting room couldn’t simply be left unattended.","The manager asked, “What’s inside...?”","Master Luo said, “We’re not sure. Someone inside smashed the surveillance camera at the time.”","The manager didn’t want to hear any more about it. Now that it was finally over, he didn’t want to revisit that nightmare.","But the meeting room still had to be dealt with. They needed to get the door open.","The manager walked over and knocked. “Is anyone there? Is anyone still inside?”","Yang Xinyan shrank behind Master Luo. “There can’t possibly be anyone...”","It had been more than a month.","Even if someone had survived by eating human flesh, they should have responded to the knocking by now. Besides, the authorities had never said anything about people becoming infected without mutating.","But if that was the case, then theoretically there should still be at least one zombie inside.","Yet the manager knocked several times, and there was no response.","If there were a zombie in there, it would have slammed against the door long ago.","By now, everyone was thoroughly familiar with the habits of both the original zombies and the second-generation zombies.","The manager said, “We’ll have to find a way to open it.”","They needed an angle grinder to remove the welds.","Master Luo said, “The angle grinder is worn out.”","Over the past month, Cui Haiyang and the other engineering guys had been working intensely to modify their protective gear, and several tools had been ruined in the process. Now the property management office was short of both tools and people.","Besides, welding was one thing; taking welded metal apart was another. They needed a welder with experience in dismantling structures to do the job.","The manager said, “Get in touch with a welder. Find someone who can handle it.”","But welders were hard to find these days, too.","The jobs resuming that day were all essential services for people’s daily lives. Small private businesses, such as little restaurants and shops, as well as workers who found jobs independently, had not resumed operations yet. They would have to wait a few more days.","For now, the manager would first arrange shifts for the cleaners, security guards, and the rest of the staff. The priority was to restore the complex to a normal state of maintenance.","After that, he planned to inspect the ownerless apartments and think about what they could be used for.","Master Luo suddenly remembered something. “We still owe Miss Jiang and Mr. Song money.”","After hearing the details, the manager was displeased. “Why did you spend money? During a disaster, wasn’t everything free for the taking?”","Master Luo argued, “That was on the first day. No one dared take things without paying then.”","He had recorded everything they had bought and how much it had cost in a little notebook. Now he took it out and showed the manager.","In fact, the kitchen had already been due for a restocking run during those two days. The delivery person would normally drop off the supplies and then go to the accounting office to settle the bill.","It had been a legitimate expense from the start.","The manager grumbled under his breath, but because Master Luo insisted, he still had the accountant pay the money.","“Be sharper next time,” he said. “Start stealing things right from the beginning.”","What kind of thing was that to say? Was that even human?","And there was going to be a next time?","There were too many things, too complicated and jumbled together. Jiang Cheng wasn’t omnipotent, and it was inevitable that she had forgotten some matters.","The property management office’s meeting room, for example.","And all those ownerless apartments.","The matter with Guo Jun’s group reminded Jiang Cheng of something. She asked in the group chat:","【Does anyone have Peng Ze’s emergency contact information?】","She wanted to remind Peng Ze’s parents to reclaim the apartment.","She had heard that some people had gotten to know one another over the past month and exchanged each other’s emergency contact numbers.","They were afraid something might happen to them.","But no one in the group had exchanged contact information with Peng Ze.","Su Yu: 【I’ll ask around.】","After a while, she replied:","【He Tian said Peng Ze’s parents had been unreachable since the first day.】","Jiang Cheng stared at the screen for a long time before slowly typing:","【Got it. Thanks.】","At noon, Vice Mayor Zheng delivered a speech.","【Countless moving stories have emerged.】","【We stand united, sharing hardship through wind and rain.】","【I hereby announce that the zombie disaster in S City has ended.】","It was over.","One after another, cities across the country announced that their disasters had ended.","Humanity had reclaimed its living space.","Of course, it wasn’t completely over. Some areas were still carrying out extermination operations.","Even a major city like S City couldn’t guarantee that every last zombie had been cleared out. There might still be one or two hiding in some overlooked corner or alley.","But they no longer posed a threat to the city as a whole.","So it was fair to say that the disaster was over.","Jiang Cheng was thinking about this when she heard someone open a window and shout into the residential courtyard, “It’s over—it’s over!”","Many others immediately joined in.","A chaotic chorus of cheers rose through the complex.","It was just like when the temporary residents’ committee had led everyone in clearing the complex back then.","Jiang Cheng smiled.","Then she thought... Was that all?","Was the world really this simple?","It was a little boring.","That evening, Master Luo knocked on her door and handed her an envelope. “This is the money you and Mr. Song paid up front.”","Jiang Cheng had nearly forgotten about it.","She accepted the envelope and asked about the housing arrangements. When she learned that Guo Jun, Master Luo, and the others could continue living in the empty apartments, she said, “That’s good.”","Master Luo stood outside the door. For some reason, he felt that Jiang Cheng, just a step away from him, was no longer quite the same as before.","He went back inside and told Aunt Pan.","Aunt Pan was folding freshly washed clothes. “Oh, that’s because Little Jiang was in charge before. She had to be tough if she wanted people to listen to her. She doesn’t have to manage things anymore, of course she’s different. She’s relaxed now.”","Master Luo thought his wife was right.","On July 24, the bus finally brought back the last batch of militia members.","That marked the end of the militia’s final cleanup operation, and the militia was disbanded.","Li Jiangbing had returned four times in total. Each time, he rested for only a day before signing up for the next round.","This time, he was finally back for good.","Some companies had begun reopening one after another, but many still hadn’t. Some people had even lost their jobs outright. Their bosses were dead, and no one was left to manage the companies.","So there were still plenty of people lounging around at home in the residential complex.","When they heard that the last batch of militia members had returned, everyone came rushing out to take a look.","Li Jiangbing had once been a burly man. Now, he was a burly, sun-blackened man.","More accurately, he was a burly man who was black in some places and speckled in others.","His armor had plenty of holes for ventilation, which had left his arms white in some sections and covered with little black spots in others.","He carried a battered backpack on his back, a steel spiked mace in one hand, and an extra-large suit of armor in the other.","He looked absolutely delighted.","Song Jingshuo’s mouth twitched. “You really managed to bring it back?”","Li Jiangbing turned around, presenting his back to Song Jingshuo, and shook his massive body a few times.","The shabby backpack—heaven only knew where he’d gotten it—rattled loudly.","Li Jiangbing was unbearably pleased with himself. “The whole set!”","It turned out that the backpack contained the arm guards and leg guards.","In theory, the militia members were supposed to return their armor after the operation ended.","But this time, the operation was truly over. Any armor collected would only end up sitting in a warehouse, so the militia members who wanted theirs were allowed to take them home.","In fact, the armor from the Tech New District was also already in the hands of ordinary people.","Li Feng had brought it there, but when he left, he hadn’t asked for it back. Everyone had simply treated it like rice, cooking oil, and other consumable supplies.","As a result, most of the team members who had taken part in the battles still had their own armor.","Jiang Cheng and Song Jingshuo’s armor was still at home as well.","Cui Haiyang rushed over. “Let me see! Let me see! Is that a spiked mace?”","Zhao Yi leaned in. “How did they let you bring that back?”","Li Jiangbing grumbled, “Don’t remind me. I wanted a cleaver, but no matter how much I begged, they wouldn’t give me one. I had to settle for this spiked mace.”","Zhao Yi said, “Of course they wouldn’t. Knives are regulated weapons.”","Quite a few people had brought their protective gear home, but Li Jiangbing was the only one who had managed to bring back a spiked mace.","Everyone had heard from former militia members that the standard weapons issued were cleavers and spiked maces, and that people could choose whichever suited them better.","But most of them were seeing one in person for the first time.","A large group of men lined up to take turns playing with the spiked mace, pretending to beat up zombies.","The people waiting in back kept urging them on. “Hurry up, hurry up! Are you done yet? Two swings are enough. There’s a whole line of us waiting!”","Song Jingshuo and Jiang Cheng followed Li Jiangbing to his home.","After putting away his beloved armor, Li Jiangbing chatted with Jiang Cheng and Song Jingshuo. “These last few days were just cleanup. Things are pretty much settled. The whole city is more or less cleared out.”","Even if there were still a few stragglers, there was no longer any need for so many militia members.","The large-scale extermination operation was over. Any isolated cases could be handled by the police, urban management officers, and ordinary citizens working together.","It was over.","“I made a nice bit of money. Are the restaurants open yet?” Li Jiangbing asked cheerfully. “I’ll treat you two to a meal.”","But Jiang Cheng poured cold water on him. “Only two restaurants have reopened on Restaurant Street. We wouldn’t stand a chance of getting a table. I’m saving you the money.”","A lot of people were itching to splurge on food in a kind of revenge spending, but the restaurants had suffered major losses in manpower, and many had also been contaminated.","The government had stipulated that the food-service industry had to undergo complete decontamination before reopening.","Song Jingshuo said, “I got a notice from my company today. I have to go back to work tomorrow.”","“Ah, work...” Li Jiangbing sighed.","The word sounded so unfamiliar. It felt like something from a previous lifetime.","Song Jingshuo asked Jiang Cheng, “What about you?”","Jiang Cheng was just about to answer when her phone rang. The caller ID read: “Mr. Peng.”","It was her boss.","Jiang Cheng: “...”","What incredible bad luck."]},{"number":81,"title":"Chapter 81","paragraphs":["Jiang Cheng went back to work.","The moment Mr. Peng saw her, he said, “I’m promoting you.”","She had to be promoted. There was simply no one left.","Mr. Peng said, “You’ll have to go on a business trip.”","All of Jiang Cheng’s colleagues who had been away on business when the zombie outbreak began had gone missing.","No one knew whether they were alive or dead. That was the norm during the zombie crisis.","The bodies burned at the youth apartment, as well as those later taken away by the government, were also people whose families had no idea whether they were alive or dead.","That is, if their families were still alive.","The people were gone, but the company’s equipment and supplies were still there. They were company assets, after all.","There were also unfinished projects for clients. Should their contracts be terminated under the “force majeure” clause, or postponed until later?","Someone had to deal with all of it.","And so Jiang Cheng was promoted. She really had become the “Supervisor Dong” she had called herself when speaking to Li Jiangbing.","She went to the office that morning, then returned home in the afternoon to pack.","Mo Li actually ate very little cat food, but Jiang Cheng still left him a large basinful.","Mo Li could open the window by himself and came and went freely every day. He didn’t need Jiang Cheng to carry him in and out through the main entrance.","Besides, Jiang Cheng believed that Mo Li must be capable of hunting outdoors as well.","“I’m going to be away for a long time. Stay home and don’t transform without reason,” Jiang Cheng said.","She did her best to simplify the message and transmit it to Mo Li through telepathy.","When they attacked Renxin Hospital, Jiang Cheng had known from the condition of the several zombies lying in the corridor outside the cannibal doctor’s room that Mo Li must have transformed at the time.","No one had seen it.","But after transforming for the second time, Mo Li had not been left in the completely exhausted state he had been in after the first transformation.","Perhaps the first time had been like that because he had already suffered serious injuries and had not yet recovered.","Now there was nothing to fear. Her little black cat was a miraculous creature capable of absorbing the sun’s essence and transforming into a gigantic beast.","Jiang Cheng turned the faucet until it dripped, so Mo Li could drink from it if he needed water. There was also a pond in the residential compound, and the water had recently been changed. Many of the neighborhood cats drank from it.","In any case, after making all the necessary arrangements, Jiang Cheng dragged her suitcase toward the door.","But Mo Li bit down on her pant leg.","“No. I can’t take you this time. I’m flying.”","Mo Li refused to let go.","Jiang Cheng had no choice but to crouch down and stroke his fluffy little head, doing her best to send him a message:","【Going out.】","【For a long time.】","【Safe.】","Mo Li finally released her and watched her leave.","With a sharp bang, the front door closed, leaving Mo Li alone in the apartment.","He sat in the entryway, his tail curled around his paws, looking up at the tall, imposing door.","All alone.","Jiang Cheng boarded the plane without a hitch. Just after she got off the plane and arrived at the hotel, her phone rang. It was Song Jingshuo.","“Our company has a very stylish new restaurant opening here. I managed to get a reservation. Do you want to have dinner together tonight?” he asked.","“Can’t. I’m on a business trip.” Jiang Cheng held the phone between her head and shoulder while busy taking her clothes and shoes out of her suitcase. “Let’s wait until I get back. The three of us can have dinner together then.”","Song Jingshuo: “...”","In fact, Song Jingshuo had wanted to have dinner with Jiang Cheng alone.","But she sounded busy, and it didn’t seem like a good time to talk.","He asked, “When will you be back?”","“Hard to say. I have to visit three cities. We’re short-staffed now, so my boss is using each of us as if we were three people.”","Song Jingshuo could only say, “Then we’ll wait until you get back.”","Jiang Cheng agreed. “Okay.”","Even while away from home, Jiang Cheng continued watching the news every day.","S City was highly efficient and introduced numerous policies, such as reducing or waiving rent for merchants and offering tax rebates and other incentives to businesses.","Merchants and companies whose property had been damaged during the disaster could also apply for government compensation.","Deputy Mayor Zheng became Vice Mayor Zheng.","Secretary Sun became Vice Mayor Sun.","Vice Mayor Sun made his first appearance on television. He might have appeared before, but back then Jiang Cheng had not known who he was.","She had spoken with him on the phone several times, so she finally knew what he looked like.","Mayor or vice mayor, they had once again become distant, untouchable figures far above her station.","Government agencies began resuming operations.","The police, firefighters, and doctors all returned to their posts.","The markets and supermarkets reopened. Freight drivers worked at full capacity, transporting all kinds of daily necessities from production sites to distribution centers, and from distribution centers into the cities.","It was a massive blood transfusion. The entire city was replenished with fresh blood.","New developments kept emerging, and new policies were continually issued to address them.","For example, the police stations would not accept missing-person cases from during the pandemic.","They had no way to handle them. If they did, merely recording all the information would exhaust the police.","The responsibility was delegated to the various neighborhoods, residents’ committees, and property management companies, which carried out a comprehensive census of everyone who normally lived in the area.","Cases involving the seizure of property—especially essential survival supplies—were likewise not accepted.","This included the people who had taken goods from Duoduo Supermarket without paying.","At first, they had taken only essential supplies. Later, mysterious disappearances of nonessential items such as bowls, plates, mops, rags, dish soap, and washbasins were also reported. But the supermarket no longer had the energy to investigate. They simply applied for state compensation for everything.","Murder cases, however, still had to be accepted.","The residents of Shanshui Yayuan reported the matter collectively.","And they had evidence.","At a time like this, owning a digital camera or handheld camcorder was considered extremely advanced and fashionable.","Some households in Deqingli had those as well.","But in most people’s minds, surveillance cameras existed only on the streets. Most people had no idea that cameras could also be installed inside their homes.","After all, most people lived in small houses and had no need for surveillance.","But the owners of the large villas in Shanshui Yayuan had generally installed security cameras throughout their homes.","The survivors of Shanshui Yayuan had preserved the evidence.","The entire process of the families being wiped out had been recorded. The proof was conclusive.","Many people from Deqingli were taken away, handcuffed and shoved into police cars.","Their family members wailed and sobbed. “Then how are we supposed to survive? That bunch of selfish bastards only cared about themselves!”","But it made no difference.","Murder was murder. Murderers had to pay with their lives.","A few households from nearby residential compounds also reported, one after another, that their husbands—the fathers of their children—had arranged to meet someone at Jixiang Jiayuan one night and never returned.","Technically, these were missing-person cases and would not be accepted.","But in one of the families, the wife’s father was a police officer. His son-in-law had disappeared, so the father-in-law went to investigate anyway.","Zhou Wang, who had been the manager and organizer of the residential compound at the time, was questioned at his home.","Zhou Wang said, “Yes, there was one day when thieves got into our compound. I was so rushed when I went downstairs that I even put on the wrong shoes. Pretty much everyone ran off. We caught a few of them, beat them up, and chased them away.”","The middle-aged man was extraordinarily calm.","He met the officer’s gaze directly and answered smoothly, without stumbling over a single word.","And so, with his wealth of experience in criminal investigations, the father-in-law knew that the man was lying.","He questioned several more residents, mostly those living on the lower floors. Since the son-in-law and his companions had actually come to steal, they would naturally have chosen the lower levels.","Everyone told the same story as Zhou Wang.","They were all lying.","They had clearly coordinated their statements.","The father-in-law wandered around the complex for a while. Then he looked up and spotted the cameras in the courtyard, and asked to check the surveillance footage.","Zhou Wang said apologetically, “It was all burned. There was a fire, and the equipment was destroyed.”","There was no evidence left, and no one to prove otherwise.","The father-in-law understood that the matter of his son-in-law had come to an end.","When he told his daughter, she burst into tears. “He must have been beaten to death, right? He’s dead, isn’t he—”","Maybe he had been beaten to death. Maybe he had been thrown to the zombies. Either way, there was no way to investigate any further.","The father-in-law smoked several cigarettes and urged her to live on for the sake of her child.","The past was the past.","The gym where Li Jiangbing worked had reopened.","His boss had spent the past few days applying for rent relief under the government’s policy, while pressuring them every day to bring in new customers.","Otherwise, the gym would go under, and they would all lose their jobs and end up starving.","Li Jiangbing was no longer the Li everyone in the complex had once feared.","He was once again the big, wisecracking personal trainer at the gym, handing out flyers around the complex and trying to recruit new members.","He had built up quite a few connections during the disaster. And back then, everyone had genuinely been eager to exercise to stay alive, so he had coached many of them.","Remembering the favor he had done them during the disaster, many people signed up for memberships with him.","Li Jiangbing thanked them profusely, smiling obsequiously.","After a long day, he went home and collapsed onto his bed. When he turned his head, he saw the protective armor sitting in the corner.","It was white as bone.","Some stains could no longer be washed out. They were the marks of his victories.","Many of the people who used to call him “Li” now addressed him as “Jiangbing.”","Lying on his bed, Li Jiangbing felt as though the era when everyone called him “Li” had taken place a hundred years ago.","The owner of the clubhouse finally returned.","And then all hell broke loose.","The swimming pool was horribly contaminated.","The trash had already been cleared away, but the pool itself was indeed filthy.","Everything had its priorities. At the time, Zhao Yi had still been occupied with providing labor for Li Feng at the Mai Duoduo supply station, so once the trash here had been removed, the pool was no longer considered urgent. He had left it unattended.","By the time the supply station was withdrawn, Zhao Yi had thought about dealing with the swimming pool, but by then he could no longer organize any volunteers.","The strength that had come together during the crisis had scattered like quicksilver once the crisis passed.","The clubhouse owner therefore stormed into the property management office, demanding compensation for the cleaning costs.","The property manager was no pushover and refused to acknowledge any responsibility.","He tore a sheet of paper off the wall and shoved it at the clubhouse owner. “Take it up with them.”","The sheet was a contact list for the members of the interim committee during the crisis.","Everyone’s apartment number and contact information were listed on it.","The first name was Jiang Cheng, Apartment 0306 in Building 2.","The manager even added, with a particularly nasty smirk, “The first person listed is the one mainly in charge.”","He had heard far too many stories about Jiang Cheng in recent days.","The property management staff were all terrified of her.","She had driven Liu Hongwang out.","In a sense, she had sentenced Liu Hongwang to death at the time.","The moment the manager heard about it, he knew that this “Miss Jiang” was not someone to be trifled with.","When there was trouble, the best thing to do was shove it toward someone who was even harder to deal with.","The clubhouse owner went straight to Jiang Cheng’s apartment, but she was away on a business trip. So he called Jiang Cheng instead.","After listening to him, Jiang Cheng told him, “You can apply for government compensation.”","The owner said, “That’s my problem. You people dirtied my swimming pool, so you have to pay for it.”","Jiang Cheng said, “Then go ahead and sue all the homeowners. If the court rules that we have to pay, we will.”","Jiang Cheng hung up, plugged the hotel’s network cable into her laptop, opened the group chat, and notified everyone:","【The clubhouse owner has come after us. I advised him to apply for state compensation. He wants us to pay, so I told him he could sue all the homeowners.】","Everyone replied:","【The state has policies in place.】","【Let him do whatever he wants. The court won’t accept the case.】","【I sympathize with him, but there’s nothing we can do.】","The owner really did file a lawsuit.","He applied for state compensation while suing all the homeowners at the same time. He was trying to have it both ways.","In the end, the court refused to accept the case.","“Cases involving this kind of situation during a disaster aren’t accepted. Just apply for state compensation.”","The court poured cold water directly on his plans.","The police refused to accept the case as well. The policy was that property damage caused by people trying to survive during the disaster would not be handled through lawsuits. The losses would be covered by state compensation instead.","The owner’s scheme had fallen through, and he left in a huff.","In the end, he paid to have the pool cleaned himself and waited for the state compensation to come through.","The exercise equipment that had been distributed among the lobbies of the various buildings was moved back into the clubhouse, and the small fitness room reopened.","But word got around that he had tried to sue all the homeowners. On top of that, his attitude had been truly awful, earning him everyone’s resentment.","Not only had garbage been dumped into that swimming pool—the remains of the cremated bodies had also been put in it.","Even after the pool was cleaned and reopened, no one went back.","Whenever people from other residential compounds came over to swim, someone couldn’t help mentioning it. Before long, the surrounding compounds knew about it too.","Business at the clubhouse became especially bleak. No one went to the café or the gym anymore.","Before long, a sign appeared on the main gate:","“Space for Lease—Contact 139xxxxxxxx.”","As for the gym where Li Jiangbing worked, this was actually good news. One competitor had disappeared.","At that point, Master Zhou finally got in touch with a welder who had experience with cutting metal.","The property manager agreed on a price with him, and the welder arrived at the Youth Apartments carrying his tools."]},{"number":82,"title":"Chapter 82","paragraphs":["Whether in the corners of the city or among the green silk-cotton fields of the countryside, scattered zombies still lurked in places, undiscovered for one reason or another.","The military had already withdrawn, and S City had established its own Urban Crisis Rapid Response Teams, stationed throughout the various districts.","Whenever a missed zombie was discovered, the team had to respond immediately. They were responsible not only for eliminating the zombie, but also for screening people in the vicinity in case any infected individuals were hiding their condition.","The electrician had never been to the Tech New District before and had not expected it to be so far from downtown. As a result, he had failed to allow enough time for the journey, and by the time he arrived, dusk had already fallen.","The property manager complained that the electrician was keeping him from getting off work, while the electrician complained that the place was too far away and demanded extra pay.","The two of them haggled bitterly for a while. By the time they finally reached a compromise, it was completely dark.","“Are you sure there aren’t any zombies inside?” the electrician asked.","The property manager slapped the door several times. “Hey! Hey! Zombie! If there’s a zombie in there, make a sound!”","But no sound came from the meeting room.","The property manager spread his hands.","“Fine,” said the electrician.","But Master Luo still didn’t feel at ease. He called over two security guards, and the three of them put on protective armor. They slipped on their arm guards for appearance’s sake, but didn’t bother with leg guards. They still had all their weapons, and brought them along.","The property manager kept saying, “There’s no need. There’s no sound coming from inside.”","Yet he retreated to the back.","The electrician looked at the several men around him. Even if there really was a zombie, they should be able to take it down.","After experiencing that month-and-a-half-long zombie crisis, people were no longer as terrified of zombies as they had been. They had grown somewhat accustomed to them.","Some even felt that encountering a zombie was no different from running into an oversized stray dog.","The electrician boldly began cutting through the door.","As the welding seam gradually split beneath the shrill buzz of the cutting wheel, the meeting room remained completely still.","Even with that enormous noise, there was no reaction from inside. Everyone grew even more confident.","The two security guards relaxed their stances.","Only Master Luo couldn’t relax.","Could the last human really have been left inside, starving to death?","The thought made the whole situation feel unbearably cruel.","The seam in the middle had been cut all the way through.","The electrician tugged on the power cord and stepped back, jerking his chin toward the door. “Try it. See if you can open it now.”","One of the guards stepped forward, seized the two handles of the double doors, and shook them. “Feels like it’s stuck.”","“Use some strength!” the electrician said.","Muttering under his breath, the guard shook the handles harder. The metal doors clattered loudly.","“Hey, I think...”","The guard felt that the doors were about to give way.","But before he could finish, an enormous force slammed into them!","The doors suddenly burst open, and a foul stench hit them in the face!","The electrician instinctively raised the angle grinder in his hands and pressed the switch.","Something crashed into him. The angle grinder flew from his grip, and he was hurled against the wall along with it, sending sparks crackling everywhere!","Jiang Cheng had yet to return from his business trip, leaving Mo Li home alone.","His daily routine was very regular. At dawn, he would go out through the window and bask in the sun in the courtyard. When night fell, he would return home, where Jiang Cheng’s scent lingered everywhere.","Today was no different.","Night had fallen. Mo Li had finished patrolling his territory and was just about to go home when he suddenly turned his head toward the direction of Building One.","His green eyes were wide and round in the darkness.","Humans would have found him adorable.","But anyone familiar with cats knew that this wide-eyed, round-pupiled “adorable” state was actually a hunting stance!","Mo Li let out a sharp, clipped meow. In an instant, his body transformed into a black streak and vanished.","The electrician sat on the floor with his back pressed tightly against the wall, gasping for breath as he stared at the object between his feet.","Half of a human hand.","The skin was blue, and the fingernails were black.","The blood seeping from the severed end was dark brown and viscous, like porridge.","That stench was all too familiar.","It was definitely a zombie.","The electrician looked up.","One security guard had been knocked unconscious by the door and lay sprawled to the side.","The other guard and Master Luo were both on the floor. Like the electrician, they sat up in shock, staring blankly.","The property manager crouched behind them, trembling all over.","The electrician took a deep breath, leaped to his feet, and shouted, “You said there were no zombies!”","As he cursed, he picked up the unconscious guard’s weapon and looked around warily. “Where’s that zombie?”","Compared with the white-collar workers who sat in offices across the city, the laborers and tradesmen had displayed relatively greater physical strength and combat ability during the month-long zombie crisis.","Master Luo and the other security guard climbed to their feet as well. They checked the guard who had been knocked unconscious by the door, confirmed that he was all right, and picked up their weapons.","When they had entered earlier, the main door of the property management center had been left open.","They rushed outside. A staircase lay beyond the door.","One flight up led to Building One’s lobby. Downstairs was the parking garage.","They chased after the zombie, but there were no security guards on the first floor.","The guard on duty that day had been the one who had just been knocked unconscious. Just then, a resident happened to enter. Master Luo anxiously asked, “Did you see a zombie?”","The resident was shocked. “There’s a zombie?”","Master Luo and the others exchanged glances.","“Could it have gone down to the basement garage?” someone suggested.","“We have to warn everyone!” Master Luo said urgently.","The property manager hurriedly pulled out his phone. “I’m calling the police!”","He dialed the emergency number and explained what had happened.","The operator asked, “How many are there?”","The manager replied, “There should only be one. It was incredibly fast. We couldn’t even get a good look at it before it ran off.”","The voice on the other end changed. It rose sharply as the operator pressed, “You’re saying it ran away?”","The manager froze, then suddenly realized that something was wrong.","How could a zombie run away? No one had ever heard of such a thing. Didn’t zombies always pounce at the smell of blood and flesh?","They would even smash through glass doors to get at people.","Sweat broke out across the manager’s forehead. “Yes, it ran away. And... and...”","And before that, he had knocked on the door and called out more than once, yet the zombie inside had remained completely silent.","It had practically pretended not to exist in order to mislead them.","Master Luo turned and hurried downstairs, heading straight for the equipment room.","The manager had just ended the call when Master Luo’s voice rang out overhead, his Mandarin carrying a strong accent from his hometown:","“Attention, everyone! Attention, everyone! There’s a zombie in the residential compound! There’s a zombie in the residential compound! Be careful!”","“This zombie is extremely fast! It’s different from ordinary zombies! It can even run away!”","“Everyone, be careful!”","The residents who had already gone home opened their doors one after another, trying to hear the announcement more clearly.","After listening, they looked at one another in bewilderment.","Someone shouted, “Holy crap!” and spun around, rushing back into their apartment.","When they came out again, they were already wearing full protective armor and carrying weapons.","There was no fear or panic on their faces. Instead, they looked excited.","The property manager stared blankly up at the broadcast speaker in the lobby ceiling. “What’s that?”","“A loudspeaker,” a security guard answered.","“I know it’s a loudspeaker. Wait—isn’t this the fire alarm system?” The manager was incredulous. “You can use it like this too?”","No one had ever told him.","The Urban Crisis Rapid Response Team arrived very quickly.","They opened the main gate and drove directly into the residential compound’s courtyard.","The entire courtyard was filled with residents wearing white protective armor and carrying weapons. They moved in groups of three or five, poking at the bushes with sticks and shining flashlights into the shadows behind the buildings.","“Anything there?”","“No.”","“Nothing here either.”","The members of the Rapid Response Team stared in silence.","Unable to hold back, one of them asked, “Why do so many people in your residential compound have protective armor?”","One of the homeowners overheard them and turned to look him over. “You’re not from around here, are you?”","“Huh? I was just transferred to the Technology New District. How did you know?”","The homeowner laughed. “Who in the Technology New District doesn’t know about our Youth Apartments? We’re the main fighting force around here.”","The rapid response team members were all wearing protective armor as well.","They went down to the property management center and inspected the meeting room first.","The meeting room reeked of zombies. But it wasn’t as bad as they had imagined.","It didn’t smell as bad as a room containing more than a dozen corpses should have.","That was because the bodies had disappeared. All that remained on the floor were clothes, scattered white bones, and hair.","The clothes were horrifying enough. The hair was even more terrifying.","Everyone who went in and saw the scene felt their hair stand on end.","The rapid response team members repeatedly confirmed, “You’re saying there were more than a dozen people inside before?”","Master Luo thought for a moment. “The first group alone had more than a dozen. Then another group went in later. After that, they sealed the doors.”","Master Luo showed them the surveillance footage from that time. It clearly showed that there had indeed been that many people.","The tapes were reused in a forty-five-day loop. The footage from the first day should have already been overwritten.","They had deliberately preserved it, just in case it was ever needed. As it turned out, it had come in handy.","After watching that person destroy the meeting room’s surveillance camera, the members of the rapid response team fell silent.","They thought of the bones that had been gnawed completely clean inside the meeting room.","It might not have been that person.","But the thought alone was enough to make their hair stand on end.","The homeowners searched the courtyard. They looked extremely experienced.","The rapid response team went down to the basement to search the underground parking garage.","The property manager had gone down to the basement once after returning, but he had never explored such a large area.","This time, he finally saw the section separated by the blast-resistant civil-defense door.","“What’s this?” he asked. “Why is the door still closed?”","He had been away from work for more than a month, and there were changes everywhere that he knew nothing about.","Master Luo said, “These are the supplies the government distributed back then. The residential compound seized them and stored them here. We planned to hand them out if everyone ever went hungry.”","But that day had never come. Under the leadership and organization of the interim committee, the people in the Youth Apartments had continued to live very well.","“Supplies?” The manager’s eyes lit up. “What kind?”","Master Luo said, “Compressed biscuits, canned food, things like that...”","The manager couldn’t even stand hearing those two items mentioned. The moment he heard them, he felt a little sick.","“Don’t say it. Don’t say it.” He waved his hand, instantly losing interest.","Who would buy canned food nowadays? Everyone felt like throwing up at the sight of it.","And compressed biscuits were even worse.","After an extensive search, they still failed to find the zombie.","Someone from the rapid response team took several photographs of the scene inside the meeting room, snapping away with a camera. Others used black body bags to collect the bones, hair, and clothing.","There were no surveillance cameras in the corridor. The camera was positioned at the customer service desk, facing outward.","The surveillance footage showed only a dark shadow darting past the front desk.","Even slowed down, the image was terribly blurry. The compound’s surveillance system was neither high-definition nor particularly advanced. It could barely make out the shape of an individual.","After checking, the team found no injuries on anyone present. The rapid response team took both videotapes with them.","“Call us immediately if anything happens,” they instructed.","At the same time, they had to notify the nearby subdistrict office, neighborhood committees, and property management offices, making sure everyone knew there was a zombie in the area and warning them to be careful.","Li Jiangbing’s work schedule was different from that of people who worked regular shifts.","He often had no work in the morning and wouldn’t go in until noon. His quitting time depended on whether any students had booked lessons.","He had a class that day and didn’t return to the compound until nearly ten. By then, the rapid response team had already withdrawn.","But as soon as he entered the compound, he saw scattered groups of people in protective armor still searching the grounds.","Li Jiangbing: “...”","He ran over. “What’s going on?”","Everyone knew him well, so they told him, “The zombie from the meeting room got out.”","Li Jiangbing fell silent for a moment, then cursed. “Fuck! I completely forgot about the meeting room!”","He asked, “No one took care of it afterward?”","“We all forgot too. Jiang Cheng probably forgot as well.”","“Of course she did,” Li Jiangbing said. “She’s the busiest person of all.”","Back then, Jiang Cheng had had to worry about everything.","How nostalgic.","Li Jiangbing turned and started toward the building, intending to go upstairs and put on his armor, but someone stopped him.","“Forget it. We’ve already searched for three or four hours. A lot of people have gone home, and we’re heading back too. We probably won’t find it.”","Li Jiangbing finally realized what they meant. “How can you lose a zombie?”","That was precisely why everyone had persisted in searching for so long.","Someone said, “Maybe... it evolved?”","Li Jiangbing’s mouth fell open in astonishment.","In the end, everyone returned home empty-handed.","The various group chats, which had gradually quieted down in recent days, grew lively again. Everyone was discussing the zombie that had appeared that day.","Li Jiangbing didn’t go to sleep until very late. He kept wondering where a zombie could possibly have run off to.","The thought kept him awake.","By August, cool breezes had begun to blow.","The moon was dark, and the night was windy.","The courtyard lay quiet and still.","As the clouds drifted by, the moon emerged, illuminating the high rooftop.","A zombie’s body had been torn apart.","Beside the mangled corpse, the shadow of a beast sat crouched.","If Jiang Cheng had been there, she would have discovered that the beast was far larger than the transformed form she had seen before.","Moonlight was, in truth, only sunlight reflected by the moon.","The beast absorbed it for a while, replenishing the energy consumed during its transformation.","Absorbing energy in its gigantic form would actually have been more effective.","But the beast knew it could not do that during the day.","Unfortunately, moonlight could not compare with sunlight. The absorption efficiency was far too low. It would be better to go home and sleep, then wait until tomorrow to bask in the sun.","The beast suddenly shrank, transforming into a small cat. Light and nimble, it leaped down from the rooftop.","Home."]},{"number":83,"title":"Chapter 83","paragraphs":["The work Jiang Cheng had taken over was a real headache.","There was no point thinking about recovering her colleague’s remains—they simply couldn’t be found.","First, she had to locate her colleague’s personal effects. She needed to report the matter to the police, taking a company letter stamped with the official seal. After reviewing it, the police would issue a letter of confirmation.","She then had to take that letter to the hotel before they would hand over the belongings.","After that, she had to take the police letter to a computer repair shop, have the password cracked, open her colleague’s computer, search through the files, and locate the warehouse where the equipment had been stored.","Then she had to take both letters of confirmation to the warehouse and find her company’s equipment.","She also needed to confirm with the client whether the project was going to resume.","Only after all of that was settled could she decide whether the equipment needed to be shipped back to S City.","Every step was troublesome, because every step involved finding people who might no longer be there. Some were dead, others missing.","One warehouse had been completely abandoned. Everyone there, from the owner to the employees, was dead.","She had no choice but to seek police assistance again. In the end, with the police’s help, she opened the warehouse and recovered the equipment.","Professional lighting, projectors, audio equipment—items worth hundreds of thousands or even millions. Fortunately, because it was a major case involving a substantial sum of money, the relevant departments had moved it up the priority list and handled it as a key case.","Jiang Cheng had spent the entire day running around outside. When she returned to the hotel that evening, she opened her computer and plugged in the Ethernet cable. Only then did she see the discussion in the group chat.","That was when she remembered there might still be zombies in the conference room.","At the time, she had considered only two possible outcomes: one person left alive, or one zombie left standing.","The odds of it being one zombie were as high as 99.9 percent.","Or perhaps there were several.","For people who had already killed hundreds, even thousands, of zombies, that possibility was hardly frightening anymore.","So she had simply forgotten about it.","She hadn’t expected the zombie to evolve further.","Several people in the group had spoken with the security guards who had been on the scene, as well as Master Luo. After learning the details, they had brought them to the neighbors for discussion.","[It definitely evolved. Otherwise, how could it have run away?]","[They said it attacked the welder first. The angle grinder shaved off half his palm.]","[Then it attacked the security guard, Little Fang, and Master Luo. It was moving too fast. Both of them instinctively raised their arms to block it. Luckily, they were wearing arm guards, so those stopped the attack. But the impact still knocked them over.]","[Then the zombie ran away.]","[Isn’t it obvious? After attacking them, it realized there were too many people and that it couldn’t win, so it fled. It must have developed intelligence to do that. Otherwise, look at the second-generation zombies. Even after losing an arm or a leg, they’ll still hop straight toward you.]","[This one doesn’t just run away—it hides, too. So many of us have been searching for so long, and we still haven’t found it.]","Jiang Cheng asked: [Was anyone injured?]","[Jiang Cheng is here.]","[No. It’s just that not finding it has everyone feeling a little uneasy.]","Jiang Cheng: [Be careful recently, and remind each other to stay alert. Don’t wander around outside at night.]","The screen filled with messages saying, [Got it.]","Everyone instinctively responded to Jiang Cheng’s instructions.","Then someone realized what they were doing and burst out laughing.","[It feels like we’re back in those days.]","Someone sighed.","[I kind of miss them...]","But some things, no matter how much you missed them, you would never want to experience again.","For example, you might miss a deceased friend or relative, but you would never accept seeing them rise from the dead in front of your eyes.","As time passed, many people who had grown close during the disaster gradually drifted apart again. They went from calling one another brothers and trusting each other with their lives to merely nodding in passing when they happened to meet in the neighborhood.","Several couples who had gotten together during the disaster had broken up. Once the bridge effect wore off, they no longer felt anything for each other.","Even Song Jingshuo had returned to his original place in the social ecosystem after work resumed.","He was no longer the perennial runner-up who was constantly overshadowed by Jiang Cheng. Instead, he was a young elite with an impressive income.","He had a large house, an expensive car, and a stream of polished, glamorous professional women around him. They all regarded him as a promising golden bachelor.","Of course, he still admired Jiang Cheng, but that affection gradually faded.","After work resumed, they went an entire month without seeing each other. With no opportunity to pursue her, and with people constantly coming and going around him, he slowly lost the motivation to keep trying.","Jiang Cheng didn’t care about any of this.","She had never intended to develop a relationship with anyone in the first place.","She hadn’t wanted one when everyone else was swept up in the bridge effect, so she certainly wasn’t going to want one now.","The matter of the Youth Apartment was discussed for several days. The rapid-response team also patrolled the surrounding area for several days.","Every neighborhood office, residents’ committee, and property-management company posted notices at the entrances of all the residential buildings. Many people saw them. When children wanted to go downstairs to play after school, their parents refused.","“There’s a zombie nearby that still hasn’t been caught.”","By then, the two videotapes had already left S City and arrived at the central group of zombie-research experts.","The experts reported to the leaders that there was yet another new case.","The leader asked, “How many are there in total?”","“Seventeen.”","Across the country, seventeen cases had been reported of new zombies that were clearly different from both the original zombies and the second-generation zombies.","Compared with the country’s vast territory and enormous population, seventeen was naturally an insignificant number.","But it proved that second-generation zombies were not the upper limit of zombie mutation.","Zombies could continue to develop and change, and no one could predict what they might eventually become.","Although the zombie disaster had essentially been brought under control nationwide, the leader still felt a heavy weight in his heart.","The zombie virus had altered the human body at a genetic level, causing the dead to walk ferociously beneath the broad daylight. And even now, humanity could not decipher the virus, let alone find a way to destroy it.","“Report it upward,” he said.","The higher authorities had to be made aware of this information so that they could prepare contingency plans.","Jiang Cheng was surprised when she received a call from the police station in S City’s Science and Technology New District.","They were asking about Liu Hongwang.","“Yes. I represented all the homeowners in terminating his employment relationship with the community.”","“There were many homeowners present at the time, and nearly all the members of the interim committee were there. No one objected. So although I was the one who proposed it, it reflected the will of everyone.”","“Under those circumstances, if we couldn’t keep things under control, the entire community would have descended into chaos. You understand.”","“We didn’t kill him or physically harm him. Everything we did was in accordance with the law.”","“The homeowners’ committee hired the property-management company, which in turn hired the property staff. We had the legal right to terminate any staff member’s employment, especially during an extraordinary period.”","“Yes, thank you for your understanding.”","The officer on the other end said, “We’re just trying to understand the situation. It isn’t a homicide case, after all...”","It was a rather unusual situation.","The person who had reported it insisted that this was murder, and that they should receive the same treatment as the people from Deqingli—that they should be handcuffed, taken away, and sentenced.","The police officer had been badgered until he could no longer stand it, so he called Jiang Cheng to make inquiries.","The fact that he had called her instead of summoning her already made the police’s attitude clear.","Jiang Cheng expressed her thanks, then asked, “Was it one of the homeowners in our community who reported it?”","“No. Uh... I’m afraid I can’t disclose that,” the officer said. “The regulations prohibit us from revealing the identity of the person who filed the report.”","But his reflexive answer had already given Jiang Cheng the information she needed.","If it wasn’t one of the homeowners, then it had to be someone from the property-management company.","When that person called again, the police told him plainly, “This is a civil dispute.”","The so-called “expulsion” and “telling him to go die” were merely the informant’s subjective interpretation. In reality, what they had done was simply terminate the employment relationship. It was perfectly legal and reasonable.","“They know the law better than you do,” the police officer advised. “Otherwise, go find a lawyer and sue them. Civil disputes aren’t our responsibility.”","The man refused to give up and went to a law firm, only to be scared off by the consultation fee alone.","The police handled cases for free. Lawyers, however, didn’t work for nothing.","This man wasn’t trying to stand up for Liu Hongwang. In fact, Liu Hongwang had no friends at all. He was lazy and slippery at work, and thoroughly disliked by everyone.","The man simply couldn’t stand Jiang Cheng, Song Jingshuo, and the others.","If he could mess with them for free, he was willing to spend the time doing it.","But if he had to pay out of his own pocket, forget it.","Jiang Cheng mentioned the matter in the temporary committee’s group chat.","Just as Jiang Cheng had said, no one had objected at the time, which was equivalent to everyone’s consent.","The group chat erupted in anger, with everyone demanding to know who had reported them. The temporary committee had poured its heart and soul into leading everyone through the most difficult period, only to be stabbed in the back afterward.","It was infuriating.","Yang Xinyan was also in the group chat, but she didn’t dare say a word.","Instead, she secretly told Aunt Pan about it, and Aunt Pan passed it on to Master Luo.","“Who do you think it was?” Aunt Pan asked.","Master Luo said nothing, but he had a pretty good idea who it might have been.","Jiang Cheng spent a month traveling around, visiting three different cities.","She could clearly feel how drastically the population had declined.","Traffic in the cities was no longer congested. Some cars by the roadside and in parking lots had gathered layers of dust, with no one coming to claim them.","At the airport, she overheard people talking about how property prices had plummeted, and rents had fallen just as sharply.","The stock market, meanwhile, had suffered a panic-driven plunge before quickly rebounding and entering a structural bull market.","Ordinary people were having a hard time. Too many had lost their jobs.","A large number of small and medium-sized private companies went bankrupt.","Individual business owners were hit especially hard. Even with the rent and tax reductions offered by the government, many still couldn’t hold on.","Countless small shops along the streets had closed down.","“Prime location, shop for sublease” signs were everywhere.","At the same time, many companies had lost a considerable portion of their employees and were now hiring.","Job fairs were being held all over the country.","The mobility of the workforce was at its highest point in the past decade.","By the end of August, Jiang Cheng had finally packed up all the company’s equipment and shipped it back to S City.","She also bought a plane ticket home.","However, from the moment she arrived at the airport that morning, she had felt uncomfortable in the head. Perhaps she had been too exhausted these past few days. Or perhaps she shouldn’t have turned on the air conditioner at the hotel the night before.","It was already the end of August. The temperature should have been dropping, yet these past two days had brought an abnormal heat wave.","Jiang Cheng boarded the plane in a daze and slept through most of the flight.","By the time she got off the plane, it was afternoon. The departure city had been overcast, and so was the destination.","To her surprise, Mr. Peng himself had come to pick her up at the airport.","Jiang Cheng was stunned. “Has our company really fallen this far?”","It felt like they were on the verge of bankruptcy and couldn’t even afford a driver anymore.","Mr. Peng’s expression became awkward. “I’m a diligent and people-oriented boss. I just wanted to check on one of my employees. Don’t overthink it. We’re not going bankrupt. I’ve got plenty of money.”","Jiang Cheng relaxed. “All right, then.”","Although this world gave her the impression that everything was “far too simple,” she still had to eat, drink, and take care of her basic needs. Being unemployed was not a good thing.","All the way, Mr. Peng kept chatting with her, asking after her health and showing concern. It was rather unusual.","Mr. Peng was in his thirties and divorced. He had originally been a moderately wealthy heir, and he and his wife had made quite a bit of money running a company together. After their divorce, the couple divided the company’s operations, each taking half.","His ex-wife handled the advertising business, while he took charge of exhibitions and events. Both continued to make money.","They had amassed a fortune during the economic boom.","Unfortunately, his luck had been poor. He had run into this zombie catastrophe, and his girlfriend had died.","His girlfriend had died.","Jiang Cheng: “...”","She skipped over all the useless information and seized on the key points.","Mr. Peng was single now. Mr. Peng was thirty-one and in his prime. Mr. Peng couldn’t stand being lonely. Mr. Peng wanted to make a move on one of the young, pretty girls at the company.","Jiang Cheng was the lucky young woman he had chosen.","Jiang Cheng: “...”","Jiang Cheng felt her headache worsen.","She was in a daze, as though she had forgotten something important.","Mr. Peng’s car was quite nice too, with dark-tinted film covering the windows.","Jiang Cheng’s head felt terribly heavy. Her vacant eyes remained fixed on the road ahead while Mr. Peng talked beside her, cultivating the image of a devoted, sensitive man and pouring out his grief over the loss of his girlfriend.","He hoped to arouse the young woman’s sympathy and, from there, develop a romantic relationship.","At that moment, the sky, which had remained overcast, began to take on a faint purple hue.","Just like that Saturday two months ago.","Jiang Cheng’s head was heavy and muddled.","Just like that Saturday two months ago."]},{"number":84,"title":"Chapter 84","paragraphs":["Jiang Cheng was so drowsy from Mr. Peng’s endless nagging that she nearly fell asleep.","“Caught a cold?” Mr. Peng asked with concern. “Go home and get some proper rest. Don’t come in tomorrow. Take a day off and see how you feel.”","Jixiang West Street was one-way, so Jiang Cheng got out at the intersection. “Thank you, Mr. Peng.”","“Get some good rest,” Mr. Peng called after her.","Dragging her suitcase, Jiang Cheng walked groggily toward the east gate of the residential complex. She had the persistent feeling that she had forgotten something.","There was a strange sensation in her heart, but she couldn’t figure out what it was.","An older woman greeted her warmly. “Little Jiang, long time no see!”","The woman was pulling a handcart and looked as though she had just returned from shopping at Maid uoduo or somewhere similar.","Jiang Cheng had no idea who she was. She was probably a resident of Jixiang Jiayuan.","Too many people in the New Technology District recognized her, and she couldn’t possibly know all of them in return. She merely nodded and greeted her. “Hello.”","The older woman walked alongside her for a couple of steps, muttering to herself, “The sky’s so overcast today. Why’s it this color?”","She pronounced the last word in her local dialect.","Jiang Cheng instinctively looked up.","Although the woman was elderly, she had danced in the neighborhood square for years and was remarkably spry. Within a few steps, she had overtaken Jiang Cheng.","After walking a little farther, she sensed something was wrong and glanced back.","The young woman called Jiang Cheng had stopped, her hand still on her suitcase. She was craning her neck toward the sky, completely motionless, as if she had turned to stone.","The older woman turned back around and continued on her way. She had to get home and prepare dinner.","Jiang Cheng stared at the sky.","That familiar, eerie purple.","At last, Jiang Cheng understood what she had felt she’d forgotten.","After the zombie crisis broke out, she had gone over everything that happened that Saturday.","Only then did she remember that the dizziness she’d experienced that day had not been the dizziness of a cold. It had been something else entirely.","It was as if something inside her mind that should have been able to expand and unfold had been gripped tightly by a pair of invisible hands. Air and blood could not pass through, leaving her in a constant haze.","And that thing being held tight was the memory of another world, which occasionally leaked out in the tiniest fragments!","If the sky’s unnatural purple had been the only sign, or if she had merely felt hazy and light-headed, perhaps it wouldn’t have meant anything.","But what were the odds of both things happening at the same time?","Besides, she had privately asked several people about it afterward and confirmed that everyone had suddenly passed out that day. She alone had experienced something resembling a fever.","After waking, no one else had shown any abnormalities. Only her strength had become far greater than it was in “Jiang Cheng’s” memories—even surpassing that of many men.","There was one more crucial factor to consider: she was a transmigrator from another world.","That factor was the key that tied everything together.","Jiang Cheng took several seconds to sort out her thoughts.","Because of her special nature as a transmigrator, she had entered an unusual state when the zombie virus first broke out.","And now, based on that state, she could conclude—","The zombie virus was about to return.","Jiang Cheng pondered for a second, then pulled out her phone. She composed a text message and sent it to everyone in her contacts.","Everyone.","That included colleagues, clients, and people from service industries whom she had met temporarily or dealt with regularly—such as the police officers, hotel staff, warehouse workers, and rental-car driver whose numbers she had added during this business trip to three different cities.","Every member of the Youth Apartments’ Interim Committee, as well as several residents who were not on the committee.","Master Luo, Yang Xinyan, and the other property-management staff.","Zhou Wang and several others from Jixiang Jiayuan.","A few contacts from Yu Jing Xiang Yuan, Deqingli, and several other residential complexes.","Vice Mayor Sun, Li Feng, Brother Dong and Guo Jun from Maid uoduo, and others.","Warning: The zombie virus will break out again today.","Return to a space where you can isolate yourself as soon as possible, and make preparations.","This is Jiang Cheng. The above is not a joke.","This message was sent to everyone in my contacts. Do not reply or call back.","More than two hundred phones chimed at almost the exact same moment.","More than two hundred people pulled out their phones and flipped them open to read the message, all of them freezing in confusion.","Mr. Peng had just reached a traffic light when he glanced at the message.","“Huh? What’s this supposed to mean?”","And she had even said it wasn’t a joke. If it wasn’t a joke, then what was it?","A young migrant worker who had come to S City to make a living was claiming she could predict a zombie outbreak.","“Has her cold given her hallucinations?” Mr. Peng wondered, genuinely concerned.","But the light had turned green, and the car behind him honked impatiently.","Mr. Peng hurriedly tossed his phone into the center console and focused on driving. He planned to call Jiang Cheng once he found somewhere to stop and check on her.","Since he intended to pursue a relationship with Jiang Cheng, he naturally had to be a little more proactive.","The clients, police officers, and warehouse managers who were in other cities read the message and frowned.","Which Jiang Cheng?","Oh—the one from the exhibition company. Now they remembered her.","What was this girl trying to do?","Although the message said it was “not a joke,” that was hardly enough to make anyone believe it.","She was just an employee at a private company. Did that mean a zombie outbreak would really happen simply because she said so?","Those who had only met Jiang Cheng once or twice did not believe the message. After reading it, they put their phones away again.","They didn’t take it seriously. Some were even annoyed that someone would joke about zombies. Nearly everyone had relatives or friends who had died during the zombie crisis.","It was a disgusting thing to joke about.","Several people at Yu Jing Xiang Yuan also saw the message.","They had first come into contact with Jiang Cheng and begun working with her after answering the nation’s call and leaving their homes.","They admitted that the girl possessed exceptional organizational and leadership abilities.","But the zombies were coming back...?","What nonsense.","Zhou Wang of Jixiang Jiayuan saw the message as well.","His first reaction was the same as the people at Yu Jing Xiang Yuan. He closed his phone, placed it back on his desk, and continued working.","Yet for some reason, he couldn’t settle down.","His mind kept replaying scene after scene of his dealings with Jiang Cheng.","When that girl turned cold, her eyes were filled with an intimidating pressure.","Zhou Wang couldn’t help glancing at his phone again.","The members of the Youth Apartments’ Interim Committee and several residents who had dealt with Jiang Cheng also received the message.","Most people were still at work at this hour.","Song Jingshuo was in the middle of a meeting. He wore a sharply tailored suit, a spotless white shirt, and a tie knotted small and tight. The air conditioning in the office building was turned up high, so a full suit was necessary to keep warm.","His gaze remained fixed on the screen of his phone.","The next moment, he snapped it shut.","Absurd.","That was the first reaction any normal person would have.","But this was Jiang Cheng.","This is Jiang Cheng. The above is not a joke.","Yes. Jiang Cheng would never make a joke like this.","Song Jingshuo lowered his eyes, then raised them again and swept his gaze across the conference room, where a group of impeccably dressed, polished-looking people sat around the table.","He stood up. “I’m sorry, but something urgent has come up.”","In the elevator, he ran into another colleague. Seeing Song Jingshuo press the button for the underground second floor, the colleague asked casually, “Heading out?”","He gave a perfunctory reply. “Yes.”","The colleague got off first and turned around outside the elevator, waving at him. “Bye-bye.”","Song Jingshuo gave an elegant little wave in return.","The elevator doors closed, freezing him in that pose as the car descended toward the underground parking garage.","Song Jingshuo strode toward his car.","Once inside, he took a pair of wired earphones from the center console and plugged them into his phone.","This year, smartphone manufacturers introduced wireless earbuds for the first time—no wires required. They were the most advanced and fashionable thing on the market, and all the stylish businesspeople bought a pair.","Song Jingshuo followed the trend and bought some too.","They were utterly impractical. The earbuds were bulky, hanging from his ears like hearing aids, and their battery life was terrible. They ran out of power after barely any use.","So Song Jingshuo still used wired earphones when he drove.","He called Jiang Cheng and started the car at the same time.","Although Jiang Cheng had told him not to call back, Song Jingshuo did not believe that applied to him.","Sure enough, Jiang Cheng answered immediately.","“Are you on your way back?” Jiang Cheng asked.","Song Jingshuo was equally concise. “I’m already driving.”","“Then that’s fine. I’m hanging up.”","No unnecessary words.","Song Jingshuo drove in circles around the exit ramp.","This is ridiculous, he thought.","It’s absurd. How could I believe something so absurd?","How could Jiang Cheng possibly have foreseen the outbreak of the zombie virus?","In fact, even now, aside from the initial announcement about a “virus,” the authorities had offered no explanation whatsoever about what the zombies were, how they had come about, or what principles governed them.","Song Jingshuo had always suspected that perhaps the authorities themselves had no explanation.","Zombies were a fantastical thing. Their very existence violated logic and scientific understanding.","If even the government couldn’t explain them, how could Jiang Cheng, an ordinary person, have the ability to predict their arrival?","How could I believe something so absurd?","At that moment, the car emerged from the underground garage, and the view suddenly opened up before him.","I don’t believe this absurd story, Song Jingshuo realized.","I believe Jiang Cheng.","The person who believed in Jiang Cheng even more than Song Jingshuo did was Li Jiangbing.","He had been negotiating with a client—a wealthy woman who looked very likely to sign up for a membership.","Li Jiangbing had been pulling out all the stops to persuade her to purchase a membership.","Then the text message arrived.","After reading it, Li Jiangbing froze for a moment before jumping to his feet.","The wealthy woman was startled.","Li Jiangbing abandoned the sales pitch and immediately told her, “Go home! The zombie virus is coming back!”","Then he turned around and rushed out of the consultation room.","“Everyone, go home! The zombie virus is coming back! Go home!” he shouted as he walked.","His voice was so loud that it even drowned out the gym’s background music.","It was a weekday afternoon, and there weren’t many people around. Only a sparse handful of customers were present, fewer than the employees.","The owner came over after hearing the commotion. “What are you talking about?”","“Have you gone crazy? What nonsense are you spouting?”","“I’m talking to you, Li Jiangbing!”","Li Jiangbing ignored him and waved his arms at everyone. “Go on, get out of here. The zombie virus is coming back!”","The owner was furious. He cursed at Li Jiangbing and told him to stop causing a scene.","“The zombies have all been killed! They’re dead and gone!”","The wealthy woman from the consultation room hurried after Li Jiangbing and called out, “Li!”","She stared at him intently. “Do you have some inside information?”","Thank goodness—someone was willing to listen.","Li Jiangbing said, “Yes. Someone I know warned me. He said the zombie virus is coming back and that we need to find somewhere to hide and isolate ourselves as soon as possible!”","The wealthy woman asked, “Is this person you know the son of some high-ranking official?”","Li Jiangbing was only a fitness instructor.","In the wealthy woman’s eyes, that meant he was either at the bottom of society or, at best, part of its lower ranks. He himself clearly had no special abilities. If he had access to inside information, then the person he knew must have connections and channels.","Even ordinary wealthy people wouldn’t have access to information like this. It could only have come through the government. That meant the person had to be the son of some high-ranking official whom Li Jiangbing had met through his work at the gym.","Why the son, specifically?","Because a son would be young. Because they knew each other. And because he might be thinking of giving Li Jiangbing a hand.","A genuine high-ranking official was a thousand-year-old fox. If he knew something, he would keep it to himself and never let a word slip.","Li Jiangbing had always possessed a keen sense of social survival.","Though he was somewhat agitated at the moment, he realized that if he admitted the person who had warned him was merely an ordinary white-collar worker, everyone around him might burst out laughing.","So Li Jiangbing stiffened his neck and confirmed, “Yes. His family has connections.”","“Believe me!” he said. “Everyone, go home right away. That’s all I’m going to say. I’ve done everything I can. I’m leaving!”","With that, he turned and headed for the changing room to retrieve his belongings.","The owner flew into a rage. “Where do you think you’re going? Your shift isn’t over yet!”","Without a word, the wealthy woman turned around and clicked away on her heels.","Several people who had been working out exchanged glances. One of them began moving, and the others followed, all heading toward the changing rooms.","The remaining instructors and the owner stared at one another.","Someone said, “Boss, maybe we should—”","The owner was speechless with exasperation. “You actually believe him?”","Li Jiangbing had worked there for nearly two years. Didn’t the owner know what kind of person he was? When had Li Jiangbing ever had access to inside information?","“What if?” someone said. “What if Jiangbing is telling the truth?”","The owner sneered. “There’s no ‘what if.’ If he had connections like that, he wouldn’t still be working here.”","Someone who could predict the outbreak of the zombie virus couldn’t possibly be an ordinary person. He might not even be an ordinary child of a high-ranking official. He would have to be the child of someone extremely, extremely powerful.","At a gym of their level, where would they possibly find someone like that?","Li Jiangbing felt that he had done everything he could. He had warned everyone, after all.","If they didn’t believe him, there was nothing he could do. He had to save his own life first.","He slung his bag over his shoulder and strode outside, calling Jiang Cheng as he went.","Yes, Li Jiangbing also believed that Jiang Cheng’s instruction not to call back did not apply to him.","That was how confident he was!","The first call didn’t go through.","He had no idea that Song Jingshuo was occupying the line.","Li Jiangbing unlocked his mountain bike, swung onto it, and steadied himself with one foot on the ground as he made a second call.","Jiang Cheng answered immediately.","“Is it true?” Li Jiangbing asked.","“It’s true. Are you on your way back?” Jiang Cheng replied.","“I’m already out!”","“Good. I’m hanging up.”","There was no unnecessary chatter.","Li Jiangbing put his foot on the pedal and began riding as fast as he could.","The gym wasn’t far from the youth apartment. He could get there in fifteen minutes.","All the members of the Interim Committee received the text message.","Of them, only Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan showed a moment of surprise. After thinking it over, they pushed back their chairs and stood up.","Zhao Yi went to ask his supervisor for leave.","His supervisor looked at him. “What’s going on?”","“The zombie virus is coming back today,” Zhao Yi said. “I’m going home to hide.”","His supervisor: “???”","“You should hurry home and hide too,” Zhao Yi added. “Ideally, everyone in your household should stay in a separate room.”","His supervisor: “???”","Zhao Yi turned to leave, then hesitated awkwardly. He didn’t really like being the center of attention.","Fortunately, the zombie crisis had given him some training. For a while, he had even become something of a public figure in his residential compound.","He cleared his throat and said in a soft voice, “I’ve received word that the zombie virus is coming back today. Everyone, hurry home and hide.”","After saying that, he lowered his head, slung his computer bag over his shoulder, and hurried away.","He left the entire office staring at one another in bewilderment.","As Zhao Yi stepped out of the elevator, his phone rang. It was Gao Yuxuan.","“Did you get the text message?”","“I did. I’ve already left the office.”","“Me too.”","“Good. Let’s go home!”","“Take a cab! Hurry up and get a cab!”","“Got it!”","What drives otaku men to believe something without hesitation and spring into action?","A sense of destiny.","Zhao Yi was faintly exhilarated.","After getting out of the taxi, he even kindly told the driver, “The zombie virus is coming. Get home quickly.”","Whether the driver believed him or not was his own fate. In any case, Zhao Yi had done everything he could.","Su Yu was astonished when she saw the text message.","She wanted to call Jiang Cheng, but hesitated when she saw the words: “Do not call back.”","If the message had been sent to everyone, surely a lot of people would be calling her. Her phone would probably be ringing off the hook.","So instead of calling, she opened the messaging app.","The app residents of the complex used to keep in touch was mainly for entertainment and casual socializing. Official business was usually handled elsewhere.","The moment she opened it and came online, she saw several group-chat icons flashing.","【Did anyone else get a text from Jiang Cheng?】","【I did. You got one too?】","【What text?】","【What are you guys talking about?】","Someone typed out the contents of Jiang Cheng’s message and sent them to the group.","The chat exploded at once.","【Seriously?】","【How did Jiang Cheng find out?】","【Does she have some kind of inside information? Didn’t she speak with the mayor on the phone before?】","【That was probably the emergency command center hotline. It wasn’t a personal connection.】","【If the mayor had inside information like this, he couldn’t possibly tell Jiang Cheng—or tell only Jiang Cheng.】","【I called Jiang Cheng. She didn’t answer and hung up on me immediately.】","【She said not to call back.】","【Maybe it’s just a prank?】","【Does Jiang Cheng look like the kind of person who would pull a prank like this?】","The group fell silent.","Because Jiang Cheng... was just too reliable.","Jiang Cheng was absolutely not the kind of person who would joke around or play a prank about something like this.","And yet everyone still felt that it was absurd. They all knew Jiang Cheng worked for an events company. Some of their own employers had even worked with that company on roadshows.","It was just an ordinary private company.","Jiang Cheng herself was simply an ordinary office worker.","There was no one especially rich or powerful—or anyone with a high-ranking official for a parent—living in Youth Apartments.","Song Jingshuo was probably considered quite elite. Even he had first relied on his family to buy him a small apartment, and only bought a large flat after he had earned enough money himself.","The residents of Youth Apartments might differ somewhat in education and income, but there was no fundamental difference in their social class.","They were all ordinary people.","Absurd. Completely absurd.","How could an ordinary person possibly predict something as momentous as a zombie virus outbreak?","Even the government couldn’t do that. If it had been able to, there wouldn’t have been a zombie disaster raging for more than a month.","So many people had died.","Su Yu also felt that it was absurd.","Jiang Cheng was just an ordinary person like the rest of them. Even the government didn’t dare announce that a virus was coming, so how could she?","And yet, while continuing with her work, Su Yu couldn’t stop glancing at her phone, again and again.","It was absurd—but that was Jiang Cheng.","Su Yu’s hand froze on the mouse.","A few seconds later, she abruptly rose to her feet and hurried off to find her supervisor. As she ran, she told everyone, “The zombie virus is coming!”","At that very same moment, Secretary Sun, who had since been promoted to vice mayor, also saw the text message.","He was stunned."]},{"number":85,"title":"Chapter 85","paragraphs":["The municipal government was in session.","The zombie outbreak was, of course, a national calamity—a sorrow that many people could not bear to remember.","And yet, for those who had displayed courage, composure, decisiveness, and perseverance in the midst of the crisis, it had also been a turning point in their lives.","Secretary Sun had never expected to become vice mayor at his age. It was many years ahead of the career path he had planned for himself.","The meeting had already covered several agenda items. They were now discussing whether to commend the civilians who had performed outstandingly, as they had in the past.","Previously, once a disaster had passed, this had always been part of the process.","Commendations, appearances on the news, red flowers pinned to their chests, certificates, prize money, and so on.","Good role models could inspire good social conduct. It was all part of developing a spiritually civilized society.","But this time, the matter was particularly complicated and delicate.","In the past, the people who had distinguished themselves during earthquakes, floods, and fires had generally been involved in “rescuing” others.","This time was different. Government officials had privately spoken with some of the organizers and leaders among the civilians, and many of them had said, “No need. Really, no need.”","Everyone seemed somewhat evasive.","Because during this disaster, there had been more than just “rescue.”","There had also been killing.","Along with it had come looting and coercive violence.","Sometimes, violence had to be met with violence.","Those regarded by the public as heroes and leaders might very well also have the blood of living people on their hands.","If it was impossible to determine whether someone was “pure white,” then it would be a serious problem if something happened after the government had elevated that person as a model citizen.","It could even have a negative influence on society.","That was why the discussion had grown so heated.","The relatively young Vice Mayor Sun frowned at his phone.","It happened to be the tea break. The meeting was suspended while everyone got up to use the restroom, make phone calls, and so on.","Vice Mayor Zheng called out to him.","Vice Mayor Sun looked up.","Vice Mayor Zheng asked, “What’s wrong? You’ve been frowning at that phone for ages.”","Vice Mayor Sun leaned over and handed him the phone. “Do you remember Jiang Cheng from the Youth Apartments in the Science and Technology New District? She just sent a mass text message.”","Vice Mayor Zheng put on his reading glasses, took the phone, and held it at arm’s length.","After reading the message, he frowned too.","“Ridiculous,” he said. “We haven’t received any news. Where did she get this information?”","Hearing that, Vice Mayor Sun felt reassured.","They were the government. They represented the state.","If something like this had happened, the state would have discovered it and issued a warning first. It was impossible for the central government to know nothing while an ordinary citizen had found out ahead of it.","“So this still won’t do. We’ve always thought this girl was excellent, haven’t we? And now look at her—she’s suddenly become unreliable.” Vice Mayor Zheng sighed.","When the topic of “outstanding civilians” had first come up, both he and Vice Mayor Sun had immediately thought of the young woman from the Science and Technology New District.","Vice Mayor Sun, who had dealt with Jiang Cheng directly, tried to defend her. “You can’t really blame her. She’s still so young—a girl, really. So many middle-aged people have suffered mental breakdowns. How can we expect a young woman like her to be unaffected?”","In the month since the pandemic, the number of patients seeking psychological counseling at hospitals across the country had soared.","The number of new patients admitted to psychiatric hospitals had risen sharply as well.","Far too many people had developed psychological problems.","And these problems often manifested belatedly.","They might not have been visible at the time.","At the time, you might simply have thought that someone was calm and rational. In reality, they might already have been insane.","Vice Mayor Sun sighed, agreeing with Vice Mayor Zheng. “Let’s forget it this time. We’ll skip the commendation segment.”","The matter was settled.","To be on the safe side, they would not establish any individual as a model citizen this time. They would issue only general commendations, without naming any specific people.","Everyone had used the restroom and finished their tea, and they gradually returned to their seats.","The meeting continued.","The government building was tall and symmetrical.","The floors had high ceilings, and the corridors were broad. Every office was spacious and dignified, without any sense of crampedness.","Except for the private offices of certain leaders, nearly all the office doors stood open, allowing the spaces to flow into one another.","People came and went.","After sending the mass text from Lucky West Street, Jiang Cheng immediately grabbed her suitcase and strode toward the eastern entrance of the residential compound.","The security guard at the east gate saw her and greeted her. “Welcome back, Miss Jiang.”","Without warning, Jiang Cheng pointed at him with one finger, first at him and then at the security booth. “The zombie virus is coming. Get inside the security booth later and don’t come out. Lock the door from the inside!”","The guard froze.","Jiang Cheng demanded, “Do you understand?”","She stared directly into his eyes, putting him under tremendous psychological pressure. He hurriedly nodded. “I understand.”","Jiang Cheng turned and strode toward Building Two without looking back.","The guard stared blankly at her retreating figure for a while. Then he glanced around, hurried into the security booth, and locked the door from inside.","The booth was small, but its door could be locked, and the windows were fitted with metal bars.","Inside were a U-shaped fork, a steel pipe, and a full set of protective armor.","There was also a case of instant noodles and sausages. After the pandemic, everyone had developed a hoarding habit. Even the stingy property manager had stocked instant noodles and sausages in both the property office and the security booth.","“Although it’s impossible for there to be zombies again,” he had said, “what if there’s an earthquake or something? Better to be prepared.”","So although the security booth was tiny, it had everything one could need. It really was an ideal place to hide.","After locking the door, the guard sat down and looked around at the supplies in the booth, a sense of security rising within him.","It was still two hours before most people got off work, so there were very few residents in the compound.","Jiang Cheng hurried along with rapid footsteps. Up ahead, Master Luo came toward her.","“Miss Jiang!” Master Luo was walking quickly too, heading straight for her. “That text message you sent...”","Jiang Cheng did not slow down. “Get back inside. If there are two of you, have one person stay in the bathroom and lock the door.”","Master Luo kept pace with her. “Is it really true?”","Jiang Cheng did not slacken her pace. The wheels of her suitcase scraped noisily against the ground. “I’ve notified everyone I could. Whether you believe it is your choice.”","She was back. She had returned.","Master Luo felt that the “Miss Jiang” from the disaster period had returned.","Toward the end of the zombie outbreak, the Provisional Committee had essentially had nothing left to do. It existed in name only.","At that time, Miss Jiang had seemed to turn back into an ordinary young woman.","But now, the decisive, ruthless Jiang Cheng of the Provisional Committee had returned.","Master Luo stopped, turned around, and changed direction. “I’m going to tell the property management!”","The property office was in the basement of Building One, so he ran there.","But the property manager did not believe a word Jiang Cheng had said.","The manager glared at him. “Bullshit! Don’t listen to her nonsense! Who does she think she is—the prime minister? How could she know about this? Why isn’t it on television? If something like this were really happening, would the government not warn us in advance and tell us to hide? Do you believe her, or do you believe the state?”","Master Luo was not an assertive man by nature, but this time he was unusually firm.","“I believe both.”","The property manager was furious. “You!”","Master Luo knew that anyone who had not lived through life and death alongside Miss Jiang could never understand the kind of trust one comrade placed in Jiang Cheng.","There was no way to explain it to the manager.","He immediately called his coworkers over the radio. “I just received word from Miss Jiang that the zombie virus is coming back today. Everyone, hurry up and find somewhere to hide. Two people to a room—one person in the bedroom and one in the bathroom. Or find another empty room if you prefer.”","“Hey, hey, hey!” The manager protested. “Are you the manager, or am I?”","Master Luo said, “I’m heading back. You should find somewhere to hide too. Xinyan, hurry back!”","Yang Xinyan had been hunched over the whole time, listening to Master Luo and the manager argue. When she heard Master Luo call her, she perked up. “Coming!”","She scampered upstairs after Master Luo, pretending not to notice the manager’s ugly expression.","The finance clerk came over at a sluggish pace. “Manager, they’ve all left, so what about me...?”","The manager was furious. “Go, go, go! Leave, all of you!”","The finance clerk happily went back to grab her bag. “Bye, Manager.”","She didn’t believe the zombies were really coming back. The government had already announced that they’d been completely wiped out.","Still, getting off work early was all that mattered.","The property management office was having a hard time recruiting people and was still seriously understaffed. Fortunately, Guo Jun and the others from Maiduo worked part-time nights, which was enough to keep things running.","Once those people left, the property management center was empty.","The manager stood there with his hands on his hips, seething.","After thinking it over, he called his wife. “I’m not coming home tonight. Something came up. I’ll stay in the dormitory, so don’t worry about me.”","He wasn’t going home. He was determined to see how this “Miss Jiang” planned to explain herself if the zombie virus failed to appear.","The moment Jiang Cheng reached the ground floor, she sensed the telepathic connection.","She raised her right hand, and the entirely black cat leaped down from a tree branch onto her arm. It climbed along her arm and shoulder, making its way around to her left shoulder.","Then it began:","“Meow—”","“Meow—”","“Stop cursing, stop cursing.” Jiang Cheng already had a headache. “I came back, didn’t I?”","Even without telepathy to translate, anyone could tell that the cat was using some very foul language.","And it was understandable. She had been gone for an entire month—far too long. No wonder the cat was angry.","During that time, Li Jiangbing had occasionally sent her updates about the cat.","Saw your cat in the pavilion today.","Saw your cat by the fountain tomorrow.","Your cat got into a fight with He Tian’s dog.","Gao Yuxuan teased your cat and got scratched on the butt.","And so on.","“Let’s go home,” Jiang Cheng said to the cat. “The zombies are coming back.”","The instant the message reached the cat through their telepathic connection, its cursing abruptly stopped.","Its tiny mouth tightened, and its dark-green eyes turned solemn.","Li Jiangbing was the next person to arrive at the residential compound after Jiang Cheng. Riding a bicycle, he got there in ten minutes.","The security guard pushed open the window and greeted him through the metal bars. “Miss Jiang just came back. She said the zombies are coming again!”","“I know.” Li Jiangbing leaned forward and glanced inside. “You’re hiding in there, right? Do you have food and water?”","“Yes, we have everything. There’s a water dispenser here.”","“Good. Then stay in there and lock the door.”","As he spoke, he pedaled away.","The security guard gripped the bars with both hands, pressing his nose and mouth through them as he shouted, “Are the zombies really coming?”","From far away, Li Jiangbing called back, “I don’t know. I’m listening to Jiang Cheng—”"]},{"number":86,"title":"Chapter 86","paragraphs":["The ones who returned a little later than Li Jiangbing were Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan.","Their workplaces were close too, both of them located in the High-Tech Development Zone.","The reason the district was called the High-Tech New District was that it contained a high-tech industrial park.","In any case, the two of them didn’t live far away either, and they came back one right after the other.","The security guard greeted them as well.","They weren’t the only ones who worked in the high-tech industrial park. Quite a few residents of the Youth Apartments worked there.","Since so many companies in the same industry were clustered in the area, even when people changed jobs, they usually just moved from one company in the high-tech industrial park to another. That was why they had bought homes there in the first place.","More people gradually returned, all of them employees of the high-tech industrial park. They lived nearby.","The security guard recognized more and more familiar faces.","Some people arrived at the same time and greeted one another.","“You’re back too?”","“Whether you believe it or not, it’ll only delay work by half a day at most. What if it’s true?”","“That’s what I thought too.”","“Mainly because of Jiang Cheng... She doesn’t seem like the kind of person who would joke about something like this.”","“Exactly!”","One after another, more and more people returned ahead of schedule.","Jiang Cheng’s mass text had been sent to all the members of the provisional committee—several dozen people.","Those people were also members of all kinds of groups: the provisional committee group, building groups, volunteer groups, death-defying team groups, running groups, fitness groups, ride-sharing groups, gaming groups, dog-walking groups, food groups, and pickup groups.","The residents of the complex were scattered throughout these various groups. Taken together, the groups overlapped enough to cover nearly every homeowner in the Youth Apartments.","So aside from those who were at work and didn’t have the app open, everyone who was online knew about it.","After finding it absurd and impossible, and wondering whether it might be a joke, many people didn’t leap to their feet and decide to go home immediately as Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan had. But after putting down their phones, they grew increasingly uneasy.","In the end, one person after another came back.","The security guard grew more and more nervous. He made another round of the security office, checking that he had enough water and food, that his armor and weapons were in place, and that the door was locked from the inside. Only then did he relax.","What was there to be afraid of? If zombies came, he would just fight them.","The Youth Apartments had the most experience with this, after all.","Jiang Cheng had only been back in her apartment for a short while when she heard someone slap the door twice and shout, “I’m back too! I’m heading in!”","It was Li Jiangbing.","Excellent.","Holding Mo Li, Jiang Cheng sat in a lounge chair by the floor-to-ceiling window, gazing intently down at the courtyard.","She saw hurried figures below.","As they passed beneath her building, she could make out Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan.","She smiled.","One familiar person after another was returning.","Wu Jiancheng, Su Yu, He Tian—even Nie Kuizhang—had all come back.","There were also many people whose names she couldn’t recall but whose faces she recognized.","They ran into one another in the courtyard and exchanged greetings before hurrying toward their respective buildings. They returned to their own apartments, separating themselves from everyone else.","Just as Jiang Cheng had instructed.","Jiang Cheng was very pleased.","She stroked Mo Li’s head.","She wondered whether anyone had considered that among these people rushing home, there would certainly be some who turned into zombies.","Jiang Cheng felt that they had seemingly failed to realize this.","No one thought they themselves might become a zombie. Everyone was thinking, “I need to get home and lock the door before someone else turns into a zombie and hurts me.”","Jiang Cheng closed her eyes and felt her body heating up.","Last time, she had mistakenly thought she was coming down with a fever.","This time, she understood perfectly. Her cells were burning.","Although the cloudy weather made it rather dim, it was still afternoon—nowhere near dusk.","This time, it had started earlier than before.","Like giving birth to a second child: the second came faster than the first.","“Will I become a zombie?” Jiang Cheng asked Mo Li.","Mo Li lay sprawled across her chest.","They had been apart for too long, and he was suffering from separation anxiety. He was especially clingy, stuck to her body and refusing to get down.","He rubbed his fluffy head against her again and again, determined to leave his scent all over Jiang Cheng.","She gently scratched his head with her fingertip and murmured to herself, “If I turn...”","What then?","Should she let Mo Li bite her to death?","Of course not.","“If I turn, I’ll bite you, and you can turn with me.” Jiang Cheng’s lips curved into a smile. “We’ll become the Invincible Zombie King.”","“If you don’t turn, run. Let’s not kill each other.”","Song Jingshuo, on the other hand, returned late.","His company was on Financial Street in the city center, and the traffic was congested. It took him more than an hour to get home.","He parked in the underground garage and hurried toward the elevator.","The moment he stepped inside, he sensed that something was wrong.","His vision went black, and all strength drained from his body.","He struggled to brace himself against the elevator and stand upright, but his legs gave way.","Before losing consciousness, he thought with relief: Trusting Jiang Cheng... had been the right choice.","This time, the transformation occurred during the transition from afternoon to dusk.","And it was a workday.","Although rush hour had not yet arrived, people were already beginning to leave work.","The roads were packed with cars and pedestrians. Office buildings were still full, while restaurants on the bustling commercial streets were beginning to fill with customers. Shopping malls were crowded with people pouring in after work.","Compared with last time, far more people were outside their homes.","They say that when giving birth to a second child, labor is often faster—but more painful.","In a disturbingly apt way, that description applied to the situation before them.","There were simply too many cars on the roads. When the mass unconsciousness affecting the entire population descended, it triggered chain collisions everywhere.","Buses caught fire, and everyone inside burned to death in silence.","Some private cars had anti-theft alarm systems. The impacts triggered them, filling the streets with shrill sirens.","Headlights flashed on and off without pause.","No one put out the fires. Some people didn’t even get out of their cars.","Some lay slumped over their steering wheels. Others had collapsed against their neck pillows. All of them had lost consciousness.","Before passing out, everyone at the Youth Apartments—those who had made it home and those who hadn’t—thought the same thing:","Jiang Cheng had actually been telling the truth.","Those who had rushed back to their apartments closed their eyes in relief.","Those who had ignored Jiang Cheng’s warning and remained outside were filled with fear and regret in the moment before losing consciousness.","Inside the government complex, Vice Mayor Sun’s legs gave out. Even bracing himself against the wall, he couldn’t stand.","He fell to the floor. From his tilted viewpoint, he saw his colleagues sprawled across the slanted corridor, all of them collapsed on the ground.","Vice Mayor Sun realized that disaster had arrived.","That young woman’s warning had actually been true.","In a building as spacious as the municipal government complex, there was little chance of anyone escaping a transformation.","Back then, there had been no survivors in the city surveillance center. They had expended enormous effort to eliminate the zombies and reclaim the building.","That had only been possible because they were still alive. They had all lost consciousness in their own homes, and therefore hadn’t become second-generation zombies at the mouths of the original zombies.","But this time—this time...","The entire municipal government leadership was inside the building.","The same was true of all the government agencies. No one had left work yet; everyone was still in their offices.","Vice Mayor Sun realized that none of the civil servants would escape.","The government was about to be wiped out completely.","Then who would organize the forces, gather supplies, and lead the people in resisting the zombies?","Who?","Once humanity lost its leadership and restraints, the upheaval of the environment would unleash a level of cruelty and evil beyond imagination.","They had seen far too much of that on the wall of screens in the surveillance center.","If...","If only he had believed that little girl...","Vice Mayor Sun, consumed by anxiety, worry, and fear for the nation and its people, fell into a coma.","This time, it seemed to be just like the last.","But this time, many people, like Jiang Cheng, began to develop fevers.","Their cells began to burn.","Their genes continuously recombined.","The human body began changing from its most fundamental units upward.","...","...","Peng Ze suddenly awoke.","For a moment, he was dazed, unsure where he was or what he was doing.","He looked around. Trees surrounded him on every side, dense enough to block his view of anything in the distance. He couldn’t hear a sound.","Then Peng Ze remembered. A zombie had bitten off part of his ear. He had been infected.","He was going to mutate into a second-generation zombie.","To avoid running into the crowds on the streets, he had gotten into an abandoned car and driven north the entire way.","The city center lay to the south. Only by going north could he get away from the crowds.","He had driven all the way to the forest park on the northern edge of the city. It was where people came on weekends to breathe fresh air, exercise, jog, fish, and fly kites.","He had abandoned the car and continued on foot, plunging deeper and deeper into the woods until he reached the dense forest far from the rubber running track.","Hardly anyone ever came here.","He had simply wanted to wait quietly for his mutation. Ideally, no one would discover him. That way, he wouldn’t hurt anyone else.","And then.","Then...","Then, just now, he had suddenly regained consciousness.","Peng Ze stood there in a daze, not knowing how long he had been in that spot. He had no sense of time passing. Could he have fallen asleep standing up? Why hadn’t he mutated yet?","It was still daytime, and sunlight streamed down through the trees.","It looked as if it should be hot, but for some reason, Peng Ze couldn’t feel the temperature.","Suddenly, he no longer wanted to stay there.","His body felt terrible, as though it desperately craved something.","There was nothing here. He had to go somewhere else to find it.","Peng Ze started walking toward the outside. He moved faster and faster, the trees on either side of him flashing backward with a rapid whoosh.","But he didn’t notice anything unusual about his speed.","He raced through the woods. A concrete path appeared ahead, and beyond it was a small earth-covered hill planted with grass and trees.","Peng Ze didn’t follow the concrete path around the hill. Why go around? He shot straight up the slope and saw the rubber looped track used by everyone in the forest park for walking and running.","Peng Ze dashed down onto it.","There was a person lying facedown on the track.","He wore professional-looking running clothes and shoes. He seemed to have just woken up as well and was slowly sitting up.","Peng Ze walked toward him, somewhat concerned, wanting to ask whether he needed help.","But something seemed to be wrong with Peng Ze’s vocal cords. The words he wanted to say came out as an indistinct “Hrrgh... hrrgh...”","The person on the ground turned back in astonishment. When he saw Peng Ze, his expression suddenly changed. He scrambled to his feet and fled at full speed.","Peng Ze reached out, wanting to call him back, wanting to tell him, Don’t be afraid. I haven’t mutated yet.","Then he saw his own hand—","Blue-green skin. Blackened nails.","Peng Ze slowly turned his palm over, his gaze fixed upon it.","So that was it.","He had already mutated.","A faint fragrance drifted over, activating his genes.","What was that incredibly alluring scent? It lingered in the place where the man had just been lying.","It smelled so good.","This was what his famished body had been craving.","Peng Ze couldn’t stop himself from running. He sped up with every step, chasing after the man.","The farther he pursued him, the stronger the fragrance in the air became.","Soon, he saw the man’s back.","Peng Ze accelerated.","The athletic runner summoned the fastest speed of his life in a desperate bid to survive.","Terrified, he ran while looking back over his shoulder.","But to his horror, he saw the zombie leap into the air, arms spread wide, pouncing on him like a giant bird!","Peng Ze locked his arms around the runner from behind.","Then he bit down, sinking his teeth into the back of the runner’s neck.","The body.","The flesh.","Meat.","Skin.","Blood.","It was exquisite."]},{"number":87,"title":"Chapter 87","paragraphs":["Jiang Cheng felt moisture on her nose.","She opened her eyes with some difficulty and found Mo Li licking the tip of her nose.","When he saw that she was awake, he let out a “meow” that sounded surprisingly gentle.","He was worried about her.","Jiang Cheng closed her eyes and lay on the recliner for a moment, clearing her head.","When she opened them again, she understood why her eyes felt uncomfortable: there was sunlight.","The dark clouds had completely dispersed, and outside was actually brighter than it had been in the afternoon.","Jiang Cheng moved Mo Li off her chest, picked up her phone from the floor, and checked the time. She had been unconscious for less than an hour.","Something suddenly flashed before her eyes.","Jiang Cheng froze. When she focused, there was nothing there—only her small apartment.","It flashed again.","Jiang Cheng held her breath.","When she concentrated, the thing appeared once more before her eyes, though it was unstable.","Jiang Cheng closed her eyes.","She could still see it. So it wasn’t actually “before her eyes”; it was inside her mind.","Jiang Cheng cleared her mind and focused.","The image finally stabilized, like a television with a poor signal.","A space.","A space with no shape, yet with boundaries she could sense.","Judging by its volume, the space was about the size of her bathroom.","When she relaxed, the image wavered and vanished from her mind.","She could vaguely sense a connection between the space and her mind, but she had to concentrate in order to visualize it clearly.","What was this?","The moment Jiang Cheng wondered what it was, a crack appeared in the seal over the memories of another world inside her mind.","[Storage Space.]","Jiang Cheng understood instantly.","And she was familiar with it.","Jiang Cheng believed that before she had crossed over into this world, she must have possessed something similar in that other world.","She stood up and looked out through the floor-to-ceiling window at the courtyard. There was no one in sight.","She was probably once again among the first to wake up.","She turned on her computer and created a post on the residents’ forum:","[Reporting In: Those Who Are Awake]","[Building 2, 0306—Jiang Cheng]","After posting, she rubbed her temples and focused on sensing the storage space.","Then she relaxed.","Then she focused again.","It was like an old television with a bad signal; she had to smack it a few times.","After repeating this for several minutes, the signal on that old television finally stabilized.","Something between her and the storage space had stabilized as well.","The words [Mental Link] flashed through her mind.","What an apt description.","Yet Jiang Cheng couldn’t find anything related to it in “Jiang Cheng’s” memories or knowledge. This was not something that originally existed in this world.","Had she brought it with her from the other world?","Jiang Cheng glanced at the glass of water on the table.","She tried it, but the glass didn’t react at all.","She placed her hand on it. The instant her fingertips touched the glass, it vanished from sight and was taken into the storage space.","[Not very useful.]","That evaluation surfaced in her mind.","It came from the instinctive impression left by the locked memories of the other world.","She must have owned—or at least used—a much better storage space in that other world.","She couldn’t say how much better it had been, but surely it hadn’t required her to touch an object before she could store it. That limitation made the space far too impractical.","Li Jiangbing woke up as well.","He woke in bed. After returning home, the sensation of impending unconsciousness had arrived much sooner than expected, so he had hurried to lie down comfortably while he still could.","As expected, when he woke up, his back and waist didn’t ache.","And he hadn’t turned into a zombie!","It was only in that final moment before losing consciousness that he had thought: Wait, I could turn into a zombie too, couldn’t I?","Oh no. If I turned, I wondered whether Jiang Cheng could take me down.","I’m so big. It might be a bit difficult for her. She’d have to jump to chop me.","Luckily, he hadn’t turned.","His head did hurt terribly, though. His brain felt as if a tiny pebble had gotten inside his sneaker—grating against him and causing pain with every movement. His body also felt hot, as if he had a fever.","Li Jiangbing rubbed his temples and went to the bathroom, turning on the faucet to splash some water on his face and cool himself down.","But the moment the tap water began rushing out, he felt something strange.","Li Jiangbing stared blankly for a moment, then put his hand into the stream of water.","After a while, he focused, withdrew his hand, and held it up before his eyes.","A water ball the size of a ping-pong ball hovered and rolled above his palm. It was crystalline, clear, and sparkling.","Adorable.","Li Jiangbing was stunned.","It took him a long while to recover. His first thought was to immediately go show Jiang Cheng!","But he suppressed the impulse at once—what if Jiang Cheng had turned into a zombie?","Oh no. He couldn’t bring himself to strike her down.","He’d have to let Song Jingshuo help Jiang Cheng rest in peace. That guy would definitely be able to do it.","Song Jingshuo woke up as well.","With a splitting headache, he sat up inside the elevator.","He glanced at the display. The elevator had already stopped at the floor where he lived.","He closed his eyes and rested for a while. Once the headache had eased slightly, he stood up. He had no weapon on him, so he pressed his body tightly against the side wall before pushing the “Open Door” button.","Luckily, there were no zombies in the hallway.","After peeking out to make sure, Song Jingshuo immediately ran from the elevator. He gripped his front-door key tightly and rushed to his apartment, unlocking the door.","Once inside, he slammed it shut. Only then did he finally feel completely safe.","He swept his gaze around the apartment. A fairly nice sculpture had once sat on a display cabinet in the living room.","Later, he had removed the sculpture and placed his cleaned armor there instead.","It was meant to commemorate that special period of time.","Thank goodness the entire suit of armor was still there, along with his weapons.","And he hadn’t turned into a zombie either.","Song Jingshuo first went over to turn on his computer. Sure enough, he saw Jiang Cheng’s check-in post on the forum.","Why was Jiang Cheng always among the first to wake up?","The thought flashed through Song Jingshuo’s mind.","He opened the post and saw that Li Jiangbing had already checked in.","There still weren’t many reports—only a scattered few—but some came from people he knew well, such as Su Yu and Wu Jiancheng. There were also several names that looked familiar, though he couldn’t match them to any faces.","Good. As long as Jiang Cheng and Li Jiangbing were safe, everything was fine.","The next question he considered was: Why had Jiang Cheng known about the zombie virus in advance?","He knew that after the second outbreak of the virus, many of the survivors would be thinking about the same thing.","They would all want to know why.","When Li Jiangbing saw on the forum that Jiang Cheng was still alive, he was overjoyed.","He called her. “I’m coming over! I have something to show you!”","Jiang Cheng said, “Put on your armor before you come.”","It was better to be prepared in case a neighbor had mutated.","Li Jiangbing put on the full suit of armor.","With the virus undergoing a second outbreak, there were bound to be many more zombies. They might have to fight at any moment.","Once fully equipped, he picked up his weapon and opened the door a crack to look outside.","Safe.","He tiptoed quickly to Apartment 0306 and gently knocked. “It’s me. It’s me.”","Jiang Cheng was already waiting by the door. She opened it a crack, looked him up and down, and let him in.","“Jingshuo has woken up too. He reported on the forum.” She walked to the table and bent over to look at the computer.","She refreshed the page, and several new check-in posts appeared. People were waking up one after another.","Hearing that Song Jingshuo was safe as well, Li Jiangbing felt even more reassured.","The Iron Triangle was all here. There was nothing to fear!","But he was anxious about something else. “Jiang Cheng, Jiang Cheng! I have something to show you!”","Jiang Cheng turned to look at him, one hand braced against the tabletop.","Li Jiangbing held a loosely clenched fist out in front of her face, then opened it.","A tiny ball of water hovered and slowly spun above his broad palm.","“I think I’ve developed a superpower!” Li Jiangbing couldn’t hide his excitement. “When I woke up, I touched some water and suddenly had this... how should I put it? A feeling. I felt like I was connected to the water somehow. I don’t know how to explain it. Ugh, I just can’t find the words.”","The consequences of not studying properly during his teenage years were now on full display in his poor command of language.","Jiang Cheng straightened and stared at the hovering ball of water.","The moment her storage space appeared, it had triggered a memory of recognition, telling her with absolute certainty that she had used one before.","But the phenomenon before her eyes stirred no such recognition.","She was unfamiliar with what was happening. Judging by the knowledge system of this world, “superpower” really was the only term that could describe it.","She asked, “Be more specific. I mean, how do you form it? How do you control it? Is this all you can do? Is there a limit?”","Her storage space had a limit as well.","She couldn’t see it visually, but she could sense an invisible boundary and the approximate size of the space.","There was a limit to how much it could hold.","Before Li Jiangbing arrived, she had already tested it with the bed, sofa, coffee table, dining table, and other large pieces of furniture.","She had quickly observed and summarized several properties of the storage space.","For example, the objects stored inside were not restricted by their shape.","From what she could sense, the space’s capacity was roughly equivalent to the size of her bathroom.","If she put the bed into the bathroom, there would be no room for the sofa, because the shapes would prevent them from fitting together.","So even if plenty of empty space remained in the bathroom after the bed went in, the sofa still could not be put inside.","The storage space, however, was different. It was not affected by shape. The sofa, bed, and coffee table had all gone in together, stacked on top of one another.","Inside, they floated weightlessly.","After thinking it over, Jiang Cheng concluded that what truly determined the space’s “capacity” was not volume, but mass.","If that was the case, everything made sense.","She had later put in a few more things and tested the limit.","Only after finishing her phone call with Li Jiangbing did she release everything and restore the room to its original state.","Not a trace was left behind.","Li Jiangbing was completely thrown by her questions. “Huh?”","He had been too excited to rush over and show Jiang Cheng his discovery to think about anything else.","Now that she was testing him, he could only rack his brains on the spot. “It’s just that whenever I touch water, I can sense something.”","“Perception,” Jiang Cheng supplied.","“Right, right, that’s a better word! It’s like there’s some kind of... uh... connection between me and tap water...”","“A mental link.”","“Right, right! Exactly!”","Li Jiangbing continued, “Then I sensed it while thinking about it. By using that ‘thought,’ I can shape it like modeling clay. It listens to me and turned into this.”","“Huh?” He suddenly realized something. “How can you describe it so clearly?”","“Perception” and “mental link.”","Especially “mental link.”","Jiang Cheng extended a finger and poked the tiny ball of water.","The instant she touched it, the ball vanished.","“Huh? Huh? Huh???” Li Jiangbing was stunned. “Where did it go? Where’s my ball?”","Inside the storage space, the ball of water remained exactly as it had been, still perfectly spherical.","But the moment Jiang Cheng opened her hand and released it into her palm, the “ball” lost its shape and fell apart into a puddle. It slipped through the gaps between her fingers and dripped away.","“Huh? Huh?” Li Jiangbing was both astonished and delighted. “You have a superpower too!”","At that moment, cries for help rang out from the courtyard below.","“Help! Somebody! Is anyone there?”","Jiang Cheng and Li Jiangbing both ran to the floor-to-ceiling window and looked down.","Because they had come from different distances, the people who had believed Jiang Cheng’s warning returned at different times.","Song Jingshuo was lucky to have passed out inside the elevator. He wasn’t the last person to enter the residential complex. A few others had arrived even later, and they had the bad luck of collapsing outdoors.","Now, two of them had woken up. One had not changed.","The other had mutated—and was chasing the one who hadn’t."]},{"number":88,"title":"Chapter 88","paragraphs":["After the first zombie crisis, people no longer feared zombies as “terrifying monsters.” What they worried about now was the danger to their lives.","The unlucky guy who had passed out in the courtyard was actually quite experienced at killing zombies. Unfortunately, he had no protective gear or weapons.","Although many people now regarded zombies as oversized wild dogs, zombies were ultimately different from wild dogs.","If you were bitten by a wild dog, the greatest danger was rabies—and there was still a vaccine for that, a safety net of sorts.","But the zombie virus was highly transmissible through blood. Once you were scratched or bitten, it was all over. To this day, the country had never announced a case of anyone being immune. So people did their best to avoid direct physical contact.","The man had returned carrying a laptop bag. In a moment of crisis, he had swung the bag around as a weapon, using it to block several zombie attacks.","But the zombie in front of him was probably a second-generation zombie—fast and powerful. Without protective gear, it was extremely difficult to deal with. So after swinging the laptop bag and knocking the zombie away, he immediately ran.","When he looked back and saw the zombie pouncing at him again, he swung the bag a second time, smacking it directly in the face and knocking it aside.","Then he kept running.","As he ran, he screamed for help. “Somebody come help meee! This is a second-gen zombieee! I don’t have a weapon aaaaah! Fuck, is anybody thereee?”","Someone should come. He had seen several people in the group chats saying that, whether the messages were true or not, they had decided to return. That was why he had come back too.","There was no way to shake off a second-generation zombie. All he could do was scream himself hoarse for help.","Li Jiangbing turned around and ran without a second thought.","Jiang Cheng didn’t move immediately, because she had to put on her armor first.","While she was getting dressed, she saw that Li Jiangbing had not yet appeared downstairs. Someone else had already gone to the rescue.","The residents of Youth Apartments did, in the end, possess a certain degree of camaraderie.","The person who had come to help wasn’t even a property owner. He was the young security guard who had taken shelter in the guard booth by the east gate.","Jiang Cheng recognized him. She didn’t know his exact name, but she knew his surname was Fang, and everyone called him Little Fang.","Little Fang had been lucky when he woke up—he hadn’t mutated. Then he heard the cries for help.","The place where the unlucky guy had passed out was actually not far from the east gate. He had fled for his life all the way to the center of the courtyard.","Little Fang cautiously poked his head out to observe. After confirming that the complex seemed relatively clear and that there was only one zombie in sight, he bravely put on his protective gear and went to save the man.","For a weapon, he chose a steel pipe over a U-shaped fork.","The U-shaped forks were meant to be used when several people formed a combat formation. They were auxiliary tools. For a solo attack, a steel pipe was definitely the better choice.","Little Fang charged out with the steel pipe in hand.","At last, someone had come. The unlucky guy finally breathed a sigh of relief.","While Little Fang attacked the zombie, the unlucky guy did not simply run away. He turned back and continued swinging his laptop bag at the zombie’s head, creating openings for Little Fang to attack.","Li Jiangbing soon appeared in the courtyard as well, and the Building Three resident also came out.","By the time Jiang Cheng finished gearing up and reached the lobby via the stairs, Su Yu happened to be coming down from the elevator in a full suit of protective armor.","Aside from Jiang Cheng, none of the female property owners had armor.","Earlier, there had not been enough protective gear, so it had been distributed first to the stronger male residents—the ones with greater physical strength and combat ability.","This wasn’t limited to the women. Among the male residents, the shorter, thinner, weaker, or less courageous ones had not received armor either.","But Su Yu had always wanted a suit of her own.","After the zombie crisis ended, the armor had not been collected. The property management office kept a few sets, while most of the rest went home with the last people who had used them.","Su Yu had posted on the forum asking to buy one, and someone sold her a suit for five hundred yuan.","It was a medium size, though Su Yu should have worn a small. The shoulder guards were a little loose, but they had straps to hold them in place, so it wasn’t a serious problem.","This was Su Yu’s first time going into battle wearing armor.","She ran into Jiang Cheng in the lobby as Jiang Cheng came down the stairs, and her eyes lit up.","There was no time for greetings. The two of them ran outside together.","By then, Li Jiangbing had already engaged the zombie at close quarters. When Little Fang saw him arrive—and spotted another fully armored male resident rushing over in the distance—his courage increased dramatically.","He shouted as he brought the steel pipe down on the zombie.","The Building Three resident also reached them. The unarmored unlucky guy backed off a little, allowing the three people in full armor to take the front line and battle the zombie.","Jiang Cheng and Su Yu also came into view.","At that moment, the zombie took a blow to the neck and fell to the ground. Its head lolled to one side, and it propped itself up on one arm, sprawled on the ground like an injured person.","Of the three people in full armor, Little Fang had the least experience.","He had taken part in the battle on the Sunday morning when the zombie virus first broke out. After that, the temporary residents’ committee had quickly been established and begun assigning work in an organized manner.","As a security guard for the property management company, Little Fang’s primary responsibility was to watch the gates, making sure no zombies or thieves got in. He was also responsible for checking residents for injuries when they returned to the complex.","Until the zombie crisis ended, he had never participated in another battle. He had the least experience of the three.","When he saw the zombie injured and lying on the ground, he rushed forward excitedly, eager to kill one with his own hands.","Since the zombie was sprawled on the ground, Little Fang had to bend forward to strike the back of its skull with the steel pipe.","That was when two people shouted at the same time.","Little Fang had no idea what they were saying. Everything happened too quickly. The zombie suddenly rolled over and sprang up from the ground while still in that prone position. Its wide-open mouth, reeking of foul breath, lunged straight at Little Fang’s face!","Little Fang was horrified.","Li Jiangbing had sensed that something was wrong the moment the zombie fell facedown.","He had always been one of the complex’s main fighters. Later, he had joined the militia, and every day he woke up to do one thing: kill zombies. Kill zombies, and kill more zombies.","He had far more experience with zombies than Little Fang.","That wounded, prone posture was too unlike a zombie. It was too human.","Yes—too human.","Humans felt pain. When injured, they lost strength, which was why they assumed postures like that.","But how could a zombie?","Even if a zombie had only half a body left, as long as its head remained attached, it could still use both hands to “run” toward you.","Zombies didn’t assume humanlike poses, as though they were injured!","Li Jiangbing realized something was wrong in that instant, but Little Fang had already rushed forward.","He instinctively shouted, “Back!” But it was too late. Sure enough, the zombie sprang up from the ground.","Li Jiangbing’s pupils contracted sharply.","Fortunately, he wasn’t the only person there with extensive field experience.","The unlucky guy had also once been part of the militia.","That was why Li Jiangbing had immediately rushed downstairs without hesitation after taking one look through the window. The unlucky guy had once been his comrade.","Because he was holding the laptop bag and had stepped back instead of joining the fight, the unlucky guy had a clearer view of everything.","He reacted even faster. He swung the laptop bag straight at the zombie!","The bag struck the zombie squarely in the face, saving Little Fang’s life.","Li Jiangbing and the other man rushed forward and smashed the zombie’s head several times.","It was over.","Little Fang sat on the ground, his heart pounding violently. He had nearly pissed himself.","How could zombies deceive people now, too?","The unlucky guy hurried over, crouched down, and grabbed the man by the head, checking him over from top to bottom and side to side. Only after confirming that he wasn’t injured did he turn to Li Jiangbing and say, “No injuries.”","His movements were remarkably practiced.","They had honed those skills back when they served in the militia.","By the time Jiang Cheng and Su Yu came running over, the fight was already over.","Jiang Cheng had seen what happened just now. When she reached them, she didn’t ask what had happened first. Instead, she said, “Let’s check whether there’s anyone else in the courtyard.”","Little Fang gathered himself, stood up, and said, “There are two by the entrance.”","Little Fang had been guarding the east gate. From the window of the security booth, he had watched one resident after another return after hearing Jiang Cheng’s announcement.","At first, there had only been a few people. Then their numbers gradually grew, before thinning out again.","Song Jingshuo was one of those who had returned late.","The group temporarily set aside what they were doing and headed for the east gate.","The unlucky guy had neither armor nor a weapon, so he didn’t dare separate from them. He picked up his computer bag and hurried after them.","Sure enough, there were still two people on the way to the east gate.","The first one they encountered hadn’t woken up yet and was lying on the ground.","Li Jiangbing went over, pried open his eyelids, and took a look. The whites and pupils of his eyes were normal, and his skin color was normal too.","“This one’s fine!”","They left him where he was and continued running toward the east gate.","Inside the east gate, just a few meters past the entrance, another person was sprawled on the ground. They could see him clearly from a distance.","But after they had taken only a couple of steps, the man moved on his own and stood up.","He had already mutated.","Everyone tightened their grip on their weapons and tensed their bodies, preparing in case it suddenly charged.","The zombie saw them and did begin to charge—but it wasn’t a sudden burst of speed.","It staggered toward them at a leisurely pace.","Everyone: “...”","Li Jiangbing: “Fuck.”","It was actually a primitive zombie.","After fighting for a month and a half, especially now that they were fully equipped with armor and weapons, they had long since stopped taking primitive zombies seriously.","Their main opponents were second-generation zombies.","Seeing a primitive zombie all of a sudden gave them an odd sense of familiarity.","But something was wrong.","Shouldn’t humans who fell unconscious and mutated directly from the virus, without coming into contact with a primitive zombie, all become primitive zombies?","After killing this primitive zombie, they exchanged glances. Unease and suspicion were evident in every pair of eyes.","Li Jiangbing said, “The one just now wasn’t a second-generation zombie either.”","Little Fang felt it most deeply. “That’s right! It actually knew how to trick us!”","The zombies had learned to feint.","Su Yu asked, “Has it evolved?”","The issue of zombie evolution had already been hotly debated on the forums and in the chat groups while Jiang Cheng was still away on a business trip.","So no one was unfamiliar with the subject.","Jiang Cheng asked the unlucky guy and Little Fang, “Did the one just now mutate directly?”","The unlucky guy knew the situation best. He nodded. “It was extremely close to me. I woke up first, and then it got up.”","The facts were clear now. This outbreak of the zombie virus was different from the previous one.","Although some people still mutated into the relatively weak primitive zombies, others could mutate directly into zombies that were one level more evolved than second-generation zombies—zombies with intelligence.","Had the zombie virus undergone a generational evolution?"]},{"number":89,"title":"Chapter 89","paragraphs":["If that was really the case, then things were going to be bad.","Everyone who had lived through the zombie crisis understood how serious the situation was.","But there was no way to draw a definite conclusion yet. Jiang Cheng could only say, “Come on. Let’s see if there are any more in the courtyard.”","For the people staying in the residential complex, the zombies breaking out at this hour were much less of a threat than last time.","That was because there weren’t many people in the complex at this time of day.","Even though so many people had hurried back after hearing Jiang Cheng’s warning, almost all of them—apart from the last few—had made it back to their apartments in time.","The courtyard was deserted. It was much better than last time.","Even in residential complexes other than the Youth Apartments, this was generally a time when there were fewer people around.","Of those who stayed home, whether elderly people or housewives, many had already started preparing dinner in the kitchen by this hour.","Office workers and students weren’t home.","People gradually began coming down from the various buildings.","And most of those who came down were wearing armor. In other words, they only dared to come down because they had armor.","Of course, there were also a few bold people who had made their own protective gear and come down without armor.","This was their own complex, after all. Especially when they saw Jiang Cheng and Li Jiangbing downstairs, they naturally felt emboldened enough to come down.","Some people were born leaders. As long as they stood there, they had the power to steady everyone else.","Song Jingshuo called Jiang Cheng. After learning that they were downstairs, he came down as well.","Unfortunately for him, the elevator stopped on the way to the first floor.","When the doors opened, a zombie outside was busy gnawing on someone. Hearing the noise, it turned its head—and its eyes met Song Jingshuo’s.","Song Jingshuo: “...”","Song Jingshuo felt that today was truly cursed.","The one lucky thing in all that bad luck was that this was a second-generation zombie.","The movement patterns of second-generation zombies were easy to predict: they moved in straight lines.","Sure enough, the zombie dropped the half-eaten person in its hands and charged straight toward the elevator.","Ever since the previous zombie crisis ended, Song Jingshuo had been worried about the asymmetry between his two arms.","He had swung his right arm so many times while killing zombies that he felt the muscles in his right arm no longer looked quite the same as those in his left.","The upside, however, was that he had trained his reflexes and explosive power to a remarkable level.","The zombie charged into the elevator. In the instant Song Jingshuo dodged to the side, his blade was already coming down.","A head fell to the floor.","Song Jingshuo had bought the knife during his travels, deep in a region inhabited by an ethnic minority. It wasn’t some crudely made decorative blade from a tourist attraction. He had spent quite a bit of effort persuading the owner to sell it to him, and paid a high price for it.","After the zombie crisis ended, he had sharpened it once more before putting it away in a cabinet.","It was razor-sharp.","He kicked the zombie’s corpse out of the elevator.","Then he walked over to the person who had been bitten. The person was already on the verge of death, but still breathing. He stared at Song Jingshuo with his eyes open, unable to speak.","Song Jingshuo tightened his grip on the knife.","Then tightened it again.","In the end, he still couldn’t bring himself to swing.","He bent down, grabbed the man by the wrist, and dragged him into the elevator.","Ultimately, he still couldn’t bring himself to cut off the head of someone who was, for now, still “human.”","He dragged the man out of the building.","By then, dozens of people had gathered in the courtyard. When someone saw him, they shouted, “Song Jingshuo!”","Everyone hurried over. When they saw the person he was dragging, those who knew him let out sighs of dismay.","Jiang Cheng asked, “Did you run into a zombie upstairs?”","“Already dealt with it,” Song Jingshuo replied.","“What kind of zombie?”","Song Jingshuo was slightly surprised by the question. “It should’ve been a second-generation one.”","As soon as he said it, he realized something too.","“Why was it a second-generation zombie?”","Everyone had only just woken up. There might even still be people who hadn’t woken up yet. So how had a second-generation zombie already appeared?","Li Jiangbing told him, “Things are bad now. They can mutate directly into second-generation zombies. And the one we just encountered had already evolved—it mutated directly into an evolved one. Ugh, that’s such a mouthful. Can’t we just call it a third-generation zombie?”","A lot of people agreed.","“Let’s call it a third-generation zombie.”","“I was already wondering whether that counted as the third generation.”","‘Third generation’ is easier to say.”","And so, without any official definition, the Youth Apartments took it upon themselves to name this newly emerged type of zombie a “third-generation zombie.”","Song Jingshuo dragged the person to an open area and released him. Then he told the people nearby, “Keep an eye on him.”","The group searched the courtyard but found no other zombies. They gathered around the injured man to guard against the possibility of him mutating.","He was covered in blood and kept his eyes open without blinking.","Su Yu couldn’t bear to watch. She went over and knelt beside his head, asking him, “Do you have any last words? Is there anyone you want us to contact?”","Li Jiangbing said, “It’s no use. He can’t speak anymore.”","He tried to comfort Su Yu. “Forget it. There’s nothing we can do.”","Su Yu sighed and gave up.","She couldn’t help feeling that her heart was growing harder too. Maybe it was because she had seen too many dead people.","Someone shouted, “Zombie!”","Everyone turned to look. Sure enough, a zombie had emerged from one of the buildings. The crowd immediately swarmed toward it.","Li Jiangbing grabbed Su Yu. “Don’t go with everyone else. The two of us will stay here and watch him.”","The noise coming from the courtyard was probably especially conspicuous in the current environment.","The residential area was separated from the technology park by some distance, with a river between them, so the neighborhood was unusually quiet at this hour.","There weren’t even the piercing car alarms caused by the chain-reaction accidents in the city. It was simply silent.","As a result, everyone’s shouts and cries rang out particularly loudly.","It seemed that the noise had drawn the zombies out of the buildings.","Song Jingshuo and Jiang Cheng didn’t move either. There were already enough people rushing over.","Song Jingshuo asked Jiang Cheng, “How many zombies do you think there could be?”","“Not many,” Jiang Cheng said. “Not that many people came back in the first place.”","Song Jingshuo sounded regretful. “If only we had official data.”","He really wanted to know the mutation rate from the previous outbreak.","But the authorities had never released any figures—not even the death toll, let alone data like the mutation rate, which would have been even harder to verify.","The noise in the courtyard attracted the zombies inside the buildings.","Although second-generation zombies were more agile than the original zombies, they still hadn’t developed intelligence. When they were drawn by sound, they didn’t open the doors and come downstairs. Instead, they simply smashed through the windows and jumped.","One second-generation zombie jumped from the tenth floor.","Even a second-generation zombie with extraordinary jumping ability couldn’t withstand a fall from that height. It slammed into the ground, likely shattering its bones, and could no longer get up. It writhed helplessly on the pavement.","The others went over and chopped off its head.","Someone even made a point of running back to tell Jiang Cheng, “It was a second-generation one, not a third-generation one.”","Jiang Cheng nodded.","Then he asked Song Jingshuo, “Do you think they’ll continue evolving after the third generation?”","Just imagining it made Song Jingshuo’s skin crawl. “Don’t jinx us.”","Jiang Cheng watched as everyone charged toward another newly emerged zombie in the distance. “I’m only wondering—why shouldn’t this be considered the evolution of a species?”","Faster. Stronger.","The previous weakness had been their lack of intelligence. The appearance of the third generation had clearly repaired that shortcoming.","As for their thirst for blood and flesh—humans had once developed from a stage of eating raw meat and drinking blood themselves.","That was simply how nature worked.","Even in a civilized society, people no longer ate raw flesh or drank blood directly, but they had merely found another way to consume them.","That was the law governing the world.","Song Jingshuo’s face was tense. “I don’t accept this kind of ‘evolution,’ and I don’t think it’s ‘evolution.’ Humanity spent tens of thousands of years building the civilization we have today. If this is what ‘evolution’ looks like, then why did we bother standing upright in the first place? Why did we learn to make fire, cook, and eat cooked food?”","He said, “At most, this is aberration. It absolutely isn’t evolution.”","Jiang Cheng shot him a glance.","Song Jingshuo said, “...If you have something to say, just say it.”","They had been through life and death together. There was nothing they couldn’t say to each other directly.","Jiang Cheng sighed. “I didn’t expect you to have such proper values.”","Song Jingshuo: “...”","So, in Jiang Cheng’s mind, had he always been someone with twisted values?","As dusk fell, more and more people gathered in the courtyard. They made plenty of noise, drawing out quite a few zombies, which they promptly dealt with.","They were all primitive zombies and second-generation zombies.","The person Li Jiangbing and Su Yu had been guarding finally breathed his last and then mutated. Li Jiangbing took care of him.","Song Jingshuo let out a sigh of relief. “Looks like there aren’t that many third-generation zombies.”","When it came to jinxing things, Song Jingshuo was the real deal.","The moment he finished speaking, a window in Building Three shattered with a crash. Two zombies, tangled together, fell from above and hit the ground with a tremendous bang.","One of them was especially enormous.","Everyone was startled.","He Tian licked between her fingers, cleaning them completely.","It still wasn’t enough. She wanted more. She knew she had to get out, so she opened the door and stepped into the hallway.","The corridor stretched a long way. She followed it to the elevator lobby, knowing that she had to go down from there.","She pried open the elevator doors with her hands. Inside was a pitch-black shaft, and a foul-smelling draft rose from below.","He Tian was just about to jump down when she heard a noise coming from somewhere else.","Following the sound, she entered the stairwell.","She lived on a high floor, and the sound was coming from below.","With several powerful leaps, she descended several floors at once. Soon, she saw the source of the noise.","A huge, fat, disgusting body.","It was someone she hated very much—Nie Kuizhang.","There had been many times when He Tian had thought, I really want to kill that disgusting bastard Nie Kuizhang.","But back then, it had only been an emotional outburst. Killing someone had been impossible.","But now, when Nie Kuizhang raised his head with blood and flesh filling his mouth, and the two of them met each other’s eyes, He Tian thought:","I can.","I can kill him.","Kill him.","He Tian leaped into the air and pounced on Nie Kuizhang.","The two of them fought as they tumbled down several flights of stairs, crashing into the corridor. Still locked in combat, they smashed through the glass at the end of the hallway and fell together.","Below them was the canopy over the building’s entrance.","With a loud crack, the canopy could not withstand Nie Kuizhang’s enormous body and the force of the fall. It collapsed beneath them.","The commotion startled everyone.","A male zombie and a female zombie sprang out of the wreckage, then immediately tore into each other again.","Primitive attacks—claw-like hands, teeth, and heads smashing into one another.","They tried to bite through each other’s throats, wrench off each other’s arms, and crush each other’s skulls.","No one had ever seen two zombies attack each other before. Everyone was stunned.","Someone shouted, “Nie Kuizhang! That’s Nie Kuizhang!”","Nie Kuizhang’s distinctive build made him easy to recognize.","But most people couldn’t tell who the female zombie was. Her hair hung loose, always covering her face, and her movements were too fast. On top of that, dusk had deepened, while the streetlights had yet to come on, making it impossible to see clearly.","Only Su Yu’s expression changed drastically.","She rushed forward, but Jiang Cheng was quick enough to grab her by the arm.","He had recognized who the girl was.","Su Yu turned around, her voice hoarse and trembling. “He Tian... It’s He Tian!”","Gao Yuxuan quietly told Zhao Yi, “It’s the girl who walked the little dog.”","Zhao Yi stared for a moment, then said with certainty, “They’re both third-generation zombies!”","He Tian let out a ferocious howl that sounded nothing like a human cry.","Nie Kuizhang tried to escape.","Back when they had both been human, He Tian and Nie Kuizhang had been on completely different levels.","Nie Kuizhang could have shoved He Tian to the ground with one blow and left her unable to get back up.","But Nie Kuizhang was not a strongman like Li Jiangbing, who had built his body through hard work and sweat.","Nie Kuizhang was simply tall and naturally big. Because his body mass was so immense, he had considerable strength as well.","But he did not possess the kind of powerful physique forged through the high-intensity training and drills of a soldier. After mutation, he was not on the same level as an ordinary zombie.","At the end of the day, he was still just an ordinary person.","After mutating into a zombie, his cells underwent a comprehensive transformation at the genetic level.","His speed and strength were greatly enhanced.","Under this kind of enhancement, the differences between ordinary people were leveled out.","He Tian was not at a disadvantage.","In fact, with the same jumping ability, He Tian’s lighter and more agile body gave her the upper hand. Nie Kuizhang’s attacks missed her again and again. His massive weight, rather than benefiting him after mutation, had become nothing but a burden.","He failed to dodge He Tian’s attacks several times, and he grew visibly more agitated, roaring loudly as well.","He Tian bit down on Nie Kuizhang’s ear and tore it off. He threw a punch that struck her shoulder and sent her flying, then turned and tried to run.","But He Tian’s desire to kill him had been strengthened along with her genes. With a roar, she sprang into the air, pounced onto Nie Kuizhang’s back, and sent them both rolling into the bushes.","The animalistic roar from the bushes suddenly cut off.","Everyone froze.","The next instant, the streetlights, set on an automatic timer, suddenly flickered on.","A figure leaped up from the bushes in the darkness of the night.","She was slender, with long hair, and her delicate features could still be seen.","But her skin and eyes had mutated beyond recognition.","In her hand, she held a human head.","A massive head twisted off its body.","He Tian had delivered the killing blow to Nie Kuizhang."]},{"number":90,"title":"Chapter 90","paragraphs":["Vice Mayor Sun sat in the corridor, his back against the wall.","One of his arms had been chewed to a bloody mess. The zombie that had bitten him was drawn away by someone else and left him alone.","Several zombies ran past him without paying any attention, not even glancing at him.","Vice Mayor Sun understood now. Once the virus entered a person’s body, the rate of infection varied from person to person. But as soon as the virus had assimilated someone, the zombies already regarded that “person” as one of their own and stopped attacking—even if the person had not yet mutated.","He watched the people running and screaming through the broad corridor, the people fighting desperately, the people sobbing in despair.","Then he stood up.","The wall had built-in display cabinets. Their glass had shattered and lay scattered across the floor.","Vice Mayor Sun bent down and picked up a fallen trophy. It was made of artificial crystal—heavy and hard. Shaped like a torch, thick at the top and narrow at the bottom, it was perfect for gripping.","Vice Mayor Sun turned around with the trophy in hand and smashed the head of a first-generation zombie.","Then he killed a second-generation zombie that had pinned one of his colleagues to the ground and was tearing into him.","The zombie collapsed to one side. Half of the colleague’s face had been bitten away. His whole body trembled as he rasped, “Help... help...”","Vice Mayor Sun looked at his wounds and said nothing. He raised the trophy high.","Then he crushed the man’s head as well.","That way, he couldn’t turn into a zombie.","One less was still one less.","Taking advantage of the fact that he had already been infected, Vice Mayor Sun did everything he could to kill as many zombies as possible.","But his strength was pitifully weak.","The entire government building had become a living hell.","When he saw Vice Mayor Zheng mutate into a first-generation zombie and stagger past him in pursuit of a clerk, the trophy slipped from his hand.","Despairing tears streamed down his face.","Mayor... Mayor, we’re finished...","The government was finished.","S City was finished.","The country was finished.","Humanity—and this world—was finished.","Youth Apartments, courtyard.","Night had fallen, and the streetlamps had come on.","The lights inside the complex were meant to create an atmosphere rather than illuminate the area. They were not very bright, casting everything in a hazy glow.","If one ignored the bluish face and the blood-soaked human head dangling from the girl’s hand, she might even have looked beautiful standing among the shrubs.","“He Tian...”","Su Yu’s voice trembled faintly.","She took a step forward. Jiang Cheng released her arm.","“He Tian, it’s me.” Su Yu slowly walked toward her. “It’s me. I’m Su Yu...”","No one stopped her.","He Tian had attacked Nie Kuizhang because he had harassed her in the past. Even after becoming a zombie, she still remembered her grudge. That meant she retained a certain degree of memory and intelligence.","She was the third-generation zombie everyone had just named.","She had broken free from the instinct to do nothing but crave fresh flesh. She seemed to be a new kind of zombie—one that had developed intelligence.","Everyone wanted to know just how much intelligence this new third-generation zombie possessed. Could she still behave as she had when she was alive? Could she communicate?","Someone had voluntarily taken the first step forward, which suited everyone’s intentions perfectly.","Only Li Jiangbing reached out to stop her, but Song Jingshuo held him back.","“Let her try,” Song Jingshuo said quietly. “Someone has to try eventually. The sooner, the better.”","Li Jiangbing understood that this was in everyone’s interests. Sooner or later, someone would have to test her.","All he could do was watch anxiously, his weapon clutched tightly in his hand.","Everyone watched as Su Yu drew closer, step by step.","Her voice was gentle as well. “It’s me. Do you remember me?”","“What about Fu Duoduo? Did you leave it at home?”","“How do you feel right now? Does it hurt?”","“He Tian, put Nie Kuizhang down.” Su Yu continued forward. “I know you hate him. He’s already dead. Let him go...”","Some people around them looked uncomfortable.","It was no secret that Nie Kuizhang had harassed He Tian. Many people knew about it.","But it was difficult for men to empathize with a girl over something like that. Most of them thought the punishment Nie Kuizhang had received was appropriate—more than enough.","Some would even say, “He didn’t really do anything. He only touched her once.”","They could never imagine how deeply girls might loathe such a thing—so deeply that even after turning into a zombie, He Tian still had to twist Nie Kuizhang’s head off.","Oh dear. Oh dear.","He Tian suddenly released her grip, and the head dropped onto the lawn.","Su Yu’s eyes lit up.","If third-generation zombies could communicate, then...","A glimmer of hope flared in many people’s hearts.","Of course, some also felt afraid. If a monster had gained intelligence, wouldn’t that make it even more terrifying?","Su Yu’s courage grew. She continued walking toward He Tian.","“He—”","Li Jiangbing’s greatest fear still came true!","In an instant, He Tian sprang forward and pounced on Su Yu. She wrapped her arms around Su Yu and opened her mouth to bite her in the face!","Zombies were mutated humans. When attacking people their own size, they naturally targeted the face, neck, and shoulders—the areas most vulnerable to being bitten and torn apart during a fight.","The armor protected the shoulders. A shell-shaped collar rose at the back, covering the back of the head, neck, and ears.","But the face was left unprotected.","Cries of alarm erupted all around them.","For that brief moment, everyone thought Su Yu was finished.","Su Yu herself thought so too. When the stench washed over her and both her arms were pinned, she truly believed she was going to die.","But Su Yu did not want to die!","She had put on the armor and picked up a weapon because she wanted to become stronger.","She wanted to protect herself, not hide behind others and be protected.","She wanted to control her own fate. She even dreamed of becoming strong enough to protect other people!","How could she die just like this?","Her desperate will to survive exploded inside her mind.","Ever since she had awakened, there had been a spot in her head that kept throbbing with a sharp, needle-like pain.","At that instant, the point of pain erupted—and activated.","Li Jiangbing shouted and charged forward to save Su Yu, but Su Yu and He Tian had already fallen to the ground together.","Everyone imagined that the two of them would roll around in a tangled struggle on the ground. Even if everyone rushed over and killed the zombie, Su Yu would be finished as well—most likely left with a face covered in blood.","But things did not happen as they expected.","At the instant Su Yu and He Tian hit the ground, the two of them suddenly began to shine.","As the light flared, He Tian was blasted away!","Everyone surged forward. Li Jiangbing rushed up and brought his spiked club down on her head, killing He Tian.","Li Jiangbing took two deep breaths. He glanced at He Tian’s lifeless body, his heart filled with regret.","He had known He Tian too.","To avoid Nie Kuizhang, He Tian had often stayed with Su Yu. Since Su Yu lived in Building Two, she naturally stayed with Li Jiangbing as well.","That was how they had gradually become familiar with one another.","In Li Jiangbing’s heart, Su Yu and He Tian had both been wonderful girls.","They were brave and hardworking, never hiding behind others. They actively participated in every group operation.","During that little more than a month, Li Jiangbing—known as “Li,” the man who could practically swagger through the entire complex—had enjoyed a few small privileges.","It was not as though no girls had tried to curry favor with him in hopes of gaining some convenience.","But although Li Jiangbing had less education than most of them, he had far more experience in the rough world than the majority of his peers in the complex. Every time, he had fended them off with a false smile.","Whenever he had a few resources to spare, he preferred to give them to girls like Su Yu and He Tian—girls who were always in front of him and actively took part in all kinds of volunteer work.","A flicker of emotion passed through Li Jiangbing’s heart, and he immediately turned to look at Su Yu.","Jiang Cheng and Song Jingshuo also stepped forward. Everyone gathered around Su Yu, staring at her in amazement.","Su Yu sat on the ground, just as bewildered as everyone else—","A small dome of pale, shimmering light had appeared around her.","A few seconds later, the dome dimmed and vanished.","But it had truly existed, and everyone had seen it. It was that dome of light that had flared up and knocked He Tian away the instant she hugged Su Yu.","Li Jiangbing crouched down beside her. “Look up!”","Su Yu did as he said, exposing her neck while Li Jiangbing examined both sides. She also held out her hands for him to inspect.","Li Jiangbing let out a huge sigh of relief. He reached out and pulled Su Yu to her feet, announcing, “No injuries! Not even a scratch!”","The crowd immediately began firing questions at her.","“What just happened?”","“What the heck was that?”","“You all saw it too, right? I’m not imagining things?”","“We saw it.”","Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan exchanged a glance. Neither could quite suppress the smiles tugging at their lips, and their eyes shone with excited anticipation.","Li Jiangbing gave a chuckle and said to Su Yu, “Good thing you have a superpower too.”","Su Yu still had no idea what was going on. After the white dome disappeared, her head began to ache. Enduring the pain, she asked, “What are you talking about?”","Li Jiangbing said, “Wasn’t that your superpower just now?”","Li Jiangbing and Jiang Cheng had not yet had a chance to discuss the matter of superpowers in detail. But now that Su Yu’s ability had been revealed in front of everyone, it first proved that they were not the only ones with superpowers. Second, there was no longer any point in keeping the matter secret.","Li Jiangbing called out loudly, “Who woke up and discovered they had a superpower? Stop hiding it and tell everyone.”","Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan exchanged another glance, then raised their hands together.","“Oh?” Li Jiangbing was delighted. “You two?”","They were both people he knew. Excellent.","But many in the crowd had no idea what they were talking about. Someone asked, “What are you talking about?”","Apparently, not everyone had a superpower.","Gao Yuxuan said, “This.”","He raised one finger, focused, and exerted himself. A tiny current of electricity formed at his fingertip.","The light was faint, but in the darkness of night, it was especially clear.","Various sounds rose from the crowd—gasps of surprise, confused questions, and exclamations of admiration.","Li Jiangbing asked Zhao Yi, “What about you?”","Zhao Yi glanced around, then walked onto the grass. He did not need to touch anything with his hands; his feet were already planted on the ground, and he was close enough.","He concentrated and gathered his strength. With a whoosh, the soil in front of him surged upward, forming a small mound about knee-high.","Sweat appeared on Zhao Yi’s forehead from the effort.","Li Jiangbing asked, “Anyone else? Don’t hide it. Sooner or later, everyone’s going to find out.”","A few more people gradually raised their hands.","Among the people he knew, Wu Jiancheng could control fire. But he needed a source of flame. He first used a lighter to ignite a small flame, then, just as Li Jiangbing controlled water, manipulated it into a tiny fireball that rolled across his palm.","Cui Haiyang raised the steel pipe in his hand. In full view of the crowd, the perfectly straight pipe bent. However, restoring the L-shaped pipe to its original form left Cui Haiyang utterly exhausted.","Li Jiangbing asked Su Yu, “What would you call yours?”","Su Yu had no idea either and could not answer.","Zhao Yi cut in, “A protective barrier! It’s insanely awesome!”","When Gao Yuxuan woke up, he touched one of the electrical appliances in his home and immediately realized he had a special ability. Zhao Yi had flowers growing at home; he had gone over to the window to check what was happening downstairs, touched a flowerpot, and discovered his own ability.","When two guys obsessed with anime and manga run into something like this, what’s their first reaction?","Of course, they called each other!","“I’ve got superpowers!”","“Holy crap, me too!!”"]},{"number":91,"title":"Chapter 91","paragraphs":["A nerd like Zhao Yi usually didn’t like drawing attention to himself.","But this time was different.","Superpowers! It didn’t get any more anime than that.","Actually, after the first zombie crisis ended, Zhao Yi had said to Gao Yuxuan, “Looking back on those two months, it was basically like living in a horror-action anime.”","“Song Jingshuo can be the protagonist.”","“Jiang Cheng is obviously the heroine.”","“Jiangbing has to be the second male lead, at least.”","“You and me? Extras?”","“Li Feng? Li Feng is the cannon fodder who drives the romance between the male and female leads forward. Though it feels like he didn’t quite do his job. He didn’t push things along very much.”","Now, just when everything seemed to have returned to normal, he had suddenly received a warning from the heroine—no, from Jiang Cheng. The sense of destiny was simply too strong.","Zhao Yi had believed Jiang Cheng without hesitation.","Then, after waking up, he accidentally touched a flowerpot, sensed something, and discovered that he had gained the superpower to control soil.","Zhao Yi seriously began to wonder whether he was living in some kind of anime.","Everything about this was just too anime-like.","Since this was an anime world, it fell within Zhao Yi’s area of expertise.","“So now we have metal, water, earth, fire, electricity, and...” He paused. “The protective barrier counts as the mental type, I guess.”","Li Jiangbing didn’t understand. “What type?”","“The five elements: metal, wood, water, fire, and earth,” Zhao Yi explained. “Look, the only one we’re missing now is wood. Gao Yuxuan and Su Yu have special abilities.”","That explanation was much easier to understand.","In short, everyone now knew what was happening. After waking from this latest bout of unconsciousness, some people had become zombies, while others had directly become second- or even third-generation zombies. Among those who had not turned into zombies, some had suddenly gained superpowers.","What Li Jiangbing called “special abilities” didn’t sound nearly as cool or impressive as Zhao Yi’s “superpowers,” so everyone automatically chose the latter.","Li Jiangbing also thought “superpowers” sounded better, and happily accepted the term.","He glanced at Jiang Cheng.","According to Zhao Yi’s explanation, her ability fell into the special category.","But Jiang Cheng had remained silent and hadn’t raised her hand. Li Jiangbing guessed that she might not want to talk about it. Although he appeared careless and straightforward, he was actually very considerate. If Jiang Cheng didn’t say anything, he wouldn’t speak for her.","Fortunately, Jiang Cheng spoke up at that moment. “So mine would count as a special ability too.”","Everyone turned to look at her.","Jiang Cheng had already thought it through. She wasn’t an ordinary member of the group who could easily keep a low profile. She had always been the leader of the Young People’s Apartments—last time, and this time as well. She was someone everyone watched. Sooner or later, they would find out.","Rather than being discovered later and earning the negative impression of “keeping secrets,” thereby losing everyone’s trust, she would be honest now.","Of course the destined heroine would have a superpower!","Zhao Yi’s and Gao Yuxuan’s eyes lit up. “What’s your superpower?”","Jiang Cheng raised the fire ax in her hand. It was still the same fire ax she had always used. After the zombie crisis ended, the bus company had taken back its four large buses, and the two forklifts they had bought from Duoduomai had been returned as well. All those shopping carts had gone back too.","But she had kept the fire ax.","Like Song Jingshuo’s weapon, it had been sharpened before she put it away.","The fire ax vanished into thin air.","As everyone stared in astonishment, it reappeared in Jiang Cheng’s hand.","Gao Yuxuan and Zhao Yi became so excited that one punched the air while the other jabbed his finger repeatedly at empty space. It took several seconds before Zhao Yi could finally speak.","“Spatial ability! Right? It’s a spatial ability, isn’t it?”","“Yes.” Jiang Cheng explained it to everyone. “I have a space where I can store things. But it’s not very large—just a small one.”","The demonstrations everyone had just given made it clear that none of their superpowers were particularly strong. Even Su Yu’s protective barrier had lasted for only a very short time, and her reaction clearly showed that using it had probably given her a headache. She had been frowning and rubbing her temples the whole time.","There was too much information to take in all at once. Everyone began buzzing with conversation and discussion, needing time to understand and absorb it all.","Li Jiangbing turned his head and looked Song Jingshuo up and down.","Song Jingshuo said irritably, “I don’t have one.”","“No?” Li Jiangbing asked, disappointed.","He had hoped that all his acquaintances would have superpowers.","Song Jingshuo wasn’t happy either.","Although everyone’s superpowers appeared weak and useless at the moment, this might only be the beginning.","Take the original zombies, for example. Their limbs had initially been uncoordinated, but now the third-generation zombies had developed intelligence. It wasn’t very high intelligence, but at least they had reached the level of knowing to run home when it rained.","The word “evolution” surfaced in his mind.","Yes, if they had to call it evolution, he could never agree that becoming a zombie was evolution.","But humans gaining superpowers was unquestionably a form of evolution.","Had he been abandoned by this evolution because he didn’t have a superpower?","Su Yu was standing right beside Li Jiangbing and heard their exchange.","She hesitated, then said, “Actually... until just now, I didn’t even know I had a superpower.”","Several people nearby stopped what they were doing and listened to her.","Su Yu continued, “It suddenly burst out just now. I was completely confused myself.”","Li Jiangbing said, “I felt mine after touching the water.”","Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan had likewise come into contact with the substances corresponding to their abilities.","Once the three of them had said that, those without superpowers couldn’t help discussing it among themselves.","“Then do we still have hope?”","Jiang Cheng spoke up.","Every time she said something, she could silence the entire crowd at once.","“Don’t worry about the superpowers for now,” Jiang Cheng said. “Go back and slowly try to sense them. Maybe you’ll have one tomorrow.”","“For now, let’s clear the buildings.”","Right, right. Everyone had experience with this.","The courtyard appeared to be free of zombies, but there could still be some inside the buildings. They had to clear out their living space first.","Jiang Cheng took out her phone and dialed a number. “Let’s go to the property-management office and get the intercoms first.”","No one answered the property-management office’s phone, which was only to be expected. Master Luo and Yang Xinyan had both received Jiang Cheng’s text messages, and Master Luo had even met with Jiang Cheng in person. He would certainly have evacuated the people from the property-management center.","Jiang Cheng called Master Luo next.","The call was answered quickly, but the voice on the other end didn’t belong to Master Luo. It was Aunt Pan.","“Hello, Little Jiang?”","Aunt Pan’s voice was lower than usual, yet very calm.","But Jiang Cheng’s heart sank. After a brief pause, she asked, “Is Master Luo still there?”","The people around her fell silent.","Aunt Pan said softly, “He’s gone. I took care of it.”","Jiang Cheng replied, “Oh.” Then, apologetically, she said, “My condolences.”","She added, “Don’t come out yet. It’s safer inside. We’ll clear the buildings shortly. We’ll talk once it’s safe.”","Aunt Pan murmured, “Mm,” and the two ended the call.","Aunt Pan hadn’t even turned on the lights.","When she woke up, it had still been daytime—brighter even than that purple-gray, heavily overcast afternoon.","Following Jiang Cheng’s instructions, they returned to Apartment 0308.","A few of the unoccupied apartments in the complex had indeed been claimed by relatives who came looking for them. But no relatives of Little White’s Dad had ever appeared, so Master Luo and his wife were still living in Apartment 0308.","Master Luo said to her, “We have to isolate ourselves separately. How about this? You stay outside, and I’ll stay in the bathroom.”","Master Luo was meticulous and good with his hands. He stretched a strip of tape across the doorframe at a low height, turning it into a tripwire.","“If you mutate, I’ll open the door from inside. When you charge in, you’ll trip over it, and I’ll, well... take care of you.”","“And if I mutate, you’ll open the door from outside. I’ll trip over it when I rush out, so hurry up and deal with me. Don’t hesitate, no matter what.”","Aunt Pan agreed. “You still don’t trust me? I can kill zombies outside without even blinking.”","Aunt Pan was a manual laborer. If Zhao Yi got into a fight with her, it would honestly be hard to say who would win.","In any case, they had set up a little trap.","When she woke up, she went to knock on the bathroom door. The sound that came from inside made her heart sink.","Master Luo had mutated into a primitive zombie. He didn’t know how to open the door.","Aunt Pan cried outside for a long time. At last, she tightened her grip on the steel pipe, pressed herself against the wall beside the door, and reached out to twist the handle.","Everything went exactly as they had agreed.","If he changed, she would deal with him. If she changed, he would deal with her. The husband and wife would handle it themselves and spare everyone else the trouble.","The tripwire worked just as they had hoped.","Master Luo charged out and immediately tripped. The bathroom opened onto the entryway, with a wall directly opposite.","His forehead slammed straight into the wall, leaving his body at an angle.","Aunt Pan gritted her teeth and brought the steel pipe down...","They would handle their own affairs and spare everyone else the trouble.","When people dealt with zombies, it was usually fine if the zombie was a stranger—or even someone they merely recognized. Their hearts had been hardened by practice.","But it was still painful when the zombie was someone familiar.","Li Jiangbing and the others had worked together to kill He Tian and the rest, but they hadn’t been troubled by it because they didn’t know He Tian.","Su Yu, however, had suffered because He Tian had been her friend.","Li Jiangbing was saddened too, because He Tian had been someone he knew and even liked.","As for Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan, they felt only the regret and pity one might have for a complete stranger.","Now Master Luo was gone, and quite a few people were upset.","Jiang Cheng, Li Jiangbing, and Cui Haiyang were especially affected.","Everyone went to the property-management office.","The fully armored group led the way, with U-shaped forks held out in front of them as they proceeded with extreme caution.","But the property-management office was deserted.","The property manager had decided not to go home that day. Making fun of Jiang Cheng had only been an excuse; the real reason was that he simply didn’t want to go home and help his child with homework.","He had plenty of empty apartments at his disposal. Many young white-collar workers had furnished their little homes beautifully, and some even had incredibly expensive mattresses that were wonderfully comfortable to sleep on.","After the finance clerk left too, the manager found an apartment with a good bed and a computer. He slept on someone else’s bed and played games on someone else’s computer.","He was having a wonderful time.","That was, until he slumped out of his computer chair and collapsed unconscious on the floor. When he woke up again, he heard the commotion in the courtyard. He crawled to the window and took a look.","The sky had fallen.","The warning from Jiang Cheng in Building Two, Apartment 0306, had actually been true!","Everyone retrieved walkie-talkies from the property-management center.","Jiang Cheng also made an announcement over the radio:","“All surviving residents, we are beginning a building-by-building sweep. Residents without armor or protective equipment should stay inside and avoid coming out if possible. At nine tomorrow morning, all surviving residents are to gather at the small plaza and report in.”","They would get everything done in one go, so they wouldn’t have to make another trip later."]},{"number":92,"title":"Chapter 92","paragraphs":["The second outbreak of the zombie virus came on a weekday afternoon, and the results were far more devastating than the first outbreak, which had occurred on a weekend night.","Government offices across the country were almost completely wiped out.","The reason was that government buildings tended to share the same characteristics: they were tall, spacious, and interconnected, with large numbers of people packed inside.","Hospitals were even worse.","If even Renxin Hospital in the Technology New District had been overrun with zombies, then the large hospitals in the city—with hundreds of people crammed into a single department—were beyond saving.","Patients waiting to be seen were packed into the corridors, and anyone trying to pass through had to say, “Excuse me,” or “Coming through.”","Universities, by contrast, suffered relatively little damage.","The first outbreak had already inflicted such heavy losses on them that few survivors remained. So many students had died. The students who had survived were still undergoing psychological treatment this month.","In fact, even the psychologists could not be sure they themselves weren’t already insane. They had to force themselves to remain calm while providing counseling to others.","Many universities had suspended classes, leaving their campuses empty.","This time, primary and secondary schools were among the hardest-hit areas.","Office buildings and shopping malls were also major disaster zones.","Restaurants fared somewhat better. At that hour, many had only just finished their afternoon break and were preparing to open for business. The evening crowds had not yet arrived.","But there was one place that was a disaster zone within a disaster zone: military barracks.","Jiang Cheng had declared during the previous outbreak that military camps would inevitably become major disaster zones. Later, the facts proved her right.","The government never announced exactly how many soldiers the military had lost, but the painfully slow advance of the troops sent afterward to rescue the cities made it obvious just how severely understaffed the army had become.","Jiang Cheng had even predicted that zombies transformed from soldiers—whose physical abilities far surpassed those of ordinary people—would be much stronger than ordinary zombies.","Everyone agreed with that assessment, but without experiencing it firsthand, it was difficult to imagine just how true it was.","Li Feng had never expected to live through a second outbreak in this lifetime.","This time, people had far more experience than before.","During the previous outbreak, no one had known that injuries would lead to infection, so everyone had fought alone.","This time, many people stood back-to-back, guarding against zombies sneaking up behind them.","Even so, many who had failed to form up with their comrades in time were left isolated.","Li Feng was one of them.","He roared as he swung a folding metal stool, knocking a zombie flying to one side.","When the virus erupted again, they had been holding an outdoor assembly. Everyone had been given one folding metal stool.","Those stools had become the weapons in Li Feng’s hands—and the only weapons available.","Weapons were actually difficult to obtain inside a military camp. Guns and ammunition were kept under strict control in the armory. Every requisition required documentation and approval, and two people had to operate the system together before anything could be issued.","Cold weapons were considered auxiliary equipment and were also stored in the armory.","At that moment, setting aside whether anyone could even fight their way across such a large military district to reach the armory, even if they got there, they would not be able to find the two people holding the keys to open its double locks.","They could only use whatever happened to be in their hands.","A heavy blow came from a familiar comrade.","The metal stool flew from Li Feng’s grasp.","Without a weapon, fighting a zombie hand-to-hand meant that even the smallest wound would eventually lead to death.","Li Feng no longer cared. His heart was filled with fury.","This world belonged to humanity. These monsters should never have appeared, much less attempted to destroy mankind.","“Go to hell!”","Li Feng roared and swung his fist.","He knew that the punch would certainly leave him injured. He knew he would be infected. He knew he would die.","Too many people had died since the previous outbreak.","Li Feng had been driven beyond the limits of his anger.","Ever since he had woken up, there had been a spot in his head that throbbed with a needle-like pain. In that instant, his rage ignited that painful point.","It erupted.","It activated.","A vast, searing heat seeped out from within his cells.","Roaring flames sprang up around Li Feng’s fists!","The terrifying part was not merely the size of the flames, but their temperature.","His blazing iron fist slammed into the side of the zombie’s head, sending it flying sideways. In the same instant, the flames engulfed its skull, scorching its eyeballs.","They bored through its nostrils and ears, drilling into its brain.","Even through the skull, the flames burned its brain.","A zombie that would not react even if its arms or legs were severed let out a shrill, agonized howl.","Li Feng had no time to concern himself with the flames on his fists. He leaped forward, tackled the zombie, pinned it down, and hammered its head again and again.","He did not stop until the zombie’s face had been charred black, its brain reduced to carbon inside its skull, and its body had ceased moving completely.","Only then did Li Feng finally stop. He raised his hand and stared at the flames burning around his fists.","The fists wrapped in fire were completely uninjured.","He had no idea what was happening, but he knew that this was his weapon.","Throughout the military camp, ability users awakened and activated their powers when faced with life-or-death situations.","An electric-type ability user sent a current through a zombie’s eyeball and straight into its brain.","A metal-type ability user transformed the metal stool in his hand into a long spike.","A earth-type ability user raised a mound of earth in a moment of crisis, using it as a barrier to block a fatal strike from a zombie.","Unfortunately, when a water-type ability user instinctively created a ball of water to block a zombie’s attack, the attack pierced straight through it. The zombie’s claws sank directly into the ability user’s throat.","Blood sprayed everywhere.","If the people in the Youth Apartment had witnessed the strength of these abilities, they would certainly have been stunned.","Compared with these abilities, the tiny flames, little water balls, weak electric currents, and small mounds of earth in the Youth Apartment were like the difference between an adult and a child.","Ordinary people and soldiers were simply on entirely different levels.","The metal-type ability user gritted his teeth and endured the needle-like pain in his brain, melting one metal stool after another into iron spikes and throwing them to his comrades.","Once the survivors had such offensive weapons in their hands, their combat power immediately soared.","The metal-type ability user was exhausting himself far too quickly. Blood began to flow from his eyes, nostrils, and ears.","But he never stopped.","Every time he used his ability, another comrade received a weapon.","He continued until several people returned from the combat engineers’ equipment room carrying engineer shovels.","Engineer shovels were not classified as weapons, but as tools and equipment, so they were stored in the equipment room.","Everyone knew, however, that military engineer shovels could easily be used as cold weapons.","With long spikes and engineer shovels in hand, the survivors finally no longer had to focus solely on defense. They roared and charged toward the zombies.","The metal-type ability user had exceeded the limits his body could withstand the very first time he used his power.","Something in his brain could no longer support the strain.","It burst.","The ability user collapsed to the ground, bleeding from all seven orifices. He died a heroic death.","The tide of battle turned.","The third-generation zombies did not lack any sense of life and death like the original zombies and second-generation zombies. When they realized that the humans outnumbered the zombies and that the situation could no longer be reversed, they began fleeing one after another.","The surviving soldiers wiped out the second-generation and original zombies.","The battle was shorter than the previous zombie-virus outbreak.","In reality, during the first outbreak, the zombies that had just awakened were all original zombies, so the initial clash ended quickly.","But at that time, no one knew that injuries would result in infection. The real battle only began when large numbers of wounded soldiers started transforming.","People were injured one after another.","People transformed one after another.","At last, someone realized the root of the problem: the zombie virus was transmitted through blood.","After dealing with the zombies, the survivors turned the blades of their engineer shovels toward their wounded comrades.","It was agonizing. It was helpless.","But no one had a better choice.","At last, the armory was opened, and they got their hands on the guns. Ending their comrades’ lives with firearms caused far less suffering than using cold weapons.","None of the wounded resisted. They closed their eyes.","Tears streaming down his face, Li Feng pulled the trigger, shooting each wounded comrade in the head.","He continued until every wounded soldier had been executed.","It was simpler and more brutal than when the Youth Apartment had herded the wounded into the conference room and sealed them inside.","But it was the most effective method.","It stopped new zombies from being created.","The surviving soldiers assembled and took stock of the situation.","Then they discovered that there were no senior officers left. The highest-ranking survivor was only a major.","The major said, “Contact our superiors immediately.”","At this critical moment, the country needed them. Even though they had just endured a battle that had drained them physically, they had to establish contact with the government at once.","There were not many surviving officers, and Li Feng was one of them.","The soldiers dealt with the bodies outside while the officers tried to contact their superiors from the battalion headquarters office.","But they couldn’t get through.","They called one number after another. The officers kept making calls, working their way up the chain of command.","No one answered.","The officers grew increasingly desperate.","The calls had already reached the capital, even the central government, yet still... there was no response.","The major held the receiver, his face blank with confusion.","Everyone looked at one another, bewilderment written across every face.","Even during the previous zombie crisis, the battalion headquarters had quickly managed to contact surviving senior officers, who had then swiftly reached their own superiors.","That crisis had happened on a weekend evening.","Senior officers did not live on the military base, so many of them had survived.","But this time...","Was there no one left to lead them?","The people in the Youth Apartment had no idea that the soldiers’ supernatural abilities had erupted with such overwhelming force. They were still smugly celebrating their own little powers.","But someone as perceptive about survival as Li Jiangbing had already realized that something was wrong.","Other people could use fire, electricity, or even earth to attack or defend themselves. But what could his water do?","Everyone’s abilities were still weak, and most people had not thought that far yet. Li Jiangbing, however, had.","The excitement he had felt when he first discovered his supernatural ability was gone. A faint unease had begun to take root in his heart.","After obtaining walkie-talkies from the property management office, everyone prepared to search the buildings.","As usual, each team was responsible for its own building.","By now, only a few apartments in the complex still had their lights on. When everyone had awakened, it had still been daylight, and most people had already gone downstairs.","After the teams were divided by building, Su Yu saw that Building Two had enough people and called out to Li Jiangbing, “I’m going to Building Three.”","She added, “I need to check on Fu Duoduo.”","Li Jiangbing knew that Fu Duoduo was the little dog He Tian had raised. He had even once balanced the dog on his head and played with it.","“Go ahead, go ahead,” he said.","Then he warned her, “Stay with the others. Don’t go off on your own.”","Su Yu followed the people from Building Three.","Building Three was now without Nie Kuizhang, Peng Ze, and He Tian. They had formerly been the building manager and the residents who took the lead in organizing things.","The residents temporarily selected someone to serve as the building manager.","Su Yu joined them.","As before, they began searching from the top floor down. Su Yu did her part as best she could.","The supernatural ability she had awakened was a protective shield. Everyone still knew very little about it, but that did not stop them from thinking it was amazing.","Su Yu felt that people’s attitude toward her had subtly changed compared with before.","When they reached He Tian’s floor, Su Yu finally saw Fu Duoduo.","She had been thinking that, since He Tian was gone, she would adopt Fu Duoduo.","They had still been chatting through their messaging app before losing consciousness that day.","“If I mutate, come and put me out of my misery.”","That was the last message He Tian had sent her.","Su Yu still remembered the message she had sent just before that—","“I’ve locked Fu Duoduo in the bathroom. She can’t open the door. If I mutate, take her home and raise her.”","Su Yu stared at the blood-soaked bathroom.","Fur and an eyeball.","A bloody handprint on the toilet seat.","Tears streamed down Su Yu’s face.","He Tian had loved Fu Duoduo so much."]},{"number":93,"title":"Chapter 93","paragraphs":["This building sweep went much faster than the first one.","For one thing, everyone had become much more experienced. For another... there were now far fewer people in the complex than there were apartments.","Many units were empty when they knocked on every door on a floor.","The efficiency was astonishingly high.","When the team led by Li Jiangbing and Jiang Cheng knocked on a door in Building Two, the person peeking out at them turned out to be the property manager.","Everyone was startled.","“Manager Wang? What are you doing here?”","There was no way Manager Wang could admit that he had stayed behind just to see how Jiang Cheng would handle things. He put on a miserable expression and said, “That Miss Jiang sent out a warning, didn’t she? So I found an empty apartment to hide in.”","As he had expected, hardly anyone had returned to claim their apartments after the first wave of the zombie disaster.","The apartments weren’t going anywhere, while everyone had far too many other things to deal with. Some people had probably lost their entire families.","At first, Manager Wang had looked at all those empty apartments and planned to use them to run a few little side businesses and make some extra money. Who could have known that housing prices and rents would plummet? There weren’t even any tenants to be found.","In the end, he had only called over two relatives from his hometown who worked in S City and let them stay for free. At least that was better than the overcrowded rental they had been living in.","A few other apartments housed property staff and the people under Guo Jun.","The rest were all empty, and Manager Wang often picked one at random for his afternoon nap.","Now he poked his head out and looked left and right, as frightened as a startled bird.","“Are there zombies here? Are there still zombies in our building?”","“We’re sweeping the building,” Li Jiangbing said. “We just got to this floor.”","Jiang Cheng cut in. “Master Luo is dead.”","The hallway fell silent for a moment.","Manager Wang froze. He looked as though he wanted to cry.","Jiang Cheng cut off his emotions before they could gather any momentum. “Everyone is to report to the little square at nine tomorrow morning. We’ll take a head count. Tomorrow, you’ll organize the property staff. We’re still living here, after all. Some things can’t be left unattended.”","This girl was assigning him work just like that?","Who was she?","Yet not one person around them thought there was anything inappropriate about it. She spoke with such natural authority that everyone listened as if it were the most ordinary thing in the world.","Huh?","A sudden realization flashed through Manager Wang’s mind.","“Miss Jiang?”","Jiang Cheng nodded. “That’s right.”","So this was the “Miss Jiang” everyone had been talking about.","Jiang Cheng had been sent out on a business trip on her very first day back at work and had only returned today. To Manager Wang, she had been someone who existed solely in legend.","Liu Hongwang had been driven out by her and had not been heard from since. No one knew whether he was alive or dead.","She had locked up the people in the conference room and even ended up creating an evolved zombie.","Manager Wang had finally met her in person. The ruthless woman everyone talked about was actually so young and beautiful.","Jiang Cheng asked, “Do you have anything to eat?”","Manager Wang blinked. “What?”","Jiang Cheng handed him a box of strawberry pie. “This will tide you over for tonight. It isn’t safe outside right now, so don’t go wandering around. We’ll discuss the matter tomorrow.”","Manager Wang thought his eyes were playing tricks on him.","Where had she gotten it from? She wasn’t carrying a bag, and she was wearing armor. There was nowhere on her that looked capable of holding something like that.","Everyone marveled.","“That’s so convenient.”","“If it’s big enough, couldn’t she store a ton of stuff in there? That would make things so much easier.”","“Doesn’t she feel the weight?”","“Of course she doesn’t. They’re not even in the same dimension.”","Manager Wang: “???”","What were these people talking about?","Jiang Cheng said, “Some people have turned into zombies, while others have gained superpowers. We still don’t know how many people have abilities. You should investigate and see whether you have one yourself. We’re going to continue sweeping the building.”","The moment Jiang Cheng left, everyone followed after her in a rush.","Manager Wang was left standing there in total confusion.","After they finished sweeping the building, Li Jiangbing called Su Yu.","“Are you done? I’ll come pick you up.”","Although they had killed all the zombies visible in the courtyard, it was already dark. They couldn’t conduct a thorough search, so there was no guarantee that the area was completely safe.","Su Yu said, “I’m wearing armor, and I have a protective barrier.”","Huh. So he was the one holding her back now.","Li Jiangbing smacked his lips, then remembered something else and asked, “What about Fu Duoduo? Are you bringing him over here?”","There was suddenly silence on the other end of the phone. Su Yu made no sound at all; the only thing Li Jiangbing could hear was the rush of air as she walked.","Li Jiangbing paused, wondering whether he should say something.","Then Su Yu’s voice came through.","“Zombies don’t have feelings.”","“Everyone says the third generation has developed intelligence, but I don’t think so.”","“They’ve merely learned how to run away. How does that count as intelligence?”","“Jiangbing...” Su Yu choked up. “Fu Duoduo died so horribly...”","But it wasn’t He Tian’s fault.","Su Yu understood that the He Tian she knew had died the instant she became a zombie.","The thing that had cruelly killed and eaten Fu Duoduo was merely a zombie wearing He Tian’s shell.","Li Jiangbing sighed and reminded her, “Let me know you’ve gotten home safely.”","Su Yu agreed.","A few minutes later, he received a text from her saying that she had arrived home. Only then did Li Jiangbing relax.","He was now devoting himself wholeheartedly to studying his superpower.","At first, he had been delighted and fascinated by it. But after seeing what other people’s abilities could do, he had begun to feel vaguely uneasy.","Especially after he had exchanged notes with Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan in the courtyard. Those two seemed to understand this sort of thing very well. They said that although everyone’s superpowers were weak for now, these abilities would definitely grow stronger over time.","They had said it with absolute confidence.","Li Jiangbing believed them.","He felt that if superpowers were truly this weak and could never grow stronger, then there would be no point in having them at all.","Besides, these abilities had appeared alongside the zombie virus. The zombies were evolving from one generation to the next, so he believed that superpowers could evolve as well.","In between killing zombies in the courtyard, he had found time to ask the two anime enthusiasts how to increase the strength of his ability.","Those two had answered with supreme confidence.","“Train. You have to train. It’s just like building muscle.”","That was excellent news. They worked out regularly; training was the last thing they were afraid of.","After returning home, Li Jiangbing plugged the sink and filled it with water. Then he began to practice.","He wasn’t the only one who had gone home and started tinkering with his superpower instead of immediately going to bed and getting some rest.","In fact, everyone with an ability had been unable to resist experimenting with it.","Su Yu was sitting on her bed, working hard to release her protective barrier and trying to control it.","She discovered that when released naturally, the barrier was tiny, like a half-open umbrella standing upright. It was just large enough to protect her alone.","If she allowed it to fade on its own, it lasted for approximately thirty seconds.","That was actually shorter than the time it had lasted when she was fighting He Tian in the courtyard.","But when the barrier faded naturally, it caused no strain on her brain. Back in the courtyard, her desperate will to survive had forced the barrier to last an extra ten seconds or so, and afterward it had felt as though a needle were repeatedly stabbing her brain. The pain had come in sharp, rhythmic bursts.","Su Yu tried to expand the area covered by the barrier and extend its duration. It wasn’t impossible, but either effort placed a burden on her brain.","In less than half an hour, Su Yu was already dizzy and nauseated, with a tight chest and an urge to vomit.","But she refused to stop.","This was a gift from heaven—a stroke of incredible luck.","Compared with the water- and fire-based abilities of her neighbors, and even compared with Jiang Cheng’s spatial ability, hers was something entirely different.","The protective shield was different from every other superpower!","If her shield became strong enough, she could protect a great many people!","Her head felt as though it were being stabbed with needles. Su Yu still went to the bathroom and vomited twice, though there was hardly anything to bring up. The first time, she vomited clear water; the second time, stomach acid.","Su Yu rinsed her mouth, then gritted her teeth and released the protective shield again.","She did not stop until her nose began to bleed and stained her clothes, and the world in front of her repeatedly went black. After wiping her nose, she collapsed onto the bed and drifted into a half-conscious sleep.","Li Jiangbing had suffered more than a nosebleed. His ears were bleeding too.","But people who worked out regularly had a high tolerance for pain. Li Jiangbing’s was especially high; otherwise, how could he have built such a muscular physique?","Li Jiangbing was also daring, with no shortage of willpower. More than that, he felt an urgent craving he could not describe. He kept going until even his eyes began to bleed, and only then did he finally lose the courage to continue.","Over the course of one night, the amount of water he could control had expanded from the size of a ping-pong ball to the size of a basketball. He was very satisfied.","He had a feeling that if he kept practicing, he might die.","People who worked as fitness instructors paid attention to regulating their clients’ exercise levels. It was not as if there had never been cases of people dropping dead from overexertion. Whenever something like that happened, the gym would usually have to pay out so much compensation that it would close down and go bankrupt.","Wu Jiancheng, the building’s floor manager, had a fire-based superpower.","He practiced at home as well.","Unlike Li Feng, he could not conjure fire out of thin air. He needed a source of flame first.","After practicing for an entire night, he had managed to make the fireball he could control somewhat larger. But the fact that he needed a source of fire really bothered him.","He began pondering what he could do about it.","Could he keep the flame on his body from ever going out?","If he controlled the flame at the smallest possible size, it would consume almost none of his brainpower.","He tried this for the whole night, carrying the tiny little flame around even when he went to the bathroom to take a dump, using it as his “source.”","He saw no problem with it and decided to keep it burning while he slept.","Then, in the middle of the night, he felt pain on his scalp. He opened his eyes to find roaring flames. His house was on fire.","As it turned out, his pillow had caught fire and singed his scalp. Otherwise, he might have slept comfortably amid the blaze.","Fire-type superpowered user Wu Jiancheng: “...Fuck.”","Gao Yuxuan and Zhao Yi were far too excited to sleep.","Zhao Yi did not return to his own home. He went straight to Gao Yuxuan’s place instead.","Zhao Yi had a single bed, while Gao Yuxuan had a double bed large enough for both of them.","The two of them kept practicing their superpowers and constantly probing for their rules and limitations.","Zhao Yi had carried a potted plant up from the main entrance downstairs. The flowerpot came with soil already in it.","Zhao Yi focused on working with that one pot of dirt.","Since the conditions limited the amount available, he decided to test its strength instead.","Under his control, the soil kept changing shape. As he practiced, the rate at which he improved rose rapidly.","Even Gao Yuxuan was astonished. “How the hell are you so good at this?”","Zhao Yi might have felt embarrassed saying it to someone else, but he had no such reservations with Gao Yuxuan.","In fact, he was a little smug. “I’ve practiced meditation.”","He had practiced for quite a long time, training himself to concentrate intensely and maintain that concentration.","He had hoped to unlock the potential of his brain and become a superpowered user.","Putting everything else aside, there was one exercise where he would place a pen on the table, focus all his attention on it, and try to lift it from a distance using mental power. Zhao Yi had once practiced that for one or two hours at a time.","With that kind of perseverance, a person could probably succeed at anything.","Except lifting a pen from a distance.","Compared with Zhao Yi, Gao Yuxuan was somewhat lacking. Although repeated practice had strengthened his tiny electric current, he soon developed a nosebleed.","Zhao Yi was startled. “Stop, stop, stop, stop! Take it easy. Don’t blow yourself up!”","The anime and manga fans had a lot of strange terminology that ordinary people were unfamiliar with.","“Blowing yourself up” was one example.","After all, that was how it always happened in manga.","Boom! The body exploded, and energy scattered in every direction.","Anime came in different varieties depending on the target audience. There were shoujo manga, shounen manga, and even grim, bloody horror stories. The manga boys read tended to be much more gory than the manga girls read.","Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan’s heads were crammed full of all sorts of bizarre knowledge.","The two of them even created a table, with one page for each of them.","Zhao Yi dictated his notes. “22:41. Soil reached a speed of forming a wall in two seconds. It takes three punches to smash it apart. Its hardness currently cannot directly withstand the charge of a second-generation zombie. No additional strain on the brain.”","“23:39. It takes five punches to smash it apart. It might be able to withstand one impact, providing a lifesaving defense at a critical moment. No additional strain on the brain.”","Gao Yuxuan typed rapidly on the keyboard. In addition to entering the data, he added a note: “Because the quantity is currently too small, the effects of material quality on cohesion speed, strength, and strain on the brain cannot yet be evaluated.”","“Requires a large-scale outdoor experiment next time.”","Then he recorded his own results. “Voltage reached 35 volts.”","There was a voltage tester at home, which was perfect for the job.","At the beginning, the voltage had been only five volts. It had risen little by little from there.","“Ugh.” He complained, “My rate of improvement is way too slow.”","Zhao Yi comforted him. “Don’t rush. You only awakened a few hours ago. Keep practicing and it’ll continue to improve. At thirty-six volts, you’ll break through the safe-voltage threshold.”","Gao Yuxuan said, “Thirty-six volts can barely kill a person, let alone a zombie. Zombies can lose a hand, a leg, or half their bodies and still be fine.”","The two shut-ins continued making quantitative records while discussing the matter.","“So I think attacking the body is pointless. The brain is the key. Look, a zombie’s wounds don’t rot, but once it loses its brain, the body starts decomposing.”","“The brain doesn’t just control the body’s movements. It probably also secretes something that maintains the body’s enhanced state and prevents it from decaying.”","“So we have to attack the brain. Electrifying the brain until it’s fried should have the same effect as smashing it apart.”","“Which means that in addition to power, we need to practice our aim.”","The two of them did not know that although their progress was slow, they were on the right track.","The electric-type superpowered users in the military camp had already confirmed this through battles on the brink of life and death.","The shut-ins remained immersed in the excitement of exploring a new world, unable to fall asleep.","They lay on the same bed, feet touching, talking deep into the night."]},{"number":94,"title":"Chapter 94","paragraphs":["Jiang Cheng had barely stepped inside her home when Mo Li slipped in through the window at almost the exact same moment.","Although Jiang Cheng and Mo Li were too far apart to communicate directly, they could still sense each other’s presence. Mo Li no longer needed to curl up in her shoulder bag and accompany her everywhere.","When Jiang Cheng was in the courtyard, she could generally sense his approximate location.","The second outbreak of the zombie virus was completely different for Jiang Cheng and Mo Li than the first had been.","Neither of them felt the slightest bit nervous.","New zombies had appeared in the residential complex, including intelligent third-generation zombies, yet Mo Li gave no warning and showed no signs of tension. This meant that, as far as Mo Li was concerned, the situation around them posed no threat.","Jiang Cheng assumed this was because there probably weren’t many zombies nearby.","That was simply how the suburbs were.","In the morning, huge crowds of people poured into the city; in the evening, huge crowds returned to the suburbs. The population traveled back and forth in mass between their homes and workplaces. During the day, the city became deserted.","Today’s outbreak had occurred before the end of the workday. In other words, the residents of the complex had listened to Jiang Cheng’s advice and hurried home in time.","But as far as the entire Science and Technology New District was concerned—or at least its residential areas—it was a ghost town.","The neighboring Jixiang Jiayuan and Yujing Xiangyuan communities probably held only a few elderly people and housewives.","Most of the younger children had died during the previous disaster, while the older ones had been at school and had not returned.","Now, compared with the zombies she was already familiar with, Jiang Cheng was more interested in the newly emerged superpowers.","With a wave of her hand, two keys appeared in her palm.","The storage space was simply too convenient. She had taken the two keys from the property management center without anyone noticing.","Not a single person had discovered what she had done.","So much had happened over the past two months.","Some things had seemed important at first, but later became insignificant and were forgotten.","The conference room was one example. Back then, everyone had possessed only limited protective gear and weapons, and no one had any experience. They had treated injuries with extreme caution and had even welded the doors shut.","Later, everyone had weapons and armor, and they had killed so many zombies that their hands ached. No one cared about the conference room anymore.","At most, there were only a few zombies inside.","By then, a few zombies were no longer worth anyone’s attention.","The appearance of third-generation zombies had indeed been unexpected, but they were merely second-generation zombies that had gained intelligence. When it rained, they knew to run home. Their combat abilities had not increased by any significant degree.","Fortunately, they had not caused any serious harm.","Another thing people had forgotten was the supplies taken from the Fifth Ring Road and locked behind the civil-defense door in the underground parking garage.","Jiang Cheng had casually asked Little Fang about them and learned that the supplies were still there. No one had touched them.","The things that had once been used to save their lives had become so unappealing after the disaster that everyone was too lazy even to look at them.","They had all eaten until they were sick of them.","After the temporary committee had naturally disbanded, the conference room and the supplies in the underground garage were considered to have been handed over to the property management office.","The property management staff would deal with the zombies, and they would manage the supplies.","The two keys Jiang Cheng had obtained using her spatial ability were the key to the civil-defense door in the underground garage and the key to the chain lock hung on the door to prevent others from getting in.","As the representative of the temporary committee, Jiang Cheng had reclaimed control of those supplies.","She put the keys back into her storage space.","The space was still too small for the keys to be of any use for the time being.","She would save them for later.","Like everyone else, Jiang Cheng spent the evening repeatedly practicing her ability. She had already tested the storage space’s limit before meeting Li Jiangbing. During her practice, she immediately pushed it to its maximum capacity and then tried to force more things inside.","For example, a roll of toilet paper.","A roll of toilet paper was naturally very light. It successfully went in, pushing the upper limit just a tiny bit further.","Then she tried another roll.","Jiang Cheng wasn’t afraid of the stabbing pain in her brain.","Something in her mind had been locked away: the memories of the world she had lived in before transmigrating.","She even wanted to know whether continually increasing the strain on her brain might shatter those chains.","Most people stopped practicing as soon as they began to suffer nosebleeds, or at most when their ears started bleeding, realizing that they were in danger.","But there were two lunatics here—Li Jiangbing and Jiang Cheng.","Mo Li suddenly raised a paw and pressed it against her, then gestured toward her face with a claw.","Jiang Cheng wiped at her face and only then discovered that even her eyes were bleeding.","She went to the bathroom and looked in the mirror. The sight was rather eerie and sinister. If she went out at night to frighten people, the effect would probably be no worse than that of a zombie.","Jiang Cheng suddenly froze.","She couldn’t help wondering what connection there was between awakening a superpower and mutating into a zombie.","Both appeared to involve changes at the genetic level. The only difference was the direction in which those changes developed.","From that perspective, could one say that they were essentially no different—that they were actually the same thing?","Jiang Cheng lowered her head and washed her face.","Mo Li stood guard on the sink.","The zombies in the residential complex no longer made Mo Li nervous. Instead, the cat was more concerned about the human girl pushing her ability past its limits at such an intense pace.","Jiang Cheng dried her face with a towel. When she raised her eyes and saw Mo Li, another question occurred to her: could her storage space hold living creatures?","She reached out and placed her hand on Mo Li’s head.","Mo Li glanced upward. “?”","Jiang Cheng rubbed the top of his head.","Of course, she couldn’t use Mo Li as a test subject. What if something went wrong?","That evening, Song Jingshuo spoke with his parents on the phone.","He was lucky. Neither of them had mutated during either outbreak.","On his way home, he had called to tell them not to leave the house and to isolate in separate rooms.","His parents were business owners. They weren’t extraordinarily wealthy, but their family was comfortable and well-off.","The two of them were now semi-retired and had bought a seaside villa for their old age. Fortunately, they had been staying there during both outbreaks.","Because the villa was far from the city, shopping was inconvenient, so Mrs. Song had stocked the house with a large amount of food and household supplies.","The villa community had a very low population density, which meant there were particularly few zombies. During the first outbreak, the residents had joined forces to eliminate the zombies in the community.","The community had originally been designed for retirees. After experiencing the first zombie disaster, many of the elderly had developed a different perspective on life and had left to reunite with their surviving children.","As a result, the already sparse population had become even smaller.","When the virus broke out, the community was the ideal place to take refuge.","Especially after the previous disaster ended, Mrs. Song became even more convinced that stockpiling supplies was useful and stored even more things. She had even bought another chest freezer.","After Song Jingshuo told Mr. Song about the mass murder in Shanshui Yayuan, Mr. Song hurriedly had sturdy security bars and a reinforced security door installed at their villa.","He also purchased protective armor, riot shields, and weapons.","Strictly speaking, ordinary people could not buy riot shields or weapons under normal circumstances. They were controlled items.","But these were no longer normal times.","During the month after the first wave of the zombie disaster ended, large quantities of such equipment had circulated on the market. They were things that had been distributed to the public for use during the disaster but had never been collected afterward.","Mr. Song didn’t even need to go into the city. He could find everything he needed at markets on the outskirts.","Some of the stains on the armor hadn’t even been washed off.","The disaster had clearly already ended. Even Song Jingshuo had believed at the time that it was “over.”","But his parents were determined to buy one, and money wasn’t an issue for them. Song Jingshuo didn’t stop them.","Who would have thought the virus would erupt a second time?","During the phone call, Mr. Song kept asking, “What kind of person is this friend of yours? How could she have known in advance? Someone with connections and a background like that must be extraordinary. You need to stay close to her. That way, if anything happens, you’ll have a better chance of staying alive.”","What background or connections did Jiang Cheng have? None at all. She didn’t even have parents anymore—only a cat to whom she could entrust her feelings.","Song Jingshuo gave a vague acknowledgment.","But he couldn’t stop wondering why Jiang Cheng had been able to predict it in advance.","Everyone had definitely wanted to know today, but they had all held back from asking. There were more urgent matters to deal with, and Jiang Cheng wasn’t going anywhere.","They could ask her tomorrow.","But Song Jingshuo was in a terrible mood.","If your entire team suddenly got promoted while you alone remained at your original level, you would feel just as awful.","Song Jingshuo had always believed that, whether in intelligence, physical fitness, or mental resilience, he was outstanding among ordinary people. He was a strong person. So how had everyone else evolved together while leaving someone as exceptional as him behind?","Where had he fallen short?","His stomach began to growl, and he realized he was hungry.","Normally, he wouldn’t eat this late at night, since it would interfere with managing his figure.","But there were zombies now. Eating his fill was the first priority. He had to make sure he always had enough energy and stamina.","Song Jingshuo opened the refrigerator and decided to cook himself some noodles.","Noodles, eggs... Then he reached for the vegetables.","The bok choy was blocked by a cabbage, so he reached in to move it aside.","His fingertip touched the cabbage.","...","Song Jingshuo remained in that position for a full half minute.","He simply couldn’t believe what he had sensed.","He found it difficult to accept.","Someone as well-rounded and outstanding as him should naturally have become part of the evolved army. He should naturally have awakened a superpower.","He had actually spent the entire evening thinking about it.","Even if he couldn’t gain an obviously offensive ability like metal or fire, he should at least have a special ability such as spatial manipulation or a mental power. If all else failed, he could reluctantly accept an earth-based ability with defensive properties.","At the very least, he could settle for water, which didn’t seem to be particularly useful.","There was a reason for that, after all: water was associated with wealth. People in finance believed in that sort of thing.","Song Jingshuo picked up the cabbage and stared at it.","But no matter what, it couldn’t be wood.","Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan had spent the entire night muttering, “Why isn’t there a wood ability?” and “Wood is the only one missing.”","Actually, Song Jingshuo felt that “wood” was merely a term based on the theory of the Five Elements. A more direct and accurate name would be “plant ability.”","Song Jingshuo focused his mind and gathered his strength.","Without blinking, he stared at the cabbage in his hands, watching for any changes.","This was incredibly frustrating.","Song Jingshuo was the kind of person who could perform mental calculations, analyze situations, and make predictions at lightning speed. In practically one second, he had already calculated the future applications of the superpower he had just awakened.","After all, during the previous zombie disaster, everyone had nearly eaten themselves sick on canned food and desperately wanted a bite of fresh vegetables.","This did not suit his style at all!","Furious, Song Jingshuo pressed his forehead against the refrigerator door.","This superpower was worse than having none at all!","The next day, the overcast skies cleared. It was a crisp autumn day, with endless blue skies and not a cloud in sight.","Everyone still alive in the Youth Apartments came downstairs to gather in the small plaza. This included Aunt Pan, Manager Wang, Yang Xinyan, the security guard Little Fang, and the others.","Every surviving resident of the complex was there.","When Jiang Cheng appeared, everyone stared at her.","The previous day, they had first needed to eliminate the zombies and secure a space to survive, so everyone had held their questions in all night, waiting for this moment.","Sure enough, someone in the crowd couldn’t hold back and called out, “Jiang Cheng—how did you know the zombie virus was going to erupt again?”","The plaza instantly fell silent. Every eye turned toward the young woman with the little black cat perched on her shoulder.","That included Song Jingshuo, Li Jiangbing, Zhao Yi, and all the other devoted supporters and trusted followers of Jiang Cheng. None of them said a word, because they also needed to know exactly how she had found out.","This was a question Jiang Cheng had to answer.","Yet Jiang Cheng said, “I didn’t know. I just guessed.”","The crowd was silent for a moment before erupting into a buzz. Naturally, no one was willing to believe her.","“How could that possibly have been a guess?”","“Because yesterday’s situation was exactly the same as what happened on June 15,” Jiang Cheng said, raising one finger. “First, the sky was purple. Second, my head hurt terribly, as if something were about to explode.”","She looked around at everyone. “Did not a single one of you notice those two things?”","The crowd froze, looking at one another.","“Was it purple?”","“Yes, it was purple. I saw it yesterday.”","“No, I mean on June 15.”","“I don’t remember that.”","“Who remembers what happened that day? All I remember is the zombies.”","“I remember a little. I was worried it might rain that day, so I brought an umbrella. I think the sky really was purple on June 15.”","When people thought of that Saturday, June 15, what they remembered most vividly was the sudden loss of consciousness and the horrifying shock that followed upon waking.","As for the weather that day, it was blurred in their memories.","The main reason was that no one had connected the weather that day with the zombies. So even if they had seen the purple sky on June 15, their brains had classified it as irrelevant information.","People naturally forgot things like that—just as you might not remember what you were doing on this date last year.","The brain’s memory was selective.","“Does no one remember?” Jiang Cheng turned the question back on them. “My head hurt terribly on June 15. Didn’t any of you feel that? Everyone said yesterday that you did.”","Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan exchanged a glance. After hesitating for a moment, Zhao Yi raised his hand and said, “Yesterday, we did feel as if our heads were about to explode. But we didn’t feel that way on June 15.”","He asked, “You already had that feeling on June 15?”","The sensation of one’s head seeming ready to explode was extremely painful.","But after it did, people gained superpowers.","That was why Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan were so concerned about it, and why they had asked.","“Yes. I had it that time on June 15, and I paid particular attention because the sky looked so strange. I heard someone say that there might be a thunderstorm, so I went home early instead of staying in the courtyard. That’s how I survived, which is why I remember it so clearly.”","“Yesterday, I started feeling the same way from the morning onward. But I didn’t realize it immediately.”","“Only after I got off the plane and looked up at the sky did I suddenly understand. The two things that had happened on June 15 were happening again.”","“That’s it?” someone asked. “What if it was just a coincidence?”","Jiang Cheng smiled.","“If it had only been a coincidence...”","“Then it would have cost everyone half a day of work and made you all come back for nothing.”","“You would have been angry. You might have cursed me or laughed at me.”","“Jiang Cheng is crazy. She’s so desperate to become the leader that she’s making a spectacle of herself, spreading rumors and causing trouble.”","Jiang Cheng said, “I can accept all of those consequences.”","“But that’s the kind of person I am.” She remained composed, just as she had every time she made the final call in front of everyone during those six weeks. “Even if there’s a very high chance it’s merely a coincidence, I—I’m still going to issue this warning to all of you.”","“Because that’s the kind of person I am.”","“Otherwise, I wouldn’t be standing here in front of you.”"]},{"number":95,"title":"Chapter 95","paragraphs":["Yes.","If Jiang Cheng were an unremarkable person who faded into the crowd, how could she have left so many unforgettable moments in everyone’s memories?","Every time, she made people sigh, “As expected of Jiang Cheng.”","For a young woman to stand out during a crisis like that and make a whole group of able-bodied men follow her commands and arrangements, she had to be this kind of person.","By this point, many people in the square had already been convinced.","But Jiang Cheng did not end the topic. Instead, she asked, “Let me ask one more time. Did no one feel that same pain in their head on June 15 as they did yesterday?”","She looked toward several people who had already known since yesterday that they had awakened superpowers.","But when they saw her gaze sweep over them, they all shook their heads and denied it. “Yesterday was the first time. Nothing happened on June 15.”","Jiang Cheng nodded. “In that case, I’ll be honest with everyone about something. You all know that I’m very strong, right? I’ve always told everyone that I’ve been strong since I was little—stronger than some men, even.”","Everyone knew this.","Whenever people privately discussed “Jiang Cheng from the Provisional Committee,” they could never avoid mentioning her “beauty, ruthlessness, quick mind, and great strength.”","“I lied,” Jiang Cheng openly admitted.","Everyone was puzzled. They could not understand what there was to lie about regarding her strength. She was strong, and everyone had seen with their own eyes that she did not hide behind others when killing zombies.","Jiang Cheng continued, “On June 15, the sky turned purple, and it felt as though my head was about to explode. When I woke up, I discovered that I had become stronger.”","Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan exchanged startled looks and said in unison, “You mean...!”","Those two understood the fastest. They had been pondering the matter of superpowers all along.","Seeing that most people still looked confused and had not grasped her meaning, Jiang Cheng elaborated.","“Yesterday, many people experienced headaches like I did both times. When they woke up, they had superpowers.”","“But yesterday wasn’t my first time. The last time this happened, I didn’t gain a superpower, but I did become stronger.”","“I realized at the time that something was wrong, but I didn’t find anyone else who was like me. I vaguely sensed that it might be connected to the zombie virus. To keep everyone from becoming overly sensitive and treating me like a potential zombie, I didn’t tell the truth.”","“Yesterday, the exact same thing happened again. This time, I gained a superpower. And this time, there were finally other people like me.”","“So I began to wonder—is it possible that what we call the zombie virus is actually upgrading and modifying us humans?”","“The first time, the modification didn’t succeed. Those who didn’t turn into zombies were people whose modification had failed to complete. I may count as someone who was partially modified successfully. Although I didn’t awaken a superpower, at least my strength increased. Looking back, my physical foundation must have been upgraded.”","“And zombies weren’t the result of an unsuccessful modification. They were... the products of a failed modification.”","“Now the second round has arrived. This time, it may be carrying out another modification based on the previous one. As a result, the probability of success has increased. Some of us successfully upgraded and evolved, gaining superpowers. Others still failed.”","“But those who failed are lucky too, because failing at least means they won’t turn into zombies. The ones whose modification failed completely became zombies.”","“This is the theory I came up with after thinking about it all night yesterday. I believe it makes sense. What do you all think?”","Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan were the first to applaud in support. “That’s exactly what we came up with! We think you’re right!”","The two of them had stayed up late discussing the matter, and their theory was more or less the same as Jiang Cheng’s.","So when Jiang Cheng presented a theory that matched their own ideas, the excitement and delight they felt was something others could not possibly understand.","Most of the residents of the Youth Apartments had received higher education.","When a theory was logically coherent, people were willing to accept it.","The crowd began murmuring, and everyone could not help discussing it with the people beside them.","Jiang Cheng gave them two minutes, then drew the conversation back to the main point.","“So that’s why. Because I had already been affected the first time, when I realized yesterday that the coincidence of the sky changing color and my headache occurring was exactly the same as on June 15, I didn’t need to hesitate. I immediately sent a mass text message to everyone.”","Put that way, this really was so unmistakably Jiang Cheng.","Yes, that was exactly what Jiang Cheng was like.","She could make a decision without the slightest hesitation, immediately and decisively. Everyone had witnessed it with their own eyes and benefited from it personally.","The question Jiang Cheng had been required to answer—“Why did you know the virus was coming in advance?”—had received an answer everyone accepted.","People sighed one after another. “Thank goodness Jiang Cheng is that kind of person.”","“If it were me, I definitely would’ve hesitated. I probably wouldn’t have sent that message to everyone.”","“Yeah, absolutely.”","Su Yu especially admired Jiang Cheng for this quality—for her decisiveness and determination.","After thinking it over, Su Yu realized that if she were in Jiang Cheng’s place, it would be difficult for her to make such a firm decision at once.","She would certainly have worried, “What if it’s only a coincidence?” and “What if nothing happens and everyone blames me or laughs at me?”","The most likely outcome was that she would have her own suspicions but lack the courage to warn anyone else. Instead, she would hide by herself first, wavering and hesitating.","That kind of decision was more in keeping with her personality.","Jiang Cheng suddenly clapped twice, interrupting the noisy discussion. “All right. Everyone, line up by building. Let’s count how many people we have.”","This meant the six building heads had work to do.","The building heads of Buildings One, Two, and Four—Wu Jiancheng, Li Jiangbing, and Song Jingshuo—were all still there.","Nie Kuizhang, the head of Building Three, had died.","The head of Building Five had never shown up. No one had seen him, and he might not have returned at all.","The head of Building Six had mutated into a zombie, and the residents of his building had gone to kill him yesterday.","Now, people had stepped up to take charge of Buildings Three, Five, and Six. None of them were strangers. They had all been members of the Provisional Committee, and everyone had already worked together long enough to be familiar with one another.","The residents formed six lines to count the number of people present.","When Li Jiangbing saw that half of Wu Jiancheng’s hair was gone, he stared in shock. “What happened to your hair?”","Wu Jiancheng looked miserable. “Don’t ask.”","Li Jiangbing guessed immediately. “You set yourself on fire, didn’t you?”","He remembered that Wu Jiancheng had a fire-based ability, so he figured it out at once. He was delighted.","Wu Jiancheng planted his hands on his hips. “Don’t laugh. I discovered an especially useful application for my superpower yesterday.”","Li Jiangbing perked up. “What is it?”","Wu Jiancheng gave a mischievous grin. “Putting out fires. Didn’t see that coming, did you?”","When people heard the words “fire-based ability,” the first thing they thought of was starting fires.","But the reverse application was putting them out.","In the middle of the night, Wu Jiancheng had been jolted awake after setting himself on fire. When he opened his eyes, half the room had already gone up in flames.","There were no firefighters to call during a disaster like this. If another fire broke out in the middle of the crisis, whether anyone survived depended entirely on luck.","But things were different now.","Wu Jiancheng’s superpower was controlling fire.","It was a little difficult for him to make the flames burn that fiercely, but whenever he wanted to put them out, the fire went out silently wherever his superpower reached.","More effective than a fire extinguisher.","That was an incredibly valuable ability. Practically a lifesaving function.","Li Jiangbing tried to find fault with it, but couldn’t come up with anything. All he could do was give him a thumbs-up. “Awesome!”","Song Jingshuo said, “Get to work first!”","“Right, right!”","Counting everyone was simple. They formed six lines, with ten people in each group, making the total obvious at a glance.","Building One: 69 people.","Building Two: 113 people.","Building Three: 74 people.","Building Four: 85 people.","Building Five: 47 people.","Building Six: 53 people.","Property management: 10 people.","Including the property-management staff, there were 451 people in total.","That was why sweeping through the buildings yesterday had gone so quickly.","There were simply so few people.","So very few.","Once the numbers were announced, the little plaza fell silent.","The last time, there had been nearly two thousand people in the entire residential complex. When they had gathered in the plaza, the crowd had stretched out as far as the eye could see.","Everyone had already been through one zombie disaster. They understood that, given the current situation, those who had not returned were probably never coming back.","Building Two had the most people. Why?","Because the residents of Building Two had interacted with Jiang Cheng the most. As a result, the greatest number of them trusted Jiang Cheng—and the greatest number had returned.","The building captains were mainly registering whether people had armor and whether they possessed superpowers.","While they were busy with that, those who had already registered came over to ask, “Jiang Cheng, are we going to Mai Duoduo today?”","They were all experienced now: burn the corpses, grab whatever they could, and stockpile trash.","The same process might have to be repeated all over again.","That actually sounded pretty good. Mai Duoduo had restocked, so the store should have every kind of item now.","Jiang Cheng didn’t answer right away. Instead, he asked, “Does everyone still have enough staple food?”","“We do.”","“I haven’t finished what I had before. But I don’t feel secure without some food on hand, so I went to Mai Duoduo and stocked up on several more bags of rice.”","“Me too!”","Even people who had once embraced minimalist living had awakened their inner hoarders after experiencing the previous zombie disaster.","They were no longer minimalists. They stocked up on whatever they could—especially food.","“Mai Duoduo is different this time,” Jiang Cheng said. “Last time, it was a weekend night, and the supermarkets were closed, so they were relatively empty.”","“Yesterday was afternoon, when the supermarkets were open as usual. There were definitely people inside. Maybe not many, but there had to be some.”","“Everyone has enough food for now. And... to be honest, I’m guessing the supplies in the supermarket’s storeroom are probably about the same as last time, but this time...”","“There are fewer people, so the supplies aren’t as urgently needed.”","There were fewer people.","Three words, spoken so casually.","Where had all those people gone?","They were all at work. All those exhausted wage slaves working themselves to the bone to support themselves and their families.","Trapped at their workplaces, unable to return.","It was heartbreaking just to think about.","Next door, at Auspicious Garden, there were probably only elderly people and housewives left by now.","Husbands and dual-income couples were likely all stranded downtown.","The elementary and middle school students were trapped at school. Vice Mayor Zheng had ordered schools to make up the classes interrupted by the zombie disaster. The children were attending school throughout August.","If they couldn’t break out, they would all end up like the people at Renxin Hospital.","Everyone sighed.","Some of the people here who had stayed upstairs yesterday were learning about superpowers for the first time.","Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan were responsible for explaining things to everyone. “The most obvious sign we know of so far is a headache. It feels as if someone is sticking a needle into your brain. It keeps stabbing the same spot, one jab at a time.”","Someone immediately spoke up. “Me! Me! I’ve had a headache since yesterday. Does that mean I’m about to get a superpower?”","And it wasn’t just one person.","When superpowers came up, Li Jiangbing felt sorry for Song Jingshuo.","He was strong in every way—so how had he ended up being the only one without a superpower? Jiang Cheng had one, and so did Li Jiangbing. The three of them were supposed to be an ironclad trio.","As everyone enthusiastically discussed superpowers, Li Jiangbing put a hand on Song Jingshuo’s shoulder and comforted him. “It’s fine. Look, people with superpowers are still in the minority.”","That was true. Those with superpowers were a minority; most people didn’t have any.","The majority hadn’t leveled up or evolved. They were still ordinary people.","But Song Jingshuo merely glanced at him.","“Huh?” Li Jiangbing knew him far too well and immediately noticed. “What’s going on? You got one? You have a superpower now, don’t you?”","Song Jingshuo looked away.","So he really did have one!","Li Jiangbing was delighted. “You got a superpower and didn’t say anything? Come on, tell us. What type is it? Fire? Metal? It can’t be earth, can it? That doesn’t suit you. Hey, mine doesn’t suit me either.”","As far as Li Jiangbing was concerned, he should have had a metal-type ability. Fire would have worked too, or earth at the very least.","How had he ended up with water?","Li Jiangbing was incapable of keeping anything to himself. He put an arm around Song Jingshuo’s shoulders and called out to Jiang Cheng, “Jiang Cheng, Jiang Cheng! Jingshuo has a superpower now, but he won’t say what it is!”","Jiang Cheng came over.","Li Jiangbing shook Song Jingshuo by the shoulder. “Tell us!”","With Jiang Cheng there too, Song Jingshuo had no choice but to pull something from his trouser pocket.","Li Jiangbing took a close look, then even leaned over and gave it a sniff.","“Huh? This is... isn’t this a radish?”"]},{"number":96,"title":"Chapter 96","paragraphs":["Song Jingshuo silently exerted his power. Li Jiangbing watched as the radish in his hands sprouted roots, then grew a lush green leaf.","Li Jiangbing was silent for a moment before turning around and shouting, “Old Zhao! Come take a look! Is this the wood type you were talking about?”","Zhao Yi, Gao Yuxuan, and a whole crowd of people came hurrying over.","Zhao Yi had long believed it was impossible for them to be missing one of the five elements—metal, wood, water, fire, and earth—but he never would have guessed that the wood-type ability they had been waiting for all night belonged to Song Jingshuo.","Zhao Yi fell silent too.","Gao Yuxuan shouted excitedly, “That’s it, that’s it! This is definitely the wood type!”","Aunt Pan suddenly said, “I understand now. So that’s how it works.”","A moment ago, Zhao Yi and the others had talked for ages, and Aunt Pan had only half understood. But the moment she saw Song Jingshuo, something suddenly clicked.","She pointed at Zhao Yi. “You deal with garbage, so you’re earth.”","Then she pointed at Gao Yuxuan. “You’re an electrician, so you’re electricity.”","Finally, she pointed at Song Jingshuo. “You make money, so you’re wood.”","Zhao Yi: “...”","No, I don’t deal with garbage.","Gao Yuxuan: “...”","I’m not an electrician.","Song Jingshuo: “...”","Song Jingshuo didn’t understand what making money had to do with being wood.","But Master Luo had died yesterday, and his body had already been brought down and placed in a pile with the others.","Aunt Pan seemed perfectly calm. She neither cried nor made a scene. Still, everyone was careful not to speak too loudly around her, as if afraid of startling something fragile inside her.","Aunt Pan muttered to herself, “I have a headache too. I should have a superpower as well. What kind could it be?”","She seemed quite certain. “It’s either earth or wood. It should be earth.”","She walked straight to the lawn, crouched down, and placed a hand on the grass.","Several seconds passed, but nothing happened.","Gao Yuxuan took a step forward, wanting to comfort her and tell her that not everyone had a superpower.","Aunt Pan suddenly drew a deep breath, gathered all her strength, and let out a thunderous shout!","Gao Yuxuan jumped in fright.","With that shout, the soil beneath the lawn suddenly bulged upward, rising to knee height! It was even taller than the mound Zhao Yi had made during his demonstration the day before.","Aunt Pan, who had neither formal education nor much schooling, had somehow accurately predicted her own superpower.","Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan stared in astonishment.","Jiang Cheng went over and crouched beside Aunt Pan. She pushed at the mound of earth with one hand. It was hard.","She turned to Zhao Yi. “You try.”","Zhao Yi crouched down too. He tried to break it apart with his hands, but couldn’t. He punched it several times instead, only hurting his hand.","Shaking his hand and grimacing, Zhao Yi admitted, “It’s sturdier than the ones I make.”","Jiang Cheng hugged her knees and said, “Auntie, this is really useful.”","Aunt Pan was delighted. “Yes, it is useful. It’ll save us the trouble of using a hoe to turn the soil.”","Jiang Cheng said, “I have a feeling we may be stuck in the neighborhood with them again for quite a while. Later, we can turn over all the flower beds in the compound. You and Song Jingshuo can work together and see if we can use your superpowers to grow vegetables.”","Jiang Cheng’s voice was soft and gentle, carrying a soothing warmth.","Everyone’s hearts softened.","Even Song Jingshuo came over and crouched beside them. “Auntie, I don’t know how to grow vegetables, but I can make plants take root and sprout. You can teach me when the time comes.”","From the moment Aunt Pan appeared that day, everyone could tell that her eyes were actually dull and lifeless.","Everyone in the neighborhood knew Master Luo, but they weren’t nearly as familiar with Aunt Pan. She had always been practically invisible.","It was only when the government called on civilians to take up weapons and save themselves that Master Luo and his wife joined the fight together, and everyone began to get to know her.","After that, whenever Su Yu came across her while entering or leaving the building, she would always greet her.","Back then, everyone had been trapped inside the safe zone. They could eat nothing but canned food every day, yet Aunt Pan’s smile had always been bright and cheerful, giving people the impression that life was still going fairly well.","Some light returned to Aunt Pan’s eyes. “You people all sit in offices. What do you know about growing vegetables? Don’t worry. I know what I’m doing.”","She continued reminiscing. “I had a little vegetable garden behind Building Six, but the manager wouldn’t allow it and had it dug up. What a shame. All those seedlings...”","She had often thought about it during the disaster. At the time, no one could get fresh vegetables or meat.","If only her vegetable garden had still been there.","The reason Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan had kept going on about the wood type the day before was that they had been thinking about vegetables.","Even after the supply routes reopened and supply stations were established, vegetables had always been among the last things to arrive, usually only appearing in the final few days.","But Zhao Yi had never imagined that the first person to awaken a wood-type superpower would be Song Jingshuo.","The moment he imagined Song Jingshuo removing his shiny cuff links, rolling up the sleeves of his white shirt, and following Aunt Pan around to grow vegetables, he found the image almost unbearably funny.","Jiang Cheng quietly chatted with Aunt Pan for a while, and Aunt Pan’s expression gradually softened.","Her husband was gone, but life still had to go on.","People needed something to look forward to.","Little Jiang and Xiao Song had told her that her superpower would be extremely useful, giving her hope.","Jiang Cheng’s phone suddenly rang. She pulled it out and glanced at the screen, a look of surprise appearing on her face.","She said to Song Jingshuo, “It’s Zhou Wang.”","Everyone was surprised, and a little pleased as well. Zhou Wang was still alive.","Jiang Cheng answered the call. “Hello?”","“Little Jiang, it’s me, Old Zhou,” Zhou Wang asked. “How is your neighborhood?”","“We’re fine. We’re counting everyone now. What about you?”","Zhou Wang let out a deep sigh. “We just finished killing all the zombies in the compound. We haven’t cleared all the buildings yet.”","It sounded as if they had made more progress than last time. They had managed to clear the courtyard of their own neighborhood without relying on outside help.","Jiang Cheng asked, “Do you have many people?”","Zhou Wang was silent for a moment before reluctantly admitting, “They’re all elderly.”","There were elderly people, housewives, and a small number of preschool-aged children.","There were only eleven able-bodied adults, including Zhou Wang himself.","Several of them were unemployed and had been staying at home. The others had simply been lucky enough to be home for various reasons. One of them was a middle-school student who had taken a leave of absence. Since he was as tall as an adult, he had also been counted among the able-bodied.","Still, they were relatively lucky. On a workday, the entire Technology New District was practically a ghost town, and a residential complex like Auspicious Garden was just as empty.","Moreover, at that particular time, many elderly people and housewives had been at home preparing dinner. There had been very few people in the courtyard, and therefore very few zombies—only a scattered handful.","Zhou Wang had now learned how to use the internet. He had posted on the neighborhood’s residents’ forum and gathered everyone he could. All eleven able-bodied people put on protective armor and went outside. When several elderly residents saw them heading downstairs, they put on their sons’ armor, grabbed sticks, and came down too.","They assembled a group of fewer than thirty people and killed all the zombies in the neighborhood.","Once they saw that there were no zombies left in the courtyard, some residents whose buildings and hallways were clear came straight downstairs.","At a glance, Zhou Wang saw a sea of white and graying hair. There were even more elderly women than elderly men. The scene perfectly embodied the phrase “the old, the weak, women, and children.”","Zhou Wang felt somewhat despairing about this new crisis.","That had happened yesterday evening. This morning, Zhou Wang had organized everyone to clear the buildings door by door. They had also found several sets of protective armor.","The day before, there had been able-bodied people without armor while some elderly residents possessed it. When the younger men tried to seize the armor from the elderly, a fight had nearly broken out.","Zhou Wang had stopped them.","During the previous zombie disaster, he had established his authority, and that authority had carried over into this one. Everyone was still willing to listen to him.","Some of them had awakened superpowers as well. Everyone felt as if they were living in a dream.","After clearing two buildings that day, someone said during the break, “What are we supposed to do this time?”","There were too few people, and most of them were elderly or weak. They couldn’t even beat others in a scramble for supplies.","Zhou Wang immediately thought of the neighbors next door.","“I’ll come over and find you,” Zhou Wang said.","“Is West Street safe?” Jiang Cheng asked.","“It’s safe. There’s only one zombie wandering around there—and it’s from your residential complex. Hey, hey, all right, I’ve killed it.”","He sounded as though he was already on West Street.","Jiang Cheng called Security guard Fang over. “Is the east gate locked?”","Little Fang was quite diligent. After killing the zombies last night, he had locked it.","Jiang Cheng led a group of people over to open the gate.","Zhou Wang’s expression was especially gloomy.","The first thing Jiang Cheng asked when she saw him was, “Are your family all right?”","Zhou Wang shook his head.","When Zhou Wang received Jiang Cheng’s text, he didn’t believe it at first. But he felt deeply uneasy, and in the end, he followed that unease and decided to go home.","His behavior was much like what Su Yu had imagined she herself would do: lacking the courage to openly warn the people around him, he had slipped away quietly on his own.","He was a middle-level manager to begin with and didn’t need to ask anyone for leave. He merely told one of his subordinates, “I’m stepping out for a bit,” and left.","Once he was outside, he called his wife and asked her to pick up their child. His wife worked at a state-owned enterprise, which had an affiliated school for employees’ children. Its teachers were better than those at the schools in the Technology New District. The child attended that school, which was close to his wife’s workplace.","But by the time Zhou Wang reached home, his wife still hadn’t arrived.","When he called, she said the child was hungry and insisted on having pizza.","Zhou Wang said a couple of things, and his wife grew angry. “How did that Jiang Cheng know? What connections does she have? Didn’t you investigate her? She has no background at all, does she?”","His wife didn’t actually believe him. She had only taken time off to pick up their child because Zhou Wang had insisted.","What she said was precisely why Zhou Wang himself hadn’t believed Jiang Cheng at first.","Zhou Wang wasn’t all that resolute himself. With him wavering, his wife was even less concerned. “We’ll head back after we finish eating.”","In the end, Zhou Wang never got to see his wife and child return.","He was filled with regret. If only he had been a little more resolute then. If only he had firmly believed Jiang Cheng, he would have had the confidence to argue with his wife and make her come back immediately.","But he hadn’t.","There was no medicine for regret in this world.","Zhou Wang naturally wanted to know how Jiang Cheng had managed to predict the zombie virus.","But he knew that Jiang Cheng had only had the phone numbers of three people in Auspicious Garden. If she had selflessly sent the warning message to everyone, then only those three people in Auspicious Garden would have received it.","The other two hadn’t come back.","The rest of the people in the complex knew nothing about it. The matter was simply too suspicious, and Zhou Wang didn’t want everyone finding out at a time like this and causing further complications. He held back and didn’t ask.","He only asked, “How many people are there in your complex?”","“More than four hundred,” Jiang Cheng replied.","The moment Zhou Wang heard that number, he guessed that these people must have believed Jiang Cheng and returned. Otherwise, they should all have been trapped at their workplaces, and there wouldn’t have been so many young people at home at that time yesterday.","Zhou Wang asked again, “Has anyone in your complex developed anything unusual?”","Everyone knew what he was referring to.","Li Jiangbing asked with a grin, “You mean superpowers?”","He raised his hand. A tiny ball of water hovered in his palm—the water he had just taken from the fountain in the complex.","Zhou Wang let out a breath of relief. “So you have them too.”","“What kind of superpowers do you have?” Li Jiangbing asked.","“I run fast,” Zhou Wang said.","Li Jiangbing blinked. “Huh?”","Zhou Wang knew that words alone wouldn’t prove anything, so he demonstrated.","With a whoosh, he shot out of sight. He raced about a hundred meters down the passageway inside the east gate, then whooshed back. The whole thing took only a few seconds.","Everyone was dumbfounded."]},{"number":97,"title":"Chapter 97","paragraphs":["Li Jiangbing ran over to call Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan.","The two came hurrying over with shining eyes. As soon as they saw Zhou Wang, they asked, “Did the muscles in your legs evolve?”","“Are you a speed-type?”","“No. Neither,” Zhou Wang said. “Actually, I control air.”","He thought for a moment, then gave a more precise explanation: “Air currents.”","When he ran, his ability split apart the airflow directly in front of him. The air divided and swept around him on both sides, while the airflow behind him pushed him forward.","In reality, he was being propelled along by the air as he “ran,” expending very little of his own energy.","Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan slapped their hands together, so excited they could barely speak.","“Wind-type!”","“I told you there had to be other special abilities!”","Zhou Wang asked, “Do all of you have superpowers now?”","Jiang Cheng replied, “Only some of us.”","Jiang Cheng looked past Zhou Wang.","Zhou Wang hadn’t come alone. He had brought an entire group with him.","Half of them were elderly, and half of those elderly people were actually old women—and they were all wearing armor.","Previously, the armor had gone first to men, then to younger men, and among the young, to those who were stronger and more robust.","Jixiang Jiayuan had originally received only a hundred sets of armor in total. Many of those had gone missing after the disaster ended.","Yet now even elderly women were wearing armor. Just how desperately short of manpower was Jixiang Jiayuan?","Jiang Cheng’s words—“There are fewer people now”—had taken on a tangible form.","“Miss,” one of the old women asked when she noticed Jiang Cheng looking over. “Miss Jiang, are you going to buy Duoduo today?”","The other old women quickly chimed in. “If you’re going, take us with you!”","This was the passageway just inside the east gate. They had to walk several dozen meters farther in before reaching the open courtyard. The old men and women craned their necks to look inside, eager to see how many people the Youth Apartments had this time.","Regardless of whether it was the last trip or this one, the Youth Apartments were unquestionably the strongest fighting force in the area.","Now that all they had left were the old and weak, they wanted to cling to someone stronger.","Jiang Cheng said, “We don’t even know what the situation with Duoduo is yet. We want to observe things first.”","After thinking for a moment, she added, “You don’t need to panic so much about supplies. There are probably plenty of apartments whose occupants never made it back. If things get truly desperate, you can try coordinating with your neighbors first.”","She didn’t say steal or rob. She said “coordinate.”","Even Zhou Wang had to admit that the suggestion made sense.","Everyone understood that in a densely populated urban area, many people had certainly never made it back.","All of them were wearing armor now, and several sets had been taken from apartments they had forced their way into.","At a time like this, there was no point talking about unlawful entry, robbery, or private property. Everything had to be done according to circumstances and urgency.","Zhou Wang said, “We just came to discuss things. Our two communities are familiar with each other, and we cooperated last time. We hope to keep that cooperation going this time as well.”","Jiang Cheng asked, “How many people are there in your community altogether?”","Zhou Wang sighed. “A little over a hundred.”","“How many of them are still useful?”","Zhou Wang glanced back. “They’re all here.”","The old men and women fell silent too, watching them anxiously.","There was also someone who looked like a middle school student, with a faint down of hair above his lip. He didn’t dare interrupt either, simply listening to the adults speak.","He seemed less composed than Little Huang.","Jiang Cheng asked, “Where’s Little Huang?”","“Haven’t seen him. He should’ve gone to school,” Zhou Wang said. “If he were here, he’d definitely come looking for me. I haven’t seen his mother either. She’s a civil servant and works at the development-zone government offices. She probably hasn’t come back either.”","Old Huang’s family of three had all been people of courage and bearing. After Old Huang’s death, Zhou Wang had continued to look after Little Huang.","If Little Huang had been home, he wouldn’t have hidden away instead of coming out.","Unlike several households whose elderly members had armor at home but refused to send anyone out—or even hand over the armor.","The people from the Youth Apartments said nothing. They simply looked at the group, their faces full of helpless sorrow.","Zhou Wang understood. He said, “We’re only hoping that if you go buy Duoduo, you’ll let us tag along. We’ll just follow along and take advantage of the protection you provide on the way. Otherwise, with this bunch of old folks, we really won’t manage.”","He clasped his hands together. “Please, everyone, give us a little help.”","Jiang Cheng turned back and exchanged looks with the others.","Interestingly, if Jiang Cheng had been alone, she could have refused Zhou Wang’s request without the slightest hesitation.","But precisely because other people were present, she couldn’t bring herself to be so cold and heartless.","After all, even Song Jingshuo—the publicly acknowledged social Darwinist and self-interested elitist among the Youth Apartments—couldn’t bring himself to ignore a group of elderly people.","Everyone whose eyes met Jiang Cheng’s gave a slight nod.","Jiang Cheng said, “This situation is different from last time. Neither community has many people left, and most households still have some food stored away. There’s no need to panic. Before we decide whether to buy Duoduo, we need to observe the situation first.”","Zhou Wang also knew that things weren’t yet so urgent. He had come mainly to state his position and maintain good relations.","Jiang Cheng hadn’t agreed, but she hadn’t rejected him outright either. That was enough.","The people from the Youth Apartments had stayed just inside the east gate to receive them, with no intention of letting them deeper into the community.","Zhou Wang thanked them repeatedly before leading his people back.","Jiang Cheng and the others headed back.","Some people were still registering over by the small plaza. Those who had finished registering were already piling up corpses in preparation for burning them.","But a dispute had broken out in one spot.","When everyone went over to see what was happening, they found Su Yu.","Everyone had put on armor before coming downstairs, and Su Yu was wearing the medium-sized suit of armor she had bought.","The armor’s original owner had come looking for her and was insisting that Su Yu return it.","Su Yu refused. “I bought it with my own money. The transaction is complete.”","The man said, “I’ll give you a refund.”","“I don’t want your money,” Su Yu said.","“I’ll give you double!”","This wasn’t about money at all.","Armor could be called the greatest invention of the previous zombie crisis.","Its protective capabilities were so excellent that once humans put it on, they could attack with full force and abandon. They no longer had to focus more on defense out of fear of being injured and infected.","It had completely reversed the balance between humans and zombies.","By the later stages, people were no longer afraid of zombies at all. That psychological transformation had also rested on a material foundation.","Su Yu naturally refused again. “I don’t want your money!”","Su Yu was a member of the provisional committee. She actively participated in all kinds of activities, and many people knew her well enough to understand her personality.","The man’s thoughts shifted, and he tried a different argument. “I’m much stronger than you. When we go out to kill zombies, I’ll be far more useful than you. It’s better for everyone if I’m the one using the armor.”","Su Yu hesitated.","She had indeed been persuaded. Deep down, she felt that her combat ability was inferior to his, and that keeping a suit of armor for herself might hold everyone back.","The silly girl was about to take it off.","Li Jiangbing swore and hurried over.","He didn’t expect Jiang Cheng or Song Jingshuo to say anything fair. He knew both of them too well and understood exactly what they were like.","For Jiang Cheng and Song Jingshuo, they would definitely rather have a stronger male fighter wearing armor accompany them.","That was simply the kind of people they were.","But Li Jiangbing was different.","People naturally had those they were closer to than others. To Li Jiangbing, Su Yu was one of his own.","He couldn’t stand by and watch someone bully her like this.","The moment Su Yu moved to take off the armor, delight flickered across the man’s face. Li Jiangbing immediately stepped between them.","“What are you doing? I’m talking to you! Don’t take it off. What do you mean? You already sold it to him!”","The first “you” was directed at Su Yu; the second was directed at the man.","Li Jiangbing was already a burly man, and wearing his oversized armor made him look even bigger—like a mountain.","He blocked Su Yu completely from view.","Su Yu still wanted to explain, but Li Jiangbing cut her off and went straight after the man. “You just had to fight over the armor a woman’s wearing? There are four hundred suits of armor in our complex! Don’t you know how to go find one in someone else’s apartment? Use your brain!”","“But...”","The man did know of several neighbors who had armor but hadn’t returned this time. The problem was that getting it would mean breaking down their doors and trespassing illegally.","“But what? What ‘but’? Which building are you in? I’ll go with you.” Li Jiangbing looked around and spotted someone he knew. “Hey, you! Bring your crowbar and come with me!”","Jiang Cheng supported this plan. Armor was far too important in the fight against zombies to be left unused.","“Anyone without armor, find an apartment that has some,” Jiang Cheng said. “Jiangbing will lead a team to pry open the doors. Get all the armor out.”","Once Jiang Cheng spoke, it was as if the “official authorities” had approved the plan.","A crowd immediately gathered around them.","“I don’t have any.”","“My next-door neighbor should have a suit.”","“I know whose apartment has one.”","Li Jiangbing led a group of people without armor from door to door, searching for suits to salvage.","Bodies began to be burned in the square.","Master Luo’s body was among them.","Aunt Pan finally burst into tears. It was better that she let it out; everyone was afraid that holding it in would make her ill.","Manager Wang ran back and forth, organizing everything and doing his best to show how useful he was.","Compared with the previous time, there were far fewer bodies this time.","But the flames were still searingly hot, just as they had been before.","The feelings in everyone’s hearts, however, were different now.","There was less fear and less grief. No one was panicking. They had all been tempered by experience.","Jiang Cheng’s phone rang again.","She glanced at the screen. The caller was Li Feng.","Thank goodness—Li Feng was still alive.","Jiang Cheng answered. “Li Feng?”","But the call was disconnected immediately.","She called back, only to have the other end reject the call again. Clearly, he couldn’t answer at the moment.","Jiang Cheng didn’t call again.","The storeroom door at Maiduo Supermarket was half open.","A zombie had been wandering around inside for quite some time, pacing back and forth near the doorway. Then it was suddenly drawn by a noise outside and finally squeezed through the gap in the half-open door into the shopping area.","The storeroom was spacious, with an extremely high ceiling. The shelves were eight meters tall.","If someone looked up from below, they would see that even the highest shelves were piled with large packages of goods.","A professional mobile ladder was parked beside one of the shelves. The platform at the top of the ladder was right next to a gap in the top tier of the shelf. Large packages of goods were stacked all around it, but not in that particular spot, creating the gap.","Nothing unusual could be seen from below.","In reality, at the very top of the shelf, the stock clerks had arranged a ring of merchandise around the edges to block the view. The space in the middle had been cleared out. There was not only a small plastic stool and a folding table, but even a single mattress.","There were boxes of snacks, water, and playing cards, along with one wuxia novel and two erotic comics.","This was the stock clerks’ secret hideout.","Normally, they came up here to slack off. Even when the manager came looking, he could never find them. If they were caught again, they would simply claim they had gone to the bathroom. In reality, they would hide up above, covering their mouths as they snickered at the manager weaving through the shelves below in search of them.","Now Guo Jun and Brother Dong were hiding there. The two of them had lain flat among the merchandise, peeking out with only their eyes exposed as they watched the zombie. They waited until it finally left the storeroom and entered the shopping area.","Only then did they let out a long sigh of relief and sit up together.","Brother Dong felt that he was unbelievably unlucky.","He knew that after heartlessly taking the supplies and abandoning his coworkers back then, there was no way he would ever be able to work with them again. So when the manager had called him back to work after the disaster, he hadn’t gone. He had simply resigned.","At the time, however, the government had pressured businesses to immediately restore logistics and help ordinary people return to a normal life.","The supermarket had been swamped with work and short-staffed, so his resignation paperwork had never been processed.","Finally, things had slowed down a little in recent days, and Human Resources called him in to settle his wages.","His parents had a rural home on the outskirts of the city, where they grew vegetables, raised chickens, and worked their fields. The population density was low, and it was safe.","He had been living quite comfortably there. Yet, of all times, he had chosen to come in yesterday to collect his pay.","And that was when the second outbreak of the zombie virus happened.","Brother Dong felt especially guilty. He couldn’t shake the feeling that Heaven was punishing him for abandoning his coworkers.","Please, don’t let him die here."]},{"number":98,"title":"Chapter 98","paragraphs":["Thanks to the continuous background music in the supermarket, Brother Dong and Guo Jun could still whisper to each other under its cover.","Brother Dong: \"We need to find a way to close that door.\"","Then the storage room would become their safe zone, keeping all the zombies locked in the shopping area.","There were all kinds of food and drinks in the storage room.","They had peed in mineral water bottles all last night. If they could close the door, they could also find a basin to take a dump in peace.","Anyway, there were basins and toilet paper.","Just as they were thinking about closing the door, two more zombies staggered in.","Brother Dong and Guo Jun quickly shrank back and didn't dare to make a sound.","If there were only two zombies, they could give it a try. The fear was that the noise from the fight would attract all the zombies outside.","Those two zombies walked deeper and deeper. Damn it, it seemed they were unlikely to stagger out again. Fortunately, they were original zombies.","Guo Jun took out his phone to check the time and found that the battery was almost dead.","He felt his pockets and found that he didn't have a spare battery with him. That was bad. Once the phone battery died, they were really doomed.","When there was only a red line of battery left, Guo Jun sent a text message to Jiang Cheng for help in the hope of a miracle.","He was now as regretful as Zhou Wang.","He should have just turned around and run back to the Youth Apartment when he saw Jiang Cheng's text message yesterday. It was only about eight or nine hundred meters away, and it would only take a few minutes to run there.","Now it had become an insurmountable chasm between life and death.","Guo Jun regretted it so much.","But they weren't originally from the Youth Apartment. When they moved in after seeking refuge there, Jiang Cheng led a group to clear a supply line. Then Li Feng established a supply point. Jiang Cheng directly transferred them here to help. Only Guo Jun stayed in the Youth Apartment, helping Master Luo with various repairs.","But at that time, Jiang Cheng was always out killing zombies.","They didn't have many opportunities to interact. Guo Jun knew Jiang Cheng was capable, but he didn't trust her as much as those who were always around her.","He showed the text message to several stock clerks yesterday. Actually, he also felt a bit uneasy.","But when he went to the manager, the manager scolded him angrily: \"Do you trust the country or her? The zombies are finally gone, and she spreads such rumors. She should be arrested by the police. We're so short of staff now. Don't cause any trouble for me!\"","People are always more likely to trust those they get along with for a long time. So Guo Jun chose to believe the manager.","Now he regretted it so much.","Brother Dong was sitting right next to him, craning his neck to see who he was sending the message to. When he saw the name of the recipient, he mouthed, \"Jiang Cheng?\"","There were two zombies staggering around downstairs, so they didn't dare to make a sound.","Guo Jun nodded.","Brother Dong didn't take Jiang Cheng's text message seriously at all yesterday and even laughed at it.","But now he understood Guo Jun.","Jiang Cheng was probably the only one who might come to rescue them now.","The last zombie disaster broke out on Saturday night, and government rescue didn't start until Wednesday. Later, it was found that they couldn't handle it, and finally the masses had to be mobilized.","Now another wave had come. The army and the police would surely lose a large number of people again.","The manpower would be even more strained. They couldn't count on government rescue.","Right now, the only thing they could count on was the Youth Apartment.","Come on, Youth Apartment! Come and grab supplies quickly!","The two men lay on the mattress still wrapped in plastic film, staring blankly at the high ceiling.","Suddenly, a blue light flashed!","There was a text message reply!","The two of them sat up straight away!","When Jiang Cheng received the text message, Li Jiangbing had just led a group of people noisily to search for body armors.","Jiang Cheng let out an exclamation and showed the text message to everyone: \"Guo Jun is asking for help.\"","Master Guo was a master at all kinds of repairs. After the zombie disaster, he still worked part - time in the Youth Apartment.","Because the property management was extremely short of staff, besides changing light bulbs and fixing power sources, he also had to take care of unclogging sewers and toilets. Everyone knew him.","Guo Jun probably never thought that these simple jobs like changing sockets, screwing fuses, and unclogging sewers would affect his fate at this time.","Because when everyone heard it was him, they were all inclined to go and rescue him.","Of course, the main reason was that even though the food situation wasn't as dire as the first time, they would eventually have to \"visit\" Mai Duoduo.","Whether they went early or late, the zombies wouldn't starve to death. They would always be there waiting.","But Master Guo might starve, die from holding it in, or be bitten to death.","So, it was better to go while he was still alive.","For Jiang Cheng, it was even better. Originally, she would have to take risks to retake Mai Duoduo without any prior knowledge. Now, it was as if there was a scout inside.","She directly edited a text message to Guo Jun: [Describe the current situation. How many zombies are there approximately? How many are second - generation zombies? Are there any newly evolved and intelligent ones? What's the proportion of each type of zombie? The more detailed, the better.]","The other side sent a text message saying the environment wasn't suitable for a phone call, so she also replied with a text message.","Thank goodness!","Guo Jun immediately started typing a text message, his fingers flying on the nine - key keypad!","[There aren't many zombies! Really not many! There were very few people on Thursday afternoon! There are only about one or two hundred! They are mainly in the shopping area! I'm hiding in the warehouse. There are two here! We can't see outside, but there really aren't many! Really!]","He desperately emphasized \"not many\", afraid that if there were too many, the other side wouldn't come.","That text message was sent out just before the phone shut down.","Then the phone completely ran out of power and went black.","Guo Jun mouthed to Brother Dong, \"What about your phone?\"","Brother Dong made a gesture of rummaging through his empty pockets, indicating that he had lost it. He didn't know where it had dropped during the panicked escape yesterday.","Guo Jun was furious.","Li Jiangbing led everyone to pry open doors and search for body armors.","Since the Youth Apartment often had collective activities, the neighbors on the same floor basically knew who had body armors and still remembered.","The Youth Apartment had a total of 400 sets of body armors, but actually, some had been lost after the disaster.","Jiang Cheng announced the situation of Mai Duoduo through the building's broadcast system. Li Jiangbing said, \"Oh, it's Old Guo. It's good that he's still alive.\"","Actually, compared with many white - collar workers in the Youth Apartment, Li Jiangbing and Guo Jun, who had similar educational backgrounds, felt closer to each other.","One graduated from a vocational high school and the other from a technical school.","Jiang Cheng called Li Jiangbing specifically to ask when he would finish.","She needed at least two hundred people.","Li Jiangbing said, \"It's hard to say. We're prying open the doors one by one.\"","Jiang Cheng thought for a while and called Cui Haiyang over: \"Can you pick locks?\"","Cui Haiyang was a gold - type psychic who could control metal. He was practicing turning steel pipes into steel spikes and was called over.","Cui Haiyang didn't expect such a request. He could only say, \"I'll give it a try?\"","He immediately found the nearest door and tried it.","As soon as Cui Haiyang touched the keyhole, he knew: \"I can do it!\"","With a click, the lock opened.","\"I can feel the shape and structure as soon as I touch it,\" Cui Haiyang said in amazement. \"Then I just need to control the lock tongue.\"","No one could have imagined that the first use developed for the gold - type psychic power was this.","Cui Haiyang ran to find Li Jiangbing. Picking locks was as easy as pie for him.","Li Jiangbing was worried about him: \"Be careful not to have a nosebleed.\"","\"It's okay for this,\" Cui Haiyang said. \"I don't feel any burden. It's very easy.\"","In the end, they found less than 340 sets of body armors.","Currently, there are only a little over four hundred people in the entire community, so the coverage rate is quite high.","Jiang Cheng assembled a fully-armored team of two hundred people. She left one hundred and forty sets of armor in the community, saying, \"From now on, there must be people wearing armor on fixed patrols in the community.\"","Things are different now. The third - generation zombies have gained intelligence. They won't rush out recklessly, attracted by sounds or living people. They might be lurking somewhere, waiting for a chance to launch a surprise attack.","The community is no longer as safe as it used to be.","She also called Zhou Wang and said, \"We're going to retake Mai Duoduo.\"","As for Zhou Wang's Senior Lightning Squad, Jiang Cheng and the others didn't actually expect them to contribute much. But if you want to seek protection, you have to show the right attitude.","It's impossible to just sit back and enjoy without doing anything.","Zhou Wang, of course, understood. He said earnestly, \"The people we can provide are the ones you saw earlier.\"","There were about thirty people. Half of them were old people, and half of the old people were old ladies. Among them, there was also a middle - school student.","Jiang Cheng said, \"...Alright then.\"","The departure time was set for the afternoon. Everyone went to have lunch first.","When they set off in the afternoon, it was indeed the same group of people they saw in the morning.","Theoretically speaking, these old men and women were the brave and responsible ones among the elderly in Jixiang Jiayuan.","The people from the Youth Apartment didn't particularly reject them.","Many young people's parents and elders were not in City S but in their hometowns. Maybe their parents also had to pick up kitchen knives and rolling pins and face the danger with their graying hair.","Moreover, many people's parents had died in the first wave and this wave.","Most of them didn't show it.","They would just cry behind closed doors. Once they went out, it was hard to tell. The living should just live on well.","Regarding the parents who had gone missing in the previous wave, many young people didn't even go back for the funeral. Because there was no sign of them, neither alive nor dead.","This was the situation across the country. Once someone went missing, it was better not to think about it too much.","Everyone's view of life and death had been changed by the zombies.","Actually, there was relatively little danger outside.","During weekday afternoons, the Science and Technology New Area was like a ghost town. Especially in the residential area, there were few people on the streets.","The zombies in the community were concentrated there because the people were in the community before they turned into zombies.","But on the way to Mai Duoduo, they noticed something - the convenience pharmacy that Jiang Cheng had once led a group to rob had been looted again.","Many small shops in the surrounding area had closed down. Even though the government had implemented policies to reduce rent and provide compensation, a large number of them still went out of business.","Only pharmacies and supermarkets, which were essential for people's livelihoods and supported by the government, quickly resumed business and restocked their shelves and warehouses.","Now, the newly - replaced glass door of the pharmacy had been smashed. Looking inside, there were a lot of medicine boxes scattered messily on the ground.","Although not everything had been taken and there was still a lot left, everyone was speechless.","Zhou Wang was extremely embarrassed and explained, \"The old people have many underlying diseases... so... well...\"","Several old people wearing armor also explained, \"It wasn't us.\"","They had gone to the Youth Apartment with Zhou Wang at that time.","The old people remaining in the community peeked around and found that Jixiang West Street was safe. The only zombie there had been killed by Zhou Wang and his group.","Then someone remembered the time when the pharmacy was ransacked by the people from the Youth Apartment.","The old people hit it off and decided to strike first!","Jiang Cheng's mouth twitched.","Actually, the situation this time was very different from the last one. Except for places like hospitals, supermarkets, and schools in the Science and Technology New Area, most places were empty.","The supplies were still in place, but the surviving population had decreased significantly compared to the last time. Theoretically, there should be far more supplies available than last time.","Moreover, everyone was more experienced this time and had armor.","If this pharmacy was gone, they could simply go to a pharmacy on a more distant street.","There was no need to be so impatient. Their behavior was really disgraceful."]},{"number":99,"title":"Chapter 99: The 099","paragraphs":["Jixiang Jiayuan was currently relying on Youth Apartments for help—one could even say it was dependent on them—yet it had sneakily snatched the pharmacy out from under Youth Apartments first. It certainly looked rather bad.","That wasn’t how one behaved when asking for someone’s help.","Zhou Wang hurriedly changed the subject. Looking at Jiang Cheng’s group, he asked, “Why are you still carrying forks?”","Several people in the group were holding U-shaped forks.","These things could only serve as auxiliary tools; they couldn’t kill zombies. To kill zombies, one either needed blunt weapons, such as steel pipes or spiked clubs, to smash their heads, or sharp weapons, such as kitchen knives, watermelon knives, machetes, or the very handsome ethnic-style steel saber Song Jingshuo carried, to sever their necks.","A U-shaped fork could only pin a zombie down and keep it from coming over.","Jiang Cheng wasn’t keeping anything to herself. Eliminating the zombies was a common challenge for all humanity, and everyone had to face it together.","She told Zhou Wang, “We’re planning to study the effects of superpowers on zombies.”","“Huh?” Zhou Wang was surprised. “Are they useful? They don’t seem to work very well to me.”","“They can be improved. You have to practice repeatedly. It’s the same principle as working out.”","So far, there were only enough superpowered people in Jixiang Jiayuan to count on one hand.","There was Zhou Wang, who had a wind-based ability.","A young, strong man with a fire-based ability.","Two elderly women with wood-based abilities.","That was it.","The situation was bleak.","Zhou Wang casually asked, “What kind of superpower do you have?”","Jiang Cheng only replied, “A support-type ability.”","She didn’t elaborate.","Zhou Wang tactfully refrained from asking more.","Someone in the group suddenly said to the person beside him, “Look, it’s Jiang Cheng’s cat.”","Everyone turned toward the voice, but all they saw was a black shadow disappearing into the distance.","Mo Li never took the ordinary route. He ran along the residential compound’s railing, leaping from one concrete pillar to the next. He moved incredibly fast; by the time everyone turned to look, he had already vanished.","Judging by the direction he had gone, he seemed to be heading toward Mai Duoduo.","Someone worriedly asked, “Is he going to be all right?”","After thinking for a moment, someone else said, “There’ve been zombies rampaging around for so long already, and Black Civet has always been allowed to roam freely. If something were going to happen, it would’ve happened by now. Cats are fast. Don’t worry.”","Someone else said, “Mo Li looks like—”","“Huh? Isn’t he black?”","Jiang Cheng knew that Mo Li had gone to Mai Duoduo first. She wasn’t worried. The little black cat had fully recovered long ago, and when she hadn’t been looking, he had even transformed and killed four or five zombies in one breath. That was proof enough of his strength.","Zhou Wang, on the other hand...","Jiang Cheng thought about it for a moment. Superpowers had appeared alongside the zombies, so they definitely couldn’t be useless. She was now devoted to discovering the uses of every superpower.","“Brother Zhou,” Jiang Cheng suggested, “why don’t you go scout out Mai Duoduo first?”","Zhou Wang fell silent.","He pointed at himself with his index finger, seeking confirmation.","“Yes,” Jiang Cheng said. “I was just thinking about what your wind-based superpower could do. It can’t only be used to run away—that would be such a waste. The supermarket is spacious. Even with one or two hundred people inside, the density is low enough for you to run around. And your speed is clearly faster than that of a second-generation zombie. I estimate the zombies won’t be able to catch you.”","The speed of second- and third-generation zombies had been enhanced. They could run extremely fast.","When Jiang Cheng and Shen Wei had fought for their lives inside the house, Jiang Cheng had kept her eyes shut and swung the baseball bat directly at the empty space in front of her. She had taken advantage of the second-generation zombies’ lack of thought and their tendency to attack in a straight line. Every swing had landed.","Otherwise, fighting a second-generation zombie alone would have been quite dangerous. They were simply too fast.","Jiang Cheng’s eyes were full of encouragement. “Brother Zhou, why not give it a try?”","Several people nearby turned to look at him.","The corners of Zhou Wang’s mouth twitched. After thinking it over, he gritted his teeth and agreed. “All right. I’ll give it a try.”","Since the heavens had bestowed him with the ability to run fast, he might as well test it out. He was wearing protective armor anyway. Once he knew what he could do, he would have a better idea of his limits in the future.","Zhou Wang started running and disappeared in a flash.","Everyone let out cries of amazement.","Someone stretched out a hand and lamented, “I’ve had a headache this whole time. Why hasn’t my superpower appeared yet? Come on, hurry up and show yourself!”","It had now been basically confirmed that headaches were a precursor to the awakening of superpowers. Aside from Aunt Pan, another three people had awakened their abilities that morning and afternoon.","One of them had awakened a fire-based ability and immediately produced a huge ball of flame, completely overpowering Wu Jiancheng’s tiny flame.","His name was Cao Jiacai. He was a security guard at Youth Apartments, in his thirties and approaching forty. Among the security guards, he was considered the oldest. Little Fang was the youngest, only nineteen.","He had also been issued a suit of protective armor and followed the others toward Mai Duoduo.","This time, every superpowered person had gone out, even those whose combat abilities were not particularly strong. The main reason was that they all wanted to test their powers.","As the saying went, “Within three steps, there must be an antidote.”","Everyone now felt that calling it the zombie virus was perhaps not entirely accurate, but they would continue using the term for the time being. In any case, the zombie virus had given zombies powerful, incorruptible bodies, while it had also granted humanity superpowers that science could not explain.","Could these superpowers be the antidote to the zombies’ deadly poison?","Everyone had spent the entire day discussing it, and they all felt that it was very possible.","Cao Jiacai’s fire-based superpower was simply too eye-catching. Many people who had touched everything they could think of without awakening a superpower refused to give up and went around touching fire instead. Several people ended up with burns.","As Zhou Wang ran, he spotted the black cat.","The cat was famous. People in several nearby residential compounds knew it—the cat belonging to the young woman from Youth Apartments.","The image of the black cat perched on the girl’s left shoulder was simply too striking to forget.","As Mo Li ran, he suddenly sensed something. He turned his head sharply and saw that Zhou Wang was catching up.","Without a word, Mo Li suddenly accelerated.","Zhou Wang was astonished. He had never kept a cat and had no idea cats could run this fast. He sped up as well. The man and cat soon ran side by side, and neither could gain an advantage over the other.","Before long, they reached the supermarket. The black cat darted away and vanished.","Zhou Wang couldn’t stop for the sake of one cat, so he could only continue running, puzzled about where it had gone.","Humans had their paths, and cats had theirs.","As Mo Li ran, he suddenly sprang into the air, kicked off a tree trunk, rebounded, twisted around, and slipped into a ventilation duct in the building.","He and Zhou Wang were taking completely different routes.","The entire process happened as fast as lightning. Zhou Wang merely blinked, and Mo Li was already nowhere to be seen.","Zhou Wang had no choice but to continue running on his own.","The supermarket’s doors stood open, and the air curtain had been whirring away for two days and one night and was still working.","The instant Zhou Wang passed through the air curtain, he gained a new insight into controlling the airflow. As he ran, he pondered what he had felt, and sure enough, his running speed increased again.","Just as Jiang Cheng had said, superpowers could indeed be improved!","Zhou Wang ran into the supermarket. Before he even entered the shopping area, he saw zombies—security guards, customers, cleaners, and cashiers.","Some of them were even familiar faces.","Although Zhou Wang was fast, this was still his first time charging alone into a crowd of zombies, and he felt somewhat nervous. He held his breath, exerted himself with all his strength, and increased his speed once more.","Feeling the airflow from the air curtain just now had improved his skill at controlling air currents without increasing the strain on his brain.","But now, holding his breath and forcing himself to move faster clearly placed additional pressure on his brain. Fortunately, it was still within what he could endure.","Zhou Wang charged into the supermarket.","Just as Jiang Cheng had said, one or two hundred people was a very small number for such a large supermarket.","While facing one or two hundred zombies alone was indeed rather nerve-racking, the supermarket itself was spacious enough. There was plenty of distance between the zombies—enough for Zhou Wang to run back and forth several times before two of them might even manage to converge.","After running a few steps, Zhou Wang’s fear diminished greatly, replaced by wild exhilaration. With this superpower, what was there to fear? If he couldn’t beat them, he could just run!","He might not be invincible, but staying alive definitely wouldn’t be a problem.","He ran so fast that by the time the original zombies reacted to him, he was already far away. Having lost their target, the original zombies returned to their aimless, shuffling state.","The second-generation zombies gave chase, but they couldn’t catch him. He used the shelves as cover, making quick sharp turns, and the second-generation zombies lost sight of him as well.","Zhou Wang’s confidence soared. He couldn’t help feeling eager to give it a try.","And so he did.","Zhou Wang’s weapon was a rolling pin.","But it was no ordinary rolling pin. It was made of ebony.","Once men hit middle age, they seemed to awaken some innate urge to collect and polish wood. But woodworking was expensive, and his wife wouldn’t allow it.","So Zhou Wang had come up with a little scheme. He bought his wife an ebony rolling pin, hard and heavy. His wife found it too heavy to use and didn’t like it, so it became a hand-held piece for him to fiddle with.","After the zombie outbreak, Zhou Wang gave his wife the kitchen knife for protection and kept the rolling pin for himself.","After all, blunt weapons and sharp weapons could both kill zombies.","Zhou Wang figured that he could use his speed to kill zombies. In theory, momentum could be converted into impact force.","The theory was right. One blow really did smash a zombie’s head apart. But Zhou Wang had forgotten that every force had an equal and opposite reaction. The hand gripping the rolling pin had to bear that force as well.","He could control airflow; it wasn’t as if his muscles and strength had been enhanced. The moment he smashed the zombie’s skull, the rolling pin flew from his hand.","Zhou Wang sprinted after it, trying to catch the ebony rolling pin in midair. If they had been in an open space like a plaza, he could certainly have done it at his speed. But this was a supermarket.","Zhou Wang could only watch as his ebony rolling pin landed on top of a shelf. Unfortunately, the goods piled up there were soft, and the wooden pin sank into them instead of bouncing back out.","Zombies surrounded him, so Zhou Wang didn’t dare linger. He raced over to the kitchenware aisle, grabbed a rolling pin at random, and swiftly retreated from the supermarket.","The group outside had deliberately slowed down and stayed away from the supermarket, waiting for him.","When Zhou Wang ran back, he finally stopped, bending over with his hands on his knees as he caught his breath. Running itself was easy enough, but constantly pumping his legs was still tiring. Middle-aged men just weren’t built for that anymore.","Li Jiangbing was observant. He spotted it at once and asked curiously, “Why’d you come back with a different stick?”","Even the color was different.","Jiang Cheng noticed something else. “Did you get faster?”","Zhou Wang straightened up, planted his hands on his hips, and grimaced as he took two breaths to steady himself. “Yeah. The moment I passed through that downward-blowing airflow at the entrance, I suddenly got a feel for the air currents. My control improved too.”","That was valuable experience.","Zhao Yi and Gao Yuxuan reminded each other, “Write that down! Write that down!”"]},{"number":100,"title":"Chapter 100","paragraphs":["Zhou Wang told everyone the general situation inside the supermarket.","Jiang Cheng asked, “No third-generation ones?”","Zhou Wang stared at her in shock. “Third-generation?”","Jiang Cheng explained, “Their various indicators are about the same as the second-generation zombies, but they’ve developed intelligence. They know when they can’t win and will run away, or even play dead to trick people. They’ve evolved.”","This was the first time Zhou Wang had heard that zombies could evolve again.","The middle-aged people looked bewildered. “Zombies can evolve too? When will this ever end?”","Would humanity ever be allowed to live in peace?","Zhao Yi cut in, “It’s fine. If they evolve, then so do we, don’t we?”","Zhou Wang thought about his own running speed. With speed like that, even if everyone else died, he could still survive. Humanity would always find a way to continue.","He nodded.","But when he turned around and looked at his team, he couldn’t help sighing. Including himself, there were only four evolved people among them.","Because of the oversight, no one had told Zhou Wang about the third-generation zombies beforehand, so he hadn’t been able to observe whether there were any inside the supermarket.","Actually, with Zhou Wang’s speed, even if there had been a third-generation zombie, he would have run away before it had time to display any intelligence.","In any case, the entire team first reminded everyone to pay attention to anything unusual the zombies did, in case they were tricked by a third-generation zombie pretending to be helpless.","Everyone had already started forming groups on the way there. Many of the teammates who had previously worked together seamlessly had failed to return yesterday. These two hundred people had been newly reorganized, and everyone was pairing up with anyone they recognized.","Taking on a second-generation zombie alone was far too dangerous. Three or four people working together could kill one in just a few moves.","Even the smallest combat unit had to consist of two people: one defending and one attacking. With armor protecting them, the chances of injury dropped sharply.","The most unpopular members of Zhou Wang’s team were the elderly women. Nobody really wanted to take them along.","Aunt Pan couldn’t stand watching this. She called out, “You there, come join us.”","Aunt Pan was a woman whose strength rivaled that of a man, and everyone was happy to team up with her. Their group already had enough people, and taking along one more elderly woman wasn’t a problem.","Li Jiangbing took one as well.","Zhou Wang took another.","The others were divided among the residents of Auspicious Garden.","That was how they distributed the elderly women among the groups.","Once everyone was organized, the strongest groups led the way, and the more than two hundred people charged into Maidodo.","The sound of their footsteps alerted the zombies in the shopping area.","One zombie after another emerged from between the shelves and surged toward the open space by the checkout counters.","Humans and zombies clashed in a sudden battle at the registers!","The best junior high school in Guangxiu District, S City, was No. 14 Middle School.","In response to Vice Mayor Zheng’s call to “make up for the classes the children had missed as quickly as possible,” the school had reopened almost as soon as S City resumed work. They needed to finish teaching the lessons left over from the previous term.","Now the school was crawling with zombies.","The campus was quite large. Every so often, a student’s scream could be heard in the distance, accompanied by a zombie’s roar, before vanishing almost immediately.","The class monitor led a line of people behind him. Everyone moved on tiptoe, carefully trying not to make a sound.","Every person, including the class monitor, held up one of the folding mats used for sit-ups. The mats could be folded in half, and when opened, they were nearly as tall as a person.","Everyone was trembling with fear.","Some of the girls had tears in their eyes, biting their lips tightly to keep from making a sound.","That was because class monitor Huang Xuetao had said, “If you dare cry out loud, I’ll throw you out to feed the zombies.”","His dark eyes were cold and hollow. He wasn’t joking.","Everyone had been frightened into obedience.","They all remembered that the class monitor used to be such a cheerful, generous boy who loved helping others. But after returning to school this time, he had completely changed.","Quiet. Withdrawn.","Sometimes, frightening.","They heard that his father had died.","But he wasn’t the only student who had lost a family member. Some classmates had never come back at all, and no one could contact their parents. Their entire families had vanished without a trace.","Many of those still alive had changed, to one degree or another.","But the class monitor was the most frightening of all. No one knew what he had been through.","This class monitor, Huang Xuetao, was Little Huang from Auspicious Garden.","Jiang Cheng’s contacts contained only three people from Auspicious Garden, and Little Huang was one of them.","But the phone actually belonged to Old Huang. University students might already have had phones, but few middle school students were given their own. The school didn’t allow them, either.","The phone was at home, and neither Little Huang nor his mother had seen Jiang Cheng’s messages.","Little Huang cautiously led the five students behind him forward. Their destination was the bicycle shed. Everyone’s bicycles were parked there.","To leave the school, they needed some form of transportation. Otherwise, it was difficult for a person to outrun a second-generation zombie, much less break through a large group of them on foot.","They had to have a vehicle.","Little Huang, walking at the front, suddenly raised his fist. Everyone immediately stopped.","He waved to one side, and the others hurried over and crouched beneath the wall, pressing shoulder to shoulder in a tight cluster.","Each of them opened the mat in their hands and held it over their head, hiding their bodies.","At a glance, it looked like a pile of mats stacked against the wall.","Of course, a normal human looking with their eyes could still easily see through the disguise.","But it was enough to fool the zombies.","Everyone held their breath and waited for half a minute. Sure enough, several zombies rounded the corner, swaying slowly as they wandered along one side of the building.","Everyone was extremely tense. The passage wasn’t very wide, and although they were hiding on the opposite side, they were still afraid the zombies might catch their scent.","Fortunately, a zombie’s sense of smell worked together with its sight and hearing. It needed to discover its prey through sight or sound, and only after getting close could it use its sense of smell to determine whether it had found the scent of fresh flesh.","The process lasted only a few minutes, but to the boys and girls, it felt incredibly long.","At last, they made it past safely.","But Little Huang still hadn’t given the order, so no one dared to move. They continued crouching there with the mats held over their heads.","Only after Little Huang quietly said, “It’s clear,” did everyone fold up the mats and stand, continuing to follow him.","Yesterday, during the second zombie outbreak, they had been in physical education class.","These few students had been responsible for gathering the mats and carrying them to the equipment room. Everyone had passed out inside.","The first person to wake up saw that Little Huang had been the first to regain consciousness. He was prying open the eyelids of every unconscious student.","The eyes changed first, followed by the skin. Prying open someone’s eyes was the fastest way to confirm whether they were about to mutate.","The student who woke first watched helplessly as Little Huang killed two classmates with a shot put. He didn’t hesitate, and every strike was steady.","Neither of those two students’ skin had even begun to change color.","Then, after Little Huang’s headache passed, he realized that he could sense when zombies were approaching. He told everyone to hide.","Some believed him. Some didn’t.","Those who didn’t were dragged away and devoured by the zombies.","One of those students shouted, “They’re over there! They’re hiding over there—”","Fortunately, the zombies could no longer understand human speech, and they merely pinned him to the ground.","While the zombie was crouched over the student, eating him, Little Huang leapt out and crushed its skull with the shot put.","Then he killed the student who had tried to save himself by betraying them.","After that, no one dared disobey or ignore anything Little Huang said.","Yesterday had been chaos. Then they heard what sounded like the head of discipline shouting from upstairs:","“Kids, hide—hide and don’t come out!”","Everyone hid in the equipment room. Through the crack in the door, they watched the teachers raise chairs and desks to fight off the first wave of mutated zombies.","Most of them had some experience killing zombies by then, but the lack of weapons was humanity’s greatest weakness when facing them. One injury meant death.","Yet even knowing that, the teachers still charged forward.","The head of discipline was surnamed Shi, and he was very fat.","He had been far too strict with everyone, enforcing rules about everything from dating to the hairstyles of boys and girls. He required them to wear school uniforms every day and forbade students from wearing overly expensive shoes. He was deeply unpopular.","Behind his back, everyone called him Fatty Shit or Dead Fatty.","Director Shi charged at the zombies with a desk held over his head, roaring as he blocked their advance and bought the students inside the classrooms time to shut the front and back doors.","Everyone shoved storage cabinets, desks, and lecterns against the doors to barricade them.","Then, through the doors, they heard Fatty Shit’s screams.","The students began to cry.","Most of the subject teachers were in poor health.","That was simply what the profession was like, especially for teachers at top schools. Most of them had one ailment or another.","Only the physics teacher, who had arrived that year, liked working out and was relatively strong. He awakened an electrical superpower. With no weapon, he fought the zombies bare-handed, driving his fingers into a zombie’s eye socket and sending an electric current straight through its brain.","The physics teacher was covered in wounds, blood flowing from his eyes, ears, and nose.","It was a fighting style that meant dying together with the zombie.","The cafeteria’s head cook, an auntie, swung her four-foot-long iron spatula at the zombies.","She was the only one who could be considered to have a weapon.","During the battle, she awakened a metal-based superpower. The head of the spatula could transform and extend at will, and the more she killed, the braver she became.","But then she encountered the PE teacher, who had mutated directly into a second-generation zombie.","The PE teacher had graduated from a university of physical education, and his physical abilities were comparable to those of a soldier.","As a zombie, he killed the head cook.","Little Huang and several others hid in the equipment room. There were sit-up mats, vaulting boxes, and basketballs and volleyballs inside. The only thing that could barely count as a blunt weapon was a medicine ball, and it wasn’t easy to use.","Without weapons, they didn’t dare venture outside.","They spent the night hiding in the equipment room. Eventually, they could no longer stay awake and fell asleep. When they woke up, the school had become eerily quiet.","Little Huang focused and sensed the surroundings. He decided it was safe outside, and they left.","He had awakened a superpower called “Danger Sense.” Relying on his perception, the group made their way toward the bicycle shed.","Along the way, they saw, in the distance, that a student in the teaching building had awakened a metal-based superpower. He had melted the legs of desks and chairs into ladders, extending them bit by bit downward from the third floor.","One student after another climbed down the ladder.","But halfway down, several second-generation zombies charged over. The students on the ground scattered in every direction, while those above scrambled back up in panic.","The noise attracted even more zombies.","Many of those second-generation zombies had been teachers who had sacrificed themselves in fierce battles to protect the students the day before.","Guided by Little Huang’s Danger Sense, the group continued forward without incident.","As they passed the laboratory building, someone suddenly called to them in a hushed voice from above.","“Students, students—”","They looked up and saw several heads poking out of a classroom on the second floor. Judging by the color of their uniforms, they were younger students from the eighth grade.","“Students—please help us!” they begged.","Little Huang and the others stacked the six mats they had among them. The students on the second floor planned to jump down and use the mats as a cushion.","Little Huang reminded them in a low voice, “Bite down on your collars. Don’t make a sound!”","The students above turned and passed the warning along.","Each of them held the collar of their school uniform between their teeth. First, they climbed out through the window and lowered themselves onto the rain awning jutting out from the first-floor window. Then they sat down, lowering themselves as far as possible before jumping.","The people below divided up the work. Some held the six mats in place so they wouldn’t come apart.","The others stretched out their arms.","The mats covered only a small area. Although most of the students above managed to land on them, they would immediately roll off and tumble onto the ground.","The others stretched out their arms to catch and steady them, helping them avoid a hard fall. They were afraid that the pain of hitting the ground would make someone instinctively open their mouth and cry out, attracting the zombies.","More than twenty students were rescued from the building.","They said, “The teachers and students in the corridors have all mutated. But there are still people in the language lab and several chemistry laboratories.”","“We have to save them!”","Little Huang actually didn’t want to go save anyone.","Because the person he had to save was in the Technology New District.","His mother worked at the district government office in the Technology New District.","He no longer had a father. He had to save his mother!"]}]);
